        StaticBook("Book of Souls", "The Creator", "This book contains the soul of a Pig\n\nPig:\n  saddle: true\nBreed:\n  in-love: 0\n  age: 0\nMob:\n  health: 10.0\n  attack-time: -\n  hurt-time: 0\ndeath-time: 0\n  pick-loot: false\n  persistent: true\n  name: -\n  name-visible: -\nEntity:\n  pos: -674.4080539210009;37.0;656.1853051031845\n  vel: 0.0;-0.0784000015258789;0.0\n  rot: 42.10591 0.0\n  fall-distance: 0.0\n  fire: -1\nair: 300\n  invulnerable: false\nAttributes:\nMaxHealth:\n  Base: 10.0\n  Modifiers:\n    none\n\nKnockbackResistance:\n  Base: 0.0\n  Modifiers:\n    none\nMovementSpeed:\n  Base: 0.25\n  Modifiers:\n    none\n\nFollowRange:\n  Base: 16.0\n  Modifiers:\n    Random spawn bonus Op: 1\n      Amount: -0.06355855737132463\nEquipment:\nHead Equipment:\n  AIR:-1(0)\nChest Equipment:\n  AIR:-1(0)\nLegs Equipment:\n  AIR:-1(0)\nFeet Equipment:\n  AIR:-1(0)\nHand Item:\n  AIR:-1(0)\nDrop chance:\nHead Equipment:\n  0.085\nChest Equipment:\n  0.085\nLegs Equipment:\n  0.085\nFeet Equipment:\n  0.085\nHand Item:\n  0.085\nSoul Data v0.2\nH4sIAAAAAAAAAAGAAn/9H4sIAAAAAAAAAF1TPW8TQRCdu7MPn0kCiUNFk4ICJIj4A1HijzgxuhDjYNEg0No3sVe+2z129xxQJEQkQpGGX4AQEjRIfEn0AQpoERUSNRIfRX5C2D37IoWRrtjZ2Xlv3psrAljglXvo8+4AA3Dg1GoiVOXedRqhVCSKQYcHxbJSgnYShbKoEzkXchUicekcpFGA3FUSIUz3kKGg3fmI\n3F1FEqo+jCsBjleezSoHTCN3SHfQQkk1Iuti9mbx6/E3Z4668yFGyNRGjJpzxuXyqNoDb40HdJOiSLlaOSi0243aGpeqdO3X4tSfys8ceCblI5HqKfvy8vnfJz9ccMsRT5jaf7t8+8WV+L4D3nqMgijKmemT0ZhpERbwaE7GZIvNdThL5BHFUkZxk4ch39KVPdQKTzTYMAn1DemEqEX26lx0MdC6G8YOTDW5UCSsch4GfMugQR5OlzuSi9jAj\n4iZtAXuBgmCEK08TNRJGNYy0dJGboP5WhxzsMGrIVF946R2DCZvcBEGmRLi98q3j7P+LQ9O1gSPq33TQ+YN8MLr2e3/PwtKTa2nxkJd18I7CRUYWA5Mb8S0x9W8ot2B9OlQJ9ff1PKQN/bXy3PGPZvqxWrSngPOeGIP3DVuBnNT1uPYfz+T//T45oXsbMEJ41Bfe2yDO96nogMzlWQwoGo+iQOi0MchhmZeW7enwrpoQWGdrQitmCHo1fT8TI\n481MCFFleppWZWu3I+VOOlWdYzxWariqn6o6zT5DLl+GG3VH33+dKzpcqD9Grp4c72zsLBKxtydS3F4aEFk1XCmlqGduxzrjTlgvmVMvmnjuRPt27PfnTwPd7bhX8J0uqAggMAAEHAm92AAgAA\nRandomId: 71b61412\n\n\n      The END.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Tales 1", "Farley III Stafyr", "Book of Tales\n\n        Chapter One\n\n      Translated by\n      Isovar Kurben\n                and\n  Norvton Stonefire\nForeword by\n  Norvton Stonefire\n\nI, Novtorn Stonefire, have decided to begin releasing the chapters and stories of the \"Book of Tales\". What the book be, you may ask, so I shall answer. The \"Book of Tales\" is less a book, but\nmore of a compendium of past times, reaching back further and more extensive into Human history than any book I know of. It tells the tale of not only my family, but the tales of many a man who lived and walked the lands before our ancestors. Written\nin a tongue long lost to the common man.\n\nTranslating it out of its original language is a difficult task, a task, on which three men before me have worked on and succeeded to various amounts. These first three chapters were\ntranslated by Isovar Kurben, the son of Galtor I. Stafyr. He received the book originally from his grandfather Beorn Stafyr, who was an aged man at that time. Let his words speak for him.\n\"Old blood runs deep          and has long\n          histories\"\n    -Isovar Kurben\n1. Chapter - Myth\n\nGrandfather had become open about his past in these past two years. He was nearing his eighty-sixth birthday, he was weak and tired. I suppose that he wished to ease his mind before heading on.\nor the stories he has told and things he had done I can understand. Yet again, it deems me that Grandfather intended to preserve something, thus he gave me this mysterious book, called \"Book of Tales\".\nIn his dying breath he told me... no, us, not to forget our roots and to preserve tales of old.\n\nUncle Hanethor was suspicious what it could mean, but he seemingly shrugged it off and turned his attention back to the progressing march\nof the undead. Father did not seem to care too much either, though he mourned remarkably. Aunt Sybilla wept lightly, but a kind smile was on her face... like she has forgiven him for something.\nI will try to maintain a constant series of entries as I progress with the book Grandfather gave me. Consider this the first.\n\n...\n\nI have given it plenty of thoughts, though I assume it is best\nto start with talking about the past with the first who belongs to it. The stories Grandfather told me are a heavy burden on my mind, but blood and family are supposed to know some day.\n\nMy Grandfather, Beorn Stafyr,\ncommitted theft and murder. For a quarrel with his father, Brimar, and being disowned by him, he had slain his very own mother, Alexandra, and stole the heirlooms of his family, leaving a mourning father with a young brother, Gorn, behind.\nThe heirlooms consist of following items:\n\nFirst and foremost, an old crown of copper with an emerald, to be worn by the head of Stafyr. Uncle Hanethor currently has it and wears it often enough.\nSecondly, our old falcon Thondor, grey feathered with a small green tabard. Father meant he had looked like that ever since he can think back, when he was but a child. He seems to be in service to Hanethor.\nThirdly, a set of armor, which deems me of incredible value. A plate armor of gold and a chainmail of silver. Nobody wears it right now, but we keep it safe, as it is... precious. There has to be something about it.\nAlso, two weapons so fine and sharp as if they were never used before, despite their high age. A foreign tongue is written on the hilts of the Longsword Hanethor and the Battleaxe (one-handed, I have to remark here) Galtor. Father and\nUncle both wield their namesakes right now.\n\nThe last heirloom Grandfather gave me was this very book. Book of Tales. Records of times past, records of events, people and items. I wonder what I may dig up...\n...\n\nIt was a dark day as we left our home two weeks ago. The undead are marching onward, nigh unstoppable. Uncle Hanethor led father and our men into a few battles, I took part with my bow.\nIn terms of heirlooms, I was able to witness the twin blades in action for the first time. As if their weapons, armors and bodies were made of paper, Hanethor and Galtor cut through the dark and dead beings with ease.\nThey were able to kill many a foe, but after losing a few men and the relentlessly assaulting undead seemed to take no end, we retreated. I can hear a horn sounding. Finishing this entry, battle calls.\n...\n\nThe Verge. Father is dead.\n\n...\nWe got split up. Uncle Hanethor's children are nowhere to be found. I only have Aunt Sybilla, Suldren, Sevren and his wife Aewves and Hunrad with me. Hunrad leads us, I do hope, to safety.\n\n ...\nThe last entry was years ago. Many a thing happened, I am an aging man now. And the last one alive it seems. I have made the decision to work on this book now, as much as I can, to preserve what can be preserved. To translate what can be translated.\nFollowing was translated by Isovar Kurben from Old Rivachegian to the common tongue. It begins with the eldest entries.\nThus it was in old times past, that the Almannir came to meet their fate. A foe strong enough to crush an entire people, such was the test of Machr, dr Gott (God?). Fyrschlund, dr Dracha (Dragon?), came to consume the lives of many of the\nAlmannir. Heroes fell in battle, one after another. Nobody could stop the beast with its insatiable hunger.\n\nEven Großma, the last of the Galdr, fell to Fyrschlund after three days and nights of battle.\ns all hope seemed lost, the last chieftains of the Almannir came together and rallied their men to their side, a force numbering the thousands of thousands. Led by chieftain Rigfyr Stoafyer, chieftain Krashgar\nRettersma, Altkönig(King?) Zubr Altbom, chieftain Haralt Stoakachl and the female chieftain Juna Wiidafrou, the five armies drew a rainbow through the lands of the Almannir, green, yellow, light-brown, red and blue.\nFyrschlund has been waiting and was prepared. As the bright colored army approached the wastelands of the Northern regions of Almannir, where Fyrschlund has eaten man and Tier (animal?), consumed the plants and very earth itself,\nhe greeted the five last heroes with an army of his own. Reeking and pitch-black, the Totamännr (?) crawled out of the cold and snowy wasteland, thousands and thousands of them, consuming the very light that shone\nupon them by the sun.\n\nFor a week the armies fought, dotting the white snow with tabards and armor of green, yellow, light-brown, red, blue and pitch-black. Fyrschlund himself became impatient\nat the unyielding Almannir and charged into battle himself, burning hundreds of the brave with his searing fire, smashing thousands with his claws and tails. And so it was time that the five chieftains of the Almannir came to fight Fyrschlund\nhimself. Rettersma died first, but took the dragon's tail. Stoakachl took his wings before being stomped under Fyrschlunds claws. Altbom crippled his legs before vanishing in fire. Stoafyer took his breath before being crushed by his jaws\nBut Juna Wiidafrou was not able to slay the dragon, too deep her wounds were. The son of Rigfyr then approached, as the last Almannir standing amidst the field of colors and dead. Fyrschlund was enraged and tried to snap at him, to devour him, to\ndestroy whatever he could from the people who have brought him to fall. Juna took her last will and power and blinded the one-eyed Fyrschlund with an arrow from one of his own Totamännr. Unseen, the son of Rigfyr, climbed on the furious,\nblind and maimed dragon and drove his lance deep into his skull, ending the nightmare. The Almannir saved their lands at the cost of their own lives. And thus the son of Rigfyr was the last of the Almannir, left alone in the endless wastelands\ncovered in what have been such fertile and peaceful people.", ""),
        StaticBook("Botany Guide", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "Sarrion's Pocket book of Botany\n\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\nFire:\n\nCrimson Vase\nFound in: Woodland's and Plains\n((MC Blocks: Grass))\n\nDrake's Tail\nFound in: Savana's, aka Caliphate.\n((MC blocks: Shrub))\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nFound in: Swamps\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nBlood Lotus\nFound in: Woodlands / Plains / Savanas\n((MC Block: Grass / shrubs in Savanas))\nFlametongue root\nFound in: Woodlands / Planes\n((MC Block: Grass))\nWater:\n\nMandragora\nFound in: Swamps\n((MC Block: Lily pad's))\n\nSerpent's Stalk\nFound in: Wood Lands\n((MC Block: Sugar Cane))\nFrost Vine\nFound in: Snowey Regions, Mountains\n((MC Block: Vines))\n\nBlissfoil\nFound In: Woodlands / Plains\n((Mc Block: Blue Orchard))\nAthin\nFound In: Snowey ice lands.\n((Mc Block: Ice))\nEarth:\n\nTippen's Roots\nFound in: Wood Lands / Plains\n((Mc block: Grass))\n\nAlabaster Leaf\nFound in: Wood Lands / Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\nSaffvil\nFound in: Swamps\n((Mc Block: Grass))\n\nClutcher's Straw\nFound in: Savanas\n((MC block: Grass))\n\nMetzli'sTangle\nFound in: Jungles\n((MC Block: Grass or Vines))\nAir:\n\nLarihei's Fingers\nFound in: Snow/Mountains\n((Mc Block: Grass))\n\nElf's Hair Vine\nFound in: Snow/Mountains\n((MC Block: Vines))\nCrouching Feather\nFound in: Wood Land's / Plains\n((MC Block: Grass))\n\nHalfling's Grass\nFound in: Wood Land's / Plains\n((MC block: Grass))\nTips:\n-Alchemist Sheers can be imbued with Unbreaking Glyph to make them last longer and Fortune for better chances to find Herbs!\n\n-If you leave alchemist sheers at 20 Durability before breaking them you can repair them with iron!", ""),
        StaticBook("Brandybuck Brew", "Thomas Brandybuck", "----==[Recipe]==----\n\nIngredients:\n\n500g chopped apples\n3 cinnamon sticks\n30ml water\n280g sugar\n700ml dry white wine\n600ml pear wine\n10g salt\n5g cactus green\n1 egg\n----==[Recipe]==----\n\nProcess:\n\nPlace apples, cinnamon and water in a wee saucepan. Cook o'er a medium heet fer 10 minutes. Add yer oder ingredients to de mix but leave yer wines aside an' stir till sugar 'as dissolved.\n----==[Recipe]==----\n\nProcess:\n\nSet aside yer mix an' let it cool. 'ave a wee smoke break like meself while it does. Den get yer container (either yer keg or jar) an' add de cooled mixture. Now ye add de wines an' seal 'er tight.\n----==[Recipe]==----\n\nProcess:\n\nGive 'er a wee shake erry tree days, an leave 'er in a dark, cool place. Wait tree weeks den spoon yer mixture an' strain de fruit, put de lid back on an' 'ave her sit fer anotha tree weeks.\n----==[Recipe]==----\n\nProcess:\n\nAfta de sixth week strain again and funnel de sediments out o' yer mixture. Let 'er sit for anotha 2 weeks and strain a last time. \n\nAn' now yer able to drink te yer 'earts content.", ""),
        StaticBook("Braxus. II .", "Braxus Ni'leya", "===================\n\n----[ Braxus.II ]----\n\n~ This is part two of a two part series.\n\n===================\n===================\n\n Afraid of becoming impure, I made my home in a cave, I became reclusive and secluded for years. The burning sensation of being able to return kept me alive. I was allowed back and started on a trial of repent, hoping to -\n===================\n\n- restore my name and reputation. Such to this day is still proving hard to do.\n\n It is the 19th of the Deep Cold, 1512. I am 248 years of age. My name is Braxus Ni'leya and I seek to keep the flames of silver burning bright for -\n===================\n\n- as long as I draw breath.\n\n--[ Maehr'sae\n        Hiylun'ehya ]--\n\n~ Braxus Ni'leya.\n\n===================", ""),
        StaticBook("Bringing of Life", "Edwyn Lynderly", "The Bringing\n             of Life.\n\n\n\n  The Notes of Edwyn\n               Lynderly\n6th of Malin's Welcome.\n\nToday begins the endeavour to grow that of a tree, from nothing more than a sapling. I travelled  to the cloud temple, I came across a small store in which to purchase a sapling during my prior task.\nI settled on a spruce sapling, I've always admired how despite being present in the coldest of enviroments they can still flourish into something magnificent. Tomorow I shall attempt to plant my newly obtained sapling.\n7th of Malin's Welcome.\n\nWith sapling in hand, I left the druids grove in search of the perfect location. Wondering into the nearby woods, I soon settled on a small clearing that would be perfect for my tree. Grasping my shovel I dug a small hole, the\nperfect size for my small sapling. Bringing it to settle within it's new home, I brushed the dirt back towards it's original resting place.  It's oddly therapeutic this planting thing. Allowing it a drizzle of water I collected from the nearby river, I\nleft the sapling.\n14th of Malin's Welcome.\n\nA few days have passed since the planting of my sapling, it's growing well. Along with allowing it daily watering, I've been applying bonemeal to help fertilize it's growth. I used a small stick to support the\ngrowing tree. I was concerned it's size would soon cause it to collapse, better it be secure at the end of the day. I'll continue to monitor it's growth over the coming month, hopefully it'll grow into something sufficient soon.. The risk is holds against\nthat of natures  prey makes me anxious.. Once it grows more, that threat will hopefully disperse. I'd rather not have to buy another sapling.\n21st of Malin's Welcome.\n\n§II nearly lost the damned sapling today. I was returning from the river bank, collecting water within my pail when I saw the small critter edging closer towards it. It had a nibble, but dropping my bucket I managed\nto shoo it away from the plant.. It'll need some defense against this, cant sit here day in day out looking after the bloody thing.\n29th Malin's Welcome.\n\nAfter several days of heaving rocks back and forth, I've built a hefty wall around my sapling. It's nothing major but should keep those small bastards at bay, moreso thanks to the lighting.. Or does that\nattract more critters towards it.. Well, a splash late now. I've considered giving my tree a name, oddly. Never really held a 'connection' to anything other than another person.. For now however, I shall name it 'Edwyn's tree.' Very original, I know.\n3rd of The First Seed.\n\nA new month, never really noticed the months pass by until I actually went to record this journal. It's now grown to reach the height of my chest, quite interesting that it grows so quickly.. However, I have been\nfeeding it hefty amounts of bonemeal on a regular basis. Those creatures that lurk the shadows of the grove are awfully useful in obtaining the bones. I've considered stopping the bonemeal, allowing it to go naturally for some time.. Yet, I must admit my\ncuriosity only grasps at my conscious to see just how far I can push this plant.\n12th of The First Seed.\n\nAnother spurt of growth from the plant! It's spectacular to watch, every day I awake to a few new branchs.. It's almost become consuming of my life, keeping me awake as I continplate what I may\nfind in the morning.. Yet, along with this I also cannot concern over it.. A large bear, happy lumberjack or even just that of a strong wind can ruin my efforts. I've still not slowed my bonemeal additions, I figure the large my tree can grow the greater\nchance it stands against these threats.\n15th of The First Seed.\n\nIt's the early hours of the morning, I couldnt sleep. Had this gut feeling something was wrong with the tree, yet whilst trudging from the warmth of my bed I found little to be concerned about. Odd.\n24th of The First Seed.\n\nI can't even maintain it's growth at this point, it's gone far beyond what I even expected. It's already above my height I believe, and yet I cannot stop with the bonemeal. It's practically an\nobsession at this point, an addiction. Even though I admit it I still ignore my own pleas, having this burning desire for it to stretch far above it's surrounding brothers.\n30th of The First Seed.\n\nNearing the end of the second month.. The growth has halted slightly, I believe the earth it has rooted itself into fails to address it's constant need for water. I need a better means of relieving it's constant\nthirst.. Perhaps if I extend the river to run alongside it? However thats an awful amount of work, I'll have to consider it over the coming days.\n4th of The Grand Harvest.\n\nYet another month, and with it my small pond has been completed.. After heaving multiple buckets of water up the small incline leading towards my tree it began to rain.. A days work, completed in minutes by that of\nnature.. Perhaps the aspects noticed by struggle and gave me aid, or just merely a coincidence. Whatever it is, the tree should be able to feed from it's new source for some time.. I've already noticed a hint of growth again, which makes me happy.. I was\nconcerned it had reached its limit.. Yet no, my little sapling has only continued to grow.\n12th of The Grand Harvest.\n\nI woke today to be greeted by a slither of growth once again, and yet, despite such I only feel disappointment. A few local brethren to my tree had given in to the drought of water caused by the massive thirst of my own.\nTheir leaves went brown, and within a few days their trunks failed to sustain themselves as rot caused them to fall.  Perhaps the excess bonemeal has only came to punish me, yet now I fail to grant it such a privlidge and even so it grows..\n19th of The Grand Harvest.\n\nSoon will come the time to show my efforts to Arin. The tree continues to grow substainally, however it's yet to poison any more of the surrounding nature with thirst thankfully.  It's been  an interesting experiance, from\nthe small sapling which could hardly survive.. Requiring a wall for protection, which thanks to my shoddy building has since fallen into ruin.. Makes quite the pretty border however, I must admit.  Now the tree remains large, I doubt I shall leave it come\nthe end of my trial. It's almost like a child at this point, even though it's constantly threatening to destroy more of it's brethren for the precious supply of water, I cannot hate it nor bring the guts to save the others.. It's my tree, and with my care\nit has far outgrown the others.\n\nI suppose that also means this will be the last time I write within this journal, and probably see it. Oh well, fun whilst it lasted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Calebe Voronwe", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Caeleb Voronwe\n\nAge: 15\n\nRace: Human\n\nGender: Male\nCondition/Injury: Suffered burns on his lower legs and arms. An accident with a lava device occured. Burns were painful to the patient.\n\nTreatment Plan: Burns are sensitive, but cream seems to help when applied.\nThe pain in his wounds seem to become far more central, rather than on the outside skin, when cream is applied. Will stay one night in the clinic for recovery.\nDoctor who treated the patient: Hileia'elr\n\nCost: 12 minas\n\nDate: 8th - 9th of The Sun's Smile, 1522\n\nEnd result: The arms were reportedly more painful than the legs, but recovered.\nThe patient left after one night, with no troubles.\n*Hileia'elr's signature would be on this page*\n\n\n-Hileia'elr", ""),
        StaticBook("CAUTION", "Maia", "ATTENTION ! ATTENTION ! \n-=-=- \nZaviel (Main Street 4) is a dark wizard Officialy. Elisa saw him killing a woman and she followed him near some ruins. I followed her. There was a talk. And Elisa got near him and CUT OFF HER OWN TONGUE WITH THE WORDS : \"I\nWOULD NOT NEED THAT BABE\"... \n\nTHIS WAS EXTREMELLY SCARY. \n\nWHEN YOU SEE ZAVIEL KILL HIM OR LOCK HIM IN CAGE. HE IS A DARK WIZARD. \n\nCaution! Be safe around dark wizards!\n            By: Anoniomus", ""),
        StaticBook("CCC Order", "Achranack Shade", "The days are dark as the doctor fall numb. Worry not vengence will come. \n Many men walk in lands of which they know not.\n But even as crows peck his remains. Plagued birds will travel to dreadlands domains.", ""),
        StaticBook("Celarus", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Celarus\n\nAge: 18\n\nRace: High Elf\n\nGender: Male\n\nCondition/Injury: Had a bite injury to the\nneck. May have been severely at risk of infection.\n\nTreatment Plan: Neck wound was cleaned via alcoholic disinfectant, any stray filth was wiped clean, and the wound was treated with pain-killers before being wrapped in bandages.\nDoctor who treated the patient: Doctor Daniel Ward\n\nCost: Free\n\nDate: 7th of The Amber Cold, 1528\n*Doctor Ward's Signature is here*\n\n\n\n\n~ Doctor Daniel Ward", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VI", "March Ash", "Here, in the deep places of the world, they lay sleeping. Gods of scale and claw, sinew and muscle. Beneath rock and magma. The crust of the earth will sunder with their waking, when the Aspects call their banners for the final war.\nDid you think their grand weapons were the trees? No. Ends are made in blood. If we are not laid low by plague, then we will be by the old reapers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Champion", "Oberdiktator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    History of the\n Valued Champion of\n    The Hallowvale\n\n Adil, the Eagle-Eyed\n\n\n   Approved by the\n   Ministry of Truth\nBorn in the hold of\nAl Dirahk, Adil was fathered by Amir Athir al-Hashim, the Amir of the Mubarizun. Adil had with him three brothers and a valued sister, Aisha, though he himself was destined to be the next Amir. Being so, he and Aisha were sent away.\nThey were sent to a mosque called Elspeth to train, Aisha in the arts of diplomacy, Adil in the arts of the duties of an Amir. For years they trained in their arts but, alas, when the time came for them to be called upon, they were abandoned.\nTheir father never showed up to greet them. Distraught, they left Elspeth to go adventuring... Roughly the same time large worms engulfed the continent. Assuming their family and friends were now gone, they stormed onward- together.\nFor ten years Adil and his sister wandered the lands, Adil playing his Oud with deft hands... And crashing bottles into the faces of ruffians alike. However as fate would have it, his wanderings rewarded him. He stumbled upon Al Wakrah, the Caliphate.\n... And his family. And though tearful reunions were in order, they found another member of their party with them;\n\nTheir father.\n\nAs the Ducal War had just begun, Adil and Aisha were both drafted.\nThe war changed Adil and his sister. The details of his battles are not important, all that is is that Adil was a man. When he and Aisha returned to Al Wakrah, they came to a breaking surprise;\n\nTheir father had committed suicide.\nThis event caused the two to break apart. Aishra persued knighthood in the Order of St. Lucien. Adil... Turned to becoming a slaver, and his soul began to rot. The years of slaving turned to years of drugs... Years of sin and whoring.\nIt was one fateful botched slave trade that landed Adil in prison. As he rotted away behind iron bars, a revelation came to him; he was a monster of pure sin. And so, upon his release, he went to find peace and forgiveness... In the Order of St. Lucien.\nWhile forgiveness may of been found, peace was not. In the order, Adil found him self constantly tormented by St. Lucien's leader at the time, Grand Master Baudric. Extreme training and constant beatings rendered Adil near whittled.\nThis was, of course, until the entire restructure of The Order. In one knight, St. Lucien had become Hallowvale Contracting, all thanks to Nafis Yar (whom Adil now calls his battle-brother). Peace and brotherhood, Adil found.\nBut his journy was far from over. In order for ome to be truly accepted into the Hallowvale they must overcome two challenges; kill a vile creature and beat Oberdiktator- or our glorious Kaiser- in a brawl.\nThe first task came when Adil was celebrating with his brothers after a battle won over a group of snowelves. During the celebration the encampment was attacked by a wendigo! The brothers took their place, Adil armed with an arbalest on a balcony.\nThe beast clawed it's way through the camp and made it inside. As it dangled from a shandelier, Adil fired a well-and-true shot into the creature's eye. This epic shot is what deemed him;\n\nAdil, the eagle-eyed.\nHowever, the arrow only made to anger the creature. It lashed out at Adil, mauling him well and- ironically and much to Adil's amusement- taking his eye as well. Though wounded, Adil's brothers revered him a hero. He was promoted to Vandar Council.\nCheif and budding advisor to Nafis Yar (whom was the Vandalore at the time), he continued his work as a mercenary for some time after his slaying of the beast. This was, of course, until the Orenian and Dwarven war began. Hallowvale had to choose a side.\nIn the end, Oren's coffers proved too tempting. Hallowvale was paid to fight orcs, snow elves, and dwarves alike. As Adil himself words it;\n\n\"I wasn't bias, I just liked money in all honesty.\"\n\nNo truer words, Adil.\nThe Hallowvale prospered well in this war. So well in fact, that Adil was invited on a secret mission launched toward the Caliphate. Led by our glorious Kaiser, the Hallowvale proposed to Faiz Charadeen... A union between the Caliphate and the Hallowvale.\nThe union was accepted of course, so birthing the Second Reich, successor of Aesterwald. Adil himself stood right behind the glorious Kaiser as the union was officially passed. In fact, the Glorious Kaiser became very close.\n... But let's save that for later in this story.\n\nShortly after this unification, Vandalore Nafis Yar retired, Frederick II, our glorious Kaiser, taking his place. And so a new Champion was required... \n\nAdil was chosen.\n\"He was my Champion, the man all Vanders of Hallowvale looked up to and had to beat in a slobber knocker fist fight wrestling match to be oathed,\" Adil had to say of the glorious Kaiser. He was awestruck in his choosing to become the new Champion.\nAnd so, comfortable in his new position behind the walls of Al Wakrah, Adil was of course admitted into the town's new Caliphate/Hallowvale garrison... Where he met his lovely court, Rajiya. Adil had little to say, just that he hopes to marry soon.\nAdil, Champion of Vandaloria, shall truly be remembered as a proper hero and Champion by all.\nThe Kaiser himself ahd this to say of the man;\n\n\n\"Adil is headstrong, but valiant. Simple words for a simple man, I knew him before his eye incident. He's the best archer I know and a Master of Filth.\nAdil and I were battle brothers before politicans and I don't think I can be very poetic with my words, but he's a good soldier and an even better man.\"\n\n\n       Heil Kaiser!\n   Praise be to Adil.", ""),
