        StaticBook("Citizenship C1", "Fitonor de Fontaine-Elmpool", "Issued by Fitonor de Fontaine-Elmpool of the Imperial Administration and given to Floyd Suttar whom is a class C1 citizen, on the 15th of the Amber Cold, 1588. This passport is legal tender until 15th of the Amber Cold, 1598, If found, please return to -\nthe Imperial Administration in Johannesburg.\n\n~Fitonor de Fontaine- Elmpool, Auditor General", ""),
        StaticBook("Clarification.", "Evelyn Nithaniel", "Dear Elluna,\n   I've been away many years. When I initially left, it was out of the absolute need to. I had been in the worst shape ever before in my life, and in such a twisted mindset, I thought it would be right.\n  I wrote myself out of your-\n-lives for I thought I had nothing left. In ways I did, in ways I didn't. But no matter what, it was selfish. I saw people blinking out of my life, and decided to just follow them in such a move. People turned a blind eye to my troubles, and it was what-\nwould eventually lead me to following the road I did. Leaving.\n  Before life had taken such a turn, it was me, Rayanne, and your mother. We were sisters, and your mother reminds me greatly of who you have become.\nI had a great many people to live amongst, but as time went on, we dwindled. People left, died, seemingly disappeared. I had Vivian, hopes high of you two and Rayanne's family becoming thick as thieves. Soon, more friends would take their own partings,-\nand sure enough, I was left to raise Vivian alone. And then Tarien, your mother, joined the party. Left you in a basket for us to discover, only a blanket and small teddy to be found. But you were left to us both. Never just I.\nI would eventually leave. Because losing a best friend was never what I wanted, raising two little girls was more than I could handle, and because as time passed, Rayanne grew.. Seemingly tired of me. Her and Ericus, they never struggled.\nAmong the pair and the family unit established, the hardships were distributed well. I wanted that for you, rather than one broken woman.\n\nBut years down the road, I returned. Happily found you to have formed your own life.\nBut I left again, eventually. My mind was still twisted, and it never clicked why I might be needed. So I left.\n\nThis isn't an apology or something to clear my name, but rather something to explain to you why.. Though there isn't quite a 'why'.\nYou're free to go on labeling me as a monster within your mind, Elluna, and to not seek contact. It'd be better to continue life as it once were, so I encourage you do that. But if searching for answers to anything I haven't covered, you are welcome in-\nmy home. At the moment I'm writing this, I reside in Haria, within the Aethermoorian district. Isaac will lead you upon request.\n\nI wish you luck in your endeavors, and commend you for the life you have made for yourself.\n-Evelyn Nithaniel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Close but far", "Corvo Attano", "I sense the voice getting stronger, it can now control me like some sort of demon.\nIt is the darkest, evil side of me that I have never seen or heard before. This is the side that allows me to kill the innocent and take from the poor.\nThe voice only comes when I am angered or am making the wrong choices.\n\nI took a mans life away today, he was innocent but the voice insisted I strangle him as I did it a deep laugh in the back of my head started to grow, I felt weak, But my grasp of\nthe mans neck would not let go, he had tears dripping down his eyes, trying to punch me with his useless fists and then suddenly I fell back, just as the man died.\n\n\"Well done Corvo, well done indeed\" the voice whispered.\n\"Please leave me alone, leave me alone\"\nI cried.\n\"But Corvo\" he smiled before chuckling...\"I am you!\"\n\nCorvo listened carefully tensing his arms with anger.\n\"Whatever you do I do, However whatever I do you do.\" The voice\nmurmured.\n\n\"Now please he said let's get to buisness\"\n\nCorvo's left hand started to move to his blunt, iron dagger, he withdrawed it waving it around.\n\n\"Perhaps Corvo! We should give this\nweapon a trying out\".\n\nA young villager was carrying boxes of food the storage shed in Illicia where they were standing.\n\n\"Kill him\" he snapped\n\"I will not a kill a young boy\".\n\"Kill him or I will him myself Corvo!\" He shouted.\nThe boy looked around and then got back to his work.\n\"I WILL NOT KILL HIM\"\nCorvo raged with anger, blood pumped heavily through his Vessels.\nCorvo felt his grip the sword tightly, he started to move unable to speak he could blink and see.\nHe crept upon the young boy grabbing him by the shoulder.\nThe boy wrestled Corvo but he was too strong for a young boy like him.\nCorvo kicked his chest and got him onto the ground, he pointed his sword at the boy.\n\"Please...Sir do not d..d..don't do t...this to me\".\nA creepy grin grew on Corvo's face frightening the boy.\nCorvo leaped onto the boy stabbing him\nrepeatedly in the chest, blood gushed out of the boy's mouth it appeared Corvo had punctured a lung.\nHe kicked the boy over again and left him to die.\n\"Need's a bit of a sharpen\" Corvo chuckled\nThe force that was controlling Corvo released and Corvo was set free again.\n\"You sick bastard, that boy was innocent\".\n\n\"Now, now Corvo you're the one who released me into your head.\"\n\nWritten by Corvo Attano. ((mrdigdug118\n))", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat: Volume I", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\nMarked Combat:\nVolume I\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\nThe Magical Versus the Mundane- The Knight's Way of Defense Against the Supernatural:\n===================Through the ages, mankind has faced countless threats, both mundane and magical. The wars against the undead have taught us techniques and-\n===================countermeasures that can be- with ample experience, skill and prayer- successfully utilized against the unholy and the profane.\n===================What is Recommended:\n-Numbers\n-Ranged Weaponry\n-Light Armor\n\nExcerpt taken from \"The Guide to Hunting Mages\"\nMarked Combat\n===================Combat Basics:\n------------\nThe 3 Stances\nHigh- Form is leaned in, knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward.\nReferred to as the \"Counter\" stance. Used in an effort to -\n===================counter-act movements from mid-guard and stanceless efforts.\nMid- Form is relaxed, blade pommel is parallel to one's waistline. Knees bent and arms relaxed. Known as the \"Assaulting\" stance.\n===================Attacks vary on situation, be in Arc or thrust. Used to counter low stance and when assaulting shielded or untrained foes.\nLow- Form is lowered, knees bent, body leaned in. The arms are left in a -\n===================half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as, \"Wounding\", stance. Used to counteract High-guard, spearmen and is only used to hinder movement or knock a foe off balance. This stance is used with two handed.\nMovement\n===================When in combat, keep the foe in your direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps taken forward or backward, instead side-step in.\nMovement, cont.\n===================When Assaulting, nature may say rush the target head on, instead, aim to the target's right or left with movements. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Should the target-\nMovement, cont.\n===================continue to stand after the inital blow, aim for immediate execution, striking to either the neck or lower-spine.\nMovement, cont.\n==================\nWhen countering, side-step, parry or retaliate. Know the range of the Foe's weapon, if the range of your own counter-acts that of the enemy's, retaliate with side-step, aiming to either cleave limb or behead the foe.-\nMovement, cont.\n===================Should the weapon be lesser or equivalent, parry and close the gap. The strike won't likely be lethal. Instead, aim to disarm or hinder.\nCombat Stance\n===================So, think of the three stances as a game of Rock, Paper, Scissors. When on even grounds, and not taking situation at hand, the three stances are as such\nHigh-Rock\nMid- Scissors\nLow-Paper\nCombat Stance, cont.\n===================When starting combat, take stance. Do not suddenly switch stance, since it exposes yourself, parry or sidestep while shifting. Shifting to counter will result in a half stance, which is a stance of valuable parries.", ""),
        StaticBook("COMMST MNFEST", "Gu-Zhizhe", "TH COMMUNIST MAIFEST\n\nCAPITALIS BAD COMMUNISM GOOD CAPITALIS BAD COMMUNISM GOO CAPITALISM BAD COMNSM GOD CAPTLMASIM BAD CMSN GD\nCPKTMKSN BD CMSMEM GGGGG\nCPIFJJPIO SBFOS FOSIFJ SOJ\njfiuaglaingoairgaoerigaiofwHUDLSGukilhojblkfdeYMBGRtynkgmjrsfeDW", ""),
        StaticBook("Confessions", "Rinaline Sirius", "Confessions by Rinaline S.\n-------------------\nWhen I first arrived in Haelun'or I was astonished. The beautiful scenery and kind people made me feel at home.\n\nBefore I arrived, I was treated harshly as though I were an animal.\nBack in Oren it was horrible, the people were cruel and I was even called a, forgive me for this vile language, \"whore\".\n\nIt didn't bother me at first, but gradually it kept happening, but a kind 'aheral living in Oren made me a beautiful dress.\nAt first, Oren had changed me, I even went as far as dying my hair with dyes I found in the Oren shops.\n\nI have stooped so low that I have even *almost* slept with the 'ata Veledin.\n\nAfter our brief time together I realized\nthat I needed to change. \n\nSo I'm back in Haelun'or where I belong, with my kin.\n\nI am not proud of my mistakes and I'm here to find a council member to tell them about my sinful wrongdoings.\nFortunately, the dye was flower based so it washed out easily with a lot of rough scrubbing. \n\nI felt like an entirely new person after I washed that dye from my hair.\nSuch an idiot, I was to have ever tried it at all.\n\nI have sinned and so I am confessing to all now.\n\nI do not wish to be considered a mali'ata, not because they'd look down on me, but because I know that is not who I am.\nMy parents were 'ata. Such disgusting 'aheral, the time I reached 50 I started my adventures to get away from them.\n\nThey were filthy impures and I wanted nothing of them.\n\nI love the 'aheral, but they. . . are not like the rest of us.\nI met some very kind people that changed my mind about the mali'thill. I look up to them, and feel like such a child because of it, but that's the truth.\n\nThank you, Haelun'or for showing me what it means to live.\nI am finally sure that I belong somewhere. \nHere.\n\nI am ready for the punishment of my horrible sins, for I deserve it.\n\nI only hope that I survive a trial if there is one,because I truly wish to be a mali'thill.", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "Haadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=           Conjuration\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\nAh, Conjuration; the rarest Arcane Art known… well, it won’t be rare anytime soon. Of course, once you begin to learn the art, you will be referred to as a “Conjurer”. A conjurer is an individual who access the Void and construct living organisms which\nare fueled wholly by the mana of their creator. Through the depths of the void, a Conjuration user will be able to summon a mighty creatures of placid flowers into reality. Alas, as a conjurer you will be constantly delivering your mana for virtually\nvery second your ersatz summon exists. You will soon come to a realisation that Conjuration uses the most of your mana unlike any other Arcane Science. In order to uphold the existence of your faux creature in reality, you must feed it prescisely a great\nportion of mana to flow within it. As the creature you summon will be downright complex, the process of building it within the Void will be rather tiresome and there is a good chance you may be drained completely of your mana until you reach\nunconsciousness, as that happens, your beast will be removed from the physical realm and be sent back to the Void. Yes, you can decide to desist the flow of mana beforehand, in which case the fauna will vanish to no consequence. Now, for you to construct\nan organism within the Void, you must first have a sharp and great understanding of both the interior and exterior of the living you wish to formulate. This can be achieved by oftenly killing and dissecting the creature you wish to summon. However, it is\nalso best to keep very detailed anatomical diagrams of the beast you wish to conjure. Remember to have note son the animal’s exterior, interior and bone structure if you want to have an accurate understanding of it. In the opaque Void, the fabrics which\ngenerate the entity are summoned bone by bone, layer by layer, muscle by muscle and organ by organ the Conjurer crafts and sculpts their being into an exact copy of their previously existing self. As a result of poor research, the Conjurer may fail at\nthis point, producing a being unlike that of its true and real form will result in an uneven and revolting entity which would certainly turn to a sludge once conjured. After a while of practice, the Conjurer would be able to summon the creature exactly\nhow it was before it was slain and have it formed with sheer stability. As it will behave akin to the life form it represents, it will follow its creator’s commands. As a Conjurer myself, I would highly recommend you begin to study roses, then petite\ninsects until you grow stronger and confident enough to move on to study and conjure anything larger. Think of Conjuration as art. You are the painter and the Void is the frame. What you paint in that frame will need to look beautiful and make sense in\nthe judge’s eyes. Bear in mind that the “judge” is the physical realm. If the judge thinks your work of  art is good, it will be accepted and be brought into reality. However, if it’s horrible and ugly, it will be stamped on and crushed and it will appear\nas an abomination in the mortal plane, you will be smacked in the face for your poor efforts, that smack will tire you. Keep practicing and your artistic skills will improve and the judge will begin and continue to accept your art. Overtime, your frame\nwill expand and leave you open to produce which the judge can view. Be warned though, the larger the harder. And yes, you can fabricate hybrid fauna. I’ll leave that for you to grasp the concept of that alone.\nAuthor: Unknown\nCopied by Guildmaster Haadi Mubdee of the Mages Guild, 1461.", ""),
        StaticBook("Coppied Letter", "-", "*The letter seems recent. The paper is old, but the ink seemed to have dried up not long ago*\nI know that you have been visited by the Order of Youth, what have you been doing to get them to notice you? Surely you are not contesting what he has done, he found it that’s for sure, and you know how his followers become when you question him.\nIblees would be jealous of their rage. You know that humans fear for their short lives, trying to remove hope of extending it will make them mad. I hope you didn’t get hurt by them, the best of health to you, may Aeriel bless your body.\nAs for what you asked me to get, I convinced the town’s people that their death were diseased. You will have the corpses sent to you in a week’s time. I am glad to hear that you have traded those foul potions for the study of anatomy and healing.\nIf you ever require any more wisdom or help in the study, do not be scared to ask me. I have been your friend for many years, and your doctor for far more.\n \nSafe study,\n     Doctor Marrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Cornfield song", "Judas Windsor", "________________________ \n\n        Song: I've been working on the cornfield\n\n-Judas Windsor.\n\n________________________\nI've been working on the cornfield all the live long day.\n\nI've been working on the cornfield just to pass the time away, can't you hear the bell ringing? Rise up so early in the morning.\nCan't you hear the captain shouting Dinah Blow your horn.\n\nChorus:\n\nDinah wont you blow?\n\nDinah Wont you blow\n\nDinah wont your ho-ho-horn. repeat x2\nSomeones with dinah, someones in the kitchen I kno-ow-ow singing Fee Fi Fiddly Aye o, fee fi fiddly aye o. Someones in the kitchen with Dinah!\n\nStrummin on the Ol Banjo...\n\nRepeat top paragraph x3", ""),
        StaticBook("Coven Inspection", "Ularoth", "Assessment of           the Iblees Coven\n\n           Ularoth\nOur trek begins within an abandoned complex carved beneath the outskirts of Alras. Upon our entry into the quaint cavern, we heard distinctly nothing; The dwelling has been long abandoned. Left standing in the strange pit of offal and rock appears to\nbe a heavyset table of lackluster quality. It sounds of splintering wood, its innards eaten away by woodworms and their ilk. The chairs that accompany the furnishing are in just as awful a shape. The thought of a gathering of naive cultists squirming\nuncomfortably in their seats amuses us. Upon the table rests a tattered board that sounds and tastes of driftwood, no doubt fished from a river. Its edges seem caked with a thin grime of taint, once carved intricately in beguiling sigils now rests on the\noutskirts of the plank in unsightly blobs of vile. Letters are etched in the board's surface, scrawled lazily in three strokes of a dull pike, at most. Wedged in a hastily dug pocket of stone lies a shape of wood, cut from the same as the board, with a\nglassen port wedged center-most.\n\nMoving away from the table, We've noticed a hallway-esque expanse to our right, whereupon a mound of soot rests. It smells of bone, the intense heat that surely singed a mound of bodies that once resided where\nthis dust dwells seemed hot enough to dissapate fetid flesh into vapor. The numerous rats that have since taken refuge in this place seem to avoid this mound of dead. We too are vaguely offput by it.\nFurther down the hallway resides nothing but a sturdy end, accompanied by a stoney pillar which bares no intrigue.\n\nResiding in the midst of this place are several chests which reek of rot. Further inspection has rendered the bins\nvastly unintriguing, as only decomposing plantlife dwells within.\n\nThe cavern-like expansive to our left has been bored into thrice, all along the right walls. We may dwell within this place after our inspection is completed. The three hovel-sized\nrooms contain a stark nothing. Further meandering has caused us to come across a single room dug into the left of the wall; our apologies.\n\n\nDeeper in the cavern is a strange chamber, slathered hastily with sigils drawn of offal.\nIts centre seems to hold a forge of strange architecture, with a shallow indent carved in the floor just about a beam of glass. One would best compare this to something of Urukai construction, albeit of rock. The small chamber remains barren apart from\nthe strangness previously mentioned. We shall scribe the glyphs that adorn the walls after the entirety of our assessment.\n\nSo to will we scrawl the sigils drawn into the floor with the same gore found amoungst the 'ritual' chamber.\n-A strange sigil comprised of a circle trapping many a piece of odd geometry is drawn here in a thick, piney sludge. The entirety of the glyph seems to resemble some sort of crucifix turned on its head-\nThe most daunting of the subterranian abode's sigils. Its relative size dwarfs the rest of its siblings. It resides on the leftmost wall of the assumed ritual chamber. It evokes a calm within us; something reassuring.\n-Another glyph is drawn, in the same ichor no less. This one vaguely depicts a conjuring fire, which a primative body lurches over menacingly. Four lines impale the otherwise lackluster rune, adorn at their ends with what appear to be eyes-\nThis dwells the backmost wall of the ritual chamber. Its paint-thick fluid seems to grasp more particulate than most. We believe it to be soot, or fine sand. Its texture is bone dry, and has chipped to our louder inspections.\n-Yet another sigil is scribed in piney ichor, accompanied by occasional streaks of ash. Its relative shape is all but a mystery, wavering this way and that with bizzare connections linking the irredeemably baffling structure together-\nWe're not sure what to make of this, its quite oddly placed. It lies near the central support beam of the cave. We can't stand to hear it much, it prods at us with a sense of unease.\nThe remainder of the scrawlings we've deemed uninteresting. They are far too simple to rival the three we've already found. If someone wishes, you may contact ourselves to delve into a further study of this place.", ""),
        StaticBook("Craftfair Letter", "Siri", "Greetings honoured guest!\n\nI am Siri, Guildmaster of Laureh'lin. The Province of Laureh'lin is interested in hosting a Arts and Craft fair within the foreseeable future, and would like to extend an invitation to you and your people!\nThe fair is scheduled within the next 3 years, probably after a new district has been made. But we are currently gathering interest for the idea, and would like to invite the skilled craftsmen and women of your people to show off in this fair with either\nskills, goods, or just to get to know other craftsman from other regions. \n\nI hope you will respond to this letter.\n\nSincerely, Siri", ""),
        StaticBook("Cragbreac killer", "Martin Greymane", "It started just outside Felsen, there he was, the killer rabbit of Cragbreac, standing atop a stone pillar, when we saw it, we knew it should be cast away into hell, but we didn't know what mess we were getting into. First he went for the ankles.\nThe poor bastards never knew what was coming, the nibbling looked painful, lucky the rabbit didn't leap upon me, for I would of lost the use of my legs, he jumped from tree to tree, victim to victim. When we saw our chance to strike we did,\nI gained enough strength to cast a lightning bolt, another caster did the same, a firebolt was also cast, but none of our magic hit, only the swoop of a mighty warrior, who there name is I forget, but they swung that rabbit into the air like\na head of a dwarf, when the rabbit recovered, it puffed up into a ball of smoke and all that could be heard was laughter in the distance, I know he will be back, im sure of it. I just hope for the sake of Felsen, he doesn't", ""),
        StaticBook("Creepy Tales V2", "[Teen] Mikazuki Mantisuku", "~The Girl in the Mask~\n\nNo one can be sure where she started. One thing was sure, she had long raven colored hair, deep sapphire eyes, a small form, fair skin, and a beautiful mask. The rumors that were spread\ncould never fully tell the story about this young girl who only seemed to appear at night. All they did tell was she was not something to be trusted or desire to see. Only one rumor seemed to be most agreed upon.\nThe story goes that a young girl lived happily in the lap of luxury with her human parents. She was of noble birth and to be wed to one of the princes. She had everything she wanted.\nThere was a masquerade ball made in her honor at her home, everyone was asked to wear masks and she was to see if she could find her \"prince\" among the men that attended.\nThe ball went well and the girl was excited. Still being just a young maiden, she was already prideful. She donned a beautiful royal blue velvet gown and lovely powder blue mask. She entered the room, excited and happy.\nDancing with glee she soon found a taller boy with a dark mask on his face. \"My prince~\" she whispered silkenly to him as she curtsied. Without a word he bowed and the two began to dance. Dizzy and joyous, she announced she found her prince.\nWhen he removed his mask, she was startled to realize it was a serving boy. Terrified, she called her guards and her father had him executed. Months passed and the girl lay in her bed soundly asleep. Her wedding gown near the bed,\nready for the next day's ceremony. A shadow fell across the room and a figure moved closer to the girl. Before she had time to scream he covered her face with the mask the serving boy wore to the ball.\nA scream ripped through the manor as the shadow vanished. Two guards broke into her room and ripped the mask from her face, only to find it had been laced with a powerful poison that ate at flesh. Horrified and fully maimed, they bandaged her face\nand tried to find a healer. Even monks could not reverse the damage that had been done and she was forced to wear a mask to cover her scars. With her fiance leaving her, she was locked away in the manor with only a few things to keep her company.\nOne night, she crept out and stole the dress away that she was to wear to her wedding. Donning the dress, she hung herself in her room, no one aware of her death till the next morning.\nWhen they went to bury her, the mother opened the coffin to find the body gone. Since that day, the young woman had been seen only at night wailing as she wandered.\nThe rumors say, if you were to see her, she would beg you to help her. If you try to remove her mask, you would be found brutally murdered with a pale plain mask on your face. But this is just a horror story meant to scare people at night. Or is it?", ""),
        StaticBook("Crimson Heart.", "[The Loyal] Mordew", "Mordew's Report, First Incident-\nStood watch upon the gates and saw Master Draethar head off into the woods, I followed, keeping myself hidden as I deemed this behaviour suspicious. I remained undetected as he entered a seemingly abandoned barn in the\nmiddle of the woods, From there I heard voices, Notably Draethar's but also some others, I caught drips of a conversation and am assured I heard speak of Necromancy and Betrayal. I returned to the City and reported this information to Medi'ir Avern.\nMordew's report, Second Incident- After some controversy involving a goblin sighting within the city, Lady Avern and myself went to visit the barn, The doors were locked and we had to force our way in. Upon entry we were 'greeted' by two people, One that\nAppeared to look like a wood elf, the second a human. The wood elf was armed but I was wearing my newly forged suit of armour and commanded him to drop his weapon, Lady Avern was also equipped with her staff and magic, they then decided to begin obeying.\nAfter Avern requested them to stand against the back wall I examined the inside of the barn, it was dark, too dark for any real functioning barn, with no ventilation. There was a smell of damp and some obvious moulding of the wooden floorboards. Whilst\nI kept the men against the wall, Lady Avern began to search a cellar entrance to the right hand side of the floor, inside of which she found a hidden switch, though pretended to be ignorant of this information for the time as we had come without the-\ncorrect force to aprehend both men. During her time searching the cellar I questioned the men, they claimed to be \"Hay salesmen\" though they had no field in sight and the barn was not suited for proper storage I can confirm there was a significant amount\nof hay present. When questioning where they got the wheat to make the hay they simply claimed to buy it, though a source for purchase was not given. They also claimed to have the Sohaer's permission to be working on Haelun'or's land, this has yet to be\nconfirmed as the Sohaer could not be found upon our return to the city.\nMordew's report, third incident-\nAfter returning to the city Lady Avern said we would need to gather forces before returning, during this time I went back to the barn alone, hiding in the trees I managed to listen to some further conversations from within\nTwo voices (not those of the 'famers' I should add) seemed to be discussing the \"Fame and fortune\" they would receive for their schemes (unspecified) it seemed one was attempting to recruit the other to their cause as I heard one eventually request to be\njoining whilst the other mentioned a presentation of \"Elf paperwork.\"\nMordew's report, fourth incident-\nA party approached the gate, requesting myself and Avern to follow them for their council in their barn, I recognised the voice of their leader from within, he was the one offering a contract earlier. A dark elf, by\nthe name \"Sonoren\". Him and lady Avern spoke in the garden alone, upon my approach Sonoren hastily asked me to leave, I remained until Avern informed me that he was no threat and that I could leave. I could a brief snippit of the conversation mentioning\nslave armies from Sonoren, this appeared to be a slip of the tongue as he then requested to leave and after some controversy he was allowed to go, leaving by diving from the garden into the lake.\nI inquired with Lady Avern about their discussion afterward\nshe told me that I needn't worry about the barn anymore and that they were no threat to Haelun'or and that Elsohaer and Elmodi'ir were already aware of the situation. When I questioned the necromancy she did not give me a definate answer but I can confirm\nit was not discussed at their meeting, I have doubts of how well informed people are about the necromancy too, though Lady Avern assured me that \"They are no threat to us, especially considering who they are.\" When I asked who exactly they were I was told\n\"It is not needed to be known\" at this my enquires came to an end as it is not my place to question a Medi'ir, only to serve.\nMordew's report, fifth incident-\nAfter speaking with Lady Avern I decided to continue the investigation alone, returning to the barn and listening once more to the conversations within, though I could be mistaken it seems they have increase in numbers\nsince earlier, I could hear a minimum of ten voices if not more from within, this therefore was awkward to report on as there was a lot of sound going on at once. After some time observing I noticed Master Braxus approach the Barn, he came alone with no\nweapons or armour and knocked upon the door, at which point two men (the same that had pretended to be farmers.) approached him and continually asked him to leave the area, caliming it to be 'theirs'. After some time watching Braxus try and explain that\nthe land was under Haelun'or's control one of the men pulled a blade to him and from what I observed he intended to attack. Therefore I then rushed from my hiding position, clad in my armour and with my blade ready, instantly the two backed off, the one\nthat had drawn his sword seemed significantly scared and instantly backed against the barn whilst the other began shouting into the barn that \"Lord Mordew is here!\" I feel as though I may have unintentionally earned myself a bad reputation of killing.\nMaster Braxus seemed thankful for my intervention and proceeded to warn those who emerged from the barn that should he or another citizen of Haelun'or be threatened by them again then they would have me to deal with. Many of them seemed honestly concerned\nby this and stepped away, forming a loose circle around us. Sonoren eventually stepped from the barn, clearly being established as their leader and at the sight of Mine and Braxus' blades suggested that we return to our city and they would return within\ntheir barn without any violence. After some talking Braxus eventually went to leave and as I went to follow Sonoren approached me, asking who my master was, I simply responded \"The Medi'ir\" and he appeared familiar with who I was referncing, he then told\nme that The Medi'ir was a former member of what he called 'The Crimson Hearts' and that I should relay a message for him to contact Sonoren as soon as possible.\nUpon return to the city Master Braxus also mentioned that he wishes to speak with The Medi'ir\nas soon as possible.\nMordew's report, sixth's incident-\nA few hours following the last incident I decided to investigate the seemingly deserted barn, the doors were still damaged from being kicked in by myself and Avern earlier so entry was simple, I made my way to the cellar\nand found the lever Avern was speaking of, it triggered some sort of mechanical passageway and then I was allowed entry into the underground complex I had suspected. The complex at the time of my visit was still under construction, it consisted of three\nfloors, the first consisting a notice board with no relevant information other than \"No magic until I return\" which leads me to assume those practicing there are under Sonoren's strict rule. I decended to the second floor and found two rooms, one was a\nstorage room that I could not access, the other was a bunk/ housing room, at the time of my visit it consisted of 12 beds, with room for four more, I beleive this is the approximate number of 'Crimson Hearts' currently on the island. The bottom floor\nconsisted of many rooms, each seemingly under construction with the acception of what appeared to be a classroom, fit to house at least 20 students, I imagine this is where they pass on lessons in necromancy to the members on the island. I could not find\nmuch else as I heard the door to the barn above me slam shut as someone returned, I fortunately had my soulstone prepared and made my escape before being caught.\nMordew's report, seventh incident- Sonoren and five of his hearts entered the city, requesting to speak in the gardens with the Okarir's present at the time. He again persisted that I was not to be allowed presence at the meeting, I kept watch at the\ngarden's gates and observed their conversation. Sonoren mostly seemed to be informing the Okarir's of his groups intentions to \"Protect Haelun'or if they are in need of aid, in exchange for use of it's land.\" None of the Okarir's protested. After the\nconversation came to a close I approached and brought up the incident with Braxus, Sonoren openly insulted him, calling him a moronic fool and none of the Okarir's present seemed to care much about the assault, one even said that \"It has already been\ndealt with.\" though they had not discussed the incident there or then and from what I am aware Sonoren or his men have received no discipline following the incident, though I am not omnipresent and can not assume such things.\nUpon the Heart's leave I\nInquired with Okarir Suliin'thill about if the hearts were to be trusted, he responded with \"For now.\" and then continued with \"Nothing is permanent, this is a life lesson, Mordew.\" I shall lower my guard against the Crimson hearts for now unless they\napproach armed or with ill seeming intentions. I fear that the Okarir's may be unaware of what I have learned on my scouting efforts though I do not question their judgements and remain loyal to their requests unless the master wishes otherwise.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Arts", "Coltaine Wick", "A sparse collection\nof knowledge on\nNecromancy,\nBlood Magic,\nSoul Puppetry\nNecromancers, fabled\npeople that few know about, few even know what Necromancy is, I shall tell you. Necromancy is a powerful and dangerous form of magic, Its the manipulation of life, it alters the Life Force, the thing all living creatures have.\nThe Necromancer can fuel there magic on there own or anothers Life Force, one could even extend there life slighty with Necromancy by draining others, given it would only add 20 years or so. People have described this draining as a \"Black Mist\".\nThis mist is Life Force and is being pulled from victim into the Necromancer, the source could be a human, or even trees and grass. If enough Necromancy is used in one place it could Taint the surrounding area. An experianced Necromancer can taint whole\nlandscapes. Another skill Necromancers have is cursing individuals.  A curse places taint on the target causing debilitaing physical and mental effects in the duration of the curse. Now in my life, ive been drained before and i can say, it isnt pleasant,\nit weakened me terribly, leaving my weary and exhausted.\nNor are Necromancers a particularly polite group. Id advise avoiding those sorts of people unless you are involved in those groups.\nNext up, Blood Magic\nTo start out no, blood magic does not give you control over blood, you wont be whipping it around or any such silliness. In the highest pinnacle of blood magic you could at most, make blood clots in a persons body. Blood magic is an extremely dangerous\nmagic, it wastes the body and makes the user insane. Blood magic is more of an enhancer, It give one the ability to evoke more and in greater power, but at a terrible cost, it should only be used as a last ditch effort to save your own hide. The art off\nBlood Magic uses the innate power in the blood, be your own or a targets blood, the key is that the flesh must be pierced and bleeding for it to function, I do believe the art requires runes of some sort but I am not sure.\nThink of it this way, lets say you are a pyromancer, a fire evocationist, lets say you wish to evoke a storm of fire yet are too feebly skilled to accomplish it regularly, you would employ blood magic to aid you, so instead of fireballs you get fire storm\nBut again, it is extremely straining on the body and prolonged use leaves the user insane, a raving lunatic. If one has it it should rarly if ever be used for there own safety.\nLastly we come to Soul Puppetry.\nThe little I know of soul puppetry makes me thinks its sort of like voodoo, it links the vivtims soul to a puppet that the soul puppeteer can manipulate and torture. But they can never kill the victim, trying to do so would break the connection.\nThe puppet must of course resemble the victim. Puppets dont need to be made of any speical or magical material, it can be nearly anything. That is the total of my knowledge on that.\nSmall notes.\nThe little I know of frost witchs is that, they are a secretive lot, they often hide amongst the general populace, they eat men. and have ice magic.\nThus I have told all I know\n\n\nYours truly\n    -Coltaine", ""),
        StaticBook("Dasyra's book.", "Archmage Dasyra", "*The books several pages are completely sparse, yet it looks aged.. As you continue flicking through, a single page is found with a rather odd symbol upon it. Examining it, you find an odd sensation overcome your mind..*\nThe feeling within your mind begins to overtake any current sensations, your vision becomes blurred and hearing vague. Instead of your surroundings, your mind is filled with the image of nothing, a small space rotating space that goes against\nyou've seen before.. Your mind becomes torn, the odd construct in your vision appearing to remove your memories, throughts and opinions and laying them out in front of you like an odd puzzle.. It examines them, every tiny little detail within the\nblink of an eye before returning them to you.. This odd feeling lingers with you, constantly upon your thoughts, always there, the image of the black space stained upon your eyes.. Madness has welcomed you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dawson's Journal", "Dawson Bailson", "*Pages before this have been torn out.\nDay 37\n------\n   I can't take this anymore. All of this damn fighting, and still nothing. The Order of Saint Amays was on of the worst decisions I have ever made in my life. With nothing new to experience other than unsensical violence, I am left gasping\nfor something joyous, and rejuvinating. My request though, is out of the question. Without quenching this thirst I find it hard to live my life. If the Order of Saint Amays was made up of honorable men like I believed it was, there would be no need  for\nthis note, but it is necesarry. I am going to do it soon. I shall end it all from this very ceiling.\nDay 38\n------\n   Goodbye cruel world. It had been fun before the damnned Order of Saint Amays, but that has changed everything. With this final entry I end everything. I shall miss you brother Jonathan, but m- (Blood covers the page.)\n(In someone else's handwritting.) Down with the Order. In with Iblees. \n-The Daemon of the Waters", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Clover", "Yden Orvir", "To Clover\n\nA million stars in the sky,\nOne shines brighter I cannot deny,\nA love so precious a love so true,\nA love that comes from me to you.\nThe angels sing when you are near,\nWithin your arms I have nothing to fear,\nYou always know just what to say,\nJust talking to you just makes my day,\nI love you honey with all my heart,\nTogether forever and never to part.\n\nPlease forgive me for my absence, it was beyond my control but every moment I was away I thinking\nof you and reliving memories that we shared, the time I was away from you just showed me how precious you are to me and I do not want to ever loose you again, it appears it is true that you never knew what you had until it is gone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Definition", "Ambros", "The Art of Definition\n\nBy Ambros\nI would live,\ndedicate my entire life\nto defining a single word\nproperly – justly. \nThat word would be:\nmelancholy\nI do have other candidates,\nperhaps I would define another\nstill stranger word: mysterious.\nWhat is mysterious?\nThat which cannot be grasped intellectually.\nThat which is still unknown, unexplained,\nperhaps the truly mysterious is\nthat which can never be explained by thought,\nthat which is intrinsically unknowable.\nHere I am defining a word with other words.\nBut I would not stop there. \nI would access zones of intuition,\na series of instruments predating language,\nlike an amulet that contains an entire cosmology\nor a monolith that served as genesis to historical memory.\nI would anchor my word to other unreliable words,\nvague words that by their very nature would\nserve as examples of the intangibility \nof my definition for mysterious.\nI would, for example, make mysterious \nsynonymous with Life, Happiness, Nirvana, etc...\nect...", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Rose", "Saeed Ibn Malek", "Desert Rose\n-------------------A Poem By Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------\nI dream of rain,\nI dream of gardens in the desert sand,\nI wake in vain,\nI dream of love as time runs through my hand,\nI dream of fire,\nThose dreams are tied to a horse that will never tire,\nAnd in the flames,\nHer shadows play in the shape of a man's desire,\nThis desert rose,Each of her veils, a secret promise,\nThis desert flower,\nNo sweet perfume ever tortured me more than this,\nAnd as she turns,\nThis way she moves in the logic of all my dreams,\nThis fire burns,\nI realize that nothing's as it seems,\nI lift my gaze to empty skies above,\nThis rare perfume is the sweet intoxication of her love,\nI dream of rain,\nI dream of gardens in the desert sand,\nI wake in vain,\nI dream of love as time runs through my hand,\nSweet desert rose,\nEach of her veils, a secret promise,\nThis desert flower,\nNo sweet perfume ever tortured me more than this,\nSweet desert rose,\nThis memory of Peace haunts us all,\nThis desert flower,\nThis rare perfume, is the sweet intoxication of the fall.\n----------------------------\nBy Saeed Ibn Malek\n(I did not make this my self irl <3 thanks for reading)", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary: Slave", "Hileia'elr", "Kivessin got his payback for me getting him banished, I suppose... He kidnapped me, and sold me to an Uruk. Roklah'Braduk, a blacksmith. So far, he's kicked, scarred, and branded me with a big 'B' on my back.\nIt hasn't been too bad so far... By comparison. Although, when Roklah isn't around, the other Uruk throw food at me and make fun of me.\n\nAside from Kivessin being pissed, Kale isn't that happy, either.\nI understand why she's mad, though. I don't think she has a right to be, but... I understand. Kale and Kivessin were an item, so it must pain her to not be able to run the clinic and see him at the same time. I'm not mad at her, though.\nAlthough, Kivessin is going to pay when I escape from this prison of a city... I don't care how far I have to go. He ruined every aspect of my life... My career, my love lift, and my own body.\nOf course, I won't kill him... I can find a punishment even worse than death for good ol' Kivessin. He told me that, \"I'll only make you go through what I did,\" and, \"I hope you've learned your lesson, Hileia.\"\nWhat Kivessin doesn't realize is that I'M the good guy here, HE'S the criminal. He killed a noble, and since he was a guard, I had to tell someone... I was the good citizen, he was the murderer. I swear, he'll suffer once I escape...\n-------------------Today, I was kicked by three other Uruk whilst Roklah was out. I wanted to communicate with them, so I attempted to speak 'Blah.' They didn't appreciate it. I was thrown onto the ground by one of them, the beaten.\nOne kicked me in the eye so hard, I need an eyepatch now... This is why I hate Uruk.\n\nAfter chopping down wood, Roklah took me to the Caliphate to auction me off. Someone tried buying me, but when the bid was too low,\nmy master just dragged me back to the Iron Uzg. Now, I'm sitting here writing, while he makes some sword.\n\n-------------------Kale... Actually visited me. She heard about the auction, and she tried to buy me back.\nI am a bit... in shock. I thought she didn't care about me anymore. She offered my master 100 minas, far more than at the auction. He decided he wanted to keep me though, simply to show me off to, 'The Rex.'\nKale wished to speak to me, but... I don't think I'm quite ready for that, yet.\n\nRecently, I've been picking up on the so called 'Language' called Blah. It's easy to do that if you stay in one place long enough...\n\"Too bad I can't use it, though... A non-Uruk speaking Blah is like... I'm not even sure. It's just disrespectful. It's alright, though. They're disgusting creatures, anyhow. I don't care to speak their language.\n-------------------\nWhilst I was cutting down more trees, Roklah and his crew joined me to get more wood for some project... I dropped the axe on the ground, then ran for the docks. Instantly, I went to the Caliphate.\nRunning away was sure to get me a beating, but I didn't care. I  wanted to visit the Caliphate... The place I hadn't visited in months. \n\nWhen I arrived, Kale was treating a patient in her clinic.\nShe instantly stopped what she was doing to greet me with open arms. Now, she's finishing up in the surgical room, and then she's going to serve us some tea.\nOh wow... That was, uh... Surprising. Not much happened, but Kale told me that she was never a 'Thing' with Kivessin in the first place! It was just to get him out of some arranged marriage... The nerve.\nWhile I am slightly upset that they lied to me about that, I also don't mind... After all, this should mean that Kale won't mind when I cast Kivessin into a living nightmare.\n-------------------I suppose I haven't learned my lesson.\nAfter returning to the Iron Uzg, I got a punch to the forehead. That was it, though. Nothing serious... Although, now I'm in Laureh'lin. And I just lost 60 mina from gambling...\nSome geezer named Lornengoth or something. Green eyes, long white beard, no shirt. Whatever, though. He won it fair and square through gambling with me all night. Lucky him.\n-------------------\nBack in the Iron Uzg... After another week of work, there's some... Tournament happening. Something the Uruk call 'Klomping.' I heard a horn sound while I was on the road, so I came to watch.\nSome people from the Caliphate were coming in to fight, so the Uruk already there needed to warm up... And guess who they used as their training dummy? That's right, the only non-Uruk there. I was just a punching bag for 10 minutes.\nWhen the arena was full of fighters and spectators, the fighting began. So many Uruk were there, but plenty of Valah, Mali, and Kah. One fight after the next, it came down to the final two: The Rex himself, and some guy named Rilkor.\nThe first match was won by the Rex. He beat Rilkor to the ground... I was surprised he was alright to keep on going! Although, in the second round, The Rex took quite a beating. In the final round, Rilkor came out on top.\nNow, he received some sword as his prize, and he's, 'Champion of the Iron Uzg.' I didn't pay too much attention... I don't care much for this type of entertainment.\n-------------------\nLooking through my bag today, while Roklah was busy repairing some tools, I found an old book written by Nienna. It was her dark arts book... I had never read it before, so I decided to give it a read.\nIt's all very fascinating. Puppets bound by darkness, mages rising dead bodies from their graves; However, one particular article caught my eye...\nSoul contractors... The idea of binding your soul to a physical document is quite... scary. Scary, but interesting. And I was wondering- Is this a possible option for revenge on Kivessin?\nNo, revenge is the wrong word... I don't want revenge. I simply want to rid him from this world to protect everyone else from his evil presence. Maybe send him into a deep sleep, where he has the most wonderful dreams.\nEither way, I wouldn't mind sacraficing something of mine to keep him from harming others... If a contract is what it takes, then that's what I'll do. I would just need to actually FIND someone with the ability to make a contract, first...\nHa, hell, I'd do it myself if I had to! Wait, no... That wouldn't work. I would still have to carry out the process myself, even if I did know soul contracting magic. And I really have no way to do that, besides kill him...\nBut who am I kidding? He's an assasin, and I'm a Mali'aheral from Haelun'or that writes romance novels for a living- Well, used to, anyways... But still, becoming a soul contractor... I wonder what that's like for them.\nI bet it's fun for them, but I couldn't imagine skinning someone alive. It must be an awful process that would drive one to insanity. And for something so trivial as a contract? Well, actually, I can see why it'd be important...\n-------------------Do I even have anything else to live for? Those gates are wide open, and I could just run out, but... What would be the point? I suppose I should learn how the world has been changed since I've been gone...\nBut what if it's changed for the worse? Maybe there's nothing left for me out there, but... If there isn't, staying in this hell hole isn't going to solve anything. I just have to run for it, if Roklah comes for my head, so be it.\n-------------------About to enter the Caliphate again... With no clothes. I'm done with this diary. After almost a year of writing, I think it'd be best to leave it as it is. Although, that just means that I can start a new chapter to my life.\n~Hileia'elr.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 3", "Fenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\" Volume One Part Three.\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: Hello once again dear reader! Our story will be taking a slow progression in action, so do be patient with the  frequency of the fighting sequences. Now, onto the story!\nChapter Eight: Look Before You Leap.\nAfter walking along the road for some time, an alluring scent caught my attention. It was coming from within the woods to my right. I decided to investigate and see if I could ask someone if there was a nearby town\nOr if they were willing to part with some food. I followed the scent of cooking food with my nose… It smelled like… fish! Delicious smelling fish at that. My stomach growled at the same time Shamone did \"I smell food kid, were gettin some of that!\" The\nSwath of hair said. “Yeah yeah, I’ll see what I can do with this little bit of money. Hope its enough for at least one fish.” I replied, squinting my eyes and looking through the trees, trying to see any signs of civilization. After walking a little\nFurther in the brush of the forest, I spotted what looked to be a clearing with a log cabin in the center. The area seemed to glow in the dimming afternoon sun. My eyes lit up at the prospect of meeting someone new and possibly getting something to eat.\nHowever, as I entered the clearing, I stepped on a large net and slipped, landing flat on my face. The trap was quick to activate, as the net snapped around me and hoisted me high in the air below a sturdy tree branch. Me and Shamone thrashed against the\nNet, but it was no use. Neither of us had a tool to cut us free. That’s when she burst through the cabin door. She had short, spiky, burnt orange hair, and stunning carrot orange eyes. She bore identical triple clawed scars  on both of her cheeks, and a\nLarge scar going all the way around her neck, just above a leather collar with a golden bell. Her skin was tanned and she wore a sleeveless suit. It had a tiny skirt, but left her legs otherwise unbarred. She wore a utility belt around the skirt, with\nSeveral pouches attached to it. She wore thick golden looking wrist guards that covered her forearms with a leather pad, not covering her fingers, as well as leg guards covered her feet to her toes, and went up to her upper thighs. The most striking\nFeatures about her though, were her strange cat like additions, including high perching chocolate colored cat ears that flicked from time to time, a tail of the same color that looked more sharp than it did fluffy, and long claw like nails on her feet and\nHands. She looked triumphantly at me, caught in what I assume was her net. “Ah ha! Like a mouse in a mousetrap! I knew I would catch a bandit sometime!” She said, briskly walking towards my entrapped self. “Nonono! I’m not a bandit! I-I just smelled food\nAnd wanted some!\" I said, frightened for my life. She just sneered at me “Oh yeah? How are you gonna prove that!” She said, as she reached behind her and… Pulled off her tail? I looked on in confusion, as she snapped the tail once. It straightened out\nInto what looked like a rod of metal with a single bladed edge, looking sharper than that of any steel... How was I gonna get out of this one?\nChapter Nine: Fish And Playfulness.\nI held my hands out through the resistant net meshing, \"Please you gotta believe me! I don't even know if I'm from around here! I don't know anything!\" I said, on the verge of a panic attack as the cat lady stood\nUnderneath me, the tip of her tail sword poking against my stomach. The woman sighed, before jumping up and slashing the netting above, dropping me to the ground. I smacked into the earth, all the air in my lungs being forced out of me from the harsh\nImpact. I gasped for air, closing my eyes and waiting, thinking I was going to be slain by this cat person any second. When I finally opened my eyes hesitantly, I found the cat lady bent over in held in laughter, her tail back where it belonged. She\nStarted to laugh uncontrollably, as I looked at her in suprise. \"Y-you aren't going to kill me?\" I asked meagerly. \"Oh my god! The look on your face! Ahahah, that shit is priceless!\" The woman said, now in a lesser fit of giggles, slowly standing back up\nTo about 5'8\". \"The names Natalia FoRune! Sorry about that little net of mine, tends to catch more people than it does animals. What's your name miss?\" She says, reaching out one of her clawed hands. I took up the hand and pulled myself up, while I\nGrabbed my hat with the other and  tightened  it back on my head \"F-Fuqua... I don't know my last name... But thanks for not killing me.\" I said, as my body unstrung itself from the stressful situation it just went through. \"My pleasure Ms. Fuqua.\"\nNatalie said. My stomach growled even louder than before, as I placed a hand on top of it to try and calm it. \"I don't mean to be rude but um... Would you mind if I have some of your food? I can pay for it of cou-\" I said, before Natalie cut me off.\n\"Ep ep! That's absolutely fine. You can come join the family for dinner! I'll bet they can't wait to see what the cat dragged in this time!\" She says, laughing joyfully at her terrible cat joke, letting go of my hand and heading towards the cabin,\nMotioning for me to follow. \"Well, go on kid! Free food!\" Shamone said, urging me on hungrily. I bopped my hat, startling the parasite. \"Oh be quiet you!\" I said jokingly to Shamone, before following Natalia. The air behind her smelled of... fish and\nPlayfulness... If that can even have a smell.\nChapter Ten: Meeting The Parents\nNadalie threw open the front door of the cabin, \"I'm back!\" She said in a sing song voice. I followed behind slowly, peeking my head through the door. There was a large table, chock full of food, with the main course\nbeing fish and rice. I licked my lips in anticipation of a meal, while Shamone nearly coated my hair in a layer of drool. There were two people sitting at the table, one male human, and one female kharajyr. The female had the same burnt orange hair as\nNatalie. I waved shyly at the pair \"Well who's this cute thing you dragged in?\" The kharajyr asked with a giggle. \"This is Fuqua! She fell into one of my hunting traps so I decided to let her eat with us! Hope that ain't too much of an inconvenience!\"\nNatalie said loudly, going to promptly take a seat, patting an empty one next to her. \"I'm Sixis FoRune, and this is my husband, Roger FoRune, make yourself at home Fuqua!\" Said the kharajyr, gesturing to the man to signify his name. I was more or less\nTransfixed on the swishing of Natalie’s tail than focused on making my way to my seat or replying. So, unsurprisingly, I tripped and stumbled over my own two feet and barely caught myself. I glowed with embarrassment, I shuffled into the chair next to\nNatalie \"So... How does your family eat?\" I asked politely. \"Dig in!\" She said, not even using the fork next to her and snatching up a whole fish, then chomping into it with fervor. Her mother did the same, but Roger picked up his fork and ate with a more\npreserved manner. I decided I was to hungry for eating normally, and grabbed up an entire loaf of uncut bread, tearing into it hungrily, before reaching out with my left hand to grab one of the grilled salmon, biting off large chunks of delicious fish. I\nKept eating like this for a while, alternating between the meager varieties of foods. After eating my fill of food (And Shamones) I leaned back in my chair. The rest of the family at the table stared at me, as I looked around slightly put off by this.\nThen Roger started to applaud, the others joining in quickly. I looked around at them, very confused. \"Uh... Why are you guys clapping?\" I asked with a suspicious look on my face. Natalie stood up, giving me a standing ovation, sticking her fingers in her\nMouth and whistling loudly, while Sixis laughed. Richard was able to explain to me \"You ate a third of the food!\"  He said in a smooth voice, a grin on his face. I looked down at the table, and discovered the lane of food in front of me was cleared. My\nFace grew very flustered, as I apologized in rapid fire succession. Natalie just slapped me on the back laughing \"That was awesome! I haven't been out eatin in a long time! Well played Ms. Fuqua.\" She said, her tail swishing happily. I breathed a\nSigh of relief and smiled. It looked like the day was about to go from worse, to ok for me... Maybe tonight wouldn't be so bad.\n===================End Of Part Three\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nParasites--->\nParasites Explained: Parasites are strange creatures, pre dating back to before the beginnings of all the races. They once posed a major threat to the minor gatherings of people, but now, being surrounded by people in major cities, have decided to change\nTactics... At least most of them have. They have now adopted to leaching off sentient beings for nutrients, while maintaining their own powers. These powers are partially transferred to the host, giving them superpowers and abilities, whether they were\nWanted or not. Attempting to follow the example of natural parasites, people created synthetic parasites, although, they were not at all ethical in any way possible. The host controlling synthetic parasites often were mutilated in order to control them,\nand more often than not, end up holding more than on parasite in their body, which leads to soul corruption. Soul corruption occurs when multiple parasites are taking from the body. They begin to leach at the persons soul, instead of the hosts food,\nLeading to mental instability and insanity. Synthetics are able to be detached from the body, while most natural parasites cannot.\nCurrent Parasites In Novel: Shamone; An unruly mop of black hair, residing on the back of Fuqua's head. His rude attitude and composure usually annoys his host. He is one of the most powerful parasites in brute strength.\nFishtail: Manifesting in Kharajyr's only, has taken a special exception to Natalie, as she is half human, half Kharajyr. Her mixed blood had a strange effect on the parasite, giving her near immortality in the way of undying flesh. Natalie still ages and\nHas shown no negative effects to the parasites presence. Fishtail himself is unable to speak. He takes the form of Natalies ears and tail, infusing himself into her at a young age. Her orange fur in those areas had turned to a shiny brown.\nHis own ability is to be able to sharpen and stiffen, depending on the circumstance. Fishtail may also be detached by the tail only, functioning as a sword at that point. He does not give his host physical buffs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid History", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n   of the Druids\n\n      by N. Evitan\nLong ago, two factions of mages fought each other to the bloody end. Good, evil, the sides mattered not, their battle devastated whole cities and forests. At this, the peak of the battle, the first dream came to a young elven girl. She began gathering\nothers around her, teaching the Druidic ways. The first druids were born from the humble beginning. Like a great wave, the young order swept across the land and surrounded the two guilds. The druids destroyed them, turning them all to mere rodents and\nanimals of the forest. The druids went on to preserve the land for a millennia afterwards.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "Aerxuis", "Druidology—What is a Druid \nby Druid Respiren\ntranscribed by Elorna Avern\nDruids are the drui, the dryw, the druwid. Nature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n For those that know the oak, the troew is both the tree and the truth. Mysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning\nmaster of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender, of unspoiled Nature. The Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements. All druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos\nThis book was originally found in the Druid's Grove in Elandriel, in Asulon. It was brought over and transcribed by Elorna Avern.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunes Of Time", "Saeed Ibn Malek", "The Dunes Of Time\n------------------- A poem By Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------Thru the sands I walk, the dunes always the same yet always different\nMy heart seeks but always turns to the gust of sand that sprays my face and wounding my e\nI yearn for the warmth of one I could trust upon my cheek Yet the sun Burns me when the thought arises\nLost I am in thoughts that burn my every being! Tell me, is there a end of this sorrow?\nWill the sky of mine give me a cloud of rain to wash my grief? \nor am I to drift deeper into the sands of sorrow becoming lost to my own desolation!\nTell me! why have the thoughts of happiness hurt me!\nTell me! When will you utter a word and then leave me to my own destruction!\noh why does my mind persecute my heart's yearn and turn everything to the sand that loses me to time!\nTell me...Will I be lost in the dunes of time never to be rescued\n--------------------------------------\nBy Saeed Ibn Malek\n  (Ibraheemc2000)", ""),
        StaticBook("Dungeons & Drake", "Zeliek", "Dungeons and Drakes Handbook.   \n\n        Modifers\n\nStr - Applies to Melee attacks, Dmg rolls, Climb, jump and swim check. Other Str checks (Breaking down doors)\nDex - Applies to range attack, Your Armor check, Reflex saving, Dex skills.\n\nCon - Applies to leveling hp, Fortidute saving, Concentrating\n\nInt - Skill points each level, Int skills.\nWis - Will saving, Will skills.\n\nCha - Cha skills, Influencing others, Clerics and paladins for undead.\nCombat\n\nAttack roll - Roll d20 and add attack bonus. 20 means crit, 1 means fail.\n\nAttack bonus - Melee attack bonus is Base attk - Str mod and Size mod.\n\nRange - Base, Dex, size and range pen\nDmg - When attack hits, roll weapon dmg and add str mod or dex mod for range\n\nAc - What you need to roll to hit, always over 10. Ac is equal to 10 - armor bonus - shield bonus and Dex mod and Size mod.\n\nTouch attack - Over 10 to hit.\nHp - When -1 hp you can't move and have a 10% chance to get back up. -10 hp you die.\n\nIntaitive - Roll d20 to determine turn order and add Dex mod.\n\nFlat footed - Before Intaitive takes place you are flat footed and loose Dex mod to\nYour Ac. This does not apply to rouges or barbarins.\n\nSurprise - If not aware or sneaked up on you are Surprised. Losing your Ac and taking a hit.\n\nAttacks of opertunity - If an enemy is attacking someone else a player can attack -\nThem back for free. yet only once per round.\n\nSpells - Spells take one full turn to charge and cast, they must roll for concentration and then for Ac and hitting.\nTreasure - Monster treasure is lvl 1 - 300gp lvl2 - 600 gp\n\nlvl3 - 900 gp", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarf Babies", "Aerxuis", "Where Do Dwarven Babies Come From?\n\nWritten By: Unknown\nCopied By: Aerx\n\n17th of Amber Cold, 1473\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nwould look like. IIIIUUUUU, it sounds. And hairy, very very hairy.\nNormal babies come when a man and a woman mate, and after pregnancy a baby is born. Well, if you notice, there are almost no woman Dwarves, but I will state why this is\nfurther in. The true ways are far more disgusting and frightening than mating can ever be, it is a mixture or ale and hair.\nDeep inside the mountains of the Dwarven towns, deep underground, are special and greatly guarded rooms. It\nis in these hidden rooms that the baby Dwarves are born. I was quite lucky that I found such a room when the guards were fully drunk and had knocked each other out. So I entered the room and by the creator! It smelled worse than the drunks just\noutside!\nIn a room which seemed filled with puke and ale, there were chunks of what looked like hair. Some of the hair like chunks were even moving. At that time I heard talking just outside the room, and in fear of being discovered, hid\nmyself behind a rock. A Dwarf came in completely drunk and with a knife in his hand.\n“By Yakemar, ay s’all ‘ave a son!”, he shouted before he cut part of his beard.\nI watched stunned as this happened, I could never believe a\nDwarf had cut his own beard, but soon I would know why the Dwarves treasure their beards so much. Releasing the knife he fell on his knees and coddled the beard near his chest.\n“Ya will be named Grikot.”, he said, and that is when it\ncame to me, all those other hair chunks, were in fact part of the beards of other Dwarves.\nThe Dwarf placed the beard chunk down, and picking a bottle, tilted ale over the beard before leaving. So you see, dear readers, the Dwarves\ntreasure their beard because it is from it that their children will be born from. So where do the small amount of female Dwarves come from? As I walked out I realized that one of the chunks was very small, and that the baby could be seen. A female\nDwarf is born when a Dwarf, being far too drunk, doesn’t cut enough of his beard, and such, the Dwarf is born beardless, becoming this way, a woman.\nNow, onto the types of Dwarves, as you should know, the are cave Dwarves, mountain Dwarves\nand mountain Dwarves. After discovering such intriguing ways of conceiving a child, I searched further and found out the reasons. Cave Dwarves are the ones where the room in inside a deep care. Mountain Dwarves, the cave is dug\ninside a mountain but it does not go very deep. Both of these type of Dwarves, as they were born inside a room by willing drunkenness. Forest Dwarves are born on the outside, from which when the drunkeness is so great, they couldn't find the room. That is\nthe reason Forest Dwarves are looked down upon by the others, they were not born in the rooms for the beard to be placed.\n\nI hope this text has helped the reader to understand the hairy way of Dwarf birth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edict-Holofernes", "Theran", "Imperial-Pontifical Edict of Holofernes 1544\n13th of Horen's Welcome\n\nIn light of recent controversy, regarding the conflicts between secular (State) knights and religious (Church) knights\nover Gentry-Rights. John 'the Lesser' and His Holiness, Lucien III have convened in the pontifical keep of Holofernes. After lengthy discussion, the following edict is instituted in both the Pontifical States and the Imperial State. Let known to\nthe realm of God, of Horen that:\n¬†\nKnights of the State are the sworn blades of the Holy Orenian Empire, as well as its Knightly Estate (the Order of the Red Dragon), in this their vows are granted by the Emperor's authority.\nKnights of the Church are protectors of the Faith, sworn to serve God and his Church, in this their vows and rights are granted by the Vicar of God's authority.\nThe practice, originating in ancient tradition, known as Damehood is\nrevised and defined in both the Pontifical and Imperial States.\nTo achieve the status of gentry in either the Church or State, one must be male.\nA Dame is defined as an exceptional warrior of the female gender, however this is an honorary title only\nreserved for the rarest of occasions and grants no rights above the individual‚Äôs class\nKnights of the Church will require a writ from the Imperial Estate in order to perform their knightly duties within the borders of the State.\nKnights of the State will require a writ from the Clerical Estate in order to perform their knightly duties within the borders of the Pontifical States.\nKnights of the State are granted, with their vows, the rank of gentry and its rights within the\nHoly Orenian Empire.\nSee: Ser Rhys Roke, Ser Oscar Lancefeld, etc, etc.\nKnights of the Church may hold titles of nobility in the Holy Orenian Empire, if possessing land and a title within the State.\nSee: Prince Charles Horen, Duke\nStephen Sarkozic, etc, etc.\nAny Knight of the State that claims the rights of a Church Knight, as well as enacting his knightly duties within the Pontifical States, shall be put under trial of the Church if not expressed consent from the\nClerical Estate.\nLikewise, any Knight of the Church that claims the rights of a State Knight, as well as enacting his knightly duties within the Imperial State, shall be put under trial of the State if not expressed consent from the Imperial\nEstate.\nExceptions to the points V, IV, VII, and VIII include men with the title of Knight derived from both the Imperial and Clerical Estate.\n¬†\nJohn ‘the Lesser’ Jrent, Grand Knight\n¬†\nHoly Ser Charles Francis, Imperial Prince\n¬†\nLucien III, Vicar of God", ""),
        StaticBook("Elemental Evo:", "Enedor Pastly", "Elemental Evocation\n___________________\n\nElemental Evocation is the art of drawing a temporary form of an element from the void using mana. This sounds simple however it is much harder to do in practice. This is because you cannot actually\npull an element from the void, you actually pull a substance that mimics the properties of a chosen element. This means when learning magic, one must study their element in order to understand how it works. \nIt is worth noting that evocationists have\nNO power over existing elements.\n\nThe Void\n___________________\n\nThe void is discribed as a dark, eternal plane of nothingness.\nWe find 'nothing' very hard to imagine, therefore the first steps to learning any\narcane magic is to meditate in order to try and understand the void.\n\nIt is believed that the creator pulled everything into existence from the void and therefore it is possible for us to use some of the void's energy\nto cause changes to the world around us.\n\nMana\n___________________\n\nMana is like an invisible liquid. It flows around the world and exists in all living things, including us.\n\nMages use mana to draw their spells from\nthe void.\n\nThe term 'Mana Pool is used to describe how much mana an individual has. Your mana pool determines the strength and duration of spells that a mage can cast. The more experienced a mage is, the better they can manipulate mana.\nTypes of Elemental \nEvocation\n___________________\n\nEach evocable element is treated as a subtype of magic as each element has specific properties that have to be studied before one can perform the magic.\nFire Evocation\n___________________\n\nFire Evocation is perhaps the most widly performed  evocation as it has many uses. One can create fireballs that can be used in combat or simply create a heat or light source for traveling.\nFire evocation is said to be one of the easiest elements to evoke but one of the hardest to control.\nEarth Evocation\n___________________\n\nEarth evocation, like fire evocation has many uses aside from combat. The art of summoning rocks and minerals found in the earth is quite useful defensive and brute force combat although the art of\ncreating and using materials found in the eath has many more uses.\n\nEarth is a harder element to evoke  as it is more solid then, for example, water.\nWater evocation\n___________________\n\nWater is a very diverse element. Water can be found as liquid, solid and gas, all of which can be evoked. \nIce is normally used in combat.\nWater can be used for more day to day tasks like cleaning.\nSteam isn't evoked much as it has little use and is hard to learn.\n\nWater evocationists also have control over the temprature of their water.\nAir Evocation\n___________________\n\nAir evocation is certainly one of the least used evocations. It generally has less uses then the other evocations. Air evocation can be used for defensive combat as one can use it to push back enemies\nand even block some magical attacks.\n\nAir can also be used for more simpler tasks such as cleaning and cooling oneself down with a breeze. Air evocation is hard to study as the element is invisible to our eyes. Instead a mage must feel it to learn\nhow it works.\n\nElectrial Evocation\n___________________\n\nElectrial Evocation is one of the most powerful evocable elements however it is very hard to control and consumes a lot of energy. \nCommonly Electrial evocationists create\nbolts of electricity to combat their enemies though they have to be careful because just like electricity, the element is easily attracted to metal.\n\nIt also takes longer to summon electricity then the other elements because it uses more energy and\nmore mana then, for example, a small ball of water.\n\nDangers/side effects of elemental evocation.\n___________________\n\nThe side effects of Elemental Evocation are similar to other arcane magics and should certainly be looked into before\ndeciding to learn the magic.\n\nSide effects include:\n\n-Decreased life span.\n\n-Becoming physically weaker and frail. (This is why many mages use staffs)\n-On some occasions mages have been driven mad by the lust\nfor power.\n\nMost of these problems are caused by the fact that magic isn't a natural task for our bodies to carry out and therefore it damages us.\nLearning magic\n___________________\n\nIf you decide you want to learn the art of evocation, the best way to go about this would be to find a teacher. This is a hard and lengthy process that can take many years, however, the way you do this is up\nto you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elinor's Trial", "Grand Druid Verden", "Travel to the three groves and inquire about the life and personalities of the Druids. Ask about their totem, why it's special to them, and how they serve Nature and the Aspects. Be kind, courteous, and friendly; this is your future family after all.\nThe Malinor circle sits comfortably at the back of the city. Just look for the absurdly large tree. The Wayward circle sits outside Rosewyn Hollow, outside former Salvus. It's very secluded, so you might want to ask for directions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elle", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHD Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Elle\n\nAge: 147\n\nRace: Half wood elf, half high elf\n\nGender: Female\nCondition/Injury: There were several fractures and protrusions throughout one of her legs.\n\nTreatment Plan: The bones in her femur and tibia have been reset and her leg has been attached to a couple splints.\nDoctor Who Treated the Patient: Doctor Daniel Ward\n\nDate: 18th of Sun's Smile, 1542\n~Doctor Daniel Ward's Signature Appears Here~\n\n\nDoctor Daniel Ward", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons V", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "New Elven Lessons:\n      Volume 5\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIn elven in order to denote affiliation the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and\nmeans in such a case 'spirit'. This also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaean'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\". \n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in\nword 'evareh' . In elven it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh - operative sing.\n-erih - operative pl. (-arih if the verb ends in -ar)", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "Lefkos Glowsbane", "Efficiency:\nEfficiency is one of the quickest and easiest of all of the enchantments to make. The purpose of this is to make any desired tool do its job faster. Using it, you may find that your pickaxe digs through stone like a knife through butter, or an\naxe may fell a tree in one or two swings. Even though it may be a cheap enchantment, it remains one of the most well known and used.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                ----x----                ---x-x---                ----x----\nUnbreaking:\nThis would probably be the second most used enchant, its purpose rather simple and self explanatory. I will review it anyway. Unbreaking is meant to make your tools harder and stronger. Tougher to break. Using it, you may notice that tools\nthat used to break after you use them for a while may still be functional. Its another easy enchantment that wouldnt cost to much to purchase.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                -x-x-x-x-                --x---x--                -x-x-x-x-\nSharpness:\nThis is a rather difficult enchantment, much to hard for a novice to make, and a rather expensive one as well. With this enchantment, you may find that your swords cut through bodys easier, making your opponents fall before your blade.\nThose that seek out an enchanter for this enchantment are normally guards, or people about to go to war.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        --x------                xxxxxxxx-                xxxxxxxxx                --x------\nPower:\nAn enchantment similar to sharpness, but for a different item. Power is made for bows, and when using it, you may find arrows you shoot from your bow hitting harder, enough to crack stone and injure your opponent more then a normal arrow. Only\nProffesional marksmen and archers will seak out this enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        xx----x--                --xxxxxx-                --xxxxxxx                xx----x--\nFire Aspect:\nOne of the oldest and harder enchantments to master. Many seek this enchantment on their blades for its usefullness. It is a must have for armies and a hard level enchantment. Adventurers and high ranking officers may seek out an enchanter\ncapable of this for their army. Fire aspect gives your blade an arcane power that, upon cutting any living creature, will set them aflame. Its thought of as a brutal but useful enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -xxxxxxx-\nFlame:\nVery similar to Fire Aspect, Flame is another hard level enchantment. It lets your arrows catch fire, and burn whatever they hit.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        x--x--x-x                -xxxx-x-x                x--x--x-x                ------xxx\nKnockback:\nOne of the best enchantments in my opinion, knockback is sure to prove useful to anyone, no matter who they are fighting. This enchantment, rather then strengthening the actual blade, strengthens the arm holding the blade.\nIt is called \"Knockback\" because at that point, if you hit someone with your arm at full force, you possess the strength to send them flying back. Combine this with Fire aspect and you can shoot little fireballs called 'your opponent.'\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xx-----                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xx-----\nProtection:\nOne of the less common used enchantments, but more useful. Protection was made to make your armor harder, so an arrow that would once pierce your heart wouldnt even reach it. The only reason it isnt commonly used is because not many\npeople have the time to wait for their armor to be enchanted.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                ---xxx---\nFeather falling:\nA rarely used enchant. Infact, not a single person has asked me for it. I will put it here anyways. Feather falling increases the strength of your feet in terms of impact for the ground. Normally if you would barely survive after a 10\nmeter drop, you would be fine for this handy enchantment. Most people under value this enchantment, until they slip and fall!\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         -----xx--                ----xxx--                ----xx---                ---x-----", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "[Ivae'Fenn Guard] Lady Nessa Anarion", "((I'm a tad bit too lazy to actually write anything in here, but this is a link to the \"book\" just type it in))\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/oz9bvn8\n\nOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO", ""),
        StaticBook("Entities that-..", "Elindor", "Entities Within Our Realm Of Existence No Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\n            §sOR\n\nVoid Translocation\n~1~ Introduction\n~2~ Study\n~3~ Sensory Overhaul\n~4~ Destruction\n~5~ Re-Creation\nIt does not take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, within and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers\n-whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no 'thing' pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creator to pull real matter from The Void.\nBut what if a 'thing'\n-be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible-\nalready existed? Then the connectino to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the 'thing' is not created, but simply  IS\nSTUDY\nTake within your hands something that exists. Any kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing an \"entity\".\nBegin your examination in the simplest of interests: Form.\nWhat size is it?\nWhat's it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n\nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily\ninclined towards this type of thinking. You cannot be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity's existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\nSensory Overhaul\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculatable values and perceiving the entity's magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective with the aid of magic, the quantity\nof information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a realm in which is not a single thing but the potential for all things. And\nthereby all things that exisst are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practice and isn't really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not. Certainly with practice comes the\nstrengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to 'feel' a rosebush from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid down, when you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you must measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so\nthat the entity is no longer isolated in this world but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones' self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more 'alive' an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana.\nAnything that has a soul is independantly existing within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist\nsomewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of glass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more 'alive' it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\nNo Longer Existing\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existance it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangible just stops and is\nno more.\nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independantly of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its divine creation re-instated, and therefore able to return to the nothing from which it came.\nWithin The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something for that fleeting moment. But without being birthed\ninto existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The Void that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the potential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that\nkeeps it sacredly linked to once again become what The Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become crude clay but remains a teapot).\nTo Return Again\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only thing that\nmaintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independant existence outside of The Void is made (i.e redoing Creator's work) will assign the potential with its destined form.\nAnd the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood job, you meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Evangelization", "Father Cedrik", "A Thesis on Charitable Evangelization, penned by Cedrik Engel, eternal servant of the Holy Father.\n\nIn nomine Patris.\n\nA man fed by another is beholden to him that provides food. Such is hardly deniable, even in the sense that a man who tends fields that\nbelong to another is beholden to him who owns the land; for land brings forth food with the labor of the tenant, and thus the tenant is fed by the landlord. This is the manner in which our world is governed. This feudal government over which our ever\nmerciful and most blessed GOD presides provides for a system that encourages loyalty and promotes a mutual understanding of responsibility. For without such system the Holy Orenian Empire would utterly crumble upon its weak foundation, and the Church of\nthe Most High Father would be left stranded upon the harsh landscapes of this Plane. Thus, the importance of the general necessity of sustenance is realized.\n\nUpon this revelation, the Church may begin to develop a plan in which the scattered masses of\nthe Pagan world shall be brought forth into the eternal light of our Father, blessed be His Divine Providence. For from the ashes of this broken world of dismal heathens and faltering believers, the Church may yet arise anew, bearing the Holy Might of\nGOD upon the mob of the proletariat, and elevate them to a higher standing, one of communion with His Divine Mercy.\n\nTherefore I beg the Church, I beseech it, to take up its Holy Standard and, in addition to the multitude of righteous practices it\ncurrently exercises, wield the almighty weapon of Charity, and spread His Love to all corners of this Earth, and perhaps the Pagan may begin to realize the falsity of his idolatrous gods, and turn to the liberating light of the Holy Father. Thus I pray\nunto Him, that he may guide the Church with His Mighty Hand and evangelize this crippled land and the whole world may cry \"Glory!\" unto the Heavens.\n\nIn nomine Patris, Amen.\n\nDeus Magnus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eveangeline", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Evelangeline\n\nAge: 86\n\nRace: \"Mali'igne\"\n\nGender: Female\nCondition/Injury: Was playing with fire, suffered a burn.\n\nTreatment Plan: Burn cream was applied to the wound.\n\nDoctor who treated the patient: Head Doctor Kale\nCost: Two mina\n\nDate: 7th of Sun's Smile, 1522\n\nEnd result: Patient left fully healed. Acted like a bitch.\n*Doctor Kale's signature would be here*\n\n~ Doctor Kale", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation Basics", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n                                                                                                  The Basics\n             Of                       Evocation\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n==================\nIn order for sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as they must know how fire feels to touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\nEvocation is often quite physically and mentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The large the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast it. And just as any other magical branch of the\nArcane tree, the mage must be capable of envisioning where he is casting his spell, and at what - that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball\nbehind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of water to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight. Despite the seemingly passive nature\nthat any one mage may seem to possess, they however remain filthy abominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child-\nfor all who walk upon God's blessed earth.\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation: Basic", "SerahLove", "In order for Sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself.\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as he must know how fire feels to the touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\n\nEvocation is often quite physically an\nmentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The larger the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast the spell. And just as any other magical branch of the arcane tree, the mage must be\ncapable of envisioning where he is casting, and at what- that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball behind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of\nwater to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight.\n\nDespite the seemingly passive nature that any one mage may seem to possess,\nhowever remain filthy adominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be promptly taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child- for all who walk upon God's blessed\nearth.\n\n\n    The Basics of Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n              - Arthur Versluis\n\n   Revisions by E.S. and A.F.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy's/Pixies", "kido122", "On Fairy's and Pixies\n     The Difference\n\n       By Sam King\nFairy's:\n\n To start we shall discuss the better known of the two, Fairy's, or sprites as they are also called. Fairy's are described as no taller and no smaller then 1 inch in height, with a wingpspand of 1 -1/2 inches. Often said to\nbe of fair skin, glowing a dom yellow and often mistaking as a firefly. They are said to dress in leaves of varieing color and design. What is most odd is that they are said to all be female, never has their been told of a male fairy, so how or if they\nhave children is unkown. Now to move on, fairy's are often very, very kind, and are seen as bringers of good luck, a good omen if you will. Keeping places neat and tidy, finding \"Missing\" things and returning them, as well as allow small sparks of\ninspiration, like small, mini, muses(Discused in another book). Fairy's are said to hail from \"Fairy Rings\", circles of varieing mushrooms, in varieing sizes. It is said that when one steps into a fairy ring, one can see the fairy's \"world\", what that is,\nis unkown, This is also were fairy's become \"mean\", as ounce one steps into a \"fairy ring\", one cannot leave it on their own accord. They will remain standing in the ring, in a odd daze, until one either dies of age, thirst, or starvation, or if someone\ncomes and breaks the \"fairy ring\", which is less then likely as they are said to be only found in the most remote parts of the forests. It is good to note, that not all circles of mushrooms are \"Fairy Rings\", as people often plant muchrooms in this way to\none encourage fairy's to come to that area, as it is said that they often fall to this trickery, thinking that it is their actual \"fairy ring\", and two to keep the legends of fairy's living. (Turn the page for Pixies)\nPixies:\n\n Pixies, often confused as fairy's, are very similar to fairy's. They are of equal size and wingspand, fair skin and glow as well, though in a more blue tint. The only real differnce in appearence is the wear dead leaves\nunlike fairy's, who wear fresh leaves. Pixies are here on out, quite the opposite of fairy's, as they are very troublesome. They often enjoy \"borrowing\" anything and everything, often the blame for anything lost. Pixies also enjoying \"stealing\"\ninspiration from others, for themselves. Pixies are said to be both male and female, and where they hail from is unknow and only seem to show up when someone, some where, is in a bad mood, so it is safe to assume they are always present.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "Thurak", "When the murders and attacks on the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and who should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind – many claimed it was the work of the surfacers,\nothers believed that such things were only possible by those living within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living Mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menocress; behind these stragglers\nto return the horror unfolded, each path and passage that journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their\ntaint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her Yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became\nquickly enraged, spitting in the faces of the priestess’ whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged; the devout and the rebels. Beneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding\ndamnation of the sun’s light, the Caverns of Menocress’ streets were littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded – The once marvelled city now rots with death and destruction… crumbling under the civil war. Bathed in the Life\nBlood of their kith and kin, the rebellion breached the Yathrins’ sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble\nborn and their ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and Mori alike stand in the un-ease union against the threat of tait to its own city – this seeded by those\nturned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\n~Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak’Braduk, 14th of the First Seed 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("Felsen Times ED1", "The Orenian Printing Company", "The Felsen Times\n\nArthur Roswell - The man behind the title\n\nOn the 1st of the Grand Harvest, 1543, I was unfortunate enough to arrange a meeting with the Duke of Istria, Mighty Lord Roswell. He was dressed in his formal garments,  the poor\n§ § quality linen, most likely assembled within one of his various child labour factories, his poorly crafted golden embroidery being a reflection of his poorly crafted attitude towards life.\n\nFirstly, what is Roswell? A fungal disease one may find\ngrowing upon one’s foot? A type of hair cream? Yes, and much more.\n\nHe perched upon his stool like a constipated gentleman would do to the base of his privy. The first thing that struck me was his large ego, much larger than his four man levy.\nMuch to my dismay the phrase “Greetings, Mr Roswell.” was inadequate and did not meet his ever so pompous standards. I was corrected immediately, oh, what a fool that I am, for this is not the way one should address a mighty and powerful Duke.\nRoswell, is famed throughout Oren, for his unfaulted Governance of the Duchy of Istria. He has surely done the late Titus de Sola proud, turning Titus’ 40,000 man force  to a band of 40 psychedelic Elves with red eyes, lead by the much respected Jentos\nthe Great. \n\nArthur of the lesser House Roswell maintained his glorious reign by removing his brethren within his Duchy. House Falkenrath, a former Istrian family that had an Intelligence Quotient greater than that of a raw potato in a muddy puddle,\nwere forced out of power by His Grace, Mr Roswell. Mr Arthur Roswell would be incapable of leading a cabbage plantation, let alone one of the major provinces within our great Empire. His town smells of damp, the streets are littered with faeces\nand the inhabitants of the Roswellian stable would likely make more fitting rulers, assuming it was indeed inhabited in the first place.\n\n“A shower a day keep the Roswell away.” - Godfrey IV\nPablo’s Single’s Section\n\n“Dear Pablo, I, the Duke of Istria am having an intimate with one of my paige boys, Jentos Blackwood. I do not know how to tell my husband or how my family will react, especially since Jentos is infected with various\ndiseases\"-Anonymous\n\nDear Anonymous, I would suggest going to see the High Pontiff, to confess your sins. Sexual promiscuity and immorality have plagued our lands, as is so evident from your testimony. I hope that the Creator leads you from your dark\nand into his light\n\n§§[Insert Your Add Here]\nBreaking News\n\nAn Orenian Defeat: 12th of the Grandharvest 1543:\n\nThis week, a great battle ravaged at the Dwarven stronghold of Kal’ordholm. Unfortunately, the Dwarven forces repelled Imperial advances and\nmaintained control over their keep. The Duchy of Istria was a large let down for the Empire, rallying only 4 men, though, what can one expect from a man who likes the smell of his own urine? After a long and hardy battle, hours of siege bombardment and\nslow advances from the Imperial forces, Oren were forced back.\nFinance & Stocks\n\nIstrian Property Development: -23% MKT CPT (1350 Minas)\n\nNorth Orenian Company: -5% MKT CPT (2043 Minas)\n\nWycome Trading company: +1.6% MKT CPT (4320 Minas)\nCourlandic Trading Company: +32% MKT CPT (4533 Minas)\n\nDrusco Property Development: +41% MKT CPT (4300 Minas)\n\nOrenian Publishing Company: +63% MKT CPT (2400 Minas)\nAbout The Publishers\n\nThe Orenian Publishing Company was formed on the 12th of the Grandharvest 1543, by Otto von Habsburg.\n\nThe Company takes inspiration from the old Petrus Printing Press, owned by Jacob Chapel, in the\ntimes of Tuvya Carrion. Dedicated to bringing the citizens of Felsen and Oren fresh news, which they deserve.\nThe company headquarters is found at 2 Newport Boulevard. Vacancies are currently open, to apply please send a bird to Otto Von Habsburg or\nor visit the office. The Company is also dedicated to publishing books of any kind. From Novels, to guides and spell tomes.\n\nThis company supports Mylas for Mayor.\nTHE FIRST ISSUE OF THE FELSEN TIMES, BROUGHT TO YOU BY THE ORENIAN PUBLISHING COMPANY LTD.\n\nOPC Ltd readily welcomes articles from aspiring writers, for a chance to appear in the next issue, please send your article to the publishers. (Via forum PM)\nAdvertisements can be purchased, to find out more, contact the publishers. (Via forum PM)", ""),
        StaticBook("Fest&Holidays 1", "Aerxuis", "Festivies and Holidays \nWritten by Unknown \nCopied by Aerx\nThe Great Hunt \nBy Unknown \nDuring the Feast of Spring, hunters from all corners of Anthos gather together to take part in the spot of hunting beasts of the wild. During spring, the animal population is at its highest.\nOther crops such as carrots, potatoes and wheat are also consumed along with the meat. Kharajyr and Orcs are most likely to pick up their weapons for the hunt, while Halflings usually plant crops instead.\nFeast of Spring\nBy Unknown\nAs the season of Anthos shifts to Spring, the citizens of Anthos hold feasts, balls and other festivities to welcome the new season.\nRebirth and renewal are celebrated across the lands. The Elves are most likely to shun the celebrations, as it represents something they cannot have, while Humans are most likely to embrace the holiday.\nUsually celebrated in conjunction with the Great Hunt.\nBlack Moon Festival\nBy Unknown\nThe day of a lunar eclipse in Anthos. Once night falls, you won’t feel the warmth of the sun for many hours to come. Although a rare event, it occurred a few times in Asulon.\nSome denizens of the word took it as a sign of the end of everything while others celebrated the strange event.\nDuring this time the rates of crime increased dramatically as criminals took advantage of the unexpected darkness.\nRed Rose Day\nBy Unknown\nRed Rose Day is a celebration of affection towards a special someone in your life As signified by its name, participation simply dictates that you five a Red Rose to a person of-\nsignificant importance, whether it be a sign of love, or a simple greeting to a dear friend.\nIt is one of the most commonly celebrated occasion. Humans, Elves and Kharajyr are most likely to participate in these festivities, while many Dwarves prefer to give gifts such as ale.", ""),
        StaticBook("First Artifice", "Leyu", "Forging your first Artifice - a Artificing Guide by Garrik Forgeheart\nCreating your first Rune Weapon is not something to be take lightly - it is a undertaking that will take you several days - if not months, to create. Here is a brief guide to creating for own Rune Weapon, although the\nprocess will vary from project to project. Firstly. You will need a item to Rune-Spell upon. This should be a weapon that can be easily maintained - since a broken weapon will lose it's runes in a effort to stay together . It should also be a weapon\nthat you are profficient with - otherwise, what is the point? For my example, i shall create a Rune-Axe, which was made with the intention of cleaving opponents armour and defenses. It is important that you give your weapon\na unique name - it will make apply runes easier, as the weapon will answer to its name, meaning that only the person holding its true name can wield it. This axe shall be called Wall-Breaker. Secondly, create a area in which you can easily sit in quiet\nand comfort - since runing can b e a hard and arduous process - and you dont want butt-cramps to be part of your weapons runes, right? Harharhar! Then, lay the weapon out in front of you, and place your hand on it. Then, think of\nthe action of the rune you wish to apply to the weapon. for instance, i thought of cleaving opponents into itty-bitty pieces for mine! the rune for Cleaving is Ar-wyrn-dur. however, for your own runes - you will have to discover the names for them\nyourself! As i said, this isnt meant to be easy! Over time, the applications of runes will build up a lattice of runes over the weapon surface . The thicker and more consistent this lattice is, the stronger the weapon will be. Take CARE over this! This\nis the important part of the Rune-Spelling! If you continue to build up these runes, eventually the weapon will be ready to use! If you've followed this guide- hopefully you will now have your very own Rune-Weapon! Use it well! Use it often! Use it\nwisely! For this weapon will last as long as you care for it! Do not underestimate it's power! Of course, every rune-weapon has it's drawbacks - all of them will have their own consciousness - and can freely choose whether to do\nwhat you want to use it for. Forcing a weapon against it's Will will have negative results- usually bad ones!\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Flower Language", "Elorna Avern Lle'hileia", "The Language\n       of Flowers\n\n\nA guide to the secret meaning given to each flower by the wood elves of old.\n\n    \n      In memory of\n      Mayilu Avern\n\n            ~*~\nWhen I was a girl I remember my mother walking with me through fields of flowers, pointing to each variety and describing what they symbolised. I do not know how commonly used this secret language was, but I will always remember the solemnity of my\nmother's voice as she told me the meaning behind each poppy and rose. Of course, the meanings given in this book do not describe the actual traits of each flower, simply the cultural meanings they are used to represent. One does not have to use this guide\nbut I hope it may inspire you while selecting a bouquet for a lover, picking a gift for a friend, or simply decorating your home and garden with life and color.\n\n\nThe Dove Druid,\nElorna Avern Lle'hileia.\nThe Dandelion\nThis simple flower is sometimes considered a weed, yet even that which is small and unassuming can hold hidden significance. \n\nMeanings: Fortitude, Constance, Faith, Wishes Coming True.\nThe Poppy\nThis deep red flower is often used medicinally to relieve pain or aid in sleep. It is often associated with both dreamers and the dead.\n\nMeanings: Dreams, Imagination, Mourning, Eternal Sleep, Relief from Suffering.\nThe Orchid\nThe orchid is as elegant as it is exotic, and its blue coloring is rare in the natural world.\n\nMeanings: Beauty, Refinement, Elegance, Fragility, Femininity, Rare Riches.\nThe Allium\nThese are a very unique looking flower, each one made up of thousands of tiny purple blossoms that form into a large, perfect sphere.\n\nMeanings: Perfection, Royalty, Many Children, a Prosperous Family.\nThe Azure Bluet\nSometimes called Eyebrights, they are a pale blue that often appears white. They are sometimes considered a symbol for the Druidic goddess Cerridwen.\n\nMeanings: Fertility, Motherhood, Peace, Cleanliness.\nOxeye Daisy\nWhen you see these daisies - actually chrysanthemums - in bloom it is always a sure sign of summer.\n\nMeanings: Innocence, Simplicity, Modesty, Shyness, Youth, Summer.\nThe Lilac\nLilacs are clusters of tiny purple blossoms that grow on leafy green bushes, and are quite popular for their aromatic scents.\n\nMeanings: New Love, Sweetness, Affection, Flirtatiousness, Spring.\nThe Sunflower\nThe sunflower is said to always point toward the sun. We could all learn something from the sunflower about optimism and looking on the bright side!\n\nMeanings: Hapiness, Sunshine, Good Luck, Good News, Friendship, Cheer.\nThe Peony\nThese flowers come in soft, pastel hues, their blossoms made up of many layers of petals. They are often associated with the wealthy and high-born.\n\nMeanings: Riches, Honor, Pride, a Carefree Life, Greed, Extravagance.\nThe Tulip\nTulips come in many varieties and can mean different things depending on color.\n\nGeneral Meaning: Fame.\nRed: Declaration of Love.\nOrange: Hope, Bright Smiles.\nPink: Purity of Love\nWhite: Honesty, Sorrow.\nThe Rose\nThe rose is one of the most iconic flowers of romance and love. Depending on how the rose is presented, it can have many meanings.\n\nFull Rose: True Love, Sincerity, Respect.\nRosebud: Innocent Love, a Pure Heart.\nThe Fern\nThe fern is a simple, green plant that bears no bright colors nor scented blossoms. Its reserved simplicity is used as a contrast to dazzling flowers.\n\nMeanings: Old Age, Wisdom, Mystical Knowledge, Sages.\nThe Ivy Vine\nIvy is another green plant that, while not a flower, holds significance in the language of flowers. \n\nMeanings: Wedded Love, Fidelity, Faithfulness, Loyalty, Eternal Ties.\nThe Mushroom\nMushrooms are not often used in bouquets or arrangements, yet they hold strong symbolism, especially in Druidic circles.\n\nMeanings: Magic, Prophecy, Visions, Virility, Masculinity, Long Life, Spiritual Journeys.\nThe Leaf\nThe symbolism and meaning behind each tree would take another book itself, but here are a few meanings associated with tree leaves:\n\nOak: Strength, Nobility, Virtue.\nBirch: Healing, Rebirth, Spirits of the Dead.\nPine: Ancient Wisdom.\nAnd so concludes this book, may it broaden your understanding of the natural world and its many hidden intricacies. May your life be long and happy, and may the Aspects guide your path.\n\n\n           ~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Fourth trimutair", "Deltion", "Hello reader I must tell you what this book is about It is the events leading up to my monk freind having a vision of the green lady. This will be the events when HE helped save me and a lady then later on had the vision he no longer rembers but I still\ncan so as the last person who knows this I will spread the word. there will be a total of 7 books that will be given to 7 people depending on there title as I beleive this to be more of a prophicy more then anything. And so it began.\nEvent 1\nI met this monk and we went on a journey to find spike our leader so I can get my orders as an Initiate.\nWe met this stunning lady who seemed to keep it a secret where he was so we began to argue with her she knocked me unconcious and did nothing\nto my freind the next Time I woke she was on the ground about to die if the monk didn't save her. I got up walked over and we began to head to a medic house to help me and her out the monk saved us both before he began to sweat horrible so I picked him up\nand headed to the Cloud temple. HE asked to be at the alter where he medditated for a while at the lapis statue. HE sudenly woke up feeling better and her started to compulse and he was blown by wind where there was none\nEvent 2 prophicy \nHe then looked at the Emerald staute and said \"The green lady will rise \" then he was uncoincous again. I carried him away. And tried to find spike to tell him of this. But I couldn't find him so he was left at his house\nEvent 3 Denial\n\nLater I went to his house to ask him what he saw He told me he didn't see anything I then asked what the last thing he witnessed he told me the time he healed me. I told him what he told me and said he didn't rember this\nHe told me of the the 4 trimutairys and how the forth is unknown to most. I told him she will rise and he told me that no one knows the gender so it can't be a she I said But you said the green LADY will rise......................... She will come\nThis is the end but beware the Green lady will rise she is the fourth and will not be mistaken I know of this from a seris of events and I will Dedicate my life to the green lady No matter how hard it becomes I believe this will happen Open your eyes and\nbe prepared for when she comes again", ""),
        StaticBook("Fred the Panda", "Riley Powell", "Once upon a time their was a little panda bear named Fred. Fred was a typical little girl panda, that grew up in a grove full of beautiful bamboo, with the elder pandas that cared for it. Her entire life, she admired these elders and wanted to grow up to\nbe one of the caretakers of her beautiful home.\n\nHer life was far from easy though. She spent a lot of time roaming the bamboo grove with her twin sister, learning about the lands, plants and herbs. Nights were spent studying and listening to stories\nfrom her family. Then one day, she was old enough to begin down her path.\n\nThe elder she spoke with told her that since she had never left the safety of the bamboo, she should strike out with her sister to explore the world outside.\nFred was very afraid to do this, but trusted the elder’s judgement. So she and her sister struck out on their own for the first time.\n\nThe road was a hard one. The two of them had no idea how the outside world was.\nDays were spent walking and trying to find their way through the odd places that fill the world. The one comfort was the nights, where the familiar feeling of nature surrounded them while camping.\nShe took joy in the sound of crickets chirping and whippoorwills singing their songs. The grass and leaves were her blankets, the trees were her bed.\nWhen she was hungry, nature provided a variety of food for her. Things were starting to not look as bleak.\n\nThen one day, the two were traveling down a forest path when a group of people tried to grab the two little pandas.\nFred’s sister was killed. The little panda retreated from everyone, weeping for her loss. She went down a darker road, one filled with hate and rage that was not her own. She was tricked into hurting those she cared about.\nFred’s heart hurt for everything that had happened. One night, she lay in the forest and realized that she shouldn’t feel this amount of pain.\n\nThe loss was great, yes, but her sister had become part of the natural cycle.\nShe was a part of nature now, and nature was still around her. In every choice she seemed to make, her path led back to nature and the bamboo grove.\nNature meant everything to her. Through her childhood and through life, it had always been there for her.\n\nEven when she pushed everyone else away from her, and let pain consume her heart, it was there. Fred returned home.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fresh Crops", "Lilliana", "-=+=-Fresh Apples-=+=-\nJuicy and tasty, the apples carry the full flavor of their grown. Grown with tender love and care, these apples are plucked in the prime, making your mouth water by sight alone.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per apple\n-=+=-Fresh Carrots-=+=-\nFreshly plucked from fertile soil, these carrots are carefully cleaned and cut to increase the taste and crunch of each bit.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per Carrot\n-=+=-Cool Melon-=+=-\nEach slice will bring you bright joy as you bite deep into the juicy red innards of our melons.\n\nPrice :: 1 mina per slice", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Witches", "Ikail", "Frost Witches.\n1: What are they?\n2: The curse.\n3: Their Magic.\n4: Disguises\n5: Their bindings.\n6: How to beat one\n7: Their rankings\n8: Where this infomation came from.\nWhat are they?\nA frost witch is a cursed women, someone who has been affected by the Witch Mother curse. Some see it as a curse, others as a boon, but in reality, it is a curse. Don't see it for anything else. You see, the curse transforms the body into a\nblood fueled machine for hatred. What the curse does is it turns their bodys to be dependent on male blood. Without male blood, a frost witch will slowly deplete, becoming a thin husk, barely capable of walking. This is what drives them to feast on men.\nThe problem is, the more men they feast on, the more they crave it. So slowly, they are becoming more and more dependent on it, and killing more and more people.\nThe Curse.\n\nNo one really understands the curse of a frost witch, but we know that it is distinguished by a blue spot on the back of the neck known as the \"Witch Mother Touch\" Much like a bruise, it is small, round and seems to be a small blood vesel\nrupture. The curse has a few stages, first, they will find they enjoy eating meat a lot more, then, they will seem to get sunken features, and become paranoid. Once recognised by the citizens of said town, they will be herded away from it, everyone\nknowing exactly what she is becoming. Since she hasn't been trained by the witch mother yet, she has no powers, and can not disguise herself, however, she does find her nails elongating, her skin starting to go colder, her teeth sharpening, and her eyes\ngetting a duller tint. Slowly, the hunger for a man will grow, and they will become rabit monsters hellbent on men. This only lasts a few weeks before a witch mother will find her and welcome her into her coven. There, she will train and learn the powers\nof a frost witch.\nTheir Magic.\n\nMany people make the mistake of calling their magic Frost Evocation, they are wrong in this sense. Evocation covers the conjuration of the element, and the controlling part of the element, however, their magic can not conjure up frost,\nand requires frost to already be present for them to bend to their will. A better term to call it would be \"Frost Manipulaton\"\nDisguises\n\nA frost witch can disguise herself as anything she wants as long as it fits a few guidlines, one is it must be female, another is it must be Human or an Elf or Halfling. A frost witch can change her disguise whenenver she wants, but it changes\nher body and face only, not her clothes. They are not completely invisible in their disguises, and can be recognised by their stone cold skin, and sharp teeth, which they retain even in the best of disguises.\nWhile in their disguises, they can not cast\ntheir Frost Manipulation, it being simpy too strenous on them to cast two high level magics at the same time.\nTheir Bindings\n\nA frost witch has one huge fault, their bindings. If you discover a frost witch while she is in her disguise, she must grant you a boon, this can not be circular (For example, you give me infinite boons) And can not harm you in that period\nof time. Granted you find out before she changes her disguise, you will have a powerful ally on your side!\nHow to beat one.\n\nOther than the boon, frost witches have a weakness to fire, it easily combats their magic, and causes them extreme pain when in close radius, much like gold to beings of the dark.\nTheir Rankings.\n\nFrost witches are organised in covens, groups much like a clan, each coven has a witch mother, the witch deemed most powerful, she is able to pass on the curse of a frost witch, and, being most powerful, is trusted with teaching new\nfrost witches, and protecting the older ones. They are expected within the coven to keep order, and break up fights. Should one of the frost witches act rashly, or kill someone who didn't need to be killed, the witch mother is also expected to hand out\npunishments.\nYou are probably wondering where all this infomation came from, if you hadn't already guessed, it was given to me by a frost witch, who I made swear the boon that she would answer all my questions truthfully.\nNo frost witches were hurt during the making of this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("FTM, Issue I", "Archibald", "-+ From the Mouth +-\n\n   Good day, good night, or good evening, or even good morning. I am Archibald Vallero. This book is quite simple. I go around asking other people questions, sometimes deep and personal, and then scribe them down in this tome\nfor you all to read and enjoy. I've no bias this time when it comes to who I ask, though keep in mind the demographics of the Descendant races. Enjoy. \n\nI will begin this first issue with an answer from one of my friends, Zeliek, a paladin of Xan.\nQI: Do you prefer a dictatorship or a republic? Why?\n\nZeliek: \"Republic. I just picked one at random. I don't even know what you're talking about.\"\nQ2: Do you think that crucifying people like the Amyasmen do is worse than torture? If so, why?\n\nShariana: \"Alright, I think that crucifixion is taking the easy way to solve something. Because torture, you have a... Hand on experience with\nsomeone. Hm... I think that is everything, really. The Amyas' have no experience with torture, and I doubt that any of them would be man enough to try it.\"\nQ3: Do you think that magic, in the future, will cause unforeseen catastrophes? If so, why?\n\nSalendys Doomforged: \"It has in the past and it will keep happening as long as there are irresponsible mages around.\"\nQ4: Do you believe that one of the Descendant races should be exterminated from the face of this realm? If so, which one and why?\n\nLyria Serthek:  \"Absolutely not. Because we all have a right to live, and why slay off a /whole/ race? Only a certain\nfew should die, and not be compared to their whole race.\"\nQ5: Do you believe that one day we will run out of continents and land to return to?\n\nCharles Fournier: \"No, why not?\"\nQ6: Thighs or breasts.\n\nForrest Sarr: \"Thighs.\"\nQ7: Would you prefer a redhead with green eyes, or a brunette with blue eyes?\n\nJon Snow: \"Brunette, of course! Redheads are usually... crazy.\"\nQ8: Do you think that any Descendant race will become extinct within the next 100 years? If so, which one?\n\nExalprick Oxenfeldt: \"Um... Yes I'll smash all their heads, crush 'm against a wall! Put them on spikes!\"\nQ9: Is the abundance of mages within the realm causing more or less chaos?\n\nDain Stormcrow: \"There are an abundance of mages? From what I understand of magic, or at least one of its major philosophies is balance. If balance\nis not kept preserved, things go out of whack.\"\nQ10: Would you rather eat a raw spider, or have a silverfish placed in your ear?\n\nDemagol Doomforged: \"Spideh.\"\nQ11: Do you think that necromantic practices are simply misunderstood, or, truly, are they just evil? \n\nAsher: \"Um, misunderstood.\nQ12: Are the four Descendant races doing considerably well given their curses?\n\nCheza Stirling: \"Some are, some aren't. Some better than others. Each race is doing 'alright' I suppose. Each has land, but they have problems.\"\nQ13: Is there truly such a thing as 'good' or 'evil' in your opinion, or is everything just formed by the aengudaemons above?\n\nGuarger Tsouderous: \"Everything is based on opinion, Archibald.\"\nQ14: What would you do if you saw an Orcish cub being bullied by a group of elven civilians? \n\nRyder Sturtart: \"Pick the cub up and take him away.\"\nQ15: Would you rather have to assassinate a loved king, or kill a new born child? Which one and why?\n\nSam Beadoin: \"King. Kings are all corrupt, no matter how loved. At least, human kings are...\"\nQ16: Do you think that immortality is achievable? \n\nOan: \"Yes, I think it is. What one must ask themselves, though, is this: How much are you willing to give up for it?\"\nQ17: Were the 'golden' ages of Aegis overrated?\n\nCharis: \"I wouldn't know, but Mister KAlen speaks of Alras as if it were golden. So, I can't say no.\"\nQ18: Would you rather kill a past lover or an old, human man?\n\nLicia: \"I have no past lovers. I am sworn to Xan and the creator only.\"\nQ19: Are aengudaemons the cause of all issues in the world, or is it truly us who has caused all these faults?\n\nMithras: \"It's a mix. Aenguls and Daemons interfere and use us because of how flawed we are. All of us differentiate, we all hold differ-\n-ent views. It makes us easy pawns in their games, they're merely bored children, you see. It's like when a child plays with a chess set. We're the pieces.\"\nQ20: Do you prefer to eat something sweet or sour at night? And why? \n\nCaitlyn: \"Sweet. Sour never tastes nice.\"\nQ21: Are we really in control of our own lives? Is our fate chosen by us?\n\nDaemon: \"We are in control of our lives. Fate is for the weak who need something to look forward to rather than doing it themselves.\"\nQ22: Who would win in a fight to the death: Blundermore or Archmage Cataris?\n\nLuthar: \"Blundermore. Despite Liches' callous and insidious nature,  our trickery only goes so far against raw holy power.\"\nQ23: From Iblees to Setherien, what has been the Descendant race's greatest threat in your opinion?\n\nJa'Mukar: \"Setherien. Because Iblees nevever did anything and he was defeated quite quickly. Where as Setherien showed his face and not hide\naway in an unknown location.\" \n\n*Translated by me, his accent was very thick!*\nQ24: Will the Human empire of Oren eventually dissolve entirely in the future, in your opinion?\n\nHorik Storasvard: \"Nay! Oren vill be forever! Because dey have da drue faith in da creador! And dey are the stronges der es!\"\nQ25: Out of all the four kinds of architecture exhibited by the Descendant races, which race's architecture do you favor the most? \n\nSer Bjorn of Bearhill: \"Human. It makes me feel safe. Other nations buildings just look . . . disgusting.\"\nQ26: If you had immortality, what's the first goal you would want to achieve?\n\nBeth: \"Uh . . . Eat a bunch of cake.\"\nQ27: From elven women to human, which one would you say is the most attractive, hands down? \n\nOliver Crowley: \"Human. Better build and often faces have more beauty to them.\"\nQ28: Where did homosexuality originate, do you think? The high elves, perhaps, or the elven kind in general? Even another race, even?\n\nVuln Shadeleaf: \"I don't know where it originated, but it sure seems likely it started with the mali'ker.\"\nQ29: House Chivay or House Horen? \n\nDread Knight Lennox(Dread Knight Noxx): \"I don't prefer either . . . both are idiotic.\"\n\n*I decided to ask him another question!*\n\nQ30: Was immortality worth it?\nDread Knight Lennox: \"Indeed.\"\nQ31: Would you rather demolish an orphanage or build a brothel?\n\nDorian Hunter: \"Build a brothel. Obviously. It's obvious. Girls.\"\nThat's the end of this book. But do not worry, this is only part one! I'm thinking of writing up another quite soon, and there'll be questions just as humorous or serious in the next one as there was in this one. Thank you for reading. Also, I'd rather\nnot answer any questions myself until after the end of the second issue, thanks. \n\n       //---\\\\\n      //       \\\\\n     //         \\\\\n    //========\\\\\n   //              \\\\\n  //                \\\\\n //                  \\\\", ""),
        StaticBook("Fund. Alchemy", "Jistuma", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nThe Fundamentals of Alchemy\n\nVolume I of V\nForeword:\nI have heard many a man ask why one, such as myself, would take such interest and dedication in the art of alchemy when there are ready-made spells that could do just the same, if not better, a job than an apothecary’s potion. My response to\nthis statement is rather simple, whereas one must have a certain gift for spell-slinging, rune-craft, and spirit-speaking, one mustn’t need these frivolous commodities to use a balm to mend a wound, shroud themselves in a nigh-invisible cloak\nwith the swig from a bitter bottle, or set someone ablaze with bottled flame. Alchemy is not merely reproducing a wizard’s spell, but it is shaping the spell in a way for the common man’s use. While magic still has its place in our world, Alchemy allows\nthose without the gift to reap the same benefits as any mage might.\nChapter 1: The Fundamentals of Alchemy\n------------\nThe Principle and Law of Equivalent Exchange:\nAs I was providing my services to a rather quaint hamlet, which also provided me information of the local flora and more of the same legends I always here of, I was approached by a man of common repute, and he produced a sarcastic, yet thought provoking,\nquestion. This question was, and I will attempt to reproduce the dialect as best as my phonetic ability will allow, “ ‘ow come, Mister, ‘hat ye’ can make all ‘dis ‘onderful stuff outta nothin’?” Now as shameful as his speech may be, the question remains\nthe same. How is it, that alchemists are capable or reshaping the spells of sorcerers for the common folk out of, seemingly, nothing? The answer to this question is simple to state, but fairly difficult to grasp, and this is the Principle of Equivalent\nExchange. Much like the money one gives to the merchant for the apple or slab of meat, one cannot have something for nothing. As the saying goes, “there is no such thing as a free brunch,” there is no such thing as a free potion. This fundamental rule\napplies to old alchemy, through the use of symbols and rituals, far more than what I call “Modern” alchemy. Although I will not get into ancient alchemy, I will state why this rule applies to Modern Alchemy. To craft a potion, for example a bottle of\nalchemist’s fire, one requires the materials. Much like a spell casted by a wizard, one cannot make something out of nothing. Know that to make a potion, and the possibilities are truly endless, one must take plants, objects, and other representations of\nwhat they wish to make. For example, alchemist’s fire could be best produced with an - -, a mixture of -  -, -  -, and a dash of -  -. Why would one need these items?\nThe - - provides the basic mixture of what we will make, and of course the better quality of the - - the better quality of the Alchemist’s Fire, but of course we will get further into this in a later chapter. The -  -, a -  -\nplant that grows most often in deserts, is often -  - and often associated with -  -. This provides an superb symbol for the element of -  -. The -  -, another powerful symbol of -  -, mixes well with the crushed -  -\nto produce something truly strong. The -  -, an optional portion, is another symbol of -  -, albeit both weaker than blaze -  - for both a -  - fire burns far greater than -  -.\nNow then, although you have these symbols of flame, rage, and warfare, one mustn’t simply toss objects into the metaphorical cauldron. Precision is necessary, as always. One must measure their mixture carefully, or they will give too much. And giving too\nmuch will tip the scales of Equivalent Exchange, causing unpredictable results. Why is this you might ask? When balance is achieved through Equivalent Exchanged, a mixture of the elements for the bottled spell of your desire, than all is well. But when\nyou disrupt this balance and push on the world, taking and forcing in too much of one or more element then the world will push back. Of course a word of caution is required, for one may think taking less is the best option when balance is not a certainty.\nThis is a common misconception for not providing enough of one element will result in the same conclusion, imbalance and chaos. This can be easily associated with cooking, too much of one ingredient will spoil the recipe, not enough of an ingredient will\nproduce similar results. Of course it could also produce blander results, and in that case a potion may not be spoiled but it will simply be weak. This is preferable to exploding, of course.\nPreparation and You:\nNovice Alchemists often question me, what advice would you provide the budding alchemist, what sip of wisdom could you provide one who desires to tap your fountain of knowledge? The answer to this is rather simple, preparation is key to any potion. What\nis meant by this is that to mix a potion that you have not mixed before, or do not mix often, you must have all the facts and supplies before you begin. This is best provided in a short list of required procedures if one wishes to keep their eyebrows,\nfingers, and life.\n1. Have all the Facts\n2. Know the Recipe\n3. Clean and check all your instruments are in working order\n4. Ensure you have plenty of whatever ingredients you are using\n5. Keep and Calm Dispostion\nI believe the only topic that requires explanation is “Have all the Facts” and by this I mean that one should not mix a potion they know nothing about. Even having the recipe is not enough to craft a potion safely, but knowledge of its origins,\ningredients, and uses are crucial. Although budding alchemists often overlook this step, it may save your life one day.\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange numbers*\n((13/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Glory to Norland", "Vykk Volaren", "==Glory to Norland==\n\nAn official song of Norland written by Vykk Volaren, a Thane of Clan Thorrson\nStrength and Honor is what we seek!\nOff in our longboats so mighty and sleek!\nThe land of Horen so bland and bleak!\nWeakness and scum is what we reap!\nGold and loot is what we now reek!\nBack to Norland so mighty and fine!\nWe wash off the blood, we wash off the brine!\nA celebration with ale and wine!\nBrawling and singing, a merry ole time!\nGlory to Norland so mighty and fine!\nIron from ice! is what we shout!\nOren flees with brothers about!\nThey fear death when we charge out!\nHelp! they scream while we make them route!\nWe’ll smack their ass and make them pout!\nBack to Norland so mighty and fine!\nWe wash off the blood, we wash off the brine!\nA celebration with ale and wine!\nBrawling and singing, a merry ole time!\nGlory to Norland so mighty and fine!", ""),
        StaticBook("GONE", "Siegfried Vallberg", "The mist rests softly on the mountain peaks like a cloth draped over a pillow. The sun tries to break through the clouds as you trek through tall, green grass wet with morning dew.\nThere are many valleys that one could walk in and never walk out.\nThe farm stretched before me like a great quilt of gold held together with thick stitching. \nThe hills rolled like a welcoming duvet of green and in them lay sleeping the bones of my sister: Anja Vallberg. \n\n-\nSiegfried Vallberg", ""),
        StaticBook("Gordon The Fish", "Audrey Caillot", "*The words are written neatly, larger than normal for the eyes of children. The words would be accompanied by little images!*\n\n  Gordon the little clownfish loved to eat.\n\nHe searched the water day and night, finding bits and pieces of food to gobble up.\nBut Gordon didn't always eat what he should!\n\nIn his trips for food, Gordon often got antsy.\n\nHe did not like to wait.\n\nSo Gordon ate everything in his path.\nGolden treasure, small trinkets, and even wood managed to be gulped up by the little fellow.\n\nGordon couldn't be pleased. And sure enough, his little fish belly grew and hung heavy.\n\nThe contents of his tummy would have\nbeen grander than even the city's vault!\n\nSo he ate and he hate.\n\nAnd he ate..\n\n\nAaand he aatee..\n\nAndateandateandate.\nSoon enough Gordon could no longer swim! He sank to the floor of the ocean, surrounded by mean, pinchy little crabs.\n\nAnd Gordon missed his home, or what was left of it, anyways.\n\nSo Gordon put off his fishy weight!\nAnd Gordon went home!\n\n\n\n     ~ THE END! ~\n             -=()=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorundyr Words", "Ketiley the Vixen", "Gorundyr Words\n\nHeilsa - A form of\nGreeting\nVoth (urse) - Sheit\nSkaag (Curse) - Feck\nPruzah (Insult) -\nInsult of blood\nKogaan - Thank you\nValokein - You're\nWelcome\nStahaem - Divines\n(Gods)\nFahdon - Friend\nDrem'kos - Peace Be\nWith You\nVonok - Farwell\nMahfaerak Laal -\nA peace Prayer for a\nlost loved one\nRah Stahaem Vaknau\nFaal - Gods Smile Upon\nYou\nSvass - Beloved\n(Pronoun)\nElska - Love\n(Pronoun)\nMundu's Agashti -\nCelebration of Love\nValda - Lifemate\n(Female)\nBondi - Lifemate\n(Male)\nModir - Mother\nFadir - Father\nNidr - Son\nDottir - Daughter\nBrodir - Brother\nSitja - Sister\nBeylund - Druid\nSonaak - Priest and\nPriestess\nKoraavaek - Seer\nSik Faanik - Rune Smith\nFey'Fahlil - Wood Elf\nVul'Fahlil - Dark Elf\nUnslaed'Fahlil - High\nElf\nFahlil - Elf\nKaaz - Kharajyr\nOgraem - Orc\nMaltaed'muz - Dwarf\nMaltaed'kolr - Halfling\nMahlaan'Gein - Fallen\nOne\nGruthr - Betryer\nLaas - Life\nJunnesebrom - King\nof The North\nSonaan - One who\nsings for enjoyment;\nmerriment in times of\nhardship, seen as\nalmost as high as the\nSonaak\nYul Tine - A Pagan\nfestival to celebrate", ""),
        StaticBook("Govt. I.D. [107]", "Adulfin Ehrlichmann", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\nName:\nRajiya al-Shamrani\nMCName: YouKnowItsJuno\n\nPosition: Librarian of the Grand Library of Al'Wakhrah.\n\nClearance:\nLevel One\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Graven Scroll", "'The Shrieking Knight'", "Graven Scroll\n-------------------[!] There appears to be Black-Speach written all over this scroll.\n\nDagalur dru,\nVadokiprus burzum,\nKruksog tutas,\nUrdanog vadokan,\nSundog de Akovia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Great Serpent", "Old Woman", "An unquenchable thirst for earth and stone,\nIt sits down low beneath the soil, \nFar beyond the mortal's reach,\nWide it may open its vicious maw, \nShaking the mountains as it moves,\nIt slithers far off and devours many, Beware of the Vermainae,\nchildren of mine, \nFor it asks not even a name before it turns dwarven flesh to gore.", ""),
        StaticBook("Greed", "Aerxuis", "Aspect Tome: Greed \nAuthor Unknown\nGreed, not even the very good can resist this emotion. Something as Evil as Greed can't even be described properly, but it can be done. The Emotion of Greed carries out in generations to come from the first evil.\nThe Evil God, Iblees, cursed the Dwarves with this evil. This Emotion, this Avarice can turn your own friends against you, and it is triggered by Temptation, which very few people can easily resist.\nThis makes Greed a very dangerous Emotion. This emotion is never good and must not be taken lightly, so watch yourself, Druid, for you might be its next victim.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grove Expedition", "Aeres", "Hevera the honorable\n\ngluttong, rage, pride,excitement, wisdom\n\nsynica will understand\ndryads will understand?\ndryads shepered 2 of the more 'foollish' guardians\n\npistil and petal crystal [x]\nDO NOT LIKE EEL\njealous eel?\ngluttonous panda [x]\nkind lizard? [x]\nbee [x]\nsynica the turtle [x]\nhestsal the eel []\ndangerous/jealous, birds don't like\nmantra the spider []\nstole something from synica\nthe lady of the grove\nsloth wants peace, peace from helping lady of the grove\n\nhestal killed melody, lady made a new guardian\nguardians can not control 2 crystals\n\nif we get sloth to open crystal without violence on mantra or hestal,\nhaverna will open crystal as well\n\npromised sloth to assist lady of the grove\n\nhaverna can not assist us in next trial, will reward us after\nburial ritual\npetals\nfeathers\nwater\ndried fruit\nburial shroud??\n\nsaplings planted on the bodies, trees grow from the bodies\n\nDepicts an alter near\na burnt tree. Offerings are given: -\nA helm of a soldier, a sword, staff, shield, and a few others too. All atop the alter is set alight: A silent mourning. A large jug of water washes the ash, and cleans the alter. (misc items could be a flower and branch.)\n\nNew sketch depicts a large -\n- A great forest burns, an army matches, uncaring of the heat, cutting down any in their path.\n\nNew image shows of a great migration. The land beneathe them rots, and people who could not escape it would dissapear, a lot follow.\n\"The fallen rose, and they too marched against us\" Behind \"What can one do, forced to cut down brother and son\" NOTHING FROM BOOK\n\n\"Once we had planted the ash trees to mark their graves.\" Behind \"Even the weight of the great tree cannot stop the\ndead rising\" Picture- Forest in dead of night, lone black figure cloaked (undead?) Sketch shifts to his face, he is smiling, lit up by the moonlight, a demetend smile dripping with some dark substance. A cloud shifts over the moon, obscuring the figure as\nhe lifts in his right hand a twisted staff. Nothing until cloud passes, figure is gone. The forest is quiet, with newly planted trees. The earth freshly turned. Quiet, until a skeletal arm breaks free of the earth, reaching moonwards. In a state of decay,\nthe risen corpse makes a great effort to dig itself from its grave beenath the tree, tearing loose from the roots. Barely clothed, plant clinging to rotten flesh, setting forth as more being to rise from trees in the distance, an army rising, roots unable\nto hold them back from their ill fate. END \n\nChildish voice \"Even the weight of the great tree cannot stop the dead from rising.\"\n\n\"And so we washed away their sins, ash and death.\"\nAltar with offerings, burned and then washed away.\nSame as before.\n\n\"We had no longer the luxury of what we once had gave\"\nElves searching a burned and rotten hillside for something, plants missing perhaps? Cannot be found, no longer lives, or what once was common is now rare??\n\"Those who feel to the dread, we promised not to forget.\" Similar scene, more focused, offerings, staff carved from branch, segmented shield, no details on helm and sword. Dried fruit, single flower.\nSmall, five petals per flower and many different.\nflowers in the bunch, picks one carefully, it is then burned, the ashes washed away. Behind: \"Though we did not forget, the ash of their sin we washed away.\"\n\n\"Those who did not rest were meted the same as the forests\" Behind: \"We had no choice but\nto burn the bodies and hope to be forgiven.\" Bloody battle, elven warriors fighting against undead army, fire and lightning, brother fighting against dead family, bodies burnt after, elves reaching for trinkets to put in ritual to put them to rest.\n\"Their funeral shrouds became the roots of the elder trees.\" Female elves weaving roots/plant matter into something. Furneral morourning of a child, child wrapped in shroud made by elven women.\n\"The children could not be guided, so small, left so alone.\" Behind: \"WE wrapped them instead, swaddled in a shroud to hide on the path.\" \nDead children. Nothing new. Foggy, fantasy-esque realm. Child wanders along path, using earlier shroud as cloak.\nDark figure approaches, large-limbed, child hides under cloak, stands still, figure marching onward, not seeing them. Dark figure goes towards figures off path, in the fog, dragging them off into the dark.\n\"Our craftsmen made staves of the elder tree branches.\" BEhind: Picture of a tree. \nElves wandering, picking fallen branches, bringing them to craftsmen, circled around a workstation. Carved into walking staves, same as others seen, for the fallen,\ntoo small for children to use.\n\"And we knew not more to offer them, save our tears.\"Behind: \"Not just ours, but those of the world as well.\" \nFurther funeral processions, mourning, looks sad, long since dead putting their own dead to rest. Individuals wash away the ashes of the offerin\nofferings of those lost in body and soul with a jug of water, mourners are helpless and hopeless, despite their rights and offerings, they feel that the dead whose corpses they lack my naver be put the rest.\nThis book contains hastily scribbled notes regarding the expedition into the ancient Elven Grove.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guest List", "Kale de Sevanés", "{!} Written in neat penmanship and hand written with fresh ink there would be a letter in cursive.\n\n\"My dearest rafiqi, Hadrian. Shokran for taking the time to hand these letters out for Gareth and I. I too have taken the time to write out a guest list\nthat these letters should be handed out to.\" \n\nKetiley Orvar\nMorvan Orvar\nAmethu Denaseth +1\nNeero Sarr +1 \nGrafess E. Sarr\nAlai Kharadeen\nArlen Kharadeen\nVargen Vallberg\nKiveck Irelia\nDaniel Ward (Gladous)\nNikolai Ruhnsted\nNemir (UnBaed) + 1\nSasha (Charoodler) \nNeci (TempestCerase)\nCarver Illinos (jjujack)", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism1", "Lelien", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume I\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThe history of Asulon is known to be rich with wars, political usurpations, monstrous drakes, and the rise and fall of nations. However, one history that eludes most modern, non-mali'aheral scholars is the secret history of elhaelun'or, and its many\ntrials and tribulations. One such excerpt (to take from a vast swathe) is the Haelun'or Schism--a short, and unusual, period of instability and disunity in the motherland. In this three volume series, one will discuss the turbulent period for the benefit\nof future citizens.\n\nThe Haelun'or of Asulon was, in this period, ruled by the echillan'thilln--the Silver Council. Much like its Malinorian contemporary, members were chosen by those whom were deemed worthy by the current council members--\nthe okariran. Two of these counsellors would begin a chain of events eventually causing the one, and only, demagogic political usurpation in mali'aheral history. Their names were Ellir'siol, the Okarir'leyun (Master of Beauty), and Nelecar, the Okarir'sil\n(Master of the Sword). \nFrom the very inception of the two working together, friction between their personalities was evident. Nelecar was a soldier with a great, and admirable, dedication to the purity of his kin. His efficient, though admittedly\nextreme, methods of protection allowed for a distinctly effective military force that has yet to be seen again within the walls of the mali'aheral. Ellir'siol was an artist, and an architect. Her mesmerising design of the Haelun’or residential district\nwas one of the finest examples of classical, revivalist mali'aheral architecture available, and is still emulated to this day.Touting overtures of peace, wisdom, and forethought, she strove only for what can be perceived as \"the greater good\" in regards\nto the motherland.\n\nDespite their own good intentions, there were many obvious faults in their actions throughout their years in the service of the cihi'thilln. Nelecar was not a forgiving mali. When a single, minor wrong was committed, he would often\nact harshly towards the perpetrator. One such case involved an insolent mali'aheral who refused the Okarir’s demands, and was summarily locked in a cell for nearly a month as punishment. His liberal use of banishment to punish wrongdoers was also a\nharshly debated affair, and was the main issue of the coming schism. Ellir'siol, however, was by contrast far too forgiving of wrongdoers. She often pressed for impure mali'aheral to be re-integrated to society, and those whose ideals were not\ncongruent with Larihei's vision were protected by her delicate, and clever political machinations. Retrospectively, conflict should have been predicted.\nThis is but a tale of two mali’aheral incapable of compromise, and such shall be shown in the second volume.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism3", "Eenhoornheid", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n     Volume III\n\n    by Lucion Sullas\nThe importance of the events that occurred during the Schism can not be trated lightly. The after-effectsm though, were seemingly mundance. With the immediate disappearance of Nelcar, the whole city simply fell to the leadership of what council was\nleft, althought Ellir obviously having significant inluence over proceedings.\n\nA detrimental effect of the Schism was the slow dissolution of what remained of the armed forces (then referred to as the 'Legion').\nThe size and ability of the soldiery was slowly whittled away, until only a few diligent guardsmen remained. Further affeted was the concept of violence in general-- the methods of the Okarir'sil no longer popular with any citzen.\nThe lacking of these two elements may explain why the mali'aheral nation had been a haven of peace for decade upon decade.\n\nOne is sure, however, that the reader is curious of the fate these two political rivals succumbed to.\nNelecar's disappearance did not last long, as he hid in the lowest levels of the city-- murdering numerous citizens over the course of multiple years. However, after nearly four decades of being hidden, the ragged Okarir'sil found his way into\nthe city, and stood in the square, confronting frightened and confused citizenry. His madness had overtaken himself, and, as a final act, he took his own life-- brokwn, thin, alone, and forgotten by history.\nEllir'siol, who strived all her life to keep all those whom she loved safe, lost her entire family. She herself turned bitter, and strayed away from the citizenry in her cold, lonely tower above the Eternal College. Eventually, she disappeard--\nalmost as if fading away with the end of her political career.\n\nLet this short history be a message of the dangers that are ingerent within the extremes of political rivalry, and extremist thinking. Should one desire to take message from these\nvolumes, then allow this humble writer to give you a final, resolyte statement. Rashness is rewarded only with destruction, and demagoguery is rewarded only with loss.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haiku's by Ana", "casanova9", "*there is a sketching of a fox*\nYour coat is pretty\nColors of orange, black, and white\nYour cutness hides strength\n*there is a sketch of a tree*\nYour hands are green\nYou wave hello and goodbye\nYour roots are endless\n*there is a sketch of an owl*\nYou are large and wise\nSleep at day, hunt in the night\nYou don't give a hoot", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfblood Chron.", "Elindor", "Halfblood Chronicles I: Birth of the Halflings\nStonehead, the third king of Kal'Urguan after the death of King Simmpa, was a more brazen ruler than his predecessors and took to him a human wife. Magdoline was a baroness and fourth wife to King Stonehead,\nmarried upon the anniversary of his second year of rule.  While Stonehead bore many children he greatly loved Magdoline and desired for her to be with child. King Stonehead beseeched the help of a Druid that his wife might conceive, and by\nSun’s Smile the following year she bore Kragnook,  the first Halfling and the first known Halfblood of Aegis. With King Stonehead's popularity among the dwarves, many sought to marry human wives and thus began a dark time for dwarf-human relations.\nMen started to fear and hate the dwarfs for coming into their villages by night and stealing women away. By the time King Stonehead's reign ended and  the fourth king, Vixnor, assumed the crown the population of Halflings had grown to fourscore and six.\nKing Dan of Al'Khazar stormed Kal'Urguan with a small force to demand the citizens of Oren be left in peace. Vixnor, who despised the marrying of dwarves and humans, agreed to outlaw the partnerships and sought to kill all living Halflings.\nIn an act of compassion Saint Dan rescued the Halflings and bade them to live in the outskirts of Oren. After the passing of many kings the Halflings established the township of Dunwood and the outlawing of interracial relationships was forgotten.\nHalfblood Chronicles II: Walking Trees\nThe second son born of Horen, founder of men, was Impaar who towered above his brothers in size and in pride. He took to him to wed a daughter of Krug, and he loved her truly. Following the banishment of Iblees, Impaar departed from Aegis in search of\nother lands that he might build a city of his own, with might comparable to his father's. In the hope that he could flee Iblees' curse by leaving Aegis, Impaar never returned to his father's house. Whether he lived forever or simply died of old age, just\nas the men of Oren, remains unknown. But his children grew tall and taller still and the descendants of Impaar became known as Ents or 'giant', for they were tall and mighty like oak trees and their skin thick like leather.\nHalfblood Chronicles III: Brutes for War\nFor poor bookkeeping it is hard to tell whether Rex Lagrak'Ursin was the sixteenth or nineteenth Warlord of Krugmar, but the feat of his victory over Orgik\"Shmed, wherein his skull was smashed like a watermelon, is a popular anecdote among orc children.\nLagrak'Ursin had greater plans for Krugmar and in his lack of foresight intended to declare war on every nation of Aegis. Aware that the army's might was not capable of such victory, Lagrak'Ursin set about to breed a super army of Halfbloods.\nHonourable men, elves and dwarves were belittled to conceive with brutish orc women. The resulting offspring were a variety of odd-bodies, many that were too weak to survive beyond adolescence. Just as Lagrak'Ursin was on the verge of a\nsuccessful breakthrough in combining a Mountain Dwarf with a Shaman, Warlord Krimpvlark lopped the Rex's head clean off and assumed control of Krugmar. The vile experiments were abandoned and the Halfbloods banished to live their days in The Wilds.\nOstracised by even those from whence they descended, the the Halfblood Orcs became known as Brutes; violent bandits and thugs who murdered travellers unprovoked, for their hatred of the pure races waxed strong.\nHalfblood Chronicles IV: The Daemon Prophet\nThere is a tale, the reliability of which I cannot discern, that before the War against the Undead there was a Druid whose wisdom could not stagger his curiosity. It is said that the hand of Iblees delivered a book into the Druid's\npossession which spoke of an ancient dark magic. From the intricately scrawled words came a horrible whispering that tantalised his mind. Altogether consumed by the shadow's grip the Druid used the book to summon Akraek: Beauty's Fury. But the Daemon\nrefused to harness its great power to ensnare Aegis and instead seduced the Druid. Upon conception the man was consumed by fire and the Daemon returned to Iblees' side no longer but one entity. Within the tainted bowels of the Nether's most alluring\nAemon grew Rott; destined not for his flesh father's time, but to emerge on the cusp of Iblees' resurrection.\nHalfblood Chronicles V: The Forgotten Elvish Cousin\nFor nigh on thirty years during the reign of High Prince Ralian, Orc diplomat Kragbar'Krump lived in Upper Laurelin and took to him an Elven wife. The practice of Elves laying with Orcs had never before been known and hopefully never would be again.\nSo the child was named Govlen, meaning 'unlikely' and was raised in Laurelin. The Boy was rich in vigor and lackluster in hair. His clumsy scaly body would break windows, knock over market stalls and mistakenly set fire to treetop houses.\nWhen it came time for his passage to become a man the Elven Council ruled that Govlen be removed from Malinor upon his return, lest the ancient forest be brought to its knees. Govlen lived longer than any Orc and took to him many wives of Kal'Urguan.\nHis sprightly fertility bore 18 children, the first of whom was Kemal, who never took to him a child. His remaining sons bore many children and by the third generation the descendants of Govlen were numbered at four hundred two score and three.\nThey dispersed themselves across Kal'Urguan becoming stall vendors and politicians, never fearful to leech extra minas from dim-witted Orcs. The Orc brutality for language referred to the Govlen family as 'Goblins', a name which has stuck with them since.\nAs the bloodline continued Govlen's blessing of long life and fertility faded until the Goblins became almost synonymous to their Orcish cousins, save their intellectual and physical differences.", ""),
        StaticBook("HallsOfTheBlind", "Dizzy Irongrinder", "The follow pages are the amalgamation of ancient texts translated from the dwarvish tounge over the course of several months study. These findings are in no way entirely factual or conclusive, but they are the closest thing we have to the truth.\n~~~~~~~~~\nthe ancient dwarves had, at one point or another, used runesmithing to trap dark creatures to an underground labyrinth. The labyrinth was kept from the public, all records of it destroyed, all mention of it censored without hesitation.\nThe ancient dwarves of the time feared what may happen should someone unwittingly, or worse yet intentionally, released the darkness kept there. Years passed by, new kings rose and fell in time, until the fateful reign of the Ironborn kings.\nThe Ironborn are famous for their cruelty and near genocide of the dwarven race, and the resulting destruction of their most valuable technologies and knowledge. However, they did not begin their reign with an iron fist.\nTo begin with they were indeed quite popular, creating many social and economic changes for the benefit of dwarven society as a whole. One popular move was to send out expeditions to uncharted territories in order -\nto survey them to see if they would make suitable mines. What one of these expeditions discovered was none other than the labyrinth. The Ironborn king was ecstatic, as deep in -\nthe personal libraries of clan Ironborn lay hidden one of the few remaining reports on the labyrinths true nature. Seizing the opportunity created by such a find the Ironborn king took no time at all to utilize the place.\nHe had the entrance of the pit magically sealed so that it may only be opened briefly at the utterance of aforementioned inscription. Why the emphasis on the ideas of vision and blindness?\nIt has long been speculated that during ancient dwarven times the punishment for the crime of murder or kin-slaying was to have one's eyes removed. The Ironborn king claimed to the public that the labyrinth they had found had been-\nconstructed with the intent to punish kin-slayers and murderers, but it was never fully completed. With the already enacted social reforms that the Ironborn used to rise to the throne already in action, the populace was rather quick to -\nshift to this new form of punishment, deeming the removal of ones eyes to be barbaric and uncivilized. The true reason the Ironborn king utilized this resource was not, in fact, for social and civil reasons.\nIt was actually one of the main reasons the Ironborn were able to control the populace so well in the events leading up to their massacre.\nAny opposers, dissenters, traitors, spies, and even simple men and women who knew too much could be quickly and efficiently disposed of without a trace.\nLittle did the Ironborn know that their attempts to silence their enemies were just as effective at feeding the creatures locked away.\nWith the collapse of the Empire of Khorvad and the Ironborn going into hiding, the last shreds of knowledge on the Halls of the Blind were forever lost. Their whereabouts unknown, until recently.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haria Laws&Order", "Amin Al-Qalishi", "The Establishment of Law \n\nThroughout time have the Qalasheen and their kin learned to live civil and respectful even during their darkest hours.\nIn order to preserve the mutual understanding that only through law and order harmony can truly be achieved, \nthe Sultan and his respective subordinates have established the boundaries between civil and savage, good and criminal,\ndivine and dark with spiritual guidance and wisdom. \n--------------------_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-___________________\n    The Yalasar Laws\nIt is not fitting for an individual, man or woman, believer or non believer, to undermine or disobey the laws set by Allah and his respective servants. For one who does,\n is indeed on a clearly wrong path.\nThe blessing of life received by the righteous Allah may not be taken from anyone, no matter the kin, belief or gender.\nThe many riches of this world belong to those that earned them.The ones that walk a path of thievery will walk a path towards exile.\nThose that not share the mutual enlightenment of Allah’s followers should be tolerated and treated as an equal, for they cannot help being born outside our sacred lands. These three laws will be the bulwark of the civility within the Sultanate,\nfor they are set in stone by the only supreme authority that reigns above all, Allah.\n-------------------_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-____________________\n\n\nThe Bayezid Laws\nIn a world full of temptations and delusions, the individual must remain on the divine path set before him.\n In order for that to be possible, a strong understanding of the true meaning of sacrifice and necessity must be present.\nThe enlightened individual of the Sultanate shall not lie, unless the truth would harm the innocent or empower the corrupt. The Sultan is the true messenger of Allah and shall not be undermined as the Sultanate’s leader as long as he remains\non the path of Allah. Malicious planning, execution or intent are to be blocked out of the minds of those that enter the Sultanate, for those undermine the individual’s divine bond with Allah. Power shall have no worth in the eyes of Allah,\nonly through merit and good intent may one truly be elevated or pardoned.Corrupting the name of Allah and his legitimacy will be strictly forbidden within the Sultanate. As we respect you, we demand respect in return.\nAny individual breaking these laws in the eyes of other kin or relatives shall lose its representation by the Sultanate, for it does not follow the true path it is required to.\n--------------------_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-___________________ \n The Mercan Laws\nFor there are many corrupted in these lands that would lurk upon the riches and people of the Sultanate out of jealousy or envy,it is essential that those that follow Allah and seek shelter in our sacred land must\nbe protected and prepared for all that evil can bring.When an individual or a collective clearly seeks to undermine the first Yalasar law, Allah shall grant permission to defend and potentially harm the underminers.\nOnly when it is a question of life and death, may the enlightened individual exceed its mortal boundary. Every being within the Sultanate, citizen or visitor, has the divine responsibility to defend\nthe sacred land from anyone that aspires for its destruction. Only the Sultan is enlightened enough to appoint his successor, for he represents Allah’s will.Ones that carry harmful goods within the Sultanate must seal\nthem and carry them out of sight accordingly. Only those tasked with protecting the Sultanate may publicly show their tools of killing as a sign of authority.\n-------------------_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-____________________The Kismet Laws\nIn order to preserve the functionality of the social stature in the Qalasheen society,\n laws must be established as an act of mutual understanding of what restrictions and liberties are for the best. Only through civil interaction\ncan those with a good heart not be swayed to corruption and dark temptations. All must be treated with equal respect and consideration within the Sultanate with the exception of increased respect given to those blessed by the Sultan’s grace.\nThose that have no wealth due to misfortune should be treated and aided if possible. Those of male gender shall not seek physical or unnecessary social contact with females after a marriage for adultery is forbidden.\nThose of female gender shall not seek physical or unnecessary social contact with males after a marriage for adultery is forbidden. Those who aim to speak their words in a public setting shall refrain from insulting or\nundermining the Sultan or his chosen brothers in administration in said public setting. Those who are found to commit the sin of adultery in any shape or form shall be sentenced at the discretion officer\nin question to the point of public humiliation and no further. Those who are found to criticise the government without express permission of said government will be given to the hands of the guards in order to execute a punishment befitting.\nThose who have chosen to willingly take the life of another without just cause shall have their life taken from them in a fashion befitting the crime itself.Any citizen who has for whatever reason evaded the payment of taxes due\nshall have their taxes doubled at the instant of sentencing. Criminals guilty of such are allowed to pay off in full at that moment. If they continue to refuse actively they shall have all of which they own reclaimed by\nthe state and imprisoned before exile.Bribery is the most sincere form of deviation from the lawful will of the state and by extension Allah and shall be punished by being forced to pay the previously mentioned bribe twice over to the government\nin addition to the punishment for the crime the bribe was meant to cover.Who who helps a murderer is by extension holding the blade himself and shall be treated to the same punishment as those who are found red handed and without mercy.\nAssaulting another of Allah’s children, without just causes, shall be met with a punishment appropriate to the severity of the crime itself. Assaulting a citizen with obvious deadly intent orwith the possession of a weapon during the assault\nwill find themselves\n sentenced with capital punishment and then exile with duration set by the presiding officer at the scene. Any citizen assigned\n exile with duration and has the great intent of returning is still required to pay all according taxes\nand dues as the state mandates.\n This may be done by entering at the gate and requesting escort by guard for the duration of their stay, paying dues and then being escorted out.Anyone that has been accused of breaking a law that\nhas not been written nor mentioned on this official document will be forced unto trial,\n which the current Sultan will oversee as judge.It is the Caliph that will choose the punishment or release of the accused as he sees fit with Allah's eyes\nwatching over them all.\n--------------------_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_--------------------The Bruhier Laws \n\nPowers of the Sultan \nThe Sultan is the head of The Sultanate of Haria. All decisions are made final by him alone.\nRelations with the Council \nThe Sultan may appoint those he sees fit to sit on the Council, at his discretion.\nThe Sultan may appoint any blood-related Qalasheen as his heir. The Sultan may revoke seats on the Council, at his discretion.\nThe Sultan may create new positions on the Council, at his discretion.\nThe Sultan may abolish positions on the Council.\nThe Sultan may change the powers of each position on the Council as he sees fit.\nThe Sultan may abolish the entire Council.\nThe Sultan may not arrest any member of the Council without just cause.\nThe Sultan may not banish any member of the Council without just cause.\n\nRelations with the Fellaheen (citizens)\nThe Sultan may call any citizen to court.\nThe Sultan may arrest any citizen should they have committed a crime or are a suspect in one.. \nThe Sultan may banish any citizen for any reason.. \nThe Sultan may give any citizen honorary titles.\nResponsibilities and Powers of the Council \n\nZiems (Vassals) \nZiems are entitled to a district or plot of land, supervised by the Sultan \nZiems must remain pure of heart and rebuke any want for wealth as this leads to corruption.\nZiems may enact justice on citizens within their holdings to a degree. All acts of crime and falsehood must be brought up with the Sultan. \nZiems may hold their own trials for citizens within their holdings.\nA Ziem may hold a trial for citizens of another Ziem’s .holdings with permission. If denied then a Mustashar or Sultan will intervene.\nIf found guilty, a Ziem may banish criminals from Harian lands, only able to be repealed by them or the Sultan.\nMustashar \nThe Mustashar is responsible for the management of the High Council. \nThe Mustashar may call any citizen to trial. The Mustashar is responsible for the upkeep of Al-Khaleed and all holdings under The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Mustashar may call any council member to trial.\nThe Mustashar is charged with relieving their position as appointed regent once an heir is of the legal age of 15.\nThe Mustashar is charged with relieving their position as appointed regent once a Sultan has returned.\n\nOffice of the Munavin The Grand Steward and their subordinates are responsible for the development of urban areas within The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Grand Steward and their subordinates are responsible for the development of rural areas within The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Grand Steward and their subordinates are responsible for tax-collecting within the borders of The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Grand Steward and their subordinates are responsible for administrating information to the populace of The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Lord Steward has the power to appoint Deputy-Stewards in The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Amir \nThe Amir is responsible for the management of all armed forces within The Sultanate of Haria and has absolute power over them aside from the Sultan. \nThe Amir is responsible for all armed encounters involving The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Amir is responsible for policing the realm of The Sultanate of Haria in diplomatic or martial means.\nThe Amir has the power to create Deputy Amirs within the Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Amir answers solely to the Sultan or his appointed regent.\nCourt of The Safeer (Emisarry)\nThe Safeer is responsible for international relations between The Sultanate of Haria and foreign nations.\nThe Safeer has the power to create embassies for The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Safeer is responsible for pursuing the interests of the Sultan and The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Safeer has the power to create ambassadors to represent the Sultanate of Haria.\n\nCourt Mesakha\nThe Court Mesakha is responsible for the management and upkeep of all official documents within The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Court Mesakha is responsible for sealing all letters sent by the Sultan of The Sultanate of Haria.\nThe Court Mesakha has the power to appoint a scribes within The Sultanate of Haria.\n\nProperty \nSelling and Buying of Property \nAll land, be it residential,agricultural, industrial, is the property of Allah under the tenancy of the Sultan of Haria.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hedge Knight", "Kale le Prevost", "Clinic of the Caliphate\n\nHedge Knight\n\nMale\n\nAge: 16-20\n\nRace: Human (Highlander)\nIssue:\nHad very minor bruise against his nose. A cut on his upper right lip and lower nose area.\n\nAppears it happened by a sword impaction to the face. Luckily there was no serious damage.\nTreatment Plan:\n\nUsed a cuitip dowsed in disinfectant to dab it upon his facial features that seem to be lightly harmed during the impact. Then a druid paste was wiped upon his face to rid of the coloring and scarring before a nose splint was placed just\n- to refrain from any broken damage to the upper nose frontal frame. \n\n1523 In the year of the, Sun Fields\n\nCost: 10 minas \n\nNot a citizen of the Caliphate\nTreated by: Head Doctor Kale\n\n*Doctor Kale's signature would be here in neat penmanship* \n\n~Head Doctor Kale~", ""),
        StaticBook("Help", "Vannessa Longridge", "\"Sahar...I fear for my life. You must wonder why I tell you this, but you have never shown any signs of anger or distrust towards me. I believe someone is plotting against me in the Palace. I do not think it is the Sultan, but rather the Emir or the Imam.\nI have recieved death threats many times...and constantly been robbed of prized possesions from my house..Please help me!\n-Iskander", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbology", "Vlad Shade", "Alchemy Herbology\n\nTippens root\nA alone weak herb but it is used for healing purposes and can stop bleeding effectively on its own and is very usefull in combonation with others\nMandragora \nA commonly used herb a very powerful base in lesser and greater form commonly used as a healing base and can be used for more destructive potions\nSerpents stalk\nA very good ingredient and can only be harmful if in combonation alone and in most combonations its used for its remarkable aspect of healing burn wounds\nFrost vine\nA very colt and blue flowered vine its only found in dwarven lands due to the temperature and is very helpful although very rare\nBliss Foil\nA very calming but yet un nerving herb it can numb down a area so no one feels any pain meaning who knows what they could do if applied\nAthin\nA herb commonly used for just its extract its very fire retardant and can be applied to non metalic armors to resist fire\nbut in combonation is a ingredient to a Greater Healing Potion\nCrimson Vase\nA very odd herb indeed its extract is one of its many uses this herb is a odd smelling flower its smell clouds the mind making decision making hasty but it can also be used in alchemist fire\nDrakes tail\nA elegant herb quite rare as well it seems that only the orcs have made its habitat their home and for good reason it only grows in barren land but it has many destructive uses\nDwarfs pumpkin\notherwise known as the alcohol flower it can be used to make a dwarven ale the recipie is odd and hidden away from most in oren however\nBlood Lotus\nA herb with flowers resembling blood can be very helpful to most peasants considering its soup has all the nutrients one wouldnt get in their daily ration\nFlame Tongue root\nA destructive herb that has a few medicinal uses in use with aqua vitae it can be a healing salve called flame spitter but in water becomes a painful extract\nLariheis fingers\na herb then when its extract is drank hightens the senses and is very helpful a new fact to the herb is its very sleek and easy to carry so not much of a problem for traveling alchemist\nElfs Hair Vine\nA vine that is found in dwarven lands commonly can be very sugary and used to get a mild energy rush in a split second you will be worse then you sttarted off so be warned on that\nCrouching feather\nA feather very commonly used in potions mostly in potions for throwing and lethal purpose\nHalflings grass\nA herb comonly used in weak poison but can be turned into a drug like affect if in a greater form\nAlabaster leaf\nCommonly used in poison but if alone in extract form and drank while the user is poisoned will counteract that of a stronger potency\nSaffvil\nA strong and deadly smell eminates from this poison and will kill the entire users body over time if drank\nClutchers straw \nthis herb has one hear it one known use and that is to paralysise the poor soul inflicted with its extract or higher potentcy poisons\nMetzils tangle \na herb only found in the jungle coils at every area on the herb and s used commonly in stone skin\nGoblins ivy\na potion used for many weak poisons and is quite rare a alchemist with their hands on this might make you sick at best", ""),
        StaticBook("Hist. of Evaral", "Ebonsquire", "The History Evalar, the First City of the Elves\n\n((Originally scribed by HiddenForge))\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundant there and in the surrounding areas.\nIt let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding areas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... Great towering trees grew in\ntheir place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these trees, for the magik embedded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empre that dwarved all others previously\nknown. The Elves lived inside the trunks of these towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries, an Astronomical Storm swept across the land, felling the magikal trees where they stood. Lightning\nstruck the exposed Earth, melting the ground and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energies of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named\nthis area Evaral, meaning 'Protected' in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but then the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated,\nthe Elves started to reach for the sky. The trees grew until the touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace once again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that\nrose with the storm. And then a terrible  thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral, preferring the new\nforests beyond its border. They spread out far across the land, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually, even they settled down and formed small vilages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting what they left behind.\nBy this time, only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did  not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other eElves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left, each family took with them a seed from the first tree, which happened\nto reside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes. And its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armor to help the remaining elves in\ntheir journeys. This armor now resides in the Tomb of Evaral, as the First Tree's spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in Evaral. However, over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them. Until one day, many\ncenturies later, it camei n the hands of a young druid. The great city of Evaral's location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still out there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it. And bring it to power once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("History III", "Clan Father Vidar Frostbeard", "Frostbeard\n History - Anthos\n    By Clan Father\n   §VVidar Frostbeard\nMany years had passed, and Goruk the Great had vanished in similar fashion to the disappearance of Karl the Orcbane. Liam Frostbeard, former Clan Father, returned to the Frostbeards for a brief amount of time before getting back to his hunt.\nUpon arrival to the new lands, the Frostbeards had once again taken positions of authority within the Dwarven Kingdom. This time, however, they had no quarrels with the reigning King. Gorum Frostbeard had become one of five Lords of the Dwarves,\ndirectly under King Omithiel, and Moruk Frostbeard had become the Grand Merchant. It was also around this time that King Omithiel proposed to Moiruh Frostbeard, making her the future queen of the Kingdom of Urguan.\nThe Kingdom of Urguan began to prosper under the rule of King Omithiel, and the Frostbeards began to prosper as well. They had kept to their tradition of remaining and maintaining the title of the richest clan, but the same could not be said in terms\nof power and strength. The Frostbeards were leaderless, lost, and near the brink of a second collapse when an unexpected arrival happened during this crisis. It was the second coming of great Clan Lord Karl “The Orcbane” Frostbeard.\nA new era was to unfold in the lands of Anthos as it did in the lands of Asulon, an era where there would be no rise and fall for the Frostbeards, there would only be ascension.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "Jistuma", "Transcribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in he Void the world of\nAegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and\nunformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\nThe power was entwined into the very\nfabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power channeled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore\nmanifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spead of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone,\nhardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil.\nBut the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his\nminions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world… But it was not to\nlast. The power of Iblees was great, even in the Void, and he worked at unraveling the barrier between the worlds… Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope\nfor salvation…\nWith the failing of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there.\n\nSo it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other to\ndarkness… They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made…\nThe History of Magic\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "Leyu", "The History of Magic\nTranscribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer. :: :: :: :: :: :: :: Before the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But\nwithin the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the Void the world of Aegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the\nworld of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and unformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just\nas man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power. :: The power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked, ever connected. So it was that\nall the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power was channelled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the\nHumans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone, hardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts,\nstrong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil. :: But the magic was not forever present\nin the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his minions back whence they came, and a\nbarrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world... :: But it was not to last. The power of Iblees was\ngreat, even in the Void, and he worked at unravelling the barrier between the worlds... Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope for salvation... ::\nWith the failing of the barrier protectingthe world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there. :: :: So it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other\ndarkness...They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made...\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hope", "Aerxuis", "Aspect Tome: Hope \nAuthor Unknown\nHope, the very true innocence in a place where all is lost. No matter what happens, a person will always have hope, but how does it affect us? It is very simple, Hope is a very difficult emotion anybody can do with right now.\nHope is the emotion that supported the birth of Life. It cannot be explained easily, but it is true.\nBut for us Druids, our trigger on Hope is very similar, but different. We have our hopes on the Aspects,\nwhich are Cerridwen and Cerrunen, we are their conduits and we expect them to assist us in our times of need...\nHope can trigger within us at any moment, when War is happening, when you're being held hostage, when a family member or a friend is dying. It can happen as much as it can, but you cannot assume to ignore it.\nIt is often described as, “The smallest light in a room full of darkness,” even the very evil have it, but their use for it is on their own accord.\nThis also causes many things, rebellions and such, for some take Hope too seriously, and it often turns them into power-hungry people. This has been an account of this Emotion, may your new found Knowledge flourish.", ""),
        StaticBook("Horen's 'Swamp'", "Daniel 'Vince' Ward", "There once was a wee lil' lass named Emporer Horen! His demease was rather petty so he stooped low, low, low. He set his eyes upon the jewel of the world, Shreck's Swamp. With a bold strut he rapped upon Duloc's gates, Shreck's castle, and demanded he\nopen the gates and swear fealty. Shreck peered down, offering him a 'bro you crazy af' look before descending. Huffing and puffing, he blew his own gates right off then kicked Horen's head right off. Literally. Before it hit the ground his corpse had been\nmutilated with Shreck's strong orkish hands to such a degree it looked like a heap of onions. That is the story of how Horen the swamp thief lost his life to Swampgoth Shreck'Lak.\n\n\n\n\ns w a m p", ""),
        StaticBook("Horse Charlie", "Klaudia Crast Warnek", "-------------------\n\n\nCharlie and the Horse\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\nWarneck\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n------------------\n-\n\nCharlie was a rich boy who had more toys than you could imagine. His family had a lot of money, and whenever he liked something, they would buy it for him.\n\n*Here would be a picture of the boy Charlie*\n-\n\nIn reality, then, he had no idea what things cost, and wouldn't bother to take care of what he had. Nor did he realise how difficult it was for other children to get toys like the ones he had.\n-\n\nA time came, though, when he was so used to all his toys and various stuff, that he began to want something different. One of his uncles found a fine horse and he gave it to Charlie, as something unusual.\n-\n\nCharlie was very excited at having a horse. He learned to ride, and was constantly on his horse, going here and there.\n\n*Dashing horses running around here*\n-\n\nHowever, he treated the horse just as badly as he did all his other toys, and it soon started looking neglected and sick. For the first time in his life Charlie became truly worried.\n-\n\nHe loved the horse, and the fact that his family had offered to swap it for a new one meant nothing to him.\n\nOne day, while in the countryside, he saw a girl with a horse.\n-\n\nThe girl looked very poor, but the horse seemed happy and looked great.\n\nWondering how she had managed this, Charlie secretly followed them, watching everything they did.\n-\n\nFirst he followed them through the forest, where he saw that she never used the whip, and never hit the horse. This was the opposite of what Charlie had done to his horse, right from day one.\n-\n\nThen they came to the stable, and as soon as they arrived the girl fed and watered the horse. Then she carefully groomed it. Charlie was surprised. He'd never done any of that for his horse.\n-\n\nHe saw that the girl spent a lot of time giving care and attention to her horse, and that she did it all on her own.\n\nThis had never entered into Charlie's mind-\n-\n\nhe had always been too preoccupied with playing and having fun to look after the horse.\n\nCharlie wanted to change and become like the girl.\n-\n\nAs no one had shown him how to do this, he went over to her and asked her to teach him how to look after his horse. After her initial surprise, she happily accepted.\n-\n\nWith her he learned how to put care and effort into things, and that if you did so you enjoyed them much more.\n\nHe learned that you could be much happier\n-\n\nwith only a few special things that you truly cared for and looked after, than with thousands of toys that were only good for a short time and were then thrown aside.\n\nBut not everything was easy\n-\n\nCharlie also learned that the care put into these things was sometimes difficult, and it needed dedication of time and effort to do it well. So much so, that it even crossed his mind to go back to his old way of treating his horse.\n-\n\nHowever, when the horse finally recovered all its strength and splendour, that first ride, alongside the girl, made him so happy that a doubling of his effort would have been worthwhile.\n-\n\nAs a result, Charlie gave up constantly asking for new toys. Grateful to his friend, he gave her many of his own toys, and more to the children of the village.\n-\n\nHe only kept those few toys he really liked. And, just as he had learned with the horse, he set himself to repairing and caring for those toys, so he could really enjoy playing with them.", ""),
