        StaticBook("Illusion", "Lyu Elibar'acal", "Illusion\n                  ~@~\n         A study of magic\n        by Lyu Elibar'acal\n                  ~@~\nMany non-mages wonder over the spectacular spectacles that an Illusionist can create, I did so myself, at one point. So I set my mind unto finding out the mysteries of Illusion magic. Now, as with all arcane arts, a user of Sensory, or as some call it-\n- Light, Illusion users must have and maintain a connection to the void. I will not go over the process in which one does this, as this is a study of Illusion, not the void. Now, Illusion allows a mage to form a sensory stigma in the void and pull it\nthrough into the real world. As with all magic though, it has its limits. As my source of Illusion knowledge has explained to me, it must follow three basic guidelines or rules. The first being that it must be logical. This means that it must make sense,\nfor example, making a giant monster appear from nothing would cause the illusion to break more easily. The second rule, is that an illusion is just a stigma placed in the mind, and thus is not physical. At last the third and\nfinal basic concept is that you must have experienced the thing that you are illusioning. For example, you could not illusion a rabbit if you have never seen a rabbit. \n\nNow, that is enough about the basic rules, let us enter into the interesting realm of\nillusion and discuss the types of illusion that a mage can make. \nFirstly, there are glamours, when in one alters an already existing object with illusion, an example being changing one's eye or hair color, or creating a disguise.\nNext there are\nfigments, an illusion made entirely new, not altering somethig existing. An example of such would be illusioning a fog rolling in, or an animal running out of a bush.\nFinally, we have phantasms, the most comples and hardest to execute illusions, this is\nbecause they do not alter your external senses, but instead, they affect your emotions. The reason phantasms are so hard to do correctly is due to the fact that they must be logical, as all illusions must be, and thus must mesh well with the target's\npersonality, lest it break. Now, Phantasms are performed as such: An illusionist forms an emotion or emotional stigma and offers it to the target's mind, usually to exact a certain behavior. A phantasm will not be able to\neasily cause an Uruk to feel compassion, or a pacifist, rage. \n\nAnd with such, this tome comes to a close, but first, I shall like to thank my source for all such knowledge, Riondil Seni, he constanly poured information over me for this book,\nso I give credit where credit is due.\n\n\n\n                   ~@~\n                    Fin\n                   ~@~", ""),
        StaticBook("Illusion Theorum", "Lotha", "https://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/153423-the-theory-of-sensory-illusion/", ""),
        StaticBook("Immortal Blood", "Leyu", "Immortal Blood\nOriginally Written in Aegis\nThe moons and stars were hidden from sight, making that particular quiet night especially dark.\nThe town guard had to carry torchlight to make their rounds ; but the man who came to my chapel that night carried no light with him. I came to learn that Movarth Piquine co uld see just as well in the night as in the day - an excellent talent,\nconsidering his int erests were exclusively nocturnal. One of my acolytes brought him to me, and from the look of him, I at first thought he was in need of healing. He was pale to the point of opalescence with a face that looked like it had once been\nvery handsome before some unspeakable suffering. The dark circles under his eyes bespoke exhaustion, but the yes themselves were alert, intense , almost insane. He quickly dismissed my notion that he himself was ill, though he did\nwant to discuss a specific disease. \"Vampirism\" he said, and then paused at my quizzical look, \"I was told that you were someone I should seek for help understanding it.\" \"Who told you that?\" I asked with a smile. \"Tissina Gray\", I immediately\nremembered her. A brave, beautiful knight who needed my assistance on the subject of Vampirism. It had been two years, and I had not heard from her since. \"You;ve spoken to her? How is her ladyship?\" I asked. \"Dead\" Movarth replied coldly. And\nthen, responding to my shock, he added, perhaps to soften the blow. \"She said your advice was invaluable. She was tracking a Vampire\" a pause, \"It killed her.\" \"Then my advice was not enough\" I sighed. \"Who says it would be enough for you?\" \"I know\nthat if a student doesn't ask the right questions, the teacher cannot be responsible for his failure. I intend to ask you the right questions.\" And that he did. For hours, he asked questions and I answered. but he never volunteered any information\nabout himself. He never smiled. He only studied me with those intense eyes of his, commiting every word I said to memory. Finally, I could detect some weariness in his eyes. I would like to commit this tomorrow night. I must sleep and absorb this. \"You\nsleep during the day\" I smiled. To my surprise, he returned the smile, though it was more of a grimace. \"When tracking your prey, you adapt their habits.\" The next day he returned, with more questions. I told him of the Vampires of Eastern Malinor,\nthe Volkihar, paranoid and cruel, whose very breath could freeze their victim's blood in their very veins. I explained to them how they lived amongst the tree trunks, never venturing into the world of men except to feed. He left, and returned\nwithin a few days. True to his word, the man returned to my chapel. There was a fresh scar on his cheek, but he was smiling that grim but satisfied smile of his. \"Your advice helped me very much\" he said. \"But you should know that the Volkihar have an\nability you did not mention. They can reach through the bark of their trees without breaking it. It was a nasty surprise, being grabbed from behind.\" \"Terrifying\", I said, \"You were lucky you survived\", \"I don't believe in luck\" he replied, \"I\ncan land a thousand blows without losing my balance, providing I get the first strike\" \"So you must never be surprised\", \"That is why I came to you. Again, I answered his questions, they taxed my knowledge. There was much to cover. The Bonsamu, who\nwere indistuingishable from men except when seen by candelight. The Keerilth who could disintegrate into mist. The Yekef who swallowed men whole. The dread Telboth who preyed on children, eventually taking their place in the family, waiting\npatiently for years before murdering them all in their unnatural hunger. Once again, he bade me farewell. Promising to return in a few weeks. I nodded, knowing then that this man was on an eternal quest. He wouldn't be satisfied but with the\nbarest hint of how things were. He needed to know it all. He did not return for a month, and on the night that he did, I could see his frustration and despar, though there were no lights burning in my chapel. \"I failed\" he said as I lit a candle. \"You\nwere right. I could not find a single one.\" \"I brought the light up to my face and smiled. He was surprised, even stunned by the pallor of my flesh, the dark hunger in my ageless eyes, and the teeth. Oh, yes, I think the teeth definitely surprised the\nman who could not afford to be surprised. \"I haven't fed in seventy-two hours\" I explained, as I fell on him. ::He did not land the first blow or the last.\nOriginally written in Aegis by an author Unknown.\nRe-scribed in Vailor by Leyu'Maehr from memory.", ""),
        StaticBook("Improving Pasnia", "Karl Klargus", "Pasnia Improvements:\n1. Establishing streets and addresses for each house.\n2. Give each house, based on their street and address, a small 3 or 4 digit code that is put on the front of each house and their assigned chest in the tax room. Ex.- RS3 \n------->\n3. Start a light taxation system that is easy to pay but also earns the Duke a steady income. The houses do not vary too much, so only one tax bracket is needed. Maybe 25 Minas?\n4. Install wood flooring in houses.\n5. Purchase a cart that travels from\nPasnia to the Human docks (or another destination).\n6. Promote immigration to Pasnia via advertising flyers and the stewards travelling to other cities, speaking of Pasnia. Possibly start a program that would give new immigrants a small kit of starter >>\nitems. Ex.- 64 wood logs, 64 cobblestone, 32 hay bales.\n7. Put more effort in a guard/levy force that is ready to do guard duty and civil protection when needed.\n8. As immigration and regular travel to the city starts to pick up, keep the gate open>>\nat all times.\n9. Build more shop stalls, and start taxing stalls as well.", ""),
        StaticBook("In Captio Evange", "gaiusmarius8", "Awasasasasasasasasasasasasasasasasasas\n\n\n\n   In Captio\n     Evangellium\n\n\n\n                           asasasasasasasasasasasasasasasasasasa\nThere upon the horizon inlaid with stars, shall the night contort.\nThe constellations shall turn and in doing such, stars will abort.\nDrawn from the farthest quarter, shall ye see stars inbound.\nThe earth battered as if a whipping post, the brights will\nastound.\nWhen such happens, know ye are an ant to the coming end of days.\nInsignificant, pray ye cower and seek repent if you are that of evil ways.\nAs the clouds lay out like a carpet to welcome the cold. The sun shines no more,\nthe skin of animals will be sold.\nManifold, lo! The merchants will be no guardian with the End.\nNo layer of fat nor fur will cloister ye from the cold snap's bend.\nHuddle like shepherd's herd to whatever priest ye seek.\nThe ice will form on\nbone, frost on breathe, He permit ye not to speak.\nWhilst ye suffer the hindrance cursed upon ye, He will race.\nOnto the farthest Steppe to gather for himself a new face.\nWhereas his formers of pain and agony have done no more.\nThan to unite those\nwho shall face their End of Days nor.\nProvided him with nothing except brute force and magick.\nHe has sought a new servant, more cunning than fanatic.\nIn the land of false believers and true churches.\nHe will render the faithful helpless and\nHe searches.\nFor the liars to pit, one against the other, as he brings.\nThe galloping to trample and stampede, who sings.\nHis praises, a shriek that shall cleft the ears of lay and holy.\nThe hooves shall strike lightning and the death delivered\nwholly.\nThe false praying will be welcomed as he explains \"Come and See!\".\nThe first of His Vanguard, drained of blood and flesh festering flee.\nRiding out amongst ye crops, a faint gangrenous cloud to breathe.\n\"Come and see!\", the second shall gleam mockingly like ivory.\nHis appearance shall make ye eyes roll back, cursing to thy' falsity.\n\"Why should I be alive at such a time!\", as he scares curiosity.\n\"Come and See!\", the third shall ride forth from a plume\nof ash.\nThe most violent, mocking the ways of old, his horse's tail lash.\nBrings a crackle of thunder and a reviving flame at each sway.\n\"Come and See!\", the last of His Vanguard comes forth this way.\nAn arrogant display, paralleling the past\nKingdoms afore the End of Days.\nA white stallion dressed in gold, a rider most taunting.\n\nLexicon of Calamity", ""),
        StaticBook("In Sheep's Wool", "Nafis Yar", "On Wolves in Sheep's Wool\n\nAn Informative Pamphlet on the Adrian Dog and Others Associated to the Breed.\n-------------------\nWhen training man’s companion, one must start from an early age. You are to drill the sort of conduct you wish to see into them, much like you would do with a new soldier under your command or your own toddler once they begin to walk. If left alone, the\ndog becomes wild growing up. It will run amok in your household and eventually it will bite the master’s hand. While usually there re ways to remedy this after it has passed the threshold, this is perhaps the exemption where there is only one route to\ntake.\n\nReader, I ask you pay heed to the words I write in these darkest of times. Look to this particular breed of Canis that has long sincebeen allowed to run wild by humanity’s predecessor’s : The Adrian Dog. Do not put blame on those men who live on\nthrough the archives, for they had only shown mercy as taught by the Orenic Faith. But understand their mistake. I urge all readers to learn from it and do not repeat it or else the dreaded cycle of Crow continues.\n\nMy words mean nothing without evidence,\nand this I can provide, dear reader. The Adrian Dog is a carnivorous beast hell bent on the destruction of others for mere amusement. It is the thrill of the hunt that gives them activity.  If they have nothing to hunt, they grow restless. Cranky, much\nlike a baby whose sleep is disturbed. But this is no mere infant! It is a monster of a beast that will bite the master’s hand when least expected.\n\nThe Adrian Dog is one who subjugates the unwilling. Looking through the archives of Athera,\nwe witness this in practice with the genocide of the Waldenian people where my grandfather once hailed from. After the forefathers of the Adrians had robbed the throne from House Chivay, they proceeded to eliminate all those that opposed. Wishing to\nmaintain their vows to the overthrown Chivay, the Waldenian people refused to follow suit with the other Orenian vassals. This was never out of greed as it was  portrayed by Crow nor was the Konigreich of Aesterwald ever meant to be. It was through sheer\nloyalty to their vows that the Waldenian people refused to back down until the supposed “Protector of Humanity” Emperor Tuvya Carrion mobilized his armies alongside Uruks and threatened to bring Aesterwald down. Only then, to protect his people from the\ndestruction that would have came, did Konig Voron Rovin I (may he rest in peace) swear fealty. But how can one trust humanity to Crow when Tuvya rejected all peace talks and his only wish was to either subjugate or destroy the Waldenian people? When\nrebellion came and the forces of Renatus and Aesterwald defeated the Crow, the latter rolled on its back in submission. In turn, the forces of Renatus and Aesterwald spared the dogand allowed it to scamper off and lick its wounds. A mistake that haunts\nus today. Where are the Waldenian people now? Nearly all dead with few scattered about the realm. Men who wished to be free were hunted down and slaughtered after unholy forces wreaked havoc upon Vanderfell - obliterated by hell fire from cultist work.\nThese “protectors of humanity” did not come to the aid of men against this hell fire. Now why allow the dog to regain the reins of humanity?\n\nNow reader, you might bring up three questions. Are the Adrians not the same as the Waldenians and only wish to\nrule themselves? Why should we wage war on a people when we all carry the curses and sins of Iblees, is this not just a product of such? What makes the loyalists so different from the Adrians? I shall answer all these as well.\n\n1.) While both the Adrian\nDog and the Waldenians sought to rule themselves, the Waldenians had never tried making claim to the Orenian throne. In fact, they had pushed for talks of an alliance to answer Tuvya’s arguments of the need for a unified humanity.\nThe Crow is gluttonous however, and pecks at anything it finds edible. Even that of rotten flesh. Today, the Adrian Dog wishes to usurp its former master and seek the throne themselves. And the Adrian Dog will not stop there.\n2.) While it is true that we as mortals carry the affliction given by the fallen one, Iblees, the Adrians have surpassed any of its limits and have grasped the sins Iblees instilled in us as the norm. Something to be proud of. The Adrians side with\nbandits contrary to their faith and for too long all walks of life have cowered at the barbarism demonstrated by these untamed beasts. A unified front is the only answer to subduing the beast that has been created overtime.\n3.) Under Olivier I Ashford de Savoie, the realm of mortals has seen order and stability absent during the rule of Crow. To allow a just man to be usurped by the Adrian Dog is not only allowing a plague on to humanity, but on to all races across the land.\nAnd you, reader, ask why this is a plague on all? Before I continue, I admit I am not Orenian. I fight for Savoie though because should he be left alone in his just fight, we will all be next. There is a young lady I know back home who cannot fight and\nonly wishes to fish in peace and live modestly. A shepherd who is soon to be married to a woman born with no eyes at birth. Despite his economic status and her affliction, they seek happiness too. There are plenty more innocent people back in my home, but\nthe Adrian Dog is one with poor eyesight. It does not see soldier or child, elderly or woman. It sees prey. And it will rip the throats of any that is not them.\nRemember the Waldenians, who tried living just lives in peace but were near annihilated by the Crow. Remember the attempted genocide on Dwed by King Heinrik Carrion in the old lands of Anthos. Remember the raids you have all faced at the hands of the\nAdrian Dog teamed among banditry.\n\nAdrian Dog whispers ‘Mina-Mina’ to you like a dumb brain and jingles coin before you. But they will claim this back for war reparations in conquests they start against YOU.\nAnd we will fall one by one to the predator if we do not take a stand now. They will hide among your people disguised and take control from the inside. They assault holy men and seek blood for coin.\nTo those who answer this call to fight alongside me, then let me be the first to say it will be an honor to fight alongside you. The words I write are true, backed up by evidence in the history of the Adrian Dog. The enemies are snakes in the grass,\nand we must cut the grass to reveal their slither. They are dogs who have been disobedient for far too long and must be dealt with before they bite the hand that once fed them. They will not stop until they are the last in the realm.\nAnd the only way to deal with Adrian Dog is to put them down.\n \n-NY\n“To never to turn the back upon a foe” - Vander Code", ""),
        StaticBook("Ink Sacks & Bubb", "The Fable Maker", "================       Ink Sacks\n    & Bubbles\n================\n\n\nScribed by\n \n     The Fable Maker\n\n\n\n==================\nThey swim as fish do.\nGlide like birds do.\nSquirm as bugs do.\nGulp as men do.\n\nAll sizes and shapes.\nMaking little sound.\nAbsent of capes.\nIn seas they are found.\nSquids of battle,\nHardly cattle.\nTis loudly said,\nThat they fought the undead.\n\n\n*A painting of a battle squid is here*\nSquids of the air,\nCan it be true?\nDo they really fly?\nWell that's up to you.\n\n*An ancient painting of an Aegian river is here, a squid elaborately envisioned in the sky*\nSquids of great size,\nTis said a great prize,\nLays hidden within,\nCreating a din.\n\n*A hurried painting of a gigantic squid, surrounded by musical notes is here*\nThough passive most times,\nBe mindful of squid.\nFor in that which chimes,\nGreat treasure is hid...\n\n*The final page reeks with the ancient scent of fish...*", ""),
        StaticBook("Insane", "Isengar Brockfall", "A stor'eh yer want ey?\nWel' believ' me'h a've got te'h stor'eh fer ye!\n\nSom' 'f te'h pages are Extracts from ma'h real diary.\nOnc' upon a'h toime...\nWai'! was t'at too cleche?\n\nHmm lemme'h t'ink 'f somethin' mor' original.\nI wok' up?\nNae t'ats stup'ed\n\n\"Yer can go fock yerself\", she sai' when a'h asked ma'h gir' friend ter marry me'h.\n\nA'h look 'n shoc' as a'h was sayin' t'is tu 'er twin sister.\nMa'h gir' friend was be'ind ma'h.\nTe'h bitc' slaps ma'h in te'h face 'nd calls me'h a'h cheatin' bastard.\nA'h watched t'em dissapear 'n te'h distance as a'h was holdin' ma'h face.\n\"Yer feckin' bitc'\" a'h called out.\nT'en a'h felt a'h han' grip ma'h arm tight'leh, A'h turned me'h head 'round 'nd a'h saw te'h Menacin' face 'f 'n Orc, wel' Olog ter be'h exact.\nHe'h was 'bout 10 ft tall, 'nd a'h was 'bout 3 ft tall.\nLucki'leh a'h new Ologs wer' prett'eh dumb.\n\n\"Miz eatz latz\" he'h growled.\nA'h troied ter squirm ou' but 'e 'ad me gripped toight.\n\n\"WAI'\" a'h screamed.\n\"Halflin' 'ave diseases\"\n\"Dizeazez?\" he mumble'.\n\"Err, ye' we'h all bor' wit' Spidtrocious diseas'\" I 'ad a'h worried look 'n me'h face.\n\"Wutz tatz?\" he'h grumbled wit' slop comin' from 'is mouth.\n\n\"We' born wit' spiders insoide ah'll bell'eh, 'nd 'f yer eat me'h yer will get em!\" \n\nHe'h dropped me'h 'n me bac', but a'h got up straight awa'.\n\"Latz dizguztin'\"\nHe'h shouted.\n\n\"No' wil' yer eat me'h?\" \n\"Nub, latz weirdz.\"\n\nA'h 'ad a'h sloight smirk 'n me'h fac', 'nd watched 'm stomp of'.\nA'h read t'is book calle' err Into the nature a'h t'ink et was called.\nEt was 'bout t'is man 'o lived 'n te'h wild 'n went crazy afte' 'bout 16 days.\n\nA'h coul' du bette' a'h thoug' ter meself.\nBut ofcours' a'h ain't goin' ter bloddy wast' ma'h toime 'n goin' inter a'h jungle.\n\nIf a'h remembe' correct'leh a'h wante' ter go 'n a'h hike.\nBut nae on' woul' com' wit' me'h\nA'h ended up gatherin' 3 friends!\nOn' was Arthur Caulfield 'nd on' was Jessie Boatwrite.\n\nA'h new t'ese two fer quoite a'h while but neve' spok' tu em.\nA'h told em ter brin' food 'nd campin' equipmen'.\n\nAs we'h set ou' a'h glanced bac' at te'h temple on' las' toime.\n\nWe'h walked throug' thic' sludge 'nd swam across a'h murky river.\nWe'h settled down 'n 'n Extrordinar'eh fores'.\nTe'h sounds 'f birds tweetin' mad' et seem loike 'ome.\n\nJess'eh pitched the larg' tent 'nd Arthur ate his Caramel Cookies.\n\"Seems rather dull doesn't it?\" Arthur calle' out.\n\"T'ats te'h fores' fer yer\" a'h laughed.\nJessi'eh smiled but didn't sa' 'nything from t'at day on.\nWow lon' toime sinc' a'h wrote 'n ye.\nBee' sixteen days now, w'ere bloddy starvin'!\nDay 33\n\nAges sinc' a'h wrote 'n yer, te'h pages ar' turnin' tu a'h mossy yellow colour.\nDay 34\n\nWe'h need meat lads, pleas' we los' weight every singl' day.\nDay 47\n\n\nA'h feel t'em gettin' closer!\nDay 52\n\nWe'h ate jessi'eh, te'h poor lad 'ad te'h mos' meat 'n 'm.\nDay 71\n\nSo tired ma'h bodies shuttin' down, ah've been livin' off ma'h own shite ter stay aloive.\nDay 100\n\nTe'h voices get closer ter ma'h everyda', sayin'\n\"Kil' him\"\nA'HM NO' KILLIN' ARTHUR!!!\nDay 123\n\nMa'h pee tastes sweete' ever'eh day\nDay 131\n\n\nLoo' at Arthur, 'e looks so Juic'eh, so sweet so meeeaaattttyyy.\nDay 149\n\n\nJ'ost 'ad te'h best meal 'n me'h whole loife toime!\nDay 000000000000\n\n\n... Woy ar' t'ese dots so small?", ""),
        StaticBook("Insanity! vol 1", "Alstasia Tintia", "Hello hello! You grabbed this book? Perhaps your interested in knowing more about INSANE people, hmm? Or maybe your insane but wanna know why? heheheh. I cant quite laugh, cause im writing a book, but hey! Im crazy, I dont care. Anyway... lets go on,\nshall we?\n\nSome may say insanity is evil, but insanity in and of itself is... neutral... I suppose. Insanity isnt neccasarily evil, as a person who is insane isnt evil. Its the insanity that does it.\nLets actually talk about insanity now. Two types of insane people though.\n1. Revelers.\n\nPeople who revel in their insanity, not wanting to hide it, wishing to cause death and destruction to all whom they meet. These are the truly unpredictable ones.\n2. The hiding ones.\n\nTheir are some people who are insane, but they do a great deal at hiding it. Perhaps they are indeed good, but their insanity is brought out through... odd things. Could see something they hate, could just get tired of hiding, who\nknows? Oh! I do! hAHAhaAhahaAHAha!\n\nAnway, when you meet somebody who is insane... you should try to figure out what their insanity is, and try to use it to your advantage to escape!\n1. Random insanity\n\nThese are insane people who are totally random. They may kidnap ye, have a nice conversation for 30 minutes, then kill ya! Ya gotta figure out how to distract em, or use random logic to trick em!\n2. The murderous ones\nInsane people who will just straight up murder ya! Ya would best run from these people!\n3. Dillusionals\n\nSome people just have dillusions of grand things. Or they just see ferrets everywhere... FERRET! \n\nTry to tell them their is a fox or something behind them, when they turn around, they may just see one!\ncreated by their mind.\n\nAnyway, im not signing this, cause im also insane, a nice person though, but I dont want anybody finding me. \n\n-A Annonymos madman/woman\n\nDunno if I spelled that right! HAHAHAH!\n*A sketch of a sword with vipers slithing around it would be sketched here, quite detailed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Into Nature", "[Arthur Caulfield]", "Day one\n\nFound a small bag filled with what I believe are materials to make a tent. \n   They just lay on the ground inside cloud temple so I picked them up before someone else could. \n   A good idea I must say. Being outside for\nso long has left half my body numb from the bitter winds. \n    I had a place in mind when I set out to do this but I had forgotten it was so damn far. I may need to stock up on food as the animals around these lands are scarce.\nDay two\n\nOn my travels A nice inn keeper offered to give me an entire sack of cookies. Apparently no one likes caramel as much as I do because she was just giving them away. \n   Of course I gave her what I had on me though she refused\nat first. I will have no need for money anyhow, in the wild you can't barter coin with a bear or an orc. \n    This entry is being written rather quickly as night is falling and I need to set up the tent before I can not see. Tent pitching requires a large\namount of effort and that will be very difficult to achieve if I am so blinded my own hands are unknown to me.\nDay Three\n\nAt the last second I managed to pitch the tent. An hour later the wind would have knocked me off my feet but the tent is holding up just fine under the pressure. \n    I chose a piece of land facing the edge of a cliff. I have\nonly glimpsed what is down below but I could make out a farm and the smell of Billy Bob's taters floating up. \n   Of course that gives me no indication of where I am, those taters seem to be everywhere. I tried them once but they were too dry for my\nliking. The caramel cookies are my personal favourite. So far I have been working my way through the sack the inn keeper so generously gave me. I have consumed over twenty cookies and they still taste damn good.\nDay four\n\nToday I explored the area, knowing my temporary home was secure and the few items I brang safe in a chest. \n   On my walk I came across a peculiar building. Upon closer examination I found it was once a\nmage's guild. The place was old and the roof had collapsed leaving chunks of brick scattered on the floor. \n   My curiousity did get the better of me because I went inside, kicking the rubbel out of the way I found very few things left.\nA bed lay in a corner, the sheets so dirty I was suddenly relieved I have been sleeping on the grass for days. The windows were stained a sickly yellow and the walls had holes the size of my fist. \n   It was obvious a wizard had not cast a spell there for\nelven years. \n   I left soon after not finding much else of interest...except a button. It hung on the wall just inside and at first appeared to do nothing. But as I pushed it I heard a noise from far off. \n   I believe this button opens another part of\nthe tower but have yet to discover where. I may go back tommorrow to investigate. But for now I need my sleep, which could be hard to get with all the racket the monsters make outside.\nDay five\nWoke to the sounds of hissing. Some sort of snake if I had to guess. When I mustered up the courage to peek outside I saw nothing.      Still dark out so going to try to get a few more hours of sleep.\nDay eight\n\nI ran out of cookies. Rationing them didn't even occur to me until I realised I was almost out today. \n   Although i'm sure it will be fine. I haven't seen any animals yet but i'm certain I will soon.\nDay twelve\n\nI have a door\nCome on in\nWalk through the door\nTo come on in\nThey can't touch me\nIf I have a door\nBut you can come\non\nin\nDay sixteen\n\nThe animals are hiding. I just know it. I can hear them talking at night. What's the matter chickens, you chicken? I just wanna chow on chicken\nchow on chicken\nchow on chicken\nyummy yummy chicken\nDay nineteen\n\nWhat does the button do? I've been here for nine hours. Everytime I push it the sound is heard from a different place. \n    A secret passageway. Wizards hiding from me, gonna keep pressing this button till I find ya.\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShooof\nClick\nShoof <---W hy is thIs one DiffErent?\nDay twenty\n\nDandelions are starting to taste better.\nDay twenty-one\n\nHeard digging during the night. Dirt being shoveled at a rather slow pace. Soon after I heard heavy breathing. Didn't go outside to check.\nDay twenty-five\n\nI feel sick. Spent most of today throwing up. The cramps in my stomach are beginning to fade but as soon as I eat they will be back. \n   I just won't eat then.\nDay twenty-four\n\nI went outside to get some fresh air. Found a hole dug up to the left of my tent. A few bones lay in the dirt at the bottom but nothing else. \n   I believe it might be a grave. Not sure who would be digging those up though.\nDay twenty\n\nTo skin an animal, especially cow, in the most efficient way you must have the right knife. \n   Take my blade, take it take it take it take it. Ferrum blades cut through everything from carrots to human skulls.\nDay sixteen\n\nOooo what was that song. like dooodooodoooda da da. No no no no chorus was bigger higher louder with lute stuck in head like doo dadada didididi no not second di but more di than first\nDay twelve\n\nThe house for wizards is staring at me. It wants me to give it power. I tried to tell it I don't know magic but IT.WONT.LISTEN\n\nIt's in my head. \n\nMagic, gotta learn a spell to please it\nDay five\n\nI liked dandelion, lemon they tasted like lemon but now I like poppies because they taste red and that's better because I can get rashes with things that taste yellow.\nDay three\n\nMAgic, learning magic. Gotta go to Raine. Raine teach me magic. I can please the guild and they will tell me what the button does. \n   Going to Raine.\nDay one\n\nDandelions", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro. Alchemist", "Jistuma", "Forward:\n\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities, and traditions.\nChapter I: \n\nThe Recipe for a Good Alchemist.\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist: a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions. For those who wish to follow the noble path of an Alchemist, you must first\nconsider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\n\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize that it is simply an effort to save you.\nIf you do not possess these qualities, dear reader it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself and others. Now, allow me to go more in-depth about what these traits mean, in order of their\nimportance to an Alchemist: Patience. Alchemy, I'm afraid, is not a fast nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time for their elembic to boil so that the extract of your ingredients may be collected for use, or simply\nwaiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time it takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my opinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital\nto an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula consisting of 25 \"parts\":\n\n>7 parts waiting (brewing, waiting for the elembic's water to boil.)\n>5 parts setting up, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n\n>5 parts testing (making sure your potion works.)\n\n>3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n>3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and collecting the condensation using an alembic.)\n\n>1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n\n>1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely dull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated\nand rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish. So, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\nCreativity. Please note that I am writing here to explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something completely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in\nthe art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There comes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more\nexplanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their own extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This\nis much more difficult that it may seem... but I shan't go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but rather, an introduction to the science.\nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone who is impulsive and stupid... 'overly' enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of enthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience.\nEnthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of the list instead of the top, is simply because by\nreading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\nChapter 2:\n\nThe Life of an Alchemist\nThe Lifestyle.\n\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guilds need Alchemists, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the\nmost fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one location whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them.\nIn my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one's options before taking a job. This is not to say that an Alchemist /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choose a life of reclusion and\nintroversion--preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency. As an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and\nwounded. These paths will play  large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one who makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who creates healing serums as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are\nof no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of a guild. This is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing\nmuch of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could have a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however--and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of\nthe science--think of it more as a specialization. I, for example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds… even research companies.\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\n\nMany jobs seem to have a set \"morality.\" Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trustworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and is, much like\none's business opportunities dictated by the Alchemist's specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more \"evil\" morality, as they would likely find their work\nwith small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a \"good\" morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people. There are not set rules, of course, a healing\nAlchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is neutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\n\nThis section will be somewhat small, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist's abode will generally have only one constant: a lab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain\nan Alchemist's supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement… Well… The earth seems to be a bit more resistant to explosions than wooden or cobblestone walls.\nFarewell:\nI thank you, reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.\nAn Introduction to the Alchemist\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C1", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\nChapter One\n\n   A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped.\nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen.\nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll.\nIt had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones.\nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said.\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\nThen looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again.\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow.\nI then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\nAs I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house.\nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.”\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("John Cage's Song", "Heruza", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Vol. I", "Fjordin Sylver", "- Adventurers Journal of\nFjordin Sylver, Pioneer\n\n- Autobiographic Info\nName : Fjordin Sylver\nRace : Wood Elf\nAge (As of Print) : 117\nInterests (Professions) :\nWoodworking\nBlacksmithing\nLeatherworking\nEnchanting\nEntry 1 - It wasn't long after recollecting my conciousness that I realized I was in the grand Cloud Temple. I did not know, and still don't know, how it was I ended up there. Equally, I did not recall what it was my life skills were. Just my identity.\nEventually, I set about the infamous Stone Road. It wasn't a pleasant journey, prompting me to spend what few Minas I had on an elegantly crafted ferrum sword, but at the time I had few options. Despite its rough reputation, the trip was relaxing.\nI came across many establishments, cities, and sometimes the occasional trail which juts off into the wilderness. Unfortunately, the latter ended up being a cluster of trees shrouding tiny villages or Druid sanctuaries. I favored the Viridium Pub.\nShortly before sundown along the Atheran mainland there was a man clad in chainmail. He pressed himself onto me claiming to be a mercenary for a man by the name of Renatus. Thankfully, there was not a price hanging over my head, but a proposal.\nInstead of coming to claim my life which had only shortly ago been reintroduced to me, the man offered me a place within the mercenary group. Being a Wood Elf, I was naturally proficient in the usage of a bow, but with some thinking denied his offer.\nFrom there, the situation almost progressed into a physical altercation, but thankfully I managed to get away without any quarrel. From there I pressed into a pine grove, until eventually emerging before an archipelago off the coast.\nEntry 2 - Initially I overlooked the archipelago, and instead favored the idea of circumnavigating the Atheran mainland over the next few days. To my dismay no land seemed fruitful enough to settle in. That is when I made my return.\nI decided to take a swim out to the islands, which were a chunk of purity and paradise. There were chickens, laughably native to the salt-striken shores of that island cluster, but beyond that there was more. Sandy stones jutting out of the water.\nTo what I can recall, each one of these islands bore some kind of lore. For example : One of which featured a cobblestone pillar, intricately placed in the center. For all I know, that was the ancient burial site of a long-forgotten hero.\nBut those were besides the point. What struck me most was a large, imposing ship nestled against a grand mesa. It seemed mechanical in nature, possibly Orcish in design. However, there were indications of Dwarven engineering. Even now, who knows?\nIt took me almost a days worth of careful scaling and climbing to finally cross the mesa and its canyon, but at last I had made it to the fertile woodlands of what will soon be Sylverwood. The land was almost pure, untouched. Ripe for the taking.\nI knew once my eyes cast upon the clearing that this was my homestead. The Dark Oak forest signature to these lands provides a natural barrier between myself (now ourselves) and the outside world. This is the kind of isolation we strive for.\nIt took me a fair few seasons, but in some time I managed to construct myself a humble abode towards the edge of the clearing. Thankfully chickens were native species to this forest, and provided me with food throughout the winter.\nIt was The Deep Cold of 1484 when I had met Artemis Caryole. He worked, and as of right now still does work, at the Viridian Pub along the Stone Road. I had wandered there after leaving the Standing Inn. one night in search of food, but found more.\nEntry 3 - Inside the tavern, Artemis was tending to a young lady by the name of Marie. 'Till this day I remain wary of her seemingly good nature (the next time I seen Artemis, he also claimed she attacked him out of rampancy).\nApparently Marie was in search of food. The harsh winter winds made farming impossible, and I myself was barely clinging onto life. All I had were a handful of rotten potatoes I had stolen months prior from a farmer.\nArtemis guide us both to a grand Elven city, which was at the time controlled by the High Elves of Athera. We were greeted by a man at the gates, presumably an archmage of sorts, who accused Marie of being a Frost Witch.\nHaving done my research on said villainous creatures I can see how she could qualify for a Frost Witch. Her skin color was rather pale, and she was too kind-hearted for her own good. Apparently she also featured a split personality.\nRegardless, I along with Artemis defended Marie, and eventually took our leave with some food from a bin servicing the community with rations. It was on our return that I met Artemis' sister, Alarica, who in the warm season sold me two heads of cattle.\nThat being said, the winter did not completely thrash me into oblivion. Once The First Seed of 1485 hit I had begun work on a small plot of farmland. The trade was tricky to learn, but come the Sun's Smile I had become somewhat less inept.\nThat season, I had also met Kayla Denn. On my routine trip up to the Cloud Temple I had sensed a lost soul. For a day or so I found myself communicating with it by an unexplainable means until eventually it embodied itself.\nShe was lost, confused, and alone. In short she was just as myself when I woke up in the Temple. For a while we walked the Stone Road, and I had forged her a rudimentary set of chainmail along with a sword. The result was a fierce ally.\nIt didn't take much convincing for her to join me on my adventure back to the clearing. When we finally arrived she immediately praised the serenity. Eventually I offered her residence within my old shack, and started construction on The Hall.\nThe hall was never supposed to be a massive project. I wanted, and still want, to make an example of our simplistic and quaint lifestyle. Instead of being constructed out of solid stone bricks and expensive aurorum blocks, I had settled for less.\nThe main goal of my home was and still is the comfort of my guests. While there isn't much space for recreation I had managed to section off a tavern-like space for company. The idea is to provide food, drink, and comfort for a content stay.\nEntry 4 - The Amber Cold of 1484 was quite eventful, much like the previous winter. This one, however, was not quite as much a fortune. A Lord stumbled upon Kayla in the Dark Oaks, searching for his brother. He immediately interrogate her.\nShe had claimed to know nothing, which was the honest truth, but this was not enough for him. He instead wandered into the clearing and met face to face with me. I gave him a warm welcome, asking him what it was he wanted from us. Not a wise move.\nThe man immediately jumped to the bargaining of our land after interrogating us as to why it was we resided so far out. He promised us a plot on the mainland to continue our ventures under the protection of his armies.\nKayla had looked up to me as a leader, and therefore waited for me to make the tough decision. After biting my lip for several seconds, I had declined the offer. I told him I had hoped this wouldn't interfere with his ambitions, and he said no worries.\nFrom that moment on, all we did was worry. But it wasn't long before we decided it was time to solidify our foundations. To do so, we settled on the recruitment of more outsiders to shape our soon-to-be-society. That was when we met Dorian.\nCome The Deep Cold, a man by the name of Dorian Hunter came charging into the clearing bow in hand. At first I was suspicious, but permit him to set up a tent outside my Hall. He seemed to me a skilled warrior, which I admired.\nIt was at that point we began to warm up. I lit a firepit outside his shelter during a blizzard, just to provide comfort for the both of us while we sat outside and got to know one another. It didn't take much convincing for him to join on my quest.\nI began construction of a house along the river bank later that season. It wasn't until the beginning of Snow's Maiden that I finished it in its entirety. Furnishings, workstations, and intricate craftsmanship of a Wood Elf. What more can someone ask?\nEntry 6 - Not long after the completion of his home, Dorian returned to the clearing (now unofficially called Sylverwood) for the first time since The Deep Cold. However, he had brought with him a pair of travellers. More specifically... magical bards.\nTheir names were Norgaladir and Lizzy. Norgaladir claimed to be te guild master, who took an interest in music (obviously) and Divine Magic. All he asked for was a 20x20 plot in cubic meters. With some hesitation I accepted, but not for the music.\nBeing well versed in the history of Aegis I know very well it was overthrown by the Undead. I do not want Sylverwood to suffer the same fate. Those who are skilled in Divine Magic can help protect Sylverwood from the Undead scourge if it hits Athera.\nEntry 7 - It's now the time of The Grand Harvest, 1486, and everything is going... accordingly. Dorian and Kayla find themselves at one anothers necks. Sometimes I swear they are cosntantly waltzing a dance of death. Those hopeless romantics... heh.\nAside from that, I have finished construction of a few more homes. These will eventually work in sync on the Community Farm. This will be the sole provider of wheat, cacti, sugarcane, pumpkins and melon.\nA typical Sylverian (denonym for Sylverwood citizen) will consist of wheat, beef, and fish products. This is to minimize the amount of farm land required in favor of cattle. In addition, cattle provide us with access to an important industry.\nThat industry? Leatherworking. A very simple craft, yet one that most races have the potential of being adept in. Leatherworking is a powerful craft, allowing one to manufacture armor beneficial to archers, and clothing to wear into the streets.\nIn order for one to obtain leather one needs cows. In order for one to breed cows one needs wheat. That is where the chain of supply comes in. The farmers provide wheat, wheat provides cows via breeders, and cows provide leather via leatherworkers.\nI myself have picked up this craft in favor of the uses it could provide me as a potential Lord. Having power means having an army and the arsenal to crack down on the opposition. Leatherworking will allow me to equip my soldiers and myself properly.\nLeatherworking aside, the town square has started taking shape. While not exactly constructed from the ground up I have taken the liberty of laying down the roads. My only concern is the fact it was constructed to the far right of the clearing.\nThis means an awkward, empty gap will be left in the left side of the clearing. My current idea at fixing this is to create a castle of sorts befit for me. While I am fond of having a small hall like the one I currently own, I feel it won't do forever.\nI am looking forward to the completion of the Guild Master's building. So far it looks a bit iffy, and I fear it will not bode well with my Wood Elf architecture. Regardless I will let him continue his work and see where it takes him.\nAside from that, I paid my semi-seasonal trip to the Cloud Temple. No bandit encounters, thankfully, but I did come across a bar fight in the Standing Inn. Met a Wood Elf by the name of Sanora who seemed to be interested in the ways of Earth Magic.\nAfter the bar fight, which resulted in the slaughter of two Uruk, Sanora and I parted ways (she went to a Wood Elf \"city\" to study if the political system has improved). She promised me she'd send word if she was disappointed with her findings.\nShould she dislike what she sees, she will potentially become a Sylverwood citizen. How grand! Further into my travels, I met another Elf. This one, however, was a Dark Elf by the name of Domalvia.\nThe circumstances of us getting to know one another were interesting. I found her buying a few loaves of bread from a dealer up at the Temple, so I offered a sack of the stuff free of charge. She was very thankful, and I said I'd lead her here someday.", ""),
        StaticBook("Juliet", "Sul'leyu 'Solar' Ashspear", "Oh Romeo, oh romeo? why the fuck did you kill yourslef you dumbass bitch for fucks sake you couldve waited for like 5 seconds but no you killed yourself and now im stuck here all alone thanks to you dumbass\nch. 2\n\nok so today i was sad BUT NOT REALLY CUZ ROmEO IS AN ACTUAL BITCH, anyway. and this cute guy comes up to me and is ike \"hey chica whats poppin\" and i said \"nothing much, hbu papi?\" then it went like \"oh ur hot\" and then like \"oh ye date me\"\nch. 3 \n\nok so the guys name was actually chip so chip and i went on a trip AND HE GOT US FUCKING LOST so im sitting in this cheap ass tent waiting for chip to figure out where the hell we are\nch. 4 \n\nso he finally came back, we're home fucking finally \nim mad at chip for kidnapping me like ffs ? anyway i forgive him tho like he's still hot\nch. 5 \n\nso i think this is the last time because its too much working writing this like bitch aint nobody got time for that anyway me and chip got married and he's still super hot so like yea bye thanks for reading buy on ebooks", ""),
        StaticBook("Junk Mail", "Thickfeet", "Is your fishing pole coming up short?\n\nCasting your line and finding nothing on the end?\n\nIf you feel like you aren't catching fish like you used to this is for you.\nNo longer do you need to train to be a master of baiting alone.\n\nFind Freud Ian \"Frodo\" Slipweed in Willow Hollow.\n\nHis patent pending Salmon Oil is a secret family recipe guaranteed to restore your\ntacklebox to its former glory!\n\n[Tiny paragraphs of warnings and disclaimers fill the rest of the letter.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser's Love", "High Dictator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    The Kaisers Love\n\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Ministry of Truth\n\n\n\n==================\nThe people of Al'Wakhrah slept soundly in their beds when the Ghouls attacked. The three Ghouls stood firm at the entrance to the city, looking for easy targets to consume. Larry Kringle, an Elven officer within the Reich Ministry of Truth, sounded the\nalarm. The Kaisereich answered. The good denizens of the Hallowvale Company answered the call, headed by the Qalasheen Champion of the Hallowvale and the Kaiser himself. The company created a line of Elves and Humans alike at the gate.\nThe three Ghouls would be no match for the Kaisers finest! The elite troops pulled out their aurum blades and laid waste to the evil creatures where they stood. They never even reached the steps to Al'Wakhrah. The Champion and the Grand Conservitor worked\ntogether to take one of the ghouls head clean off! The Kaiser himself slashed with no mercy, finally impaling an aurum dagger int he eye socket of one of the animated corpses. The last was slow, behind the other two. This nightmarish creations of Iblees\norigin were hacked down by an unknown citizen of the Kaisereich. The unknown solider of Good. The Kaiser, under instruction from a wandering Cleric, ordered the building of a fire to burn the bodies of the fetid Ghouls. The group rallies, all lending a\nhand to rid the world of the monstrosities. \n\nThe Kaiser had few words for the valiant group that night, but offered his humbles thanks to all those who helped secure the safety of the children inside the walls of Al'Wakhrah. His humility\nwas unexpected, and took the group by surprise. It was then that they realized, we as an Empire, as Vanderlorians, are stronger together than we are apart. The Humans and Elves worked hand in hand, under the grace of God, and were victorious.\nThe Kaisers strongest words were the quietest spoken. \n\n\n     HEIL VANDALORIA\n     HEIL ROVINKIN\n     HEIL DECIMUS\n     HEIL TRUTH", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Varak Notes", "Archmage Crumena", "Research notes on the Kal'Varak by the enlightened Magi Auvreaeath in Asulon. No date available.\nRescribed by Arch-Mage V. Illwindior on the 2nd of the First Seed, 1473.\nThe Kal'Varak is an ancient, crystalline artifact dug up by the dwarves of Karik. J ust prior to their unearthing of the hibernating dragons. The properties of the c rystal are strange, it seems to be nexus of the magic, but no mage has so far\nmanged to manipulate it. The remebrancers studied the artifact at great length, stori ng it in their enclave in Karik. They never managed to find out exactly what the Ka l'Varak does, but they did mange to get it to transmute pieces of gold into strange\nelixir that gave the user resistance to fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kane's diary 1", "Alfric Kane", "[!]\nIf you read this, this is Kane's diary/note book.\n*Inside the first page would be a black lock of hair with the description saying*\n\n\"Adam's Hair.. the only thing I have of his left.\"\n*The second Page would have another lock of hair, this time brown with the description*\n\n\"The one I loved the most.. although she made/makes me feel pain I can't throw away she still ment the world to me\"\n\"The year was 1629.. the day my boy's life was taken by my once loved wife.. I always will remember running my hands through his hair.. the boy had lots to live up to back then.. but my wife couldn't keep up with him.. bless his heart he was only 3 when\nshe killed him.\n\n[!] The writing would stop and a hand drawn picture is displayed below with a small button glued next to it. The picture would show Kane's boy Adam.", ""),
        StaticBook("Katari", "Sarrion", "Kitari the Wise\n\nAge: Unknown\n\nRace: Elf Origins\n\nBlack hair and beard, typicaly standing at avarage look and heights. Katari is known as one of the older mages and one of the more elegant teachers\nof the land, as he's had many students in the arts of evocation.\n\nMagics Known:\nArcanism\nMental Magic\nTelekenesis\n\nCan Teach:\nFire Evocation\nLightning Evocation\nGroups Associated with:\n\nUnknown Origins.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keys", "Murdervish", "Call into rains of the cloudless,\nAim towards aches of the lye,\nEast is the face of the faithless,\nSand and the snows do collide.\nAsh had feln down upon our heads,\nReds have been the skies,\nSaffron of silks had tied to us,\nHills had all crumbled to cries.\nInvert the face of the faithless,\nFall into sands by the snows,\nTrek into deserts most dangerous,\n ((The last line of the poem is blacked out.))\nClo Abfkxiq, tel qxrdeq jb ql yb xyib ql obxa.\nClo Kxccld, tel qxrdeq jb ql yb xyib ql qefkh.\nClo Flxkkfp, tel qxrdeq jb ql yb xyib ql pjfib.\n2-9-18-4\n3-1-12-12\n0-4-0-6\n12-1-20-0\n19-5-22-5\n14-0-20-23\n15-0-6-9\n22-5-0-19\n5-3-15-14\n4-0-9-14\n20-5-18-22\n1-12-19-0\n12-9-22-9\n14-7-0-19\n8-18-5-23", ""),
        StaticBook("Killin' a troll", "Jentos", "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n     Killin' a troll\n\n\n  By Jentos Adam, last representant of the house of Blackwood.\n\n\n\n\n\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\"Dear reader, in this book you shall learn to: recognize, flee and kill a troll.\"\n\nIntroduction\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\"Troll. Nasty, cruel and stupid creatures capable of destroying whole towns, And fierce war-beasts.\"\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\nWere to find a troll?\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\nTroll's can be found about everywhere in these wild lands. From the frozen dwarven plains. To the heat of the Caliphate!\"\n\n\"Troll's like to live in unforested mountainous regions, dark caves in the\nmountains. Or in a big clearing in the forest.\"\n\nRecognizing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxWho has never pictured a troll? Big ugly figure walking in the forest? But the're are alot of different types of orcs and sub-trolls like half trolls half\nmen!\"\n\n\"Trolls can vary from 8 feet when young to a giant 20 feet tall!\nThey have a relative big orc like head with a few men-like features.\"\n\n\nFleeing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxRunning away from a\ntroll in a rather forested area is easier than in a mountainous or flat region.\"\n\nTactic's: \n\"If you find yourself in a forested or near a forested region, your best bet is to simply go we're the tree's are smaller so you can slow the troll\nand get out of its reach.\"\n\n\"Hiding in a cave isn't a good idea, a hungry troll is apt to wait a long time to be able to get his supper (especially if it's the trolls own cave!).\"\nKillin' a troll!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"In this final section, you will learn how to \n\n       Slay\n      -----\nThese mighty creatures!.\n\"The troll's weak spot, (like many other beats) are the eye!\nUnfortunatly it is easy to see that being able to get a good shot at them isn't easy.\"\n\n\"The trick is to, hack the legs until it falls, wait t'ill it reaches down or bend or simply attack it\nfrom a good height!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"On this. I say to you! Have thy luck I never had!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Kira Winterleaf", "Kale le Prevost", "Grand Hospital\nHead Jaraah Kale \n\nPatients Name: Kira Winterleaf\n\nAge: 8\n\nRace: Wood Elven\n\nGender: Female\nCondition/Injury:\n\nA regular eye appointment set up via. bird.\n\nTreatment Plan:\n\nGave the typical eye exam resulting in a near sided blurriness which resulted in the use of glasses.\nDoctor Who Treated the Patient:\nHead Jaraah Doctor Kale\n\nCost: 10 minas\n\nDate: 1553 of the Cold Winter, 13th\n{!} Kale signature would be written here on this last page\n\n~ H.J. Kale le Prevost", ""),
        StaticBook("Knowledge", "Mr. Black and Stronghold", "Cactus Green - 6M\nBlack Cactus - 16M\nBlue Cactus - 22M\nPure Quartz - 12M\n\n^^^ Base Prices ^^^\n\nThese prices are 20% cheaper than our closest competitor's.\n\n\n-------------->\nSelling:\n\nWe want exactly the amount of minas indicated in our prices back per unit of drug sold. However, you can sell the drugs at a higher price and keep any profits you make. So if you sell cactus green for 12 minas, you get to keep 6.", ""),
        StaticBook("L3: Cervitaur", "Athe'lor", "I was first introduced to the Cervitaur language rather recently, today being 16th of The Deep Cold, 1491, by a Cervitaur nonetheless. For some reason, Plazea (The Cervitaur) was within Haelun’or but unable to speak Common, only another-\nlanguage foreign to me. I then took it upon myself to teach the half-man, half-deer how to speak Common, at least enough to be able to translate words for me.\nThis sparked our ‘friendship’ as I encouraged Plazea to translate words from Common into Cervitaur, although clearly after a few days the creature no longer wished to translate and would avoid the topic. Even still, I believe with the words I was-\ngiven are enough to for me to finish translating, and I shall explain why. Not only is Cervitaur similar to Mori’Quessir in the manner that the sentence structure is nearly identical to Common, but there is a pattern to the letters.\nMany times did I hear Plazea say the word ‘good’, or as it translates into Cervitaur, ‘Ruun’. Yet, on more than one occasion, did I hear Plazea say ‘Guun’. Was this mispronunciation? My question was answered-\nafter Plazea told me the word for language, ‘Relriera’. However, in another sentence the creature used the same word, but said ‘Lelriera’. Do you notice the pattern, reader?\nLanguage, Lelriera; language, relriera. Good, Guun; good, ruun. I believed the key to unlocking this language was in the difference between capital and lowercase letters, and my hypothesis was correct. When a letter is capitalized, it remains the same.\nHowever, in Cervitaur when a letter is lower-case, it may turn into a variety of things (or may also stay the same). The next few pages will include capitalized words, and lowercase words I have translated.\nIrrar = yes [] Yar\nLu = no [] Nu\nHarru = hello/Hello\nRuunfirra = goodbye [] Guunfirra\nFirra = bye [] Birra\n\nRserr = grass [] Gserr\nLlruwas = flower [] Fruwas\nWedas = water/Water\nSil = run [] Ril\nRunadainar = sometimes [] Sunadainar\nAir = is [] Ir\nIlnasrdeln = understand [] Ulnasrdeln\nRelriera = language [] Lelriera\nErru = also [] Arru\nEln = and [] Aln\nRdillll = stuff [] Sdillll\nFuuc = book [] Buuc\nRuun = good [] Guun\nFen = bad [] Ben\nCairr = kill [] Kairr\nAyair = evil [] Eyair\nAs the reader may be able to tell, translating from Cervitaur to Common is not all that difficult, you must merely know which letters replace which (and only lowercase letters are replaced). If you were to write a sentence in Cervitaur in all capital-\nletters, yes, it would seemingly translate into the exact same thing; the trick solely lies in being able to replace lowercase letters with other lowercase letters. If one seeks conversation in Cervitaur, you are encouraged to speak with the author.\nI now tuck my words to sleep, and pull the blanketed leather cover over them. Sweet dreams; may you find yourselves in the hands of those who pursue knowledge. \n\n-Athe’lor", ""),
        StaticBook("Lady Ceona", "Colbert", "Your holy Lady Ceona, I'm writing this to let you know that I'm resigning from the reigment, if I am forced at the point of a weapon to call my holy Lady Ceona a lady, then she should know that is not ladylike at all, for that is far from ladylike and is\nmuch more forceful, if you were a proper lady, holy Lady Ceona you'd have learned that the best way of coercion is by words, not blade, and for that, for your actions, for your dull tougne, and for your ability to give up easily in coercing someone, I am\nleaving this town, and its residents behind, for I am needed elsewhere.\n-You know me\nPS: Hurt Garoll because of this and I really won't like it.\n((OOC)) There's no signature, even if the book thing normally has one, NO METAGAMING ME\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nYou're a whore's daughter who married into her position who has an inferiority complex that they need everyone to call them by their rank, I wish for you to return to your proper trade, your mother's trade, for that is where you work best.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lady's Diary", "Unknown", "My first saint day in Oren I was able to meet up with my dearest brother. I met my cousins and my uncle as well, though during the most darkest of days. \n\nHamelin took me to the palace and we were greeted with my brother holding a head of a man. He was\nto speak to the Emperor about things which I am not sure of. We waited until time passed that was rather far too long. \nRushing down the corridors we managed to get to the scene of an assassin who sliced the back of the Emperor. \nFalling, he tried to\nmuster up his strength as my brother Jon and his men quickly jumped into action. So much blood was spilt...it was no place for a Lady. Uncle and my cousin escorted me after they took the Emperor's body.\nWe went home, shaken up and in grief. My brother\ncame home later in blood of a elven. He seemed rather...distraught about everything. All I could do was encourage him. May God be with the house of Horen and may God be with us all.\n\n7th of The Amber Cold, 1585.\n       -Katherine de Savoie\n4th of Malin's Welcome, 1586\n\nSeven skies!\nSo much has happened.\nJohn Owyn is dead, along with John Agustus. Now it is Philip who is Emperor. Yes, the one that the late John Owyn said that Philip and I would be a match. GOD help me.\nMy brother plans to follow through with those plans and so I must get a wedding dress. I am terrified to be honest. \nI know I should be brave. I am a de Savoie. This is not the de Savoie way.\nNow to plan for something else...though his uncle is quiet charming, I must admit...just brother said he isn't Important. And brother is right all the time. \n\n        -Katherine de Savoie\n15th of Snow's Maiden, 1588\n\n I never had once hated anyone in my life until now. Lady Anselm. I shall remember that name until I die. Whether she is to pass or not by then, I willl remember. She fears I would use the Emperor, to coy with him and fill him\nwith fantasies...she is the worst. I would never do that to the Emperor, to Philip...I love him too much to want to harm him even if I was ordered to by himself! I just wanted to invite Lady Eva and her son to a concert...since I was begining to like\nher. I am not even sure what she thinks of me now. Seven skies...Creator save me...save me from this evil woman. I am prepared for war, for taking care of our children, for even dying for Philip. I would do anything, but\nI need strength to pass this. I cannot stand hypocrites...cannot stand them at all. *Wet marks splattered across the page as if they were tears and smudged some of the words.* \n        Katherine G. de Savoie\n16th's of Malin's Welcome, 1588\n\n Two more months until I am to be wedded to Philip. My heart feels like it is going to burst ever since he...held me so tight in his sleep...the way our bo- no, no this isn't decent. I shouldn't have played the game\nwith him...but what else where we to do while under attack? My heart cannot stop beating like a bunch of bees in a bee hive. He is even letting me use his bath before we wed! Oh seven skies! I just have to survive until the wedding night. For him, for me,\nand for us.\n\n\nKatherine Gabriella de Savoie\n23rd of The First Seed, 1588\n\n Rumors again...he doesn't believe me...it is pointless...I just want to be alone...\n\nKatherine Gabriella de Savoie\n24th of The Deep Cold, 1588\n\n Philip and I did not marry. I am glad, for I am free now. However, I  will never forget the names Lady Anselm, Lady Lydia Locklear, and Miss Charlene. Their bloodlines will never cross my own. Brother is going to send me\nto Leopold's lands. I fear he will do something rather foolish. Then again, I...well may do something foolish as well. \n\nKatherine Gabriella de Savoie\n1st of Sun's Smile, 1589\n\n It has been a while. A lot of things changed. I've made gifts for family and friends and have been giving out gifts to people of stuffed animals and makeup to women. I...gave Arminius a hand made waterskin.\nJokingly, I embroidered a potted red tulip into it since a few months ago he had given me a potted red tulip. The gift he had given me was something I cannot even fathom still...it was beautiful. His family's library.\n...Creator help me. I am unsure of what these feelings I have right now...unsure what to do with them. Though when I am around him, I feel safe. He hears me, and I hear him. I want to wrap him in my arms and tell him everything is alright. To flood his\nwoes with happiness and the sun as he has done so for me. I thought I was in love with Philip...but this...this man, Arminius von Aesterwald...he is my friend...my dearest friend that I cherish and l---. *The three letters would be blacked out with a few\nink splotches as the correct three letters were placed to spell out 'like'.* I can't even believe I suggested that we should marry! What has gotten into me? I...should speak to brother soon.\n\nKatherine Gabriella de Savoie\n[ The diary ends here, droplets of blood on the pages. ]", ""),
        StaticBook("Last Goodbye", "Laura", "Dearest mother,\n    I could not stand it any longer. The pain of losing her, the heartwrenching mornings and evenings lying in that bed, spent in that room, with that crib, the crib that held those twins. I could not stand the nights alone, the awful\ngrief. I thought that I could get over her. I thought that I could make myself not love her. I was wrong. It only got worse. I told Treemma to be with Katelynn. I want her to be happy, I want her to be so happy, because she deserves it, she does. I know\nthat I'm not a monster, or an abomination, or an abberation, or anything like that. I'm a person, a real person. I have emotions. I have heartbreak. So, mama, please do not blame Treemma for this. She doesn't deserve the guilt, because she is not at fault\nhere. I'm sorry that I can't be around longer, but I'd only get more and more low. Please don't lose yourself over this. I love you, and I love dad, so, so much. You two mean the world to me, you mean as much to me as Treemma does. Please be happy for me.\nI've left this existential nightmare for a better world, a better life. Who knows what awaits me next?\n\n[!] The ink on the following pages seems more recent than the last. [!]\n\nI hate to leave a mess, but I can't stand it\nanymore. The pain is too much. I have to do it now, or I'll lose my mind. Goodbye, mama, and goodbye, papa. I love you both more than anything. We'll meet again, someday, somehow, I'm sure of it. We can all be happy then.\nInfinite love,\nLaura", ""),
        StaticBook("Laureh'lin 'Law'", "Salendys", "\"It's a long story. But basically, I was meant to be 'arrested' and handed over to the Sirame. I just willingly turned myself in. However, they did not give me a trial. In fact, Artmimec specifically rigged his own 'legal' system so there would be none. -\n- No trials. Ever. At all. For no one. Which basically allows the 'guards' to also act as judges and sentencing 'criminals'. Naturally, their guards are crooks and corrupt beyond redemption, so they hand out punishments on the spot and as they see fit.\nIn essence, they can gut you for stealing a loaf of bread. You can imagine that the word \"justice\" has a very different meaning in Laureh'lin.\nIn my case, Artimec gave the order to cut my tongue off. They ripped it off with glowing red hot tweezers.\nJust for their own sick amusement. Then they shoved an equally hot metal rod into my mouth. And even after all that, they refuse to lift my banishment and attack me on sight.\"\n\"I was 'punished' for crimes I did not commit. Denied a fair trial, treated with less dignity than a mule. All the while having to endure the twisted and sick fetishes of the ones that dare call themselves the upholders of justice.\"\n\"What good are laws when the ones who write them are corrupt and care only for their own gain? Who does one truly serve by remaining lawful and enforcing unethical regulations meant not to protect and help govern the people, but to punish those who dare\nstand up to a corrupt system?\nThis is the Law of Laureh'lin. \nSeek not for justice here, for it's a word with no meaning to those who live here.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin: Vol I", "Aluuvia", "=======================          A Tale of\n          Laurelin\n Vol I: Mayctor's Folly\n=======================\nLaurelin was once the capital of Malinor, home of all Mali in the ancient realm of Aegis. There were other settlements which were made and grew over time, such as Ravenhold, but most Mali choose to reside in Laurelin for many reasons.\nThe city had everything a Mali could want or need; Nestled in the woods south of the King's road, there was not a place there untouched by nature's hand. The Elves have walls, though they rarely needed them, and home not only on the forest floor,\ncovered by crisp fallen leaves in autumn and flowers in the springtime, but also up above, nestled within the branches of the trees themselves, though unobtrusively.\nThere were creeks and waterfalls as well, that babbled and bubbled their way through\nthe woods.\n\n   But what the Mali of Laurelin benefitted from most was not her tall trees, her wide canopies, or her babbling brooks. It was her people. In those times, Malinor was guided by a council of princes, and one\nnot unfit for it's job. The High Prince, Native, and Archdruid Swifty took care of the trees and land that Laurelin sat upon, nurturing the trees and flora. The lower Princes and Princesses took care of Laurelin's citizens; Prince Toren made sure the\nnation's food supplies never ran low, and Princess Danie addressed the concerns of citizens. Relations with the other nations were peaceful and well taken care of by High Diplomat Lafthi and the diplomats who worked under him.\nBut this book is not intended to regale us with a tale about the peaceful, serene days of Laurelin. It is about the time when monsters crept from the woods, when blood was spilled and lives lost. When darker times came, the Elves looked to two group\nfor their protection; The Pathfinders, lead in name by Lord Blackthorn, though in reality by another, and the Sentinels, lead by High Guardian Mayctor.\n\n   High Guardian Mayctor was not your typical Mali, as he was of a logical\nsort and not given to flights of fancy or careless deeds in the least. No, despite being a Mali'ame, his movements and thoughts were just as calculated as the most studious of Mali'aheral. All he did was carefully considered first, for each act to him\nwould affect the future of Malinor and of Laurelin. He was the one who insisted on the walls of Laurelin and upon her gates; He was the one who insisted upon the river that flowed about the walls, acting as a moat, and upon the working drawbridges.\nThe Elves were immortal, this much was known; But Mayctor worried if they were truly eternal. Though long-lived, their population was a mere fraction of that of neighboring nations, of Kal'urguan or Krugmar or Oren. If the other nations turned\nagainst Malinor, Lafthi's political maneuverings would not save them. Only sword and shield, bow and arrow, power and prowess.\n\n   He urged the High Prince to shut them off from the other nations, worried their brutality\nand filth would infest the Elven people. But the High Prince would hear none of such outrageous suggestions. He demanded Lafthi send spies to the other nations, to watch for threats, but was swiftly refused by one not wishing to jeopardize the\nalliances and relationships carefully crafted between Malinor and the other nations.\n\n   Mayctor seethed for some time, unable to think of a solution to his dilemma. He could not bear the thought of his people suffering a foul fate,\nbut he could not think of a manner in which to guarantee them their eternal Princedom.\n\n   That is until one day he came upon a single book, hidden in the library of Malinor. Old and dusty, the thing had not been touched in many a decade.\nMayctor took the tome in his hands and within it found the answer to his dilemma and much, much more.\n\n   Malin was absent from the lands, as were the other Brothers, as was the Creator and all other divine presence.\nDevoid of anything else to turn to, Mayctor made a sacrifice for his people that would stain the history of the Mali for the rest of eternity.\n\n   For his people, or perhaps, for himself, Mayctor sold his very self to the Fallen One.\nLong before the Undead rose, Mayctor had given all of his self save his soul in dedication to the Fallen One, and even that last remaining bit would eventually fall to Iblees as well.\n\n   For many years Mayctor toiled in\nsecret service to Iblees, gathering but a scant few fellows to his side. \n\n   And while Mayctor had entered the pact with the best interests of the Elves of Malinor forefront in his mind, this did not last. His ideals eaten away\nby corruption and taint, which fed upon the once noble Mali like the maggots that would later have at his rotten corpse of a body. \n\n   Paranoia and hatred over took him, and by the end, he would care not for the Elves, who in his mind,\nwere the ones to betray him first. \n\nMayctor's desires were twisted, blackened as his heart. And as much as he had once sought to save Laurelin, he soon sought to destroy it.\nAnd so it was.\n\n\nIn due time the full fury of Iblees would be unleashed upon the realm of Aegis; A boiling pot suddenly overflowing, while the Mali had had warning, it was not heeded fast enough.\nThe full power of Iblees unleashed, and Laurelin was burned to fine ash, nothing of her left in the end but dust. Though many grabbed what they could to flee to the nearby portal leading to the Verge, much was lost in the carnage, and untold lives.\nCenturies later and Malinor still endures; But when Laurelin fell there was a great shattering, and never again has any government or nation of Mali ever been able to amount to the same unification as Malinor once had.\nIn the end, Mayctor sought to bring about the end of the Mali, despite having once sought nothing but their safety.\n\n   And in this goal, he may very well have succeeded, for as the centuries drone by, the Mali fail to progress.", ""),
        StaticBook("Learn to Read", "Saviordude", "=(^x^)= Cat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= Cat in hat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o( Cat in hat, with a bat.\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o(\n\\(     )/ Fat cat in hat, with a bat.\n*This book continues on like this for several hundred pages, allowing one to pick up the written word with the magic of Rhyme and Pictures*", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Rianna Shah", "*A well written document was stacked atop a collection of books which had been left neatly for collection.*\n\"Sharing knowledge is something I am very interested in.\n\nI had noticed your store on visit to Alexandria, and wish to contribute.\n\nThese are from my personal collection, and I do not have copies. So please\ntake good care of them.\n\nSigned, Rianna Shah of Haria.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Kale", "Hileia'elr", "Dear Kale,\n\nLike I said, I planned on quitting my job anyhow. My original plan was to pursue my life of research, to spread knowledge throughout the world. Then I realized...\nAfter you \"Fired\" me, I simply assumed that you were just going through some tough times, as you had been slightly off the past few months. But I soon saw that you had changed for the worse, the once happy Kale we knew into a bitter one.\nAnd as I continue to debate with myself, I came to see that everyone I cared about had changed in some drastic way; You have had all the happiness drained from you, Alina left to learn the Dark Arts, and Kivessin-\nWell, we know what became of him...\n\nEither way, it has come to my attention that everyone around me has changed. This life holds little for me anymore, so I plan to finish my research...\nAfter that, I will need to purchase some remedy- A poison, maybe- And research what it is like to experience death. I will be commiting suicide.\nYou had grown quite angry towards me and Kiveck recently, calling us \"Smartasses,\" and \"Rude little shits,\" or whatever it is you said. I was quite confused, and still am, but regaurdless, I apologize.\nI may be coming off as rude to you right now, and it may seem as if I'm mad at you myself. I would like to ensure you that this is not the case, as I am anything but. However, I do feel sorry for you, as you have taken the same path as countless others.\nWith that being said, good luck with your love life. I know for a fact that Kiveck is in love with you, after picking up on several hints. I thought that this may be of interest to you, that is all.\nPlease inform anyone who may also want to know of my death- Ketiley, Beltran, Sarrion, Nienna, Kiveck, Jingeh, Amras, Illithri, Eloh'ra, and whoever else should know of my decision to kill myself.\nYour last words to me were, \"Have a nice life.\" So, I will say the same to you. I wish nothing but the best from you, Kale, and my only request is that you revert to your old self. Smile every day.\nVan'ayla, llir. I want to say that we will meet again in the afterlife, but unfortunatley, such a place does not exist. \n\nHave a nice life.\n\n-Hileia'elr", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Kale~", "Zahrah", "\"Ms Kale.\n\nMy name is Zahrah and I am the partner to Nafis Yar. I wish to speak with you. . \n\nI wish to learn medicine and healing and hope that I would be able to ask that you or one of your\ndoctors would be willing to teach me.\n\nI know basics though I wish to learn properly.\n\nI reside with Nafis along the docks - if you wished to send a bird.\"\n\n---->\n[[Malinor is my MC name. If you want to reply and I'm not online let me know on Laurelin or Lirinya. . :) ]]", ""),
