        StaticBook("Peculiar Beasts", "William Roswell", "Peculiar Beasts and Creatures\n\nBy Mark Birch\n\n\nThroughout my days I have seen several beasts and... creatures, to say the least. This book I will share my adventures involving these creatures, and how to\ndefeat them.\n\nChapter 1: The Golem\n\nThis was no ordinary golem that you see wandering around, it was giant, stone, and had a staff with a ruby on top. An orc, a goblin, and I went hunting, and saw the ruby. We did not see danger because it\nwas merely a statue at that moment. I went to retrieve that ruby, but I was thrown off. All of us were confused until the beast started walking towards us. It's mighty stone arms swung below him, any hit could be fatal. We fired arrows at it, but they\nsimply ricocheted off. The orc had an idea of shooting the ruby, thinking it could be a life source. We did so, but got the same result as before. The Golem was now close to us, it swung it's arms and the orc dodged the blow, but I was hit and thrown\naway. The Golem advanced towards me, and then the Orc shouted, [Translated for better understanding] \"Use a pickaxe!\" I looked into my bag, and threw the pickaxe at the golem. The area which it hit crumbled, it was not the best blow, but did enough.\nThe goblin decided to jump onto the Golem's back. This left it unbalanced, and the Golem fell... Crushing the Goblin's legs. The orc and I took haste and ran to the immobile golem. I swang my pickaxe at the ruby, it burst into hundreds of pieces, and the\ngolem froze. We had done it! The goblin was freed and carried back... But I saw the staff on the ground, intrigued by it. I took the golem's staff home and still have it today.\n------------------\nI learned that if you plan on hunting, bring a variety of\ntools. You never know what you could face.\n\n\nChapter 2. Ghost Pirates\n\nYou may be thinking: What a joke! Ghost pirates? No such thing!!! But, yes, there is such a thing... I have faced them twice.\nThe first time I met them I was with 4 people. We venture along the lands, eventually reaching the shore of what used to be the dark elf colony. There was a  ship, it looked delicately made, but now the sails were torn. There were holes in the deck,\ncannons lined, skulls of dead sailors. We ventured around for a while until our group heard moaning and grumbling from beneath the deck. With caution, we advanced down the stairs to face an undead! He reaked of dead flesh and wore a mangled sailor uniform\n. One of our men fought him, unfortunately we had no aurum. His blows would hit, but simply not bother the creature at all. The combat lasted like this, him throwing blows and me shooting arrows at it for a while. That was until our Captain emerged from\nbehind the beast! He took out an aurum sword and severed it's body! It was dead... But there were more. This time we found another inside the captain's quarters. The same process happened, but this time the zombie was not as gullible. He fought our\nCaptain , putting up a remarkable fight, until the Captain threw aurum arrows to me. I caught them, knocked the bow, and took aim. Although we did kill it, it managed to bite a crew member and a good part of of his face was shred off. I patched up his\nwounds. We believed that was all the ship had in store for us. But no..................................\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nShortly after our dramatic fight, some creaking was heard below the ship. It was not a beast, nor a person. The ship was simply.....\nCapsizing!!!\n\n\nWater leaked through crevices or broke the wood. The Captain and I ran down to the gun deck, the hull was already submerged! We attempted to drag the cannons onto one side to even out the ship. But it was too heavy for us to do.\nAfter this feeble attempt I pushed the cannon out a hole, this did slightly work but our crew retreated to the main deck. We scampered to the quarterdeck and inside a room. All of a sudden eerie green mist emerged from the sea. It... Was a ship! Ghost\nharpoons were fired into the wood, and tore the ship to pieces! A voice boomed among us, it was their captain! He ordered us to leave the ship, but Captain resisted because he wished to take this ship for us. Eventually they sorted out a deal, and we were\nleft stranded... At the docks.\n\n-------------------That was my first experience with the Captain who I soon learned to be named \"Captain Skal Limlock.\" Eventually, our crew met him again....\n------------------\nA few years later we were on our\nship that was name \"The Tailor\". It was a glorious ship, it had blue and gray sails, beautiful wood, and a few ballistae. We went sailing, all was tranquil.... That was until we saw an obscure broken dinghy pass us. We halted for the time being... One of\nour men went down to inspect it, there was nothing. Our crew heaved him up, and were bewildered by this occurance. Until the mist grew, and turnt green... Suddenly an chained bolt dove out of the most and lodged it's way into our main mast!!! Captain knew\nwho it was... Without regrets we engaged in combat, shooting ballista bolts, however they did nothing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Penelope Perdiot", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatients Name: Penelope Peridot\n\nAge: 16\n\nRace: Human \n\nGender: Female\nCondition/Injury: A stab wound in her left side. A ghost stabbed her with scissors.\n\nTreatment Plan: I plan to disinfect the wound, give her something for the pain and then sew it shut if needed.\n\nDoctor who treated the patient: Kiveck Irelia\nCost for treatment: 5 minas\n\nDate: 18th of the First Seed, 1523\n\nEnd Result: She has healed sucessfully and the stitchings worked perfectly.\n*Doctor Kiveck's signature would be here\n\n-Kiveck Irelia", ""),
        StaticBook("Petrusian Men", "Cederick de Bolbec", "Orenian Support\n\n[!] The Wax seal of House de Bolbec is Stamped at the top of the document.\n\n\"It is on this day, that I shall speak to my allies, as follows in Petrusia.\"\nList of Formal Allies.\n\nProfound Clergyman.\nFarmer A.\nAymas A.\nAymas B.\nAymas C.\nAymas D.\nAymas E.\nAymas F.\nAymas G.\nGuard A.\nGuard B.\nGuard C.\nGuard D.\nOffical A.\nOffical B.\nOffical C.\nMerchant of Status A.\nTavarn A.\n\nFamily FAO\nFamily Gre\nFamily Vis\n-His Grace,\n\nCederick Augustus William Hanover Gregory de Bolbec Winchester", ""),
        StaticBook("Pirate Insults", "Nemir", "How to\n          Insult\n           Like a\n             Pirate\n-------------------          Written by:\n   Nemir Valnelis Ward\nSo you want to talk like a pirate?  Well you've found the right book!  After reading this, you'll surely knock your enemies down wish just your tongue.\nStarter words:\n- Idiotic\n- Parrot-loving\n- Mumbling\n - Blathering\n- Bleating\n- Sheep-brained\n- Pin-headed\n- Pig-breathed\n- Cricket-sized\nMiddle words:\n- Seaweed-slurping\n- Duck-billed\n- Pus-faced\n- Toothless\n- Knuckle-dragging\n- Cross-eyed\n- Scurvy-ridden\n- Clam-tongued\n- Yellow-bellied\nLast words:\n- Whale-fart\n- Cow-pie\n- Sack o’maggots\n- Cabin boy\n- Swabber\n- Waste of skin\n- Bag of vomit\n- Anchor-head\n- Piece of filth", ""),
