        StaticBook("Strange Note", "unknown", "Beyond the shattered realm their descendants stumble. Fate not altered, time hath fumbled. After a time of Draakar's ire Cover the fringe, torrid winds and fire. Traverse the the maker's mark and seek. A truth that Ancestors beseech", ""),
        StaticBook("Survival Guide", "ThePrroman", "Page 1\nIntro:\n\nHello everyone, this book was written by an experienced survivalist in hopes that all who wish to venture out into the wilds be prepared for the trials and hardships they may face along the way.\nAfter reading this booklet you will be able to survive on your own without any extra aid from outside sources.\n\nNow let us begin then.\nChapter One “What You Will Need”:\n\nThe most important items that a survivalist needs to well... survive, are the tools that he/she either finds or brings with him/her on the way to their journey into the wilds.\nHere is a list of helpful items:\n1. Flint & Steel\n2. A Small Hatchet\n3. Preserving Salts\n4. Needle and Thread\n5. Skinning Knife\n6. Waterproofed Satchel\n7. Small Fishing Hook\n8. Sturdy Clothing\n9. Sufficient Rations\n10. Common Sense\nOnce you have acquired all the supplies listed in the previous chapter you are now ready to begin your journey.\nFirst things first, to survive in the wilds you need to know at least a basic background of the\nenvironment you plan on venturing into, such as weather patterns, what kinds of vegetation grows in the region, as well as the different beasts that make their home in the area. Remember to study maps and acquire as much information about the region as\npossible before you decide to make the trip. Failing to do so could result in dismemberment or even death.\nOnce you have done your research and acquired all of your supplies for the trek into the unknown, you will finally be ready to begin.\nChapter Three “Setting Up Camp”\nIn this chapter you will learn the basics of setting up a safe and reliable camp site to live in during your stay in the wilderness. \nOnce you have found a suitable place to set up camp, you need to make\nsure that the area you have picked is in fact a safe place to stay in. To do so, please check off everything on this list:\n1. Is it dry and warm?\n2. Does it protect you from the elements?\n3. Is it close to a source of water?\n4. Can you easliy find it if\nlost?\n5. Does it protect you from unwanted visitors?\n\nIf all of the above checks off as okay, then you have done a great job in picking out a location for your campsite!\nChapter Four “Exploring The Wilderness”\nSo far so good, if you gotten this far then that means you haven’t killed yourself yet. Good job!\nIn this chapter we will be going over the basics of wilderness exploration.\nWhen an experience survivalist arrives in uncharted lands, they usually do one or more of these things listed: \n1. Find a high place and survey the lands before you, taking notes of key land marks in the immediate area.\n2. Preparing themselves for long treks away from the safety of their camps, make sure to pack extra food, you may be away from home for a while!\n3. Preparing for all possible outcomes. Think of everything that could happen\nwhile you are away from the camp; things such as being captured by jungle pygmies to the occasional bear destroying your camp can be easily be prevented if you just prepare ahead of time.\nCarrying out with at least one of these tips can make your life out in the wilderness much easier, and could possibly save your life.\nChapter Five “Returning Home”:\nCongratulations, you’ve survived your trip and are ready to break camp and return home with a multitude of new stories from your trip. Remember that when you are ready to leave to make sure you try to leave\nthings just as they were when you first arrived at the location you chose for your camp.\nOnce you have finished returning things as they once were, you can then begin to journey back home.  Make sure not to forget any trinkets or trophies that you\nmight have found while exploring the wilderness!\n\nThanks for reading.\nA little bit about the Author: \n\nCharles Silverblade was born in the small farming town of Riven, where his cousin Uthor Silverblade helped raise him and teach him to become a fine young man in terms of Oren society. When he turned 18 years of\nage, he enlisted in the Oren Military as a conscript and quickly ascended the ranks of hierarchy in the military until he finally acquired the title of Ser and received Knighthood in the Order of the Red Dragon. Charles now lives with his Wife and four\nchildren with the rest of the Silverblade family who reside in the Duchy of Furnestock.\nThe Essential Survival Guide\n\nWritten by Charles Silverblade\nCoppied by Rhonir\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Susan the Donkey", "[Psijic Laurehl] Katie Natura", "Once upon a time, there was a donkey named Susan. He was one of the smaller donkeys the farmer owned, and hardly ever was used.\n\nOne day, as Susan grazed in the pasture, the farmer's daughter came to Susan and patted his head. \"I need to go into the\ncity today, Susan. Will you carry me?\"\n\nSusan hee haw'd in reply and lowered himself enough so she could mount the saddle.\n\nOn they rode to the city. The trip was long and hard, but Susan was determined to prove that he could\ndo anything the other donkey's could do.\n\nWhen they arrived in the city, the farmer's daughter smiled and told Susan he did well. \nShe left Susan tied in a stable as she went to shop.\n\nHours passed and Susan waited for the\nwoman to return. Finally, after several hours, the farmer's daughter returned with many packages.\n\nSusan looked from her to the packages and knew there was no way she could carry them all. The farmer's daughter thought of this though, and a\ncart was brought over. \n\nThe stablemaster hooked Susan into the cart and the farmer's daughter climbed on. \n\nThey set off out of the city, and after a while Susan began to think this was easy. Oh, he was so wrong...\nComing around a bend in the road, a giant hill stood before them. It hadn't seemed so steep on the way there.. but now!\n\nSusan stopped in the road and hee haw'd for all he was worth. The farmer's daughter encouraged him onward.\nAs Susan reluctantly climbed the hill, he kept thinking 'I think i can, I think I can.'\n\nHe stumbled on a rock once and the cart slid back. But onward he pushed.\n\nFinally, they reached the top of the hill! Susan breathed in\nrelief. From then on, the farmer started using Susan more. He had proved himself a worthy steed because he believed in himself.\n\nWhen you believe, you can achieve!", ""),
        StaticBook("Tablet Riddles", "Cheza", "\"The Breaking\" \n\nNow broken, once whole. 7 knots in a rope.\nThe children of sea, betrayed by their hope.\nUnfinished promises, an entente unbound,\nas both of our tribes, lay sleeping underground.\nA prophet, the ocean, master of none,\nMaster of nothing, fatherless son.\nFather of nothing but what has been done,\na rope now broken, leaving its sons.\n\"Grieving of brothers.\"\n\nMan of him does not trick us like them\nman of him will not slay us instead.\nFor men of stone fall not for his act.\nFor men of stone still remember our pact.\nWe care now for seven, sons of the ocean.\nBut even now, we lose all motion.\nTired we slumber beneath the dirt.\nAs we return to dwell in our mother's hearth.\n\"Tales of the fall\"\n\nLet it be known, the danger of words.\nDanger of silence, danger of herds.\nDangers of mouthless phrases unheard.\nDanger of trickers and mission spurred.\nRest now, for tricksters do trap us alive,\ntrap us for power, trap us and bind,\ntrap us in guilt, worry hindsight,\ntrap us in questions of why we were blind.\n\"A price paid\"\n\nPeople yearn for gold and silver,\ncoins of copper, bars and silver.\nSilvers of soul, shards of dust,\ncurrency of monsters, beings above.\nCurrency they pay, brothers in debt,\nto the trickster of faith as he marks them for death.\nMark them for harvest, a farmer that sows,\nReaping of lives come a second toll.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VI", "March Ash - Eath'Lur Edition", "The swamps have always been a place for reclusive druids to go and meditate. The muck holds thousands of years within it, an ancient story of the land. Corpses of ancient men and women, who will tell me more about the history of this place\nthan books ever could.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Alchemy", "Kardel the Elder", "We will begin with one of\nthe most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist's Arsenal. Fire represents rage, anger, §§hatred\n*The word Hatred is circled in blood* and gusto *The word gusto is also circled in blood, the rest of the pages are torn out, and only a note lies on a surviving page over the text. djhsbgkdjskdgjhskjfghksjdhgksjhgksjfhgksjfhgksjfhgksjfhgksj\nakdjhsdkgjhskfjghskfjghskjfhgksjfhgksjfhgksfjhgksjFire is passion; it is hatred and gusto. . .these are the emotions i feel torwards you\n\n-Your /son/ \nskjdghlajfdhgldkfjhgkdjfhgalkdjfhglkjdfhglskjdglksjdflhgksjdfhglksjdlgksjdglkjsdhflgkjshfdglkj", ""),
        StaticBook("TEB Vol. I", "VonEbs", "The Eldest Brother:\n A History of Malinor\n       Volume I\n    The First Sky\n===================\nMalinor as we know it began after the Collapse, an obscure event which lead to the collapse of any civilization that may have existed before 1300. When one of\nthe symptoms of the Collapse, the erasing of the collective memory of all who survived the Collapse, wore off, High Prince Native banded together what was left of a wood elven colony, as well as the dark elves and high elves in the region surrounding\nLaurelin. He set about consolidating his position in Laurelin, assisting many elves in setting up lives in the capital. Very few elves are left from this time, almost all having gone missing at some point during Aegis, so accounts of the early days are\nsecondhand at best, many times having been passed from pointed ear to pointed ear until reaching the writer. By most accounts, Native picked an array of Princes to help him govern the growing elven population, some notable ones being\nPrince Toren the Farmer, Prince Flefal the Engineer, Princess Arianna, and Prince Lafthi the Diplomat. The mining paradise of Ravenhold was founded, home to such notable elves as Khel Oussana, Haelphon Adecchio, and future Prince Ebs Telrunya.\nAfter the initial years in Laurelin, most of the High Council, including High Prince Native, were barely ever seen in Laurelin, and Malinor suffered. The Gauntlet, an obstacle course that offered a large minas reward, was opened rarely, and almost every\nelf immediately entered the Wardens or the Druidic Order upon entry into Malinor. The only functioning part of Malinor’s government were indeed the Wardens, the elite defenders of the forests of Malinor. Lead at first by the ruthless Blackthorn, they\nprotected the forests while the High Council squandered away the Princedom. Native’s only notable action during this time was nearly destroying Ravenhold when he caused the mine to collapse.\nWhen Kal’Bryst was destroyed during the onset of the Undead invasion, the High Council’s reaction was nonexistent. During the great northern wars, in which the humans struggled for survival against the undead invaders, the elves hid in the south, with\nvery few participating in the defense of Alstion.  The Wardens instead focused on removing Wrath from Wrath’s Clutch, an Undead citadel in the South that threatened to cut off Alras and Al’Khazar from Laurelin and Kal’Urguan. Countless wardens and other\nelves perished in attacks on Wrath’s Clutch, which was repeatedly assaulted so that prisoners being held there, most notably Princess Indelwehn, could be freed. No matter how many times the walls were breached, the forces of the United Aegis Coalition\n(UAC) could not dislodge Wrath until very late in the war. Indelwehn became notable for leading the wardens in the defense of Sanjezel, leading to the signing of the Malin-Krug pact, a long-lasting defensive treaty between the Holy Princedom and\nKrugmar, which was signed by Princess Indelwehn and Wargoth Mogroka’Gorkil. \n\nMalinor had a token presence in the Verge, its official settlement, overseen by Princess Lirinya, lacking utility and security. More enterprising elves and a few humans united\nunder Viscount Ebs, who founded the city of Fionn, which flourished for a time, until all but the mentally unstable abandoned the Verge during the massive slime and spider invasion. At this time, Laurelin abandoned its old Council Chambers to allow the\nMages Guild to have a place to set up away from the unstable north.\n\nFor a time, Malinor had a High Princess, Sorious, the wife of Native. After her death, the High Council passed a law stating that being the spouse of a Prince does not\ninherently make you a Prince. Native later fell in love with the owner of the Treetop Inn, which flourished in the trees North of Malinor. The owner, Lirinya, quickly rose to prominence in Malinor, gaining the title of Princess quite quickly. Her down to\nearth nature and her humbleness disguised that she was Undead. Gaining trust from a besmitten Native, she betrayed Malinor, destroying Ravenhold during the rule of High Princess Indelwehn.\n\nWith the appointments of Princess Indelwehn and Prince Mylas,\na new generation of Elven leaders took the helm of the nation. Ebs, a high elf, and Sythra, a dark elf, convinced High Prince Native to disband the corrupted Wardens, who were being used by the cruel Prince Quazar as an aggressive force, sparking conflict\nwith the other nations. The Vanguard was formed, with Sythra in command. With the appointment of Prince Ebs as High Prince Native’s final act, the High Council, guided by the still mostly absent Princes Toren and Lafthi elected High Princess Indelwehn to\nthe highest position in Malinor. They then added then Treelord Haelphon and Sythra to the Council, and removed the Archdruids from the Council, as in that time, the druids grove was a pit of filth and crime, all but sanctioned, and most certainly indulged\nin by Respiren and Dusk. This was a Golden Age for the elves, as their international power and influence waxed to a point where it could have been argued, after the fall of Al’Khazar, that Malinor was the stablest and most powerful state in Aegis.\nUnknown at the time of her election was the deep taint hidden in the heart of Indelwehn, installed during one of her stays in Wrath’s Clutch. Her second husband, Bircalin, and her friends watched in horror as she changed. It is still not clear if she was\naware she was tainted, however, she broke the Malin-Krug pact, refusing to aid Krugmar in their war against Urguan and Oren, and made a series of disastrous mistakes. She attempted to have Prince Ebs assassinated for questioning her,\nhowever he barely survived, and after a year recovering in Hanseti, he returned when Indelwehn was charged with the murder of a small child. The High Council attempted to cover up her crimes, but realized she had to go, and voted unanimously to remove her\n, revealing to the public only that she had resigned. In a near tie, Haelphon was elected High Prince, with Sythra losing by one vote. By this point, Prince Mylas had been killed during an Undead attack, and his body had been laid to rest outside the\nSister City, a suburb of Laurelin. At this time, the High Council met in the Sister City, as it was too easy for Undead spies to listen in on proceedings in Laurelin.\n\nMalinor established good relations with the Kingdom of Renatus after it emerged from\nthe Phoenix Rebellion, but the final days in Aegis were characterized by fear among the High Council. After the falls of both Al’Khazar and Alras, refugees flocked to Malinor. Prince Ebs set up the Alrasian refugee camp East of Laurelin, but the Alrasian\nofficers and Vanguard struggled to keep order in the once peaceful city of Laurelin. During a magical experiment by the druids and mages, Arkelos, and Undead, destroyed the Gauntlet, spreading miasma around Laurelin. As elves prepared to flee the\ncity, the druids managed to restore the air, however the damage was staggering. The High Council, despite the pleading of a few members, refused to build additional fortifications around Laurelin, instead opting to give Deltaro Black, an elf who\nthought he was much more competent than he actually was, permission to remodel the front entrance to make it more “naturey.” Laurelin did not stand a chance in the final battle, and as the dragons leveled the once proud jewel of Laurelin, the elves fled\nfor the Verge, many of which were openly weeping, where they were met by chaotic conditions, as the elven government has fallen apart. Treelord Alan managed to build an elven ship, but travel conditions were horrid, and many elves were lost in the voyage.\nAnd so the elves set out for Asulon, to brave a strange new world full of dangers they could not have possibly conceived as they left Laurelin.\n\n~Ebs Telrunya, Former Fourth Prince of Malinor", ""),
        StaticBook("Tele Studies", "Cablam", "Telekinesis Studies by Armin Ambertoe\n\nUses of telekinesis:\n- lifting objects\n- throwing objects\n- holding objects in place\n- deforming objects\n- changing a moving object's direction\n- slowing down objects\nApplications in a real life scenario:\n\n- lifting a box\n- throwing a ball\n- shooting a projectile\n- holding an object in place\n\nOut of the box ideas:\n- cleaning the house\n- farming\n- fishing\n- Drawing, painting (art stuff)\n1. Weight\n2. Speed\n3. Amount of objects\n\nWeight: The weight of an object determines how much mana it posseses. For one to perform telekinesis they must use more mana than the object posseses. Therefore, the heavier the object the more mana it\nwill take to lift it. \n\nSpeed: As an object is moving it becomes more difficult to focus on the faster it moves. This is because as its location changes it becomes more difficult for a mage to latch a mana anchor onto it.\nAmount of objects: As stated earlier, the way one lifts an object with telekinesis is by expending an amount of their mana equal to or greater than the mana of the object they wish to lift. Therefore when attempting to lift multiple objects a mage must\nsplit their mana amongst the objects. The same cumlulative weight can be lifted however it is just split between the multiple objects.\nTalk with other Telekinetics\n\nTelekinetic 1:\n- Uses telekinesis around the kitchen while baking to help with getting things from across the kitchen, saving her the effort of having to walk around the kitchen constantly.\nWas once tied up and kidnapped by a lady and used some heavy steamer trunks to bludgeon her captor.\nTelekinetic 2:\n\nUses it to tidy up. Also used it to kill a man with a door who broke his ex-wife's ribs.\n\nUses it to read multiple things at once. Uses it to shoot pointing things at people.\nTelekinetic 3:\n\nUses telekinesis to fuck shit up.\n\nUses it in enchanting, making objects travel at high speeds and to ensnare things or make them lighter.\n\nAlso uses it to touch dangerous objects.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thank You", "Grant Hemsworth", "Dear friend,\n\nI thank you profusely for your help in moving into my home here. I could not have asked for more wonderful friends and neighbors. Feel free to come by whenever and for anything.\n\n- Grant H.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Agustus Raid", "Finel Cole", "I am keeping track of what things I see, hear, feel, and touch. What I also eat, too. I will record what the people are like, what they think of the destination, their occupation. There is a long journey ahead of me, and I hope this is a success.\nSo far I am in Oren. The people around me have this wierd accent. I will classify these things in my way. I will attempt to make my own language for it to spread around. I will call these people Orenians. The architecture around here is very complex.\nThis job that I am doing right now is a Menel. A Menal is someone who records the information around them and makes new things. Now, there is something called Mountain Agustus. Who lives in there are fighters. Protecters of Oren.\nDwarves are attacking. There will be a battle. Todays date is the 30th of The Grand harvest, 1456. This battle will be called The Battle of Oren. The humans are currently in a world war with everyone. I will call the world war, The War of All.\nThe humans fought the dwarves over, but it isn't over yet.\nThe dwarves have taken over the fort. We have lost control. We are contesting over Fort Vekaro, which is the fort that we lost. The battle is not over yet. The dwarves are almost in.\nI am not calling it a battle anymore. It is no longer The Battle of Oren. It is now The Agustus Raid. Orenians took back Fort Vekaro, no one has won the The Agustus Raid. The dwarves will come back.\nThey have come back. We fought them back, but they WILL come back. It turns out they were a mix of races in the group. Elves, orcs, and dwarves. They went back to their city, Kal'Alras. Orenians are strong. But are they strong enough?", ""),
        StaticBook("The All-Theory", "Archibald", "The Theory of Everything, by Archibald Vallero\n-------------------\n\n    In this tome, I wish to explain to all my beliefs on why things exist with direct connection to the realm known as the Void. At times, you might be confused. This is entirely\nunderstandable given just how abstract this idea of mine might be.\nIf any of this offends you, I will let you know right now that I did not intend to offend or undermine anyone's religious beliefs. If that is what you believe I intended to do by the\ntime you've finished reading this book, then sorry. \n\nNow, let's begin.\nThe Void\n-------------------\n\n    Many readers probably have no idea what the Void is, which is why I've decided to begin this with an explanation so that non-mages can be at the same level of understanding with mages as to what the Void is.\nThe Void, in short is a dimension where everything exists simultaneously along with nothing. It is all that is and all that will ever be, but at the same time there is nothing there. One point I should emphasize while explaining this is that the Void\nIS another dimension. Implant this into your mind: the Void is a completely separate dimension to ours. Now, the use of the Void to mages is simply to draw the ability to create from it. Another keyword I'd like for you to remember is 'creation.' It will\nbe mentioned continually throughout this tome. As said before, voidal mages are able to create an array of elements and entities by exhausting their mana, which is essentially every living being's life force. Mana flows through our veins, and with it we\nare able to connect to the Void and bring about lightning, flesh, fire, water, air, earth, 'raw' energy (arcane energy), and the ability to alter the world or the people around us through different types of illusion or alteration. We use the Void to bring\nabout the CREATION of something or another that would otherwise be inaccessible to non-mages. Now, all of us have a mana anchor in the void, which is what it sounds like. Our mana, while in our bodies, is also connected to the Void, and this is what\nallows all non-mages to become mages. Now, with this explanation, I wish to bring up my theory.\nThe All-Theory \n-------------------\n\n    So, now you understand what the Void basically is. Good. Now, what if I told you that, since the Void is a dimension where anything is possible and, while it is in a constant state of balance and\nunbalance, it was still able to create /everything/. What if the dimension is the epicenter of ALL creations? What if it was even the creator of /our/ Creator? Think about it like this . . .  Mana can be found in all living, organic beings. This means\neven grass, trees, all abundances of animals, and us. This mana is what allows for there to be a mana anchor, weak or strong, to the Void for all beings. While the grass you stand on might have an extremely weak mana anchor, there is mana there\nnonetheless. Necromancers can drain the life from anything with mana in order to power themselves, meaning that, indeed, all things have mana. Even the stone of castles or the earth beneath us might have mana, though it might be in such an insignificant\namount that nothing can really be done with it. If we move up the chain and start with trees, there's more than likely more mana in them than both grass and stone, since Graven's are capable of manipulating their own mana to creator a connection or bond\nwith the tree that allows it to stay there. The tree is also involved in this process, though, by allowing for their to be a connection in the first place. Perhaps they have enough mana to have such a thing be done. Next is us Descendant races.\nWe are able to cast spells that closely resemble elements we can observe in modern day life, but with more manipulation involved. I won't go into specifics, but it requires the touch of our minds to create ice sculptures, fiery animals, and other such\nabnormal things. \n\n    Now, I did say that mana flows through our veins, but what if, just like stone, our skin, bones, and other bodily particles also contained mana? We are beings of mana, from the bottom up. All other things are made of mana,\neven if it is difficult for mages to tell. This leads me to believe that we were all created by the Void, but with middle-men inbetween the process of our creation. \n\n    Let's delve further into the nature of the Void for just a moment. We can use it\nto create a myriad of things. Here comes the confusing part of this theory, but I will try to summarize it as such first before explaining.\n\nInanimate materials have low mana, not able to create anything. We are animate along with animals, and some\nanimals are capable of being magical while us Descendant races can connect with the Void to create. Aengudaemons are powerful, capable of creating amazing and wondrous things, an example being the Arch-aengul Aeriel creating the Ascended, or Metzli\ncreating the entire race known as the Kharajyr. This type of creation is far beyond the Descendant races' abilities. Then there is the Creator, which many believe has created the aengudaemons and all of us. This could be true. But now, answer this for\nme: what created the Creator? The answer to this, I have deduced, is the only dimension capable of bringing about everything material and animate, or the Void itself. It is to my belief that the Creator is simply a powerful entity that has a immensely\npowerful connection to the void, allowing for this being to acquire a massive amount of mana and the ability to create the aengudaemons and us all. Essentially, the Void brought about the powerful being known to us as the Creator, which had a greater,\nintense mana anchor and mana pool, that this creator of ours was able to use everything available to it in the Void (which is everything conceivable) to create this world, and the aengudaemons. \n\n    There's also a pecking order, I've noticed. The\nVoid is the creator of all, it is a dimension/entity/being capable of granting power and creating any and everything, and as it had created our Creator, since the Creator has such a close connection to this dimension, this being's powers closely\nresembled the Void's. Then there are the Aengudaemons, some ranking higher than others. They have an immense amount of power, but have physical restrictions. An example would be the fact that they can only shape our realm through us lower beings, as\nthe paladins resemble Xan's hand, or the clerics resemble Tahariae's hand, or the cultists of Ikuras resemble Ikuras's hand. Then there is us. We do have a connection to the Void, but at only at a great cost. The more we master arts that allow us to\ncreate wards, elements, or bring things back to life or even drain mana from other living beings, the more our muscle mass and sanity disappears. We are thinning out. We are losing ourselves as we continue. This leads me to my next theory.\nThe All-Pure\n-------------------\n\n    As said before, the more one attempts to bring something into this realm, the more mass, or particles of themselves, they lose. I've lost around twenty pounds while still maintaining a healthy diet as I\nattempted to master conjuration, but if I were to try and learn even more evocations or magicks of another kind, I would be even far more thin. Weak. Decrepit. We lose our corporeal selves as we delve into the power that allows us to create. This leads me\nto the other observation that the more closely connected one entity is to the almighty Void, the more of 'themselves' they lose, or, rather, the more they lose their body, the greater their ability to manipulate elements and, naturally, everthing else.\nWhy this occurs I'm not /entirely/ sure, but an idea that's come to my mind is that it's the cost, as everything has a cost. The cost for becoming more god-like in being is that you lose what we know as ourselves. We lose our body and our 'mind.' This can\npotentially explain why Aengudaemons are able to have such great power in their own realm, creating what they want at their own whim, but as soon as they enter an earthly vessel to interact with us, they only become the equivalent of a powerful mage,\nrather than some being with the capabilities to destroy and create. The cost for having a body like ours is that they lose some of the powers that makes them 'them.' At the same time, once they are killed in this world, they are still able to ascend back\nto their own and retain their original powers. All very interesting, indeed.\n\n    The real aspect of the All-Pure theory involves 'purity.' In my belief, the closer one is to obtaining the ultimate power that the Void grants, creation, the more\n'pure' they are. In this sense, non-mages are not as pure as voidal mages. Inanimate objects aren't entirely as pure either, and are on the bottom of the order. This does not mean that one being deserves to live and one to die. It is simply my outlook on\nthings. Now, with this new theory, it is fact that mages who are granted their power from an aengudaemonic force, such as paladins, clerics, and cultists, are not as pure as voidal mages. The purest one can be is when they are able to siphon\ntheir spells of creation from the Void, the dimension where, believe, all life truly originates! The reason why paladins and clerics are not as pure as voidal mages is due to the fact that they are drawing their power from a being lower than the Void,\nand rather from an aengudaemon which had been created by the Void. They are drawing their power from a weaker source. The Void is the most powerful, truly. This could also explain why they, the aengudaemonic siphoners, are able to retain some muscle\nmass and weight while us voidal mages are weakened. We're closer to reaching the nature of the 'nothing-yet-everything' Void, while they are granted their power from a lower and less powerful being which takes its power from the Void. If they were to cut\nout the middle-man in their magicks, they would end up being like the voidal sorcerers: able to create more elements and manipulate this world further, yet at the cost of them losing more and more of their bodily matter. \n\n    With this in consideration,\nI do believe that there is a Creator. I believe, though, that our Creator is, frankly, a being who has such a powerful connection with the Void that it was capable of bringing our kind about along with the aengudaemons. But the true Creator is the voidal\ndimension. \n\n    With this, I conclude my novel. I hope you, brave scholar, found this piece of literature interesting and profound in its content. Thank you.\n\n         -Archibald V.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bards Ellis", "Dread Knight Verin", "The Bards\n              Of \n             Ellis \n\n\n\nBy Verin Etitlan\n    Edemah Etitlan\n    Eiheiu Darky\n\"There once was a bard,\nDashing and daring,\nThe queens pants he did start to mangle, and they found him, and threw him to shambles.\n\nOut on the floor, cold as ice, his hair scratched and withered like lice --\nThat lonely bard, he did song. Of a place to the east, where no men could ying.\n\nThe druids, his home he did fine, and once more did this lonely bard find; \n\nHe took the archdruids pants and threw them a mangle,--\nAnd there they found him, and threw him to shambles!\"\n- Verin Etitlan.\n   Kalos/Anthos\nThe Will of God:\n\"The man looked down in fond reminiscance at the man he once knew. His dagger upraised in firm defiance, astrew its' blades handle, and he spoke, like the angry vassal of the messiah. \"You. Are. Done.\" The blade plunged down, slamming int\no the mans heart, and the ether came for him.\"\n  Edemah Etitlan\n     Kalos\nThe End:\n\"The armored man looked down to his creation, to its' mangled body. Its' child of any other, and it worked. Its' firm machinations elliciting no response, the ether calling out, trying as it would to grasp the man, to give him the end..unable.\nHe became his son, in all but name. His father his lord, forever in vein. His own son gone, lost to the ether he hoped for each day, he wishes he could go there, one day.\"\n   Unknown.\n     Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning", "Beltran", "\"In the time of Axios was the creator, his numerous forms wrought by his stature. He formed the mountains and the lands, and spilled his blood upon the sand.\n\nThis sacrafice we call it is the Ocean. All life spills his gift and returns to his-\nembrace. Zhythuiel was his name and he brings his greatest gift. From the sand he melted into glass, and created his servents the fish. From deep lava caves, he bent the rock and formed the mighty whales. From the sky he pulled down stars and forged them-\ninto coral. And from the moon he bought back rocks, carved into the most beautiful of shells.\n\nWe are not of his creations, we are land dwellers, scant of his grace but the creator's gift is his greatest mercy.\nCardinal Whuthul was graced by his presence, the creator himself riding onthe back of his mighty turtle. He gave him the book of which to summon him and instructed him to enlighten his fellows.\n\nThe gift of the book was mighty indeed, and trinkets so to-\nspread his word. The ShellFaced daggers was one such and we have the grace of housing one.\n\nNovice, you must understand we are one of many. This church is of a congregation of many, for the church does-\nneed to spread it's limbs.\"\n\n[!]Below is waxed the signet of an octopus man, surrounded by arcanic letters incromphensible to all.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Black Hero", "Guz Volaren", "The Black Hero and The Lonesome Devil\n\nThe Black Hero was so strong that the other Elves feared him and because of this fear they locked him up and mutilated him, they ruthlessly cut off his limbs and subjected his mind to torture, he slowly fell into\nmadness, his mind could not take the beating as well as his body, he snapped, escaping from the jail, he amassed allies, he got new arms, stronger ones, ones that could not be broken by ordinary means, he assumed leadership of a bandit group.\nHe was feared by all, nothing could stop him, he amassed his riches then retired, his family's family's could live an easy life, his life had lost purpose without fighting, after all, it was natural to him, the only thing that was natural to him.\nThe other Elves had forgotten about him, but he would return, offering his services as a soldier underneath them, he had forgiven them for what they had done to him, and he hoped that the Elves forgave him, and if they hadn't he would gaurd them until\nthey did, he honestly and truly cared about what others thought of him he couldnt stand them thinking of him as a villain because after all, he was a villain, was a villain, now he is a hero, The Black Hero.\n\nI'd like to apologize to all that I hurt but I\nam to afraid to do so, if any one gets this journal i'm probably dead I hope you will share this with the other Mali I truly am sorry and I hope you can forgive me, I am The Black Hero.\n-Guz Volaren", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bonds", "Vlad Shade", "The True Art of Alchemy:\n\nAlchemy isnt just a passion or a carrier\nits a art beyond that of anyother such as one might call cooking a culinary art alchemy is one of its own beyond any limit it is seen as a art beyond our human eyes\nWe see alchemy as a combo of herbs to just benifit us but the truth is alchemy isnt just that it is the blessed art of making something from once useless materials you can even spring forth the life of your own body with them\nWe are but the  essential elements of these potions mixed togther to do nothing but fix our inperfections but it can be so much more we can be of the greatest kind of race working togther we can become what we deisre by one bond", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bones", "The March Ash", "Buried November’s bones here. They will find peace in this place. Said a prayer.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Brave Woman", "Amin Al-Nabeel", "Brave woman\n__________________\nShe is the bravest my eyes have ever seen\n\nA lion bows, in shiver and fear\n\nI am on my knees for I can not believe\n\nA woman so beautiful, among us she breathes\nI offer this world and everything within to her feet\n\nI say proudly that I will protect her with fists\n\nShe smiles, then gently she says to me\n\nI am a woman, strong and I do not need\nProtection,\nfor I may seem fragile\nBut I am stronger than steel\n\nI do not know what words to speak\n\nFor I desire her love, and love her miserably\n\nBut I have only my heart to offer\nAnd she deserves better than me\n\nIt does not matter that I love her endlessly\n\nShe lives in a world that the devil dreams to flee\n\nAnd yet she stands strong with a smile shinning through her lips\nWith a laugh musical, poetry to my ears\n\nShe is a brave woman, gentle and free\n-------------------____________________-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_\n\n\n       The End\n_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-------------------__________________", ""),
        StaticBook("The Diamond[s]", "N.Y.", "vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvThe\nDiamond[s] - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\n(A collection of poems written by a soldier. Found in the rough.)\n\n(Includes 5 Poems)\nThe\nPrayer - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nI worry if I go to war,\nMutts will come knockin’ on my door.\nPlease protect my loved ones, Lord.\nMake me hard as diamond \nso I can crush these hordes.\nAnswer this, I’ll never ask for more.\nI wrap this prayer up and trace the cross\nOn the tabard that my grandfather wore.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe\nLifestyle - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nI’m afraid of my lifestyle.\nI’m figurin’ out my life now.\nBut f**kas comin’ at my life now.\nIgnited powder to blow my house down.\nThey don’t wanna see me breathin’ this evenin’.\nNo matter how much I try to reach em’ and lead em’.\nI lost my eye because of one fatal accident.\nI guess my swordplay needed more practicin’.\nThat’s when I learned that war wasn’t for every-body.\nNearly lost mine so I killed the f**ka’ before they got me.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe Old\nTendencies - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nOld Khalestine, city filled with Hash fiends.\nCrazy Hassan used to ride camels with a mad lean.\nThat’s how you remember it, that’s how I remember it.\nI done caught a couple arrows, been stabbed,\nHence why I keep my sword strapped.\nAnd truthfully, I think over half yall’ b***h made.\nAnd if you don’t trust my ‘A’ Grade,\nGo on, my Qali, come and test my blade.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe Woman sent\nfrom Allah - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nYou shine like diamonds,\nYou’re bright as gold,\nYou soothe my achin’ soul.\nTruth within your eyes,\nNever told me a lie.\nI hold you up to the sky,\nI tell you that I might die\nbefore I hit twenty five.\nbut you give me peace of mind\nand remind me that I’m alive.\nOur reunions are a surprise,\nSo bright that with you I’m never lost.\nWhen I first stumbled into you,\nI knew that you were sent from God.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nThe Land\nOf Eden - N.Y.\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nOpen up your eyes, tell me what you see in-\nside of me, tell me exactly what you thinkin’.\nCould this be love, that be how it’s seemin’.\nAnd you should know that I been meanin’\nTo take you back to our slice of Eden\nWhere the flowers and the trees are meetin’.\nJust hold my hand, I can take you to that land\nGoodbye to sand, where our people damned.\n\n vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv", ""),
        StaticBook("The Edict", "Karim Vayle", "The Crimson Edict\nAnd reasons you should join:\n\n1. We believe in equality. It doesn't matter what your race is, you're a potential member. That also means we don't tolerate slavery, so you've gotta help deal with that if we find any.\n2. We know you don't like necromancers, and we don't either. That also applies for any dark magic that screws with or hurts other people.\n3. We're more than just mercenaries. We're a thriving community made up of all kinds of people, including those who don't do much fighting. A good example of this would be the handsome and charming Head Bard, Karim Vayle.\n4. Almost-free lodgings! You need to be active and a contributing member, but other than that you don't have to pay a mina to stay!\n5. Loyalty. We're not gonna sell you out, mostly because of a life oath. That means you don't fuck us over either, or we're gonna hunt you down.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements", "Jerry_Man", "PROLOGUE\nThis book was recovered from Aegis and is dated around 1378 of the last age of Aegis. The author has since dissappeared from existence.\nWATER\nThe neccesity of life. All animals, plants, and even we, the races of Aegis, need it to survive. Water can often be associated with emotion, art, time, and especially healing.\nEARTH\nIt is the first thing you need for almost everything, to ensure stability and endurance. Earth is a reliable element, peaceful and tranquil. Earth is the most passive and strong element, although it can be quite destructive.\nAIR\nIt is invisible, unpredictable, unreliable, soothing, inspiring, and destructive. Air is the representation of everything we cannot see; our spirits, our souls, our minds, and our hearts.Of that what lies beneath, or beyond some\nscholars say. The unpredictable and changing wind can become a devestating Hurricane, or a playful breeze.\nFIRE\nIt has been an important part of all cultures and religions in the past to modern day Aegis. Fire is bright, strong, takes charge, and wants control. Fire is never subtle, it proudly shows itself. Fire never stops unless acted upon by\nanother element or force, and it consumes everything it touches.\nTo Become A Mage\n There is much an apprentice must learn before becoming a Mage. Your Guild Master may send you on quests of sorts, but I prefer to study in the Library, the source of much information. Here, you can learn everything you need: ...\nThe Elements, Self-Control, Mage Powers, and much more. This is the first part in become a Mage, studying. You need to learn all you can from your experiences and readings. Once an Elven Week has passed, possible longer, you will be asked to gather\nmaterials. These will be used to create your staff. The particular ingredients in your staff will cause a different outcome,  than if you were to use different materials. This Staff you create will be specially connected with you, your spirit\nenergy will be infused with the energy of the staff, thus the connection. Once you have earned your staff, you will become a Mage, and be given a job within the guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elven Threat", "*Abdul Kareem Jiwaz", "Elven Threat.\n\n\nThis book will give you the truth about the elves living in Khalestine. The agenda they have and why they are here.\n\n*there appears to be no signed author to this book*\nAs-salamu alaykum dear reader! In this book you will read about the true intentions of non-humans living in our dear Khalestine. \n\nDon't be fooled by the beuty of the elves or the cuteness of the Kharajyr because they wills you no good oh chosen of Allah.\nNo. They are here to ruin our beutifull city. To destroy our Qalasheen culture and to destroy our faith in Allah and the phrophets (Peace be apon them).\n\nThe elves are the worst of them. They are devils. That is why they look human but are not.\nHey have long. Thin fingers so that they may reach into our pockets. The pockets of Qalasheen people and take not only our gold but our culture! Our faith!.\n\nAsk any of them! They care not for religion. They care not for anything because they are lazy.\nAnd yet there they walk. On our streets. In our armies.\n\nThey care not for Khalestine, Allah or Qalasheen people! Just look when there is prayer in the mosque. There are no elves!\n\nNo they are sitting in the taverns drinking! Preforming sodomy!\nThey have long ears so they can listen to the guard's footsteps before they sneak into the palace. They are nimble so they can crawl into every window every small gab!\n\nThe Qalasheen are Allah's chosen! And Khalestine is Qalashen lands!\nThe elves also support the being known as the druids. These are the devils beings. You can see it on them. They are deformed by what they call ''blessings''.\n\nIt is the devils blessings they have recieved!\nBewary of these. They are dangerous and not to be approached. Like all elves they use their friendly appearence to lure you into a trap. \n\nA deadly trap.\n\nSo beware the Elf! It wills neither you or Qalasheen any good!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Far Glade", "Finalhazard", "T̼͖͓̣̩h̸͔̺͚͙̙̭͔e͇̟̦͖̜ ̺̲̯̼̗F̜̥a̺̼͜r̲ ̨̝Gl̨̙͓͔͉͖̺͉a̰̥̰̭͍d̥͝ḛ ̨̪̭̱̙͙̜̗ìs̫͚̫͍̯̼ ͍̲͓̪̕a̭͡ ̠́p̵͖̯ͅl̤̺̖͟ͅa͍̼͓͚̳̥c̸͔̼͔̖̖e̴͈ ̡̟͈o̟̺̣͕̮̦̦f̧͇̼̺̺̠̰ ̛̝̗̫l̢̖͚͇͚̫͓͍e̛g̛̦e̪͖̟̘͍n̦̪̙͙͕̬̼d̬̠͉́.̬̝̟̺̣̲̹\nI̲̫̤t̜̲͎̘̫̳ ̼͈̞͕͕e͍̻̼̪̺ͅx̺̳̖͈ͅi͠sts̬̤ ḅ͠o̡̘t̟h̸ ̳̘͙͓͇̕i̡̠͖̭͖̹n̷̬͍͕ͅ,̢͕͓ ̨͚a͔̩nd͇̘͎͠ͅ ̫͍̞̱̟͝ͅͅo҉͈͎̰u҉t̙s̜͈̠͎̣i̦̱̲̲̱̞̰͜d̠̩e ́o͏̪͍̘͇̣̙f̥ ͙͚̞̦̲͖Ṿ̵͍͇̜̻a̡̖̟ì̤l̘͖̠̪̟o̴͉̭̭̼̪̰̳r͕̰̞̣͖̹̱̀\n̥̥̣̤̠̣̟O̴̩̣̣͇̳ͅn̙̪͉͕̰ȩ͙̝̮̳ ͔m̤̬̠a̷̺̥͓͔̪y͖͈̦̥ ̜c̤̖o̷̻̠̤n̢̗̺s̫͢i̳͕̻̥d͉͍̪͜ͅe̶͉̱r̟̳̫͕͍ ̠͈i͓t҉̫ ͙͔͙a͈̟̬̻̪ ͉͞'̭̼n̴͉a̴̖̠̻t͖̹̖̀ṳ͓̲r̫̟̩͙a̮l͡'̵ ͉͚͉̣̠̙g͙r̳̩o̮͇̦̙̯̭̠͠v̺̺͙̠ͅé̹̝̺͉̮͓ ͇͕̯̞̲̦̼o̬̬̫f̲ ̣s̙͍͉̰̀o͉r̙͔̟̮t̰̣̗̩̻s̮͎̫̗͙̘ͅ\n̹̥̰̱̥̼̹E҉̮͙̩̱͔̫v̶e҉̺̬̥͇̝ͅͅn̻̠ ̡̫wh̗̗̺̜̝̟͘e̡n̵̘̬̰̗͍̦̪ ͞d͙̖e̱͓̕ͅs҉͔̯͈̤̱t̳̮́r̫̤̱̗̯o̴͚̣̟̲y̮e̻̤ḍ̩͎ͅ\n̖̕i͍̦͉̘̙͇͞ͅt̵̘ ̠̪͙̀s̜ţ͚̙i͇̦l̘̝̣̟̝̰l̮̟ ͞e̢̠̺̣͖xi͔̼st̙͈͘ͅs̫ ̺̺͚͟f͇̝̠͍̘̕or͏̫̮̤ ̣͎͕͚̞͖i̜̥̥͇͝t͉ ̵̤̣is̮̗̬̣̗ ̙͍͖p̪̻̟̦̤͢a̛͚̝̟rt͇̘̣͇ ̸̱o͉̪͓̗͎̥f ̩n̰̙̠͇͖͓a̹t̩̦̮̹͔̹͎u̢r҉̥̙̥e̢̼̤̠̲,̻̤̯̤\na̞̖̺̯̼̬̹͜n̹̼̜͎d̙̳͙͎̗͓̫ ̞͓͉d̪̦̞̲̟͟eḁ͓͍̱͔̦t͖̫̭͕͠h͢ ̺i̛͎s̰͔̰̞̖̕ ͍͖̤͚̯̱͘a̺͓͞ ̳̥p̞͍̤͓̜̣a̖͚̰͎̫̖r̶͙̖̗͉t̵ ̮̲̥̳̫̜o͈f ̝̬̳̞̳͍̲n͖a̗̥̭̞̠̝͝ͅt̳̜u͎͇̦̦r̨̝ẹ̘ ̧̹j̷͙̜͇̫̗̟us̠̩̮̞̲t͏͈ a̛ş̬͕̬͓ mu̳c̤h҉͇̞͖͙ ͙͝a̞͙̭͞s̫̻̹͙̀ ḷ̮if̭̣͍̕e̞͍͓̜͙̯̭̕.̹̲̗̜̳̥ ̳̖̹̜\nW̩̗̖̻͕i̠̝̤̺̥͕ţ̙̹h̸̳̘͇ͅo̩̪̮̣̬ut̻ ̹̦̟̟̠͠d̟͚̤̟̻͎e̟̺͝a͖͓̣͓͙̼ṱ̗̮̘̤̀ḩ͚̯̖̝̟,͖͈̻̥͚̝͙ ͕͚͔͔͕͙͖͡ĺ̜̫̮̤̘̟if͚̯e̜͎͚̻͉ ̴̰̟̳̳̝ͅh͕̻͍͚̬̲͝ą̟͙̼̩ͅs̹̟̦̠̭̩͎ ̧n̗͟o͇ͅ ̛͍̫̗m̨e̵a̳̣̬͕̰͞ǹ̞͉̱̠ͅi̵͍̬̼̻̼̣ͅn̟̮̟g̩͎͠.͏̤̫\n̜̱̞̥̯̥W̰̼͉̤͔i̴̜͙̼̭t̶̜h͇̜̗͈̝o̸͇̜͎̘̪̦u̟̣̼t̲̰͕̻̝͍̰ ̺͝l̶̘̜̤̻̖̪i̩̱̦f̛̮̹e̗̱͇͓,̶̱͎̦̞ ̗̬̣͔̳̥̣d̸̥e͍͘a̷̟̦̗̻͎̪t͇̯̭̠̮h̡ ̡̦͚̬͚i̹͢s ͜a̡̻̭͉͍̩̠n̬͎ ̱͙̯́ͅa̳̩̼̬b̲͉͎̟̫̰̰͠s̝̠̭̼̫͢o͎͟l̴̹̯͎̹u̫͝t̰̟e͖\nw͈͓͙͚̟͇i̵͖͎͍̖͕͎̹t̶̠̩̱̜̳̞h̥ ͏̱̱̬͎n̢͔̗ͅo̰̝̙̞ ̵̯̣̮̣ͅp̼u̪͇̜̱͎̭̘r͇̼̦̥̭̫p̧o̬s̼̙̗̰͙̰ͅe̦̥̬͖͘ͅ.́", ""),
        StaticBook("The First Ent", "Pinsir99", "The Ents are mysterious creatures that were found within the forests of Aegis, and now in Asulon. Little is known about them,, but they are often found near sacred groves or ancient trees, keeping them protected and free of disruption.\nBut the tale of the first Ent is interesting in itself.\n\nIt is said that the Aspects granted ancient and wonderful power to a certain tree older than time itself. This tree, far wiser than the entire forest,\nyearned to protect his kind, but could not do much from within the confines of his roots. So, he waited for the stars to align, and produced a seed of gold, and let it fall to the foot of his gargantuan trunk to sprout.\nThrough the course of many moon, this seed grew until it became a tree half as large as its father. However, it found that its roots were not bound in the soil, and so it walked. It roamed the forest, finding purpose under the gentle\nguidance of the Eldertree. The Ent soon found humans attempting to gel an ancient oak, which cried out in agony. Letting out a roar, the great being assumed its role as guardian of the forest, and tore through the men with unforgiving vengeance.\nAnd such is the story of the first Ent.\n\n~Unknown Origin\n\n(Copied by Aerius Adurond)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Pepe", "Asher Highwind", "The Legend\n         of the\n      Golden Pepe\nThe forgotten history of the descendants of the four races the great war of the pepe. \nAfter Ibeless had been casted into the firey pits of the nether, the world lay in ruins after the great horde of undead Ibless unleashed upon the world.\nA great power known only as \"Tythus\" decided to bless the descendants with the greatest gift of all. A way to rebuild, and thus the first pepe. Was born, he sent 4 to the pvp defaulters of the plains of Oren, 3 to the cyber dagger ears within the forests,\n4 to the squeakers under the mountain of Urugan. But Tythus needed to mantain power over the races, thus he created One Pepe to Rule them All, from the fires he forged, The Golden Pepe\n\nSeveral summers passed and the descendants lived in\nharomny with the pepe's at there side. But the power of the Golden Pepe had consumed Tythus and he wanted more power. Power that the Pepe was as if speaking to him, whispering into his ear evil thoughts to take what the descendants had that he was so\nmuch greater than all of them. And thus the whispering of the Pepe sepped into his mind, it turned the once peaceful Tythus into a Steam buying evil doer. He waged a bloody war against the descendants with the power of the Pepe at his side none could stop\nhim until a young hero by the name of Billy Bob cut the Pepe from Tythus's grasph without the pepe to sustain the evil that was inside him he faded into the air, but instead of casting the Pepe back into the fires from wince it came ((wait this sounds-\nfamiler)) He chose to weild the power of the Pepe for himself until he was slain in an ambush but before he took his final breath the Creator smiled down upon his actions to defeat the evil Tythus and brought him into the Seven Skies as his farmer. To\nharvest the fields for all enterinty ((it was awful, pretty sure he went crazy from looking at all the taters)) Yet the pepe was lost no one is quite sure what became of it the story of the pepe drifting away throughout the generations now simpily ghost\nstories that parents tell there children to keep them doclie. But the Pepe is out there somewhere looking to whisper into the next ear to start the next great war of the descendants... Lying... Waiting...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Gorundyr", "Ketiley Strong-Heart", "*It is clear to see that this book was hand written in coal. The lettering quite eloquent and fluid.*\n\n\n       The Eight Divine\n\nCopied down by Ketiley of                  Orvar.\nA Brief explanation of the           Gorundyr's Gods.\nGorund, The Invincible Light\n\nGorund, the Invincible Light is regarded as the creator of time and space by the Gorundyr priesthood. It is said that he rules the cosmos atop a celestial steed made of the stars themselves.\nIt is with his blessing that sun rises at dawn, and from his wrath that it is smashed into pieces upon the earth at dusk. Gorundyr Priests believe that the darkness of night is to prepare the mortal beings for the coming of Maratsu the Fallen One,\nfor it is with his flight that the last battle will be fought.\n\nLagara, the Goddess of Life\n\nLagara, the mother of all life, sits atop the Heart Tree, an immense tree that connects the mortal world with the cosmos.\nWhile the tree has never been seen by man, legend states it is here where she plays her magical harp. Lagara’s melody is said to keep the seasons in order and ensure that all things grow. Her form is one which closely resembles a human, as she created man\nin her image. Said to be of impossible beauty, many men would give their lives for a chance to look upon her divine form.\n\nBelenus of the Hunt\n\nIn ancient myth, Belenus is said to have been a mortal man who fell in love with Andarta, maiden of\nA hunter and gatherer, he gave up his life to pursue the whispers of Andarta within her forest. Unbeknownst to him, she became infatuated with him as well. One night, as the hour of twilight neared, she visited him in the form of a white haired human\nwoman. Feeling their love was as ancient as the trees themselves, Andarta bound herself with Belenus under the moon and the stars. With this, Belenus’ mortal form was destroyed and he was granted a seat beside the gods.  Belenus took the form of a Green\nMan, a humanoid figure that appeared to the eye as both man and tree. His love for Andarta is so fierce that he has pledged himself to defending her forests and the spirits that live within.\n(Shrines and rune stones have sprung up all around the forest\nto honour both Belenus and Andarta, with hunters and young lovers often leaving gifts and sacrifices at these places in the hopes of winning their blessings.)\n\nAndarta of the Forest\n\nAndarta sacrificed her divine form in order to create\nthe forests for she saw no other way to achieve the beauty that Gorund had shown her in his vision. It is said that she is Queen of the Forest Spirits, mythical beings that inhabit the trees themselves. Stories of Andarta often portray her as an angry\ndeity, untrusting of others around her. This is largely attributed to the betrayal of Maratsu, for if one of her brothers could commit such evil, surely no one could be trusted. Her forests are her domain and she is very wary of outsiders, be they mortal\nor divine. Offerings are made to Andarta in the hopes of gaining her acceptance and the veneration of the trees and forest spirits is a common practice among the Gorundyr peoples.\nDraug of the Sea\n\nDraug is said to be a colossal being, the largest of the gods. He rests on the sea floor in a deep slumber, awaiting offerings from the mortal men above him. The beating of his massive heart controls the currents of the ocean, and t\nslight movement of his breathing drives the tide.\n(The Gorundyr are excellent sailors, strongly developed by their need to explore and trade. It is a common practice to throw one tenth of all treasure plundered into the sea, as an offering to Draug. Ma\nsailors will sacrifice animals or throw offerings to Draug before they start a voyage in the hopes that he will guide them safely on their journey.)\n\nOknar of the Mountains\n\nRevered by blacksmiths and stonemasons, Oknar is said to be a giant st\nwho wanders the tallest mountains and their peaks. Many believe that earthquakes and landslides can be attributed to Oknar, for he still roams the lands in an attempt to perfect his work.\n(Gorundyr craftsmen can be seen singing prayers as they work, an\nit is the beauty of the land that they wish to emulate with their craft. All things created by the hands of the Gorundyr are dedicated to Oknar, and small rituals and offerings are performed whenever something is constructed.)\nArgal of the Sky\n\nArgal is one of the three sky gods, the other two being Maratsu and Ankou. Taking the form of a massive eagle, it is his task to patrol the skies and await return of his fallen brother. Argal became Master of the Sky\nafter his brothers defeat and it is believed that the slightest movement of his wings can cause the fiercest storms. Sailors often sing to him and pray for clear skies on their travels.\n(Shrines dedicated to honouring Argal are usually found atop the\nhighest mountain peaks, and require days of journey to reach. Most who make the journey do so to offer their gratitude for his protection of the skies.)\n\nAnkou the Gatherer of Souls\n\nAnkou is also known as the Blood God and the God of Death.\nFormed in the image of a great hawk, Ankou is the third and last of the sky gods. When a being dies and gains the favour of the gods, it is he who guides their soul to the heavens so that they may rest. Ankou took the betrayal of his brother to heart and\nnow he has begun gathering the souls of the dead to fight in his legion at the last battle.\n(Warriors of the Gorundyr pay their respects to Ankou by offering him the blood of their enemies. Glory and victory in battle is achieved in the name of Ankou,\nit is the blood of heathens that he feasts upon.)\n\nMaratsu, The Fallen One, is never spoken of publically by any Gorundyr. And his past will quite possibly remain hidden from voice.\nTraditional Practices:\nAnimism and Offerings -\n\nThe Gorundyr revere the gods and their ancestors. Dozens of ancient shrines litter the land, all designed to give homage to different gods.  Food, ornaments, precious metals, these are all common gi\nat these shrines. Rune stones are also erected around the land that tell ancient stories of the gods, often attracting many travellers looking to learn more.\nAncient groves are also considered places where the barrier between the spiritual world and th\nmortal one are most weak. Members of the Priesthood will often travel to these places to see a clearer picture of the gods and their plans.\n\nSacrifice\n\nSacrifice, both human and animal, is common practice among the Gorundyr people.\nSuch acts are reserved for certain times of the year, such as before a harvest or before battle. Warbands that capture survivors from their raids often sacrifice the ones they do not see fit to take as slaves.  Human sacrifice among the Gorundyr\nthemselves is less common and is seen as a great honour, their sacrifice is believed to bring great favour from the gods.\n\nBurial and Afterlife\n\nDeath is far from final, or so the Gorundyr believe.\nBurial practices consist of burying food, weapons, and ornaments with the dead. It is believed that while the mortal form will stay behind, the souls and their possessions will be gathered by Ankou and brought to the heavens where they may dine and\nslumber with Gorund. Only those whom are seen as worthy in the eyes of the gods would be ascended to the heavens and granted immortality. Those whom are deemed unworthy in the eyes of the gods will be forgotten, their mortal being the last step in their\nexistance. The Gorundyr bury their dead in large burial mounds, dozens of bodies often occupying a single one. \nCremation is not practised by the Gorundyr, and is in fact feared by all. It is believed that the burning of ones body will also destroy the\nsoul, preventing their ascension to the heavens. It is common, then, to burn those who have dishonoured the gods, such as heretics or traitors.\nPolitical System\n\nThe Gorundyr are a prideful folk and place most of their respect on strength. Operating on a clan-based system, each clan owes no allegiance to any other, leading to a lot of inner conflict over lands and resources.\nBarid the Reaver, of Orvar, grandfather to Morvan of Orvar, created a new title called the Yagar or “High King” as it is commonly known, and has been the only man in history to hold such a title. Until recently, Morvan now hold the Yagar title.\nGeography\n\nThe Gorundyr come from a region they called the Savaar, an isolated region in the northern reaches of Anthos. Mountain folk by blood, they thrive in the harsh conditions of the frozen north.\n*On this page is a map of the Gorundyr's current ocation with coordinates.*\n\nX: 127\ny: 59\nZ: -135", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great War", "Saviordude", "The Myth of the Great War\n-------------------Thousands of years ago a terrible war broke out between two mighty guilds of mages - one good and one evil - that controlled great empires. Mages on both sides vowed to fight until they were utterly triumpha\nseeking to purge their rivals from the earth. With fearsome magic and drake armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning a final victory.\nIn the proces of their warfare. the mages wrought vast devastation on the world. Forests caught fire an\nblazed till fone, islands sank into the sea, and entire races became extinct. Eventually the Aspects awakened from their slumber to witness the savage confict. Shocked by the destrucion, the Godess sent a vision to a single elf; the woman who would become\nthe first Arch Druid, Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a Druidic Order to preserver the fragile remains of her worlds ecology. With the guidance of the Aspects, the order grew in strength until it finally had the power to\nintervene in the mages's war. The force of young Druids pooled their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts.\nOnce the former mages - no longer caring about good\nversus evil - slither, bounded, loped and crwaled off into their ruined habitats the Order began to heal the world. Since then, the Druidic Order continually works to prevent such destruction from ever occuring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars\nof good and evil no longer mar the precious earth. But the order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the guilds of warring mages; those good and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows. Each guild claims it had been on the\nverge of victory and would have won, had the Druids not interfered.\n\n-Transcribed by Ol' Treehugger", ""),
        StaticBook("The Healer", "N.Y.", "vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvDevotion\nTo The Healer\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\n(A collection of poems written by a soldier who was clearly devout.)\n\n(Includes 5 poems)\nLetter to\nAllah, The Creator\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nAllah the Creator, the magnificent.\nPlease tell me if I be heaven sent.\nForgive me, my dirty deeds was desperate.\nIn this world of sin, I got a moral deficit.\nDeath to me the only thing that’s definite.\nCorrupt rule the world, \nbut when you’re dead that’s irrelevant.\nSometimes I think back to the old days.\nStart slippin’, fallin’ back to my old ways.\nLivin’ dangerous, \nI hope I live to see old age.\nPardon me, I’m just goin’ through a cold phase.\n\n-Your Servant\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nI Relapsed When \nI Wrote This\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nIn the kitchen, cauldron open for the heat.\nCookin’ all night, the house stink of green.\nGot my shirt off, it’s a Khalestine summer.\nI hope these fumes don’t wake my mother.\nMy rafiqis come over to tell their stories.\nWorried that they smell it, get em’ out in a hurry.\nAnd I ain’t ever comin’ out, I’m stayin’ in my home\nUntil the water boils hotter than where Shai’tan roams.\nFill a pipe with freshly cooked green, \nGet this shit off my chest.\nShow me some far off dreams,\nAnd leave me to rest.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nIdle Thoughts\nShai'tan's Toy\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nIt’s like everyday that I wake up,\nI stare into space, don’t say much.\nWipe my brow, numb from the face up.\nIt’s still hot but the summer’s over.\nShort on luck like a three leaf clover.\nBut still hopin’ that you walk in\nSo that we can get to talkin’.\nAllah says that I don’t get to forget you.\nBut it’s I that chooses to wait for you.\nEven if you don’t come back.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nAll Of The\nChild Soldiers\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nNow this little dwarf got a sword \nFrom the local blacksmith’s forge.\nHe bought it with the mina \nHe got from his chores.\nHe robbed the baker’s store\nTold her get down on the floor. \nPut the cookies in the bag, \ntake the gold out the drawer.\n\nLittle Pordinski got a sword \nHe got from the rebels\nTo kill the farfolk infidels \nand Savoie Devils.\nA sheathe on his waist,\nA bandana on his face,\nPrays to Godanistan everyday\nthat Brelus isn’t leveled.\n\nAnd Little Qali got a sword\nto cut through the cord\nThe white man tried to hang \nhim from for the Lord.\nHis rage couldn't be ignored,\nLeaped into the air and soared,\n“Allah take them with me!”\nWas the last thing he roared.\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\nBefore I pen this last poem, I wish to show my appreciation to the woman that had taken me in as her son when I was a young Qali. She has by far been one of the kindest folks I've come across in my life thus far. Although I do not consider myself a\ngood writer or even a writer by trade, she has urged me to take on a hobby when I have idle time on my hands to help me feel better about things. These poems are not just about me. They portray the stories of dead rafiqis and those unable to get their\nvoices out there. So shokran, Mama. This next piece I hold dearest to me - it's something different and close to heart.\nDevotion To The \nHealer - The Poem\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv\n\nThe Diamond, albeit once precious to others,\nis trapped - it cannot move if it cannot adorn.\nUsed to being loved, the loneliness set in.\nIt implanted ideas of dullness, imperfection.\nThat the diamond is no longer worth anything.\nThat is when the healer who came from nowhere\narrived one day. Wishing to break the internal\nstruggle, the diamond calls out to the healer.\nThe healer is taken back, surprised by the \ndiamond’s gesture. She too was alone for \nquite some time. The diamond spoke of wishing\nto see far off lands and wanting new friends.\nIt spoke of adventure and fighting monsters.\nThe diamond wanted to see the world and \nrecreate what it had lost before it was trapped.\nThe healer smiled and held the diamond tight in her\nhands so not to drop it. She felt the cracks in the\ndiamond - far from the truth that it would last forever.\nBut the healer was kind, and over time mended these \ncracks thus making the diamond whole again.\nWhile they went through their ups and downs, \nthe diamond loved the healer and the healer loved the diamond in turn.\nNot just for eachother’s outward\nappearances, but for what was inside - whatever\nthat was. Despite the love between the healer and\nher jewel, feelings of inadequacy and the growing\ndependence on each other became too much.\nWishing to find herself and become a better person,\nthe healer left the diamond in their home with promises\nto return when she could be stronger for the diamond.\nThe loneliness returned and the diamond feared\nthe healer was wearing rubies, sapphires, and emeralds.\nThat she no longer wanted the diamond. Overtime the\ndiamond began to blacken and it no longer sparkled\nlike it did when adorning healer. It wanted no\nother wearer and shunned all attention that came its way.\nThrough all the trials and tribulations the diamond went \nthrough, the hardships endured and the pain it caused\nto others, the diamond was now no different than a piece\nof coal. It was then that the diamond could not fulfill its\npurpose - that being to adorn the healer and help her shine. \nNow it questions, if the healer does return, would she still wear him even if he was no longer precious?\n\nvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv", ""),
        StaticBook("The Heist", "Elrach", "Well, well well. It seems as though you have once again, despite your best efforts, become a pawn in one of my rather elaborate ruses, and it seems as though the end result of said rusehas left your state being of a lesser quality than you had dealt\nthe card hidden up my sleeve while being none the wiser. And yes, while it is true that you will eventually recover from this recent turn of events, it remains unclear whether your social status on this city will remain at its current level,\nor if it will take a turn for the worse. After all is said is done, at the end of the day, you will have to accept the fact that you just got the short end of the deal. I hold no remorse or regret for I am and always shall be a master ruseman.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Heretic", "Beltran", "\"The mountains form, rise above the land, but mountains deepers beneath his hands, rise higher than any mountains so, for mountains beneath the ocean knows.\n\nFrom his tentacled form, his terrible eye, doth the ocean formed by thy, many hands, he is-\nthe creator, oceans his tears and lakes his liquor. \n\nWorship his form, worship his name, for his name is key to this game. Of life between it's ocean depths, else thy be felled, to an untimely death.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Hungry Bunny", "Unknown", "The\n   Hungry Bunny\n\n     by Unknown\nA hungry bunny once found the vegetable garden of a rich man who never, never, never ate vegetables. So the hungry bunny ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then he went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the hungry bunny brought another bunny and then there were two hungry bunnies. They each ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the two hungry bunnies brought another hungry bunny and then there were three hungry bunnies. Each ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the three bunnies brought another bunny and then there were four hungry bunnies. They all ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the four bunnies brought another bunny and then there were five hungry bunnies. They all ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the five bunnies brought another bunny and then there were six hungry bunnies. They all ate a cabbage, two heads of lettuce and three carrots. Then they went hop-hippity-hop right home.\nThe next evening the rich man who never, never, never ate vegetables wondered what happened to his vegetable garden. He never guessed the six hungry bunnies hiding behind the fence ate his cabbages, his lettuce and carrots. But we know better!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kal'Varak", "Archmage Crumena", "The Kal'Varak\nRescribed by Arch-Mage Crumena V. Illwindor on the 2nd of the First Seed, 1473.\nThe Kal'Varak, which roughly translates as 'Mind City', is an ancient crystalline artifact. It was dug up by the dwarves of Karik just prior to\ntheir unearthing of the hibernating dragons, but the faded scratches on the side suggest it has been discovered at least once before this, perhaps by the original inhabitants of Karik. It seems to be some sort of powerful magical nexus, exerting a\nsignificant magical influence without appearing to draw magical power anywhere, as if it somehow generates it itself. Despite this, the Kal'Varak is useless as a source of magical energy. All of its power is turned inwards on itself, giving the\nKal'Varak the bizzare property that gives it its name. When a living being touches the Kal'Varak, their mind and soul are forcefully drawn from their bodies into the Kal'Varak itself. Once inside, they find themselves in a strange dreamworld, often\ntaking the form of a maze, populated by their memories, dreams and nightmares. In the Kal'Varak, people appear as they would wish to be, some see themselves as stronger, taller, more attractive, sometimes as a different race\nentirely. While the ability to walk through one's mind and the minds of any others currently 'in' the Kal'Varak may seem enticing, the dreamworld is dangerous. The dreamworld responds to moods, fears and doubts, often turning a\nguilty memory into a full-blown nightmare in an instant. The more complex the mind, the more labyrinthian the maze, and those with dark pasts they'd rather forget are often forced to face them within the Kal'Varak. Even more dangerous is\nwhen the mind and crystal form a world that one would not want to leave. The collapsed body outside the crystal still needs food, water, and is still vunerable to harm. If the body dies, the mind cannot return to it. Somewhere in the Kal'Varak maze is\na door, and those more experienced with the dreamworld can find it more quickly than others. The door is always relevant in form to the person it belongs to, often impossible to mistake for one's own. Sometimes the door is not even a door, but it is\nalways clearly an exit. Passing through your door returns you to your body, but if you pass through the wrong door, you may find yourself in the wrong body entirely.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Light Behind", "GusanoArentonio", "So long to all my friends\nEveryone of them met tragic ends\nWith every passing day\nI'd be lying if I didn't say\nThat I miss them all tonight\nAnd if they only knew what I would say\nIf I could be with you tonight\nI would sing you to sleep\nNever let them take the light behind your eyes\nOne day I'll lose this fight\nAs we fade in the dark\nJust remember you will always burn as bright\nBe strong and hold my hand\nTime-it comes for us, you'll understand\nWe'll say goodbye today\nAnd I'm sorry how it ends this way\nIf you promise not to cry\nThen I'll tell you just what I would say\nIf I could be with you tonight\nI would sing you to sleep\nNever let them take the light behind your eyes\nI'll fail and lose this fight\nNever fade in the dark\nJust remember you will always burn as bright\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your\n\nSometimes we must grow stronger and\nYou can be stronger when I'm gone\nWhen I'm here, no longer\nYou must be stronger and\nIf I could be with you tonight\nI would sing you to sleep\nNever let them take the light behind your eyes\nI failed and lost this fight\nNever fade in the dark\nJust remember you will always burn as bright\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes\nThe light behind your eyes", ""),
        StaticBook("The little golem", "Yden", "The little golem that could\nBy Yden\n\nJames was one of many golems in golem school, he was taught lots of subjects but he was best at following instructions class because he studied hard and practiced, when James got his degree in following orders he\napplied for a job, he would serve the common folk, James demonstrated his ability but he was much too cumbersome, he kept bumping into everything and his feet were too big, they broke floor boards and cracked the stone beneath his feet, his smaller friend\nTimmothy got the job instead so instead he applied to serve a knight, again he showed the knight what he could do, he shined the armour but his hands were too big and he was too strong, he simply crushed the armour like paper when he handled it so his\nmedium sized friend Jakob got the job instead. James was feeling very sad at this point, he felt like nobody wanted him, he was too wide, his feet were too big, he was too strong and his hands were too big but in one final attempt to serve a master he\napplied to serve the king, the king allowed him to perform and he excelled, the king had marble floors, the strongest floors money could buy, every room was huge so he would never bump into anything and the kings armour was made of mythril, not even James\ncould bend mythril so James was given the status of kings golem and served the king with honor until the king fell ill, James was very sad but he served the prince instead to carry on his great work!\n\n-Yden \nAlso see; The golem who learnt to love\nAlso see; The musical golem", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mother", "Dak'ir Des'Nox", "Delilah De'laronge\n       The Mother\n\n\n\n\nDark Elven Ancestors\n       Volume 1.\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Dak'ir Des'Nox\nDelilah, or Della as those who knew her referred to her as, was a kind hearted mali'ker with a heart as big as her belly. She was no warrior, nor was she a doer of great deeds.\n\nDella was a champion of another kind. One of the home. Kind words were her\nweapons and a warm meal her shield. Born in Asulon, she and her family traveled from city to city for work. All the while, Della honed her cooking skills through out the years. \n\nIn Anthos, the Mother encountered one of the few things you'd hear her say\nshe detested, The Black Scourge. Della cared for all and seeing the Scourge ruin village after village, city after city. It racked her heart with grief. So it was not uncommon for her to grab her frying pan and fly into action if she suspected someone of\nbeing associated with the dark order. \n\nBut it was in the cold lands of Thales that she came to settle with kin. The short and rather round woman found herself at the gates of Ker'lomi. Within days she had settled into the tavern and made our\ncold cavern into a warm home, full of laughs and small comforts. Sweets to hearty stews, or even a knitted scarf. \n\nDella remained with our kin for a long time, until the elven civil war of Athera. Not long after those events she departed the land and\nhas not been since. But she remains in the hearts of those who knew her.\n\nThough her fate was never known, we honour Delilah as 'The Mother' for her deeds of love and kindness.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mountain", "Ted Dekkar", "~Misunderstandings~\n\nListen, children, to a story that was written long ago, about a kingdom on a mountain; and the valley folk below.\n\nOn the mountain was a treasure, buried deep beneath the stone.\nAnd the valley people swore, that they'd have it for their very own.\n\nSo the people loved the valley, sent a message up the hill, asking for the buried treasure; tons of gold for which they'd kill.\nCame an answer from the kingdom. \n\n\"With our brothers, we will share all the secrets of our mountain, and the riches buried there.\"\n\nNow the valley cried with anger!\n\"Mount your horses, draw your sword!\"\n\nAnd they killed the mountain people, so they won their just reward.\n\nNow they stood beside the treasure, dark and red; turned the stone and looked beneath it...\n\"Peace on Earth\" was\n\n       all it said.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pumpkin Lord", "A Ravenous Adventurer", "So Hungry.. so very, very hungry I was... lost in the wilderness I was, oh yes, lost I was.... no food... just filthy water... tasteless water...\n\n And then... I saw him... A walking pumpkin... pumpkin pie... food... precious, precious food...\nI lunged at it... I chased it.. oh, it smelled so sweet... I chased it away from the city... the foul, filthy human city.... until an elf... cruel, disgusting elf...\n\nThe elf approached the delicous, precious, pumpkin man... he wanted to kill it...\nI wished the same.....\n\nWe fought him.... the pumpkin man.... then the treacherous, filthy pumpkin man offered a trade.... his body to the elf.... for my arm...\n\nThe treacherous, filthy elf.... he took my arm... but not before the evil pumpkin man....\ndecided he wanted the elf's arm instead....\n\nThe evil, pumpkin man... he cut off the filthy elf's arm...\n\nThen... we fought him... and finally... the filthy elf got his finger.... and ran off...\nThen.... I got one of his.... other fingers.... Then.... the pumpkin man shouted....\n\n\"I am Knox, the Pumpkin Lord!\"\n\nThen... he ran off.... and I did as well.... limping towards the moat.... pumpkin finger in hand... only one arm....\nHungry...\nSo Hungry....\nBut so much pain....\nCan't write... any more...\n*This page is soaked in blood and smells faintly of pumpkins*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sea", "Elluna Koortova", "The Sea\n*The writing would be beautifully written in script.*\n\nThe Sea.\n\nMystery. We all recognize the sea, but what do we know of her? All I know is that her visage captivates me so. She..\nHas a gentle appearance with harmonious waves that run across her surface.. The pervading warmth from the glimmering rays that run off the essence that is her beauty. However, what captivates me most is her endless depth. What lies beneath the sea?\nWhat secrets doth she hold? Well.. All I can do is gaze into her shimmering eyes, and wonder. What thoughts run through her flowing mind? Indeed, I’d wonder if her radiant beauty has ever paid much heed to me, a bystander.. -Ink drip-\nNonetheless, she is the one I hold feelings for. The person who is my sea, you, Gaelyn. \n\n\n*There would be a few fancy squiggles here.*\n\n\n    ~A Bystander~\n*Cough, Cough, A Cassius,*\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sewer", "Arthur Caulfield", "The Sewer\n           By\n         Arthur\n        Caulfield\nIt is the sewer, in which I live. A rank and stinking tunnel of which no man would ever set foot. I am alone down here, sitting quietly, waiting. The darkness creates shadows of harrowing ghouls. Even I find myself jumping at each echoed sound.\nThis is why I am paranoid. No sound is ever pure. In a world of tunnels and halls every sound is one that has been bounced around and repeated over and over, so that by the time it reaches your own ears, you may never know where it originated.\nBut of course, the question you ask. Why would such a feared creature such as me, be afraid of boogie men in the dark? I tell you now, in the sewers I am not to be feared.\nFor if you have ever ventured into a sewer at what would be the lowest point in your life, you will know that what lay down there would destroy the minds of high elves and orcs alike.\nNothing stops them from venturing to the surface, they could invade cities, burn down petrus with their horrid image. The eyes of citizens would melt, leaving only liquid to run down their cheeks.\nOf course, I get ahead of myself, for if you are reading you have not been down here. To a place of O such abandoned horror, not too mention the distaste of all who are civilized. Which is why I would like to describe for you,\nthe image of such creatures scarier than me. \n   Bright yellow spots on their backs, painful and sore. Balding heads, with fragments of fragile hair left and unkept.\n  Spines so bent they can not walk without pain.\nFeet featuring sharp toe nails that could cut a nobleman's sword. Noses that smell and pick out their prey. Skin as pink as a rich woman’s nails but as soft as fresh dough in your hands. \n  This is what I face every day.\nThough down here there is no day or night, only darkness all of the time. I feel myself going crazy, I don’t understand it. I have over a dozen eyes but am subject to the worst view and the most terrifying life.\nYou shouldn’t try to save me. I would hurt you. My fangs, over three inches long equipped with venom, would paralyse you before I even realised what I had done.\n   It’s not your fault. And it’s not mine.\nI can’t run the risk of greeting something that could be my doom. I’ve seen plenty of my own kind decapitated, ripped apart and eaten. I don’t want to hurt you, but I don’t want to die. \n  This is why I choose to stay in my tunnel.\nIt is mine. Scattered with web, damp and dark. Far enough away from any nest of the abominations. Close enough to the entrance that I can hear the world. \n  I can’t leave of course. No one down here has ever done that.\nGoing out there would scare the civilized. And scaring the civilized means being taken down by a mob of weapons. So I sit down here, content with just listening. \n  Every now and then I will here parts of conversation.\nSomeone bought a stale loaf of bread, another is excited about a wedding. I do not understand the context of what they say, but I revel in the idea of having a conversation with another being.\nI am apart of an aggressive species. Dominance is the only way to live life. It is my duty, nay, my instinct to destroy every other of my kind. I do not want to, I must.\nI enjoy the rain. It is supposedly cleaner than the water down here. It does not have the musky odour or the putrid colour. \n  The sound is hypnotic, listening to each drop hit the earth above calms me, it lets me ignore every other sound.\nIt let’s me remove my guard for just a day, before I am aware of the dangers once more. \n  Somedays, when all is quiet. And only the ripples in the dirty water move.\n  I stare at the tunnel walls.\nI wonder how long ago it must have been, when humans built it. How long ago it must have been since they were last down here.\n   The walls have begun to deteriorate, sometimes I hope it will crumble,\nand I will be sealed into this tomb worthy only of my presence.  Even with eight legs I could not escape that fate. \n   But my kind is supposed to act on instinct, and so I do.\nSo I do not look for a way to better my existence, I simply live out what has been given to me. I do not try to escape.", ""),
        StaticBook("The SoulStream", "Zafirah", "The SoulStream\n\n\nThis illustration covers the realm known as the soulstream, a dimension of the ArchAnguel, Aerial.\nIt's a place where all souls of the deceased travel after death.\nAt this moment, the individual that had just perished will find themselves peering down at their own lifeless form that harbored their soul. Only then to have a bright light manifest, this is actually a rift being formed. Which cannot be be seen by any\nstill inhabiting in the mortal realm. Unless they too are lost souls, an example being ghosts. If they too step into the rift. The spectral being will be pulled into the soulstream.\nThere are three different sections of the soulstream, which will be labeled here, but explained more throughly in a separate of their own with these pages.\nDesert of the Damned\n\n\nThis location within the soulstream is the first to be discussed. It's where all the warped, twisted souls of dark beings go after they finally pass on into true death. It's a place much like what it's name suggests.\nA barren, desert-like location that carries no forms of life like structures. Cold and warped by what such be its natural colors, the ground also twists and sways with a rippling effect. It serves as a permanent prison for all corrupted and evil beings.\nThat being those who had mercilessly murdered, tortured, cast any kinds of warping to others souls and even traitors end up here. They are left to wander aimlessly, unable to progrss through to find peace, only suffering is found here.\nSacellum of Aerial\n\n\nA grand city, that shines with white and gold colors.This is where the souls of fallen Ascended tend tirelessly within to carry on Aerial's will, guiding good mannered souls that lived as kind mortals further along.\nThe Ascended that have moved fro mthe mortal realm also keep an eye upon the unruly souls of the damned outside it's walls. Making sure they're kept in check and thwarting any attempt of entering this location.\nAerial herself remains in the very center of Sacellum, constantly directing those within her domain, and upon the mortal realm. And so it shows the eternal duty of all Ascended, in life and death to keep the journey of the soul moving forth.\nAnd protectign the soulstream itself with all their strength and wits. If failure ever transpired, the corrupted souls cast into the Desert of the Damned would threaten to wash over her great city, causing unheard amounts of chaos.\nThat is why an balance of living and Ascended must be kept for the natural consistency must be established.\n\nThe fight against the dark will never end until all twisted souls, last tainted Daemon and Drakkar lay in ruin. Only on this day will\nthe struggle finally be over with.\nWell of Distribution\n\n\nThe final location of the soulstream is located within the center of Sacellum. It serves as the final location for all souls passing through the 'city of light' as have personally named it. They are then sent to where they\nbelong, whether it's the Seven Skies, Xan's Realm, or any of the multible locations a soul can finally call home after death. One thing is certain, this place is vital to Aerial's will and making sure the souls of the dead do not build up here over time.\nIt's supposedly shaped like that of an actual, massive well. Where they're carried off and transported safely and without disruption. Thusly carrying out hte natural cycle of life and death without any tampering from outside powers.\nThis concludes the explanation on the Soulstream and what transpires within.\n\n\nThe document read here was recorded by Zafirah with the direct information given by Master Sage Heial.\n\nMay Aerial Guide you.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Story", "The March Ash", "The time I spend in the waking world seems only moments compared to my time in the Far Glade. How I wish it were the opposite. There is a feeling of inevitability about this place, that I fear will infect the rest of my life.\nThe Far Glade tells a story, but it is one that is still being written. Despite it all, November, I know that our story is over.", ""),
        StaticBook("The tail of Bell", "Beltran", "Come hither and hear my tale, of how my status in life how somehow becometh reversed, grant me one moment with forsooth's ear, and allow me to regale you with my taleth of nobility in the humble parish of Caliphate.\nIn the rolling lily fields of Pennsylvania I sprang forth from the womb\nMy days filled with the innocent pursuits of boyhood\nRetreating from the hot sting of the sun’s rays I frolicked in the most carefree way.\nSport shooting pheasants with my dear kin folk. When a band of miscreants, true rapscallions who's hearts contain no morsel of goodness.\nEnacted wrongful tribulation upon thy peacful shire. I engorged in a bout of fisticuffs of no true magnitude, mymothe-\nr,.. trembling with fear. 'Off with you!' she cried to the esteemed estate of your mon uncle. Philip Banks esquire.\n\nWith a whistle I hailed a carriage and secured passage to aforementioned estate\nInscribed on the carriage were the letters F-R-E-S-H and the driver carried on his person a six sided trinket of vice\nLet it be noted this chaise was truly without equal\n\nHowever I paid it no mind and ordered that we depart post haste\nI promptly arrived on the grounds at a juncture around seven in the evening\nAnd I called to the quartermaster “Release me from thy fowl stench, you are utterly macabre.”\n\nI gazed upon my royal grounds, I journey no longer.\nTo sit on my throne as the Prince of Bel-air.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tiny Hippo", "Elluna Koortova", "The Tiny Hippo\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n   By Gaelyn Sarino\n\n         ©1454\nThere once was a tiny hippo, in a tiny world, in a tiny universe.\n\nHis name was Tiny Hippo.\n\nTiny Hippo had a tiny cart.\n\nHe loved that cart, and they went everywhere together.\nLaughing and playing all throughout their tiny world. \n\nThen one day, Tiny Raven swooped down and stole the tiny cart.\n\nThis made Tiny Hippo very sad, but he decided he would be brave\nSo the next day, he walked up the tiny mountain…\n\n...Crossed through the tiny Valley….\n\n…..Climbed up the tiny oak tree….\n\nAnd shanked Tiny Raven’s tiny bitch ass.\nAin’t no one fucks with Tiny Hippo.\nAin’t no one.\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Vander Code", "Lexa", "=-=+=-=+=-=+=-=+=-=\n\n   The  Vander  Code\n   =-=+=-=+=-=+=-=+=-=\n\nAn excerpt taken from:\n The Vander Ideology\n\n Written by:  Nafis, Vandalore I Antiquus\n=-=+=-=\n  We as Vanders will come to know this code by heart of course, but for the time being this book will help you remember everything there is to be known about the Vander Code.\n         =-=+=-=\n=-=+=-=\n  -The Vander Code is held with the utmost importance among us as Vanders.Not only does it offer stability, it is a goal for the individual to strive towards in hopes of becoming a better person in a world that is cruel and corrupt.\nTo both accept the state of the realm and still strive to thrive in what many would find uninhabitable.\n          =-=+=-=\n\n “The weak deserve to die so that the strong may flourish.”\n~ Nafis, Vandalore I Antiquus\n-=The Vander Code=-\n          =-=+=-=\n“To serve the Vandalore in valour and faith”\n“To refrain from the wanton giving of offence”\n“To live by honour and for glory”\n“To obey those placed in authority”\n“To guard the honour of fellow Vanders”\n“To at all times to speak the truth”\n“To persevere to the end in any enterprise begun”\n“To never to refuse a challenge from an equal”\n“To never to turn the back upon a foe”", ""),
        StaticBook("The Writing Desk", "Romane Niwarsay II", "In the attic, the creeking of rustic wood echoed through the dim, candle lit room below. Out of the shadows the shapes of what would be shelves adorned with books, nic-nacs, and various clutter all accompanied by their various histories and stories\nuntold. There, where the candle's flame licked from, was a desk amongst the shelves of meaningful paper bound with cracked leather. A chair accompanied the said desk and included an individual who diligently penned creative writings\nwith every mark. The individual had been working at their task for quite some time on that wintery day.\nBundled within their warm clothing the individual perspired, as a writer would, great stories of fantastic events unlived by mortal beings. On the\nopposite side of the room from the desk gleamed a lone window glittered with gentle snow. The howl of crisp wintery wind rapped at the glass pane asking to be let in. In isolation, the envigorated writer continued at their mission. They continued\nspinning tales of unspooled woes, threading histories to interweave their nature, and like most tailors, the individual wanted to make a living. Yet in the cruel world the lets death rain frozen from the sky, the individual knew that it was an unreal\nproposition to which they shook their head with dismay. They pondered for a time at which they would be freed from the chambers at which they remain. Trapped in the darkness, the ever lasting darkness, that crawls up their towers of sanity\nonly to knock on the door of grief.\nYet the writer continued on, trudging through every word, every sentence, every paragraph. With breath growing cold they took a pause to recollect their thoughts, only to remember that\nthey had a lone mug of tea steaming at their side. With an eager reach of the hand, the individual noticed that the mug was surprisingly light. Perhaps even empty at that. To no surprise it twas yet the wordsmith could not ponder as to why it was empty\nwhen they had no thought of drinking the drought dry previously. With another shake of the head in disapproal, they set it down onto the rough cut rustic desk and rested their cold cheek onto the cold fist that would drag the pen accross a page.\nThe candle, growing ever so stout, stood stalwart at the individuals perpetual glare. They wondered, somberly if there would ever be a time that they would kindle a flame of happiness. Perhaps to have something good graciously given\nto them as if to make everything worth it all. Even with the position of their state of mind, the wordmaker resented nothing as everything they possessed was just enough, even though they wished for more. \"How could anyone not wish\nfor more?\" they asked to the darkness surrounding them. Which then replied resiliently, \"Because they may already have it all.\" --A Short Story by Romane Letus Niwarsay II ((Arctic_Guard))", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome: Air Evo.", "The Scribe", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocationist Alatar of the Mage Academy.\n\nRecopied by The Scribe\nTable of Contents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\nChapter 1:\nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by complete darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas.\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it’s ‘blank’ concept. Meditation is most efficient and common way, as I have found.\nLearn how to blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to create your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and Air are essences to all life around the realm of existence. You breathe it into your very self.\nWith the art of air evocation, you manipulate it. Wind is unpredictable and one of the best studied branches of arcane magics. You must experience the element in it’s true from before you can even think about summoning it.\nIn order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a region of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it.\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch how tthe wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or carries it away.\n\nChapter 3:\nAfter you have learned all there is to to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; You may begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Though combining all of this. A small amount of wind may be conjured.\nWARNING: You may pass out a few times upon first connection.\n\nChapter 4: \nAfter you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationists arsenal.\nThe first and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large and forceful push at an enemy. Secondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado.\nA skilled air evocationist can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most objects out of your sphere. That concludes this tome.\n\nFor any other questions, feel free to visit the Mages' Guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tour Guide", "Kage", "Access to castle by a single bridge\n\nOnly one gate at first enterance to city, Iron\n\nSecond gate into Plaza, only one iron gate\n\nMultiple enterances to plaza on all sides\n\nBath house for some sexy times...\nCatherdral cause why not, left exit from plaza, turn right and straight ahead\n\nNorth gate, leads to fucking no where but around the edges of the island\n\nsecond plaza through right exit of first\nLeft from second exit up to castle, only singular gate, both doors locked\n\nSecond bridge to south gate\n\nMain shop area in first plaza and through main gate\nNot a very busy city, no guards seen and only one visiting citzen spotted\n\n\n~By The Amazing Ker", ""),
        StaticBook("Transfig notes-1", "Lefkos Amethil", "Transfiguration Notes\n\nA simple account of a beggining Transfigurationist attempting an early staged transmutation upon a piece of Ferrum, aiming to turn it into a rod. Written by Lefkos Amethil.\nFirst it began as being handed a simple ferrum sphere from my teacher, given instructions on how to learn about it, figure out the mana signature of it, and how it reacts to near everything. Once this could be achieved, I would be able to transmute\nthe Ferrum sphere.\n\nI began to meditate with it daily, sending my mana out and 'poking' at it in a sense. Over time I would gain a familiarity of the ferrums 'mana signature'. Mana signatures generally relate to the fact that everything, inanimate\nand animate, have mana held within it. The mana signature itself is the specific way mana lays itself out within materials, as well as how much mana is actually within it. Learning this was only part of it, and I next had to experiment with the ferrum. I\ndid everything I could do, until I was sure I knew everything about the metal. Then I aimed to actually transmute it.\nI stood before the ferrum sphere then, letting out a sigh as I connected with the void. I held my palm out towards the object then, concentrating on my own mana. I imagined, and forced, it to leave me. This came to be in the form of red wisps of light,\nthe color of my aura, beggining to exude from my very hand and enveloping the metal upon my command. I imagined the Ferrum as I would an element in the void, and aimed to control it in the same way. The same way I increase the intensity of my sparks while\nsummoning electricity, as well as how a fire evocationist grows the heat of their flames.. I imagined this affect upon the ferrum, and willed it to happen. I near instantly began to grow tired, yet continued this. I quickly began to feel the metal heating\nup, growing red underneath the already crimson shade of my aura. I then controlled it the same I would an evocation, slowly shaping it out. The metal bent, and sweat poured down my face. Eventually it formed into a crude, yet still apparent\nmetal rod. Afterwards I stumbled back, exhausted. As soon as I recovered, I began to repeat the process with other materials..", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_ASUL_2(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Travel journal", "Sirari Aeraendsyr", "8th of Snow's Maiden-\n\nSince traveling away from my beloved home of Vailor and ending up in the Isles of Axios with many others, I have finally started to create my own path in life. In the city of Haria I took up a few hobbies.\nThe first would be breeding. Being of wood elven heritage, it's only natural that I would take a liking to animals. My mage friend even helped me build my own animal pen. I took it upon myself to make it my permanent residence.\n\nThe second thing I've\ndecided to do goes hand-in-hand with breeding; and that is leather working. I can't wait to find some iron ingots and make saddles, in hopes in find a horse somewhere in the wilderness and tame it. \nAnd that's not everything either. I decided to expand my\nhorizons to places other than Haria..\n\nIn the wood elven city, I've finally become a dedicant. I can't wait to become a Druid, and maybe one day I will find my parents' seed and join them. They would be so proud of me, and perhaps we could start our own\nseed in some other old forests. \n\nMy teacher is Prince Artimec. I respect him highly, but some others don't seem to feel the same way, due to experiences of him having strange intentions with women. It's understandable, and for this reason\nI will make sure to keep our relationship completely non-personal. \n\nSpeaking of becoming a Druid, something has been bothering me... someone told me there is a third Aspect named Nemiisae, whom is the true Aspect of death. I was debating on whether or\nnot to ask my teacher about it. This is something I haden't heard about in my 123 years of being alive, until now. The thought that there is the possibility of a God that doesn't get the the worship and prayers they deserve, is truly saddening. Although\nfrom what I've been told, this Aspect doesn't care about being known. She works in the shadows, valuing only the natural decay of life. Because of course, there would not be life without death. It's a cycle of beauty.\n\nFor my last note, I'll\nadd that I'm debating on helping Oren with their writing counsil. Due to the war between them and Haria, I'm not sure if this will occur at all. But it would be a nice extra thing to do with my time..", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "Dela Vaik", "My time in the Oder of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. Lets start by steps.\n\nstep 1- Cleaning the wound\nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or deeper wounds you'll need something\nwith alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sort. (Of course you need to take the dirt out if there is any in the wound first.) \n\nStep 2- Suttering the wound.\nFor that you will need a needle and some thread. sounds easy right? well not\nreally, you need a steady hand and you also so need to do it by theese... Lets call them sub types.\n Sub type 1\nheat up the needle incase it holds any illnesses.\nSub type 2 clean the thread\nYou need to do it because you do not want dirt in\nthe wound.\nSub type 3 shuttering\nYou startat well the start of the wound or gash.(warning this does not include small wounds.) you'll then shutter it like you are sewing a rag, a messy, bloody rag that screams like a little girl, a rag non of the\nless.\nStep 3- bandaging\nA bandage can be almost any thing, a old rag (as long as its clean.) A bed sheet (as long as its clean.) etc. then you just wrap it up. Done.\n\nBy: Kristoff Herrick", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "Kristoff Herrick", "Wound healing\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet's start by steps\nStep 1- Cleaning the wound. \nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or\ndeeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. (ofcourse you need to take the dirt off first if it has dirt in it). \nStep 2- Suttering the wound. \nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread.Sounds easy\nright? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these...Let's called them sub steps.\nSub Step I Heat up the needle. You need to do that incase of the needle carring any illness.\nSub Step II Clean the thread.You need to do\nit beacause you don't want dirt on your wound.\n \nSun Step III-Suttering You start at well the start of the gash or deep wound (Warning this does NOT apply for small wounds.) \nYou'll then sutter like your sewing a rag, a messy and bloody rag\nthat screams like a little girl, non the less a rag. \n\nStep 3-Bandaging\nA bandage can be almost anything, a old rag (As long as it's clean) A bed sheet (As long as it's clean) etc. Then you just wrap it around the wound. Done\nNote: If there's any sign of infection after or  before you done this process you'll be better off cuting off the leg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tristan The Bard", "Aepholis", "The soft breeze touches Tristan's skin, as he wakes up in his lower class bed, small windowcrack open. Tristan gets swiftly up on his feet, as he'd grab his favorite turquise blue shirt, buttoning up, as he fetches his black pair of trousers.\nHe'd grab his colorful royal blue coat from a hanging rack, along with his feather trilby, heading to the local inn, flute slinged over his right shoulder.  As he heads to the local inn of Aldersberg, whistling a small tune, a nice smirk on his face.\nAs he enters, the inn seems crowdy, the brightness moody and candles lighting the place. He nods firmly to Ciera, aswell as two other lovely ladies. He orders a glass of red wine from Ciera, handing her the sufficient minas.\nHe slowly gulps it down, as he brings the flute up to his puffy lips, a soft and gentle melody starting to play. Three burly mates arch a brow at Tristan, shaking their heads disapprovingly.\nOne raises, walking forward to Tristan.\nTristan nods to the lad, as his flute is suddenly pulled away from his lips, drool connecting between. Tristan frowns, as he'd hear a crack, the man breaking the pipe in half. A elegant man, puffing on his pipe raises, heading to the scene.\nHe'd nod to the burly man, of the name Tor, as he'd put a hand gently on Tristan's shoulders, shaking his head, grip on his gold-tipped cane tightening slightly, as he'd give Tor a hateful and mean look, before walking away with Tristan.\nTor grumbles, sending a kick for the back of the elegant man's knee, causing him to fall facefront, making quite the ruckus. The man chuckles, as he'd raise, dusting dust off his fine clothing, tilting his head at Tor, smirking widely.\nTristan gulps worriedly, as he'd step a bit back, glancing between the two. The elegant man turns again, as Tor sends a punch for the back of his head, grabbing a bottle from a table, breaking it on the edge of the table itself.\nThe elegant man is hit in the back of the head with a fist, as he'd swiftly turn on his heel and send the gold-part of the cane into Tor's jaw, a loud crack being heard. Tor cringes exremely, falling to the ground, as the elegant man turns yet again.\nThe two burly chaps raise from their seats, one unsheathing an axe, while the other draws a dagger. The elegant man frowns slightly, as this will be a challenge. He notes that a few of the customers have left the establishment.\nHe glances at Ciera, that remains behind the counter, a slight frown on her small face. He'd take a step back, as the axe wielding mate charges at him, putting a foot infront of him, causing him to fall onto a table.\nThe lad holding the dagger approaches slowly, sending a slash for the elegant man's chest, as the man would send his cane onto the dagger wielder's temple. The dagger chap falls down to the ground, unconsious, as the elegant man turns.\nThe axe wielding chap charges, as he'd send a punch for the elegant man's nose. The elegant chap is punched, stumbling back, before sending the tip of his cane into the attacker's adam's apple, causing him repeated coughing, before he'd fall down, dead.\nThe elegant man turns to Tristan, before he'd glance at all the three defeated men, darting his eyes at Ciera, letting out a simple \"Apologies.\" as he'd grasp onto the collar of each one of them, throwing them out. Tristan grins happily at the elegant lad\nThe elegant man nods to Tristan, glancing down at the flute, frowning slightly, before he'd nod to Ciera and Tristan, heading out by himself, shutting the door, of course.\n-This novel is dedicated to the innkeeper herself, Ciera Lefevre. May she enjoy the reading of this fiction, and give me an honest opinion.\n\n-Aepholis Celadithel.\n*An image of a lurky, slender and tall blonde-haired elf, with orange eyes, covers this page, the inn being his surroundings.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Undru's Notes", "The Lord of Undru", "One will always come.\n\nIt never dissappears as long as the Sildur is up in it's hands.\n\nWe won't die.\n\nIt's not the End\n\nWe are the End.\nDeath is only the start.", ""),
        StaticBook("Unification Act", "Jacob Chapel", "Articles of Unification\nAs Issued Upon the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1477\n\nSection I: Realms & Culture\nSection II: Assurances\nSection III: War Council\nSection IV: Unification Terms\nSection V: Imperial Codex\nSection I: Realms & Culture\n1. Realms of Oren are to draft, adhere, and uphold their own provincial laws, whilst in adherence to existing Imperial laws.\n2. Realms of Oren are permitted to engage in territorial growth, independent of Imperial Influence\n3. Realms of Oren and their vassals are permitted to engage in foreign conflict alongside other nations, granted the Empire holds no stance in said conflict, such as in cases of rebellions in foreign nations.\n4. Realms of Oren are permitted to establish a realm-specific Knightly Chapter, in accordance with the Grand Knight’s powers and the Chivalric Code.\nSection II: Assurances\n1. The Electorate shall never be suspended or interfered with by Imperial influence, the duties of Emperor never to be passed on hereditarily.\n2. The wide-spread cultures of Oren shall never be infringed upon\nin name of Cultural Unity, whether by majority or minority, recognizing that the cultures that make up our Empire are vast and equal.\n3. Realms of Oren and their vassals shall never be targeted or ostracized for the formation of federations,\nwhether political or economic, so long as such formations act in no way treasonous to the Emperor and the well-being of the Empire.\nSection III: War Council\n1. The formation of a War Council, composed of all recognized marshals of the Empire, to ensure cooperation between martial forces.\n2. The formation of an Imperial Militia, composed of all Knights, sworn blades, levy-men, and militia of the Empire, to ensure a defensive body exists for the quick response to threats.\nSection IV: Unification Terms\n1. House Rovin and their vassals to join the Holy Empire of Oren, their existing territories made the Realm of Aesterwald.\n\n2. The Realm of Aesterwald to be recognized as the cultural heartland of all Northerners,\ngranted the right to be lead by their titular Konig.\n\n3. The streamlining of all Houses of Nobility, whether of Aesterwald or the Crownlands, in accordance to the Imperial Codex.\n4. House Rovin named as Duke Elector, to reserve a seat and vote within the Electorate.\nSection V: Imperial Codex\n1. The Imperial Codex to be drafted post-haste with the appropriate input and revision by Noble Lords.\nSignatories:\nVoron Rovin I, König of Aesterwald\n\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion, Emperor of Oren", ""),
        StaticBook("Unknown", "Unknown", "Ellir\nAsul\nBarbu\nEloem\nTahorran\nCelia'onn\nLeyulin\nFaesu\nSan'thill\nLuci'onn\nSirame", ""),
        StaticBook("Unsigned Book", "Lorena Faeliel", "Chapter 1: The Start of a New Day\n\n   The sun was bright, the grass was soft. A group of men standed in a group by the glisening ocean. As we waited we told stories of times of olde. \n\n  Today was the day of new hope. We were finnaly blessed\nwith the pleasure of calling a castle our 'home'. We began with a firm plan of how to get the works in motion. I was to build a farm, they others where to gather resources.\n\n  Suddenly after some mass confusion arised, slowly eroding after a quick\ndiscussion. It became  more a worry about food then shelter, so we began to fish. Unforuntaly none of us were well trained fishers. catch after catch we began to fish No Man's treasure from the sea.\n\nNot so long, The sun was setting for it's work was\ndone for the day. And the tents were pitched. Letting all of us a soundless night among the stars.\n\n  It wasn't before long the men captured some animals to support their food problem. They would survive another day.\nAfter a fort night of smooth survivle, no building prgress had been done, however the brother of Markus de Sazkozy had be convicted of murder. Which was only to be a misunderstanding for Drevin de Sazkozy was only protecting his Duke.\nThe next events turned to be upsetting, After a fight at the Town of Felsen, Drevin fought for his people of Adria, Later conviced a traitor by his brother. Markus was merciful, Letting his brother live through guidence of his Steward. Drevin was\nsentanced to enprisonment. Later He brought him to Felsen to give him a trial.\n\n  After a long session of Drevin's defence, We held a fair trial with fair jury in the Cathedral.\n\n After the charges, Drevin was claimed a Traitor and\nsentanced to be locked up in the stocks and pay 1100 Minas to the King.\n \n Cast out of his Family and Nation Drevin was now a labeled enemy of the De Sarkozy Barony.\nChapter 2\n The Tide of War\n===================\n[!]\n\nThe book has dried blood stains on the rest of the pages, a large hole sinks through the corner of this page!", ""),
        StaticBook("Urgent Letter", "Unknown", "--------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-------------------------------------\n===================The location of this said beast and phenomenon is unknown. This creature, is something of nightmares... It's limbs are quite long and it has claws which can turn the thickest hide into butter. Over the recent weeks, I have spotted this\n===================-creature a number of times. It is accompanied by some sort of phrase which lingers in the back of your mind.\nI do not know the origins, or even the behaviours of this creature but it does terrify myself. I have seen many a party go\n===================after it. Their bodies are normally found as unidentifiable mounds of flesh when I check the nest once again...\n\nI worry for the Vailorians...\n\nThough there have been rumors and small gestures that the creature\n=================== -is able to break swords with the strength of its hide. It's vacant eyes able to pierce the visage of the bravest men. Even those whom believe in gods and aspects think this creature was a mistake. A myth which has come to life, to\n===================-haunt all those whom try to find it.\n\nThe Cannibal roams, it hunts and it will kill.\n\nThe Vailorian Bounty Company will have to be contacted to try and defeat this beast, as my own company has fell prey to it for far too long.\n===================May the bounty company have mercy upon my troubles, knowledge will be found in the coming weeks.\n\n\n-Terryn Cairse\nVailorian Explorer.\n===================[!] The last page is covered in maddened illustrations of humanoid figures, with small suns lining the corners. Lines gesturing from the sun towards the darkened humanoid.\n[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Vanlor's Journal", "Ayche Raven'kor", "Electrical Evocation is the hardest subtype of all five and takes time to master, the road can harm and set yourself in danger, and even death. To begin mastering it one needs to understand what electricity really is. Is it strong light? An advanced form-\nof fire? No, I sincerily doubt it. I believe electricity or lightning, whatever you wish to call it, is pure energy. It can be channeled, it can harm, and it can be controlled, the most important of all, arcane magic is about controlling, and thus; so is-\nthe electrical evocation one casts. There is a drawback for the beginning mages, though. As you would progress out of the zone I am now, your attempts to conjure electricity can be very dangerous, a failed attempt can lead to serious burns, -\n- paralyzation and death. It is indeed not the simplest. The pros of successfully casting this is that few can whitstand your bolts, however, it does indeed take time to charge the bolt in the first place, but as it fires, it happens in a blink.\nYet again, there is another thing with this. An electrical evocationist has to be constantly aware of his/her's surroundings for a reason. For example, you charge a bolt outwards your target but a large anvil is next to it, your bolt wouldn't direct-\n-itself at your target, but instead at the direction of the anvil, this is because of how metals acts with electricity, it's like a form of magnet. It's not recommended to fire electricity at a pool of water you're also in, for example, as the energy -\n- channel throughout the water you're in, and thus you would be affected also.\n\nHere I have quickly noted several objects that would conduct with the subtype electrical evocation,\nI stopped by an anvil this evening, larger than usual, ferrum.\n\nI'm having memories of an aurum passage way back in Riga, probably not there by now\n\nFerrum gate at Felsen, I guess it would conduct.\nI've tried emitting sparks to test what kind of subject would conduct the evocation, I have found this many,\n\nFerrum, Aurum, cellulosa, anvils, cauldrons, water, liquid substances, humans ( don't ask), several plants, o.s.v.\nFerrum and aurum, they're metals so they conduct electricity quite well.\n\nCellulosa, trees seems to channel electricity aswell, abit shabby.\n\nAnvils and cauldrons, they're mostly made out of metal, so yes.\nWater and liquid substances seem to conduct the spark to it's whole range, it seeming to be quite well on doing so.\n\nHumans and other organic beings, don't ask.\nSpark Count:\n\n10th Snow's Maiden: 2\n\n8th Malin's Welcome: 3\n\n10th Malin's Welcome: 2\n\n2th The Grand Harvest: 2\n\n4th The Grand Harvest :4\n7th The Grand Harvest: 2\n\n3rd The Amber Cold: 3 \n\n10th The Amber Cold: 2\n\n17th The Amber Cold: 2\n\n1th The Grand Harvest: 2\n\n17th The Grand Harvest 3\n14th The Grand Harvest: 3\n \n12th The Amber Cold: 4\n\n1th The Deep Cold: 2\n\n7th The Grand Harvest: 3\n\n9th The Amber Cold: 2\n\n4th The First Seed: 5\n21th The First Seed: 2\n6th of the Deep Cold, 1538\n\nYou've officially become proficient enough to no longer need me - thank you for learning with me. This journal is yours to keep, as well as an acceptance to the Order of Magi, should you desire it. Good luck. -Ayche", ""),
        StaticBook("Vault of Vailor", "greener161", "-x-x-x-x-x-x-x-x-x-    The Vault of Vailor\n-x-x-x-x-x-x-x-x-x-\n\nA cold harsh winter's night brewed outside of the Dwarvish capital. The men gathered their equipment and the party ventured forth into the mountains. The Ironborn camp was\nthe target. A spiralling staircase descended into the thick snow and stone. Alone stood a dark shadowy dwed. Weapon he hand he fought the dwarves. He was slain and the door was opened. \n\nWithin the vault ancient dwarvish scripts\ndescribed a golem to khorvad. In the middle a brazier needing to be filled with Ironborn blood to open the way. A haste decision was made to grab the fallen corspe and slice its neck, the blood dripping into the brazier.\nThe second door opened a large fire sprawled pit with khorvads symbol within lay in the centre. Horrific screams and hideous monsters emerged. The dwarves swiftly killed the creatures. \n\nThe final door opened within multiple book-\nshelves. Towards the rear was an ancient golem of some sort. The Dwarves managed to activate it the golem sprung into ancient demanding the date. It had been 1000 years since the golem had been awake. The golem told the Dwarves of his origins being made\nby Ironborn and Starbreaker. The golem eagur to leave he treaded through the snow back to the capital. Many questions left to be answered. \n\n-An account by Odin Ireheart.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vengance", "Erik Stalfen", "A sorrowed day had struck, with the loss of a great friend. \n\n   I had been going to the Caliphate to check up on Iron prices hoping they would have dropped. To my dismay the prices lie the same, but as I began to leave the city a man stopped me.\nThis man had a corrupted look that lie upon his face. At first he began to question my ears and then my beard. He quickly realized I was a Half Elf and begin taunting and insulting me. Luckily for myself he could not come up with anything that I hadn't\nheard before. \n\n   As I was besting him in our game of wordplay some random Dwarf began to watch. This Dwarf had something strange about him, but what, I did not know. Then thankfully a true friend of mine was on her way to the library but saw my troubles\nand stopped to help. \n\n   To our dismay another man came and he was with the one who dared insult me. The two quickly stopped insulting myself for I had bested them in wordplay. Unfortunatly, they begun to insult Sahar and the Crimson Edict.\nWe were not going to stand by idly while they argued this but then the Dwarf joined in on bashing the Edict.. \n\n   I had turned to speak to the Dwarf and then the first man who was named Otto, attempted to stick a dagger in my stomach and in my armpit.\nThe dagger to the gut did nothing thanks to the iron armor I wear under my uniform, but the dagger to the armpit infiltrated the armor.. I began to bleed and it only got worse as he continued to turn the dagger.. At this same time I saw the other man,\nwho was named Bryson begin to attack Sahar.\n\n   As the battle had begun the Dwarf had made it clear what side he was on.. it was not ours.. So he began to create some sort of bright light that had blinded me and Sahar..\n\n   I could not see Sahar at this\npoint or anyone for that matter, but I knew Otto was right in front of me so I tacled him to the ground. I had began punching his face in with my spike gaunlets, but then, the Dwarf walked over..\n\n   This Dwarf put his staff close to my Gorget, I could\nfeel the heat arcing off his staff and then he told me to roll off of the man..\n\n   I did as he said or else I would have been electrocuted without a second thought. He told me to go into the tunnel that led to the residential district, and for Otto to\nhelp his friend that was attacking Sahar.. \n\n   We get into the tunnel and he told me to let him see my wound.. I began o tear the uniform where I had been stabbed and then he pulls out a potion and poors it on there healing my wound instantly..\nI asked him why he was saving me and he said due to a comment I made about the Coalition having their head.. He was part of the Dwarven Council of three.\n\n   I found out his name was Gauldrim and that he had high ties to Oren which is why he refused to\nhelp Sahar. He only allowed me to live since I made the comment about teh Coalition, he said he does not want conflict with them.. After we spoke Gauldrim nearly vanished and I was able to escape.. Sahar was not..\n\n   I vow vengance on Otto and Bryson for\nthat day. When I get a hold of them, they will never see the bright of light again.. Their bodies will be mangled.. Blood will poor out of them but I will cauderize the wounds so they live and feel more pain.. Those poor bastards will know what true\ntorture feels like.", ""),
        StaticBook("Verden's Summary", "Jallentime", "I sent Bartley to Glowshroom cave to collect spores from the rare breed of mushroom that grows inside. His small and quiet stature made short work of sneaking past the spider nest located inside.\n\nHe did well.\nThe point of this lesson was how we, as druids, must understand nature before we can make any attempt to aid it. This was coupled by also learning the proper technique used to observe spiders in their natural habitat without interfering more than needed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Veris Edu. Bill", "Azoth Hawksong", "[!] The following book is transcribed in small print. The words are written neatly.\n\nThe book seems to glow softly at the edges, its paper smelling fresh and delightful. The pages are smooth and crisp to turn.\nFOREWORD\n\nAs your presiding Education Advisor, I - Azoth Hawksong - ensure you that this bill will be followed and maintained throughout my administration, so help me Aeriel.\n\nA. Hawksong\nTHE VERIS EDUCATION BILL\n\n\n\n\nINTRODUCTION\nBy decreed order of High Prince Kalalian Vortral I of Veris, this bill written by the first established Education Advisor of the nation is published to enact a total education reform for Veris, its citizens, and all land operating under the governmening\nbody. It is today on the 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1619, that this bill is submitted to become active and viable as law in the land of Veris beginning 30 days from submission.\n\nThe topics covered in this legislation will construct the foundations for an\neducational system of schooling under Veris Law. This bill will be able to be amended and changed by agreement of both the Education Advisor and two-thirds majority in the governing body of the nation ONLY. No other ruling will dictate any changes unless\nenacted by the presiding High Prince. In this event, the changes will only be in effect for 30 days and cannot be enacted once more unless the prior amendment process is completed.\n\nThe bill is provided as follows:\nESTABLISHMENT\nPOWERS AND OVERSIGHT PRIVILEGE\nUpon enactment of this bill, the civilly elected chair of Education Advisor will become the dominant ruling member of any and all education activities within the borders of Veris. Activities rendered under “education” will be decided in a case-by-case\nbasis by both the High Prince and Education Advisor only. If both parties disagree, a two-thirds majority is needed in the rest of the governing body to decide the verdict.\n\nThis bill also establishes the Education Advisor as the presiding Dean of the\nUniversity of Veris for the entirety of their elected term. By their appointment, the Dean holds rights to any and all management and changes made within the University itself. This provides the Education Advisor the right to decide any major or minor\ncorrections inside University regions without oversight from the governing body. However, in the event that the Education Advisor is unable to perform their duties, a two-thirds majority is needed by the governing body to change one ruling by the\nEducation Advisor within their rights.\n\nThe Dean is allowed any and all Oversight of Student and Faculty ongoings within both the context and region of the University. This allows them the ability to render civil punishment under a trial ran exclusively\nby the Dean. If the severity of the offense is criminal, the Dean has the option to either deal with it internally or provide the offender to Veris officials for a criminally proceeding. A two-thirds majority of the governing body is needed to overturn\nthe decision of the Dean in a criminal proceeding only. All civil cases are required to be handled internally.\n\nUnder this law the Dean also has the ability of Accepting and Excluding students and faculty members of their own accord. This is\nnon-negotiable and cannot be overturned by a governing body. However, the Education Advisor can be asked the return to the matter at their own convenience or concern.\nECONOMIC ESTABLISHMENT\nUpon enactment of this bill, the Education Advisor will be given a lump sum of 1,000 minas every Elven Month by the governing body for structural upkeep, payment of faculty, and whatever else the Advisor determines needed for the benefit of the\nEducational system. If in the event the Advisor spends minas on something personal or not related to the University or governmental upkeep, they can be placed on trial by the governing body. If viable evidence is provided to the trial, no ruling based on\nemotional input alone can be subjected to enactment.\n\nThe University will charge tuition of a flat 150 minas per student per every 2 Elven Weeks enrolled in courses. 50 minas per student will be returned to the government as a tax while the other 100\nminas are put towards paying faculty and general upkeep of the university.\n\nThe University will also be allowed to accept donations to be used for these payments as well as the establishment of scholarship funds. Scholarships will be distributed every\nElven Month to incoming or established students for their academic abilities as judged by the Dean and Faculty.\nPROTECTIONS AND RIGHTS\nThe protections of the Education Advisor, students, faculty, and all others under the Education branch of the government will be protected by this bill when enacted. The Freedom of Expression will be upheld by the Advisor of Defense as well as any and all\ncivil or criminal proceedings in the court of law. Any subjects taught or inferred at the University level by any under this bill will not be responded to with criminal allegations or actions. If this does occur and is agreed upon by the Education Advisor\nand High Prince, then the criminal proceedings will end and a grant of 200 minas will be given to those prosecuted as penance for the violation of this bill's defined rights.\n\nThe University will maintain an Open Door Policy for any and all students.\nNone will be rejected for anything outside of academic ability, drive, and a reasonable level of sanity and responsibility. If this is violated by the University Dean, they will be forced to revoke their decision and pay a total of 300 minas if found\nguilty by a University faculty proceeding under the jurisdiction of the High Prince. A two-thirds vote is required to find the Dean guilty by the faculty of the University.\nCONCLUSION\nThis bill is hereby enacted by the signature of the presiding High Prince and Education Advisor.\n\nx... Azoth Hawksong\n\nX... _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _", ""),
        StaticBook("Viceroy Edict", "Siri", "Edict of Viceroy\n1514\n\nRecorded by Siri Ihelia\nBy decree of His Majesty, King Olivier de Savoie, the office of Viceroy has hereby been established. The position, along with a seat on the Privy Council, grants the Viceroy authority over all the provinces in the Reformed Kingdom of Oren, and grants\nthese following duties:\n\n1. The responsibility, entrusted by the King, to act as his chief liaison and representative in all provincial matters.\n\n2. The right to govern the provinces in a manner that best reflects the well-being of the Kingdom.\n3. The duty to ensure a loyal and law-abiding populace within the governed provinces.\n\n4. The responsibility to represent all the provinces during crucial matters of state.\n5. The responsibility to represent all the provinces in any foreign affair or domestic affair.\n\nReaffirming these duties, the Viceroy will have authority over the Province of Laurehlin, the Protectorate of Haelun’or, and the Ancillary of Ker’nor\nfor an indefinite period. The office of the Viceroy is to be held by Lord Helton Chivay.\n\nSigned,\n\nHis Majesty, King Olivier de Savoie\n\nHis Excellency, Viceroy Helton Chivay\nAuthors notes: While Helton Chivay was appointed Viceroy for all 3 subsidiary states, he has never once wielded his power, save for one incident of a small rebellion in Haelun'or over some dispute for the position of Sohaer. One must ask themselves is non\naction is the correct way of governance for the elder races, or if a more active hand would have brought the mali-kinded up to the expected size of a duchy in Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vilyal's Journal", "Yhorm Aldyhr", ". . .it wasn't long after Heinrik's discovery of our refuge that Yaila's nightmares began again, we thought that this place would provide ample distance from her erstwhile plagues, and for a time it proved successful. Yet once more, it would appear\nas though we are unable to escape the ignorant of our past, they come forth once more seeking to put all we have sought to keep safe to the flame. I fear Oswald, yet his power knows few bounds, perhaps we might yet find a luminary to guide our\nfrightened people towards the sanctuary they so desperately seek. . .", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Transloca.", "Evelangéline", "About Void Translocation:\n\n- Void Translocation, the voidal art of storing objects in the void, is one of the provailing magical arts in the means of utility.\n\n- A Void Translocationist can place and retrive objects-\nthat they have placed in the void anytime and anywhere they desire. \n\n- Although it may seem fairly easy for the eye, it requires intensive studying and observing to be actually translocating even the smallest of objects.\nBasic Understanding:\n\n- First of all, although it may seem that the object is being transferred inside the void in one piece, it isn't. The object breaks down into tiny pieces, moving freely inside the void. To call for the object, a void transloca-\n-tionist has to remember the physical properties of the object.\n\n- The magic happens in a rather interesting way. First, a lavander speck of light appears at the desired location of the void translocationist, growing larger-\nto fit the size of the object. Then, the void translocationit simply pushes the object inside the lavander circle of light, the light swelling in side before dissapearing again. To recall an object, the translocationist does the same with the lavander-\ncircle of lightly. Only this time, the object starts to form at the enterence of the light, before simply dropping down. One can say this could be used to drop heavy objects on others' head. One would be correct. However, it'd be a lot slower and mana-\nwasting way of attacking if not mastered than the other evocation arts, which is the main reason this magic is used for utility, not offense.\nConditions for Translocation:\n\n- The translocationist must be knowledged of the object, having it in clear vision. One cannot translocate an object behind walls. To further explain, a translocationist needs to know the physical properties-\nof the object before even attempting to send the object to the void. During my studies, I have carried a notebook with me to note the properties of the objects I wanted to translocate. Like my doll, or the anvil I keep with me for any emergency smithing!\nFirst, make a list of the physical properties of the object.\n\nWhat does it look like?\nIs it soft/rough?\nWhat colour is it?\nIs it cold/hot to touch?\nIs its surface smooth or rough?\nHow does it react to-\nfire and pressure?\n\n- These are only examples, there may be more if the translocationist feels there is more properties to cover. For example, I'll be covering a simple silver knife's properties on the next page;\nSilver Knife,\n\n- Made of silver, is durable\n-Cold to touch\n-Reflects light\n-A small 'Eva' is carved into the handle part,\n- Shaped like a long rectangle but with a sharp edge,\n-Used for cooking-\npurposes,\n-Durable, doesn't bend with pressure;\n-When reacted with fire, keeps shape when reacted with the average heat of the fire.\nMore Things to Know:\n\n- As in all magical arts, one must not use more than their existing energy. Failure to do so will result in fatigue and maybe even death.\n\n- As the objects gets more complex, the mana required-\nto translocate it increases as well. Because of their extreme complex design, living beings cannot be translocated in any instance.\n\n- For being fairly complex and lacking solidity, liquids also cannot be trans-\n-located.\n\n- As the mass of the object increases, so does the mana required to translocate it.\n\n- For any questions, do not hesitate to contact me, Evelangéline for further information.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 2 : Gy'waka", "Arnorian", "Training.\n\nA Gy'waka is not a horse. If you displease it in even the slightest of ways, then you can expect to be launched right off it's back. If one tries to become the Gy'waka's master, then you will never be able to successfully mount and ride one.\nThe bird is a creature to be respected, after all. To even get onto it's back, the Gy'waka must fuly trust you, and you it.\n\nTo begin, a Gy'waka must be first trained to register a Kha's voice. The training Kha will first produce soft clicking sounds with\nhis or her mouth while gently pulling on the reins to direct the bird's head in the direction of which way you wish it to turn and face. After the bird finally obeys and turns it's head, you feed it something as a reward. It will not take long for the\nGy'waka to understand that obeying your commands will result in being fed. The tricky part is getting the Gy'waka bird to remember which command is which.\n\nThe Gy'waka will recognise a Kha as a friend, but it will not recognise any other\nrace as such. The Gy'waka are fed on anything vaugely meat-like, so the corpses of other races are also in their deit. This makes the Gy'Waka see other races as nothing but prey, and will not respond to them in any other way, in fact they may even attack\nif a non-Kha makes an attempt to mount them. It would take a lifetime for a Gy'Waka to be taught otherwise, and by that time it would be too old to do anything beneficial. This is pirely a Kha' mount.\n\nAppearance.\n\nThe Gy'Waka stands upright at about\n11 feet tall. It has a very large beak, and a pair of firm, strong legs at it's rear. Each Gy'Waka has dull, grey coloured wings with a beautiful red stripe down their backs. Their chests are very lightly feathered, and their skin can be seen clearly\nthrough it, their legs however, have no feathers at all.\n\nThe males and females are very similar in almost every way, however there is one key difference that will allow you to tell them apart instantly. The males have a large cluster of\nred feathers sticking out of the back of their head, while the females have nothing there at all.\n\nLife Cycle.\n\nA Gy'waka will on average live up to the age of 85, at which point they will be too old to continue their day to day life, so\nthe other Gy'waka will kill and consume it. If they were not killed by other birds, it could easily live up to the age of 100. A Gy'waka will be fully grown by the age of 22, as it is at this age their red stripe will appear. The Kha' know when a Gy'waka\nis ready to be trained by waiting until it plucks it's feathers, and grows the red stripe down it's back.\n\nAs mentioned before, the birds are not stupid and they will never attack their own young. In fact, getting between a Gy'waka and it's young would\ncertainly result in your death, even if they're not related - All Gy'waka look out for each other's young. So, you can imagine it's not wise to go anywhere near the children until they reach the age of maturity. This is the only real danger the Gy'Waka\npresent to the Kha'.\n\nAfter a male and female Gy'waka mate, the female will lay one egg at a time about two months after they've mated. Unlike some other birds, a female will lay no eggs at all if she has not had them fertilized by a male. After that, an\negg takes on average one month to hatch, and the fledgling will stay close to either it's direct mother, or a another of it's kind until maturity.\n\nWritten by Charles Napier, Dean of Naturalism and Professor of Kharajyr studies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Volume 156", "Lily", "Diary of Katina\n\nVolume 156\n\nThe Watch of the Okar\nEntry one, Tulatha has just\nbonded her Okar, Lan, this Diary will recant what they did, effects will be in the next Diary, so I can keep all of these in order.\nSo what Tulatha did from what I can tell is she skinned a live wolf, they tried a dead wolf skin, she said it failed.  Something about it doesn't have as much power, and its useless.\n\nNext she and Lan mixed 3 bowls of blood, one of hers, one of his, and\none of their blood mixed together, in which case she drew a huge symbol which is drawn below \n*The symbol is drawn here*\n\nInside they wrote their names in their own blood and then made the joint symbol.  \n\nThe bond of friendship,\n*A symbol is shown*\n\nA bond of lovers\n*A symbol is shown below*\n\nA bond of Criminals\n*A symbol is shown below*\n\nA bond of loyalties\n*A symbol is shown below*\nApparently the benifites of doing this are increased speed, increased hearing smell and sight but decreased touch and taste...\n\nWe'll see what happens with those two later...", ""),
        StaticBook("Vordak", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Vordak\n\nAge: 19\n\nRace: Troll\n\nGender: Male\nCondition/Injury: Was shot in the left shoulder by a stray arrow. The patient showed receiving little pain, if any.\n\nTreatment plan: Simply to pull the arrow out of the flesh, and then soaking up any blood with a rag.\nDoctor who treated the patient: Dr. Kale\n\nCost: 10 minas\n\nDate: 11th of Sun's Smile, 1521\nEnd result: Patient was very calm during the entire procedure. The arrow was easily pulled from the muscle, and the patient showed very little signs of pain. There was some blood, but was easily cleaned up afterwards.\n*Doctor Kale's signature would be on this page*\n\n\n\n~ Doctor Kale", ""),
