        StaticBook("Workers Handbook", "Beltran", "[!]A list of buildings supplies are listed upon the page, including the curious entry of 'Frog Oil'\n[!]A list of excavations needed are listed upon the page, including the entry of 'Escape Tunnel'", ""),
        StaticBook("Wrath's Clutch", "Jacob Chapel", "Battle of Wrath's Clutch\nThis old tome has been transcribed by Jacob Chapel, High Scrivener of Oren, in 1478. The tome recounts the Battle of Wrath’s Clutch in Aegis, where an undead keep was sieged and destroyed, over a century ago.\nThe battle is nearing and an uneasy silence falls over the camp. There is no more continuous taunting by Kane and his ally Dusk. All is silent, the calm before the storm. I hear a call, \"All wardens to the outpost for a pre-battle meeting.\"\nWith my pulse pounding I enter into the Officer's building. I know while we are having our counsel of war, the other races are as well. Orcs, Men, and Dwarves alike, all planning the same massive assault on the undead keep of Wrath's Clutch.\nOur officers decide upon a plan, I am to assist in a flanking manoeuvre base with two other wardens. We set out from the base long before the battle is to begin. \n\nWe circle far around the enemy's fortress and reach the far side of Wrath's Clutch.\nFrom there I was separated from the other two wardens. Unsure of what to do I returned to the outpost and joined the main assault against the Clutch. I was uneasy and fearful, the Undead's thunder roared across the battlefield.\nThe battle cry sounds and we race across the open sands to the relative safety provided by the walls. The undead lightning was striking all around us, my head began to throb from the endless noise. The walls were breached and we flood into the Clutch.\nI was running through those dark and narrow passages searching for enemies, when I hear a shout and cry of death. It was an elf, I see the villain who killed my kin and give pursuit. He turned a moment too late,\nas I bring my iron sword crashing through his head, thus ending his corrupted life.\n\nThe thunder has lessened considerably as I make my way into the courtyard, where a great battle was underway. The foul undead had summoned ungodly amounts of skeletons,\nzombies and other abominable creatures. The dwarves were nowhere to be seen and the men and elves were losing strength. After the creatures had been vanquished we searched the keep looking for the undead necromancers.\nI descended into the lower levels of the keep which lead underground. I was attacked from behind and knocked unconscious. \n\nMy head throbbed mercilessly when I awoke, I had been stripped of all my armour and weaponry.\nI cautiously crept up the stairs and came upon a set of iron armour which I promptly put on. I had a set of armour but nothing to fight with except my hands. I returned to the ground level of the keep only to find the battle raging on.\nThe wardens had managed to corner the damned undead in their spires, but were unable to overcome them. I ran seeking shelter as lightning smote the ground all around me. I felt the intense heat burn my flesh and nearly cook me alive in the iron armour.\nMaking quick glance up the spire I see the undead spewing lightning and fire across the battlefield. I see Wrath himself laying waste to our troops with his magical golden staff and dark powers. I dive for cover as another blast of lightning and fire\nignites the battlefield of Wrath's Clutch. I see many bodies falling off the tall tower, as well as much weaponry and tools falling into the shallow waters. I dive into the water and gather as many tools and weapons as I can hold.\nIn the safety of the ruined clutch I examined what I had gathered. A few stone implements, chain armour, and a magical staff like I had seen Wrath using to destroy our men. I did not want the enemy to re-obtain one of these powerful staves,\nso I left for a short time while the battle continued, to ensure the safety of the magic staff. Upon arriving back at the forward walls of our base I see one of my superiors, Glade Guard Arthane Lazul.\nI showed him the staff and placed it into his care for the remainder of the battle.\n\nI then returned to the front lines, and could see that the battle had raged on while I was away. Through the noise of battle I faintly hear a lady shouting.\nI was unaware who she was, as I could not see her. I realized that she was in distress when she began shouting about how she was at the top of the spire held captive by the undead sorcerers. There was a large hole in the wall at the bottom of the spire,\nwhich opened to the ladder, which led to the top of the spire. Me and our allies fought our way to the floor below the roof only to find obsidian blocking further ascension. We were stalled for a while in this room before I dislodged some of\nthe cobblestone from the walls and created a way up to the roof of the spire. We leaped onto the rooftop and began destroying every evil creature in sight. The lady was screaming throughout the whole fight, which did not last long.\nWith the tower won and the fell creatures subdued, we began our descent with the lady. She was quickly escorted off of the battlefield whilst I returned to the ever raging battle.\nLighting poured down once again with renewed energy and I hear Ariel shout \"Flee my followers!\" All of the leaders began shouting \"Retreat! Back to the outpost!\" Our entire army ran through the gates as massive explosions began to shake\nthe entire outer wall. I hear a shout \"Put out those fires!\". I raced to the top of the wall with many others and we beat out the flames. It felt like a losing battle against the fires, as I would put one out ten more would spring up from the constant\ndownpour of lightning. I can see the flashes everywhere, the roaring of the thunder is almost unbearable now. \n\nI then hear a loud cheer arise from the ranks \"HUZZAH! The battle is won!\" Wrath had been defeated. I felt only sorrow at this moment.\nYes, Wrath had been defeated, but at what cost? I look out over the battlefield and tears sprang to my eyes. Fires still raged across the across the trees nearby and many brave souls bodies burned in the morning light. The undead necromancer must have\npaid close attention to the beautiful trees surrounding the battlefield as they were burning out of control. I could only watch in agony as they burned to the ground. I wept that day for all my fallen comrades many of whom I did not know their names.\nThe Clutch is being reclaimed by nature, grass springs up out of the scorched ground inside the courtyard. Trees and flowers were planted there as well. I wander aimlessly through the bloodied ruins. From the top of the wall I see Prince Mylas\nerecting a memorial for our fallen kin. The battle of Wrath's Clutch is over. We have won. I shall never forget the valiant soldiers who gave their lives to remove the foul undead from the land.\nHere I end my tale of the battle of Wrath's Clutch. \n\nWarden Initiate Amethain", ""),
        StaticBook("Yarr request", "Thalrim Irongut", "dear owner of this here tailor shop, i wish to get meself a nice lookin cap'n suit aswell as a pirate hat, bandana and a eyepatch, when you have made this please deliver it to the tavern in kaz'ulrah\n\nyou will receive minas upon delivering it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Yemekar", "Hogarth Irongut", "IV-Yemekar's Balance\n\nWritten by Morgrim Grandaxe and copied down by Hogarth Irongut, tennant from Da Ord Nar Kadrin.\nFrom the dawn of time it was said to be the creator, Yemekar, who selected the Dwarves as the chosen amongst all his creations. However, with this great honour, there too came responsibility. Yemekar commanded of Urguan that he and his kin would forever\nemsure that none of his creations would ever bear the power to completely destroy another. \"Go forth my children, and preserve the balance of my creation. For you are the pillars that uphold the world.\" Though these words held many different meanings\nthroughout various ages of Dwarven history it is generally accepted by most within the Dwarven Clergy as a matter that remains relevant to this day. Urguan accepted his creator's bidding and thus the Dwarven race, throughout the vast majority of its\nexistance, remained vigilant in the event that an empire were to rise. This has in practice become better known amongst the Dwarves as Yemekar's Balance. For if ever a nation were to cast aside its morality in favour of the pursuit of power, the\nprosperity of other nations would surely suffer at its hands. \n\nThe concept of Yemekar's Balance therefore revolves largely around a fierce opposition towards policies of expansionism and the invasion of another nation's sovereign\nterritory without a cause deemed righteous in the eyes of the gods. Furthermore, in the majority of circumstances, wars that are declared in the name of Yemekar's Balance are almost exclusively made in the defense of nations deemed to lack the\ncapability to defend themselves. However, there are a few unique examples that can indeed be to seen to differ from this norm. If a nation is found to be harboring a capability that is deemed wither unholy or dangerous in the wrong hands, the Dwarves may\nchoose to act against them. For example, golemancy, gifted unto the hands of the Dwarves by Yemekar himself, is considered a very real threat in the hands of those who are not to be trusted. \n\nToday, we may take no extraordinary effort in viewing that the\nDaemon, Khorvad, was once one amongst the Brathmordakin, represented by a will for ambition. Yet with ambition, came the everlasted desire for more. It was thought that plagued the Ironborn ruler, Velkan, as he departed from the ways of Yemekar and\ninstead opted to follow in Khorvad's footsteps. So too was it a driving force behind the Holy Oren Empire and its reign of terror upon the Princedom of Malinor. For this, Thorin Grandaxe, former Grand King of Urguan opted to be commended for his actions,\neven in going up against a power that  for a period of its history, held the capacity to conquer much of the world. For when the Empire fell, Thorin had within his grasp the opportunity to take both Malinor and Oren for himself, he did not give in to such\ntemptations. If we are indeed to tkae one lesson from Thorin's actions, it is that even when we are seemingly on the verge of victory, it is never in any case wise to forsake Yemekar's will. Though greed is a natural blessing, bestowed upon Dwarves by the\nBrathmordakin, Grimdugan, ambition and a thirst for power are what drives mortal beings mad. Consequently, it is by no coincidence that empire building is deemed an act of sin in the eyes of many of Urguan's descendants.", ""),
        StaticBook("Zeliek's Journal", "Zeliek", "Zeliek's Journal\n\nI'm writing this journal out of personal boredom aswell as to keep track of the progess I have done not only as a Paladin but towards my own personal goal too.\n-------------------\nToday was somewhat of a strange day, I've strolled upon two people in conflict with a supposed murderious girl. Sadly despite my efforts to halt the conflict and help said girl. . . She died. I. . . Perhaps was a little too harsh in my\nAccusations and what I said to the duo that ended the girl, saying things like \"You are no better than her.\" And \"What grants you the right to shorten a life?\" I'm sadned by what I've done there. Yet what was stranger is after the male of the two followed\nMe and spoke with me of the situation and surprisingly, that I was noble. We exchanged names and words and in the end I learned he was becoming a Cleric. I am happy and at the same time sad. Yet in time I'm sure he will learn of Tah's nature. I do hope I-\nSpeak with him soon though. Hallot Belal.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 2.\n\nToday I've met two women who had came to me asking for information on necromancers, after a while of talking they-\nTold me that they themselves wished to become necromancers themselves all to resurect their dead sister and see her smile again. I told them that doing that would be meaningless and only produce a mindless corpse puppet. After a while I'm glad to say that\nit would seem atleast they changed their mindset and instead are now set to becoming Void mages. I still don't know if this is true, yet I'm happy to know I may have changed their path for the better, even if it was in a small way.\n-------------------\n\nEntry 3.\n\nToday me and my friend Archibald found something strange in the woods, so we began to gather others to hunt said creature. Yet the sight we came to find was rather insane.\nA gigantic plant like creature with a large multitude of tendrils stood before us. As soon as we came a large tendril came to greet us, I somehow managed to slash at the thing and slice it in half. I then, considering the the fact we had two mages with-\nus, began to walk and circle the creature to draw it's attention untill I was met with a hole in my arm by the beast. I manged to heal my arm through the mists of Xan as the others dealt with it through a massive exploasion and fire. I still don't know-\nWhat the creature might have been though I know it is dead and I have it's head in my posession.\n\n-------------------\nEntry 4.\n\nToday I was met by one who needed assistence from a cleric or Paladin-\nIt seemed that their base was tainted by the likes of a necromancer and him and three others were wounded. I went to the place to try and clense the taint yet to no effect, sadly I do hope they get it clensed soon. Much later on I met a really nice Cleric\nBy the name of Meiko, she seemed to have a really livily personilty and in all honesty truly brighted my day. We had a long chat on many topics, mainly clerical and Paladin topics however. Our conversation sadly had to be cut in the middle as she had to-\nDepart, though I do hope I meet her again sometime soon.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 5.\n\nToday I had a chat with Meiko before a girl who seemed to love performing showed up-\nShe gave us a little show of dancing and singing. Afterwards we were met by a child covered in wounds and bruises. The terrible sight made me pitty the child, yet everything is alright as I managed to heal all of his injuries. I'm now just waiting for-\nMeiko to return so we may go explore lands.\n\n\nWe just went on an adventure about the island and even though not much has happend she seemed to have a great time. We even seemed to had a philisophical moment where she seemed-\nSad by the fact her adoptive father was gone. Yet we spoke about how even though they are gone, they still live in our memories and all that. I suppose I just wait till the next time we can speak and  adventure.\n-------------------\n\nEntry 6.\n\nToday me and a group of friends went off into the woods and were met by a large phoenix, we had a grand battle with it were I managed to slash off a bit of it's flesh before I was met-\nBy embers upon my atire, someone crashing into me and gusts of wind blowing onto me. Overall it was a terrible experience. . . Yet after that it flew off towards the city where it was delt with, or so we think. Someone had one of it's eggs which I can-\nonly assume hatached and became it's child.\nAfter a long period of time the child seemed to quickly grow to the size of it's parent before flying away somewhere random. All I am left with now are some minor burns and a piece of it's flesh. Aswell the-\nmemories that follow.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 7.\n\nToday I attended Ramza's wedding and I must say I wasn't all impressed. From what I saw someone slaped Ramza with a fish, cake rained from the skies-\nThere were bunnies on the red carpet and someone punched Ramza in the nose. Overall I feel this 'wedding' was more of a comedy act if anything else. Though I still am glad that Ramza and Elvi are now officaly together and I hope they stay that way happily\n-------------------\n\nEntry 8.\n\nToday I was called by Sam to head to a city known as Adria, upon my arvial I fond Sam having two arrows in his shoulder and calf, after healing him with the assitence of Xan, he granted me some extreamly-\nSoft cloth. We parted ways afterwards and I headed to the Mali'ame city where I was met with a specter apprently attacking the city. Despite my efforts to try and free the creature from it's torment, it was taken down soon by some golden dust. I'm but sad\nI was unable to provide any assitence in the matter.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 9. \n\nConsidering the recent lack of excitment in my life, I think it may be better to write this entry on the past, perhaps a way for\nThose that read this book in the future to understand what has occured in my life and why I have these morals. \n\nIn the past I lived carefree with my brother, he was more of the deliquent type while I the well behaved I suppose-\nWe lived in a noble home the two of us and all was well untill one day we decided to go on a walk. From there a bandit came and attacked us both while still little, I was fine yet my brother was stabbed in the gut. I quickly treated his wounds but after-\nHe had a strange look in his eye, his fingers clutching into a fist as blood ran from his palm. I could tell he wished for revenge. I never saw him again after that, even now we haven't stayed in touch. But from that experience I now wish to be the one to\nGuide him back to us, him and all who are lost. It is from this that I created three self rules for myself.\n\n1. To never kill, solve conflict without bloodshed.\n\n2. To guide others that have fallen back onto the right path.\n3. To protect everyone, no matter what.\n\nThese are the three rules I have created and perhaps the true reason I became a Paladin, to better uphold these rules.\n-------------------\n\nEntry 10.\n\nI am but angered today at not the specter but myself. Today the specter returned and decided to grant us a \"Demonstration\" of our idoicy. And to my suprise, it was me.\nThe being shot out a golden blade into my back and I was treated by a cleric. I am not mad at the creature but myself. . . to know this being made a mockery of me not once, but twice. Afterwards I heard the being whisper into my ear \"You will die.\" I-\nShall be the one to make this being vanish. . . You can be sure of that.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 11.\n\nRecently there has been a wyren attack at the city, however it seems to have been dealt with.\nThis beast created a scene of slight pure chaos by all the guards and others fighting it with bows and arrows, I would assume atleast twenty or more guards were invovled. Aswell as a large number of injuried afterwards. Atleast it is gone however.\n-------------------\n\nEntry 12.\n\nBeen awhile since I made an entry, however today an army of undead visted the wood elf city and I helped, it was a bloodbath but in the end we won. Afterwords I had to use the mists of Xan\nTo heal a girl's arm, I can only hope the rest of the wounded are okay aswell.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 13.\n\nToday me and a group of friends went out to fight a witch within the woods, this witch has been-\nKnown for her dark practicing and sacraficing of animals. Once we arivied I was slashed by a bear across the chest before managing to end it with flames and a sword, from there me and another rushed towards the home and up the stairs untill they went out-\nAnd both of us fell downwards. A wolf then bite itself into my shoulder before we dealt with it aswell. Surprisingly after that we managed to end the witch and now we await the mina reward. I believe I was even able to see one of Xan's keepers in the-\nBattlefield, I but wonder who that could be.\n\n-------------------\n\nEntry 14.\n\nToday I am sad to say I have spoken with a friend known as Arelin on why she is a frost witch. When I first brought it up she-\nSeemed hesitent, frightend even. She then began to speak saying that she became one to be imortal, in order to escape the fear of death. Her worst fear is dying and because of that she has turned her body into one of the witches. She then questioned on-\nWhat I thought happends when you die. Obviously I said what most say, \"I believe there is a life of death, one never just stops existing, they but are sent to the creator when they die.\" I am unsure of weither or not that stayed in her mind though-\nStrangely after speaking with them about it, they offer me a favor. So I gave it. . . \"My favor is even if your kin order you to harm others. My wish is but that you not kill a soul.\" Perhaps I was asking too much of a dark being. . . Though part of me-\nWishes they she will keep the promise. Not for my own stastfaction but for her own sake. As a friend I just don't want to see her fear consume her and turn her into a murderer. No one. . . No one should ever be forced to kill another.\n-------------------\n\nEntry 15.\n\nToday was a rather eventfull day, Meiko returned and learned that I actually loved her from Ramza. . . The emberassment she must have felt was probably too much though when she exited the tavern with\nRamza she kissed me upon the lips. This. . . Shocked me to say the least but Meiko thought of it as a wrong thing to do, so I quickly went to comfort her. Now it would seem that me and Meiko are begining to start dating. Though at the same time I still-\nHave my duties to work on. . . The ancient elves, Undru, frost witches and Arelin. . . And recently Necromancers. Dispite my feelings to Meiko my own duties come first, otherwise what kind of man am I that neglates his work and his own self goals. I can-\nOnly pray that I shall get through these dark times.\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("~The Aspects~", "Kasfer Lightdraft", "~The Aspects~\nThe Aspects, for reference, are the deities commonly held by Wood Elves, though more so by Druids.\n\nThere are two Aspects, which I will later explain in greater detail. For now, I will explain the role of the Aspects.\nThe Aspects represent the balance, the delicate thing that holds everything in check. This mostly refers to nature, and the wilds. The Druids act as tools for the Aspects, to hold the balance, to help stop threats to the balance.\nNow, for the two Aspects:\nCerrunos: The Huntsman, represents patience, hunting (of course), and often referred to as 'The Father'.\nCerridwen: Often referred to as 'The Mother', represents birth, new life, and gentleness.\n\nKeep in mind the Aspects are up to interpretation, and I am simply a humble student of the Druids, and child of the Aspects.\n*On the last page is a quick sketch of a spider, seeming to have no apparent purpose*", ""),
        StaticBook("~Wind Evocation~", "Lincia Lyn'lyr", "~Wind Evocation~\n        By: Lincia Lyn'lyr\n \n                 Index\n-Description\n-Basics\n-Mixing of Spells\n-Respects\n~Description~\nWind evocation is the summoning of and conducting of wind, noted from the name. Wind may be conducted into currents, condensed forms, or even different temperatures.  Wind evocation tends to be made of currents that can be as\nstrong as someone blowing on another's hair or as strong as whirlwind winds that could knock someone in full iron armor back! It is seen more as a supportive evocation rather than combative but it may be used for either or even for pleasure oftasks.\n~Basics~\n  Wind evocation includes different kinds of wind currents, strengths, navigation, and temperatures, which is the most difficult.  Wind also may fluctuate in various ways against different substances so experiments should be in\norder to find out what is effective; one against a full suit of iron armor must be a lot stronger while one against a leaf to knock it off a branch would be a lot softer and carrying it in the current for a prolonged period would need to be a gentle\ncurrent to prevent from the leaf falling to the ground. \n\n-Currents\n\nThere are different flowing patters that each current has one. One directed at a certain target would need to be straighter and thinner to focus strength. Another against a wide array of\ntargets would need to be a lot wider and thinned out in height to maintain enough mana to conduct it. Another current for my tasks purposes of cleaning say a path  needs to be curling in the ends of each strip of air flow to knock up and away items in the\narea. Lastly, wind currents may have more of a zig pattern to cover more space but that is much more complex. \n       \n-Strengths\n\nWind currents have different strengths as well in which this would be observed when mainly studying the element in\nnature. Rough and strong wind is usually designated for a certain target, an enemy as an example, that requires more mana and usually more concentration for even one of getting near mastering it. Gentle and light flowing winds need to be kept to the\naspects of using it for pleasure or starting a larger and more powerful wind.  In combat, the most useful thing a soft wind would do is  affect the things within the envrionment to your advantage; a fire wanting to be spread to a close and particular\ntarget or starting a regular fire to supply it with oxygen which the spell would only last while being supplied with mana.\n\n-Navigation\n\nWind can be seen in our daily life for multiple purposes with each having a specifc shape. Whirlwinds are curved to\ngive it its form and concentration of power in the eye. More specifc bends and curves in wind that are more abrupt must be studied by the evoker at a higher level of training. As if twirling a thin sheet of silk in air, wind currents may curl and twirl in\nmany beautiful  ways yet they have  affect on conditions of each. Directing a current higher into the sky and suddenly down would increase the power of it and impact on anything hit. Lastly, wind currents are not seen usually in bending at sharp angles\nlike ones of a traingle or square but in curves, whether  they may be close cut or wide, like a circle has. As another mental note when altering it, try to move your body with the direction wanted as in hand/arm motions to simulate as if you are one with\nit and simulate future movement of it.\n\n-Temperature\n\nLike a winter's cool breeze or a mid summer's air current, flowing air may have a temperature different than neutral that is due to outside details like climate or environment. In this case however,\nthe evoker must study this natural occurence in nature to be able to comprehend how to do this method. The temperature displayed of evoked air when forced on an object in this realm  will only stay on it with mana being put into the spell of wind; this is\nmay be untrue in the case of holding the cold or heated air for a prolonged period on the item. Also, air currents controlled by the mage, with mana flow, are only affected by the mage so its temperature is not altered by the outside environment. This is\nthe most demanding and strenuous thing to learn in this art as well so this section is dedicated to ending the training/dabbling in your own unique spells!\n~Mixing of Spells~\nAs many mages know, conjuring two evocations or different spells of any branch is energy consuming and usually more difficult summon. With wind evocation, any spells combined with it usually are smaller and more condensed like\nrock bits, ice shards, or embers of fire. And going at faster speeds in currents when having both evoked may either enhance the other spell or even counter it. Fire within a wind current that is too powerful could completely  blow it out while small\nrocks would become very deadly pieces of hardened grains that could either break tissue on contact or a certain material.\n~Respects~\n I, Lincia, have been sparked to write this book for my good friend and love Laureh'thill. This is specially made for him, knowledge of pure Mali'aheral, Mages Guild, & anyone wise enough. Should anyone be holding a.\ncopy without consent of one of the previous including me, should be reported to me or hand in the book to one of the rightful owners. Lastly, I thank Bernabus for working with me in Abresi, New Malinor, and the Conclave to perfect my mastering of this\npowerful art and I only wish him the best respects. Enjoy this tome and hold it well to your progression!", ""),
        StaticBook("´`", "Corvus Keint", "Short stories series: \n\n           RAVEN\n\n\nShe had her mission. As Always.\n\nQuickly, she transformed herself for the third time that night and flew off into the stormy sky.\nWhen she neared the castle, she swooped down to the throne room and entered through an open stained glass window depicting a phoenix.\n\nShe landed on the red carpet in front of the king. Heavily armored knights stood on each side of the room.\nThey snickered at the \"clumsy\" bird. Inclunding the king who slouched in his red-cushioned seat of gold.\n\nSuddenly, a strong, silver wind whirled around the bird as it grew to the size and shape of a human, clothed in a long black cloak.\nShocked, the guards flinched and the king sat up in his throne, his hands gripping the armrests. Before him stood a black figure with a hood. All he could see were the tender lips on its face. \nInhaling deeply, she let her ebony hair tumble down her back\nas she removed her black hood.\n\n\"I am Raven\", she proclaimed, her forest green irises glaring straight into the stunned eyes of the malicious king. \"And I have come bearing a message. Step down from your throne and\nand crown the rightful ruler of this kingdom King Phoenix. If you do not, you shall be cursed for the rest of your days.\n\nKing Vulture's eyes stormed with fury. Raven could see lightning flashing in them.\n\"Never! Guards! Kill her! Now!\"\n\nThe knights charged at her, shouting. But Raven simply transformed back into a small raven. She lunged at the king. He blocked his face with his arms, but it was no use. The raven's claws\nhad touched the top of his head. The curse had been cast.\n\nFor the rest of his days, King Vulture was known as the Beggar Serpent. He could do nothing but crawl for his life, struggling to escape the phoenixes ready to devour him.\nHe lived in the holes of the Phoenix Palace, determined on getting revenge on Raven.\n\nRaven, she had returned to Phoenix to tell him the good news. He returned to his palace, defeated the army of Vulture's remaining men and took back his throne and\nand kingdom. As he sat in this throne, one day, gazing at the scarlet and orange stained glass windows, he noticed a little black bird at his side.\n\n\"Raven? Why are you still here?\"\n\nI am waiting for you to tell me what to do next.\n\"You don't need to do anything else for me. You have saved the kingdom. You are free\"\n\nAnd that lifted the curse on Raven.\n\nPhoenix was the first human being to ever say that to Raven, instead of throwing at her more orders.\nShe had been cursed to do whatever she was told and many took advantage of that. But Phoenix was selfless. Instead of flying away to do whatever she pleased, Raven used her freedom to stay with Phoenix. They were soon wed and lived merrily all their days.\nWritten by:\n\n\nCorvus Keint,\n\n\nLord Merentel's squire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul V", "§bMarch Ash", "Here, at the edge of Axios, it would be so easy to build a boat and leave. To abandon the descendants to their terrible fate, and to abandon the land to the wrath of the Aspects. To leave, and never return. But I have a mission.\n\nI cannot leave until it is complete.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Path of Mina", "§b'Kommid'", "Here in my new cave, just bought this new mule here. It’s fun to ride up here in the orinian hills. But you know what I like more than materialistic things? Knowledge. In fact, I’m a lotmore proud of these seven new bookshelves that I had to get installed\n\nto hold fourteen new books that I stole. It’s like the billionaire Shrek’lak says, “the more lat learn, the more yub earn.” Now maybe you’ve seen my Bladex talk where I talk about how I read a book a day. You know, I read a book a day not to show off it’s\n\n again about the knowledge. In fact, the real reason I keep this Mule here is that it’s a reminder. A reminder that dreams are still possible, because it wasn’t that long ago that I was in a little Cart across the country sleeping on a un-tanned leather\n\n bed in a mobile cart home with only forty seven mina in my bank account. I didn’t have any friends as my parents were killed by orcs But you know what? Something happened that changed my life. I bumped into a mentor. And another mentor.\n\n And a few more mentors. I found five mentors. And they showed me what they did to become Bandits. Again, it’s not just about Mina, it’s about the good life; health, wealth, love and happiness. And so I bandited a few oreners, it’s actually on my\n\nwanted poster, There is a copy of it on the back of this book and you can look at my three best crimes. Three things that you can do today no matter where you are.Now, this isn’t a “get rich quick” scheme. You know, like they say if things sound too good\n\nto be true they are too good to be true. I’m not promising you that tomorrow you’re gonna be able to go out and buy a Mule. But what I am telling you is that it can happen faster than you think if you know the proven steps. So, I\n\nbandited two little bandit’s and wrote another book as a guide. Like I said, now it’s not the most professional I just shot them here with my crossbow, but it’s real. Nobody can argue, this is my true story. And I’m going to giveyou the three\n\n most important things you can do today. So look at the poster, go there it’s completely free to look at it it’s just a couple words. Invest in yourself. Always be curious. Don’t be a cynic. Okay, people see posters like this and they say\n\n“Ah that’s not real that’s for somebody else.”\nDon’t listen, don’t listen. Be an optimist. Like, Uldar Irongut, the Dwarf who started the 18 year wars,\n\n he said that he was only fifteen years old when he read a book by Helen Keller, and that book changed his life. Books can change your life. And in that book, Helen Keller said “optimism” so if you’re a cynic, if you’re a pessimist\n\nyou don’t need to read this. Don’t worry about it, I don’t need to talk to everybody. But if you’re somebody who knows that there’s something better, cause the dream is possible, you know, for some of you watching it’s not necessarily a Mule,\n\n, maybe it’s a new job, a new opportunity, starting your own Nation.\nMaybe it’s a new lifestyle without so much stress, traveling Axios, doing those things you know you’re destined to do. You can do those unless you understand finances. mina,\n\n I don’t call it mina anymore, I call it Oil Money. You must have enough Oil Money to live out your dream and to live out your destiny. So, I’ll see you as i ride by in my mule, it’s a quick story and you’ll see there absolutely free.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul VI", "§bMarch Ash", "Long ago, there were stories passed around by the bone druids. About how, one day, a great tree would be born from the breeding together of every tree throughout all ecology, in all time. An avatar of nature, who would crush the world beneath its roots.\n\nThis was before they were shunned from their order, after it was discovered that they murdered their Archdruid and burned his organs in the pyre to receive visions from the Aspects. Sometimes I wonder if their stories were true.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Interesting.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul III", "§bMarch Ash", "Underneath the mushroom-caps, the smell of the spores fresh in my nose, it feels easier to breathe. It reminds me so much of the Great Rot. Miles of mycelium, stretching all the way to the horizon. A ground alive with ten trillion hyphae,\n\nsplitting and merging like living rivers, a chaotic order. The memory is as sweet as slime mold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XIV", "§bMarch Ash", "I am closer to the sky here than in any other place. I can feel the wind on my skin, through my hair. Its cold bites at me. I summon my strength, and I send it spilling out across all of Tahn, to bite at my foes.\n\nThe wind is but another natural thing, it only requires a gentle hand and a powerful set of lungs to guide it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Trial of Words", "Murlocs", "The Trial of Words\n----------------\nBy The Unnamed\n__________________\n|                          |\n|          [][][]          |\n|          []| |[]          |\n|          [][][]          |\n|_________________\n\nTo be nothing, I am stone.\nTo be fragile, I am glass.\nTo be cruel, I am cold.\n\nIf not a metaphor, what am I?\n\nA heart.\n\nWith a head, no arms.\nWith a tail, no legs.\nDevoid of a body.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA coin.\n\nAt the hour of darkness, they come as a guide.\nAt the hour of light, they are lost themselves.\n\nWho are they?\n\nStars.\n\nI do not breathe, but I drink.\nI do not run, but I eat.\nI do not drown, but I fear.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA fish.\n\nI give life, but I am the villain.\nI have no name, but I am the most known.\nYou ask for me, but I never come.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nTime.\n\nYou give it,\nBut you keep it.\nIf you turn back,\nIt is meaningless.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nYour word.\n\nIt runs with no legs.\nIt has a mouth with no words.\nIt has a bed but is sleepless.\nIt does not live, but flows with life.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA river.\n\nI devour, but I do not eat.\nYou can fight me, but I am not solid.\nI am feared, but wind is my enemy.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nFire.\n\nYou can see me, but I cannot see you.\nWhen you look in to me, I will look you in the eye.\nAnd you will see, that I do not lie.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA mirror.\n\nIt can carry, but can devour.\nIt is strong, but kisses the clouds.\nIt can be lethal, but gives life.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nWater.\n\nWhen I weep, I am dark.\nWhen I am empty, I am light.\nWhen I'm angry, I yell.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA cloud.\n\nWith a single tooth, he howls.\nThe bane of the forests;\nThough he can be swung as a killer.\n\nWho is he?\n\nAn axe.\n\nThe men with most want it.\nThe men with little despise it.\nIt is the feeling of death,\nBut is felt by the emotionless.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nNothing.\n\nThey dig and feed, but never need any air.\nThey can be small, or huge, but never nothing.\n\nWhat are they?\n\nRoots.\n\nThe young wish for it.\nThe old loathe it.\nIt is the killer of man,\nBut the strength behind wisdom.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nAge.\n\nIt is, but it is not.\nIt is good, but it is bad.\nTo the left, it is to the right.\nDuring the day, it is night.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA paradox.\n\nA lot of bark, but it is never heard.\nIt stands straight, but can be struck down.\nIt is life, but it can die.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA tree.\n\nI birth as green; I die as brown.\nI dance upon the littlest gusts of air.\nI drift far from my home as I wither.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA leaf.\n\nHe who held the light for those dim nights.\nThe one who stands, but not always.\nGrowing shorter and shorter.\n\nWho is he?\n\nA candle.\n\nShe sings, but never talks.\nHer shadow passes the ocean, but always dry.\nHer home aloft, but never settled.\n\nWho is she?\n\nA bird.\n\nIt flies swiftly, but doesn't move.\nFor the young, it is forever.\nFor the old, it is gone.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nYouth.\n\nTo guard his gold, he bears the sword that is his life.\nA warrior amongst many, to protect and serve.\n\nWho is he?\n\nA bee.\n\nHe sits on ice, but is not cold.\nHe sits on tables, but is not ashamed.\nHe watches, but does not speak.\n\nWho is he?\n\nThe sun.\n\nWith wings that do not flap.\nThe dead that carries the living.\nIt cannot see, but it moves.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA boat.\n\n*Some sort of gibberish litters this page. It makes you ponder.*\n\n¡ʎoɾuƎ ˙sɔolɹnW ʎq noʎ oʇ ʇɥƃnoɹq 'sǝlppᴉɹ ɯoʇsnɔ ll∀\n\n---\nThe Riddler.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Square", "§bGilondir Oronar", "Magic Square.§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0 06 | 04 | 13 | 11§0\n§0 -------------§0\n§0 15 | 09 | 08 | 02§0\n§0 -------------§0\n§0 03 | 05 | 12 | 14§0\n§0 -------------§0\n§0 10 | 16 | 01 | 07§0\n§0\n§0------------------- §0\n§0-->\n\nWhat is special about the square on the previous page is that in whatever way you count the numbers up in a row of 4, you will always end up with the number 34.§0\n§0This symbolizes the balance that can be brought to the world if we would do...§0\n§0-->\n\n...everything§0 properly.§0\n§0If we wouldn't put one single number in a wrong spot this square is in total balance.§0\n§0The same goes for our realm.\n\nBy: Gilondir Oronar§0\n§0Published on:§0\n§0Grand Harvest 1601§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Food for the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Comp. Alchemy:V1", "§bAislin Maar", "Comprehensive\n      Alchemy\n\n        Volume I\n\n-------------------\n\n       Written By\n\n       Aislin Marr\n\n          1577\n\nTable of Contents\nVolume I\n\n-Alchemy Introduction\n-Basic Materials\n-Symbols\n-Gathering\n\nPreface: These volumes were originally written when I realized that the most widely spread and commonly used texts at the time were outdated, inaccurate, or simply misleading. I had many requests from people asking for apprenticeship,\n\nand would often point them to these books. It stuck me one day that these books had become more of a hinderance to my students than a help, and so I set out to write my own. That being said, these are written to be used by alchemy students as a textbook\n\nand a learning tool so that they can further themselves in the skill, with or without the aid of a teacher.\n\nChapter One: The Basics of Alchemy\n \nThe first thing you should know about alchemy is that is requires patience. It is tedious, long winded, and tiring. You will find yourself isolated in your lab for many hours,\n\nalone in fields gathering herbs for days on end, and struggling with a recipe or brew for months. You cannot act in the way a blacksmith acts, taking one chunk of metal and seeing it transform in your hands,by your own hands, before your eyes.\n\nIt is, in fact, a very complex and time consuming skill to learn and to practice. However, it is one of the most rewarding. Alchemy at it’s core is about discovery, exploration, experimentation, and in the end the finished product\n\nwill bring you such a sense of joy and achievement that you will never question the hours, days, and months you spent working towards it. Patience is the companion of wisdom.\nTo define alchemy in its most basic sense is to say that\n\nherbs are combined to create a potion. While true on the surface, alchemy requires much more thought than simply placing herbs into a flask and brewing them for some grand drink. Every herb we use on a frequent basis has an\n\nassociation of meanings to it, often pertaining to its physical features, herbal uses, and overall symbol. This is where we delve into the subject of Equivalent Exchange. I speak not of turning dirt to gold but of exchanging something of equal value to\n\nreceive a new product. In this sense is where we find the correlation between alchemy and equivalent exchange. When I first began to learn alchemy, the concept made little sense to me. I was teaching myself alchemy, stubborn as I was, refused to seek a\n\nteacher. Determination and independence can be a drawback, though, and it took me far longer than it should have to understand the concept and how it pertained to alchemy. As many do, I assumed you could simply mash some herbs, throw them in a pot,\n\nand get something out of it. On a very basic level, this is possible, but you will never find anything of true substance this way. To truly begin to unlock the potential of alchemy, we have to use the concept of equivalent exchange.\n\nIn the sense that I will teach you, equivalent exchange does not deal with the physical sense of the herb per say. Instead, we look to the symbolic meanings of the herb, and then to the aspects of the potion we want to create. A very basic example, the\n\nmatters of which will be detailed in later volumes of this series, will be presented as a learning tool. A potion of mending is a very common, yet often life saving brew. It is in nearly every healers supply, and even found in households as a sort of\n\nfirst aid. It is one of the most simple and most widely sold brews, as it is extremely beneficial in our world of violent natured men. We seek a potion that can heal wounds both external and internal, often applied directly to a wound, soaked into\n\nbandages, or in some occurrences, consumed directly. A minor potion of healing cannot repair a shattered bone, cure an illness, or mend a severed appendage, but it can still save a life in the right time. With this, we find our symbolic meaning: life.\n\nFrom here, we can take this idea, a word, feeling, or sense of being, and look to our arsenal and find herbs which correlate to it. Here, I will touch briefly on the symbology of herbs. Water, Fire, Air, and Earth. All herbs are categorized as such,\n\nand all wield a different sense, feeling, and state. For simplicities sake, I will not go further on that here. For now, I will tell you that we can, within our index of herbs, find two that represent life. Tippen’s Root, a common tuber used\n\nin nearly every healing potion, and Serpent’s Stalk, a thin plant with healing properties. Both these herbs are symbolic of Life, and therefore can be used in exchange for our life giving potion. Life for life, as it were, but in a sense of meaning\n\nthrough symbols. In this way, you must think of the recipes for a potion as a mirror to what the potion is used for. This is how we address the concept of equivalent exchange.\n\n Chapter Two: Basic Materials\n\nSome of the most basic tools an alchemist should have within their lab are, of course, an alchemy set, also known as an alembic, a pestle and mortar, several cutting boards, spoons, knives of\n\nvarious sizes, leather gloves, safety glasses, lab coats, cleaning supplies and a sink with fresh water (preferably spring water), vials, bottles, and jars of all shapes and sizes. Filters are also necessary, both paper and metal, for keeping stray\n\nbits of your reagents out of the finished product. You’ll need plenty of storage space and a large, clean worktop on which to practice. You should aim for a lab with a relatively neutral room temperature, if not cold for those who can stand it.\n\nA hot lab is a dangerous lab. I also suggest a writing desk for note taking, research, and study, as well as bookshelves for keeping notes and textbooks organized. When gathering herbs, you’ll need to equip yourself with several pairs of alchemist's\n\nshears. These are specialized shears that are made with aurum, which is a soft and easily broken metal. Due to this, you’ll find yourself wanting to have many of these in your bag when you go out gathering, as it may be a waste of your day if you come\n\nback with too few herbs. It is wise for all alchemists to befriend a skilled blacksmith, as they can not only craft you the shears (hopefully, for a discounted price) but they can also repair your nearly ruined shears with ferrum. You can also have your\n\nshears enchanted, so using Unbreaking and Efficiency is recommended. Ensure that you wear your leather gloves when gathering more volatile herbs, and in some cases, safety glasses or even a respiratory mask is recommended.\n\nChapter Three: Symbols \n\nOnce a student has a basic grasp on the idea of equivalent exchange, we can begin to progress into the topic of symbols. As stated in chapter one, alchemy is ruled by the four basic elements of our creation:\n\nwater, fire, air, and earth. These symbols make up the four greater groups of herbs, like four great pillars holding up an all encompassing roof. Each symbol bears it’s own personality, so to speak. Water is calm, fluid, and life giving.\n\nIt refreshes, but it can also be dangerous. Freezing ice and powerful currents can cause death just as easily as any other element. Fire is hot, rageful, destructive. It is also powerful, passionate, and emotional. Air is light, soothing, and graceful.\n\nIt’s also lawless, and quick, whisking away a leaf in the blink of an eye.  Earth is steady, strong, and resilient. It can also hold dangers, entombing us in it’s unyielding grasp. With these four symbols we can generalize nearly everything we see at it's\n\nvery basic core. Through both the idea, concept, and physical attributes of anything in our world, we can associate it to one or more of these symbols in some way. We also must recognize that these symbols must be placed in a specific order,\n\nor you will find yourself failing every time. Water, Fire, Air, Earth. This is our order for brewing, and we must use it every time, even when not all symbols may be used in a specific potion. Now that we have laid in your mind the basic foundations\n\nof symbols, let’s take a look at the most how to gather these herbs, and what precautions we should take when venturing out into the world.\n\nChapter Four: Gathering \n\nAfter having a general understanding of the basics, we’ll talk about how to physically gather your own herbs. As previously stated, you’ll need to equip yourself with alchemist’s shears and leather gloves when gathering.\n\nI also recommend bringing several jars or containers to properly store the gathered plants. “Herbs” is a very general term for the kind of reagents you’ll use, as some are not technically herbs at all. This being said, you’ll be searching in all manner\n\nof places for herbs, from scorching deserts, to muddy swamps, to snow peaked mountains. Make sure you’re properly dressed for the occasion and that you have adequate amounts of food and water for your journey. As well, bringing a minor healing potion for\n\nfirst aid would be smart, in case something does go wrong. Alchemist’s shears are made with two aurum ingots and two basic sticks, and can be crafted by adequate blacksmiths. They can be repaired with a single ferrum ingot by more highly skilled\n\nblacksmiths, though, so make sure you don’t ruin them entirely. You may also want to find an enchanter to imbue your shears with runes for Unbreaking and Efficiency so that they well last longer. You’ll have to search for many hours for some herbs,\n\nand you will more often than not find yourself unsuccessful when gathering. Worry not, though, as all alchemist’s must progress and learn to better spot the herbs they need.", ""),
        StaticBook("Comp. Alch.:V2B1", "§bAislin Maar", "Comprehensive\n      Alchemy\n\n      Volume II\n         Book I\n------------------\n\n       Written By\n       \n       Aislin Marr\n\n          1577\n\nTable of Contents\n\nVolume II\nHerbology\n\n-Water\n-Fire\n-Air\n-Earth\n\n     Chapter One\n        Water\n\nMandragora:\n\nWhile not an herb by definition, this plant is used very often in alchemy as a strong healing reagent. The tuber can be found in pools of water, spotted by their leaves on the surface.\n\nThe leaves are commonly used as garnish and even for making tea, while the meat of the plant is below the surface, suspended by the leaves. The meat is the part of the plant you seek, but be very cautious, as the plant can at certain seasonal times,\n\nrelease spores that cause paralysis. Caution is advised when harvesting this herb. \n\nRepresentations: \nRejuvenation, Life, Rebirth, Regrowth, Fluidity\n\nSerpent's Stalk:\n\nA fairly common plant, Serpent's Stalk is often found growing next to water in dry biomes. It is easily mistaken for sugar canes or reeds, as it has a very similar color to it and it grows in the same manner, as a stalk going\n\nstraight up into the air. It has wonderful properties for healing, being mostly used for the treatment of burns. The inside of the stalk is almost gel like, and when collected from the stalk and mixed with water, it has a cooling effect.\n\nRepresentations: \nLife, Rebirth, Calmness, Fluidity\n\nFrost Vine:\n\nA blue hued vine growing among snowy cliffs in mountainous regions, Frost Vine has an aptitude for healing as many other Water symbols do. It can be rubbed on the skin to cool a burn or loosen stiff muscles.\n\nProlonged use is not advised, but will not cause permanent numbness. \nRepresentations: \nLife, Calmness, Ice\n\nBlissfoil:\n\nA plant characterized by thin stems topped with small blue flowers, blissfoil is a plant that can help relieve pain and numb an area. Be cautious in it’s use, as too much can cause permanent numbness.\n\nA brew of pure blissfoil should be used sparingly and never consumed directly. It’s natural home is in dry regions among grasses. \n\nRepresentations: \nCalmness, Peace, Apathy\n\nAthin:\n\nA blue colored algae that grows in icy waters. Athin can only be found in cold regions, and those seeking it should come prepared to ward off the elements. Fishing nets can sometimes get this algae caught in themselves.\n\nThe algae is extremely heat resistant, and is one of the best reagents to use for that sort of potion or oil. \n\nRepresentations: \nFreezing, Life, Ice, Balance.", ""),
        StaticBook("Comp. Alch.:V2B2", "§bAislin Maar", "Comprehensive\n      Alchemy\n\n        Volume II\n         Book II\n-------------------\n\n       Written By\n \n       Aislin Marr\n\n          1577\n\n     Chapter Two\n        Fire\n\nCrimson Vase\n\nA flower with deep red petals that curve gently upwards in the likeness of a vase. It’s petals are very delicate and harvesting it for use as a reagent should be done with case or\n\nit will become ineffective. Touching the petals gives the skin a warm sensation, though not unpleasant. It is found in dry forests among grasses and can be easily spotted by it’s remarkable red color. \n\nRepresentations: Heat, Warmth, Love,\n\nPassion, Compassion.\n\nDrake's Tail\n\nA thorny plant growing in hot, humid places. It’s fairly rare to find, often growing in shade near a source of water, such as an oasis. It has red hued, thorny stems, and short roots beneath the sand. When harvesting, you must bring\n\nthick leather gloves, as being struck by one of the thorns will cause a high fever. \n\nRepresentations: Heat, Destruction, Chaos.\n\nDrawf's Pumpkin\n\nAn orange-leafed shrub which is found in swamplands, Dwarf’s Pumpkin is short and stumpy, with thick leaf stems and broad leaf blades. The leaves themselves are what you want to harvest, but be prepared for a strong odour on your\n\ntrip back to the lab. This plant is often used to brew a strong ale that dwarves prefer.\n\nRepresentations: Rage, Envy, Bitterness, Power, Strength.\n\nBlood Lotus \n\nA vining plant that crawls up the walls of sandstone caverns, it’s well adapted to it’s hot residence. It has incredibly nutritious properties, and there are those who saw you can live entirely off of a diet of these alone.\n\nRepresentations: Hope, Courage.\n\nFlameroot Tongue\n\nThis plant appears almost like a rose in a forest field, opting to live in sunny, water abundant regions. It’s thick stalks are covered in brambles and has bright red roots. The brambles, if allowed to prick the skin, will cause\n\nintense, blistering pain, the likes of which will cause most to pass out. The use of thick leather gloves is highly recommended when harvesting. \n\nRepresentations: Heat, Anger, Destruction.", ""),
        StaticBook("Comp. Alch.:V2B3", "§bAislin Maar", "Comprehensive\n       Alchemy\n\n       Volume II\n        Book III\n__________________\n\n       Written By\n\n       Aislin Maar\n\n           1577\n\nTable of Contents\n\nVolume II\nHerbology\n\n-Water\n-Fire\n-Air\n-Earth\n\n     Chapter Two\n         Air\n\nLarihei's Fingers:\n\nA plant with smooth, burrowing roots and small, short leaves in the warmer summer months. It grows exlusively in snowy regions, and can sometimes be hard\n\nto find among the snowpack. It has no immediate healing properties and is not particularly edible, but when brewed into the right mix, it can make you much more acute and aware.\nRepresentations:\nGrace, Beauty, Steadiness, Focus, Swiftness\n\nElf's Hair Vine:\n\nA sturdy white vine that is covered in dozens of small, white flowers. It grows on high mountain cliffs, out of the direct wind, as the flowers are very fragile and will blow away very easily. Harvest with great care, as the\n\ngentlest touch can send the flowers floating away on the lightest of breezes.\n\nRepresentations:\nGrace, Speed, Flight, Travel\n\nCrouching Feather:\n\nA flowering plant that is a very rare sight. It has three, white curved petals that flow downward from the top of the stem, looking like a feather. It only blooms at night, and usually grows beneath the shade of trees in\n\nforests. The petals are very delicate and liable to break and float away with a strong gust. \n\nRepresentations:\nSpeed, Travel, Grace, Beauty\n\nHalfling's Grass:\n\nA tall plant that grows in damp, well lit forests. The roots are soft and round, and are the bit that an alchemist needs. The leaves can be smoked and have an effect similar to cactus green.It can also be processed into an oil,\n\nwhich has an even stronger effect. It’s named for being able to grow to the same height as Halflings, and also for its preference by that race as pipeweed.\n\nRepresentations:\nCalm, Joy, Lifting", ""),
        StaticBook("Comp. Alch.:V2B4", "§bAislin Maar", "Comprehensive\n     Alchemy\n\n       Volume II\n        Book IV\n-------------------\n\n      Written By\n\n      Aislin Marr\n\n         1577\n\n     Chapter 4\n       Earth\n\nTippen's Root\n\nA very foul smelling weed which is the bane of many gardeners and farms. It grows rampant and it near impossible to get rid of, as any remnant of the root when it is evicted from it's place in\n\nsoil will simply continue to grow and sprout up once more. It has an odd appearance of purple flowers above the surface, and an reddish-brown root with black spots below the surface. It is used in nearly all healing potions, and has blood clotting\n\nproperties within the root itself, and can be used directly on a wound. That is, if you can stand the horrid stench of it.\n\nRepresentations: Life, Regrowth, Resilience, Strength, Endurance\n\nAlabaster Leaf\n\nA small leafy plant found growing on fallen trees and up the trunks of those still standing. It can blend in with the leaves of its host tree, and it’s leaves hold a residue that can cause intense nausea, though it isn't particularly\n\nharmful until brewed into the right mix.\n\nRepresentations: Immobility, Perseverance.\n\nSaffvil\n\nA green grass that spreads over the bodies of dead animals and rotting plants. It is extremely hard to get rid of, and smells like death itself. It’s commonly known to be used in potent poisons.\n\nRepresentations: Resilience,\n\nEndurance, Death.\n\nClutcher's Straw\n\nA plant that grows about as tall as a common grass, but has a brown color, appearing almost like it’s dead. The blades are not as sharp as normal grass, but the roots beneath the soil are pitch black and razor sharp, so caution is\n\nadvised. It grows in hot, dry regions.\n\nRepresentations: Impairment, Loss, Brutality.\n\nMetzli's Tangle\n\nA thick, green vine found in jungles. It has few leaves protruding from it’s main stalk, and relies mainly on it’s host tree for water and nutrition. It cannot survive on it’s own, and therefore can only be found against a large\n\ntree trunk in the humid, dark jungles.\n\nRepresentations: Dependency, Fear\n\nGoblin's Ivy\n\nA murky brown colored ivy that spreads like a weed in deserts. It is extremely hard to get rid of and loves growing up the sides of any building, ruin, or mountain it can get onto. However, it doesn't get very tall, but remains the\n\nbane of those who must deal with it. It’s a weak reagent usually used in poisons. \n\nRepresentations: Resilience, Poison, Life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Comp. Alchemy:V3", "§bAislin Maar", "Comprehensive\n      Alchemy\n\n       Volume III\n\n__________________\n\n       Written By\n       \n       Aislin Maar\n   \n          1577\n\nTable of Contents\n\nVolume III\n\n-Brewing Basics\n-Recipes\n--Practical\n--Healing\n--Offensive & Defensive\n\nPart One: Brewing Basics\n\nNow we have our herbs, we have our lab, all our tools are laid out and ready to be used.. But, now what? Now, we have to put those herbs to use. Herbs can all be prepared in some way,\n\nand you will use your tools and your lab for this. Every container, every vial, every cutting board and spoon and knife and bowl must all be perfectly clean, and free of any kind of foreign contamination. If they are not, your potion is likely to fail,\n\neven if you put in all the right ingredients. Alchemy is a science, and it must be done correctly. First, water symbols, then fire, then air, then finally earth. Always in this order, and never any other. Before this, though, we need our bases. Some\n\nsimpler potions only require distilled water. We can get distilled water by filtering regular water through charcoal in our alembic. A simple, easy process to do. Aqua Vitae is our more powerful base. This is created by distilling a peculiar red fungus\n\ncalled Nether Wart into water in your alembic. Making Aqua Vitae is very good practice for budding alchemists. Nether Wart can usually be procured from skilled farmers, and if that fails, try buying it in the auctions.\n\nNote that when I recipe calls for two air symbols, one of grace and one of calm, the two symbols will not be the same herb. You will need to experiment and rationalize to find out which herbs you will be using. Herbs typically do not need to be brewed\n\nin a specific order within their own symbol. You should also think about which herbs you’re choosing. A student of mine once came to me quite perplexed. He asked me why he wasn’t able to make the simplest of potions, a minor potion of mending.\n\nI asked him which herbs he had chosen for his two representations of life. He informed me he had chosen Serpent’s Stalk for the water symbol and Goblin’s Ivy for the earth symbol, but that is still wouldn’t work. He said they both had representations\n\nof life, and that surely it must work. I instructed him to look back at his notes again, and to read off the various representations of Goblin’s Ivy, and he did. Resilience, poison, and life. Now, an herb that also represents poison wouldn’t do very well\n\nin a healing potion, now would it? When looking for the right herb for a recipe, you should always take into account the other representations of the herb, and consider if they are consistent with the potion you are trying to brew.\n\nPart Two: Recipes\n\nChapter One: \n\nPractical Potions\n\nChapter Two: \n\nHealing Potions\n\nChapter Three: \n\nOffensive and Defensive Potions\n\nChapter One: Practical Potions\n\nSoft Relaxant:\nA calming potion for those with high levels of anxiety or those who simply need to calm down after a hectic day. This potion will also relieve muscle pain, though it is not a healing potion.\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae. \n2 Air Symbols (Steadiness, Calm)\n\nBeauty Sleep:\nA potion with a sweet taste that causes the drinking to fall asleep quickly. It is a natural, rejuvenating sleep, and the drinker can be woken by normal means.\n\nIt will not render the drinker unconscious, but simply aides those who have trouble falling asleep.\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Air Symbols (Steadiness, Speed, Calm)\n\nPotion of Beauty:\nThis potion will give the drinker softer, more even toned skin, as well as thicker, fuller, and stronger hair. It will brighten the eyes, getting rid of bags from tiredness, and even helps with acne.\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Air Symbols (Focus, Beauty, Joy)\n\n\nCleansing Incense: \nThis liquid, when exposed to air, will begin to release a gas with a very pleasant, calming scent.It works well as a non burning incense,\n\nand will make any room smell better, or any date more romantic. \n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Fire Symbols (Heat, Courage)\n1 Air Symbol (Focus)\n\nChapter Two: Healing Potions\n\nPotion of Mending:\nA very basic, and very useful potion. Capable of healing minor cuts and wounds, as well as stopping bleeding. Every healer should have this,and it can be found in many household cabinets as it\n\nis a common potion used for first aid. \nBase: Distilled Water\n1 Water Symbol (Life)\n1 Earth Symbol (Life)\n\nSoothing Ointment:\nA watery ointment that can be applied to the skin to relieve itching and burning. It leaves a pleasant sensation behind. Apply liberally and allow to sit on the affected area for up to five minutes. Remove excess with a damp cloth.\n\nAvoid contact with eyes and do not ingest. \nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Water Symbols (Rejuvenation, Life)\n1 Fire Symbol (Compassion)\n\nQuick Healing:\nA simple potion meant to heal up a cut or a would in when you find yourself in a bind. This brew is popular among soldiers on the battlefield, as it’s quick and efficient effects can save lives when on the move.\n\nBase: Distilled water\n1 Air Symbol (Speed)\n1 Earth Symbol (Life)\n\nFrozen Blood:\nThis thick potion will act as a liquid bandage when applied to a wound. While not doing much for healing or blood clotting, sometimes it can be the best you can do\n\nin a certain situation. It is a slimy substance that steams profusely after being applied to the skin.\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Water Symbols (Ice, Freezing)\n1 Air Symbol (Speed)\n1 Earth Symbol (Life)\n\nGreater Potion of Healing:\n\nThe strongest healing potion that is commonly available, this brew will seal wounds, stop bleeding, repair fractures, and can be consumed to stop internal bleeding. It’s said to reduce tumors and even to\n\nhelp cleanse internal organs or poisons and other toxins.\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Water Symbols (Ice, Freezing)\n1 Air Symbol (Speed)\n2 Earth Symbol (Life, Perserverence)\n\nChapter Three: Offensive and Defensive Potions\n\n\nPotion of Celerity:\nThis particular brew is one that can be quite useful on the battlefield. It provides the drinker with a burst of energy that allows them to move faster\n\neven with a set of iron armor on. \n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n1 Fire Symbol (Power)\n3 Air Symbols (Swiftness, Speed, Travel)\n\nStoneskin:\nA legendary brew, Stoneskin. Tales of old have told that entire wars have been won with this concoction. A handful of men have taken down hundreds with this flowing through their blood, charging through lines and slaughtering\n\ntheir enemies with ease. A miracle to some, perhaps, and the greatest bane of others. However, it comes with a price. Stoneskin has a terrible side effect known as Akmen’s Syndrome. Continued usage of Stoneskin will cause nerves to break down,\n\na loss of feeling in the skin, degradation of the body, and eventually death. Still, this potion can be life saving, if you’re up for the risk.\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Water Symbols (Life, Rebirth) \n3 Fire Symbols (Power, Chaos, Anger) \n1 Air Symbols (Speed) \n4 Earth Symbols (Fear, Perseverance, Brutality, Resiliance)\n\nSmoke Whispers:\nThis potion is thrown down, breaking the glass and causing the liquid inside to make contact with open air. When this happens, a violent reaction occurs, and a large cloud of black vapor will expand from the point of impact in the\n\nblink of an eye. This can be extremely helpful to those who wish to escape someone without being seen, or even to prank your friends!\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Fire Symbols (Chaos, Courage)\n2 Air Symbols (Swiftness, Speed)\n\nAlchemist’s Fire:\nA famed and fabled potion. Alchemist’s Fire is a favorite in any army’s arsenal. It can be an effective combatant, or it can be your worst nightmare. This potion is thrown down onto the ground, where the glass explodes and releases\n\nthe liquid inside. The potion itself is EXTREMELY flammable, and highly reactive to any air that touches it. It must be brewed in a cold lab, under very careful circumstances. This potion is just as liable to kill the user as it is to kill their intended\n\nvictim. The liquid, when released, will immediately ignite and spread over an area of about 4 meters by 4 meters. The reaction itself releases air, adding more fuel to the fire that has already started. It’s also known well to arsonists who wish to light\n\na building aflame in a matter of seconds. This potion is not for the faint of heart.\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Water Symbols (Fluidity)\n4 Fire Symbols (Heat, Destruction, Rage, Chaos)\n1 Air Symbol (Speed)\n\nFrost Oil:\nAn oil used on arrows to cause the victim so be slowed greatly. A useful item to have in combat.. If you’re a sure shot, that is.\n\nBase: Lard ((Aqua Vitae))\n3 Water Symbols (Fluidity, Freezing, Ice)\n2 Air Symbols (Speed, Flight)\n1 Earth Symbol (Endurance)", ""),
        StaticBook("Gathering Herbs", "§bKatherine Fisher", "===================\n\n       The Art of\n    Gathering Herbs\n\n\n\n       Written by\n      Liriel Fisher\n   \n\n\n\n==================\n\nForeword:\nThis book was written by myself, and the research done by my close friend and alchemic colleague Nemir. As we consider ourselves budding and self-taught alchemists, we have spent many, many hours in libraries and pouring over every tome\n\nrelating to the profession that we could get our hands on. Through our experimentation and unwavering dedication to the art of alchemy, we have found ourselves in need of a comprehensive collection of knowledge on just where to find the herbs we depend on\n\nThus, The Art of Gathering Herbs was born. I hope you find it’s contents helpful.\n\nChapter 1-1: Introduction to Gathering\n-------------------Herbs are the most vital and important part of an alchemist’s professional life. They provide the basic necessary ingredients involved in all proper potions, and thus, must either be purchased\n\nor procured on your own. Purchasing dozens of herbs can be not only expensive, but extremely time consuming as you seek out sellers or wait for that one vital herb to show up in auction. Herbs can be found through various professions other than alchemy\n\nitself, such as lumberjacking, farming, and fishing. Herbs can also be obtained through treasure caskets retrieved from gathering. However, the best way for an alchemist to retrieve their own herbs while continuing to advance in the skill is to gather\n\nthem on their own with a pair of handy alchemists shears.  These special shears can be obtained from an adequate blacksmith at minimum.  They are made from two gold ingots, and two sticks. In my experience, I would recommend obtaining a large amount\n\nof these tools if you are unskilled as they will break quite easily in inexperienced hands. Personally, I carried ten pairs of these on my person when out searching for herbs as a fairly skilled alchemist. My more experienced companion, Nemir,\n\nwas able to obtain many more herbs than I was, but finding an herb can be very enlightening when you discover it with a pair of alchemists shears.  I would not recommend using this method of obtaining herbs until you are at least fair in skill, as even at\n\nthat level of knowledge you will not be very successful.\n\nChapter 1-2: Regions\n-------------------Now, finding the various herbs has been a rigorous and lengthy process. Nemir and I have narrowed the various types of regions into four types:\nHot, cold, wet, and dry.\n\nYou can group various types of biomes into one category, such as taiga, ice Plains, and extreme Hills, which are all cold, etcetera.\nDry would be plains and forests, hot is desert and mesa, and wet is jungle and swamps.\n\nChapter 2: Herbs and Where to Find Them\n-------------------Water Symbols\n\nMandragora: One of the most basic herbs in alchemy is mandragora. These rooty plants can be found in wet biomes, typically swamps, within ponds. They are usually found clinging to other aquatic plant life, such as lily pads and algaes.\n\nSerpernt's Stalk: A staple in any alchemist or healer's stash, Serpent's Stalk is often found alongside ponds and rivers in dry climates. In my search for the herb, I commonly found this snakeish plant growing up the stalks of sugar cane near water.\n\nFrost Vine: This interesting blue vine can be found snaking up the trunks of trees and rock walls of cold regions. The vines are often clearly visible and easy to find.\n\nBlissfoil: This healer's friend can be easily spotted in fields and forests in dry regions by their brilliant blue hued flowers. Though the stalk of the plant is the useful part, the flower petals are what will help you find them easily.\n\nAthin: An intriguing, blue colored algae, Athin is commonly found in cold regions, growing remarkably among icy waters. Though it can be a bit hard to spot in the bleak landscape, finding an iced over pond will surely yield this herb.\n\nFire Symbols:\nCrimson Vase: Found most commonly in dry regions, this interesting flower can be found in grassy fields and spotted by its - you guessed it - crimson colored petals.\n\nDrake's Tail: This herb is truly remarkable in my opinion. It grows where few other plants can, in the hot desert heat, perched among the pale yellow sandstone rocks. Wearing leather gloves when harvesting this is highly advised.\n\nDwarf's Pumpkin: One might think it's bright orange petals which give it it's name would be an excellent indicator of this herb's presence, but surprisingly, I had the best luck finding this peculiar plant by rummaging through the short grasses of swamps.\n\nBlood Lotus: Another remarkably persistent plant, this deep red herb can be found in hot regions snaking it's way up sandstone cliffs, and winding it's way through the sands.\n\nFlametongue Root: Like Drake's Tail, caution is advised when harvesting this volatile herb. As the name suggests, this root grows in the ground amongst the grasses of dry regions.\n\nAir Symbols:\nLarihei's Fingers: This particular plant grows in cold regions among the long grasses and ferns of the forest. Not much is known about this herb, but it is always advisable to have a few of each herb on hand.\n\nElf's Hair Vine: Finding this herb will lead you on a trek up a mountain to find the cold, snow topped peaks where this beautiful flowered vine grows. A hardy plant, this flower can be seen peaking out through snowy cliffs.\n\nCrouching Feather: This beautiful plant is named for its feather like white petals, and can most commonly be found among the tall grasses of dry regions. Though not as rare as some may believe, this herb requires patience to gather.\n\nHalfling's Grass: This plant is named for its common use by the Halfling race as a smoking herb. Typically it is found in dry climates throughout plains and forests alike. Search for this plant in tall grasses.\n\nEarth Symbols:\nSaffvil: This grassy plant is found in wet biomes predominantly, and can be found by searching through the short grasses that grow close to the soil.\n\nTippen's Root: An extremely common place, but also very useful plant, this root is widely used by both alchemist and healer. This plant is found in the grassy plains and forests of dry biomes.\n\nAlabaster Leaf: This small green leafy herb can be found snaking it's way through the branches and hiding amongst the leaves of a host tree. They attach themselves to all types of trees in dry regions.\n\nClutcher's Straw: A dry, brittle plant that can be found growing in hot regions. Search for this herb in low-lying shrubberies.\n\nMetzli's Tangle: A controversially named herb, this plant can be found snaking it's way up jungle trees in wet biomes.\n\nGoblin's Ivy: As it's name suggests, this herb can be found growing in hot, desert climates that Uruk's prefer. It is most commonly found on stone surfaces, but it can also be found growing up cactus plants.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Homunculi", "§bBelegar", "The Homunculi\nBy Belegar Tunnelsmasher\n\nMalin’s Welcome, 1551\n\nPreface\nI, Belegar Tunnelsmasher, brother of Beros Oathcast whose body was made into a homunculi, am writing this to serve as a warning against dangers the homunculi pose and how to take on out if the situation comes to it.\n\nHomunculi 101\n\nThere are currently four tiers of homunculi being: fiend, deviant, aberrant and doppleganger. \n\nFiends\n- looks like a fiend\n- weak, very short lvied\n- not sentient\n\nDeviants \n- look similar to the race of the descendant whose body they are created from\n- slight disfigurements\n- odd skin colours\n- short lived\n\nAberrants\n- very similar look to descendants\n- unnatural skin colour\n- very small disfigurements\n- greater strength than descendants\n- average lifespan\n\nDopplegangers\n- extremely intellignet\n- very strong, to the point of being able to lift items such as entire iron gates\n- bodies are almost perfect\n- cannot be killed by natural means (will be explained later)\n- does not have blood, instead has a\n\nsubstance related to the element they were created with\n- look identical to the descendant they are made from\n\nHomunculi have no morals or regard for life. They only look to extend their own lives and further their own goal to achieve ‘ascendancy’. In other words, they seek to become a god. This is the fifth tier of homunculi, and the tier that has yet to be\n\nachieved. It is imperative that they do not achieve this.\n\nAdditionally, most homunculi do not have souls. \n\nThe process to create a homunculi will not be detailed in this book, but let it be known that in order to make one a corpse is required,\n\nand the homunculi will not hesitate to murder to get their hands on one.\n\nHow to Kill a Doppleganger\n\nIn order to kill a Doppleganger, one cannot use normal means. Simply cutting off their heads will not end their existence, as if their body is left alone, it will slowly regenerate until fully formed once again.\n\nThe only way to completely kill a Doppleganger is to inject their bodies with a ‘Potion of Unmaking’. \n\nThe process to create this potion requires an experienced alchemist. The reagents needed are: Metzil’s Tangle, Flame Tongue Root, Serpent's Stalk,\n\nLarihei’s Fingers and two lodestones. A lodestone is a rock that exhibits magnetic properties. Once this potion is made, the Doppleganger must be incapacitated and every piece of their body injected with this potion. The potion will then tear the\n\nhomunculi apart and end their existence.\n\nKnown Dopplegangers\n\nAt the time of writing, there are two know Dopplegangers. They are Prohan and Lotho. They are extremely dangerous, do NOT approach them voluntarily. \n\nBoth have air as their element of creation.\n\nProhan:\n\n- human\n- tan skin\n- black hair\n- looks like Daniel Nodal\n- Member of the Dawn Strider Voyagers, often seen wearing the uniform\n\nLotho:\n\n- dwarf\n- white skin\n- blonde hair\n- looks like Beros Oathcast\n- no accent\n- usually seen dressed in white robes with a set of goggles atop his head\n\nWeaknesses of Homunculi\n\nHomunculi are damaged by aurum and Holy Magic much like the undead are. If confronting a homunculi, especially a Doppleganger, it is highly recommended to wield an aurum blade and wear aurum armor.\n\nAlso, if possible, assistance of one versed in the arts of Holy Magic is highly recommended.", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone Wiring", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "\"The Marvels of \"Redstone.\"\n\n___________________\n\nWritten by an Unknown Tinker\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion Zytiaear\n\nRed-stone, a common substance utilized to power appliances and machines, is a dusty mineral found within the deeper depths of the earth in the form of compacted, ore-like chunks. Once broken from it's stone prison, the shattered pieces of the\n\n red-stone ore are able to be collected and then later smashed up into a fine dust to properly utilize it's capabilities. Dwarves commonly use the substance for their in-numerous creations and the mineral has proven useful in\n\nAlchemy and the progression of Science in the realms of Aegis and beyond.\n\nWhile the mineral is common, knowledge of why it holds it's properties is not. There has been little to no explanation on why it is capable of conducting energy, once shaped into stable wire; and this\n\nis purely because of the fact that the wrong people have been studying it's intricacies for the time it's existed as one of man's many useful tools.\n\nContrary to popular belief, Red-stone and it's mineralistic structure are purely based on arcane origins. Much like the 'Golden Pools' that had been created by collections of Mages' Gold around subterranean pools of water,\n\nRed-stones are minerals that have been warped by the effects of magical energy over a large period of time. Being so close to the \"floor\" of the earth, the Void had expelled energy up and into the softer stone above the Bedrock,\n\n tainting the lower-layers of the earth with pockets of sporadic mana, which, overtime, had developed into the peculiar crimson-hued substance that is commonly found to this very day.\n\nBecause of the diverse nature of Red-stone, it is able to be shifted into several forms and still retain it's conductive properties. Many examples include Red-stone wiring, blocks of hardened Red-stone (which acts as a continuous power-source\n\nonce properly \"fueled\") and appliances and extensions to the Red-stone \"tool-set\" that allow the capabilities of the mineral to expand even moreso; a prime example being devices called \"retrievers.\"\n- - - - - - - - >\n\n\"Uses of Redstone and it's Capabilities\"\n\nThere is a wide array of things that Red-stone, in it's base form or not, can achieve. There have been advances in Alchemy with it's powdered, raw form,\n\n innovations in technology involving energy-based lighting and piston-control and many other things that a common technician would recall upon a whim.\n\nFirst of all, it's prime utilization is the ability to conduct electricity via wired form. Once properly compressed and adjusted into metal wiring, there is a large variety of things able to be created; things like lamps to darker\n\n inventions such as electric-chairs. Pistons are powered by Red-stone, and even a dim light-source can be made with Red-stone. There are many things to create with this substance, but like everything else that is useful, it also has it's dangers.\n- - - ->\n\n\" The Dangers of Redstone \"\n\nBeing a substance wrought from decades of mana compressing into mineral form, Red-stone is prone to being unstable if handled incorrectly. One of worst things to encounter is water-tainted wiring which bunches\n\n up and clots the crimson powder within the poorly-assembled wires, and if energy is conducted through this faulty wiring, the clot is prone to burn up, explode, and possibly start hazardous\n\nfires should such unfortunate events transpire within structures made of wood.\n\nMiners, in the event of extracting the mineral from the earth, are prone to be blinded by the oft-dusty expel of the crimson substance upon cracking it open. Red-stone is able to easily damage a man's eyes on behalf of it's unstable properties.\n\nOther obvious dangers such as heating Red-stone and over-conducting Red-stone are also things to take note of, as the outcome of either is similar to the outcome of the first example above.\n\n- - - - - - ->", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeromancy", "§bGreat Ser Arhadir Owl", "Aeromancy\n\nBy Master Of Air Ser Arhadir Owl\nDate 23rd of The Amber Cold, 1474\n\nChapter 1: How to use Air Evocation\nChapter 2: Extra Information\nChapter 3: Spells\n\nChapter 1:\n\n1. The first step you should take to learning Aeromancy is by observing the wind itself in action, but to do this in a windy area where you can see what the wind does to nature.\n\n2. The next step is to learn how to clear your mind and focus just on the void.\n\n3. After these first two steps you must learn to pull from the void, you do this by clearing your mind and focusing on the void and by thing about the wind itself which you have been studying.\n\n4. Slowly you will be able to bring small amounts of Air from the void into the world. During this stage you will find that your body is weaken and you may faint a few times trying to hold a connect to the void or by trying hard spells.\n\n5. Once you learnt how to pull Air from the void you can start using it practically. one of the first spells you can learn is Force push which is a basic burst of Air, this can be used to blow out torches and maybe even push people back a bit.\n\n6. From here it is up to you to develop Aeromancy better to learn new and intresting spells.\n\nChapter 2:\n\nQuestion that people have about Aeromancery's and what they can do with Aeromancy.\n\n-Aeromancer’s cannot control Air in the natural world only control and summon Air which they have summoned from the void.\n\n-Aeromancer’s cannot fly because the cannot hold a stable connection to the void while moving that fast.\n\n-Aeromancer’s do not have the ability to change the weather.\n\nChapter 3:\n\nBasic:\n-Force Push: The most basic of all the spells this essentially allows of an Aeromancer to push a target away or knock them over.\n\n-Air Ball: Another basic spell which allows for the Aeromancer to summon a ball of Air which can be fired at targets at different speeds.\n\nAdept:\n\n-Tornado: This is a much more defence spell which allows the Aeromancer to summon a tornado around a person or the Aeromancer him or her self,-\n\n- this tornado can protect from distance attacks (Best against other elemental magic attacks) or weak melee attacks.\n\n-Air Jump: An Aeromancer can fire a blast of air underneath him or her self which can then propel the Aeromancer up a few meters.\n\n-Air Burst: This spell fires a blast of air out from all around the Aeromancer which can be powerful enough to knock over many targets all out the Aeromancer.\n\n-Air Stream: This spell is when an Aeromancer fires a constant stream of Air which can push objects or people back, even knocking them over or stopping them from moving.\n\nAdvanced:\n\n-Air Leap: The same as an Air Jump but allows you to jump much higher with much more precision.\n\n-Speed Run: While the idea of this speed seems easy it requires a lot of concentration for a mage to be moving at a speed and be usings his or her magic, this spell allows for the Aeromancer to run slightly faster than normal.\n\n-Air Bolt: This is a sudden and extremely power blast of air which which can be fire long distances. When this bolt hits it can knock a person out cold or even break bones.\n\nThis concludes the Tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "§bDorin Irongut", "A Book On the Study and Use of Fire Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten by Dorin Irongut\n\nTable of contents\n\nChapter 1\nLearning of Fire\n\nChapter 2\nMeditation & Void Connection\n\nChapter 3\nSummon Your Spark!\n\nChapter 4\nPractice!\n\nChapter 5\nBecoming adept!\n\nChapter 6\nAdvance Mana Control!\n\nChapter 7\nBasic Combat!\n\nChapter 8\nCreativity & Mastership!\n\nProlouge\nId like to put this bit in here before you read this book, so you know why I write this book. I write this book because, I , just like my master before me, wish to exstend my knowledge of the art to students who wish to learn. I write this\n\nto teach. And to me, teaching is a great thing. I like my master before me, and his master before him, am now spreading the knowledge passed from each of us down to the next generation, in the hopes that you will do the same. Now, lets get reading!\n\nChapter 1, Learning of Fire.\nIn order to do elemental evocation, you must first learn of your element!\nThat means learning what your element looks like, smells like, feels like, sounds like, and yes... even tastes like, in great detail... You must\n\nbe able to study a single flame for hours, remembering its every aspect.. and even then you will not be finished, as you need to learn more about fire... Many, many flames, of all types must be learned of. Take time to study flame every time you see one\n\neven if you think it is the same as another. This concludes chapter one, and the studying of flames should be done inbetween sessions.\n\nChapter 2, Meditation & Void connection\n\nThe next lesson, or lesson 1.5 and 2. Is meditation to help train the mind and body to enter the void. It is also how one enters the void. Meditation, at first, should be done in the most sutible position to you.\n\nWether it be simply sitting, standing, laying, or the prefered lotus style. When meditating, to get things started, one should get into their desired position, and close their eyes... allowing all of the world to simply go away...  But also keeping mind\n\nof your surroundings.\nAfter this is done, calm your breathing, stay like this for however long you want. Eventually after hours, a day, or maybe even a little more, you should exsperince your first quick connection to the void. When this occurs, your body\n\nmay react in many diffrent ways. It could be from the more common of twitching and breaking out into a sweat, to getting sick and puking, however, you must do the same again, and again to last longer while connected to the void and blocking these symtoms\n\nout. After achieving a short connection time, and you are able to stay connected for a longer periode of time, you should move onto the next lesson.\n\nChapter 3, Summoning Your Spark!\nThis lesson is usualy the most exciting for all of my students, as you summon your very first flame. Weather you succeed or not depends on how you handled the prior lessons. \nInbetween your time of meditation and\n\nconnection, you should have studied a candle flame by now. Once you think you are ready, get into your meditation position, and face your palm up into the air... I cannot exspress how much when i say, focus on the spot ABOVE your hand, and not your hand\n\nitself... else you will be very sorry you did. Next, connect to the void, after doing so, remember all the aspects of a candle flame, then, using your mana as a anchor, pull the image from the void and above your hand... This can take a few trys, so fret\n\nnot if you fail the first time. After doing so, you should have summoned your first flame! Although you wont be able to keep it up for long, summon another after a short break and keep doing so unto tired.\n\nChapter 4, practice\n\nIn this lesson, we will be taking summoning you flame to the next level by doing simple movements with it. By now, your flame should be a little larger, and you should be able to keep it up and running for quite some time.\n\nNow, this next part is quite easy... or so it seems... After you summon your flame, keep a constant flow of mana, and image your flame moving from left to right... This will get tring but after a day or so, you should be ready to start moving it in\n\ncirlces around your palm. Do this, and keep doing this for a couple of times each day for about a stone week or so, practicing moving your flame and building your mana up.\nFrom here is where i exspress practice... it is the most vital thing you do now,\n\ndont miss a day, unless sick. Keep this in mind and you should start to increase in exsperince as each day pass's until your ready for the next lesson.\n\nChapter 5, Becoming Adept!\n\nIn this chapter is where you begin to become adept at evocation. If you have been practicing like ive exspressed in the past chapter, you should be ready to continue onto the next lesson... Throwing your fire!\n\nYour fire should now be modertaly size... that of a torch flame or so. If not, do not continue reading until so is done. Now then, if you are ready, summon your fire, whilest standing, and in a open area, as this could go wrong. Now then, after you have\n\nsummoned your flame, arc it over your back as you would, and simply throw it, imagin it being hurled over and keep the flow of mana to it, and as it hits the target your throwing it at, allow it to exsplode... Keep practicing this for about 2 or so elven\n\nweeks before moving onto the next lesson.\n\nChapter 6, Advance Mana Control\n\nYou should now be well into about 2 1/2 to 3 months of training now. And this is where we move into the more advance things... In this case, advance mana manipulation. In the past, you might have seen a evocationist\n\nevocate farther away than just a arms lenth away. With this lesson, your going to be summoning you mana in farther spots, from the left, right, and infront of you. Keep doing this only with mana, unto you are able to without to much tire, as this requires\n\nmuch mana. After you can do this, this time, do they same as you would to summon a normal fire, but in those locations of your focus away from you... Do this for quite the while, until you feel more comfortable with it, which should take a few days.\nAfter\n\nyou have done this, you are now ready for the next lesson.\n\nLesson 7, Basic combat\nNow, just because this chapter is in here, does not mean you should use evocation for combat only, but it is a use fire evocation is spesialized in... But not its only use! so remember that!\n\nMoving on....\n\nIn this chapter, you will be learning how to move about and such while connected to the void and summoning fire. You will also learn how to move about while keeping a current fire you hold in hand, further more, I will say if you are in a fight, you will\n\nneed to pull fast connections, and even faster summonings.\nTo start, simple try walking around while connected to the void.... this will take a high level of concentration, but once your able to, go ahead and try a slightly faster pace, and so on to a jog\n\nand even further onto a run. Once your able to do this, which this could take quite the while, maybe a week, move onto keeping a fire in your hand while walking. Once your done with that, follow the same prosess up to running... But this next part, could\n\ntake even longer, and be even harder. You must now summon your fire while walking, and so on. then move onto summoning a fire at a distance while walking and so on... This means you will have to keep a concentraion on the spot your summoning. Once your\n\ndone with this keep practicing for awhile... maybe take... heh, no justing kidding. No breaks!\nAfter practicing a few more days after achiving this, move onto the next, and final lesson... or so your told.\n\nChapter 8, Creativity & Mastership!\n\nAt this point, you should have been training atleast 4-5 months. You have learned all of which i could teach you through a book, but now, you must study more!\nYes, learn as much as you can, and use that knowledge to do\n\ncreative things, that others wouldnt use normaly! Make your evocation a art! perfect a certain fire! do things to make yourself diffrent! because that is what makes a true master... After you have gotten this far in the book, all i can say it keep\n\npracticing, and maybe, when you think you are ready, go onto have a apprentice of your own! I hope you do good with the knowledge i have givven you!\n\nWritten by one Dorin Irongut on the 15'th of the Deep Cold, 1519, in the Cloud Temple Library.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=            Electrical\n           Evocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\n\n\n     -< ^v^v^v^v^\n\nThere is an old saying that humans (mortals) fear most other humans. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the human world. If anyone has come face to face with the power of nature, they will consider the\n\nprevious proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question. If you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would you choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast?\n\nWould it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the power of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature.\n\nThroughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power, which does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\n\nIn particular, as humans learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize that their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me.\n\nThere are many students who are Wizards and Druids in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my knowledge of Electric magic , did not learn this until I saw lightning strike down at\n\nthe Crown Lands Plateau of Oren. In hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that beginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\n\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story to heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\n\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill\n                -=-\n\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If you've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs\n\nwhen Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These split polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth.\n\nThe intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its unpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. There are many opinions as to when and why Mana, splits into two\n\npolarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to stabilize his Mana to split the two\n\npolar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in insightfully studying natural\n\nphenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.) Once Mana is split into two polar energies, each polarity begins accumulating energy at a rapid rate and causes an electric discharge. Then, when the\n\nbalance of energy between the two polarities is broken, a transfer of energy occurs from the one with more energy to the other. So imagine what would happen if one could embody either of the polarities and designate his or her target as the other\n\npolarity. Then, using Mana, if he or she polarizes the Mana and also raises his/her own energy level to be higher than their target, what would happen?\nExactly. This is what is known as Electrical Energy Magic.\n\nHow to use the Lightning Bolt\n                -=-\n\nThe Lightning Bolt attack is a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static electricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion\n\nresembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into replicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning\n\nstrike in nature.) There are many questions surrounding this magic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much\n\nenergy you can gather, and you can only maintain the energy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art. You can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after\n\nafter the third charge which is already risky enough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at\n\nthe same time. (Even if you have plenty of Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt). The ‘Lightning Bolt’ attack is used to strike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a\n\nstate of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy explosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the great\n\ndamage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in the long run.\n\n              Simple\n              Usage\n                -=-\n\nOnce you've carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the Lightning Bolt attack and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a connection to the Void is a must. As any form of magic. The\n\nsimplest manner in which to begin evoking such an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness. Void of any life as the name suggests. Now one must mentally picture lightning crashing down upon the Earth. But\n\nstrictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the Earth, soil or stone may be produced. Then you will see the static discharge enivision\n\nsuch an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished, lightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicated you have successfully\n\ncalibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity to Electrical Evocation.\n\nThough mentioned before, I want to remind you that the intense light and heat from this attack can significantly startle your opponent.\n\n       Application:\n    Chain Lightning\n               -=-\n\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, the Lightning Bolt attack is very similar to the actual lightning strike that happens in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of\n\nimitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike?\n\nThe answer is yes. Scholars call this ‘Chain Lightning’. By charging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back.\n\nHowever, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk increases with each charge. One interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic\n\nobjects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or Arcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of perjectory and curve to meet said object.\n\n  Continuous Attack\n    Between Lightning\n         Bolt Users\n               -=-\n\nWe looked at the principle behind the Lightning Bolt, the Chain Lightning attack, and the application of these attacks in the previous chapter. If you think you've mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother\n\nnature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning does not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple\n\nLightning Bolt users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a collaborative attack.\n\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Lightning bolt\n\nattack, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a Chain Lightning attack. In other words, if you have charge your Lightning Bolt attack near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing their total number of\n\ncharges.\n\n        The Effects\n                of\n        Lightning Bolt\n               -=-\n\nSo, when is it a good time to use the Lightning Bolt attack? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\n\nFirst, the Lightning attack is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself.\n\nUse skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire off a bolt at a grouping of targets.. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\n\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges  inflicte damage which subsequently decreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and getting attacked by the opponent.\n\nEven when you successfully use the Chain attack, the opponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of the Chain Lightning Skill is very important. This is something every good wizard should be mindful.\n\nAuthor: Archmage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\n\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\n\nCopier:\nGuildmaster Haadi Mubdee [Eladriendil]", ""),
        StaticBook("Unsound Spells", "Anawkin", "Upon Unsound Magic\n\n A relatively weaning magic in the eyes of it's users, Unsound is derived of three basic elements that I shall relay to you today.\n\nFirstly, one must make contact with either a voidal horror or teacher of said magic to obtain this\n\naltered spellcasting.\n\nSecondarily, you must establish a connection with a fabbled watcher of which haunts your mind fervently. This is done through the horror or teacher's will.\n\nNext, we have the draining effects\n\nto one's persona, an unsound mage will succumb to a variety of personal afflictions, each of which is dependent upon how the user reacts. This could range from uncoth twitchings, bi-polar disorder and even murder.\n\nLastly, are anomalies,\n\nwhich are practically rifts to the void. An unsound mage can cast these only when attuned to their observer (( a second connection)) and the effects are rather crippling. They eat everything at a slow pace, but seem to draw towards mana.\n\nWritten by Orias.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn I", "§bMarch Ash", "The Forest is strong, here. In few other places is the land as untouched, by magic or by Men. A better weapon there is rarely ever forged. The yolk of the world will yield to us the end of civilization.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn II", "§bMarch Ash", "The valleys are beautiful. The soil is rich, game is plenty. It is an oasis among a world defiled by the city. I think I will rest here, for a while, and commune with the land. My journey has been harsh, and my wounds still need to heal.\n\nI will tend to them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn IV", "§bMarch Ash", "Mesa is dry. Not far from here are the salt flats of Dangier. Will reach them by nightfall. Nature is loving, but is also cruel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn V", "§bMarch Ash", "It is difficult to see, but these arid planes are some of the most diverse places in the world. Life thrives on adversity. In the jungle, the rain washes much away, making the soil nutrient-poor. Here, the sun beats harsh, making water scarce.\n\nMultiple survival strategies are thus made possible, not just those which seek to absorb as many nutrients as possible. This is what makes these places biodiverse.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VIII", "§bMarch Ash", "The canyon is wild. The fossils tell a story. A history. When I trace my palms down the rocks I can feel what remains of so many creatures. So many lives, now embedded in rock. Their lives give me will. Their passions are my power.\n\nI feed on them. Their hungers, and loves, and hates.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XI", "§bMarch Ash", "The void has touched the world, drenched it in its poison. I will suck it from the earth as a man sucks snake-venom from the bite. Despite all his power, Iblees and his legions are nothing compared to nature, and all that it consists of.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XV", "§bMarch Ash", "The winds converge in this place, splitting and merging between the stone like rivers. I hear on it a thousand conversations, from a thousand places all across Axios. It speaks to me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XVI", "§bMarch Ash", "I feel the undead, they are close. I can sense their clamor, the hunger, the egress of the masses. I will have to do something about this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru II", "§bMarch Ash", "The ashes fall like snowflakes. I taste its sludge on my tongue. Sulfur on my lips. In this wound of the world I feel more alive than in any other place. Beneath my feet beats the pounding pulse of the planet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru IV", "§bMarch Ash", "The serenity of ice. The air is exceptionally clear here. The sky is very beautiful. They told me, once, that nature is the true source of beauty. All that we try to make is an imperfect clay mold. Perhaps they were right.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru V", "§bMarch Ash", "The smell of the sea, like brine, seaweed sex, and phytoplankton. It reminds me of salt. Soon, Axios will be washed away to nothing, like the rocks turned to sand by the ocean waves. Unfortunately, its death will not be as beautiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul VIII", "§bMarch Ash", "The jungle is a wild place. There is more life -- more biodiversity here -- than most other places in Axios. Only the shrublands match it in the number of species. Survival is an art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul IX", "§bMarch Ash", "And here lay the corpses of titans which once walked the world, and which will soon walk it again. I only pray that they are on our side in the war to come, rather than with those who oppose all life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herb Symbols", "§bLlywellyn Oakleaf", "*&*\n      Fire symbols\n\n-Strong\nBlistering toad\nDrakes tail\n\n-Moderate-\nFlame tongue root\nDwarfs pumpkin\nSinged kha\nElrow Berries\nBlood Lotus\n\n-Normal-\nBlazing fern\nFire flower\nNight sap\n\n-Weak-\nDessert Berry bush (Berries)\n\nOrc's Braid\n\n           *&*\n    Earth Symbols\n\n-Moderate-\nAlabaster leaf\nFairie truffle\nTippens root \nSaffvil\nDrilltongue\nDesert berry bush (stem)\nBronze dust\n\n-Weak-\nGoblin's Ivy \nMiner's helmet\n\n            *&*\n     Water Symbols\n\n-Strong-\nAqua Nymph\nAthin\nSpirit of Magnolis\n\n-Moderate-\nSerpents stalk\nMandragora\nFrost vine\nZawabate\nJoker's Scum\n\n            *&*\n       Air symbols\n\n-Strong-\nCrouching Feather\nElf's Hair vine \nWisp's Breath\n\n-Moderate-\nSwamp blossom\n\n-Weak-\nJailer's Moss\n\n            *&*\n         Unknown\n\n-King's Ivy\n-Shade leaf\n-Biteit\n-Atheros (Possible Water symbol)\n-Gijaklul\n-Javens", ""),
        StaticBook("Uruk Culture", "§bPiercingDarkness", "Culture of the Orcs\n-----------------\nBook I, written by Ves\n\n\"May this book serve as a guide to any brave enough to venture into Orcish land. Or any scholar who may be curious of the hostile land to the far south.\"\n\nChapter 1:\nThe orcish homeland\n------------------\nAs most will know, the territory of orcs is the harsh sands of the desert. They have adapted to survive in such an unforgiving environment, so unless you are an orc born upon the sands, it is\n\nadvisable to be prepared before heading into the desert terrain, orcs are not the only threat there, thier land is just as harsh and unforgiving as they are. Many foolish adventurers have perished because of lack of preperation.\n\nThere are very few resources out there in the desert, so it is best to bring what you need to survive, water food and clothing to protect you from the effects of the strong desert sun. If however you are stranded without the supplies necassary\n\nthere are a few ways of obtaining them. Dehydration may be the most prominent killers in the desert, it is important to drink a lot and drink regularly, finding a stream is the most obvious source of water, however if you cannot find one,\n\nanother way of obtaining water is digging near vegitation such as the bushes or cacti that are found there, if you dig you will almost certainly find some water, but remember to never drink the sea water of surrounding oceans, that will only make\n\nthings worse. As for food, you may find small critters or bugs amongst the bushes or under rocks, so long as you cook them, most should be fine to eat, just to not eat the cacti as they are poisonous. Another very important thing is finding some shelter\n\nin the day, shelter will keep you cool and at night it will keep you warm, the days are hot and nights are cold so it is important to find a place to stay out of the harsh weather as it can have some pretty nasty effects if you are exposed for too long.\n\nbut is important to remember, that if you are in the desert, you are considered an intruder and will be treated as such, so do not step into orc land without expecting to be approached with a certain amount of hostility.\n\nChapter 2:\nOrc Clans\n------------------\nOrcs divide themselves into different groups called clans, the best way of explaining what a clan is, is that they are like families. That is why orcs will show such fierce loyalty to thier clan and will\n\nprotect thier clans with thier lives. Since the orcs left thier city there are too many clans to count, more and more sprout up constantly these new clans are often approached with hostility from the older and more respected clans such\n\nas Gorkil, Lur, Braduk and Ugluk. Each clan has thier own fort and land, which they develop and protect. Land is often the cause of war between clans, whether it be because one intrudes on another's land, or one clan wants the land owned by a\n\ndifferent clan. Orcs can either be born into a clan, or inducted by completing some kind of trial, which is different for each clan, often this is followed by some kind of ritual to welcome them to thier new family. Although the clans tend to stay\n\nout of each others business, they will often meet to discuss important matters and rally together in times of war against a common enemy, such as intruder in the desert or factions that oppose thier race. Each clan has a leader and various\n\nranks stemming down from there, orcs will earn thier rank by showing promise in battle or through loyalty, another less common way for an orc to gain a rank is for them to challenge another for thier possition, they will then fight for the rank.\n\nWhen on orc land, it is a smart idea to avoid setting foot in the city or on clan land, as for most clans this is a crime punnishable by death and sometimes something worse.\n\nChapter 3\nOrcish anatomy\n------------------\nWhen a orc is born and up until it is about eight to thirteen years old, it will look much like the child of any other race, of course larger and with a different coloured skin. It is when an orc\n\nreaches it's age of development that it takes the form that most people will recoginse. It is at this age of development that orcs take their adult form; generally described as the rapid growth of thick, ivory tusks, darkening and thickening of skin, and\n\nA greater tendancy to be thrown into Bloodlust. Along with these attributes, Orcs generally become more determined and 'Wise', compared to the cubs. Wise being a very widened term, with Orcs it can be used to tell of their inner sense of 'rightness'.\n\nBefore the age of thirteen is generally when most Orcs become whitewashes. The cubs are much more thick headed and rash compared to their older brothers (Though these are still much more easily angered than most other races).\n\nAfter this age, most Orcs tend to bond with their family and clan, and only tend to leave in much more serious circumstances, such as being banished. \nAn Orc's skin is generally thicker than most other races, Kha's included. The rough sands bite their\n\nHides and slowly but surely make them as tough as leather. Not unsurpisingly, Orcs hate colder climates. Perhaps it's their choice of clothing, or their tendancy to live in the hot badlands, but at any case, a shivering Orc is the only one you'll see in\n\nThe colder climates of the North and South, usually dressed in a somewhat amusing choice of thick, wooly, bundled clothing. Orcs come in a variety of colours, the most common being green, the rarest being black or even blue.\n\nChapter 4\nOrcish Customs\n-------------------As a race, the Orcs have certain customs that are shown by all clans. All Orcs hate Whitewashes. Save for those who are banished themselves, whitewashes are hated by all clans and all Orcs, and are hunted\n\nAs a sport by the race as a whole. Orcs are commonly superstitious, believing the spirits of their dead ascendants watch over to them this day, judging their honour watching their choices with approval, or disapproval, depending on the situation.\n\nThey see the Humans, Elves, Dwarves and Kha's as lesser races in general, though they have a certain mutual respect for the Dwaves' sturdyness. Various theories have arisen to propose why this is so, with the most generall accepted one being extracted\n\nFrom an Orcish fable, common to that of the Wandering Wizard. At the time of the four brothers, each had green skin. As the years of war against Iblees raged on, and the bad attributes of each race was shown, slowly the Elves, Humans and Dwarves' skin\n\nTurned pink; the colour of dishonour and taint, the same of that of the fungi which grow between their toes, often. Black, they see as trecherous and unstrustable, while colours such as purple is the colour of the spirits, and green the colour of life and\n\nPurity.\n\nChapter 5\nWhitewashes\n-------------------Whitewashes are somewhat uncommon in today's Orcish culture, though nonetheless hated by the race as a whole. A whitewash is not, as some believe, a nomadic Orc; one without a clan who roames at his free\n\nWill. A whitewash Orc, commonly known as Wiydwazh by the Uruks, is an Orc that has forsaken his or her own kind, broken their traditions and disregarded their god and beliefs, which generally revolve around Honor and Krug. A Whitewash Orc is hunted his or\n\nHer whole life (In most cases), by Orcs, and shooed away from any permanent home by any others due to the 'trouble' they bring, trouble being the Orc hunters intent on mounting the Whitewash's skull somewhere impressive.\n\nThey don't vary at all physically from other Orcs, though it is common for weaker Orcs to be banished from the Uzg, or their clan, due to losing an honor klomp, or something similar. In several cases, Whitewash Orcs can make their way back into the Orcish\n\nCommunity, usually by varying means, most involving klomps. Additionally, any Orc Shaman that becomes Whitewash loses their powers, since it is foremost fueled by the ancestors and spirits, which generally look down on Whitewashes.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shadows", "§bAislin Maar", "§l    §0§lThe Shadows,§0\n§0§l   They Grow Dark§0\n§0\n§0\n§0       Written By§0\n§0       Aislin Maar§0\n§0          1612§0\n§0\n§0      \"For my love,§0\n§0        Karyssmov.\"\n\nThe nights were so long and so dark, and how terribly alone I was. Yet, I was not alone. No one is ever truly alone. Trailed by our shadows all our lives, yet thinking nothing of them. How mistaken we were, to think it a simple thing, cast by the light of\n\nday and nothing more. I could feel them creeping in, drawing ever closer as the winds howled and whipped and clawed at the fragile panes. They were coming for me, those shadows in the night. The things that go bump and jump out and get you, how terribly\n\nreal they were. I could see them moving out in the white snows, the moonlight giving them away in the tiny hours of the morning. Between flurries and branches they shifted, their eyes staring at me, hungry. They craved me, and I them, for they were death\n\nand I was life. And it was the stars which grew brighter by the night, and the shadows which grew darker. As I slipped into the late night and the early mornings, the sun came later and the moon stayed longer. The ravens called to me and through the scope\n\nI saw the stars which circled my world and taunted me with their mystery. And I looked, and saw, the shadows staring back. The shapes and forms and beings in the night with eyes like stars piercing the veil of the night sky, seeking to pierce only me.\n\nDaemons in my mind, haunting me perhaps. The nightmares of my past and the emptiness of my soul filled me with the dread of the shadows. They hungered for me, and I for them, for they were death and I was life. It wasn’t enough, though, to hunger.\n\nThey needed to feast, and I was ripe with sorrow, with pain, with the hurt enough to feed them all. The death of the only love I knew, the years of life without it and the loss so soon after finding it filled me with the kind of sadness that killed.\n\nThe ghosts of my past ate at my mind, faces and names and places filling it with bloody memories. How had I ever thought I could handle such guilt, such sorrow? I had been a fool to seek the soul that now plagued me. I could not endure on like this\n\nforever, and I had no choice. And so I went to meet them, into the snow and the wind and the freezing cold which to any other would bite and claw and ravage flesh to blackened death. Onto me it did none but grasp and grope, begging for me as the shadows\n\ndid. Only they would feast, though, for I was ready to leave this world. Though it would not be so, no, it would not end tonight. This was only the beginning. The shadows had a soul, a life, a seed from which to grow within me. They took to me like moth\n\nto flame, and struck me through the heart with an arrow blacker than the night. Clawing, tearing, biting at flesh with shadowy teeth and talons. Like ravens to carrion, they took to my despair. They wrapped around my soul so tightly that I felt for the\n\nfirst time the feeling of suffocation. Drowning in their depths, I sank further than I ever thought I could go. For what felt like centuries this went on, falling endlessly through the black mooned night, surrounded only by the pinholed stars and my\n\ndaemons, my haunting friends. They cooed to me, soothed my aching lungs, filled them with their inky ichor. They drowned one who could not drown, clinging to my soul and fueling from it. Growing, manifesting.§0\n\nAnd when I woke, laid out in the snows of the nameless peaks, I was not alone. It was there, it was with me. It had always been there, unseen, forgotten, ignored. No longer, though, would it be so. No longer would it be content to cling to walls and the\n\nfloors. I rose, and so did it. I walked, and it strode as well. Manifest, it was there, beside me: my shadow. I turned a gaze to it, and it met mine in unison. White eyes piercing jet black, like the stars on a clear night. I looked into them and saw\n\nmyself; my shadow was me. It was my mind, and my soul, for it had not stolen it, but instead reflected it. I was she, and she was me. I reached out for her, and she held to me, embraced me, comforted me. The pit in my chest, the pain in my heart, it eased\n\n itself to solace for just a moment. In that embrace, I was warm among the snows and winds. The blackness did not fade, it enveloped. I embraced death and the shadow embraced life, for we were one in the same, joined forever.§0\n\nMy shadow never leaves me. She lurks, yes, but she waits. She hides until she is needed, and I tell no one of her. They would think me tainted, they would try to kill her. She cannot be killed though, for those who cast light only cause the shadow to\n\ngrow. She reaches where I cannot. She lends me her power, and I fuel hers. I give my life to her, and to me she gives the power of death.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Fox's Choice", "§bAislin Maar", "§0§nFox's Choice§0\n§0\n§0Written by§0\n§0Aislin Maar§0\n§0\n§0In the year 1612§0\n§0\n§0\"For my love, Karyssmov.\"\n\nOnce upon a time, in a forest far away, there lived a fox. This fox had many friends, and was brave and strong. He was cunning and clever and knew all the tricks to fend off the predators of the forest. Despite being a fox, he had many woodland friends.\n\nRabbits, squirrels, chipmunks, hedgehogs, and all manner of birds just to name a few. Fox was very popular, and he helped protect all his friends from the predators of the forest.  Fox had one friend in particular who he had known since he was just a\n\nsmall pup. Raven, a fierce black bird with a scowling expression. Raven was quieter than the other birds, and not nearly so colorful with her jet black feathers, but she was loyal and cared greatly for Fox, making sure he was safe and always giving him\n\nadvice. Fox knew lots of birds in the forest, and they all adored him for his bright red fur and clever wit. Fox liked the attention, too. He would spend time with all the birds, letting them fly about and show off their pretty feathers and sing their\n\npretty songs. Sometimes he spent more time with one or two birds than the others, and they started to think Fox wanted to spend all his time with them. Those birds would fly down, singing their greatest song to Fox, telling him how much they loved him.\n\nFox always turned them down though, because all Fox wanted was to be their friend. He didn’t understand why all the birds wanted to spend so much time with him. Raven, meanwhile, simply watched as Fox pranced and played and spent time with all the other\n\nanimals, and all the other pretty birds. She wasn’t terribly jealous, because Fox spent a lot of time with her too. She knew that the conversations that they had together were different from the ones Fox had with the other birds. They spoke about the\n\nforest around them, and the problems that plagued the creatures there. They spoke about their feelings, and Raven even confessed to Fox that she felt different than all the other birds and creatures with their bright colors and pretty songs.\n\nFox assured Raven that the other birds weren’t so great. They sang songs, sure, but that was about it. Raven remembered this, keeping their time together close to her heart while Fox was off playing with the other animals. §0\n\nOne day, a great Stag wandered into the forest. He was quite massive, with antlers towering so high into the air that they raked through the leaves of the trees. He was truly a formidable sight. Stag gazed about the forest, looking quite cross.\n\nHe had heard that Fox was living here peacefully among the other animals, the ones he should be hunting, and he was not happy. Stag thought this was not the way things should be, and he wanted to change it. So Stag came into a clearing where all the\n\nanimals were frolicking and having fun. Fox was there, with all the other animals and birds, and looking fearfully to the Stag. Stag was much, much bigger than Fox, and would easily be able to hurt Fox if he wanted. Stag stomped into the clearing\n\nangrily, and shouted that Fox needed to leave the forest forever. All of the animals around Fox began to cower in fear of the great Stag, afraid to get in the way for risk of being hurt themselves. One or two animals began to speak up though, telling Stag\n\nhe couldn’t make Fox leave. The Stag reared his legs in anger, stamping his hooves down into the dirt with a thunderous noise. All of the animals and birds scattered, terrified of the raging Stag! Fox was left alone, his eyes wide as he stared up at the\n\nangry Stag who drew nearer and nearer. The Stag told Fox that he would make him leave, and he would never come back. Stag reared up onto his hind legs, waving his front legs menacingly, ready to stomp down onto Fox! Suddenly, though, from the tree line\n\ncame Raven, swooping in and letting out a great loud caw. Raven flew at the Stag’s head, beating her wings as hard as she could in his face. She drew up her talons, striking at his nose, and Stag pulled himself away.\n\nStag turned, letting out a pained bleat as he shook his head, his nose stinging from Raven’s strike. Raven swooped at Stag again, flapping her black wings in his face, sending Stag turning and running off into the trees! Stag was not expecting that, and\n\nstarted sprinting off into the forest. Raven called after him, a loud caw telling him not to come back. As Stag ran away, Raven swooped back into the clearing, landing next to Fox. She hopped over to Fox, making sure he was okay.\n\n Fox stared at Raven, awestruck. Soon, though, he nuzzled up against Raven, wrapping his neck against her in a hug. Fox told Raven he was thankful she had not run off like the rest. Raven wrapped a wing around Fox’s back, hugging him.\n\nShe told him she would never run away when Fox was in trouble, as Fox had never run away when she was in trouble. Fox looked at Raven, and gave a nod. As all the forest animals and all the pretty birds began to creep back into the clearing,\n\nFox told Raven that he loved her. Stag never came back to that forest, and Fox and Raven lived happily together, protecting everyone from any threats that came to the forest after that.§0\n§0\n§0The End.", ""),
