        StaticBook("Child Crusade", "§bWalter Marshall", "The Tragedy Of The Childrens Crusade\n\nAn accurate account ofthe massacre at the Silver City gates.\n\nBy Walter Marshall\n\nUpon the frigid and barren peak of Mount Augustus, a small assemblage of noblemen, soldiers, and guardsmen sit in a circle. Their grimly-set visages dimly illuminated by the moonlight, the men mutter tersely amongst themselves.\n\n The first to rise and speak is the Prince Boris Carrion..\nBoris paces back and forth in thought, his downward gaze denoting pensiveness. At last he speaks, an alarming tone in his voice. “The crowned prince, my cousin Roy - where is he?\"\n\nSer Lothar Horen turns to Boris in response to his frantic query. “Our last report tells us he is encamped outside of Haelun’or, the Silver City. Your cousin has amassed an entourage of boy soldiers, and he has embarked on a children’s crusade.\n\nSer Baron Corbett VanCleef acts as his guard.” Boris stops in his steps, his eyes narrowing as he glances out towards the glimmering spires of the distant elven holding. “Corbett? A loyal man. But in times such as these, we do not know who we can trust.\n\nBring me my cousin Ser, bring me my nephew, and should the Baron attempt to stop you, put a dagger through his heart.” Boris then gives a quick glance to Dederick Varodyr, who stands expectantly as he leans on his greatsword. “And you, ser?\n\nTake my ward with you, it’s about time he met the son of Heinrik.” Ser Lothar gives a quick nod, striding away. Dederick scrambles suit, following after Horen in his brusque pace.\n\nFrom the edge of the forest, Dederick perches himself on the thick branch of an ancient tree, brushing the leaves to a side to peer down at the bustling camp below. His hawk-like gaze scours the large congregation of nomads,\n\nglancing down at the children as they dart in and out of the rows of tents. Many of the young boys and girls heft up swords much too big for themselves, as they move to converge on a single lad under the looming shadow of Haelun’or.\n\nA young boy within the camp, with a bejeweled crown upon his head, swings his oversized sword wildly as he roars loudly. “In the name of the King and holy Godan! Attack!” At the rallying call of their boy leader,\n\nthe droves of children rush towards the gates of the Silver City with unimposing cries, attempting to lift the gate to no avail.\nDederick, with a look of relief upon his face, clambers down from the tree, joining Lothar at the massive timber base.\n\n“It’s him! It’s the crown prince Roy!” With an air of mirth, Varodyr begins to jog towards the group of children, Ser Lothar following with an unimpressed grunt as they near the children’s militia.\n\nAs the mass of youths surround and swarm the steel gate, hanging from the bars and whooping indignantly, Roy Carrion turns to the distant thundering sound of hooves against the cobbled roads. Riding in hard from Vekaro,\n\nthe encroaching throng of horsemen heave up the crimson banners of the Decterum. Giving a boisterous chuckle at the sight of his father’s army, Roy lifts his sword with a triumphant cry as he bellows towards the gatehouse.\n\n“Your city is truly in peril now, elves, for Heinrik’s legion has arrived! Fear the men of the Decterum, for your days are suddenly numbered!” As the young prince continues to hurl imprecations at the unyielding gates of the elven city,\n\na new and alarming sound reaches his ears - the clash of swords accompanied by shrill cries of terror. As Roy shoulders his way past the mass of armored boys at the gates, his eyes widen in despair at the treacherous and cruel sight before him.\n\nThe soldiers of the Decterum advance on the children in the camp, cutting down the young crusaders mercilessly and callously setting fire to the tents as they go. The youthful and inexperienced boys stand no match for the hardened and pragmatic soldiers,\n\nand they carve a swath through Roy’s camp as they cleave their way towards the fearfully paralysed children at the gates.\n\nMeanwhile, the two sent to rescue the crown prince stand similarly frozen in shock at the appalling and insidious massacre. As they watch the sacking of the camp, and the men of the Decterum redden their blades with the blood of the youths,\n\na deep sense of dread ran over them. Had they failed their prince?\nThe remaining children, who stood at the gates, rapped frantically on the iron bars they were moments ago attempting to pull open. Corbett VanCleef, the steadfast servant of Roy,\n\nsparred with many members of the Decterum, but as they surged onwards and surrounded him, he was brought to his knees with a series of blows and shackled. Roy, spinning around confusedly amidst the massacre,\n\nwas hoisted from the ground by a passing uruk and evacuated before the men of the Decterum could kill him.\nMeanwhile, both Lothar and Dederick watch in disarray, at the events unfold before them. Dederick began to rush forth, unsheathing his sword,\n\nbut Lothar stopped him with gritted teeth - to run into the folly ahead was sure and certain suicide. As the men watched helplessly, the surviving rabble of child crusaders swatted fruitlessly at the gates, begging for mercy.\n\nBut no mercy did come that day, and at the hands of the Decterum the gates of the Silver City were awash in red.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 1", "Catarrh", "The Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHear what mi blah, young one, for mi blah lat h’dub honors by which the orc lives, agh h’dub pillars on which he stands.\n\nSTRENGTH\nVALOR\nBOLDNESS\nCONTENTMENT\n\nWISDOM\nFORTHRIGHTNESS\nDISCIPLINE\n\nStrength is the simplest honor. It is by nub means easy to attain, but very easy to lose. It comes with the weight of earth, yet drifts away on the currents of the river from the unwary. Yet, for he who keeps watch, it\n\nstands firm as iron. By it, the body stands strong. Without it, the bones fall as dry reeds. By the strong outer self, the strong inner self is protected.\n\nValor is that which compels us to stand. By it, we face our enemies agh conquer our fears. Turn nub\n\nfrom the challenges of life. Cower nub before latz foes. Stand agh face those who oppose lat.\n\nBoldness is that energy by which we charge into the flames. Be unafraid of risk. It is the gate to many rewards. As valor makes us stand our ground,\n\nboldness commands us to press forward.\n\nContentment is the key to satisfaction. Trust nub in wealth, for gold flees as the sands on the night winds. Trust nub in land, for many lands agh whole continents have been lost before this ash. Be content with\n\nlatz lusk agh latz bread. If you have a blarg, a mate, agh cubs, lat be truly blessed beyond measure.\n\nWisdom is born of a strong mind. It is more practical than philosophy, agh goes beyond mere knowledge. It is the ability for right living, common sense,\n\nwit, resolution of life’s problems, agh success beyond material gain. Gruk for latself, but heed the blahings of those more experienced with the respect agh consideration due them. Learn from life, agh apply latz learning in a way that means something.\n\nForthrightness is honesty agh directness. It is intentional clarity of blahing, agh the absence of deception. Blah truth. Blah to blah, nub to flatter. Do as lat blah, agh let latz blah be latz bond. If lat blah it, mean it. Live it\n\nDiscipline is that\n\nwhich keeps latz life in order. Without it, all other honors forsake lat, for honor demands that the honorable governs his life with the will of iron. Hard work agh control of the self hold body agh mind together.\n\nStand firm in all these things, agh lat\n\nwill stand indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Red Priest", "§bBrutus Norrington", "Protect us. O Lord of Light.\n\n\nFor the Night is Dark and Full of Terrors.", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis 4", "§bRalph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nFourth Edition\n\nIn this edition:\n\n*Ithelias Literature Award\n\n*Great Alrasian Purchase\n\n*Orc Attack in Karovia\n\n*New Orenian Anthem\nAnd more!\n\nIthelias Literature Award\nBooks of Oren, home of the Verbo Veritatis newspaper, is proud to announce the “Ithelias Literature Award” given to the most noted writers among Athera. The award is given to those that excel in the art of combining words to\n\nknit together an exceptional piece of literature, worthy of the honours of being recognized as a true masterpiece. A grand novel, a poem, every kind of literature is valid to be picked. The award will be given every Saint’s month and it will be funded\n\nby Books of Oren and his Highness, our emperor Tuvya Segismundovic Carrion to promote culture among our people. \n\nThe award will be a document stating the prize, and a sum of minas for the three best works of art.\n\nThe rewards are:\n\nFirst prize: 2000 minas\nSecond prize: 1000 minas\nThird prize: 500 minas\n\nTo join the competition send us a bird, with the book included, or just visit the store at Abbey Road 13a, Petrus.\n\nWinners will be announced in two Saint’s weeks!\n\nThe Great Alrasian Purchase\nWith the disappearance of the peoples of Alras in recent days, Emperor Tuvya made hasty moves to purchase the old lands of Alras from a local squatter. Recently annexed and renamed as the duchy of Karovia,\n\nPrince Aleksandr Carrion now sits as ruler of the new and burgeoning town, a proper homeland for the Raev in Oren being established.\n\nOrc Attack in Karovia\nIn Karovia, which recently joined the Empire of Oren after the Great Alrasian Purchase, orcs assaulted a defenseless young man. While this was happening Jacob Chapel walked in on them. He tried to hide, but was quickly\n\nfound by the savages, and captured and kicked to the ground. There were three, a large male orc, an apparently pregnant orc and a goblin. They went by the names of Malgroth, Shadback and Smelleh, respectively.\n\nAs they were busy extorting Jacob Chapel, the Emperor Himself arrived at the scene, covered in his Blessed Armor of St Augustus, wielding his Holy Axe of the Seven Skies. The male orc was quick to rush towards Tuvya, but his broadsword was no match\n\nfor the armour. After a short fight the Emperor’s sword was covered in orc blood. However, the goblin had just struck his pickaxe into the young lad’s chest, blood covering the ugly gobbo and the lush grass. The pregnant orc and the goblin quickly\n\nbolted off, Tuvya chasing after them, and killing at least one.\n\nThis was no help to the lad though, as he lay dying in the grass. He passed soon after Jacob Chapel took his confessions, and lies in an unnamed grave just outside Petrus. He died on the 3rd of the Deep Cold, 1474. May the Creator bless his soul.\n\nCaroline Hightower has composed the anthem of Oren\nThe new anthem of Oren, Thirty to One, has been composed by the great talent that is C. A. Hightower. Its great lyrics will surely inspire the peoples of the Empire and fill their hearts with pride.\n\nThe anthem is available for purchase at Books of Oren, Abbey Road 13a in Petrus. Contained within are the lyrics and instructions for the music.\n\nAmoss’ Crimes\nPart 1: Assault on the Uruguan Ambassador\nLegend tells of a white wizard, namely Amoss. Many say he is a psychopath, others call him a cannibal. I am here to confirm that both of these are true.\n\nTwas a cold and wet day. As I was heading to Petrus, a gentleman with a white beard approached me, asking me for help. I of course was obliged to help him find somewhere dry to stay. I offered my office and we began walking.\n\n As we were walking I was kicked to the ground and bound in chains. He gagged me and I was dragged to the Orc capital. I believe this was an attempt to ignite the conflict between Orcs and the other races. Luckily a man witnessed this event and alerted\n\nEraborn Greyhame. He gathered an army of Humans and Dwarves to come to my rescue. I was rescued, but my captor still lurks out there. I feel that he is a direct threat to Oren and to his Majesty Tuvya himself.\n\nUpon returning to Petrus with many wounds from the attempts of Amoss to eat me, I was in a dire position. Luckily I was helped by a very kind gentleman, Jacob Chapel, who along with the city doctor saved me from the brink of death.\n\nAmoss’ attempts to kill me were not at an end though. He corrupted my own Co-Ambassador with a large sum of money, and had him try to assassinate me. Several shots were fired at me, and he also attempted to stab me.\n\nLuckily the he was captured by the guard forces of Petrus and justice was served.\n\nA report by Ambassador Grigor of Clan Grandaxe\n\nPart 2: Treason in Oren\nAmoss’ crimes didn’t stop with the attempted assassination of Grigor Grandaxe, soon after the last events Faramith Greyhame released information about a conspiracy, of which Amoss, Eraborn Greyhame, and the rangers were part of\n\nTheir plan was to assassinate Yukov Carrion, beloved son of the Emperor, and after that try and seize Petrus. Their plan was foolish and the mad man named Amoss was captured quickly.\n\nWords from the High Pontiff\nGreetings to the progeny of Horen,\n\nI bid you lot fair weathers and fair harvest. I write to address the peoples in a distinguished press, the Verbo Veritatis, in hopes the Pontificate can expand its listening base to those\n\nmore secular. And many have been, thanks to the ill-efforts of my predecessors, who've distanced many from the Church's goals.\n\nYet I hope to act with clemency and charity, and insure that the Church serves the denizens in Oren, enlightening them of the\n\nfaith, administering their poor and sickly, writing its histories, ministering a breadth of education, and establishing the epicenter of Oren's culture, intellectualism, and spirituality.\n\nAt hand, the firstmost goal of our Church is to train and induct new members of the priesthood, and finish the translations of the scripture. The former has been going great, and the Church number swells to new heights not seen in decades, though many\n\nstill are recruits and hence ill-fit to wholly minsiter. We hope to teach these Acolytes and Deaconry every two to three saint's days. Secondly, is the Canon; the Church has been working intensively on drafting a Common adaptation of its Holiest book,\n\n the best of the Holy Scrolls, and the foundations of its Church, so that it may be spread to more of Oren's populace, who languish in uncertainty and apathy in regards to the Allfather and his worldly instruments. We have developed two identical\n\nmanuscripts of three of the seven books, a miracle in itself, yet we await a third to be sure that is His ordinance.\n\nUnfortunately, the feast day of St. Tobias had to have been cancelled due to a rogue guard locking the city off from the good parishioner\n\nduring the time of the ceremony. We hope to reschedule another feast day and fair soon enough, and we must apologize with this inconvenience. Whilst the Church has not made its presence wholly yet, this is due largely to an inexperienced budding\n\npriesthood and an undeveloped Canon. Once those are developed, we may engage in more active missions and more frequent rites and sermons.\n\nMay the Allfather protect!\n\nRoyal Marriage in Danger?\nThe proposed royal marriage between the Imperial Prince, Aleksandr Carrion, and the Waldian Princess, Lynn Rovin, may be in danger of breaking down! Harsh verbal arguments have broken out between Lynn and Aleksandr involving\n\nAleksandr’s twin brother Yakov. Yakov merely made a comment about the Waldian accent, which the princess took personal offense to. She then started yelling at Yakov and also took her anger out on poor Aleksandr, who made no such comment.\n\nLynn Rovin has also been heard slandering the Vanirs, calling them “Rude” and “Disrespectful”. The cruel woman also tried to deny little twelve year old Lorina Carrion her right to be the flower girl at the wedding, and instead tried to put a Waldian\n\ngirl, not even related to her, in the position instead. The Rovin has shown clear disrespect and disregard for the Prince, the Imperial Crown, and Oren itself. And yet Aleksandr Carrion has shown fantastic persistence in marrying her for the sake of\n\nuniting all of Humanity under one Empire. May the Creator have mercy on his life.\n\nA report by Jarrik Bloodstone", ""),
        StaticBook("Translocators", "§bArchmage Haadi", "~*~\n      On the creation\n    of translocators\n                  -\n\n\n\n              \\o/\n              -O-\n              /o\\\n\n[!] Along the page you see many strange markings and drawings. They look to be rough copies, at best. There appears to be some sort of archway built of stone, below it, several odd circular schematics, or perhaps a map. Next to the map, the phases of the\n\nmoon trail along.\n\n[OOC] View in browser:\n\n tinyurl.com/slatrop\n-------------------\n\nAn odd name, indeed. Though, the actual device is far more mysterious and eldritch in nature. Translocators, Lori Oathcast refers to them as. Crumena took to calling them closets, as per their birthplace, the closets within Rasmot's magical porta-potty.\n\nRegardless, the process for creating these translocators is a fairly complex ritualistic one that involves both a skilled Void Translocationist with knowledge of the subject, and a fairly powerful enchanter capable of binding the spell to the locations\n\nin question.\n---\n\nCreation\n\nAn enchanter holds the magic to the spot. One who knows how to send matter to the Void and bring it back again must have learnt to create what is like a 'gateway' into the Void. More than just the item itself, but anything that touches it. Even\n\nair. Then again you do it on the other end and the mage attempts to pull the block back through the Void and the enchanter binds that to a doorway or pillar or something. In short, one must reach into the Void and pull out an open space.\n\nMaintenance\n\nAfter time, it will need a mana supply or one end will fizzle out before the other and create an endless hole. It's advised then that you have the enchanter available fairly often to refill whatever large mana gem or crystal you wish to power\n\nthe translocators' magic with. As far as i'm aware, this would be the only option, unless one would be able to get ahold of Kalameet's notes on the mana obelisk. For the ignorant, this is large pillar in which sums of mana are stored for use. The mana\n\ncannot be pulled out by any means by a magi to fuel their own spellcasting, but instead it exerts energy needed to power enchantments in the area. I'd elaborate further, though i'm only going off of what i've seen myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Skyfall Anthem", "§bBell Sano", "The\n      Skyfall Rebel\n          Anthem\n-------------------\n\nWritten by Bell Sano\n\n14th of the Amber Cold, 1532, less than a year before the Skyfall Rebellion\n\n((To the tune of \"I'm a Good ol' Rebel.\"))\n\nOh, I'm a smart ol' scholar, now that's just what I am, and for the Aulic Council, I do not give a dam'n. I was proud to be a Blackcoat, I only wish we won, we won't forgive Godfrey for anything he's done.\n\nI hates the Vandorian nation, and everything they do.\nI hates the Lexicon of Nafis, and the Frederick Code, too.\nI hates the Royal Marshal, his sword dripping with our blood.\n\nI hates the winged banner, n' trashed it all I could.\n\nI rebelled with L. A. Dreathen, for six weeks, that's for sure. Was wounded by an eyepatch during the Skyfall Massacre.\n\nWe were safe inside our walls, and knee deep in the snow, but the Redcoats fought the Vanders, and that sure goes to show.\n\nBut back in '34, they left us in the dust. We retreated to Courland, before they conquered us. They died of mountain frostbite, but not our golden cross, I wish we had gotten freedom, instead of Sarrion's loss.\n\nWe can't raise our iron, n' chop 'em down no more. But none of us gonna love 'em, now that's for certain, sure. Yet stand up tall and strong, sir, be proud of who you are, now only a pile of rubbish, leaving the land a scar.\n\nI'm a smart ol' scholar, that's just what I am. And for the Aulic Council, I do not give a dam'n. I was proud to be a Blackcoat, I only wish we won, we won't forgive Godfrey for anything we've done.", ""),
        StaticBook("Short Story 1", "§bRegenald", "\"The Wizard Who Stole My Name\" By Regenald\nThe Highlander\n\nI knew a wizard, a strong one at that, truly a man of magic.\nThe magic he would focus on was mental magic I would find out years later.\nI started by telling him stories at a fire he had made.\n\nThere was Ale' and food that filled me quickly, I loved it all truly I did, so I decided to tell him a story of my first battle, and all of it's funny attributes.\nHe laughed and groaned, he clenched his heart and choked up food. He absolutely loved it!\n\nBut I was the fool, telling a fools tale, thinking that I was the high and mighty one that night, oh I was wrong, yes I was.\nHe took my name and my memories, saying he didn't want my tales to be told to anyone else. He said if someone guesses my name -\n\nThen I would have my memories back, who am I, I pondered to myself, and what is this wizard speaking of?\nI knew he was telling the truth, so I went off to tell the tale of the time I lost my name, asking, no begging, for people to guess just 1 name.\n\nI went to Felson where I spent most of my days at a bar, telling my story, and drinking my days away. \nBut one day I met a man by the name of Jester, a great man indeed.\nI told him my story and asked one thing\n\"Who am I?\"\nand he replied\n\nRegenald, and I be the wizard that you seeked!\nImpossible I thought he looks nothing like him, could this truly be the man?\n\n....\nI knew this story, yes I did, for it wasn't about me but it was a childrens tale\n\nThe man in the story was named Regenald, it was read to me when I was a small child.\nHe remembered the book for his parents read it to him, that damned wizard gave me a story of children.\n\n\n    Next page for\n         Information\n\nHello, I am the author of this small story or book, what ever you want to call it, I am Regenald, a highlander,  it was completely made up but I quite enjoyed it, I've really gone from Bar to Bar telling people this story but instead acting like it was -\n\nreal and it really draws people into it\n\n\nThank you so much for taking the time and reading my short story, even if it was complete shit,\nIf you see me around buy me a drink!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Age of Time", "§bLocke Lamora", "As we delve into the depths of our mind realize we to are a facet of the earth which surrounds us. We are but one little slice of a larger whole, appreciation is not often granted to the lands which provide us sustinance, and joyous harvests. From the\n\nHalflings to the mighty Uruks we are all but apart of a greater thing. Though we may see wars tear us apart, and love bring us together this life is not one we must choose to walk alone. A wise man may ask a younger man to carry on his task for he has\n\ngrown to old, and must pass the torch; such is the rythme of life it flows, and goes on just as the mighty Ice caps of the Dwarven lands melt giving way to the heaving flow of the rushing rivers pulling down the banks of sediment, and tumbling trees as\n\nthough they were sticks. Do not forget that blood is thicker than water both may flow, and both may coat the hands of a man; but a man with blood upon his hands is a murderer and a man with water upon his hands is but a ghost among the thousands of others\n\n. My words are dauntingly flitted with age, and I misconstrue the times with my own ideals and thoughts; to be presumptious I'm but a speculator of the past, present, and future. This day you are a boy innocence praises you for you are the envy of its\n\njuvenile prosperity, the next day you're a man wielding the blade of a warrior your body marked with the scars of one who has given, and taken what life gives to those who try to sieze it with steel opposed to the words of a politic; such still hold the\n\npower of daggers with precise proper meanings spewn about courts to determine the fate of the gods kin. Tread lightly upon the paths that lead to power; serpents stalk the grass, and false turns are but a harmony compared to what awaits your journey into\n\nthe den of the lion. Lift me up, and praise me men say for their deeds reflect honor, and vitality; do you not see the death of another man as but a morose crime, but you've no empathy for a man whos claims rival your own he is but a body among the\n\nhundreds you will slay to achieve your darkest desires. Let dread fill your days for all men rot, and one day to you will taunted by the shouts, and screams of blithering souls aghast at your crimes; victims to your genocide. Your fingers scrape the edge\n\nof a blade, a thorn pricks your finger a drop of blood to appease the gravens of death. Is it that man fears death, or the thought of not being remembered as a man noble enough to be written upon pages of parchment, and stuffed high away within the\n\nshelves of a vaulted study or library their tales told once a day, week, year, or even decade so long as it is spoken their memory lives on in those pages. Is this what men strive for? Is life the leaves of a tree waneing and woeing to the seasons bidding\n\ntill one day they dry up basking within the sun that granted them what others may call eternal life just to be swept away in the lonesome breeze collapsing into dust to be spread once more amongst the soil so life could spring its fingers of life just one\n\nmore time from your decayed remains. Truth lies not in words, but in the actions of these words it is the doing not the saying that is valued. We forget the luxuries of a simple yes or no; when I'm to not know your yes from your no then I'm but a stranger\n\nlooking into your fantasy that seems to slowly flip pages, each new page describing what has graced your greedy hands filling your desires, and sating your thirst for vengeance; and bloodlust against your foes. Life is a circle in which we all must live.\n\nA younger me would know these words to hold no meaning, an older me sees them as a golden relic to be treasured and safe kept for all to read; and glance but a piece of what lay within the expanse of centuries walking the lands of this world. So be it I\n\ndream of the skies, and drifting away. Dreams fuel us they are the embodiment of our hope, they are our ambition and the force that compels us to do the things we do for others. Dark times come, and go but do not stand, and proclaim you are afraid to bare\n\nwitness when you've brought such a darkness down from the heavens, and now the clouds are glinted with the tinge of power for which you asked for soon it will course through your blood; and turn your soul sour and corrupt its tendrils soaking up your\n\nessence and tainting you to the core of your being. \n\n\nThe Philosophies of:\nLocke Lamora", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\n\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\n\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\n\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\n\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\n\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowess\n\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\n\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\n\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\n\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\n\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\n\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity of\n\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\n\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\n\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\n\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\n\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\n\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\n\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\n\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\n\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvation\n\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\n\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\n\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\n\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\n\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for in\n\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\n\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\n\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\n\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\n\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\n\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\n\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\n\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\n\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the grace of love\n\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\n\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\n\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\n\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\n\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\n\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers.\n\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\n\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\n\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repugnant\n\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Weapons of war", "§bWalter Marshall", "Weapons Of Modern War\n\n By Walter Marshall\n\nVolume I, Weapons of the Golden Crow\n\n23rd of The First Seed\n\nKaedreni Longsword\n\nThe Kaedreni longsword is a staple weapon of all Highlander forces. Able to be wielded with a single arm and carry a shield alongside it. This razor sharp blade is a formidable weapon when used by a professional.\n\n\nHaensetic Arming Sword \n\nThe Haensetic Arming Sword is the primary weapon of the Brotherhood, It is given to fresh Man-at-arms upon acceptance, Although many prefer to use the Kaedreni Longsword when they-\n\nachieve a higher rank and gain access to more weapons, no man in the Brotherhood forgets their Haensetic Arming sword.\n\nScylfing Hand Axe\n\nThe Scylfing Hand Axe is deadly close range weapon popularized and produced in bulk by the Colborn family for use by Haensic soldiers when facing heavily armored foes hand to hand.\n\nTheir expert make and craftsmanship led to the victory of many Haensetic battles. A true staple of the Brotherhood and Colborn artisanry.\n\nStrannik Lance\n\nThe Strannik Lance is a formidable halberd that was adapted from the heavy Ruskan cavalry known as the Stranniks. Now used as a pike in order to fend off cavalry charges,\n\n it is a staple of the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow when fighting those who may be on horseback.\n\nAdunian Claymore\n\nThe Adunian Claymore is a giant sword capable of destroying any foe. Used without a shield, the Claymore is wielded with two hands. If it does not cut through armour, the sheer trauma of being hit by it is enough to stagger a man.\n\nWaldenian Warhammer\n\nThe Waldenian Warhammer is a fairly bulky weapon of significant weight reserved for the slaying of undead or heavily armored opponents. With a blunt face on one half of the head and a piercing crow’s beak on the other.\n\nThe hammer is crafted of the finest northern steel providing a good strong weapon with lots of power and weight behind its swing.\n\nKaedreni Arablest\n\nThe Kaedereni Arablest is a common weapon found during sieges and other large skirmishes, its long range and tough oak stock make it not only durable but deadly.\n\nHowever its increased reloading time and overall bulkiness prevents most soldiers from carrying one when not expecting large conflicts.\n\nBarbovic Lever Crossbow\n\nThe Barbovic Lever Crossbow was made famous during its tenure in the Gold Corps when protecting Felsen from Dreadlanic raids. Carried often by the defenders. The Barbovic Lever Crossbow was a medium power quick reload crossbow.\n\nThe men who wielded it praised its ability to fire shots in quick succession while being easy to maneuver within the tight streets and alleys. Mostly used by men on patrol or in urban environments.\n\nBarbovic Shield\n\nWhile many of the  new recruits are given whatever shields are present, that is not the case for the more experienced men of the order. There is a delicate balance between the weight of the shield, and the protection it offers.\n\nThese shields have been forged with that balance in mind, crafted in a curved rectangular fashion. The size offers a fair amount of  mobility to the user, while the curved design is effective at deflecting many different kinds of arrows and projectiles.", ""),
        StaticBook("Feudal Rights v2", "§bChristopher d'Ibelin", "A SUGGESTION OF A FEUDAL LAW\n_____________________________By Francois d'Ibelin. \n\nSecond Edition and transcription by Christopher d'Ibelin. \n\nA document wherein a suggestive replacement for the Feudal Law of Oren is contained.\n\nIntroduction\n-----------------------------Greetings, fair men of the new Empire. The Feudal Law was a document detailing clergymen, burgher, peasants, yeomen and nobles, and the roles thereof. This was accepted by the good King Olivier, yet it is doubted\n\nthat a similar document is required for the Holy Orenian Empire of his Imperial Majesty, John I. I find this most distressing. The Feudal Law was itself an expression of traditional privaleges.\n\n-Ser Francois d'Ibelin\n\nI.Definitions\n\nI.A feudal vassal (otherwise known as a secular vassal) is a secular nobleman who owns a landed title within the Empire, be they directly or indirectly loyal to the crown. With these category, there are two further subcategories:\n\nOne:Minor nobles are those nobles who are lower than the rank of count.\n\nTwo:Senior nobles are those who are counts or higher.\n\nII.A senior clergyman (otherwise known as a Canon vassal),\n\nis one who holds an ecclesiastical, or non-secular title, titular or otherwise, that is a bishopric or higher.\n\nIII.Those who are under this rank are categorised as lesser clergy.\n\nIV. Landed gentry are those who hold a knighthood and an estate but hold no other titles. For example, a duke who is also a knightly estate-owner is considered part of the senior noble class, not the landed gentry.\n\nV.Those commoners who are not bound to any land, own no property and lack any sort of allegiance are called free subjects, these being the majority of our empire. \n\nVI.Those skilled commoners who work in the arts and crafts\n\nor any trade for a liege are known as craftsmen. \n\nVII.Those commoners bound to the land of a secular or canon vassal in agricultural labour are called serfs or villens.\n\nVIII.Those who hold council titles in a county, ducal, princely\n\nor imperial council are known as unlanded nobles.\n\nIX.Those who hold such titles as “Lord Mayor” and are given governance of a city are known as burgher titles.\n\nII.Vassalage and Obligations.\n\nI.The vassals are obligated to support their liege during a war. If the Emperor calls the realm to war, then he may be sure that the vassals give their full military strength in support of his cause; if they do not,\n\nthe Emperor is at will to revoke their titles or imprison them.\n\nII.The Emperor is obligated to maintain the feudal privileges of the vassals; if he rules with tyranny, and attempts to revoke feudal laws such as this,\n\nvassals are under no obligation to follow him. \n\nIII.Each man of the landed gentry, unlanded nobles and secular vassals is required to keep a destrier or a courser, riding horses; his own arms and armour of the highest quality.\n\nIV.It is the feudal duty of the commoner to be armed with the most basic of weapons.\n\nV.Burgher vassals are free from the obligation to fight or provide levies, as they provide extra financial contributions to the realm.\n\nVI.The clergy likewise are under no such obligation.\n\nVII.It is thus requested burgher taxes can be up to double those of the feudal vassals, however, they are under no obligation to go to war with their liege.\n\nVIII.The Emperor is obligated to defend his vassals and come to their aid when they are attacked. \n\nIII.In Respect of the Lexicon of Ashford and the Ducal Law.\n\n[note-henceforth the Lexicon of Ashford has been superseded\n\nwith a new law, yet the principle remains the same - Christopher.]\n\nI.It is said no Emperor will revoke the privalege of the dukes to create their own ducal laws, no Emperor shall ever revoke this privalege, this privalege will not be revoked!\n\nII.The Lexicon of Ashford takes place only in those duchies without a Ducal Law, or that are in possession of the Emperor.\n\nIII.Counties, baronies and so forth may not make their own laws.\n\nIV.In Respect of the Rights and Responsabilites of the Commoners.\n\nI.It is said that the commoners of any rank are only to be judged by either the Law of Ashford or their respective Ducal Law, by no other law they may be tried, and\n\nonly when proven guilty may they be persecuted. \n\nII.Further, the serfs can be expected to marry at the behest of their liege. This is because their children will be serfs as well.\n\nIII.No noble may displace a law-abiding citizen unless he has been inactive for one Saint’s week.\n\nIV.He shall not be permitted to visit a man’s court without the approval of his liege.\n\nV.Any man born of a free family shall not be taken as property of any foreign or local power.\n\nVI.Each peasant, whether serf, yeoman, or otherwise, has the right to own weaponry. [and, furthermore - a responsability if an adult male]\n\nV.In Respect of the Incarceration of the Nobles and Clergy.\n\nI.The clergy are only to be imprisoned by their liege only with the approval of the High Pontiff.\n\nII.The Emperor may only\n\nrevoke a man’s titles or imprison him on one or more of the following conditions: He has a legitimate claim on one of their titles, he has committed treasonous acts with ample evidence to support such a case, he has committed a crime\n\nof the first or second degree.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Valiant Soldie", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n\n\n    The Valiant Soldier\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Reich Ministry of\n    Enlightenment and\n    Truth\n\nYoung Billy played in his garden the day they came. A soaring Eagle upon their tabards, these were the Kaisereichs finest. \n\nHe watched them parade into the Caliphate, and watched a throng of curious people begin to cheer them into the city, eager to see\n\nthe fighting men and women of the Kaisereich. The clapping continued for hours as the troops poured in, banners held high, it was if it was a public show of solidarity with the common man. \n\nYoung runners ran beside the parade, handing out small\n\nflyers to those who would take them. The flyers listed places men and women alike could sign up for the Imperial Army, the fighting force of the Kaisereich. One such places was the Recruitment office in the Caliphate, near the main gate.\n\nAlongside the runners and the parade, men on horseback and wearing a thick leather coat and a snazzy black cap were the Ministry of Truth Officers. They were helping to distribute flyers to the runners. They handled the media, arts and news within the\n\nKaisereich. \n\nAnd last but not least, came the officers of the Kaisereichs Imperial Army. The mighty officers, and the Champion of Hallowvale, a Caliphate local! The black children in the crowd roared as they saw him. They shouted \"Praise the Champion!\"\n\nOne of the officers at the end of the parade brought forth a large rolling float - and people saw a portrait of the Kaiser. As the float came closer and closer, a figure emerged through the portrait - it was only the Kaiser himself! The crowd roared with\n\npraise and love, the parading soliders could barely contain the crowd for their show of unabashed dedication to the Kaiser. He waved to the crowd, and made a stirring speech about re-vitalization of the core aspects of the Caliphate, and how we as a\n\npeoples were going to make the Caliphate better for all. \n\n\n            PRAISE\n              THE\n            KAISER", ""),
        StaticBook("The Caterpillar", "§bAnnette", "The Hungry\n       Caterpillar\n          =-+-=\n\n            By\n    Annette Elendil\n\n\n \\_/-.--.--.--.--.--.   (๑′ᴗ‵๑)_)_)_)_)_)_)_)o\n\n\nIn the light of the moon, a little egg lay on a leaf...\n\nUntil one sunny morning, the leaf grew warm and.. \n\nPOP!\n\nOut of the egg came a tiny, and hungry, caterpillar..\n\nHe started to look for some food..\n\nOn the first day, he ate through one red apple...\n\nBut.. He was still hungry..\n\nOn the second day, the little caterpillar ate through two juicy green pears..\n\nBut..\n\nThe little Caterpillar was still hungry...\n\n\n...(,(,(, \")\n\nOn the third day..\n\nHe ate through three pretty purple plums.\n\nBut.. the little caterpillar was still so very hungry...\n\n\n...(,(,(,(, \")\n\nThen, on the fourth day.. The little caterpillar ate up four yummy red strawberries!\n\nBut.. he was still hungry...\n\n\n\n...(,(,(,(,(, \")\n\nOn the fifth day, he found a snack of five bright oranges.\n\nBut..\n\nThe poor little caterpillar was still hungry...\n\n...(,(,(,(,(,(, \")\n\nOn the sixth day.. the little caterpillar had a feast!\n\nHe at through one ice cream cone, one pickle, one slice of cheese, one slice of salami, one lolipop, one slice of pie, one cupcake, and one big slice of watermelon!\n\nThat night..\n\nThe little caterpillar had a terrible ache in his little buggy belly..\n\n\n\n\n...(,(,(,(,(,( ;~;)\n\nThen.. on the seventh day..\n\nThe caterpillar ate through one nice, green leaf.\n\n\n....(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,( -u-)\n\nAfter that he felt much, much better!\n\nBut now, he wasnt hungry anymore..\n\nAnd he wasn't a LITTLE caterpillar anymore..\n\n\n\n    ......(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(\n\n\nHe was a big, fuzzy, FAT caterpillar!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(,(,(,(,(,(, \")!\n\n\nHe build a special small house around himself, called a cocoon.\n\nHe stayed in his little house for more than two whole weeks!\n\nThen.. \n\nOne morning..\n\n\nHe nibbled a hole in his cocoon.\n\nAnd pushed, pushed, PUSHED his way out!\n\nAnd...\n\n He had become a beautiful, colorful butterfly!\n\n\n       __ \\/ __\n      /o \\{}/ o\\\n      \\    ()    /\n       `>  / \\  <'\n       (o/\\/\\o)\n\n          The\n          End", ""),
        StaticBook("Thanhium", "§bOrithur", "-- == Thanhium == --\n\nWhat is Thanhium?\n\nThanhium in its most natural form is an ore burried beneath the earth, bearing a similarity to the commonly decorative ore known commonly as 'Lapis'. However, the traits of Thanhium\n\nare quite different, and easy to spot. For once, Thanhium is often located in incredibly large veins of ore close to the surface, and are consistently found in areas covered in both snow and frost, but as I will explain later, this is no coincidence.\n\nThanhium in its ore form is significantly more brittle than Lapis, but it is most noticible by its freezing aura. Thanhium is incredibly cold to the touch, and when in a large amount, like a vein of ore, it is capable of changing the very nature of the\n\nbiome it resides in to one of a deep cold, ridden with frost and snow. One example of this would be the Frozen North of Anthos, that was only frozen due to the masses of Thanhium ore burried beneath its surface.\n\nIs it dangerous?\n\nThanhium is one of the most destructive, and toxic substances known to our world, particularly when ingested. Thanhium is quite poisonous to all mortal men, however its affects vary between mages and non-mages.\n\nWhile it is known to have the victim struck with intense headaches, in mages it interferes with their personal supply of manner, and from here the effects may vary. Some mages report having a massive rush of uncontrollable mana, others, more commonly,\n\nclaim that the Thanhium negates their magical power entirely. Non-mages would find themselves arush with a newfound power they can't possibly hope to understand. They would become quite surged and overwhelmed with mana, likely rendering them uncouncious,\n\nor even killing them outright. Death is possible with both mages and non-mages alike, and it has been recorded that close proximity to Thanhium for an extended period of time, causes severe cases of madness.\n\nWhat do I do with it?\n\nThanhium must be processed and purified for its usefulness to be extracted. A variety of methods exist and many scholars of Thanhium's nature will give you a different example on how to bring the ore\n\nto its purest form, creating that of a 'shard' or 'crystal. It is important to note that the Thanhium does not generate cold, it instead draws in heat and leaves cold in its wake, transforming this heat into mana. It is for this reason that Thanhium in\n\nits purest form is commonly used to empower enchantments, and keep them sustained. Enchantments can tap into their supply of mana and feed off it indefinately while it continues to drain heat from the air to fuel itself. The ore\n\nas a rule is more useful when in purified form, and from here it has a variety of uses, ranging from a powerful explosive, to a deadly poison, to a useful attachment to an enchantment, allowing for enchantments to be sustained with mana, and a great deal\n\nmore. I have personally found ways to forge unique armours fashioned from Thanhic alloys, and have studied into the effects of harnessing the power of Thanhium to change the very weather.\n\nWhat more is there to Thanhium?\n\nThe short answer, is that we do not know. Constantly new discoveries are made surrounding Thanhium and its many properties. The study of Thanhium is a particularly rewarding field to any\n\naspiring scholar. Its potential is almost limitless, but it is to be noted that while great things may be achieved through Thanhium, it is in its nature a destructive element. While it is capable of achieving great good, it is admittedly easier to achieve\n\ngreat evil. Responsibility is a necessity when handling Thanhium, for in its study I know from experience that its dangers become quite apparent, its potential as a weapon is often stumbled upon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Crow", "§bWalter Marshall", "History Of The Brotherhood\n\nA comprehensive history of The Brotherhood Of The Golden Crow.\n\nBy \nWalter Marshall\n\n\nNear the close of the infamous Third Human-Dwarf War, the Urguani quickly crumbled, with numerous dwarven holdings falling to the hands of King Andrew of Oren. Most important of these newly conquered fiefs was the Hold of Hiebenhall,\n\nthe last Dwarven Hold in both Northern Athera and on the River Picataris, decimating the Grand Kingdom of Urguan’s vital supply line of timber and coal to the war effort. The victorious capitulation was lead by the one named Karl Aleksandrovic Tuvic,\n\n leading Oren-aligned levies of the County of Ayr and was joined by his Vladovic kinsman of Woldzmir.\n\necause of his role in its capture, Karl Aleksandrovic was aptly named Count of Siegrad by the King of Oren, beginning to slow process in subjugating the neighboring tribes which enjoyed extensive autonomy under both the Urguani yoke and the past Kingdom\n\n With his new office, Karl Aleksandrovic took new arms under the urging of his fellow peers and guardians, upholding the newly christened House Barbanov,\n\n named for one of the numerous Raev Princes of yore, and wielding the standard of the gold crow upon a black field, in honor of his grandfather.\n\nWhat came with his appointment was Count Karl’s creation of a primed levy force, attempting to reorganize the previous wild militia from the ruins of Waldenia and be akin to those like the noble houses of mainland Oren.\n\nIt equated into the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow, which became Count Karl’s personal retinue and staging force, joining him in the ending days of the Third Human-Dwarf War, his elevation to Duke after the death of his uncle in 1505,\n\n and his later death by the hand of the Adunian Flesh Worm Mordangai (ironically the spawn of the previous Adunian Flesh Worm Wundergar which was slain by his uncle nearly two decades before).\n\nHis son, Siguine Karovic, inherited with his demise, the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow swearing their loyalty and resuming their original post. With Duke Siguine’s unmatured age,\n\n Count Tarcell of Valles took charge as regent and wardfather for the young ducal figure, becoming de facto ruler of Haense and sole leader of the Golden Crow. Compared to Duke Karl’s constant involvement and participation in Oren’s affairs,\n\nCount Tarcell of Valles took an isolationist approach, and the Duchy of Haense and the Golden Crow remained mostly within their borders.\n\nDespite the rising tensions and conflicts between Duke Hughes of Adria and King Olivier of Oren,\n\n it came to great surprise when Count Tarcell of Valles led the Haensic levy in pillaging Dour Watch under the guise of peace, nearly killing the brothers Clement and Augustus de Sola. The Duchy of Haense informally begins to help the Adrian dissenters,\n\nand begins a full coalition against the King of Oren in 1518, for which Count Tarcell of Valles formally signed in Duke Siguine of Haense’s name.\n\nIn the spring of 1518, the Coalition forces of the Duchy of Adria, Vanaheim, and Haense scored numerous victories over the Royalist forces, with Duke Hughes of Adria marching the Adrian footman deep into the Druscan Marshes,\n\n with Count Tarcell of Valles flanking north and the Vanaheimic forces under command of Lord Britannus Vanir marching deep into the crownlands. However, the offensive began to crumble.\n\nNumerous northern lords under the Vanirs of Vanaheim launched a revolt, angered in the Vanir’s choice in supporting Duke Hughes of Adria against the King of Oren, but more importantly was the early death of Count Tarcell of Valles.\n\n The assaulting Haensic forces were intercepted by the Kaedreni loyalists of Grand Duke Cantonus, where despite the Golden Crow’s ability to beat back the ambush, Count Tarcell was captured. He was tried for treason and found guilty,\n\nbeing executed in Castle Praha in the autumn of 1518.\n\nDuke Hughes of Adria retreats back to his namesake duchy, where the Golden Crow under the young command of Duke Siguine of Haense, now of majority age, meet with him.\n\n However, before the next assault can occur, Duke Hughes is assassinated and the coalition enters into turmoil. The Golden Crow voice their loyal and loud voice to Duke Siguine,\n\nfor which he wins the election amongst the lords to become the newly titled Lord Paramount. In the spring of 1520, Duke Siguine leads the forces into the Druscan Marshes once more.\n\nHowever, with Duke Siguine’s inexperience at such a young age, the lack of guardianship with Count Tarcell’s execution, paired with the late frost which decimated Adrian crops and the land blockade on the Duchy of Vanaheim,\n\nthe Coalition is defeated at the Battle of the Blackwald in late 1520, forcing the combined forces to retreat into the fortress of Barrowyk.\n\nDuke Siguine, with the remaining forces within northern Adria, sends a token force of Golden Crow, led by the priest Enoch of Haense and Ser Sarus Mallister, to defend Haense from incursion. The pair successfully raid Royalist supply lines,\n\nhowever does not stop the Royalist capture of Barrowyk in 1521 and the later Sack of Brelus, which led to the fall of both the Duchy of Adria and Vanaheim.\n\n The remaining force of Golden Crow, however, did not surrender and it would take until 1524 that Haense falls to the force of Jan Kovachev in the name of King Guy II of Oren. The Golden Crow is officially disbanded,\n\n and many flee with other Adrian rebels from capture.\n\nBut, after the succession crisis that occurred with Duke Stefan of Carnatia and later Duke Jan of Carnatia, the House of Barbanov once again finds itself in a ducal coronet,\n\n inheriting the title as Duke of Carnatia which is formally renamed to the previous title of Haense. Duke Petyr takes the leading role, the posthumous son of Duke Siguine of Haense to Kamilla of Woldzmir,\n\nwhere he officially refounds the Golden Crow to once again stand as the protectors of the Barbanov line.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 2", "Catarrh", "The second book of the Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka, agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHeed mi warning, all who are wise, for mi blah lat h’dub dishonors by which an orc is ruined, agh h’dub shames which may befall him.\n\nWEAKNESS\nIRRESOLUTION\n\nCOWARDICE\nAVARICE\nTHOUGHTLESSNESS\nDUPLICITY\nCOMPLACENCY\n\nWeakness, blah’d plainly, is the absence of strength. Be nub frail, agh neglect nub the body. He who can-nub defend himself, how can he defend that for which he stands? To give place to weakness is\n\nto keep latz bub’hoshest treasure in a fortress of straw.\n\nIrresolution is the way of he who falters in the presence of adversity. Do nub quail when the storm thunders. Do nub turn away when latz enemies roar. Be nub like the rabbit, who, when he is\n\nfrightened but a little, flees to his hole for safety. The rabbit is prey, agh the orc must never be prey.\n\nCowardice halts the feet, agh binds the spirit. Nub hosh thing comes to the coward, for the coward takes nub risk. The coward never takes the\n\ndifficult path. There is no success for such an ash. All his ways are worthless, agh his life profitless.\n\nAvarice is the heart of the empty spirit. Lust for gold blinds the eyes to truth, agh numbs the mind to wisdom. It makes the senses dull, such that\n\nhe whose life is governed by the mina can-nub perceive honor, agh hears nub the call of Krug.\n\nThoughtlessness is to the mind as weakness is to the body. The ash who gruks nub is nub’hosher than the blind or the deaf, for he chooses himself nub to gruk\n\nthe way to live rightly. He is blind to the way in which he should walk, agh the advice of the wise enters nub his ear. All his workings are senseless, agh his feet lead him to shame.\n\nDuplicity is the forked tongue of the dishonorable. The duplicitous\n\nash blahs “yub” with his mouth, but “nub” in his spirit. His blah can-nub be trusted, for he is a serpent agh a companion to serpents. With his face he grins agh flatters, but behind his back he bears a double-edged dagger to betray lat. Do nub be like\n\nsuch an ash, for the number of those who will hear him dwindles by the hour.\n\nComplacency is the quicksand upon which the glob builds a blarg. It is a hosh-smelling poison, agh a smooth road which leads to ruin. Complacency lulls lat to sleep with a soft\n\ntouch agh sweet songs, but, when lat have awoken, it has stolen latz strength, latz mate, agh all latz bread.\n\nThe ash who falls into any of these falls surely agh quickly to his destruction.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lucienism", "§bBaudric von Aesterwald", "===================The Essential Handbook for the Followers of Saint Lucien de Savoie\n-\nDictating the Reformed and Reaffirmed Doctrine of Saint Lucien\n-\nRecorded by Pious Ser Baudric von Aesterwald\n==================\n\nLucienism -\n\nLucienism is the traditionalist-oriented branch of the Orenic faith that identifies with the theological teachings and theory of Saint Lucien of Savoie, or Velvyn Ashford. His teachings form the basis of the Lucienist sect of the Church of\n\nthe True Faith.\nIn its time, Lucienism was a radical and reform-oriented movement brought about by the remainder of the Order of the White Rose and various Kaedreni settlers. In its beginnings, the sect was only in the limited membership of those in the\n\nformer Kingdom of Kaedrin. There is no one man responsible for continuing on his teachings, and most were spread by word of mouth for nearly half-a-century after his death. Saint Hadrian of Leuvaarden, the Count of Sarkozy, was responsible for the\n\ncollection of Saint Lucien's works post mortem.\n-------------------The five basic principles to Lucienism are dictated around ones own belief and understanding of the Creator, and the instructions and guidelines He set forth for humanity to adhere to.\n\nI. Belief\nA follow must put his faith wholly in the Creator as the sole true God. Contrary beliefs to the principles of Saint Lucien must be removed like a malignant tumour - for surely if such a tumour was left to grow the results would be most\n\nunfortunate. Lucienists are fervent in their beliefs and are often hard to convince and convert. Their primary tool for conversion is intellectualism and zealous missionary effort, but they have been known to use the sword if absolutely necessary.\n\nII. Worship\nThe one true God, Creator of the universe and of man, must be worshipped according to the clergy's set guidelines and methos. This includes attending holy sermons whenever possible, usually once every Saint's Week, and through self-prayer.\n\nIII. The Study and Preaching of God's Word\n\nLucienists, being the most conservative sect of the Church of the True Faith, had in the past often encouraged fellow Lucienists to become respected clergymen. This, however, is not the only way in which\n\nthe faith may be observed. Lucienists, since their incarnation, were allowed to freely study the works of God and the Church at the beckoning of Saint Lucien. A cornerstone of Lucienist belief centers upon the individual's ability to freely read and\n\nexpress opinion on such matters.\n\nIV. Sanctity of Marriage and Appropriate Gender Laws\n\nThe sanctity of marriage must never be disturbed. Violations of the sanctity of marriage can include, but are not limited to:\n\n- Sexual or other carnal relations outside of marriage. (Offspring of such unions may be considered violations)\n\n- Sexual or other carnal relations with a nonhuman of the lowest degree, such as a Dark Elf or Orc.\n\n- Sexual or other carnal relations with a member of the same gender.\n\n- Adultery, impropriety and disloyalty to one's spouse\n\n- Carnal thoughts such as the coveting of another man's wife\n\nAdditionally, women cannot hold clergy or chivalric titles or inherit land titles unless no male alternative is available. Males, unless proved infirm and unable to inherit accordingly, always come first in the line of succession, by tradition.\n\nV. Veneration of the Saints\n\nIt is believed that those consecrated as saints are holy and exalted and as thus should be revered and spoken of in a light of praise and adoration. While they are of course second and inferior to God,\n\neach saint and their aspect can teach a valuable lesson about the ways of the world and theology in general.\nWhen there was a Pontificate, the High Pontiff acted as God's representative and was hence able to determine God's chosen. In the absense of the\n\nHoly See, the process of canonization ahs been halted until a new prophet is found to re-establish the Church.\n\nIn conclusion, the violation of these five pillars or \"rules\" is believed by Lucienists to remove one's self from the grace of God. While this stands, though, Lucienists believe in the forgiveness of sin, so long as they are not repeated.\n\nThe Rule of Lucien is further expanded upon by various lower guidelines. Although not as prominent, these guidelines are equally important for the Lucienist man and woman.\n\n1. The Sinfulness of Idolatry\n\nIdolatry is a sin and is absolutely heretical, promoting pagan ideologies instead of the grace of God. God is the only deity worthy of worship, as He is the only deity. The worship of saints or other idols is strictly\n\nforbidden. It should be noted that this takes primacy over pillar five - while saints can be venerated, anything bordering on idolatry  is a grave sin.\n\n2. Sacrilege\n\nSacrilege is a sin beyond no other sin and almost literally deadens the offender's soul. They are damned to burn in the fires of the stages of the Nether. To harm a holy individual, clergyman, or to harm something of holy value, as in\n\na house of worship or holy symbol is sacrilege.\n\n3. Lay Preaching\n\nWhile Lucienist clergy no longer exists, it is taught that the word of the faith can be spread and preached by any ordained or not. It is expected of all follows of the faith to spread the grace of God to any non-believers, in the\n\nattempt to enlighten them of their flaws and guide them to the True Faith.\n\n4. The Family of God\n\nAll who believe in the True Faith and adhere to the teachings of Lucien are part of the family of God. Those who know and spread the faith should be revered by their peers, ad they are who guide the future to the knowledge and wisdom\n\nof Lucien.\n\n5. Excommunications\n\nAfter the corruption of the Holy Mother Church during the Imperium Tertius, the act of excommunication is rare. Without the guidance of the Pontificate to separate apostates from the faithful flock, it is up to the individual to\n\ndetermine the intentions and beliefs of those whom they may communicate with and aid. Hence, it is impossible to conclusively determine the credibility of one's faith. But when definite doubt is cast, or when speaks openly against the Faith, it is the job\n\nof the faithful to give no service, no aid, and no gift but that of the word of God.\n-------------------\n\nIn the name of God, use this knowledge to preserve yourself and live within His grace.\n\nDeus Magnus.\n\nSpecial thanks to the Rovin-Winter Banking Company for investment into the research and preservation of this document and former documents. House Winter had nothing to do with the production of this document.\n------\n\nPublished 1551\n3rd Edition\n\nWritten with the use of the original doctrine of Saint Lucien of Savoie, as recorded by Saint Hadrian of Leuvaarden.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "§bThe Sequoia Druid", "The Nature of Druidic Healing\n\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\n\nDruidic Healing is a topic many are curious about, but few, even among Druids, wholly understand the cost on the one performing it.  Most Druids use living reagents to assist in the mending process, this is so that they can draw on the living essense\n\nwithin the reagent and draw less from themselves, but a skilled Druidic healer can also safely mend wounds without any reagents onhand.\n\nDruidic healing is, quite simply, an exchange of living essence from the healer to the patient.\n\nThe Druid focuses upon the living tissue around the wound and asks the patient's body to mend itself, giving of their own living essence to aid in the healing.\n\nThis is where the cost and risk of Druidic healing is, and you should heed it well.\n\nA druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, but all of our healing derives from ourselves and it is possible to cause lasting damage to oneself while healing the wounds of another. This is why living reagents are used, to lessen the need to\n\ndraw from oneself.\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashes to broken bones to some far worse. They all draw from you to some extent, even when using reagents.\n\nSimple wounds you may not even notice the drain upon yourself, it depends how strong your healing has become, and how familiar you are with the process. Practice truly makes perfect in this regard.\n\nI am of the belief an example of a mistake is the best way to pass on a lesson, so I will share how I nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back on Asulon. He and some of his soldiers had been lured out to the base\n\nof a rogue mage that had harassed their kingdom for a long while. When they gained the upper hand and cornered the mage, his trap was revealed, the walls of his base were lined with explosives, and he detonated them.\n\nThree of the soldiers died in the blast, the others dragged a severely injured but alive King back to Skravia and to my inn, knowing I was a healer. His wounds were great, part of his skull was visible on the top of his head,\n\nand he had shrapnel wounds all across his body, blood everywhere. There was nothing to do but try, I coated the wounds with a mixture of living slime and bonemeal, then began the healing process,\n\ndrawing upon the living essences as well as myself to stabilize and mend the kind King laying before me. It took nearly two hours, but his wounds sealed and he was alive and left in a coma for a few days.\n\nHowever, I had given of myself far more that I should have, my skin was pale, almost white, and my eyes had lost most of their color and I could hardly breathe. I am told I lost consciousness, I awoke five weeks later, my every limb sore,\n\nmy hair a shade lighter, but my skin almost back to its normal tone. A fellow Druid, Jena, had to come out to restore some living essence to me or I would have perished within the first day or two, I was so weakened.\n\nTake my mistake with you if you seek to heal, you give of yourself, there is a limit you will reach and you should not go beyond it or you risk your life.  Find your balance between personal sacrifice and reagents to ease your burden,\n\nyou almost always have something available to ease your personal strain, even if it is the grass around you or a planter of flowers outside the window, any living essence can ease your burden\n\nif the situation is a bit beyond your ability to heal safely with nothing on hand.\n\n\n~Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "8th of Suns' Smile, 1595§0\n§0\n§0Today I visited Death's End, and met three met in the Tavern. They were discussing politics, which I took great interest in. I was eventually shown around, and I have taken a liking to the place. Perhaps I will stay here for\n\nwhile longer, though I am beginning to miss Papa and Broderick. I will have to purchase a cloak soon - it is far too cold to remain here without one.§0\n§0\n§0~§0\n§0Ericka\n\n17th of The Amber Cold§0\n§0\n§0One of the men from the Tavern came in again, and introduced himself as Rakim Yar. We spoke for a while, yet he was rude and constantly snapped at me. He then tried to bring me back to his chambers, which I\n\nrefused, naturally. For a Knight, he is quite rude, but there is a certain charm to him.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka\n\n1st of Snow's Maiden, 1595§0\n§0\n§0Rakim showed me his dog today, Shorty. I have never seen an animal like that kept as a pet before, but he seems harmless enough. I learnt that Rakim has lost his parents, and many of his friends. Perhaps\n\nthat is why he is often so brash. He asked me to support him, and promised to marry me if I did, and if we loved each other. He is unusually forwards, but I admire his confidence. I have missed company like this, since Rutger left. Perhaps Rakim will\n\nbecome a close companion of mine.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka\n\n30th of Snow's Maiden, 1995§0\n§0\n§0Today I purchased a set of armour from a Smith, and it will be ready soon. I am excited, yet I worry that many will not take me seriously. There have been some famous woman\n\nfighters, but here, women are not allowed to officially fight.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka\n\n6th of The First Seed, 1996§0\n§0\n§0Johannesburg has been destroyed. I went to go see the ruins today, and a High Elf let me use a device to view it safely from a distance. I did not expect it to upset me as much as it did, but the\n\ncity I had called home for the entirety of my life is now gone. Rakim was worried I had gotten poisoned, but I feel no side-affects. Only the grief that seems to grip me. My Papa was killed in the blast, so I have been told. He had stayed behind, trying\n\nto gather belongings before the Imperials destroyed their own home. I am unsure where dear Broderick is. §0\n§0\n§0My armour was finished today. Rakim says he is to become Arch-Chancellor.§0\n§0~§0\n§0Ericka\n\n14th of Grand Harvest, 1956§0\n§0\n§0I have been practicing with the long-bow, though I am not too good with it, yet. Rakim saw me, and told me he cannot use his right hand - a chunk of his shoulder is missing. He has not yet been to see a Paladin or\n\na Cleric, so I doubt it will be able to be healed, now. He tells me he wishes to convert me to Owynism, and that we will be married in an Owynist ceremony. I shall comply, for now.\n\nI visited Rakim in his chambers last night, something that is not proper in any faith. ut he says that he loves me, and will marry me soon anyway.. He says he could marry a Horen, if he wishes to. But I cannot compete with a woman of that standing. All\n\nnoble women are beautiful, and wear fine clothes, and are proper. I will have to make the effort to be more Noble. I have let myself get to a point where I cannot afford to fail to another woman.\n\n27th of The First Seed, 1597§0\n§0\n§0I made my first connection to the void today. I did what the book said, making sure to be in a safe place. It took me hours, and I collapsed after my first success. I spent all day after practicing ,to the\n\npoint where I can easily light candles. Rakim returned, and I managed to light the fire for him, but I became very fatigued. I will rest for a few days before practicing again. Domestic magic is easy compared to other voidal magics, so I\n\nhave been told. It will help me be a good wife. I will not be outdone by a Horen.\n\n4th of The Deep Cold§0\n§0\n§0I met a man today named Arnorian. He claims to be an ascended, and a Marked Man. He seems pleasant enough, and wished to speak to Rakim,  though the man seemed a little too over friendly. I have never\n\nreally interested men enough for strangers to compliment me, so it made a nice change, though it was uncomfortable. Nicolas came and interrupted him, luckily. I believe Nicolas will be a good friend to me.\n\n21st of The Deep Cold§0\n§0\n§0Arnorian came to see me, as I wished to ask about the monsters. We were in the Tavern, when Rakim approached us, and the two of them got into a small argument over who would train me. I do not understand\n\nwhy the stranger was so aggressive, but he would not leave, so Rakim and Nicolas dealt with him. It was quite sad, really. I have never seen either of them lash out like that. They both then started to train me with an arbalest, but I am awful at it.\n\nPerhaps I will have to practice more on my own.§0\n§0\n§0~§0\n§0Ericka.\n\n1st of The First Seed, 1558.§0\n§0\n§0I met some other soldiers today and two women. We went outside to spar, and I fought John. We stopped though as we both got called away, but I believe I was winning. He did hurt me though, I have a few cuts\n\nand bruises, some that may need stitches. There is a sharp pain in my abdomen, but it is likely nothing major.§0\n§0\n§0~ Ericka\n\n10th Grand Harvest, 1598§0\n§0\n§0The wound I received from sparring with Jack started to hurt again today, when I was out looking for Cleo. Rubens tells me it is infected, and he has taken me to his home in Courland. The stitches had come out during\n\ntraining, and he needed to clean the wound, by reopening it. I can only remember the first few minutes of such, the pain was unbearable, and I slipped out of good mind. Nicolas says he will carry me back the next day to Bastion.§0\n§0~§0\n§0Ericka\n\n31st of the Grand Harvest, 1598§0\n§0\n§0I visited the new Orcish city today, and met a Paladin, who agreed to come look at Rakim's arm. I hope he visits soon.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka\n\n7th of Snow's Maiden§0\n§0\n§0Rakim promised me we'd be married soon, and had me speak to the man who would be doing our ceremony. I realised though that despite our grander home, neither of us have any money. Perhaps I will take up a small job elsewhere, in\n\nCourland or the such, to try and provide for us, as Rakim is far too busy.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka\n\n20th of The First Seed§0\n§0\n§0I went to Courland today, for the Rovin-Staunton wedding, and while I was there I saw the new King Tuvya with a high elf man. I later learnt this man was a wraith. I was about to travel home, when I saw him by the carts, with\n\nlarge staff. He started casting spells, but Ser Hanson arrived, and a Knight. They seemed to retreat to the shoreline, so the three of us pressed forwards to catch up with them. Hanson was injured, but the Knight managed to push the elf back into\n\nthe water, before leaving. Once he and Hanson had left, the elf had changed into a set of dark robes, and possessed the qualities of a wraith. He wanted me to grovel on the ground for him to spare me, but instead I told him I was with child. He seemed\n\nsurprised by this, and then asked me to name my child after his son, Haakon. He seemed to have a conversation with his staff for a long while, before turning to me. He told me he intended to drain me, which he did, leaving me weak and in agony. I crawled\n\nacross the beach to try and gather my strength as he left, but my knee had been broken, as he sent my own sword flying towards it, in an attempt to make me bow to him. Once I had awoke I wrote to bastion and a group of soldiers came to assist me. Ser\n\nElrach gave me some potions, and fixed my knee into place. §0\n§0\n§0I will find a gift for him.§0\n§0\n§0I intend to stay away from Hanson. I told him to go and fetch help for me, but instead he left me there alone.§0\n\nElrach tells me I lost my child.§0\n§0\n§0Ericka\n\n4th of the Amber Cold§0\n§0\n§0I met Almas today, Rakim's sister. She seems sweet enough, but I am not sure she likes me. I did see her with Caius though, and the pair seem quite close. Perhaps they will marry soon.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka\n\n1st of The Deep Cold§0\n§0\n§0Rakim tells me he 'dealt' with Hanson, yet the man follows me around, stands besides me, and engages in conversation like his deeds meant nothing. We also named our son, Jaco. I worry though that this\n\nincident will affect my ability to have children later on, once we are married. Elrach tells me it will not, but I have heard many stories of women unable to have children.§0\n§0\n§0~ §0\n§0Ericka\n\n20th of the First Seed, 1600§0\n§0\n§0I partook in wargames today, with the other soldiers. I did quite well, however I will have to ask Rakim for much more training.§0\n§0\n§0~Ericka", ""),
        StaticBook("Rebirth of Evil", "§bLilyana", "The Rebirth of Evil\n\n          By\n\n        Lilyana\n\nShe awoke in dire pain and confusion as the livelihood of the Crimson Fist’s purpose and existence, literally, weighed heavily upon her. The Champion’s mind sporadically showed images of a battle that just collapsed the temple containing most, if not all,\n\nof the Sanguine Hand, sending them to an early demise. Shouts meant to be full of victory turned into blood curdling screams of pain and death as they were overrun by their attackers. As she clawed at the gravel and dirt that trapped her, she tried\n\nlistening to her surroundings for other survivors calling out to her. But all her ears could hear were the memories of the stone walls around her cracking, sliding, grinding against one another, as they began to collapse inward on her and the others, and\n\ntheir screams. Oh how the memory of the screams tortured her mind, forcing her bloody and gashed hands to sift quicker. Her hands digging and sifting faster, trying to escape the memory,  but the images and sounds only seemed to come faster as she tried\n\nto flee, keeping in tempo with her movement. \n\nWith a heavy grunt and thrust, she thrusts her arm through a small lit-opening, finally feeling the cool air touch her skin.  This bolstered her will, giving her the strength to push herself through the\n\nsmall opening and back into the outside world. The elven woman lay there in the cool morning fog for what seemed like an eternity,  time completely lost to her, breathing in deeply the fresh air.  Slowly, from the dense fog a shadowy figure approaches her\n\nexhausted self and shoves a bow and arrow into her face. Panting, the woman looks up at the figure as he pulls back his hood, revealing the rugged features of a hunter. The man pulled back the weapon slightly from her face and asked her for her name.\n\n“M-my name…”, the elven woman spoke between her labored breaths, “ My name is Cora.”\n\nSeeing Cora’s condition and state, the hunter took pity on her that fateful morning and led her to his dwelling in the forest.  There, he fed and dressed her wounds,\n\nnursing her back to health. Cora slowly came around to the man, knowing all too well how easily it is to lower ones guard when they begin to trust someone, but never spoke about the Crimson Fist. When he did question her about her past, she simply said\n\nthat she was a servant to the people that owned the, now, pile of rubble that he found her at. The man nodded, knowing it rude to question a person’s past, and went about his business. However, no matter how hard he tried to focus on cleaning his\n\nmorning’s kill or divert his gaze, he was mesmerized by Cora’s beauty and soon felt for her. Cora, knowing that the Crimson Hand’s was either utterly destroyed or scattered to the winds and that her previous life was too dangerous to try to start again\n\non her own, accepted the hunter’s affection with open arms and soon gave birth to a child of a rare complexion. The child’s skin was pale like snow, his hair like fine straws of white gold, and his eyes….crimson like blood. Because of his defining eyes,\n\nCora named him, Haemon, the Blood Child. \n\nHaemon’s features were the most exciting thing of his life as he lived a dull life in the forest. His father taught him how to string a bow, to catch a fish, to chop wood, and skin a kill. He promised to take\n\nhim hunting when he was rightfully a man and left Haemon in charge of keeping order at home when he left on his numerous hunting trips. Cora took to motherhood surprisingly well. Her swift and accurate hands that once sliced a man’s throat before they\n\ncould blink now directed a needle and thread through cloth; her strength and determination that kept herself alive during fights with armed guards now carried in loads of firewood or cleaned the wash. She watched over Haemon throughout the years grow into\n\na fine young man, but also watched herself age. She knew that with her death, the Crimson Fist died as well, as did its unfinished work. So, as her husband left on one of his hunting trips, Cora brought Haemon into the cellar of their small home.\n\nThere, she had him swear to keep this information from his father, and showed him the history of her people, of his people. Haemon was fascinated by the information, rituals, chants, and stories his mother knew and begged to know all of it.\n\nSo, every time her husband would venture out into the woods, Cora would teach Haemon the ways of the Crimson Fist.\n\nThis continued for many years until the night before Haemon’s eighteenth birthday, when everything changed.\n\nThe hunter returned home earlier than expected, bringing with him a new bow to give to Haemon as a gift to use on their first hunt together. However, when he approached the home, all he could see was darkness through the windows. He quickly entered\n\nthe home, noticing that the fire and candles had been empty and snuffed for quite some time. The darkness however, did allow the light from the under the cellar door to draw his attention. He opened the door quietly, filling the room with light,\n\nand was met by the voices of his family, however could not make out what they were saying. Descending the staircase he saw his wife and son, dancing while around an open fire. An animal’s carcass and bloodied knife lay next to the flame and\n\nits blood was painted on their naked skin in weird designs and letters that he could not understand. Haemon was the first to notice his father’s presence, quickly dropping his hands arms, breaking the dance, and backing away from the cellar door.\n\nCora noticed the Haemon’s fear and quickly turned, meeting the horrified gaze of her husband. He, softly, began to question Cora and Haemon, but neither responded, both afraid to unveil the lies they have been keeping from him. The hunter became angry,\n\nhis voice raising as he stepped down the stairs, approaching his wife. Cora remained speechless, not knowing what to say or do, she simply looked at the floor. In a fit of tears and rage the man grabbed Cora’s arms and forced her against the wall,\n\nshouting at her, begging to her, for answers. Haemon watched in horror and fear as his father slammed his mother against the wall across the room, shouting at her, asking her questions, spewing lines of secrets, lies, and betrayal. But it was only Haemon\n\nthat noticed the fire in the center of the room grow larger and only Haemon that heard the flame telling him to stop his father. Haemon tried to cover his ears to escape the raspy voice but the flame’s voiceresonated inside of him, demanding Haemon to\n\ntake action.\n\nHaemon closed his eyes and screamed out, trying to smother the flame’s voice with his own, but when he stopped screaming, all was quiet. Haemon opened his eyes to see his hand firmly around the bloodied knife that had sat in the\n\ncenter of the room, and the knife he held was deeply embedded into his father’s back. His father twisted around to look at Haemon’s eyes as he desperately tried to reach for the knife in his back. Blood began to leak from his mouth as he tried mouthing\n\nwords, words that Haemon would never hear. His father fell towards the center of the room, his head cracking on the hard stone floor, blood leaking out of his body towards the fire. Haemon backed away from his mother who now shriveled into herself against\n\nthe wall, staring at her dead husband, at the pool of blood forming around his body.\n\nThe blood of the innocent man pooled and grew, eventually reaching the fiery claws of the flame. With an immense heat and power, the flame jumped high and turned\n\ncrimson, sparks flew from it in all directions. Haemon now stared at the fire, mesmerized by the dancing of its flames and heard the voice that spoke to him earlier, this time much clearer. He could not disobey it if he tried, the pull it had on his very\n\nbeing was too strong, so he walked into the flame. Cora tried to reach out to her son, but her body was frozen, whether in fear or by the flames own power she did not know, but when she called to him nothing escaped her throat. Haemon did not feel\n\nthe flame burn his skin, but felt it burn his insides, as if it had reached into his heart and soul and burnt them to ash. He could not scream out nor did his body react to the pain that his mind was feeling. His vision slowly became dark and blurred, his\n\nsense of feeling seemed to numb away, and his mind began to close in on itself.\n\nWhen Cora woke the next morning in her bed she quickly wretched onto the floor. The nightmare was so real to her, the heat of the fire, the smell\n\nof her husband’s blood, the image of her son walking into the fire, all shook her deeply.  She struggled out of bed and walked down to the kitchen, finding it cold and dark as it was every morning. She started a fire and hung a pot of water to boil while\n\nshe called out to Haemon to wake. However, he did not return her call. When she checked his bed, he found it vacant and undisturbed from the previous morning’s making. Fear struck at her as she turned to look at the closed cellar door. Slowly approaching\n\nit and wrapping her hand around the latch, she closed her eyes as she opened it and was greeted by nothing but the smell of burnt flesh. At the bottom of the staircase she could see her husband’s burnt skeleton in the same spot it was\n\nleft in her nightmare. She cried out and slammed the cellar shut and turned to run from the house, only to see a figure standing in the doorway, shadowed from the sun coming in around the figure. Its glowing, deep crimson eyes\n\nwere its only distinguishable characteristic.\n \nThe figure spoke to her with two voices, both familiar but from different lives.\n \n“Hello, Mother”", ""),
        StaticBook("Word Exercises", "§bBenjamin Berric", "_____________§0\n§0__S_B_2ERVANT§0\n§0AP0L1_N______§0\n§0__E_A_O______§0\n§0__3RR4W__G___§0\n§0__R__R___R___§0\n§0_____E___E___§0\n§0__5AN6E7M8N__§0\n§0__L____E_N___§0\n§0__U____D_____§0\n§0_Y9LLOW______§0\n§0______E______§0\n§0______2WORD__§0\n§0______T______\n\nUnScRamBle!§0\n§0Use the hints to help!§0\n§0\n§0Like a Dog: FLOW§0\n§0\n§0Chopping wood: XEA§0\n§0\n§0A fine snack: DREAB§0\n§0\n§0In the night sky: TRAS§0\n§0\n§0Protection: DELISH§0\n§0\n§0Pointy: WAROR\n\nWhich way is right?§0\n§0Find the correct way!§0\n§0\n§0Sword___OR___Sord§0\n§0\n§0Number__OR__Nombar§0\n§0\n§0Fort____OR__Furt§0\n§0\n§0Flag____OR__Flehg§0\n§0\n§0Horse___OR__Hers\n\nFill out all assignments on a seperate work book and turn it in.", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancers V I", "§bFreyr Mantisuku", "Investigations into Necromancers Volume I\n\nA picture of a man in dark robes standing over dying man a stream of dark green is slowing from the dying man into the robed man hand, two decaying zombies stand behind the dark robed man awaiting his orders*\n\n\nArthur: Freyr Mantisuku\nCo-Author: Crineas Acosta\n[Forewarning: Do not confront Necromancers unprepared]\n[Always Bring a Paladin or war cleric with you during hunts]\n\n\nA Short Introduction\nNecromancy is the defined pragmatically as the utilisation of Life-Force. Necromancers usually have tell-tale signs of their necromancy,\n\n It is like poking a hole in a bucket they can take others life force with the imbalance but their own life force is slowly drained.\n Necromancy is the draining of life-force for nefarious purposes commonly, it’s an art shunned by many.\n\nAppearance\nThey look like us, For all you know one could be next to you they are very hard to find the only true tell is that many will have a very pale look and are extremely sensitive\n\nand weak but this does not go for all necromancers. Basically, signs of decay on their bodies would be a significant give-away.\n\nBehavior\nDue to the extreme difficulty of actually picking one out in a crowded this second cant be added in details.\n\nStrengths\nThey have the power to resurrect the dead and use them as Minions.\nThey can drain the life force of living things leading to a quick death.\n\nWeakness.\nLike all mages they are physically weak and can be killed easily..\nSome instances, holy magic can effect them but it's not always the case. \nThey also have the ability to curse other by modifying life force.\n\nOrigins and Additional details\nHow mortals found this magic is unknown, but it's safe to conclude that the undead under Iblees was instrumental to the art during Aegis\n\nIt’s likely that they drain life-force whilst using their own bodies to draw it, whether through physical means or through other ways such as mists.\n\n\nA note of warning. \nLearning Necromancy is a taboo and would lead to severe repercussions on one’s own wellbeing and health.\n\nNotes:\nAny extra, Corrections or confirmations on information can be\nSent to Either Freyr, or Crineas (( samsan99, Sharkali ))Further Volumes will be compiled as more information is made available.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Artificer I", "§bBelestram Sylvaeri", "The Tragedy of§0\n§0      The Artificer§0\n§0       In Two Parts§0\n§0\n§0         Part I§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By Belestram of the Venerable House Sylvaeri,§0\n§0\n§0Written this Sixteenth of the Deep Cold, 1609, for Aislin Maar.\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0In Princedom fair, in days of old,§0\n§0There toiled craftsmen, wise and bold,§0\n§0\n§0Who by their labour did abide,§0\n§0To pierce the veil which doth divide\n\nThis mortal world, and one beyond,§0\n§0And crossing there, could thus abscond§0\n§0\n§0With truths forgotten, learned anew,§0\n§0From Elder Gods both false and true.§0\n§0\n§0One such there lived, of  manner stern,§0\n§0And of his kin did most discern,\n\nFor strove he, always, for ideal,§0\n§0And grinding failures 'neath his heel,§0\n§0\n§0Disdained of Elves, and hid his skill,§0\n§0Among far wooded, forest hills.§0\n§0\n§0Until one day, by fate's decree,§0\n§0He found an eldritch, ancient tree.\n\nWith leaves of gold, and boughs of white,§0\n§0Which shone like silver in the night.§0\n§0\n§0A relic of the past, it stood,§0\n§0The first among that sacred wood,§0\n§0\n§0Whose roots drank deep of mighty spells,§0\n§0Which Elves of yore spun on the dells.\n\nThe elf was stunned, his soul was bound,§0\n§0And in that place a purpose found,§0\n§0\n§0To carve in wood a likeness keen,§0\n§0A sculpture, as had never been.§0\n§0\n§0He toiled long, and slaved away,§0\n§0Compelled by force beyond his sway,\n\nUntil at last, his labour done,§0\n§0He stood and wept beneath the sun,§0\n§0\n§0For there before him, pale as death,§0\n§0Stood woman lifelike, lacking breath.§0\n§0\n§0Her eyes did gaze unto his own,§0\n§0And stirred a feeling, never known\n\nTo him- a pressing, urgent love,§0\n§0And he beseeched the gods above,§0\n§0\n§0To grant her life, and make her whole,§0\n§0To soothe his own beguiled soul.§0\n§0\n§0But here, my friends, we must take note,§0\n§0Of passion's plea is often wrote,\n\nAnd ne'er a wise thing is it, for§0\n§0The outcome one might oft abhor.§0\n§0\n§0The elf-lord's love did seal his fate,§0\n§0For gods of old are scarce innate,§0\n§0\n§0And love to know the hearts of men,§0\n§0To bless, and curse, (and curse again.)\n\nThe Elder Ones made swift reply,§0\n§0These gods of sound, and stone, and sky,§0\n§0\n§0A wind there was, a clamor brash,§0\n§0And from that tumult, lightning lashed.§0\n§0\n§0It struck the figure, gave it life,§0\n§0And beauty there was born from strife\n\nLike none which ever had been seen,§0\n§0And none which ever since has been.§0\n§0\n§0And feeling, seeing, knowing so,§0\n§0Her wooden eyes did find a glow,§0\n§0\n§0And cheeks like apples flushed with red,§0\n§0Just as the smitten elf had pled.\n\n___________________      §0\n§0    End of Part  I§0\n§0\n§0-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("House Barbanov", "§bWalter Marshall", "History of House Barbanov\n\n\n\nBy Walter Marshall\n\nHOUSE OF BARBOVIC, called BARBANOV in the normal speak, claims lineage from Saint Joren Horenson himself, the first of the High Kings of the North. Further down, the house claims descent or kinship from Barbov the Black, its nominal description,\n\nRovyk the Stern, Saint Julia of Paradisius, Saint Lothar of Balian, Saint Adrian of Leuvaarden, Blessed Jan Jeremi, Blessed Francis the Martyr, Blessed Otto of Vanderfell,\n\n and most importantly, coming from the loins of Exalted Sigismund himself, Prophet of Revelations.\n\nThe House stands as a ducal family in the Holy Kingdom of Oren, with Lord Karl III. holding the duchy of Haense, inherited from his Rovin uncle. Once, however, the family stood as Imperial Princes, the Lord and Lady Barbanov’s father,\n\nAlexander I being Emperor of Oren. Even so, from the Lord and Lady Barbanov’s maternal side, they were once Princes of the Hansetians, being of the now destroyed and defunct Kingdom of Aesterwald.\n\nHOUSE BARBANOV OF HAENSE has no long lineage, that be accustomed to its parent houses of Karovic and Rovin, or its cousins of House de Sarkozy, House of Kovac, or even House of Vladovic.\n\nThe House comes from the loins of EMPEROR ALEXANDER I CARRION and his wife, PRINCESS ARABELLA ROVIN, married per a peace contract between the Empire of Oren and the newly vassalized Kingdom of Aesterwald.\n\nThe union, however, was nay a happy one.\n\nAfter the start of the infamous RENATUS REBELLION, sparked by protests of the arrest of the Grand Knight, the Princess stole the two babes born of her and Alexander’s coupling; the twins Karl and Lorin.\n\n It is unsure how the Princess transferred the babes unnoticed, but eventually the twins found their way under the tutelage of PRINCE OTTO ROVIN, with their father deposed and presumed dead and their mother dying of a hunting accident.\n\nUnder the guise that they were his bastards, the two babes eventually grew from sucking on the teat, to toddlers, and eventual kids, roaming the Waldenian Royal keep aimlessly, as children do.\n\nChange appeared, however, when KING VORON I ROVIN died, replaced by his Raevir-hating son, KING ARN III ROVIN. It is under King Arn’s reign that the Raevir minority of Aesterwald was pushed out, killed, or worse.\n\nHis hate went so far, eventually to curse HIGH PONTIFF DANIEL I, a known Carrion bastard, and declare a schism, putting his own kinsman Hubert as anti-Pontiff. Despite propaganda within the Northern kingdom,  it did not bode well to the populace.\n\nDefeat after defeat, and the SCHISM WAR, as it came to called after the Duchy of Savoy came to aid of the Kingdom of Akovia, rolled on. Desertion from the Waldenian ranks became more frequent, with even the King’s own kin abandoning his unjust cause.\n\nOTTO ROVIN, taking along the child Karl and Lorin, left the Kingdom (before, of course, posting the Condemnation of Arn’s Reign). Otto and the children fled to CYRIAUM, where he took work as the Papal Guard of HIGH PONTIFF DANIEL I.\n\n. It is here where Otto finally told Karl and his sister of his true heretige, where the High Pontiff confirmed as true.\n\nFor the next ten years, Karl trained underneath not only his Uncle, but of the numerous heroes of the SCHISM WAR. As his uncle dealt with the political nature of the Waldenian Realm, Karl fought with the likes of BLESSED EMMA VLADOVIC,\n\nthe woman-warrior with a thirst of heretic blood, the unifier of humanity himself, KING ANDREW I VYRDA, and the current king, KING OLIVER I ASHFORD. From the teachings of King Andrew and King Oliver,\n\nKarl grew to understand the affairs of state and nobility, eventually growing out from the child of a drunken uncle to a successful and witty statesman. It is also during the SCHISM WAR that Karl took up his name BARBANOV,\n\n after urging of his cousin and High Pontiff Daniel I, in honor of BARBOV THE BLACK.\n\nAfter KING ARN III ROVIN died from burning down his precious Vanderfell and Eagle’s Perch, Karl joined his guardian Otto to pick up the pieces. Forming the unsuccessful NORTHERN COMMONWEALTH,\n\nKarl help fight against the Dwarves in the FOURTH DWARF-HUMAN WAR, taking a penchant to the killing of midgets and eventually,\n\n the High Elves who killed the fair KING ANDREW I VYDRA. It is then when Karl, with Vladov allies and the small retinue of the Commonwealth, took the HOLD OF HIEBENHALL, eventually to be named SIEGRAD,\n\nthe new capital of the Northern Realm. Karl established himself as the COUNT OF SIEGRAD thereafter, holding the title to this day.\n\nOnce his guardian and uncle, OTTO ROVIN, left to go chase down rumors of Arn living within the secluded land of AELDIN, Karl took up the reigns of the Commonwealth, disbanding its entirety and eventually to name himself the DUKE OF HAENSE.\n\nAs of now, the DUKE KARL III BARBOVIC stewards his capital of SIEGRAD, one of the most populous cities within the Kingdom, as well as working where his uncle left off: rebuilding the Northern Realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flagship", "§bSt. Thomas Denims III", "----The Flagship---§0\n§0AXIOS WAR BULLETIN I§0\n§0The Amber Cold, 1583§0\n§0\n§0--Contents--§0\n§0~Grand King Executed§0\n§0~Oren Suffers Loss at THE GORGE§0\n§0~Allies Stand Firm Behind Emperor Philip Frederick§0\n§0~Religious Roundup: Reforms and Schism\n\n~Debate in Haelun'or Over Security§0\n§0~Haria Reigns in Military\n\nGRAND KING ALGODA EXECUTED BY ORENIAN -------FOES-------§0\n§0\n§0Algoda, Grand King of Urguan, was executed by Orenian officials after being seized in the Orenian town of Ostermark. This has hardened opinions in Kal'Omith in favor of the the war and the\n\nSenate of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan will be convening this Saint's Day to select a new King.\n\nOREN SUFFERS HUMILIATING LOSS AT THE GORGE, ATTEMPTS TO CONSOLIDATE CONTROL IN LORRAINE§0\n§0\n§0The forces loyal to the Holy Oren §0\n§0Emperor Philip I Frederick were decimated and roted from the field of battle in the opening classh of the\n\nStaunton rebellion. The Stauntons and their allies held firm against a numerically superior and more advanced foe. This marks a rare loss for the Holy Oren Empire and promises to prolong the current conflict.\n\nTHE DUCAL CITY OF§0\n§0~~~~~~METZ~~~~~~§0\n§0\n§0Metz, located in the Archduchy of Lorraine, has experienced heavy fighting between rebels from the Staunton family and loyalists led by Sir Otto. Forces loyal to the emperor currently control the city,\n\nwhile rebels control much of the rest of the Archduchy of Lorraine, setting up what is sure to be a pivotal battle in the current war.\n\nALLIES STAND FIRM BESIDE PHILIP I §0\n§0---FREDERICK---§0\n§0\n§0The Dominion of Malin and the Kingdom of Haense have reaffirmed their loyalty to the throne of the HOE despite the recent loss. However, public opinion in the Dominion of Malin appear divided,\n\nas many wonder why elvish blood should (and indeed was) spilled in the internal affairs of the valah. Old debates about th true independence of the Dominion and the true allegiances of it's leadership have also resurfaced. The Kindom of Haense, however,\n\nhas moved to actively supress any rebel activity within its border in addition to aiding the war effort.\n\nRELGION ROUNDUP: REFORMS AND SCHISM§0\n§0\n§0The Church of Lorraine, also known as the Lotharic Communion, has announced a schism from the Church of the One True Faith. The rebels of Lorraine and Savoy have often raised\n\nallegation of interference against the Emperor in regards to reforms of the Church, and this appears to be the logical course now that the rebellion is being waged.§0\n§0\n§0Additionally, the Accords of Johannesburg were\n\nadvanced by the Emperor and High Pontiff Adrian I, further cementing the state control over the Church of the One True Faith. Only time will tell whether the schism will be sealed and if the reforms will stand.\n\nDEBATE IN HAELUN'OR OVER SECUIRTY§0\n§0\n§0Cahir aep Ophael, Braxus Ni'leya, and Icarus are vying for an appointment as the elokarir'tir. Cahir appears to have the most support among the citizenry, but it is up to the Silver Council to decide who\n\nget the post. There is pressure on the Silver Council to act swiflty, as recent events have revealed that lax security can lead to needless bloodshed within the Silver City.\n\nHARIA REIGNS IN §0\n§0---MILITARY---§0\n§0\n§0The Lord Regeant of Haria, Fakhri Kharadeen, has established a court system to prevent the military from harassing citizens and visitors with little to no oversight. This will hopefully make Haria\n\na more pleasant place to visit, having removed the threat of state violence against individuals without any due process.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~Ebs Telrunya§0\n§0EDITOR IN CHIEF§0\n§0~St. Thomas Denims§0\n§0PRINTER OF PONCE", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mariner", "§bBelestram Sylvaeri", "The Fate of the Mariner§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By Belestram of the House Sylvaeri§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Written this Twelfth of Grand Harvest, 1609, for the enrichment of a certain Lady.\n\nThe constellation known as \"The Mariner\" is among the brightest in the night sky, and eldest in the memory of the Descendants. Taking the form of a man with arm outstretched, this conglomeration of stars is beloved of the seafaring peoples of the world-\n\nfor no matter the location of the viewer, his hand will always point northward. He is known as Narnir'vallei in the Elder Tongue, and is personified by many true figures throughout Elven history. His companion is known as \"The Grieving Maiden\", and plays\n\nan integral part in the tales which surround these stars.§0\n§0\n§0The following is an excerpt from the \"Lays of the Old Princedom\", a translated and abridged compendium of the oldest verses in all Elvendom. While lacking the beauty of the original text, it\n\nconveys in simple verse the tragic \"Fate of the Mariner\" and to this day remains the only version of the Elven story in the Common language.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0     ~~~~~~~~§0\n\nIn ancient days, before the fall,§0\n§0'Neath eldritch bough, in silver halls,§0\n§0\n§0There trod an elf whose heart was true,§0\n§0A Prince, a mariner, and who§0\n§0\n§0Wrought ships to sail the sapphire plain,§0\n§0In calm, and in torrential rain.\n\nHe loved the sea, and knew her charms,§0\n§0And bore the fury of her storms.§0\n§0\n§0This noble seafarer of old, of silver locks and manner bold,§0\n§0\n§0Was loved in turn by fairest maid,§0\n§0For whom his noble heart had sway'd.\n\n\"I will return upon the dawn,\" §0\n§0He sweetly vowed to her, \"and yon,\"§0\n§0\n§0\"Together we will ply the shore,§0\n§0And venture seaward, nevermore.\"§0\n§0\n§0The sea is fickle, grudging, vain,§0\n§0And in dark passion did disdain\n\nThe sailor's word, and took his life,§0\n§0To spite his earnest, loving wife.§0\n§0\n§0Her heart thus rent, with love unmade,§0\n§0She leapt from highest promenade,§0\n§0\n§0And broke upon the crags of stone,§0\n§0Her mortal coil of flesh and bone.\n\nAnd so it is, lliran, and so,§0\n§0Unto the stars they did bestow,§0\n§0\n§0The image of their tragic love.§0\n§0Their form can oft be seen above,§0\n§0\n§0The Mariner, and very near,§0\n§0The Maiden, lantern raised austere,\n\nTo guide all sailors, as he swore,§0\n§0To return home forevermore.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunaii I", "§bArnorian Elendil", "In the first years of Aegis there were no Kingdoms or cities, but scattered and pitiful tribes of Men, Elves, Orcs, and Dwarves - The four great races. Buildings of stone and wood were unknown to the primitive people, who roamed the\n\nwild lands, fighting and travelling, never settling down or pausing to build. The chief tribe of mankind was the Harenite branch, a group of fair and tall warriors, strong hearted and led by Haren, the firstborn of Horen. Soon, as the tribes of mankind\n\nbranched out further and delved deeper into the more wooded areas of Aegis, the Harenites soon encountered a tribe of Elves - the Mali'Dun, let by Sarai of Malinor. Violence broke out very quickly, and a tribal conflict\n\nsoon developed. The war lasted for twenty years, until both tribes expended all that they could in a high-stakes battle over a hill called Caragdur. The results were catastrophic to both sides, with many of the warriors of either\n\ntribe being slaughtered in battle, or dying soon afterwards. Peace was declared out of necessity, and Haren and Sarai wed to cement the peace, and alliance.\n\nThe Descendants of Haren and Sarai\n\n(And the Harenites that followed their chieftan's example) found themselves physically different from their respective parent races, warranting a new name for themselves. The origins of the term Adunian, or 'Adunaii' are\n\nunknown, but that is what they called themselves. These new people were energetic, strong, healthy and fair, and found that in them was mixed the ambition of man, and the caution of Elves. This hybrid vigour led them to become the dominant race of\n\nancient Aegis, paving the way forward with many breakthroughs and records. It was the Adunians who first mastered the art of boat-building, as well as the Adunians who built the first fortified settlement - Idunia.\n\nThe Early Adunian society was hierarchal, Adunians on top, then Elves and remaining Harenites, and finally at the bottom, were the common Highlander folk that made up most of the rest of the human population.\n\nAs with most systems like that, this ended up breeding strife - A Highlander named Owyn fashioned himself as a rebel after two or three centuries of Adunian rule, and with surprising speed, force and tact overthrew the Adunian Royal\n\nfamily in a daring palace raid. The rebellion was swift, ending almost as quickly as it had started. The Monarchy was executed, and the Adunians were barred from ever stepping foot in the Kingdom of man under 'Godwinson's rule.\n\nThe King that had taken the blow was Arendil - Godwinson had slain him in the attack on the palace, but Arendil's son Elendil was more fortunate. He had been out of the palace on a hunting expedition, and informed by fleeing Adunians to not\n\nreturn to the Palace, but instead to turn North, to the White Coast. He quickly took his role as leader of the refugees, ordering a fleet of ships built, the flagships being called the Alcondaras and the Nen-Girith. They\n\nset sail as soon as the ships were sea-worthy, as it was a great fear that Godwinson would recind his choice of exodus, and simply chase the Adunians into the sea with horse and spear. The Exiles sailed for three months, braving\n\nSea-Blizzards, Iceburgs, and towering waves. Many ships did not survive the trip, as they were hastily put together. In the decades after this, every town or public building would have a shrine to the Atalante, those who were consumed\n\nby the icy depths. Tragedies behind them, at the begining of the fourth month, land was sighted in the form of a great Island, rich in all goodly things. The Island was called Al'Ildic, and the shore upon which the Adunii first landed was called\n\nCape Pelori.\n\nThe Adunians settled the shoreline and interior quickly, building simple thatch houses and wooden walls, to give them some solace while they surveyed the rest of the Island. Paths were soon\n\ncleared around the Island, and particularly around the signature landmark of the Island - Three Marble white peaks, dubbed 'Lalaith's Three' in memory of Arendil's slain wife. Elendil ordered a capital be build at the foot of these mountains,\n\nand this was soon done. The Capital was called Meneltarma. Many years passed under Elendils rule, and he had carried the Adunians through one of their most pressing times. By the time he passed on, the capital was no longer an shanty\n\ntown, but a solid city, of marble buildings and gold inlays. He passed the crown down to his youngest son Braen.\n\nBraen Elendil started many of the traditions that Adunians for centuries after held, the most\n\nnotable ones being the wearing of circlets, the carrying of Durendal and the system of inheritance. He set up the inheritance so that the youngest son of the family would always inherit, thus ensuring the longest possible\n\nrule for the Adunian Lord. The Circlet wearing came from Braen's possession of the Circlet of Horen, which the Adunians believed to have belonged to Horen himself, before it was given to Haren, and eventually passed down the line. Braen also\n\nhad himself a blade forged named Aranruth, a sword that held within it some strange power to fight evil. (Later, this blade would prove it's historical merit by being used agaisnt Harbingers effectively.) Braen also started an official military\n\nof the fledgeling Kingdom - the Adunian rangers, men skilled in the ways of the wild, with knife and bow, stealth and secrecy. Of course, there were very few actual threats to the Kingdom, so they were rarely used.\n\nBraen's grandson Amandil did a striking thing to highlight his reign as Lord; he ordered an expedition be made back across the sea to the original homeland, and mainland Aegis. More than 600 years had passed since the original\n\nexodus, and the old nobles of the court had desired to see what had become of Godwinson's people. They loaded the Alcondaras and the Nen-Girith with sailors and soldiers, along with the Royal retinue and crossed. They made it to the shorelines of\n\nAegis, made a camp, but for reasons unknown to us did not stay very long at all. They quickly returned, and Amandil had a quiet reign after that. Amandil's son Anarion led another expedition, this time laying eyes upon what the old world had\n\nbecome. Anarion encountered scouts from the Kingdom of Oren, and was brought to the city of Al'Khazar. Once the language barrier was breached, friendly relations and trade agreements quickly followed. This was the first contact\n\nthe Adunians had had with the outside world in over 700 years.\n\nPart I of Adunaii written by Arnorian Elendil, son of Artorus, son of Halboron.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mysterious Badge", "§bTyrell Blavier", "*A large and decorated \"V\" lies in the center of the page. Around it lies repetition of the phrase \"Pax et Gloria. Safe.\"*\n\n       Agent One\n         P-APP\n          -Q\n          -TB", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Brynden:", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "§bSalendys", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-        Arcane\n      Evocation\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nThis book was written to help students and aspiring students of arcane evocation to better understand this magic and ease their learning.\n\nWritten by: -Salendys\n\nChapter 1: What is Arcane Evocation?\n                           \n\nArcane Evocation is the art of drawing pure magical energy from the void. It can then be shaped as anything the mage can think of. This is a creative form of magic\n\nwith mostly artistical uses. While it is possible to use this magic in combat, only a skilled arcanist can do so, and even then it is not as strong as the other types of evocation. If your intention is to acquire a means of dealing damage, then this is\n\nnot the magic for you.\n\nChaper 2:\nArcane Energy\n                           \n\nArcane energy is a rare element. In fact, it does not exist naturally in the world. It is an ethereal substance almost exclusive to the void. Because of this, Arcane Evocation is\n\nthe most difficult type of evocation to learn.\nAs with all other types of evocation, one must fully understand the element that is being evoked. The only way to study arcane energy is by observing an evocation of someone who already knows this magic.\n\nThis means it is practically impossible to learn without a teacher.\n\nNow, for those who already have a teacher and seek to complement their lessons with further knowledge, the arcane element can be described as follows.\n\nIn it's purest form, arcane energy is invisible, shapeless, odorless, completely inhert and very volatile. It can be compared to air or smoke, having a similiar composition than most gaseous substances.\nThose who have observed evocations may have noticed\n\na fine, thin mist surrounding them. This is because it isn't a single mass. It is in fact a conglomeration of countless tiny wisps of energy that together give the illusion of being a single object.\nSmoke is perhaps the thing that visually resembles\n\narcane energy the most in our world. Studying its shapeless and volatile nature may be of big help to understand arcane energy.\n\nChapter 3: Aura\n                           \n\nAura is a field of mana that surrounds living beings. More complex beings, such as descendants, have a colour associated to their aura. Each individual has their own colour for their aura.\n\nSome believe that the colour depends on one's personality. This isn't always the case, however, and anyone may have any colour.\nThis colour doesn't change, unless other forces somehow manage to tamper with your aura, which is usually very bad.\n\nAuras are very relevant to Arcane Evocation in particular.\nWhen raw arcane energy is drawn from the void, it instantly mixes with the mage's aura, making it visible and giving it colour. It is a common misconception to assume that arcane evocationists\n\nmanipulate aura itself. In truth, it is simply the product of mixing aura with arcane energy that is being manipulated, not the actual aura.\nAnd no, arcanists cannot see other people's aura or make it visible.\nAura is a very personal thing, like\n\nyour own soul.\nThis means your evocations can never mix with someone elses, or other types of evocation.\n\nChapter 4: Beginner steps\n                           \n\nAfter you have managed your first evocation, there is not much you can do. You will only be capable of producing a small wisp and hold it for a short time. The best thing to\n\ndo is to keep practicing. With each successful attempt you will be able to hold the wisp a little longer. Make sure to have rested enough to be completely recovered after each attempt.\nEventually you will be able to hold your wisp for about five minutes.\n\n[!] A detailed drawing of a wisp hovering over an open hand occupies most of this page.\n\nAt that point you'll get enough time to figure out how to get your wisp to do things. You are in control of your evocation, but must learn to control it properly.\nTry moving it around slowly. Think clearly of the movement you want it to make.\n\nAt first a few inches is all you can manage at a time, but with practice it'll get better. Another good excercise for beginners is to make it shrink and grow slightly in size. Adding and removing the amount of energy in an evocation is a basic\n\ntool that is key for the later stages of learning.\nOnce you can comfortably manipulate the size and movement of the wisp with relative freedom, you can start to attempt shaping it. Simple geometrical shapes such as cubes, spheres and cylinders\n\nare the easiest to achieve and you should start there.\nImagine the arcane energy taking the desired shape with as much detail as possible. Do not lose focus once the evocation has taken the desired shape or it will become amorphous again.\n\nThis is the end of this book. Hopefuly this will help many students to complement their learning of arcane evocation.\n\nA book dedicated to advanced students and even novice arcanists will be written in the future.\n\nThank you very much for reading my book and I hope you found it helpful.\n\n[!]What appears to be a drawing of a chibi dark elf in robes giving the reader a thumbs up lies in the bottom half of this page.", ""),
        StaticBook("Air Evocation", "§bAyche Raven'kor", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocatonist Alatar of the Mage Academy\n\nRecopied By\nAyche\n\n\nTable of Conents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\n\nChapter 1: \nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by absolute darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas.\n\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' \nconcept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found.\n\nLearn how to blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to paint your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self.\n\nWith the art of air evoction, you manipulate it. Wind is unpredictable and one\nof the best studied branches of arcane magics, You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it.\n\nIn order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a  region of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it.\n\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch how the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or carries it away.\n\nChapter 3:\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; you may begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\n\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this. A small amount of wind may be conjured.\n\nWarning: You may pass out a few times upon first connection.\n\n\nChapter 4: After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal.\n\n\nThe first and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large and forceful push at the enemy.\n\nSecondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado.\n\nA skilled air evocationist can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most objects out of your sphere. That concludes this tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "§bMythras Sylvari", "Conjuration:\n          \nConjuration, is the bringing of life forms formed in the void by the conjurationist, into the world itself.\n\nThe three sub-magicks of Conjuration, are.\n- Primodrialism\n- Perenial\n- Morphonic\n\nMorphon, is the conjuring of animals, and the creating of them as a entity. \n\nIt's to bring a animal into existence, after lots of study put into the animals insides, and outsides, essentially, interior or exterior.\n\nPerenial, is the conjuring of plant life, after the study of the interior and exterior workings, to do such, is the arcane art of the conjuring of perenials.\n\nEssentially, the conjuring of a studied plant.\n\nPrimordial, is the bringing of elementals into the physical plain.\n\nYou must be learned in the art of evocation, and the added art of conjuration.\n\nIt's essentially summoning creatures made of your arcane element.\n\nConjuration, is as said, a hard art, the many theories enacted suggest slowness in the power of the art.\n\nTo evoke animals and plants, and even elementals, is a valuable skill.\n\nSources:\n\n- Goliath\n- Random Magician \n- Learnings in delver bas.\n\n- Inquisition\n- Theories", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome: Air Evo", "§bUradriethiel", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocatonist Alatar of the Mage Academy\n\nRecopied By\nUradriethiel\n\nTable of Conents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\n\nChapter 1: \nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by absolute darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas.\n\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' \nconcept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found.\n\nLearn how to blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to paint your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self.\n\nWith the art of air evoction, you manipulate it. Wind is unpredictable and one\nof the best studied branches of arcane magics, You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it.\n\nIn order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a  region of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it.\n\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch how the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or\ncarries\nit away\n\n\nChapter 3:\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; you may begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\n\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this. A small amount of wind may be conjured.\n\nWarning: You may pass out a few times uponfirst connection.\n\nChapter 4: After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal.\n\nThe first and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large\nand forceful push at the enemy. Secondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado.\n\nA skilled air evocationist can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most objects out of your sphere. That concludes this tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Telekinesis", "§bSanguine", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~       Telekinesis\nA guide to learning\n\nWritten by Magister\n      Sanguine\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\nFirst off Telekinesis is a form of Alteration magic, Alteration magic impacts the world around it unlike its void counterparts.\n\n Telekinesis works by altering the force of gravity pushing down on an object. The process of telekinesis is rather simple Focus on an object then with the help of the void alter its gravity allowing it to float.\n\nAlthough at higher progression you will have a better grasp of the object being able to redirect, push and stop different objects.\n\nStarting out you should only be able to lift a few small objects such as a Pebble, but with time you will be able to lift more and heavier objects and that pebble you started with will now be a boulder.\n\nKnow you must have learned a thing or two but here are some Practical uses of Telekinesis: \n~Throwing knifes: They are light allowing you to throw them at your enemies with ease\n~Doors: No problem for any telekinetics just apply force against it.\n\n~People: Now the living are a bit tricky to manipulate so you must indirectly using clothing is a good bypass for it.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Arcane, V1", "§bMeldur the Blue", "______\n\n     Understanding\n       the Arcane\n          ______\n\n     Published 1472\n         Volume I\n\n\n\n\n  By Meldur the Blue\n\n        Chapter 1\n\n    Like in all fields of study, for one to adequately learn and retain knowledge of the Arcane arts, he or she must first understand the origin of what is widely known as magic. If a student were to attempt to do so without proper\n\nfoundation, there is a high chance that he or she would be unsuccessful, and, even if he or she was successful, there is a great risk that the knowledge gained would be used to inappropriate ends. Just as a politician would study history so as not to make\n\nthe same mistake twice, so must an Arcanist. \n    And so this is what the earliest parts of this book will aim to cover, namely where different forms of magic come from, how it has evolved over the many years, and important figures of study whos works and\n\ndiscoveries will prove beneficial to the process of understanding the Arcane.\n\n        Chapter 2\n\n    All forms of \"magic\" can be divided into two main categories, the first being Void Magic, and the second being Diety Magic, each named after their respective sources. The first of these two categories is the one which we will focus\n\non at the moment.\n    As mentioned previously, all Void Magic comes from the Void. The Void is the term for an endless expanse of nothingness, not physically of this world, that contains everything that has ever existed or been sensed in the material\n\nworld. In other words, nothing exists in the Void except for endless potential. At times, a being may attempt to make contact with the Void. If the attempt is successful, he or she may draw potential from the Void and use it in the material world. This\n\npotential can come in nearly any form. However, the being who attempts to draw it must first be very familiar with the form they wish to it to take. This difference in forms of potential gives us the different fields and sub-sections of Void Magic.\n\n    Now because technically, any being has the ability to draw potential from the Void, any being also has the ability to practice Void Magic. This makes Void Magic the easier of the two main categories to learn. However, it can be difficult to establish\n\n╔══════════╗\n║\n║\n║   **************      ║  A diagram of the\n║    five elements\n║ is depicted on this\n║          page\n║   **************\n║\n║\n║\n╚══════════╝\n\n╔══════════╗\n║\n║\n║   **************\n║   A table of tips\n║ for connecting to\n║     the Void is\n║ shown on the page\n║   **************\n║\n║\n║\n╚══════════╝\n\na connection the the Void, and even more difficult to maintain that connection while drawing potential from it. First, the user must abandon his or her mental perception of reality, and instead open it up to the endless possibility of a limitless nothing.\n\nAs our minds are finite, it is impossible to grasp something infinite. Because of this, it is only possible to access certain parts of the Void, and not its entirety.\n    Connecting to the void is an exhausting and daunting task, and can take many\n\nattempts, especially on one's first experience. In order to establish and maintain contact with the Void, one must use the mystical energy which fills our bodies and world known as Mana. Just as performing physical tasks costs physical energy, so does\n\nperforming magical tasks cost magical energy. When Mana is depleted, or when the user is distracted, the connection to the Void is broken and any potential taken from the Void returns to it.\n    This brings us to the two governing laws of all Void Magic.\n\nThe first is called the Law of Conservation of Reality. It states that anything performed by magical means takes up the same amount of energy as if it were performed by non-magical means. In other words, there is no endless supply of energy for magic. The\n\nsecond law is called the Law of Creation, and states that something cannot be created from nothing. This is to say that all magical feats require an equal sacrifice to perform, usually in the form of Mana. It also states that all Void Magic comes from the\n\nVoid and must return to it. Now this second law is governed by what is called the Evaglno Effect, which says that just as seemingly super-physical feats can be performed at times through the help of adrenaline, so can super-magical feats be performed, but\n\nat an equally taxing and detimental cost.\n    Now there are four main Archetypes of Void Magic, used to more easily classify the fields themselves. They are Alteration, Mental Manipulation, Evocation, and the Dark Arts. This book will not go in depth on\n\neach individual field of Void Magic, but it will provide a brief description of each Archetype.\n    Alteration is the most difficult of the four Archetypes to learn. It involves using the Void to shape and alter objects that already exist in the physical\n\nworld. Subtypes include Transfiguration, Telekenesis, Translocation, Household Magic, and the Whimsical Magics.\n    Mental Manipulation involves using thoughts, experiences, feelings, and images from the Void in order to affect the user's\n\nmind or the mind of another. It is a very dangerous form of magic, although it cannot physically injure someone directly. The subtypes are Illusion, Mental Magic, and Cognitism.\n    Evocation is the broadest of all Void Magics, as well as the easiest to\n\nlearn. Through Evocation, a magic user can \"evoke\" potential from the Void and manifest it in a physical way as elements, objects, or living things. Subtypes of Evocation are the Five Elements, Arcane Evocation, Arcane Shielding, and Conjuration.\n\n    The last Archetype of Void Magic is without a doubt the most evil and dangerous. The Dark Arts are manifestations of pure evil, and serve no purpose other than the corruption of the world and the harm of others. They are outlawed by most Nations, and\n\ntheir use will yield dire consequences. Subtypes of the Dark Arts include Contract Magic and Okar, Necromancy, Shade Magic, Soul Puppetry, and Fi'hiiran'tanya, also known as Magic Blocking.\n\n        Chapter 3\n\n    As even the simplest of creatures is aware, our world is governed by beings of higher power known as Aenguls and Daemons. They are still ruled by the mightiest of all beings, the Creator, who brought everything into\n\nfruition out of nothing, including magic and the Void.\n    These Aenguls and Daemons are constantly seeking to interact with the physical world in some way, and because of this, many of them offer supernatural powers to otherwise mortal beings. We call\n\nthese powers Diety Magic. Diety Magic is more difficult to obtain than Void Magic, because one must be granted it by the Spiritual Entity itself, though control can be taught by other mortals with the same blessing. \n    All dieties expect something of\n\ntheir followers, and so not fulfilling these obligations results in what is known as an unattunement from the diety. This is known as the Law of Servitude, and states that a diety may at any time grant or take away magical abilities at a whim. This is not\n\nto say that it happens often though, and usually requires some sort of grave act of disobedience.\n    Now because of the first two laws of magic, we must assume that even Diety Magic requires some form of energy or sacrifice to perform. However, in this\n\nspecific instance, it does not only tax the user but the spirit as well. The magic used feeds off of the connection that the user has made with his or her mystical patron, and so when that connection is used up, no more magic can be performed for a period\n\nof time.\n    Due to their shared belief in the same or similar Dieties, many users of Diety Magic band together to form Guilds, Orders, and even Cults dedicated to the study and responsible use of their respective field of magic. Popular examples of such\n\ngroups include the Druidic Order, followers of the Aspects Ceridwen and Cernunos, the Ascended, servants of the Aengul Ariel, and those who practice Muun'Trivazja, Kharajyr Priests of the Daemon Metztli.\n    Now those Dieties which grant magical\n\nabilities often wish to establish a strong sense of contingency when it comes to their followers. As a result, Aenguls and Daemons alike have been known to strip magical abilities from their followers who attempt to practice other forms of magic. A common\n\nexample of this would be the Aspects \"unattuning\" a Druid if he or she were to establish a connection with the void. It is because of this nurtured sense of contingency that many practicioners of Diety Magic have harbored a mistrust and dislike of\n\npractitioners of Void Magic, and vice versa.      Now because there are a great deal of Aenguls and Daemons willing to bestow power upon mortal servants, the number of Archtypes used to categorize the many different fields of Diety Magic is far higher\n\nthan that of Void Magic. They include Druidism, Shamanism, Rune Smithing, Clerical magic, Monk magic, Ascended magic, Undead magic, Scourge magic, and Muun'Trivazja. Although there are more Archtypes, the Archtypes themselves are less internally diverse,\n\nin other words, they each hold far fewer fields.\n\n        Chapter 4\n\n    Now as we learned earlier, the use of magic still requires the expenditure of energy, whether it be through Mana or the connection with a Diety. However, most mortal bodies are not at all used to using these particular forms of\n\nenergy, and as such it can take a more costly toll on the user's physical body. This phenomenon is known as Corruption. The fourth law of magic, the Law of Corruption, therefore states that the more energy one puts into developing Arcane ability, the less\n\nis available for non-magical tasks. Therefore, in theory, an entirely magical being such as a spirit could not take on a real, physical form, except for through magical means.\n\n        Chapter 5\n\n    Just as with all things, magic was brought into existence by the Creator at the beginning of time. At first, magic was a very, very rare phenomenon. Not many people had access to it, and even fewer understood it. Only\n\na fraction of the currently known fields of magic were know during the first hundred or so years of recorded history, but great efforts were made to discover more.\n    Now as time progressed, mortals began to further explore this expanse of nothingness\n\nknown as the Void. Great wizards arose, and new fields of magic were found. The Arcane Arts were born as an object of study, and more and more people began to understand, study, and practice.\n    It was not at any specific time that the Aenguls and\n\nDaemons began to meddle with the affairs of Men, they did. As their involvement grew, so did the power and number of their followers, thus leading to the earliest Diety Magic Guilds being formed. These Guilds and their Void Magic counterparts yielded some\n\nof the mightiest, wisest, and maddest wizards the world has ever come to know.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Magic", "Jistuma", "Transcribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer\n\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in he Void the world of\n\nAegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and\n\nunformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\nThe power was entwined into the very\n\nfabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power channeled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore\n\nmanifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spead of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone,\n\nhardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil.\n\nBut the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his\n\nminions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world…\nBut it was not to\n\nlast. The power of Iblees was great, even in the Void, and he worked at unraveling the barrier between the worlds… Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope\n\nfor salvation…\nWith the failing of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\n\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there.\n\nSo it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other to\n\ndarkness… They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made…\n\nThe History of Magic\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((08/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Origins", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Arcane Magic:\n       Origins\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\n\nSince long into the past mages have existed. Pulling their spells and magic into reality. Different mages find themselves specializing in different forms of the arcane. However, the root of this magic throughout those who practice the arcane magic\n\narts is the same. Each arcane mage finds their source of magic from a realm known as the void, to which each living and sentient being is connected.\n\nThe void itself is a realm of infinite potential, yet almost paradoxically is entirely comprised of\n\nnothing. It is from this absolute and undetermined potential which spells and magic is pulled forth from. Connecting only with their minds a mage must take this void and change it into the form which they desire. For an evocationist this may be their\n\npreferred element; be it earth, wind, water or fire. For others this may be an illusion, pulling fourth light and twisting and bending the minds of their targets.\n\nHowever, it is to be noted that pulling such power from the void is no easy task. For\n\none to be able to control both the amount of power and the form of their desired magic is no easy feat. Indeed, many a novice find themselves rendered unconscious simply upon their first connection to the void. But, with practice over time balance is\n\nachieved and thus some of the most potent arcane magic is created.", ""),
        StaticBook("Air Evocation", "§bprincetonlax21", "This selection will offer insight into the subtype of evocation named Aeromancy. I do not particularly enjoy the name, so please do not use it.\n\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocationist Alatar of the Mage Academy.\n\n Table of Contents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\n\nChapter 1:\n\nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by complete darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas. Hypothetically,\n\nanything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. \n\nThe first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' concept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found. Learn how to\n\nblanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to create your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\n\nWind and Air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self. With the art of air\n\nevocation, you manipulate it. Wind is very unpredictable and one of the least studied brances of arcane magics. You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it. In order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a\n\nregion of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how the pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it. \n\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch\n\nhow the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or carries it away.\n\nChapter 3:\n\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; You\n\nmay begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void.\n\nFirstly, you must find a place of peace. Next, use your blank canvas to imagine a air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very\n\nblood. Though combining all of this, a small amount of wind may be conjured. WARNING: You may pass out a few times upon first connection.\n\nChapter 4:\n\nAfter you have mastered basic connection, you can\n\nmove onto some of the key spells in a air evocationists arsenal.\n\nThe first, and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large and forceful push at an enemy.\n\nSecondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado. A more skilled air evocationist can can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most object out of your sphere. \n\nThat concludes this tome. Feel free to\n\ndiscover your own path in the special art of air evocation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Void-Origins V1", "§bScholar of The Void", "Theory of Void-Based Origination - Volume I, Origination and Supporting Facts.\n\nGiven the nature of the following text, the author requestions anonymity.\n\nTable of Contents\n\nI - Statement of Theory, Page 3.\nII - Fallacies of the Creator, page 8.\nIII - Void Nodes, Page 15\nIV - Cast vs. Nature, Page 20\nV - Conclusion, page 25.\n\n                    I\nStatement of Theory and Support.\n\nPresented and supported in this text, and in following volumes, is a scientific theory as to the void's role in the creation of the world as we know it. An act commonly attributed to the\n\nomnipotent deity called \"The Creator\", it is the purpose of this text to provide evidence to an alternative means with fewer conflicts with the facts of reality.\n\nSupport for the theory, which will follow, can be initially comprised of three main points\n\nwhich will be detailed in their respective chapers. \n\nThe theory, as well as these three points, are as follows.\n\nThe Void is the origin of both our world and lives, brought forth by a means akin to a mage's spell.\n\nSupporting this:\n\nThe logical fallacies alongside a sentient 'creator'.\n\nThe recorded, known, effects of the Void on our world.\n\nThe nature of void-summoned elements and life, and\n\ntheir being capable of perfectly mimicking what is natural.\n\n                   II\nFallacies of the Creator.\n\nBy many names, a single, all-powerul being is the backbone of many modern idealisms. The idea that a sentient being existed before existence itself is popular.\n\nIt also, on a fundemental level, fails to make logical sense.\n\nThe core belief of these religions are that this creator was the one responsible for the world, the void, and all other planes of existence.\n\nThe flaw in this is the idea that sentience can exist without an environment for it to be housed in. \n\nThe abilities to see, hear, or feel are all useless when nothing exists to be seen, heard, or felt. And since these senses are the\n\nbases of thought, it can be inferred by extension that without these environmental stimuli, sentience cannot exist.\n\nWhile we can never know with complete certainty that this god does not transcend logic, the best solution is the most\n\nsimple. The Void, being both perpetual and infintesimal, has existed since before existence itself. It has been the constant throughout both reality and whatever lies outside.\n\nIt requires much less exceptions to accepted logic to assume\n\nthat the void is what created reality than a being did. When one sees a mountain, they do not assume the mountain was made by hand - merely that it has always been there.\n\nThe way by which the void has brought to life our world shall be\n\nexplained in the following pages.\n\n                   III\nVoid Nodes.\n\nWhile in the vast majority of cases, the void cannot permanently change our world (For example, a mage's spell disappears when he releases it), there are recorded instances of such a thing happening.\n\nOne such instance was discovered in Anthos, where a void node under a southern Mage's hall had permanently altered a cavern with it's energy.\n\nHumming with energy, and the stone itself changed into all manner of material, the detonated void node\n\nbrought proof of two things - That the void can permanently sustain a physical change, and that it can enact itself on pre-existing material.\n\nThe first of these two facts is of most importance. The second will be addressed in a later volume.\n\nThe fact that the void can permanently alter the world is the basis of this theory.\n\nWhile what was created was random and without logic or pattern, it did create. In the node's aftermath existed material where none had existed before.\n\nIt did not simply change things, but created as well. The net sum of what was found after the node's change was greater than what had been there before.\n\n                    IV\nCast vs. Nature\n\nTwo types of magic interract with the void in the way closest to this theory's concluded way by which reality began. These are evocation and conjuration.\n\nEvocation, for the unaware, is the summoning of a chosen element from the void for temporary use within our realm. Usually weaponized, known forms are as follows: Air, Water, Fire, Earth, and Electrical.\n\nConjuration is similar, in some ways, but\n\ninstead of a simple object a conjurationist summons forth a living being. \n\nThe key point with both of these magics is that, in a skill mage's hands, the summoned element or creature is indistinguishable from a 'natural' piece, found in our world.\n\nIf a Earth Evocationist wished to form a stone exactly like one she had found, and she were skilled enough to do so, the summoned stone would be entirely identicle to the original. The same applies to all evocations as well as conjuration.\n\nThese facts in mind, in tandem with the void nodes' nature, provide evidence that our world could have been created as a result of the void, in a manner akin to evocation with a single key difference being that this is permanent.\n\n                    V\nConclusion\n\nFollowing volumes will include parts of the theory which answer possible conflicts with parts of the world. Volume II will cover the presence and divinty of aenguls and daemons.", ""),
        StaticBook("ELECTROMANCY", "§bonm224", "ELECTROMANCY\n         GUIDE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Richard Tarus\nAdapted: Amras Lúinwë\n\nWhat is electric evocation?\nElectrical Evocation is the arcane magic form whereby a mage creates Electrical bolts for his or her purposes. Unlike other types of Evocation electrical bolts is intended to be much more difficult to control due to its\n\nspeed and high energy nature. Mages who specialize in electrical evocation will be able to form electrical bolts and streams of electricity to electrocute their targets.However, electrical evocation requires much more energy than for example\n\nfire and therefore a single electrical bolt requires much more energy than a fireball. This however is made up for by the fact the lightning bolt is somewhat equal in power to the two fireballs which could be made in the same time period.\n\nStrength\nAn electrical evocationist is capable of producing powerful electrical bolts\nBolts may travel from any point to point with speed and reliable accuracy.\nWeakneses\nElectrical evocation takes a greater amount of time to produce a bolt\n\nthan other types of evocation\nElectrical evocation is dangerous to learn and during some phases of learning the mage can be incapable of producing any spark which will not injure themselves.\n\nProcess\nReaching Tier 1:\nWhen you begin to learn magic, you will start a Tier 1. At that point in time, you are unable to cast any form of magic unless you have some sort of experience and have connected to the void.At this tier you will learn\n\nhow to connect to the void, and then research electricity as an element itself. Connecting to the void will take perhaps even years of practice, and once completed,you may still have some difficulty. Researching electricity would consist of practically\n\nfinding any sort of detailand then taking note of it.\nReaching Tier 2: \nAfter their advancement from tier 1, and their connection to the void, they can now create a multitude of sparks and perhaps an even minor bolt,albeit difficult to\n\ncontrol till towards the end of Tier 2.  Even though they can create sparks, users at this tier may have an overload in which the sparks will practically burst outwards towards the conjurer.In this tier they will need heavy loads of practice in order\n\nto become more proficient with a minor bolt.\nReaching Tier 3:\nIn this tier they can finally create a full powered bolt withought major troubles, and have full proficiency. At this point they can now create streams of electricity,\n\nthough they will simply spark and singethe target, rather then cause major damage. With this tier, they are novice mages. \nReaching Tier 4:\nNow, the electrical evocation users can create the \"call-down\"of electricity, aka a bolt from a high point\n\nin the sky. They can create multiple bolts in a shorter time, although a fire evocationist could create fireballs in an even shorter time.The call-down is not very proficient, and will rarely land on the user's target.  In this tier,they can create great\n\nstreams of electricity that will do some good damage (burns, etc.) They are very proficient with the bolts now.\n\n For more information go to this link, there is the same info + RP guide:\nhttp://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/88498-improved-electricity-guide/", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "§bEvelangéline", "About Fire Evocation:\n\n-Fire Evocation, one of the six evocation arts is the utilization of fire by the evocationists. Although Fire Evocation is not very hard to learn, it is one that must be practised a lot about, because of its destructive behaviour.\n\nBasic Understanding:\n\n- Fire evocation, as the other types of evocation arts, is powered by the void. The evocationist who has a connection to the void calls forth the fire from the void. One aspect that is not known by many is that the fire formed is -\n\nnot real on this plane of existance. A thing that I tell to my students, \"The fire is fake, only the effects of the fire are real.\" is an accurate statement, considering this.\n\n-The origins of the art are unknown, although It is one of the oldest arts.\n\nProgress of A Fire Evocationist Student:\n\n- Fire evocation is easy to learn, yet hard to master. So, a Fire Evocationist needs to take their time and have stable observations and practises to use their potential to a maxiumum.\n\n- During the first five elven days, the student needs to form a stable connection to the void, through meditating. While meditating can be done in any position, it can also be done for flexible amounts of time. For example, while many evocationists -\n\nchoose to meditate for at least half an hour once. I meditated for five minutes six times a day. The important thing is efficiency, and focus. The student needs to clear their mind in order to form their first connections to the void.\n\n- After the evoca-\n\n-tionist forms a stable connection to the void, they work on conjuring low-powered flames, propably shards of embers. During this period, the evocationist must be observing how fire burns, how it spreads, and how it affects the substance it burns on.\n\n- After an elven week, the evocationist will get started with conjuring small flames, not exceeding the size of a regular candle's fire. During the beginning of this period the evocationist will be greatly fatigued, propably not being able to hold the -\n\nfire for long. The time of the evocation will increase from ten seconds to a few minutes if done correctly. The evocationist should focus on increasing the size of the flames and lenghten the duration of how long they can hold the flame.\n\n- After this period, the evocationist will be able to evoke bigger flames, propably not exceeding the size of an elven fist, after the two elven weeks of the period.\n\n- Next period, the evocationist will focus on shaping their flames as spheres.\n\nTo be able to throw fiery balls of fire at objects. The evocationist will fail to throw a ball of fire successfully the first five elven days, then will be fatigued after one small ball of fire. During the ends of this phase, the evocationist will increa-\n\n-se the size and range of their fire spheres, the phase lasting for nearly two more elven weeks, exactly one elven month after the evocationist had first started to learn.\n\n- From the start of the next phase, the fire evocationist will-\n\nbe having covered most of the parts to be known, moving to a period of practise. The evocationist will be able to evocate walls of fire and flames that are distanced from the evocationist. However, as the distance of the fire increases from the evocation-\n\n-ist, so does the difficulty and mana requirement. The evocationist at this point would be able to form multiple fire spheres before being fatigued, not exceeding an amount of three. While the wall of fire can be maintained for an average of thirty-\n\nseconds. After this period, is the mastering period.\n\n- A master of fire evocation has learned how to effectively and efficiently use their mana to cast larger flames, calling fires to this realm of existance quicker. Gaining the ability to-\n\nevoke large areas of vigorous, reactive fire; fire novas. Bear in mind that an evocationist should never try to evoke more than their training has given to them.\n\nMore Things to Know:\n\n- Although fire may be engrossing and exciting, it also is very dangerous. More than the other arts actually, at least in my point of view. You cannot, simply cannot manipulate the fire you have summoned, meaning that-\n\nif a fire evocationist accidentally set an object on fire, they cannot extinguish it. So try to remain calm, and don't cause accidents.\n\n- To further explain the lack of fire manipulation, I'll go into slightly more detail. A fire evocationist cannot-\n\nutilize already existing fire. They can only summon flames from the void into this realm of existance. Once they summon the flames and use them, they are out of control. As I say to my students: The fire is alive, it has a mind of its own. You cannot -\n\nforce it to do anything. You can only convince it.\n\n-Lastly, an evocationist of any type shouldn't ever push their limits too hard, to exceed their level. If an evocationist proceeds to cast magic for too long-\n\nthey will get extremely fatigued, then maybe even lose their life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "§bRosso", "Water: seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of live, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbinger of eradication.\n\nDespite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromance yearns to wield.\n\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from the ability\n\nto control \"mana,\" but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is\n\ndifficult to put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it become more simpler tasks.\n\nMany mages use a staff when evoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for instance, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties\n\nthat is possesses, and also because it has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it forms a stream from the end of my\n\nstaff that maintains itself midair. From here, I can move it, project is somewhere, or allow it to dissipate.\n\nOne thing about water evocation that differs from the other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice\n\nwater evocationists begin with controlling pure water in its liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled ((approximately late tier 3)), he is able to change the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defence than liquid water is,\n\nas it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block oncoming projectiles, as a form of short-distance defense, and as a method of harming others. I have personally mastered a technique of blasting an enemy with water, and then freezing\n\nthem in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from the heat of the sun or a torch. To break void ice, the hydromance must either completely lose concentration, or another\n\nmage must do something to break the ice (i.e. a pyromancer melts the ice with magical flames). Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as the wisps of steam are too difficult for even the most trained evocationists to control.\n\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\n\nIntroduction to Hydromancy\n\nWritten by Ev Ar'ahern\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Translo", "§bSab'Aoth", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=                 Void\n         Translocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=            \n   \n        -<= (O)\n\nVoid translocation is the art of bringing and placing objects into and out of the Void. Mana is what fuels our world and is in all forms of objects and beings. Void translocationists use said mana to perform their art. By copying the mana that an object\n\nor person has exactly they are able to place and remove objects into and out of the Void. One must copy the pattern and amount of mana that is inside the object or being before they may perform said art. As per such they simply need to create a connection\n\nto the Void and form a portal of sorts to place and take objects into and out of the Void. However people are unable to be transported to to the Void due to the complex and large amounts of mana they have. The same is said for other large objects, As well\n\none must be careful when performing said art because if an object is placed into the void for too long, their bodies and very being itself would be torn asunder and transformed into mana itself. This process would take about one to two elven weeks to\n\nreach.\n\n\n[An astonishingly complex drawing of a portal of sorts is detailed along the page.]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Study of Air.", "§bThe Scribe.", "A Study of Air.\n\nAir has always been a curious element. It is said to be the element of the free-minded. Those who wish harm upon others and seek to delve into chaos shall not find themselves working with the air around themselves easily as a manipulated\n\nelement. Now, as many of you prospective mages are probably jumping up and down, I am going to say now; This is not a book on how to learn Air Evocation. It is merely a study of the properties of air observed over time.\n\nAir is a gas. Much as when water is heated to a boil it turns into a gas, air is constantly in a gasseous state. However, the boiling temperature (temperature at which liquids turn to gas) of air is far, far lower than any witnessable temperature upon any\n\nrealm the races have currently visited. I believe that if we visited a realm where air was a liquid, it would be covered with insurmountable oceans, and we would all drown.\n\nAir moves from high concentration to low concentration. Upon working with a bellow, I was able to pump more air into a box than currently resided with in. After opening the box, a breeze was produced. The opposite was produced upon\n\nusing a bellow to remove air from a sealed box. A slight breeze was created blowing into the box. \nIf one places a leather bag into a large jar, and seals the bag upon the lid of a jar using thick rope, one shall find that pulling that bag up from the jar\n\nis a difficult task. This is due to the amount of air within the jar. The air on the outside of the jar is exerting force due to its concentration, while the air on the inside is extering less due to its lack of concentration.\nThis is also an effect of\n\nsuction. The lesser amount of air tries to pull air to it to equalize the concentration, but it cannot pull the air through the leather.\n\nAir is finite. There is only a certain amount of air within a certain amount of space, and that air can be exhausted through breathing.\n\nAir is comprised of multiple elements, though I do not know what they are. This was a rather unfortunate experiment to test. I locked a squirel in a contained box, and then submerged the box underwater. Obviously, the animal died as\n\nthe air in the box ran out. But, when I opened the box underwater, bubbles were created, leaving me to believe there was still gas located in the box. The question is, if the squirrel inhaled all of the air, what was left?\nI hypothesize that\n\nthe lungs of creatures only use the majority of air to breath, and other trace elements are left over as they are not needed by our lungs.\n\nAir can absorb heat just as a solid or liquid can. Upon heating a rod and holding it in a room, the space around the rod remains heated, obviously, but when the rod is removed from the room, the air within the room is still heated.\n\nThis next section is comprised of recounts of scientific interviews about air.\n\nThe properties of air are weight, color, density, air mass and pressure.  ~uncited mali'aheral.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of Aegis", "§bMonk Scribe", "Fall of Aegis\n\nThe miasma in the north lingered ever more so. Galahar was evacuated and the cloud temple became our final stand. From the temple I shouted out into the crowds, summoning those who where chosen by the Nations as their champions.\n\nUpon arriving to Laurelin, I called all of the champions into Dawns Bakery, where a secret entrance lay.\n\nThe High Priestess handed out blessed armor pierced, enchanted in Aeriel's grace. To each of the champions. We then took a small passage,\n\ninto what was once the Laurelin Gauntlet. Entombed in a massive oak tree, lay Vardak's portal from the nether. \n\nThe champions gaze into the portal and grip the hilts of their weapons tightly. \n\nI step out of the way\n\nof the portal, clench my soulstone in my hand tightly and wish them good luck. As I vanish the brave few enter head first. \n\n- Spoken by Native in the Elf in the Deep Cold, 1351.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism2", "Eenhoornheid", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume II\n\n    by Lucion Sullas\n\nNow that one has learned of the two figures involved in this debacle, let us discuss the event itself. Should you not ahave read the previous volume, most of what shall be written will be nothing but a confusing morass of information.\n\nOne suggests you perform the logical action, and return to the previous volume prior to reading this one.\n\nNelecar's afore-mentioned zest for banishment had been mostly tolerated by the council, aside from the\n\nconsiberable opposition from Ellir'siol. However, one event sparked a final, fatal banishment. The husband of Ellir'siol, Talias, the second-in-command of the military under Nelecar, was exposed, along with other individuals (whom shall not be identified,\n\ndue to a number still living and present within the nation), as attempting to subvert, and remove Belecar from his position via aggressive action. Upon learning of this, Nelecar immediately called for the banishment of all those involved.\n\nElli'siol, understandably, attempted to argue Nelecar out of doing so, but only managed to stall his pronouncement with the help of other council members. When the decision was made public, Elli'siol showed her true colours.\n\nIn a move to directly parody the acts of Nelecar, she 'banished' the entire populations of the city, and majority of the citizenry followed her out of Haelun'or-- those won over by her popular and public dislike of the Okarir'sil. Piling upon boats,\n\nthey left the Emerald Isle to the town of Ceru-- a cliffside village and quasi-colony that bordered the Kingdom of Renatus. Here, they settled for a time, and waited.\n\nHere Ellir engaed in disgraceful, demagogic, rabble-rousing, and appearled to illogical emotional thinking to further solidify and justify her actions. This went on for many months, while Nelecar and his few loyal supporters remained within Haelun'or-\n\n-slowly losing confidence in their actions.\n\nAfter months had passed, and her ravenous support had died down, Ellir returned to the city-- deeming her point had been made. However, it was noticeably adsent of Nelecar.\n\nHis supporters remained, and were thankfully not pursued by the 'victors'.\n\nThe prologue and effects of this event will be discussed in the final installment of this series.", ""),
        StaticBook("Abstract", "§b[Sohaer] Kalenz", "The Valleian'Acal of Larihei and the effects on the physical body.\n\nLomanih et al.; Malin's Welcome 198\n\nIn this paper we will attepmt to categorize, without searching for too through an explanation, the effects of enchanted\n\ngold-infused pools. We will begin with the physical alterations and come to accept that continued exposure to the pools will only lighten one's skin and hair tones while potentially increasing a subject's height. We see that neither of these effects are\n\nharmful to the physical body.\n\nWe will also conclude that these pools bolster an Elf's magical prowess and their natural talent to channel the Tanya that flows through our earth. We will illustrate why this increased acuity only has\n\npositive effects, and the suggestion of hallucinations or a clouding of judgement is beyond preposterous.\n\nFInally we shall discuss the benefits of bathing in the pools and encourage all of Malin's pure children to do the same.\n\nThis shall be done by introducing a concept known as the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, which will be the driving philosophy behind our arguments.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Enchanting", "§bSarrion", "On Arcane Enchanting\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following are my own personal notes taken from my research from interviews with other Transfigurationists and my lessons from Avenel.\n\nIn Transfiguration there is a sub-classed spell base called Enchanting. Enchanting is the simple art of transmuting either a command for an object or a spell  to bind to an object with a medium\n\nground  that powers the spell. This medium ground is almost always a mana crystal, which is any gem though the rarer the gem the more mana it can hold. The transfigurationist is to first channel his/her mana into this gem and fill it entirely\n\nwith his mana, then transmute the spell or command into the gem and bind it to the object arcanely. This whole progress burns /a lot/ of mana in the mage's mana pool, and it a dangerous art that can either kill the mage\n\nor cause a mana fluctuation. This is why that sometimes a mage may set up an enchanting lab with a “Mana Obelisk”, for those who are ignorant in the topic a Mana Obelisk is a large gem pillar that has\n\nbeen enchanted to contain a large mass of mana, that way when it comes time to enchant the enchanter can pull the mana from the crystal to the gem, not having to use their own mana.\n\nDo note the creation of a Mana Obelisk is very intricate and will need to be activated by two or more Transfigurationists.", ""),
        StaticBook("cEwk", "HI3_", "m I    na   M    e\n         i       Z \n     c   EW               k .", ""),
        StaticBook("A slim grimoire", "§bUnknown", "ＦＡＬＬＥＭ´ＲＯＣＨ\n       ＢＨＡＫＴＡＬ\n         III\n  III     I     III\n   I   I  I  I   I\n   IIIIII I IIIIII\n     I  II II  I\n     II  III  II\n      IIIIIIIII\n        IIIII\n        IIIII\n        I I I\n          `     '\n\n           [!]\nAn odd grimoire with tattered black leather\ncover sits in your hands. By the looks of it, it probably has something to do with magic, but the entirety of the book is written in an odd language that aches the head of those who can't read it.\n\nHazk,\nmerin'gnu vegaati zu'nokion. \n\nRe'nokion talsh vokarl\nya'pelosr therthe'pelosr-bhaktalserthek-unkra zu'gathan.\n\nE\nOdurnur blothr zu'kraemsal\n\nDu\nPelosr'basular koneg\nqsuzph'dvemd\n\nDo'nekaro kuram savurr'zu bhakthal.\n\n[]  []  []  []  []  []  []\n\nKraemsal lerikah odurnur ubyz'fikt koneg vurrsht-chelion\nil do'jhorvastur \nsavurr'vegaati qsuzph'dvemd\n\naza uvot, do'varsku -\nO'ag'vokarl\n\nE\nDo'odurnur bhatti'dvemd\n\nDu\nDo'kree haurz qsuzph\nkon kreoz'bhaktal\n\n           [!]\n  Pictures have been\n  drawn alongside the\n  instruction.\n\n            [!]\nThe first picture seems to have an odd lump of rock.\n\nIn the second one, some sort of hollow figure has been molded from the ore.\n\nVe\nDo'kree thur'hadan\nfhi al'kraemsal\n\n   o  -->  ö\n   O        []/\n\neg zmask, a'kyoni Kha.\n\nCul\npelosr'basular koneg'qsuzph\n\nZin\nDo'infinst qsuzph egodar burz'fhi yatha\n\n\n     Undere dayn!\n\nqsuzph lerikah ezg saiz undere aldunr lerikah al'kraemsal.\n    ö \n  \\[] -> ,;     ✔\n\n            [!]\nAnother set of pictures are on the side. In the first, the figure is made to resemble a kharajyr.\n\nIn the second one, the kharajyr shrinks considerably in size.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n             ☬\n\n\n\n\n\n                   -1496\n                   - Z.C.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fi'hiiran'tanya", "Toodles", "Fi'hiiran'tanya\nOriginally written by\nValia'laure Faeifeth\n\nTranscribed for the Library of Dragur by\nRevion M. Tathron\n\nThe following is a transcript of a book found in the ruins of a house in Celein.\n\nThe Smile of Larihei Heals the Mind Like Milk Heals the Body.\nThe Lifting- Sacrifice\n\nThe Ritual of the Lifting is different from that of Untempered Fi, for it is the stringent conditions which make for the true, Tempered Fi's creation.\n\nThe ritual of the Elibar'acal follows, and yet it is sufficient but not necessary to create a Tempered soul.\n\nThe sacrifice is tied to the Altar, imbued with the magic of Fi. The room is lit only by the light of a Fi' orb in a specially made lamp.\n\nGold dust is scattered upon the sacrifice as the following is read. Each in attendance may bless themselves as they so desire.\n\n<Transcriber's note:\n\nBoth the Elvish and common versions of the Ritual have been removed, to deter those who seek to practice this vile art.>\n\n<Basically, it detailed how the Golden Owl is saving everyone from monsters. It wasn't worth reading, believe me.>\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nMilk is passed between those in attendance in a Silver Chalice. It is drunk by each in turn, symbolising they are worthy of the Milk of Larihei, and therefore her smile.\n\n\n\nYour body unfit for the milk, Your mind unfit for the smile of Larihei, \nYour very essence forfeit.\n\nThe Milk is refused to the sacrifice, symbolising they are unworthy of it. A blade imbued with Fi' energy (read: Fi'chant, just as the altar is)\n\nis used to cut the sacrifice's throat and as this is done droplets of blue will pool on the blade's tip.\n\nBlood is collected in a clay pot. The droplets will spin and form a blue light which will become stable (PK)\n\nor will explode in a flash of light (no PK, soul escapes). It is required an orb be present to power both the altar and the blade.\n\nFi'hiiran'seth\n\nThis subtype of the magic focuses on the negation of Arcane Magic. Whether Evocation, Conjuration, Illusion, Runes, or Alteration, if can either send a forming spell back to the void or eat away at a created spell.\n\nThe magic will also steal the aura needed for Shade magic, but has no affect on existing tendrils.\n\nFi'hiiran'acaele\n\nThe second subtype of the magic can stop all Deity Magic. (For example: Clerical, Druidism, Shamanism, Monk, Muun'Trivazja, and Ascended). Unlike its brother subtype, which funnels mana away into the void,\n\nFi'hiiran'acaele disrupts a connection, interfering with someone's ability to connect with their chosen deity. This can be small, when they cast a spell, or large, severing a connection for a time.\n\nStrangely, neither Fi'hiiran'acaele or Fi'hiiran'seth affect Necromancy.\n\nThe mage must be a first-time magic user, never having connected to anything, Deity, Void, or otherwise.\n\nThe mage must be of good condition. Fi'hiiran'tanya corrupts the body twice as much as a normal magic, and the mage's increased metabolism may wither them away without proper care.\n\nThe mage must perform the Ritual.\n\nThis Ritual, developed by the Elibar'acals, is the source of the mage's power. They much find a sacrifice (a character willing to be permanently killed) that they know well, and kill them on the altar.\n\nIt is in this moment, when the soul is leaving, that the mage will connect to the Void for the first time. The soul will be returning to The Cloud Temple,\n\nand the mage will grab it, trapping it in a state of Limbo. A state of half-death, forever caught in the mage's grasp. The soul will become a tool,\n\nand will eventually forget its old self, becoming more and more compliant. There is a small chance, in the beginning years, that the soul will attempt to wrest control, though no soul has ever gained full control.\n\nPhysical and mental strain\nLoss of weight and muscle mass\nIncredibly realistic lucid dreams and nightmares, leading to a confusion on what is real and what is imagined.\n\nEnchanted areas will leave a Fi'hiiran'tanya user fatigued if they stay in there for too long a time period.\nProblems with breathing, blood loss, internal bleeding, and the rate at which wounds heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hallowed Umbrage", "Geoboy66", "I write the following epitaph with dire haste so much so that the winds part ways my words.\n\nMy account of these events may not be entirely accurate,§  something completely acceptable under the maddening, fear stricken haze that I have been left in.\n\nI sit here now quill in hand, wounded with a gash so dreadfully dark that I'm not sure if it really is a wound at all.  I have become a well of life, bountiful as the succulent navy mists ooze out of this growth, this... anchor; ever so dark and dreadful.\n\nMy pilgrimmage to this place hath cost me the trust and faith of my only friends as despite every loud, nagging warning against venturing here, my back was turned and my hands covered my ears.\n\nIt is the weakness of Man to succumb to the allure of power, riches and knowledge that of which the Abyss is said to contain. Trust me when I say that the power hidden away here is done so for a reason and should never belong to any mortal man.\n\nFor were the corrupting mind of Man ever to wrap their greedy fingers around such incomprehensible things, it would mean our doom.  The Trolls Harpies and Gryphons of our world pale in comparison to the horror of the deep, dark beyond.\n\nLegends tell of the Abyss as the ruins of Aegis, a land from which Man's forefathers hailed.\nI would hesitate to call the state in which the Gods left the motherland in a ruin, for truly there remains little left here at all.\n\nFor this Abyss, this endless chasm to which there seems no end is both the catastrophic ashes of a world once living and breathing as well as a prison for every lost soul that the world sunk with it. North, South, East, West - it all leads to despair.\n\nI hath deviated from the guiding compass to venture in a new direction; downward.\nFor I suspected that within the bowels of this crushing nightmare there must be both a ceiling and a floor.  I, a pawn controlled by adventurous urges, took a fatal dive.\n\nMy sense of time has long since fled, abandoning me like many other luxuries that once made me whole.  After a measurement of time far longer than any measurement of time I've ever thought to measure, I reached the feared and fabled end of this void.\n\nI dare not write about the countless demons that scour the ebon plane despite the insanity they so passively inflict.  They do not deserve the honour of being referenced alongside the Lord of the deep, dark below.  Darkness Incarnate.\n\nAs my wailing, shedding flesh forced itself through the dense acidic atmosphere, my feet began to fail me.  Time hath come to truly give up, and turn back I thought.  Yet my thoughts were ruptured by a presence so overwhelming that I could not think.\n\nAs I fought with myself to open my eyes I stared upon what could only be described as a living shadow, embodying umbral hellfire frigid enough to lock my very bones in place.\nRadiating in darkness so hollow that the Abyss stood brightly aflame beside him.\n\nHe worse armour, the first sign that this impossible creation was indeed Man.  Ancient was his armour, charred and blackened from what I cannot begin to imagine.  Yet his armour, heavy as it appeared did not hinder him.\n\nHis form suddenly shifted all at once, phasing out at one place and in again at another.  The realm was at his whim, as he did not simply move through it, but had become it.  Now, the Dark Lord towered above me, reeking of ash and death.\n\nAll past experiences seem like a petty joke when compared to the awesome perspective I had been blessed with. This Man, whose blood red eyes pierced through the very veil of the Abyss had drawn forth his weapon.  A terrible greatsword, massive in size.\n\nDripping with the howling souls of the damned.  This blade, serrated like the peak of Mount Ire was shoved into my heart, slotting into my flesh like a key within a door.  In the seconds before my consciousness faded I heard something.  I heard a voice.\n\nA voice that would rival a Dragon.  It was then that I knew for certain - This was the Old Lord of Umbrage, King of the Abyss.  One whose name does not touch the lips of the living, and whose sight is known only to the dead and the mad.\n\nHis perverted shriek defiled every corner of the Abyss, his siren call summoning the dark to his side.  As the black visage of the Old Lord faded from my sight, I heard his words.\n\n      R A D I A N T\n I S  T H E  B L A C K\n         S  U  N", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I was planning to murder someone......", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Today is so nice day I wish I could see the weather like this everyday when I wake uo and see the outside through the window.§0\n§0\n§0Do you know why I like to see the weather like blue sky and not much cloud on it? It because it makes my mind clear as snow\n\nI am Franz, the  son of man who worked as architect in Empire of Oren. I used to design a house like him but now I am working as a guard of Courland. I think it's kind of good work, The king of courland is better than emperor.\n\nI wish I could live in Half-ling's town once.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0      Ravondir's§0\n§0              Artifacts§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0             [!]§0\n§0A drawing of a spear, sword, and staff rest here.\n\n  The Sunken Spear        of Feelings§0\n§0\n§0This spear looks like a regular spear, but has a great impact on Descendants. It can bring up feelings of your significant other from long past or recently. It saps\n\nyour strength, and replaces it with despair. You cannot move, except for all of the sobbing you will do.§0\n§0Do not touch it with your bare skin, or you shall feel the true pain of love.§0\n§0-------------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru III", "§bMarch Ash", "On the mountaintop, the stone beneath my feet, I see kilometers of frozen wastes all around me. The wind bites at my skin. The cold helps me to concentrate on my mission. To change the descendants, or destroy them utterly. It is harsh.\n\nBut, they have the choice to die, and that is mercy.", ""),
        StaticBook("B. Winthrop", "§bJames Norrington I", "Issued by Steward James Norrington I of the Imperial Administration, given to Benedict Winthrop, whom is a Class C1 Citizen, on the 10th of Amber Cold, 1588. This passport is legal tender until 10th of Amber Cold, 1598.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0                       -->\n\nIf found, please return to the Imperial Administration in Johannesburg.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Signed: Benedict Winthrop§0\n§0\n§0Confirmed by: Steward James Norrington I.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Lightning is a form of rapid energy that is discharged and released from clouds. It moves in a non linier fashion, often shifting until it reaches its target. Lightning through its shifting motion can be directed or conducted towards both water and metals\n\nThis perticular element strikes at incrediable speeds and is extremely hot when it makes contact. Its speed also gives it a quick impressive ammount of force that can knock a man off his feet. Electricity ranges from a simple spark to lightning itself.", ""),
        StaticBook("30 Strictures", "§bYpres Signus", "Stricture 1: One must never find joy in the death of any man, woman, or child. §0\n§0\n§0Stricture 2: It is right for one to be bound in matrimony as to create lifemates, but one must never force such a sacred act on another\n\nStricture 3: One must never make love outside of marriage.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 4: One must restrict themselves from gluttony and drunkenness.\n\nStricture 5: One must restrict themselves from un-marital lust and intercourse.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 6: One must restrict themselves from taking what is not theirs.\n\nStricture 7: One must restrict their tounge from lashing words, for words are made to build up, not harm.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 8: One must restrict themselves from needlessly striking out against someone.§0\n§0\n\nStricture 9: One must not allow one's lust for revenge overtake them. Just retribution may be needed, but vengeance is reserved for the Gods.§0\n§0\n\n §0\n§0Stricture 10: One must not deceive or harm one another with words.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 11: One must not abandon those whom trust one for support.§0\n\nStricture 12: One must allow their hearts to not be apathetic to their brother's burdens.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 13: One must respect their family, for they're of same blood.§0\n\nStricture 14: One must not show hatred to anyone due to their race, their age, or gender.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 15: One must restrict from the use of substances which muffle and cloud the emotions as to use to deal with their pain.§0\n\nStricture 16: One must support all whom are widowed, lame, or otherwise unable to support themselves.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 17: One must not harm any man, or woman without the cause of just retribution.\n\nStricture 18: One must be submit under the discernment of others as to have a understanding of what is brought by justice, and what is brought by anger.\n\nStricture 19: One must keep themselves accountable to their spouses. And likewise hold their spouses accountable.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 20: One must not allow one's anger to provoke trouble, and pain.\n\nStricture 21: One must allow themselves to be counted as equal unless proven otherwise by content of character.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 22: One must not challenge or disobey those whom are appointed to authority.\n\nStricture 23: One must find mercy within themselves to be patient with the mistakes of others.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 24: One must find joy in whatever he has, whether little, or great.\n\nStricture 25: One must find the purest of joys from their spouse.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 26: It is in due right, and in way of nature that those bound in marriage should enjoy the privileges of sexual intercourse and relations. Yet,-\n\n it is to be kept between the 2 lifemates, not extending to others and creating such things as orgies or brothels, for they are detestable and disgusting.§0\n\nStricture 27: One must support and nurture their spouse as they would themselves.§0\n§0\n§0Stricture 28: One must love their spouse more than any worldly thing, or person.§0\n\nStricture 29: One must not hide their true nature from their spouse. For it is the true nature of lifemates that must be bound together.\n\nStricture 30: One must honor and follow the strictures if they wish to live a pure life, contented, and compassionately.\n\nPersonal copy of Avayla Winterleaf, mate to Aeran Winterleaf.§0\n§0\n§0May mercy and forgiveness be despensed to her in bountiful qualities, so that she herself may give others forgiveness and mercy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru IX", "§bMarch Ash", "In salt and ice eternal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls -II", "§bJacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Horen\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Amber Cold, 1471.\n\nUse these words as a source of strength and widom.\n\nThe years passed and went on and on, as time is wont to do. The Decendant, after being cursed by the Great Devil, adapted their lives to suit their new roles. There was, for some time, peace and prosperity amongst the original realms created by the\n\nCreator. One day, upon the cusp of which a red sun rose from the east, King Horen of humanity was approached by an Aengul, a divine messenger of God. This Aengul shone magnificently, illuminated by the light of God, its shades and colours twisting\n\naround one another as it addressed Horen. Its wings swathed in blinding white, it opened its mouth and through it the Creator spoke.\n“Horen of Man. God has chosen you as his divine prophet, as his mouthpiece on this world, until the day of\n\nyour ascent into the Seven Skies at his order. You are the almighty king, the Creator’s chiefmost servant on this hallowed earth. Be jubilant, for you are second to none but me! Humanity is the holy divine being of God, the human body remaining the most\n\nunadulterated, original form of the Creator’s design, not possessing of neither corruption nor mutation. You are the chosen people, and you shall carry out my commands, and your people alone, not your brothers and their kin, shall swear to my commandments\n\nThey are as follows!\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the Creator and Guide of everything that has been created; He alone has made, does make, and will make all things.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Divine\n\nare the Creator’s regents in this realm and that their obedience is worship to the Creator.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Aenguls and Daemons are the Creator’s servants.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator\n\nBlessed be His Name, is One, and that there is no unity in any manner like His, and that He alone is our God, who was, and is, and will be.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, has no body, and that He is free from all\n\nproperties of matter, and that there can be no comparison to Him whatsoever.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the first and the last.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name,\n\nand to Him alone, it is right to pray, and that it is not right to pray to any being besides Him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that all the words of the Divines are true.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the\n\nprophecy of Horen I our teacher, blessings be upon him, was true, and that he was the chief of the Divines, both those who preceded him and those who followed him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the entire scrolls that is now in our possession is the\n\nsame that was given to our Divines, blessings be upon them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Holy Scrolls can not be corrupted\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, knows all the deeds\n\nof beings and all their thoughts.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, rewards those who keep His commandments and punishes those that transgress them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that there will\n\nbe a revival of the dead at the time when it shall please the Creator, Blessed be His Name, and His mentions shall be exalted for ever and ever.”\n\nAnd so Horen listened, and he repeated the Creator’s words, and he carried the word\n\nof the Creator to his people, who listened as he did. They kneeled before Horen, first of the Divine, and pledged the commandments and supremacy of humanity over all but God. The realmn of man rallied underneath the Regent of Heven, arming themselves and\n\nerecting great fortresses, beginning the golden age of the Horen dynasty. For truly, it was decreed that humanity was second to none but the Creator, and the chose people would carry out his command until the end of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alexander Augustowski§0\n§0William Silversteed§0\n§0Oliver Staunton", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn X", "§bMarch Ash", "It is amazing that not a kilometer from here the world has been consumed by the void, yet in this place nature has recovered. Despite all of Iblees' machinations, the resilience of nature is more powerful.\n\nSo long as a single glade survives, the world might recover. I hope the Aspects are patient enough.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Azdrazi", "§bIcarus Adil", "The Azdrazi\n\n        Haelun'or,\n           Axios\n\n     Published 1592\n\n\n\n     by Icarus Adil\n\nThe Azdrazi\n===================   The Azdrazi are an odd creature, draconic in nature, which have recently returned to some prominence in the land of Axios. Upon their head are long, brown horns, and their skin is unmistakably scaly. Their eyes are ora\n\nand serpentine, their pupils slitted, long and thin. They can retract these fearsome features to a certain extent, though not all choose to. At a glance, the Azdrazi are monsters, and will likely strike fear in the hearts of those who see them.\n\nFortunately, this is false.\n   In this work, it is my hope to spread understanding regarding the Azdrazi, for these misgivings not only pose undue risks to their well-being, yet also hamper them in pursuit of their noble task. The Azdrazi should not be\n\nregarded as monstrosities of evil, or as ne'er do wells of any sort. Instead, they should be treated as neutral creatures pursuant of a righteous task, as I shall explain below.\n   To begin, one must look to the history of the Azdrazi, for their existe\n\npredates most of our own. The creatures first emerged during the Great War, borne with the sole intent of stopping the darkness of the Betrayer Iblees. Much of their history has been lost to time or otherwise destroyed, but it is known that the current\n\niteration of Azdrazi stem from the line formed by Azdromoth, prior to his present affliction.\n   The current brood of Azdrazi began with the stirring of one known as Alistair, the child of Azdromoth, and father of the remaining Azdrazi, at least as far\n\nas is currently known. He returned and began to create other Azdrazi, though the method of doing so is still unknown. Unfortunately, it was not until after this began that they learnt of Azdromoth’s descent to existence as a Drakaar, a fate most Dragaar\n\nescape by confining themselves to stone.\n   With this knowledge, the Azdrazi have severed ties with their progenitor, instead pursuing the goals their very existence is predicated upon. They exist to protect man against the forces of darkness, and\n\nhope to one day find a cure for the blight which affects their father and grandfather, Azdromoth the Arch-Drakaar.\n   Though these creatures have found conflict against the Paladins of Xan, as is natural giving their order's aversion to the dragonkin,\n\nwould seem a truce may be found. The disciples in the Cult of Azdromoth also combat the Azdrazi, as is natural for those who worship the Arch-Drakaar in its present form. Yet beyond this, the Azdrazi hold no conflict with man, and should indeed be treated\n\nin accordance to their intentions: to protect man against the dark.\n   In conclusion, I encourage all who find themselves in the presence of Azdrazi not only to stay any hostility based on assumptions of their aesthetic, yet also to thank them for thei\n\nservice to the realm of mortality. It seems that we all owe them our appreciation, and they are yet to find it.\n\nNotes\n===================\n\nThe information for this piece was gathered through the author's interview of Mister Suldaeroth and Mister Favnir, two Azdrazi who freely gave information regarding their existence. Their support of\n\nintellectual pursuit will not go unforgotten, so long as the information they have offered does not prove false. If you see them, thank them for their service both through this tome, yet also against those who promote darkness in our realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul IV", "§bMarch Ash", "It can take ten thousand years for a stream to carve a new valley. But it will still do so, it has an endless resolve. It is difficult to truly grasp the immensity of generational time, let alone geological time.\n\nNot even in the histories of a hundred families will the mountains grow a meter, but they will still grow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Blanket:§0\n§0-Flammable §0\n§0-Tweed knit§0\n§0-Sage green leaf dye§0\n§0-Seventy two degrees§0\n§0-Flexible solid§0\n§0-Shatters at negative one hundred and one degrees.\n\nSoil Pot:§0\n§0-Bisqueware§0\n§0-Baked clay§0\n§0-Oak bark stain§0\n§0-Eighty one degrees§0\n§0-Brittle on edges§0\n§0-Shatters at negative one hundred and ninty degrees.\n\nStool:§0\n§0-Flammable§0\n§0-Willow wood, spotted grain§0\n§0-Emerald green stain§0\n§0-Worn seat§0\n§0-Shatters at negative one hundred and ninty degrees.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Sarrion, First Enchanter of the Enchantry.§0\n§0\n§0\"Are you familiar with the concept of Voidal Horrors?\"§0\n§0>I've never delved into the study of horrors as Crumena or Avenel had, Cognats. The most I know is that they're monsters from\n\nthe unknown. I've never personally met one.§0\n§0\n§0\"Would you like to?\"§0\n§0>No. I like my humanity. §0\n§0\n§0\"Is Crumena, the senior, alive?\"§0\n§0>No idea.§0\n§0\n§0\"Are you acquainted with the junior?\"\n\n>No, I don't believe so. §0\n§0\"Are you versed in the likes of mental magic?\"§0\n§0>I am.§0\n§0\n§0\"When you penetrate a mind, does it appear as a proverbial plane?\"§0\n§0>It depends on the mind, most can be described as a plane with many doors to wander\n\nthrough and explore vast memories.§0\n§0\n§0\"Have you ever encountered entities with anomalous minds?\" >Yes.§0\n§0\n§0\"Can you describe your encounter?\"§0\n§0>It's odd to say. They can be more broken than others and some even have direct\n\ncontrol where they can cause you pain if they wished. It is their mind, you are the guest.§0\n§0\n§0\"Would you be interested in attempting to peer into a Horror's mind?\"§0\n§0>No, not at all. Curiousity kills the cat, the mage, his humanity.\n\n\"You took to the Voidbinder, no?\"§0\n§0>Yes, I did.§0\n§0\n§0\"Given the power and the mind to host it, do you believe an inner plane could materialize?\"§0\n§0>Perhaps, it's definitely possible.\n\n\"Regarding the likes of translocational locomotion and movement between space, how might you think -- in theory -- one may enter a concrete plane?\"§0\n§0>Indefinitely, I honestly believe there are doors to different planes and realms that were once forged\n\nand forgotten that we may stumble upon now. There are many possibilities in this field, it is hard to say. §0\n§0\n§0\"Have you heard of Arcane Displacement?\" >I am one of the main practioners of it. The Enchantry was the first place to utilize such a feat.\n\n\"With your knowedge in the talent, do you believe mental magic and Displacement may meld to allow movement into concrete minds?\"§0\n§0>Honestly? Yes, it may be able to.§0\n§0\n§0\"Can you describe the basic usage of a Displacement warp?\"\n\n>You may two doors weaved with an identical pattern into its charm. You can activate the portal with a passphrase and move to and fro. In a very simplified way of speaking.§0\n§0\n§0-Uldrivt Xivilas questioning Sarrion Zytiaear.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades", "§bTriplewing", "------Shades--------------------------  I     I         I    I\n II   II    I   II    II\n  III III  II  II   III\n   II  II II    II II\n    III III  III III  II\n   IIIIIII  III  IIIIII\n     IIIIII I I IIIIII\n     IIIIIIIIIIIIIIII§\n\nIn the time of Aegis, a\npale and apparently evil man lived by the name of Lucas Black,\nhe acted as the leading figure of the Shades. Capable of such feats as corrupting apprentice\nof the archmage into the state known as shade. He is not where t\n\nbegan from, but he is one of the most notable people to be a shade.\n\nThese people known as shades are often deemed evil, but is that\ntruly the case? Many seem to think that the\nshades have vanished,\nand that they have.. but rumours spread\n\nShades are capable\nof performing an apparent former form\nof Arcane Magicks; the      Shade Magic\n-------------------Shade Magic is magic\nthat seemingly draws it's power from a gem.\nIt's often simply called 'tendrils' since that's what r\n\nmagic. The Shade Gem, where the shades would draw their power to perform the magic from, is very powerful, but rumours say that the gem was broken. Actually.. when it was found, it wasn't active, but it was re-activated by an Archmage.. but somehow it's\n\nstill broken. The shades can't use the\nmagic unless it's activated, apparently.\nChances are that it's\njust made up though.\nThe magic in action looks like black tendrils, a bit like squids tentacles. Their\nmagic is destructive, and corru\n\nsomething to seek for.\n    Some say the Shade Magic is blessed by Iblees, and therefore truly unholy. Known shades are very few though; \nIn Aegis, Lucas Black\nwas known to be one.\nIn Asulon, Salamandra\nwas known to be one.\nThey have\n\nor very subtle in their actions in Anthos thus far, but I've heard that a man named Adorellan is one.\n  If the Gem is currently broken, this\nman I mentioned can somehow still use the tendrils.. or maybe it's\nnot broken. The Shade\nGem on the\n\nlooks like this:\n-------------------             [!]\nThe page has a detailed but quite\nsmall illustration of\nthe gem. Depicted\nfrom an upwards\nperspective.\n-------------------\n\nThe Shades are truly\na faction shrouded in mystery, but atleast I could reveal some of them.\n-------------------        Ein Sarard\n       ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n   1st of Deep Cold\n   ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n  Schattenburg, 1453", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Symbols", "§bSarrion", "Alchemy Basic's\nSub Volume I\nSymbols\n\nBy: An unknown alchemist of the alchemist guild.\n\nRe-written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\n\nDuring my times as a student, I was very skeptical of most of the theory of alchemy. One of the things I could not understand was the need for Symbols. If the representation and properties of a reagent are what is used,\n\nthe elements they fit in are not necessary to be stated. After a few years of becoming an alchemist I finally realised the purpose, it is because not only do ingredients have perfect representations, but the sibling representations are as well\n\nnecessary to create proper results. Perfect representations would never be able to be properly used and leveled, and no reagent has only one representation. For such, attaching a symbol to an ingredient\n\nfits far better than attaching only the representations. By choosing the representation or symbol you can decide the properties of what you create. One could use the representation of life for healing potions, but depending if it’s an\n\nearth symbol or a water symbol, it will have other smaller scale representations that will distinguish them. A water symbol will provide a more smooth and fluent healing rate, making the wound heal nicely, and the earth symbol will\n\ngive more strength and resilience to the healing process, perhaps making it hard to get the wound reopen. Everything fits into at least one of the four symbols or elements of alchemy, Fire, Water, Earth and Air.\n\nThe way you look at what a symbol represents is looking at the element in question and assessing what properties it has and what it is associated with. You do not look exactly at what the element is, assessing a symbol to a reagent is\n\n more about symbolism than pure correct connection. It’s to aid the alchemist design and investigate the ways of alchemy in a more practical way, without having to reach so fully into the details. Each ingredient or reagent may\n\n also be of different strengths depending on the properties and rarity it holds. Those which are rarer have a greater value than those which are common, and as such they are have as well more strength of use in alchemy.\n\nAn ingredient may be a Weak, Moderate or Strong symbol, those of greater strength required quite more skilled hands, but the payoff might be quite better.\n\n=[Fire]=\n->Starting with the more easily explainable one, fire is the symbol very used by alchemists that focus themselves on improving skills of fighting and giving new arsenal to use in wars. While I don’t find myself using many fire symbols,\n\n they are an absolute in the making of many of the truly fantastic deeds of alchemy. Most of the representations of fire are quite easy to grasp, because they fit perfectly onto what fire truly is. It may represent heat, burning, consumption,\n\ndestruction, warmth, power and chaos. Most of these have as such a great use for damaging others or to give power to oneself or others. Alchemist fire for example, is a great demonstration of what could be done with the use of fire symbols,\n\nfire in a bottle. Devastating and powerful, it is most likely the most dangerous conception that an alchemist can create. The representation of chaos is one more confusing, one that may bring unknown results as controlling chaos is quite\n\nhard job to have. Fire does have another way you may look at it, as many poets might say, “the flames of passion ran deep in his heart, but he acted as in a burning rage.” Fire may also represent emotions, both those\n\nof anger, regret, rage, confusion, and those of love, passion, confidence. These representation are especially useful in potions to improve oneself, and in poisons to bring damage emotionally to others. The mythical love potion though, is one that is\n\nby experience impossible to have in full effect, as love is in it’s own way subjective, and varies from person to person. The closest thing that may be created is one that gives well being and peace of mind, or ecstasy.\n\nMost of those are considered drugs.\nAs for the properties one may find generally in fire symbols, the idea of heat is normally present in them. A flower or plant that is warm to the touch could be a good indicator of a fire symbol.\n\nThe effects it might bring to a person might be associated that way as well, such as becoming feverish, or feeling a burning itchy sensation on touch. And of course the flavour of many of them, which I don’t really advise\n\nto be a way to figure out what kind of symbol it is, is most of the times spicy and strong, sometimes sweet as it goes well with raising emotions.\n\n=[Water]=\n->Sometimes even said to be the base ingredients, a symbol of water is essential to all potions and oils that alchemy can create. This is of course due to it’s liquid and coherent state, or it would not be a potion or oil. The base is the main\n\ncomponent of a potion, where all other reagents are added and mixed in. It is important to refer that it is considered a base only to the creation of potions and oils, but in the other more exotic fields of alchemy, they are not used as such.\n\nNormal water is the most simple of bases to use, not very useful for any powerful potion, as it’s not all that pure, it’s used mainly in minor potions. Distilling it would purify it and make it far more useful in lesser potions.\n\nThe purest form for a base you can find, is aqua vitae. Aqua vitae can also be called Alcohol, or distilled alcohol, it is simply the result of distilling brews such as ale, wine or any other intoxicating beverages.\n\nWith it, the most powerful of potions can be created. The other base one could use is lard, which is used only in the creation of oils.\nNow onto the representations that define a symbol of water. Like when you imagine\n\na stream of water, you imagine calmness, fluidity, peace, order and balance of nature. Continuing with the balance of nature, you have to understand that water is one of the fundamentals of life, and as such, water represents many parts\n\nof it. Life, regrowth, rebirth are the most important of representations, making water symbols sometimes the most important in healing potions, and antidotes. Tasting a water symbol normally brings the other representations that water might have,\n\nfreshness and a minty flavour are normally what you get from safe to eat water symbols, even going so far sometimes descending into cold and ice, another two representations of water. Do not think that just because water symbols\n\nmay represents life and are used in a lot of healing potions that they’re safe to eat, even water symbols might be essential to the creation of poisons, as a stream may be a thought of life and balance,\n\nbut a strong river might be the location of one’s death.\n\n=[Earth]=\n->While the water symbol is considered the base for potion making, I consider earth symbols the bases for other more advanced sections of alchemy, such as Transmutation and the creation of Chimeras. Such is because while potions need\n\nto be fluid and in a liquid state, transmutation is performed mostly on objects, and the creation of chimeras requires great representations of life and connectivity if one is ever to be created. More of the advanced alchemy will be left for another book,\n\nbut I wanted to leave the idea that the selection of a base is not randomly selected but adapts itself to what the alchemist wishes to create. The earth symbols concentrate themselves more on solids and life.\n\nTo better understand the symbol, one must think of the two greatest visualisations one thinks about when the idea of earth comes to mind. Those two visualisations are the rock, and dirt. Such have the representations that will fit with all of the symbols\n\nof earth. A rock is resilient, hard to break and strong. It’s used a lot in buildings creating structure and protection, and all these characteristics are representations of the symbol. A rock may also be associated with minerals and metals, two\n\nrepresentations very much sought out in transmutation. Once one thinks of dirt on the other hand, he does not receive the same thoughts as when with a stone. Dirt is different, dirt is used mostly for the growth of plants, the propagation of life.\n\n This is the second part of the symbol of Earth, one that might not be the most easily noticeable. It represents life, regrowth, rebirth and connection. Plants grow in it, and animals life over it, feeding of the plants, and so fauna and flora are\n\nas well the last representations of earth, making them the most suitable for the creation of chimeras.\nI do not advise trying to eat any type of Earth symbol. While it may represent life as well, it leans more for survival of life, than saving of it.\n\nThis means that normally earth symbols are not suitable for eating, either having extremely bitter tastes, or being straight up poisonous.\n\n=[Air]=\n->The symbol of air is perhaps the hardest to explain in all of the symbols. When one tries to imagine air, he may think of the wind, or of what he breaths, perhaps of smoke. What could one bring from those? These are quite simply almost\n\n impossible to see, you can not see air, you can not see wind, you feel the wind and hear it’s sound, and you breath the air. One of the first representations to speak of would be of perception, without air you would not be able to see\n\nbut it comes from that fact that you do not see air, yet know it’s there, and percy the effects of it. The rest of the representations are around the idea of speed and quickness. Perhaps a thought we all have when we imagine speed,\n\nwe can think of the movements in the air, the fast animals traveling through the air and ground almost provoking a wind in itself. Not the best way to explain it, as those images are quite hard to have. Of the most easy representations to think about,\n\nyou may think of fight and travel, and for such you only need to think of a bird. The palate one gets on these symbols are normally quite bland. Having almost no taste, no aroma, almost like the normal air in the mountains.\n\nA last mention on air symbols, is always it’s representations of fragility and grace. The ingredients of air are ones that in most cases are very thin and weak, easily broken and destroyed maybe simply by the moving of the hand near them.\n\nGrace is a representation I adore to use in potions of healing, and oils of well being, because they bring the condition of the skin to a more natural and graceful way. Yet I consider them hardest symbols to use,\n\nas the harvesting of the ingredients, the handling and the storage has to be extremely precise.\n===================End.\n\nLook for:\nAlchemy Volumes I, II, III.\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Water Element Herbs:§0\n§0Mandragora: Found under lilypads§0\n§0Represents life, rebirth, rejuvenation§0\n§0\n§0Serpents Stalk: Reedike plants next to bodies of water§0\n§0Represents life, calmness, fluidity, rebirth§0\n§0\n\nFrost Vine: Vines found in snowy, cold biomes.§0\n§0Represents life, calmness, ice§0\n§0\n§0Blissfoil: blue flowers found in tall grasses in dry biomes§0\n§0Represents calmness, apathy, peace§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n\nAthin: Blue algae found on ice or in icy waters§0\n§0Represents freezing, life, ice, balance\n\nFire Element Herbs:§0\n§0Crimson Vase: Found in tall grasses and next to red flowers in dry biomes§0\n§0Represents heat, warmth, love§0\n§0\n§0Drakes Tail: In shrubs in savannas and deserts§0\n§0Represents heat, destruction, chaos\n\nDwarf's Pumpkin: Orange shrub found in swamplands§0\n§0Represents envy, bitterness, power, strength§0\n§0\n§0Blood Lotus: Red flowers grown on vines in deserts and savannas§0\n§0Represents courage, hope\n\nFlameroot Tongue: Red flowers found in forests§0\n§0Represents heat, anger, destruction\n\nAir Element Herbs:§0\n§0Larihei's Fingers: Found next to the roots of trees in cold and snowy biomes§0\n§0Represents beauty, steadiness, focus, swiftness.§s§0\n§0\n§0Elf's Hair Vine: Found on vines in snow biomes§0\n§0Represents speed, flight, travel, grace\n\nCrouching Feathers: Found next to roots of trees and bushes in forests§0\n§0Represents travel, grace, beauty§0\n§0\n§0Halflings Grass: Found next to roots in forests.§0\n§0Represents lifting, calm, joy\n\nEarth Element Herbs:§0\n§0Tippen's Root: A foul smelling root found near tree roots or shaded areas.§0\n§0Represents life", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§3§l§nEnchanting Glyphs§0\n§9§nEfficiency§0\n§1O§0XXXXXXXXX§0\n§0X§1OO§0XXXXXXX§0\n§1O§0XXXXXXXXX§0\n§0XXXXXXXXXX§0\n§0\n§9§nUnbreaking§0\n§1O§0X§1O§0XXXXXXX§0\n§0X§1O§0XXXXXXXX§0\n§1O§0X§1O§0XXXXXXX§0\n§0XXXXXXXXXX\n\n§9§nSharpness§0\n§0XX§1O§0XXXXXX§0\n§1OOOOOOOO§0X§0\n§1OOOOOOOOO§0\n§0XX§1O§0XXXXXX§0\n§0\n§9§nProtection§0\n§0X§1OOO§0X§1OOO§0X§0\n§0X§1OOOOOOO§0X§0\n§0XX§1OO§0X§1OO§0XX§0\n§0XXX§1OOO§0XXX\n\n§9§nThorns§0\n§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0\n§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0\n§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0\n§1O§0X§1O§x§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1O§0\n§0\n§9§nLooting§0\n§0X§1O§)§0XXXXX§1O§0X§0\n§1OOOOO§0X§1OOO§0\n§0X§1O§0XXXXX§1O§0X§0\n§0XXXXXXXXX\n\n§9§nFortune§0\n§1OO§0XXXXXXX§0\n§0XX§1O§0XXX§1O§0XX§0\n§0X§1O§0X§1O§0X§1OOO§0X§0\n§1O§0XX§1O§0XX§1O§0XX", ""),
        StaticBook("Liches.", "§bJakir Axem", "[ In eloquent writing the word Liches, is spelled out on the front cover of the book. The words striking and glowing a faint golden. Under it are the words. By Jakir Axem. It seems the writing glows brighter as you get closer to it. Inviting you in.]\n\n[What seems to be a man shrouded in black, and clad in a dark robe. Staring out at you, watching from under his hood. The hands of the man seem to be skeletal and he is flanked by two undead zombie like figures. The words under it.] \"A Lich.\"\n\n[For the rest of the book, the writing seems to return to normal black ink, with less time spent on the style of writing to help the reader to clearly see the writing and understand the lessons in the tome.]\n\nChapter one: Introduction.\n\nFor many years Liches have roamed the earth, we do not know where they first come from. But we do know they have been around for a very long time. I myself have killed a few, but they are not to be taken lightly.\n\nI was gifted with the power of gods, many who read this will not be, so I decided to make this guide so you may be able to fight them without the help of others. In this book you will find the information one might need as well as my own personal.\n\nexperience with these dark beings so you may better survive the next encounter you may have with them. It will only have the basic knowledge for we do not know it all, and do not wish others to try to copy in their dark arts.\n\nChapter two: The Lich.\n\nThe Lich is a creature made of dark magic, usually necromancy. At first they were thought  to of come from the dark power of Iblees. This is true, but those Liches are long passed, today Liches are made\n\nfrom necromancy and many a necromancer has tried to transcend into Lichdom. But you may wonder why there is not hundreds running around. It’s because the process is deadly and requires a lot of time and effort, and also the knowledge\n\non creation which has been lost to most. They use the power of necromancy to move a large portion of their life-force into an object referred to as a phylactery, this is their power supply, for it connects directly to the Lich in question.\n\nThe only problem being it could be hidden anywhere, so the permanent death of a Lich is unlikely but it also has a time it can live, due to the removal of life-force and the tether. The Lich will die in the end and it can’t stop it.\n\nChapter three: Combat.\n\nAs undead creatures, the main weakness of a Lich is gold. Gold is the bane of all known undead and as such. One should use golden weaponry over all else. Liches are unable to use necromancy due\n\nto the lost of most of their life-force and are also unable to access voidal or divine magic. But they are strong and smart. Bound to the will of the necromancer that created them but also free to do as they please otherwise.\n\nThey know fear and they will target the most dangerous person first. I myself have killed only a few, and they all have tried to kill me first. Only by me being ready was I able to stop them killing me and becoming their next victim.\n\nA few Liches are known for ranged weapons. Due to the lack of magic they use alchemy and bows. They are the cause of the Fringe Plague for it attacked me directly with a stronger version of the plague I was only just able to bat away in time.\n\nSome even wear armour, but they are made of bone and dead skin, so non golden or divine weapons are almost useless when fighting them. So be careful when facing them, they are not something one should take lightly and even more so if you are alone.\n\nChapter four: Personal experience \n\nI am a user of divine magic, and as such I have had to face them at their most deadly and worse. They tend to enlist the help of necromancers for extra help. As such I have\n\nI have had to fight the beasts of the necromancers and Liches. One being a monster made of young Mali children sewn together and made alive again with the vile magics. The lich that caused the Fringe Plague\n\nI had to remove after it infected most of Alras killing many and infecting many others. To which I had to remove the plague from. They are deadly creatures and some of the worst beings you can find, I hope you\n\nnever have to use the information found within this tome, for it is a true horror what these dark beasts will do to those who mealy get in it’s way, or if it feels like having fun.\n\nEpilogue: \n\nI Jakir Axem made this book to help others in fighting Liches, this book will no doubt be one of many, you can tell it is of my own design by the cover. . If it does not glow, then the book is just a copy.\n\nThank you for taking the time and reading this tome, I hope it helps you should the worse come to pass, and I hope that you never have to use it. This is part of the collection I shall be making on this subject,\n\nranging from as many dark beings I have come to fight, and find within the world. Thank you once again, and if we do meet out in the world, understand that what I do, I did by choice, and that even if you do face these things\n\n, you can move on and you are not alone.\n\n[Once again the fancy writing returns, the small signature of Jakir Axem written in golden glowing ink pulsing lightly at the end of the book.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Magic & You", "§bNienna Calm", "Dark Magic\n      And You!\n-------------------  A Guard's Guide to\n  Identifying Dark \n          Mages\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\n\n      ForeWord\n-------------------This book was written with the intent to educate the guardmen and women of the Caliphate of Khalestine. However, should you find this book in your possession, I would suggest reading it anyways. It is a good\n\nguide for identifying Dark mages.\n\n     What is a\n    Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including Pacts with dark gods, Rituals set forth by\n\nIblees, and other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\n\n    Necromancy\n-------------------\nNecromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. It's age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\n\nthis world today. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state. Since Necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life, or reports of people feeling drained after\n\ntouching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\n\n   Frost Witches\n-------------------Frost Witches are monsters of Ice and Snow who disguise themselves as women and prey upon the libido of Men. The Frost Witch is an easy threat to counter in the hot weather of the Caliphate, but requires constant\n\nvigilance to identify. A Frost Witch's true form is bright blue, but using her curse's magic, she is able to take any form she pleases, so long as that form is female. Frost Witches use these disguises to trick men into a false sense of security,\n\nwhereupon they will take their true form, and devour the unsuspecting male.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe easiest way to identify a Frost Witch is by touching their skin. A frost witch's body temperature is colder than anything one could imagine.\n\nThere is no way for them to disguise this. Also, because of this impairment, any disguised frost Witch will show signs of great fatigue under the Caliphate sun. Any women demonstrating a severe aversion to high temperatures and regular food should have\n\nthe temperature of their skin checked immediately.\n\n       Shades\n-------------------\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, second personality that desires for only chaos and\n\ndestruction. Shades are capable of corrupting every form of Arcane magic, empowering their spells with the dark powers of Iblees himself.\n\nHow to Identify:\nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only\n\nrevealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air. Their ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of\n\nbeing a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics, and these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a Shade.\n\n Soul Puppeteers\n-------------------\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), They are able to bring sickness, pain, and even death to a\n\nperson from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\n\nHow to Identify:\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer\n\nstraight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies. If you suspect someone of Soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it's the\n\nonly way to confirm for sure.\n\n Soul Contractors\n-------------------Soul Contractors are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word. This would be potentially useful, if not for the material they must fashion these\n\ndocuments on. Soul Contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken whilst they were still alive. It is a brutal and horrifying process, that speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\n\nHow to Identify:\nLike Soul Puppeteers,\n\nit is hard to identify a Soul Contractor. The only way to tell for sure is to either catch them in the act, or discover their flaying equipment, which may not even be on their person.\n\n   Black-Dragon\n     Parasites\n-------------------A more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its hosts and causes\n\ncauses them to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how is parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you keep any suspected carrier of this foul creature far away from\n\none's person at all times. It is unknown at this time if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they be either expelled from the city on sight, or, in extreme cases, purged.\n\nHow to Identify:\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\n\nare easy to identify. All carriers of the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area. If you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full-body search immediately.\n\n General Warning\n    Signs Of A\n    Dark Mage\n-------------------\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general. These are by no means\n\ndeciding factors in a suspect's ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nBe Suspicious Of Any Persons you see that:\n\n-Wear Primarily Black Robes.\n\n-Are Hooded at all times\n\n-Possess bright red eyes.\n\n-Project a magical Aura that Black, Gray, or Red in color.\n\nAs a guard of the Caliphate, it is up to YOU to root out these psychopathic evildoers wherever they might rise their ugly heads. For the sake of our grand city, do your duty well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren History: I", "§bJacob Chapel", "History of Oren\n       Part I\n\n\nThis history has been collected by me, Jacob Chapel. Sources are various scrolls and texts and the museum of Petrus, beside common knowledge and tales. Enjoy.\n\n((Written by Pepernoot))\n\nIf you're interested in the history before Al'Khazar, I suggest you pick up the first part of the Holy Scrolls, the Nativities. If you're interested in the history past Siegmund Carrion's election, then you need to find part two of The History of Oren.\n\nThe days of Aegis\nThe history of Oren begins in Aegis, the land of the Descendants. To the west of the Cloud Temple laid its lands. The capital of Al’Khazar was surrounded by pastures, farmlands and forests, and to the north laid the snowy lands,\n\ncontaining cities and towns such as Alstion and Snowy Fields. In the south were the islands known as the Whisper Isles, surrounded by the calm waters of the Whisper Lake, and filled with fishermen and craftsmen such as glassblowers.\n\nThe first king was Horen himself. Many Kings ruled the Kingdom wisely after him, Kings such as Saint Daniel. The Kingdom’s grand city was built by this King Daniel in 1300. Eventually King Pampo Perea, Saint Daniel’s seneschal, took power, with Edmund\n\nSheffield as his seneschal.\nAs time passed the Undead became stronger and bolder in their attacks on the Kingdom. Snowy Fields fell and was razed, but soldiers from Alstion retook it and the town was rebuilt. This turned out to be futile eventually as\n\nthe northern towns fell one by one. Even King Perea himself was killed by the Undead, within the tall walls of Al’Khazar. Edmund Sheffield took his place, but was corrupted by the dark forces and turned to the Nether. His “abduction” was accompanied by a\n\ngreat siege of Al’Khazar, in which a portal to the Nether opened in the city square. After a great battle the City of Man was sacked. Human refugees poured across the Kingdom and the city of Galahar, built on the ruins of the old town of Kramoroe, was\n\nnamed capital.\n\nEdmund’s son Enor Sheffield took his place, but under his rule the situation worsened drastically, the corruption of his father and his own weakness led to great dissent in the Kingdom.\n\nMeanwhile Gaius Marius, Hochmeister of the Teutons had carved out a realm for himself to the east of the Kingdom, and had even participated in wars against Oren, allying with its enemies. It is important to note that even though the Undead threatened\n\nOren, and although Oren was the strong defence between the Undead and the rest of the races, this didn’t deter them to wage wars against the Kingdom. Infighting between the nations of Malinor, Krug, Urguan and Oren was common.\nRebellion brew in the\n\nKingdom, and in Galahar the Phoenix Rebellion formed. As the weak King Enor saw his position wasn’t tenable anymore he named Gaius Marius as King of Oren. This treason lead to the rise of the rebellion and a war between the part of Oren controlled by\n\nthe Teutons and the Phoenix Rebellion, led by Eze’kiel Tarus as the Phoenix King. Eventually the two sides reach an agreement, splitting the realm into two parts. The Kingdom of Renatus, ruled by King Tarus, and the Realm of Hanseti, ruled by Gaius.\n\nAfter giving up his crown the mad King Enor and his followers settled on an island, and together with Queen Dawn Perea, wife of the old King Perea he created the nation of Salvus.\nHumanity could not rest though, as the Undead continued their march\n\nrelentlessly. In 1349 Galahar was attacked by the forces of evil, but even though the attack was repelled, the city was evacuated for fears of Miasma. Eventually Aegis fell in 1351, and the humans fled through the portal to the verge,\n\nalong with the other Descendants. \n\nA new dawn in Asulon\nAfter a brief stay in The Verge, the Descendants settled in the new lands of Asulon. Oren was still divided into the three Kingdoms, and Renatus settled around their new capital of Arethor.\n\nIn these turbulent times a new human nation sprung up, the Kingdom of Seventis.\n\nWhen King Eze’kiel resigned from the throne, Renatus was ruled by the Regent King Reynard Lycian until Godfrey Horen appeared. Godfrey claimed direct decent from King Horen\n\nand quickly received support from the Dukes and other nobles of the realm. He consolidated power and strengthened the Kingdom, which was plagued by instability and attacks from the other nations.\n\nSoon after Godfrey started his reign a coalition against\n\nSalvus formed by The Kingdom of Seventis, Alras, the Orcs and most importantly what was called the Twilight Army. This coalition did not have official support from Renatus, but most of its nobles supported it. Opposing the coalition were Salvus itself,\n\nthe Dwarves of Urguan and the Realm of Hanseti. After the humiliating defeat, and the betrayal of Queen Dawn’s guards, which murdered her, Salvus was absorbed into Renatus.\n\nAs the great plague hit Asulon, the Kingdom of Seventis was hit most severely,\n\npresumably due to its location close to the Cloud Temple. Most of its inhabitants died, allowing for an absorption into the Kingdom of Renatus to protect the weakened towns.\n\nThe Teutons could not stand by idly as Renatus grew, and went to war against\n\nthe Kingdom. Swiftly the war turned against their favour, and it became clear that they were losing the war. To avoid destruction of his nation, Hochmeister Mirtok surrendered it to King Godfrey, saying the words “I will die for this nation, but I will\n\nnot let it die for me”.\n\nThe annexation of Hanseti meant the unification of humanity, and the Holy Oren Empire was formed. In the Empire the Crownlands, Salvus and Hanseti were ruled as separate kingdoms, with the Emperor presiding over the individual\n\nkings, while also being king of the crownlands.\n\nAfter a rebellion against the crown, House Tarus, House Elendil and House Norsem were shunned and fell out of favour in the Empire. Soon though, the lands of Asulon were submerged by floods,\n\nand a second flight was needed.\n\nAnthos, a land plagued by war\nJust as the flight from Aegis, the new land was not reached in one trip. There were stops at the isles of Elysium and Kalos. One notable thing in Kalos was the formation of the\n\nPhoenix Kingdom, by Eze’kiel Tarus. The kingdom was quickly destroyed, even before leaving for Anthos.\n\nIn Asulon the Teutonic Order was nigh destroyed by the Flays, and the Hochmeister killed. A few remnants of the Order made it to Anthos, albeit\n\nwithout a Hochmeister to guide them. The Teutons settled on the southern side of the ice wall of the North. Meanwhile the Empire of Oren settled a bit further south, with Abresi as their capital.\n\nSoon after arriving it turned out this land was not as\n\nsafe as the Descendants had hoped. North of the wall the Teutons discovered a savage race of boarmen and a land filled with dragons.\n\nThis was not the most pressing issue to Oren though, as the Empress of Oren was kidnapped by the Orcs, and a joint\n\nHuman and Dwarf force invaded their capital and massacred nearly every orc present.\n\nEver present Elven aggression led to a crusade against the Princedom of Malinor. The Order of the White Rose quickly destroyed their forces and burned the Malenorian\n\nfarms. The elves eventually surrendered to the siege, proving the enormous strength of a united Oren.\n\nUnited it would not be for long, as the Teutons rebelled. In the first battle, at Kralta, the Teutons were crushed. At the second battle the\n\nBlackmonts stood alone against the Teutons on the Iron Fields, outnumbered two to one. The Teutonic Order was victorious.\n\nThe civil war was decided at the Siege of the Dreadfort, where the Chivays, and the Carrions (then bannermen of the Blackmonts)\n\ndistinguished themselves. The defeat at the Battle of Iron fields had led to close cooperation between the White Roses and the Blackmonts, which turned out to be more than the Teutons could handle. Although the Dreadfort was severely damaged the siege\n\nwas broken and the Teutonic Order defeated. Soon afterwards the Teutonic Order was disbanded by Emperor Godfrey.\n\nThe Scourge, the name of the goatmen and the dragons from the north made their first move south beyond the wall, destroying the old\n\nTeutonic castle of Greywyn with flames, and taking it for their own.\n\nThen, in a huge shock to the empire, Emperor Godfrey died. He was succeeded by his son, Horen.\n\nAs the princedom of Malinor was absorbed into the Empire as\n\nprotectorate, the expansion of Oren led to great concern with the other races. They formed a coalition and in the War of Anthos they attacked Oren, putting a halt to the expansion. Most prominent in the coalition were the Dwarves, angered by the\n\nexecution of one of their Dwarven lords by nobles of Oren. In the Battle of the Crossroads the coalition was defeated though, by a brilliant Orenian flanking manoeuvre.\n\nIn 1415 the Empire was left in disarray as Emperor Horen left, along with his\n\nmost loyal houses. The dwarves used this weakness to form their Grand Kingdom of Urguan in the War of Asulon. They dissolved the Empire of Oren and many parts, including Salvus and Adunia swear loyalty to the dwarves as vassal states. What remains of the\n\nEmpire was renamed to the Holy Kingdom of Oren and ruled by William Horen. After more chaos and disarray many more little human states sprung up or seceded from the Kingdom, leading to the current prominent Houses, states and cultures. \n \nEventually the\n\nGrand King of Urguan, Thorin Grandaxe dies. This caused the human vassal states to be released from their oaths to the dwarves. This made way for a renewed unification. As King William was pushing his powers and support from his nobles to the limit,\n\nHouse Winter made a secret pact with Ruska. This forced King William to step down, giving control of Oren to his cousin Silus. This was only temporary, as the states of Salvus, Oren, Ruska and the new state of Herendul were confederated into an empire,\n\nwith an elective monarchy. At the election Siegmund Carrion was voted in as Emperor of Oren.\n\nThis concludes part one of Oren's history. The events after Siegmund Carrion's election, up to the first years in Athera will be discussed in part two.\n\n((So you made it to the end. I hope you liked it. You can leave a message to me on the forums, username: Pepernoot))", ""),
        StaticBook("Alc. Potions II", "§bSarrion", "Alchemy: Potions\nPart II\n-------------------Please read Part I.\n\n-Sarrion di' Pascali\n\n=[Potion of Smoke Whispers]=\nike in the magical stories where the hero throws something into the floor and a cloud of smoke is formed, this potion creates the same as the vial shatters. Creating black smoke which releases fast, it allows the\n\n thrower a distraction or the ability to temporarily incapacitate the adversaries. Brewed over the course of four weeks, this potion is literally smoke in a bottle, and like it, it creates irritation when breathing and to the eyes.\n\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Air Symbols (Flight, Transport)\n1 Fire Symbol (Combustion)\n\n=[Potion of Sleeping]=\nUsed by people of all kinds, this potion’s objective is placing someone to sleep. It might act fast, it might act slow, it might be to help with sleeping at night, or it might be to knock someone out. The use will dictate the power\n\n the potion has to be made. Minor potions will have more of a relaxing result, making resting far more easier to achieve. Lesser ones have to be drank, and soon after the potion will take effect and the one to drink it will not even\n\nnoticed he passed out. Greater potions on the other hand, might not even need to be drank, only smelled. This is particular good for doctors when needing to operate, as it does not force the patient to drink something.\n\n To force it on someone might not have some good results, as the potion does take it’s time to give it’s effect, enough to fight back. It is worth noticing, that if the recipe is only read by the symbols needed, the lesser potion\n\nof sleeping is the same as the lesser potion of mending. Always be careful with the representations of the symbols you use.\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n2 Symbols of Air (Flight and Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n\n=[Potion of Freezing]\nA peculiar potion, which it’s only intent is freezing or cooling something, or perhaps to just keep cold. I invented one of the potions, the potent one which quickly freezes water on contact, making it something impossible to drink\n\n and dangerous to the touch. This potion must actually be kept in a thick glass vial, and it then must be surrounded by fur, or something of the like as to keep it your hands from freezing and stopping water from getting\n\nstuck to the vial. Another recipe was made by my student, it is far weaker, and more for a use in someone’s body. To put it simply, it is a protection of a person’s cold, which seems quite horrible for most times.\n\n Yet if you’re travelling into very hot climates, it could save one’s life.\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbols of Water (Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Ice, Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Protection)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Hardiness)\n\n=[Waterbreathing Potion]=\nA remarkable potion which allows someone to breath underwater for long periods of time. The biggest side effect of this potion thought, is that you stop breathing air. Made of rare ingredients,\n\nmainly the liver and gills of a mermaid, it turns someone temporarily into a sort of human fish. Your skin between the toes and hands starts webbing, only falling out a few hours after the effects of the potion are gone. Being too long inside\n\n of the water also makes it so that when you finally leave, your ears seem to pop, and you can not hear for a few minutes. The most important part of the potion, is the creation of gills on the side of your neck, it is these that allow you to breathe\n\n underwater, yet not above. For the first few moments of the transformation, someone can not breathe in or out of water, it may create panic in some people, yet they must remember to go into the water, because they will not be able to breath out of it.\n\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae mixed with a bit of seawater\nMermaid’s Gills and Liver\n1 Symbols of Water (Fluidity)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n\n=[Frost Oil]=\nAs an oil, this concoction has an external use and is not to be drank. As I move on to the oils, the type of base fixes itself to only lard. Lard has a more viscous consistency which allows it not to drip when coated on something.\n\nThe Frost oil, or Oil of frost, is the first I will speak of. An oil which has similarities with the potion of freezing, but whose effects last longer, enabling it to be coated in weapons, armor or clothes. It’s effects are quick cooling what it touches,\n\nbut it reacts weakly to air, meaning it’s effect happen mostly through contact. Using such an oil on clothing or armor might make the wearer cold, but such could be the objective if one is travelling into hot deserts or inside volcanos.\n\nOn the other hand, while it might make the cloth or armor it was placed cold, it also offers a protection to the same cold, as something already cold, can’t get colder. As such, if one would use the oil of frost in cloth,\n\nhe would find himself getting colder, yet if the oil was used on the outer layer of plate armor, it would assist with protecting against cold winds. If placed on weapons, it has the most use on swords. A slash of the weapon on\n\nsomeone’s skin would slightly freeze the area. You might think a frozen cut would mean that the blood loss would be lower, and it’s true, yet freezing the area will make the skin turn slightly blue, and the opponent will have difficulties moving\n\n the area, this way slowing him down. The cut makes the cooling enter more into the flesh, perhaps even forcing someone to have to remove the frozen flesh affected, perhaps even amputating a limb. The biggest worry of using it on tools\n\nand armor is that it also cools it down substantially, and when badly brewed will make metals very easily shattered, when well brewed they will still suffer some problems in lesser effect.\n\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Water(Cold, Ice, Frost)\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude)\n\n=[Flame Oil]=\nThe Oil of Flame does almost the exact same as the Oil of Frost, yet instead of cold, it works with burning. In contact with the skin it will leave huge burns, but of course you do not apply it to the skin. On weapons,\n\nwhen striking the enemy, it will cause great pain a kind to burning. The flesh will become red and start to create puss. While the Oil of Frost might slow the opponent, the oil of Flames inflicts greater damage on him. The weapon does not escape\n\ndamage, while with the Frost Oil the weapon may shatter, with the Flame Oil it corrodes it. While the effects do seem like those of a flame, it does not actually heat an object up. It actually make it more flame repellent and heat resistant.\n\nOf course the resistance isn’t perfect, and a wooden sword coated with the oil will still catch ablaze, it does tarden the effects. This means if applied to armor or cloth that is not touching the skin, it creates a sort of heat and flame\n\nprotection. In the recipe it is found the use of a water symbol, and one might ask why such a representation is required in such a fire centric concoction. The explanation is rather simple, it calms the fire symbols of destruction and power, balancing\n\nit to not create an extreme reaction, which normally is represented as an explosion while brewing.\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power, Destruction, Burning)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Water (Calmness, Balance)\n\n>=[Alchemist’s Fire]=<\nOne of the greatest means of attack from an alchemist, their creation of fire. Many times referred to as ‘fire in a bottle,’ a more correct term would be ‘liquid fire.’ The alchemist is able to access the properties of fire and\n\nadd them into a liquid, making it highly volatile and dangerous. Getting hit by a bottle of it would result in being completely covered in flames. Of course it’s not always used for combat, and many times it is used to cleaning metal utensils,\n\nsuch as cauldrons and knives from contaminants and impurities. Some may say it’s a waste to use such a powerful potion on cleaning, but it’s use that way may also be associated with it’s danger. Alchemist’s fire is highly dangerous,\n\nboth while brewing and after. To brew it, not only must the temperature of the concoction remain constant, that temperature must be almost freezing. The room must be made almost specifically to create it,\n\nas it must be freezing cold. Some alchemists have started using Thanhium to have a cold room in their labs instead of heading to the tall mountains, or the cold Tundras. In those conditions the alchemist’s fire is made, and even brewed in freezing\n\ntemperatures, it still can burn your hand. The bottles must be made of glass, and to fill them, thongs of sorts must be used, as if your hand touches the liquid it will be burnt, even will gloves. Never should an alchemist fall\n\n into the mistake of using a wooden cork, as the liquid will burn right through it and most likely blow in the hands of the handler, they must always be made of glass. Now onto the dangers of the bottles. If they are kept stationary,\n\nthey won’t be dangerous, it’s problems start when they are moved quickly or hit. Some alchemists keep them in Athin made sacks to prevent some of it’s force if the bottle is broken, yet even so the alchemist would be burnt. Falling\n\nwhile carrying these bottles, or being pushed, punched, thrown to the ground may result in a bottle breaking. For them to be useful they must break, but that is the bane of the carrier as well.\n\nThe safest way to use the bottle is to drop it, it results in it blowing up when hitting the ground in almost all cases. While it does explode, it’s explosion is not one like tnt, but more of many tiny shards of glass and fire sent flying everywhere.\n\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Symbols of Fire (Destruction, Power, Consumption)\n2 Symbols of Water (Fluidity)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Potions", "§bSarrion", "Alchemy: Potions\n-------------------Glossery based off\na book written by an Unknown Alchemist.\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\n\n=[Potion of Mending]=\nOften times the most used potions of an alchemist’s arsenal. Mending potions are those to aid the hurt and injured with their effects of repairing flesh and bone, as well as body and mind. Potions of Mending are\n\n normally administered both internally and externally. Pouring it on bandages to place over wounds is a normal way of using it, as well as drank as well. For illnesses it is just drank, and for minor cuts and bruises just\n\nplacing it on the wound is enough. Minor wounds require only minor potions, and no better potion should be used for these kinds of injuries. This is because greater potions, those designed for greater injuries are often\n\n time a way to escape death, or save from devastating injuries, and side effects result from extreme fast regeneration or reconstruction of tissue and bone. Paralysis of the area, scarring, chronic pain and small deformations\n\nmay appear from the greatest of potions, yet their effects can be as great as repairing a shattered bone, returning vision to a cut eye, closing wounds in seconds. Even though those things are possible, sometimes\n\neven faster than with magic, they do not only require the use of the potions, but as well medical expertise. A potion to fix up a shattered bone requires it to be administered directly into the bone, and that means the flesh must be cut to expose it,\n\nwhich to do safely is quite the task. Of course even though the patient will he healed quite fast, he would be in no condition to do much for a few hours, fast healing is tiring for the body.\n\nRecipe:\n \n \n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Quickness)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n\n=[Potion of Regeneration]=\nA quite potent potion, it is part of the healing potions, but has a recipe on it’s own due to it’s complexity. It’s recipe is both dark, and it’s effects slow, but with amazing results.\n\nThe potion is able to remove scarring, and most of all, regrow missing limbs. Taking months to fully regrow the limb, they would then have to be retrained, and strengthened. It’s the most powerful healing potion an alchemist can\n\ndo, and to make it one must be quite adept at alchemy making, but as well face a choice which would leave most healers with a sore throat. The base used is not Aqua Vitae or Water, but the blood of the person that requires the potion.\n\nThis means the potion only might work on one person. Mandragora is used for it’s rejuvenation representation, and the other main ingredient is the liver of a mother of the same race. Not using the same race woman will result in horrible mutations,\n\nand weird growths, and not perfectly made potion will as well result in weird growths instead of the required limb. The mix of the ingredients are also quite reactive, which means it will take a skilful alchemists to make it carefully.\n\n It becomes a dark colored liquid when complete, and throughout the making, the heat must be correct and constant. The other ingredients are not always the same, as the recipe like other greater healing potions.\n\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Blood\nMandragora\nLiver of a Mother\n2 Earth Symbols (Life)\n1 Air Symbol (Grace)\n\n=[Potion of Stoneskin]\nA potion that almost seems like a legend come true. This potion is one great in an alchemist’s arsenal. It makes one skin as hard as stone, armor without armor, able to protect itself against blades and arrows quite efficiently.\n\nOf course like hitting stone, some chipping of the skin might happen, and that will appear as wounds once the effects of the potion wears out. There are two major side effects of this potion. One of them is the fact that drinking\n\nit is extremely hard. Some that have drank it consider the taste worse than poison, and I do believe, as they are alchemists who I think would try poisons on themselves. After the effects of the potion the result is also one like being sick.\n\nVomit, extreme nausea are very common effects. The other side effect is what happens if the body can not fully handle the potion. They become like a rock, unable to move, fully paralyzed yet indestructible as well.\n\n It is a rare effect, I would say happening one in five potions drank, but losing agility is a normal side effect of it. There is only one rank of this potion, anything\n\n less and it’s effects won’t be worth, anything more and the body can not take it.\n\nBase: Distilled water\n4 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude)\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n\n=[Potion of Strength]\nAnother highly sought after potion, this one is capable of enhancing the strength of someone, sometimes making an elf as strong as an Olog for short moments. Making such temporary changes to one’s body may bring quite\n\n the great amount of pain, yet it’s great way to achieve victory in a duel or fight. The major problem, like that of the potion of stoneskin, is that the body is not adapted to this amount of strength. It has been heard about\n\npeople who drink this potion falling in pain as the effects of the potion come, or after the effects end, due to crushed bones, or destroyed muscles. If used in the right dosages and not excessively though, the side effect\n\n is normally tired muscles. The minor rank of this potion is quite good for training, and it’s effects quite safe, considering it only gives one a small power boost, good for lifting heavy weights out of a cart.\n\nRecipe:\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n===================\n\n=[Potion of Celerity]=\nAlso know as potion of agility and potion of speed, the potion of celerity is the one that raises the movement speed and reflexes of the body. Normally wanted to be used for combat, many find it better to use\n\nwhen following prey while hunting, or even by thieves to quickly escape when seen. The side effects happen as all do when the body is changed temporarily, the body is not made to move faster than it\n\ndoes, and forcing it to do it may bring extreme pain to the muscles after the effects are done.\n\nRecipe:\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n\n=[Potion of Accuity]=\nAnother air based potion like the potion of Celerity, the potion of Accuity is an amazing potion to create and use. This potion provides the drinker with heightened senses, and may be prepared to all senses, or to specific\n\nones for more potency. Often times uses for hunting or for taking a job in hard tasks with require great vision, hearing or touch. In a competition of cooking for example, the judges might drink this potion beforehand for greater ability\n\n to judge the taste, and it is said that with it, someone might smell poison in their drink when there is no smell to sense. The result of enhancing the senses for a short while, is the worsening of them afterwards for a short while.\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbol of Air (Perception)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n3 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n\n=[Potion of Wizard’s Wisdom]=\nEver wanted to feel like the great scholars of old? Then this potion is the one to use. A potion able to enhance the mental capabilities of the drinker temporarily. Fantastic even in it’s purple color, it enhances one’s\n\n problem solving, reasoning, and general thinking ability. Of great use to alchemists as well, especially when formulating new potions and you find yourself stuck on a problem. This potion will aid you, not by giving you ideas as soon as you drink it\n\nbut by clearing your mind, making you think fluidly, and giving you a new perspective on the matter. It’s reagents are many, so to create them you would take quite the lengthy time, and the migraines it creates\n\nare long, yet if you enhancing it with purer ingredients will diminish some of the migraines. Another point about this potion could perhaps be it’s effects when dealing with memory loss, it might make the person\n\nhave an easier time remembering, mind invasion from mental magic, becoming fully in control of your own mind placing the mage outside of control, and while being interrogated or lying, you will appear far more truthful in your responses.\n\n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Air (Perception)\n\n- Lesser:\nBase: Distilled Water\n3 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n2 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n3 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n2 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n\n- Greater:\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n5 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n3 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n3 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n\nPlease refer to Part II for the rest of the potions. Thank you.\n-Sarrion\n\n===================To be Continued...", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorcerer Types", "§bGerald Elgan", "===================                                                                                             Sorcerers: Recognizing the Various Varieties\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n==================\n\nAmongst those who possess distinctly closer bonds to the void, a few different kinds have been recognised. This short excerpt will attempt to bring the reader through these varied distinctions, and hopefully provide aid in attaining some small measure of\n\nenlightenment in the subject matter.\n===================Types outlined:\nThe Common Robed Mage: Page 4-7\nHousehold Mage:\nPage 8-13\nBattle Mage:\nPage 14-22\n===================\n\nThe Common Robed Mage\n==================\nThe typical conjurer, often accompanied by a staff- draped in long cloaks, adorned in all manner of strange runes and odd colours, is often depicted as an old man with long, grand beards and a vast\n\n\n==================\n-reservoir of knowledge esoteric. There is no doubt that this variety is the most renowned and favored. The Common Mage is often the most well-versed in the forbidden art of magical combat- with stronger spells and\n\n\n===================\n-hexes, and (depending on the proficiency of the caster) all the more perilous.\n\nHowever, with these strengths, come weaknesses, for the Common Mage is often by tradition, frail and\n\n\n===================-lacking in physical prowess- endurance, hardiness and such- due to the almost fanatical obsession that they so often possess with the search and acquisition of more knowledge, and in turn, more power of origins profane.\n\nHousehold Mage\n===================The common Mage's humbler counterpart of lesser renown, the Household Mage could very well be the lowly servant a small measure too efficient at the task of cleaning, or the unassuming cook who heats the furnace a moment-\n\n\n===================\n-too quickly.\n\nThe subtlety of the magic these beings possess and and put into practice makes them quite difficult to discern. One could, perhaps rightly, assume that such beings might hardly\n\n\n===================-pose any considerable amount of threat, due to their lack of experience and utility in the field of combat.\n\nHousehold Mages can be either shunned members of the secluded Mage's Guild\n\n\n===================-or apprentices who, having acknowledged their inferior ability or lack of talent, had decided to follow an entirely different path, and seek a livelihood in a different environment. \n\nTheir spells are most\n\n\n===================\n-often simple and pose little to no danger- these sorcerers are seen as more benevolent than the common Mage, and physically more robust; though such things are quite difficult to confirm, given the elusive and subtle-\n\n\n===================nature of the mages in question.\n(Witch Maid/Mage of Cleaning.)\n\nThe Battle Mage\n===================The rarest and least liked of the known types- The Battle Mage is seen as the bane of chivalry and honorable duels, with little care for learning more of their art. The Battle Mage is more often spotted in places where\n\n\n===================-war and conflict are as commonplace as frost on a cold winter's morn. He is often the result of a fighter who, through rigorous and excruciating training, has learnt both the way of the sword and the art of magic-\n\n\n===================-applying both theories and practices in harmonious synergy. The existence of this being suggests the existence of some clandestine groups or orders that have handpicked and set aside some select candidates for the\n\n\n===================-rigors required to achieve this balance.\n\nThe training of a Battle Mage is the stuff of tales and legends- often known to be one of, if not the most dangerous path to the art of the arcane. Apprentices that were\n\n\n===================-found to have been fit candidates were often heard to have died of various accidents-including but not limited to: Death by fire and cinders, of spell failures and eternal sleep, of ice and water, and of broken shards of\n\n\n===================-marble or glass. The fortunate few- if one could call them such- that did manage to live through the horrors of their training and ire of the common folk, quite often found themselves unable to resume the lives they one led, now bent\n\n\n===================-purely on suffering and death as heralds of doom and ruin.\n\nBattle Mages are often not as proficient in the art of magic as their more focused counterpart: the common Sorcerer. However, their skill-\n\n\n===================with and mastery of the blade may, at times, more than compensate for this lack of further magical prowess and potency. Hence, it would be most unwise for the regular mage to step within range of the Battle Mage, for the Battle-\n\n\n===================Mage, neither frail nor unfit, could quite as easily close the distance, and deal a devastating blow.\n(Warrior-Witch/ Spellblade/ Witchman /Mystic Knight. )", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Botany", "§bSarrion", "Alchemy: Botany\n-------------------This glossery is a detailed explaination of the Botany with in alchemy, and was written by an unknown alchemist.\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\n\n=[->Earth<-]=\n          Weak\nName: Goblin’s Ivy\nRepresentation: Resilience, Poison, Life\n\nDescription: One of the most easily found flora of the deserts, this plant is easily identified as a\n\nbrownish green vine with small leaves. It is found mainly clinging onto old buildings or ruins of the deserts, and on the dry cliff sides. It is quite a resilient plant, able to survive in extreme hostile conditions, and\n\nwith a very low or no amount of water close by. Removing it also becomes a problem, as it seems to regrow on the same spot after someone goes to the long labour of removing it all. It is these properties that brings the plant such\n\ngood uses, it’s representation of resilience makes a welcome addition to any stoneskin potion, even while being regarded as a Weak reagent. A few poisons may also be created by use of this reagent,\n\nmainly ones weaker, some to create nausea or ill disposition. Easy to find and prepare, it is normally used by those new to alchemy to learn the craft.\n\nLocation: Clinging on ruins, stones and cliff sides of dry regions.\n-------------------\n\n          Moderate\nName: Saffvil\n\nRepresentation: Resilience, Endurance, Death\n\nDescription: Possibly the most horribly smelling herb in all of swamplands, many alchemists make use\n\nof their nose when trying to find it. This green grass is green and grows on the corpses of animals, on dead wood and plants, and sometimes on the bottom of big trees. This plant is one that is extremely hard to remove from anything,\n\nas it spreads very quickly and strongly. Normally to remove it, you would have to remove the “host”, the plant or animal that it is growing on. If you do not, it will spread all throughout it. This means that the plant has a great representation\n\nof Resilience and Endurance, but this plant, unlike a few other Earth symbols, does not represent Life and Regrowth, but Death. This means this plant is mostly used in the creation of poisons,\n\nand one particular myth of an aging potion.\n\nLocation: On the bodies of dead plants and animals.\n-------------------\n\nName: Alabaster Leaf\n\nRepresentations: Immobility, Perseverance\n\nDescription: This plant is mostly characterized by it’s leaf’s alabaster color. Most often times found in the dryer regions of the forest growing around fallen trees.\n\nQuite small in size, harvesting it may prove a difficulty to the untrained hands. The best method would perhaps be taking the whole plant, with roots, and then remove the leaves as you may use them. The extract one gets by crushing the leaves is what\n\nan alchemist should use. It comes with it’s natural alabaster hue, which serves as paint to many. The extract is mildly poisonous, creating dizziness and nausea to those that consume it. It’s main uses are in antidotes, oils, and of course, poisons.\n\nLocation: Forest dry regions next to fallen trees.\n-------------------Name: Tippen’s Root\n\nRepresentation: Life, Regrowth, Resilience, Strength, Endurance\n\nDescription: Tippen’s roots is one of the most used\n\n reagents in the making of mending potions, it is even said, that it is required to be present in all healing potions, or the potion will be of weak quality. It was named after the botanist that had first discovered it around hills and\n\nin dense forests. It’s location of growing is often the same of that of Alabaster leaf, besides fallen trees, but as well next to carcases of animals and great bugs. It is quite a pleasant sight when compared with the death around it,\n\nas the plant of the herb blooms into purple flowers. What one has to use though, is the roots. They are of a yellow color, with spots accentuated a bit more darker. Many carry these roots around, even those with no knowledge of it’s use in alchemy.\n\nThis is because from the roots one can easily make a remedy which may stop bleeding near instantly. In it’s unprepared it’s strength isn’t as great, but it still may save countless lives. The problem with this root is a simple one, it’s smell.\n\nThe odor that the plant releases when the salve of the roots is spilled is enormous. While using it you may gag and even vomit from thinking that you are placing such foul-smelling balm onto an open wound. After such,\n\nthe smell will not escape you for a few hours. It’s traits in healing bring the herb representations of Life and Regrowth, but it also has great representations of Strength and Endurance.\n\nLocation: Forest, around dead trees and animals.\n-------------------Name: Desert Berry Bush\n\nRepresentation: Protection, Resilience\n\nDescription: The Desert Berry Bush's appearance is that of a withered rose bush,\n\nlong brown/grey stalks with big pointy thorns, yet without any leaves. It doesn't appear to grow higher than four feet, but most of the thorns are longer than an inch. It grows inside cactus forests, as in, where there  is great concentration\n\nof cactus. Never has one been alone in the desert’s sands without a cactus near it. The bush gives Berries of a strong red color every full moon. These don't last long, as animals of the desert appear to enjoy it's taste quite dearly.\n\nThe berries are extremely sweet, something very strange to find in the desert, so no wonder the animals enjoy it. The stalks are not like the berries, if an animal by any chance passed the long thorns to rip and eat the stalk, I believe\n\n would fall dead in less than a day. As you cut the stalk you notice that the insides are green, instead of the dead brown. From it it's juice flows a lot, yet of course it's poison to drink it. Eating the liquid or even touching it causes rashes and all\n\nsomeone wants to do afterwards is scratch the area, even if it’s the mouth. Too much of it and it kills of course, and it sound be painful. The thorns create the same effect, so without gloves, the hand starts itching and becomes red for about a day.\n\nIt doesn't seem deadly to descendents and probably kha's, but it does explain the small rodents found dead near them. A thorn is poisonous, and annoying, just doesn't kill big animals. The stalk seems to have far more uses in\n\nalchemy when compared with it’s berry, especially in oils of protection and potions of stoneskin. It represents protection and resilience, the thorns and it's poison nature being the reasons why. To prepare for it I have found it hard,\n\nas when cut, the juices drip quite fast. You can't remove the bush from the ground, as it's roots are too big, so they have to be cut in the spot. Feet long pieces of stalk are enough, yet one would have to almost tilt the plant\n\ndown so that the cut doesn't face down. Gloves are essential in gathering it because of the thorns, and after cutting, I advise placing it in a long bottle, with the cut end pointing up.\n\nWhen being prepared, the alchemist should be careful as to lose as little bit of the stalk as he removes the seemingly dead outer layer of the stalk, before using it in his potion.\n\nLocation: Desert Cactus Forests\n\n          Strong\nName: Starved Coyote’s Tick\nRepresentations: Protection, Resilience, Connection\n\nDescription: The Tick that I speak of is probably the only non flora which I speak of as an Alchemy\n\ningredient in this volume. Mostly it can be found on coyotes the first ones discovered on the bodies of thin starved coyotes, giving them the name. This does not mean it does not appear in other animals, like desert\n\nhares and rhinos. As long as it is an animal that grows in hot climates, you may be lucky enough to find one. If the animal has a lot of fur, it may be hard to find the tick, but due to it’s size, just passing a hand through the animal may\n\nmake one find the tick. It might get as big as a thumb, very fat of pure brown color. It would seem many times as a lump in the animal’s skin, and trying to remove it is mostly impossible. The Staved Coyote’s Tick, once grabbing onto some meat,\n\nwill never let go unless it wants to. Fire, Ice, or even swings of a warhammer only damage the skin around it, the tick itself resiting more. It’s collecting is done by cutting the flesh that the tick is grabbing, and only when all the meat\n\nis removed from the tick, does it try to find another place to grab to. This is a dangerous thing to do, as if an alchemists isn’t careful, even with gloves the tick may grab onto the skin, and never let go. When I say never,\n\n I truly mean it, no one can make the tick let go, most likely the finder would have to be removed, or at least part of it, that or one would learn to live with the tick, as it doesn’t seem toxic or poisonous to an animal. With characteristics like this,\n\n it is no wonder that it is a strong symbol of earth, representing Connection, Protection and Resilience.\n\nLocation: Bodies of animals of hot Climates\n\n     =[Fire Symbols]=\n->Weak\n\nName: Desert Bush Berry\n\nRepresentations: Empowerment, Overwhelming\n\nDescription: The Desert Berry Bush's\n\nappearance is that of a withered rose bush, long brown/grey stalks with big pointy thorns, yet without any leaves. It doesn't appear to grow higher than four feet, but most of the thorns are longer than an inch. It grows inside cactus\n\nforests, as in, where there is great concentration of cactus.Never has one been alone in the desert’s sands without a cactus near it. The Desert Bush Berries are the berries given by the Desert Berry Bush.\n\nThe bush gives Berries of a strong red color every full moon. These don't last long, as animals of the desert appear to enjoy it's taste quite dearly. The berries are extremely sweet, something very strange to find in the desert,\n\nso no wonder the animals enjoy it. The use of the berries are mostly in culinary, serving as treats, in jams and to bake. As for alchemy uses, it behaves as a fire symbol, as is custom to red ingredients. In this case not because of the color,\n\nbut because of the strong flavor it has, almost overwhelming. On the other hand, it doesn't appear all that useful nor seems to give great use in equivalent exchange. Great to be used by new alchemists in their training, as it quite safe.\n\nLocation: Desert Cactus forests in Full moon days.\n-------------------===================To be Continued...\nPlease look for:\nAlchemy: Botany II", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "https://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/164585-the-obelisks/#comment-1555843\n\nFormed", ""),
        StaticBook("Pursuing Purity", "§bAshanaak", "------=+=------\nFor Those Who Pursue Purity...\n------=+=------\n\n\n\nA Guide for Those Who Pursue Knowledge of Tahariaean Clericism\n\n------=+=------\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq\n------=+=------\n\nThe Masjid al Nur al-Haqq is the building before you, serving as a gathering place for the clerics of the Aengul of Purity, Tahariae. Tahariae has given us the abilities to establish Purity in this\n\nrealm, which comes in two forms. The first is the eradication of injuries, blemishes, and sickness from the mortal races. The second is the eradication of the servants of darkness throughout the realm, such as dark mages, tainted beings, and those with\n\nfraternal relations with such beings.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Five Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nWhen one becomes a cleric, they must follow a set of five tenets, or five main rules, told to the Prophet Braxis in Anthos by Tahariae Himself. The rules are to ensure the cleric knows what he\n\nor she must do for Tahariae and His duty. Breaking even one of these rules will mean forceful disconnection from Our Lord:\n\n[*] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae. [*]\n\nThe other clerics are much like your brothers and sisters, a family. You must always be ready to come to their aid, and to allow them to die intentionally is impure.\n\n[*] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae. [*]\n\nNever stray from your duty, your duty is to heal those in need and to purge the darkness that roam around Vailor. To allow a simple matter to draw you away from such duty is impure.\n\n[*] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure. [*]\n\nNo matter their race or personal prejudice, cast all hatred aside, as we aid all. Help guide them onto the right path and ensure they are healed and protected from Impurity.\n\n[*] Do not spill the blood of the innocent. [*]\n\nDo not attack or kill an innocent person, even if they have insulted you or another. We clerics are the healers of the innocent, not slaughterers of the innocent. Such is impure.\n\n[*] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will. [*]\n\nTahariae’s power is only for His Mission. To use it to harm those innocent of crimes or for your own selfish needs is impure.\n\n------=+=------\nWalking the Path of Purity\n------=+=------\n\nWe are willing to take in those willing to become a cleric, although becoming one is not a simple matter of gaining His power and using it of your own free will. One must be willing to undergo\n\ntrials and be prepared to put Tahariae’s duty before all, including what is most precious to you personally. Most of all, you must follow the Tenets without hesitation; failing to do so will mean permanent disconnection.\n\nIf you truly have desire to bring\n\nLight and Purity into this realm, you shall meet with one of our masters and put through a series of trials that the master decides. These trials will help demonstrate to us your devotion and dedication, as well as help you understand the roles of the\n\nclerics. Once your trials are complete and the master deems you ready, you will be brought before Tahariae Himself. If He deems you ready, He will grant you His blessing of Light, and your duty as a cleric shall begin under the guidance of the master who\n\nconnected you to Tahariae.\n\nIf you wish to walk the Path of Purity, leave a letter explaining who you are, why you wish to serve Tahariae, what skills you have, and if you have any questions regarding us. Simply leave the letter in the chest at the\n\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq, in the Caliphate of Khalestine, and await our response.\n\nIf you require healings, protection, or blessings, do not hesitate to send a bird to one of the Four Archons of the Masjid al Nur al-Haqq.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Four Archons\n------=+=------\n\n-[ The Mind ]-\nRamza Mantisuku\n((Zeeer0))\n\n-[ The Mouth ]-\nAshanaak\n((Ventusyr))\n\n-[ The Heart ]-\nAndriel Z'lorn\n((jlyoko))\n\n-[ The Arm ]-\nElvira Mantisuku\n((Farryn))\n\n[!] This page is dedicated to a map of the Caliphate, with a small, simply-drawn temple symbol in one of the corners of the city. [!]\n\n((-2197, 1061))", ""),
        StaticBook("On Wraiths", "Toodles", "On Wraiths\n\nBy: Someone who isn't stupid enough to reveal their true name.\n\nNot much is known about the actual physical characteristics of Wraiths by the author, but what they do know shall be written down. Wraiths (also known as Harbingers) are shadowy undead beings with a proclivity for killing.\n\nThe most recent incarnation of Wraiths are produced by the machinations of the Drakaar Mordring, through the utilization of certain altars, one of which is in the Sunless Sanctum. (The process of becoming a Wraith is described in another book.)\n\nThe Wraith, once created, is bound to Mordring's Will; basically, to bring about a resurgence of the Dragonkin. Wraiths have the ability to summon some form of Vessel, which fill with lifeforce when a mortal dies in the vicinity of it. It takes fifteen\n\ndeaths for the Vessel to be full, upon which a Dragon or Drake will spawn. If the Vessel is destroyed before the amount of lifeforce is acquired, all the accumulated lifeforce will vanish, but the Vessel can still be summoned. If the Wraith attempts to\n\nharm the newly-made Dragon or Drake, the Wraith will perish. After thirty years, Wraiths are released from Mordring's service, but they retain the ability to summon Vessels. Wraiths have the ability to husk\n\nempty bodies, much like Wights; but there are unknown complications regarding the eyes of such a body.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Mans Descent", "§bIlkazar", "A \nMans\nDescent\n\n\"The few people who know the name Coltaine Wick, likely associate it with evil deeds, dark mages, and other such unsavory things, but he wasnt always a nefarious old man. As a young man during the Stormlord Rebellion, he happily\n\nserved his king and country of Oren, he was like any average man. But in war someone has to lose and in this case it was the side he fought for. As the rebels took over all he had ever cared for, his regiment was disbanded, he himself\n\nwas outlawed from Petrus, and a 500 mina bounty was placed on his head, things were not well for him, every day he feared would be his last, he never lost faith in his fallen king though, and still wore the honored Crow on his clothing\n\nearning him many beatings. It was in this low point in his life that he first began to tread the path that would lead him to darkness later in life.\nHe was drinking away his sorrow in a pint of ale at the then famous Standing Tree in when he first came\n\nacross one of the orginal Wraiths, beings of such horrific power they the could reduce a man to an ashen husk in mere moments. The aforementioned Wraith Vinzakra was making a grand time slaughtering people outside the tavern he sat in.\n\nAll Coltaine could do was watch in awe, wheels turning in his mind he thought \"There is a man with the power to control his fate, if I had but a portion of such power, oh the things I would do!\" It was then he set off to find that wretched being\n\nand serve it in what way he could. So he went to Embermoor, long rumored to be a haunt for necromancers and the like, which he soon found out to be very true. He was allowed to join the Adherency there, and serve Vinzakra for some time.\n\nMurdering and terrorizing the people of Athera became second nature for him in the time he spent in the Adherency, after a time he went off to study the art of earth evocation, being taught the art by a Graven, when he had returned, the Adherency had been\n\ndestroyed, losing yet another home, Coltaine drifted around from cult to cult for decades, necromancers, dreadknights, shades.\nHe served them all and faithfully, never betraying those we would call friend.\n\nAnd, after managing to sell his soul, he will continue to serve the dark for all of eternity.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("On Liches", "§bIlkazar", "On\nLiches\n\n\nVolume One\n\nBe warned reader,\nthis is not a guide on how to combat a lich, such is very dangerous and should be avoided if at all possible.\n\nA Lich is, in the simplest term, a skeletal mage. They are a form of undead, skeletal beings who use the arcane powers to destroy any who may stand in there path. Being undead they have much the same weakness's as other undead creatures have,\n\nsuch as an aversion to gold, it may not kill them outright but it does cause great pain. Clerical magic also being there weakness, the holy magic has the potential to destroy them and make them reform elsewhere. There skeletal frame is also very fragile.\n\nIt is very easy for one to smash a liches bones apart though such would not cause the lich pain or distress. Besides those cases, a lich feels no pain, you can immolate the creature in flames yet it will still stand, stab at it at your own peril\n\nfor that also does not cause it pain. They do not sleep they do not eat they do not get tired. Liches are created in a secretive necromantic ritual, the people who are made into liches are widely regarded to be skillful mages if not masters of there\n\nchosen art. The difference between a mortal mage an a lich is vast, a mortal mage will get tired and fatigued while casting\nA lich has no such limitation, they can continue to cast till there mana runs out completely. Liches learn how to\n\nhandle there mana vastly better, they tend to outpreform most any mortal mage in combat and otherwise. Liches also get the added ability to drain the life of a target to fuel them, leaving behind a blackened husk.\n\nThere is but one way to truly kill a lich, and that is destroying there phylactery. A phylactery is an object that has the liches soul bound to it. They are always very well hidden, thus making liches a terrible foe to fight.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electricity", "Fury_Fire", "12th of the Deep Cold\n((6:30))\nLightning struck some distance away. After searching for some time, it was found to be the root of a tree that had been struck. Upon examination, it was charred, a slight stench coming from it. By all appearences, the tree\n\nlooked to have been burned. The only thing that told me otherwise was the static electricity still in the air for a short time around it.\n\n6th of Malin's Welcome\n((12:40pm))\nSanctuary\nLightning had struck only a short distance away, in the nearby forest. After searching, the path of earth that was struck had been found. Being even near the strike that had happened moments before left\n\nthe taste of metal in my mouth, and the smell of burning grass. The ground looked as if it had caught aflame for some time, yet the downpour had put it out. Other then that, the lightning strike itself was caught in full view. It had shot down\n\ndiagonally from the sky, other minor areas branching off from the strike. It had been followed by a loud clap of thunder.\n\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:44 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, a Telekenisis user.\nShe mentioned tha\n*The rest of the page is ripped out*\n\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:45 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, telekenisis user.\nStated that every time one connects to the void, they get a tad weaker as their magic grows a tad stronger. Explained that they would clear their mind, much as done in\n\nnormal meditation, and then one would imagine said element in their mind, along with their target. As they did this, they would envision a connection with the void. Often, one would twitch someplace when they connected, and their bodies would be put under\n\ngreat stress.\n\n5th of the grand harvest, 1554.\n((11:25 AM))\nI sat in my home, having connected with the void. The spark I summoned remained there for some second, before I would aim to brighten it, as shown before. As this happened I would grow tired almost immediatly,\n\nthe spark vanishing and I fell over, exhausted. I had felt something different then the normal rate of mana consumption, however. As I forced myself to use the mana required to make the spark brighter, I felt something that could only be described as a\n\na portion of 'life force' being withdrawn. I couldn't quite tell the amount, but I assumed this was my mana. All I could learn from this attempt was that it used up more mana then a normal spark.\n\nSometime in the Amber Cold, 1554\n((1-2 am-ish?))\nI allowed myself to be struck by electricity in my Augur form. Almost all feeling left me side pain, my entire body feeling as if it had become static. Side that, I could not tell much else about it.\n\n15th of the Amber Cold.\n((9 PM))\nI had now grown familiar with telling the amount of mana being used. As I would brighten my spark, I now fully felt the mana leave me. I had over time grown accustomed to how much Mana I had anyways, which\n\nis a major help as I determine the usage. I remain aware that my mana pool will end up growing eventually through meditation anyways, yet I would imagine it would be slow enough that I would grow used to it as such happened.\n\n11th of the First Seed, 1556.\n((5:44 PM))\n\n[!]Page has been torn out angrily!\n\n16th of the Deep Cold, 1557.\n((10:39 PM))\nI sat upon an altar in a forest with Nemir, preparing to shoot a bolt of electricity. It began with normal meditation, and the summoning of several sparks. I would concentrate them within the center of\n\nmy palm, forming a 'bolt', of sorts. After this I would hold my hand out and release it forward.\nThe bolt would hit the ground, leaving the air with a light feel of static for some moments before it would vanish and the brunt of fatigue hit me.\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1559\n((3:30 PM))\nAt this point, not much had changed side my bolts growing steadily stronger as well as my ability to cast more. At this point I can cast three before I run out of mana, and the chance of me forgetting to\n\ncut the connection with the void before firing is minimal. I have finally noticed to conductive affects of metal, having cast near an iron rod once. My bolt had veered in midair, hitting the rod instead of continuing to go straight.\n\n12th of the Amber Cold, 1559\n((6:50 PM))\nA Kharajyr female was attacking a group of elves as I stood back and raised my hand, curious on how powerful my bolts had truely grown. Sparks began to form as well as sweat upon my brow, soon collecting\n\nwithin the center of my palm to form a bolt. It was obviously weak in power compared to Locke's, yet still okay in my eyes. Soon I let it fly towards the Kha, and the effects were surprising. The Kha fell over, stunned for some moments as the elves took\n\nthat chance to grab the Kha and bind it. Upon further inspection, the Kha bore a charred burn mark where the bolt had hit- although likely only caused due to her fur temporarily catching aflame.\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1562\nThis hasn't been written in for some time, but it's about time to continue it. Since my last entry, my bolts have grown to full power and I'm able to cast three in a row before being unable to cast another. A full powered bolt\n\nwill easily leave burns on someones skin and make them paralyzed for some while. Alternatively, I can call a bolt down from the sky.. Such is done as a normal bolt is made within the hand. The difference would be that you're treating a point in the sky as\n\nthough it would be what you were summoning with instead of your hands. This alone would cause much more mana, and you'd also need a view of your target. It would take as much mana as though you summoned a normal bolt and shot it to that point in the sky.w\n\nPast that, you would pour much more mana than a normal bolt of electricity into it, soon to the point where it would be a full powered bolt of lightning ready to be launched. At first it would remain very hard to aim, and almost every  shot would miss.\n\nThese would not grow more powerful, and the reason you summon it in the sky is simple: Controlling that amount of mana close to you is stupid and dangerous. Even if you controlled it, the amount of electricity would harm you even if you are the creator.\n\nAs you continue doing such, it will become much easier to aim and not stress you as much.\n\nFinal words:\nThis book was originally aimed as a record of my learning, yet eventually I decided that it could be used to help any aspiring Electric Evocationists learn. It does not cover everything about the magic, although it still does with a lot of\n\nit. And I urge any who would use it to be cautious and find another electric evocationist to assist them in learning, be it as a teacher or mentor. This magic is dangerous to learn and at times I nearly killed myself with it.\n-Lefkos Glowsbane", ""),
        StaticBook("To Be a Wraith", "Toodles", "Becoming a Wraith\n\nBy: Someone who's not stupid enough to reveal their name.\n\nPrerequisites:\n-Must be a practitioner of the dark arts or undead.\n-Must have a 'catalyst'; some sort of bone that the Drake, Satar, gives to certain people.\n\nThe hopeful Wraith must acquire such a catalyst, and then place it on a certain type of Altar, one example of which is located in the Sunless Sanctum. Upon doing this, they must find, kill, and take a bone from three mortals.\n\nThey then must take these bones to the altar... But the author is not quite sure what happens to them. But once they've been used, the Wraith-to-be must stab themself with an Aurum sword. After much immolation and probably pain, they\n\nwill become a Wraith. Huzzah!", ""),
        StaticBook("A White Tome", "§bAshanaak", "[!] The tome is bound in white leather, with only a silver diamond encircling a silver dot embossed on the front cover: the Clerical Eye. Its pages would be marblesque in color, with silver trim, and the writing a flowing font in black ink. [!]\n\n>>--<<=+=>>--<<\nThe Utterings of Tahariae\n>>--<<=+=>>--<<\n\n\n\nAssembled and Recorded by the Prophet Ashanaak in Vailor\n\n------=+=------\nThe Five Sacred Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nAs Recorded by the Prophet Braxis in early Anthos:\n\n\n[I] Shelter and protect thy brethren.\n\n[II] Cannot stray from thy faith.\n\n[III] Shall guide the lost.\n\n[IV] Shall not kill, harm, or spill the blood of the innocent.\n\n[V] Abuse of thine gift and punishment shall fall to you.\n\nAs Interpreted by the High Priest Heshakomeu Sohae in late Athera:\n\n\n[I] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae.\n\n[II] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae.\n\n[III] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure.\n\n[IV] Do not spill the blood of the innocent.\n\n[V] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Four Revelations\n------=+=------\n\nAs Recited through the Prophet Ashanaak by the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, between the years 1436 and 1442:\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Judgment: The Apokalytiria\n---------------\n\nI am the Glory of the Rising Sun. I am the Bringer of Light. I am the Lord of Purity and the Archon of Justice. I am the Vehement Lord. I am Tahariae. Witness Me, My Chosen\n\nProphet. Witness Me.\n\nI, the Divine Stag, He Who Walks in Pure Light, the Great Purge, have merely watched My Servants for too long. You have Divided, and Divided you shall fall. You failed to Understand the Mission I had given you, and so you have\n\ndeteriorated into mere wandering healers and warriors who know only my Blessed Name. Your mockery of Faith and Piety offends Me, and so I return once more. Witness Me, Ashanaak, My Chosen Prophet. Witness Me.\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Wisdom: The Eight Woes\n---------------\n\nAnd now, my Chosen Prophet, recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their hearts for their Sins:\n\n[I] Woe to those that turn against Me and My Mission, for they must be cast out of thy ranks.\n\n[II] Woe to those who only know Me for My Blessing, and not for My Mission, and do not recognize Me and My Glory in prayer except when My power is needed.\n\n[III] Woe to those who refuse to heal the Innocent, to return to Pure form what has been rendered Impure.\n\n[IV] Woe to those who let the Impure, the Beings of Darkness and Evil, and the Descendants who bring harm to the Innocents, walk free when they cross thy path.\n\n[V] Woe to those who cause harm to the Innocent, for they are those you are sworn to protect.\n\n[VI] Woe to those who are sexually immoral, who give themselves outside of the holy bed of marriage, who dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent.\n\n[VII] Woe to those who give themselves over to perpetual drunkenness and intoxication, for they dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent. Such is only acceptable in celebrations and festivities.\n\n[VIII] Woe to those who steal, cheat, and utter vulgarities, who abuse the Innocent with their tongues and hands.\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Valor: The Eight Commands\n---------------\n\nAnd now, Ashanaak, I give you these Commands. Recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, that you may live a Pure life:\n\n[I] Go forth, and spread not just my Light among the Descendants, but My Words and the Truth of My Glory.\n\n[II] Go forth, and become true Clerics among the Descendants: scholars, protectors, and leaders, to guide the Innocent with words, justice, and wisdom.\n\n[III] Go forth, and guard yourself against marriage, for service to Me demands complete and total commitment. If you do marry, do not marry those who serve Darkness and Evil, for in doing so you taint the very nature of holy matrimony.\n\n[IV] Go forth, and kneel before Me in maniael: private prayer, gratitude, and submission before My Glory when you awake and before you sleep.\n\n[V] Go forth, and kneel before Me in manaakh: prayer, worship, and submission in fellowship with your Brothers and Sisters in Me once each Elven year.\n\n[VI] Go forth, and respect the fallen clerics who I have sent back to you, to listen and follow what they have returned to say. And when their wisdom has been imparted, that you will have the strength and courage to send them back to My Halls.\n\n[VII] Go forth, and follow My Chosen Prophet, for they shall be My Light in the darkness of the world for you.\n\n[VIII] Go forth, and in My Blessed Name, use any means necessary to bring Purity to the Taint and Darkness that has become the world. The realm must return to how it once was, when the Four once ruled in Peace and Taint had not yet manifested. Through the\n\nsuffering My Mission shall bring you, remember that it is not out of Moral Good that you must do these things, but out of Necessity.\n\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Hope: The Anachorisi\n---------------\n\nDo all that I have commanded for you to do, and do not do all I have commanded you not to do, and you shall not perish. Nay; once suffering consume you and you leave thy mortal coil,\n\nI shall welcome you into My Sacred Halls, to forever be with Me in Purity, to forever be witness to My Sacred Light, forever and ever more.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Anamniseis\n------=+=------\n\nThe Interactions the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, has had with His Clerics, as Recorded and Collected by the Prophet Ashanaak:\n\nIt was in Aegis that the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, first came to mortalkind, but He did not reveal His blessed name. In mortal man’s wonder at His eternal and pure radiance, He was worshipped as the Creator, and only the most holy of clerics\n\ncould serve Him.\n\nIt was in Asulon, Aerial, the Arch-Aengul, lost the ability to grant power to Her servants, and the Aengul Gazardiael withdrew His blessing, thus why He is known as the Abandoner. Tahariae, in His infinite kindness, granted the clerics\n\nHis Blessing, so the holy work of healing and the purging of evil could be done still, yet He still did not reveal His blessed name, and the clerics believed their patrons to be Aerial and Gazardiael.\n\nIt was in early Anthos that He revealed Himself and\n\nHis Sacred Mission of Purity to the Prophet Braxis, that the bodies of Mankind be whole and protected from the forces of evil, and that taint be removed from the realm, and that the realm be returned to the Purity that existed when the Four Brothers first\n\nwalked the Earth.\n\nIt was in late Anthos, when the clerics were few and Setherien and the wraiths threatened the realm, that Tahariae chose four to be His champions, perfect representations of His four aspects: Judgment, Wisdom, Valor, and Hope.\n\nTogether, they fought the many threats to the purity of the realm.\n\nIt was in late Thales Tahariae summoned forth His clerics to investigate a portal, through which we were to enter. The Abandoner, Gazardiael, confronted Tahariae, and the two did battle\n\natop the mountain on which the portal was located. After the battle, and Gazardiael briefly pushed back, Tahariae manifested before the gathered clerics and their allies as a radiant white stag. He told us the portal required two keys to open, as well as\n\nthe Itharel of Wisdom Hosper, who had been captured by forces unknown. “O Lord, can you tell us where Hosper is?” I asked. “Nay,” He responded. “A dark force clouds My vision; I cannot see him.” So began the quest for the keys began, of which I was\nnot\n\ninvolved any further in.\n\nIt was in Athera that the Order of the White Lance, a union between the servants of Tahariae and Xan, Aengul of Gaurdianship and Order, was formed. Alas, it was not to last, and so began the Schism and the Conflict of Light. In\n\nlate Athera, Aldrik, Second Itharel of Hope, was given a vision by Tahariae commanding the Clerics and the Paladins to reunite, but such did not come to pass.\n\nIt was in Vailor that Tahariae commanded His followers to leap from high places and He would\n\nsave us. It was a test of faith to prepare us for His message: the realm was passing through a Great Cycle that must occur, lest the world be consumed by the Destroyer. However, in order for the Realm to be protected, four Harvesters wielding scythes must\n\ncut down many innocents. “For it is not out of Moral Good or Holiness that we do these things, but out of Necessity,” sayeth Tahariae unto us. So great was His insistence we trust in Him that two of us briefly lost connection to Him for not leaping\n\nenough, but they were forgiven, and His Blessing returned to their hearts.\n\nIt was many years later, amidst the assault of the clerics by the Being known as the Undying One, that Tahariae revealed His new commands by speaking through the cleric Ashanaak,\n\nchoosing him to be His next Prophet.\n\nSuch is the history of the actions of the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, in our realm. May our actions be a testament to the Glory of Tahariae, Blessed Be His Name.\n\n[!] An ornate picture of a stag facing the viewer is here. Its antlers are tall and winding, and a radiant halo surrounds his head. [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Soul Puppetry", "Fury_Fire", "The following pages in this book cover a sparsely known Dark Magic known as Soul Puppetry. If this book is found by anyone, it is likely stolen and should be placed somewhere safe and where none will find it.\n\nSoul Puppetry, unlike common belief, is not used to control people in any way, sense, or form. There are no set list of spells, and there are drawbacks on the user. The closest control goes is forcing emotions upon people to the point that they may act\n\nupon such. Mages who practice this will notice a percentage of what they cause coming back upon them in return.\n\nA Soul Puppeteer begins by first learning how to make basic puppets, mimicking the race of the target they wish to inflict their magic upon. These puppets would begin by the molding of clay, making the basic shape of the person. Normal humanoid for\n\nhumans, larger puppets for Orcs. Kharajyr would have ears and a tail. Elves just having ears. Once the clay is shaped, the Puppeteer wraps a layer of moss around it. These signify the 'veins' of the target. After, a layer of hay is wrapped around it all\n\nto both act as the 'skin', and keep it from falling apart. The next bit is when it gets tricky though. The Puppeteer must find a way to extract the blood of the person who they wish to inflict. Such can be done however the puppeteer wants to do such.\n\nWhen the blood is got, even so much as a drop, the puppeteer would push eye sockets in and place the blood in each. They would take hold of the puppet and take a breath, holding it into their chest. They would invision the person that the puppet will be\n\ntied to, imagining him or her as the puppet, before letting the breath escape them and imagine it flowing into the puppet. The connection would be made, and the target would feel a dark presence awakening within them.\n\nThe next step would be complicated. In the end, it would also be similar to the first bit. The Puppeteer would imagine either an emotion or feeling- likely starting with something along the lines of anger. They would take a breath and hold it, imagining\n\nthe very concept of the emotion, before releasing it and willing it into the puppet, likely holding and squeezing its head whilst doing such. Holding the head allows for ease when doing mental curses. As a begginer, the Puppeteer would only make the\n\ntarget mildly annoyed, whilst recieving about half of said anger back upon themselves. Other emotions are easily practiced and learned even without the teachers guidance. Later in learning, the Puppeteer may learn how to inflict pain upon their targets as\n\nwell as horrible curses. Anything the puppeteer can think of can be done, and the more skilled they get the less drawback they recieve. Lower skilled Puppeteers would only hold the connection for twenty elven minutes. Higher skilled could hold them for\n\ndays on end, casting different curses upon someone, although only one at a time. Eventually, the Puppeteer is taught how to create new curses, which is when it is harder to tell what is happening with their victims.", ""),
        StaticBook("-Fire Evocation-", "§bGarsto 'Spark' Leaf", "{-----------------}         Fire Evocation\n{-----------------}This book is about Fire evocation.\n\nThe Fire Evocationists conjure appears to be real. But it is fake. One does not have power over the elements. For an Evocationist to conjure fire fr\n\nvoid they have to understand the element in the real/physical world first. The easiest way of bringing Fire into the physical world would be to light a torch by using Evocation or by creating a fire which then lights a fire. As a mage becomes more\n\nexperienced they can eventually form balls of Fire which they could shape into objects of Fire.\n\n((The Next part of this book is OOC. Its mainly for ones who already know Magic but want to Emote it. It is OOC. Remember that...\n\nGarsto is focused on a spot on a hay bale in front of him.\n\nis twitching a tad with his eyes locked on the position of the hay bale. He is muttering something. \n\nA tiny faint orange flame appears on the hay bale.\n\nThe flame gets smaller and blows itself out.\n\nGarsto falls back into a chair in fatigue.\n\nThat was an example of a Tier 1.\n\nThe next is Tier two.\n\nGarsto is concentrating on an unlit torch in front of him.\n\nHis forehead is sweating and he is breathing heavily.\n\nA Spark flickers on the coal in the torch.\n\nThe Spark lights the coal which results in the torch being lighted.\n\nGarsto's kitchen is now lit by the torch.\n\nStumbles in Fatigue.\n\nThat was a Tier Two. Next is a Tier Four.\n\nGarsto is concentrating with his hand outstretched towards the cow.\n\nHe begins to breath heavily and his forehead is sweating.\n\nHe mutters something. Flames erupt from his hand spinning into a shape.\n\nThe Shape looks something like a small dagger. Its not clear though.\n\nOpens his eyes and mutters something sending the fiery dagger towards the cow. \n\nThat was all OOC remember.))\n\nIts suggest that you meditate to help your self connect to the void. This can help you improve and go through tier 1.  At Tier two the user is able to hit a target most of the time. At the end of tier two the mage will be experimenting with conjuring Fire\n\nballs. Its said by Tier three the mage can conjure small fire balls successfully which they can conjure as Explosive or just normal. They can also vary the temperature of their fire. \n\n((Ooc: If you dont emote Fatigue you aren't doing it right.))\n\nUnless you are tier five and you are conjuring a small Spark. Even if you are Tier five you can still have Fatigue depending on how big the flame. Attempting to summon white hot flames. eah, not a great idea. You would die of heat. Or lack of Mana.\n\nSummoning fire from a distance takes time. ((Ooc: Summoning fire ON or BENEATH someone isn't allowed.)) You cant mold flames until you start to reach the end of Tier two. Even then you can only just about mold it into a ball of fire. With difficulty.\n\n((Ooc: Controlling a flame that is in the Physical world and was made in the Physical world, not drawn from the void would be considered power gaming.)) You will have increased heart rate, breathing heavily and will still get sweaty at levels above tier 3\n\nFrom personal experiences I learnt that when pulling from the void it feels like 'tugging a rope to pull something from nothingness.'\n\nI hope this book helped you with what you were looking for about Fire Evocation.\n/Signed Garsto Leaf./\n\n((Ooc: If I find you use this for some description wether its for the lore of your magic application or anything else. I will make a comment on your post saying its a copy of what I wrote origionally for when I tried to apply for magic.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Red Velvet Cake", "§bSamantha Ashby", "Red Velvet Cake\n----Required Ingredients----\nHalf a cup of butter\nTwo cups of sugar\nThree eggs\nTwo tablespoons of salt\nFour tablespoons of refined cocoa\nOne teaspoon rose red dye\nOne cup cultured buttermilk\nOne tablespoon vinegar\n\n----Ingredients Continued----\nThree cups of flour\nOne teaspoon vanilla extract\n\n-----Frosting Ingredients-----\nTwo cups of creamed cheese\nTwo cups of powdered sugar\nOne stick of butter\n-----------------------------\n\n1. Gather all ingredients and prepare your oven. Your worksite should house two bowls, a wooden spoon, a whisk, a cylindrical baking pan, and a pastry knife.\n\n2. After gathering the required ingredients and tools, set the half-cup of butter into the bowl. Begin mashing and pressing the butter with your wooden spoon until it reaches a cream-like state. Gradually add the sugar as you cream the butter.\n\n3. Crack the eggs against the side of the bowl, and deposit the yolks into the mix you created in step two. Mix well.\n\n4. Take the cocoa powder and the rose red dye, and pour them both into a seperate bowl. Mix well. Pour into main bowl after mixing.\n\n5. Add the salt, flour, buttermilk, and vanilla. Beat well with the whisk after adding each item.\n\n6. Add the vinegar last, and stir mix the batter until the surface is smooth and free of bumps caused by dry ingredients.\n\n7. Pour the batter into your baking sheet, and set the sheet onto the highest rack in your oven. Check back often, and ensure the fire never licks the bottom of the sheet.\n\n8. Clean any tools that need to be re-used, as well as your mixing area.\n\n9. In a clean bowl, add the butter and cream cheese you set aside for the frosting. Once again, mix until creamy.\n\n10. Add in the powdered sugar, while continuing to mix all the ingredients together. When it's a full smooth cream, add in the vanilla.\n\n11. Make sure the frosting is  smooth and creamy, suitable to taste. Wait for the cake to finish baking.\n\n12. When the cake is finished, extinguish your oven's fire. Use a set of leather gloves to remove the baking sheet, as it will be quite hot.\n\n13. Remove the cake from the sheet. If this is difficult, take a knife and slide it around the edge of the sheet to seperate the cake, then take up your gloves once again and turn the sheet over. Don't worry too much if any sticks to the sides of the pan.\n\n14. Cut the cylindrical cake into three even sections.\n\n15. Use your pasty knife to spread the frosting over the top of one of the sections. Afterwards, take one of the non-frosted sections of the cake, and set it upon the frosting. Repeat.\n\n16. If done right, your cake should have three layers, with frosting between each layer. Spread more frosting around the sides and top of the cake, so it seems as if it's a single, solid mass.\n\n17. Should any cake remain stuck to the inside of the pan, which is highly likely, scrape it from the pan. Sprinkle the cake shavings over the top of the cake, as it will make the cake more aesthetically pleasing.\n\n18. Cut, and enjoy.\n\n------Red Velvet Cake------\nA somewhat exotic and uncommon confection, it's known for it's unique colouring.\nIt's somewhat acidic taste is highly acquirable, though the vinegar can be excluded if one simply wishes for a colourful chocolate cake.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sorrow", "§bThe Inquisitor", "The breastplate of another champion. His exact 'placing' in the Glade's timeline is unknown, but it's obvious that he cared about the place deeply. While not being a religious man by any-means, he had his morals.\n\nHe entered The Glade with a group of soldiers, although he was the only one to stay. He found peace within the Glade, and quietly becme it's guardian under the watchful eye of Aureus.\n\nThe sorrow he feels comes from having to kill the very fellow soldiers he entered the Glade with, in order to protect it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alteration §0\n§0Originally by: §0\n§0Lefkos Amethil §0\n§0Copied and edited by:§0\n§0Cheza\n\n-- == What is mana?§0\n§0In simplicity, mana is an invisible substance that encompasses us and everything we see. Even lowly rocks have mana residing within them. What makes people different than objects in terms of mana is the fact that we, as Descendants,\n\nare capable of growing and manipulating our mana pools. §0\n§0\n§0-- == How come we see mana when something is transmuted?", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Crineas Acosta§0\n§0Mali§0\n§0Age unknown§0\n§0Yellow hair, blue eyes, fair skin§0\n§0Despite appearances is infact male§0\n§0Azulines ex-husband.§0\n§0Upset over Azulines mental suicide and has blamed me, presumes he has the ability to track me down.§0\n§0Situation may feed negatively\n\nupon Mirabells psychology and physical well being.§0\n§0Crineas may need to dissapear, concider usage of Crineas' previous knowledge.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunai : Rangers", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Origins ~*~\n\nDuring the reign of Braen Elendil, the Adunian Lord came to see that with the ever rising population of their race, he would soon need a military to keep order instead of relying on the good will of his citizens. And so, he asked his\n\nbrother Cirimas to gather the most elite and loyal soldiers he could find, and bring them before him. The names of these four men were never recorded, but it is known that one was of house Lorsmor, and another of house Loyola. The five men stood before\n\nBraen, all were well trained in the arts of stealth, the longsword, shortsword, dagger and longbow, learning from their fathers and their father's fathers who had to outrun and hide from the Rhodir and other men of Owyn Godwinson during their exodus from\n\nIdunia. Braen decided that based on their traits these five men wouldbe known as the Adunian Rangers, and they would serve as their race's first personal military force. Over time, Cirimas and the four rangers slowly built traditions and organization\n\nthroughout the order, and gained more men along the way.\n\n~*~ Uniform ~*~\n\nTraditionally the rangers had no official uniform, but they were told to stick to a certain code to do with what items of clothing they wore;\n\nthe rangers would wear leather boots, fingerless leather gloves, a leather belt, a large coat and a cloak over the top. The coat of Cirimas was passed from Captain to Captain in the rangers, as was occasionally his cloak. All of this would be over the top\n\nof whatever other clothes they wished to wear.\n\n~*~ Fort Arendil ~*~\n\nThe rangers lived in a large cave system under the hill which Al'Ildic stood upon, though the caves had been renovated to be more like an underground\n\nfortress. Said fortress was named after Arendil, the last King of Idunia, and was meant to be used as a fallback point if Ildon ever came under a siege that it was unable to hold off. Sadly, in the final battle of Ildon in which it fell to the undead, few\n\nmanaged to get inside the fortress before it's gates had to be shut to save those inside.\n\n~*~ Watchtowers ~*~\n\nAs the Adunian Kingdom spread over the land, the ranger's decided that they could only keep order in Ildon itself from\n\nfort Arendil, and would have to find a way to do so in the towns, farms and estates that surrounded it. And so the watchtowers were built all over the kingdom. In each watchtower, a single ranger would live along with up to 15 other initiates whom he\n\nwould use to keep order in the surrounding area. The Garrison of each watchtower was rotated every fortnight.\n\n~*~ Traditions ~*~\n\n-The Final initiation for a ranger was for him to be taken out into\n\nthe woods where he would swear an oath of service to the Adunian Race.\n\n-No women or men of non-Adunian blood were permitted to join the rangers.\n\n-An heir to the Adunian throne would have to spend five years in service\n\nto the rangers before he could become lord.\n\nIt is often thought that it was tradition that all young men joined the rangers for several years after they turned seventeen, though in reality seventeen was simply the age where one was permitted entrance\n\ninto the order, and over time it became a popular trend to join the rangers as soon as one was allowed.\n\n~*~ Ranks ~*~\n\nRanger Captain: Supreme commander over the Rangers.\n\nFirst Ranger: The Captain's most\n\ntrusted ranger, and therefor second in command.\n\nRanger: The primary rank of the Adunian rangers, and only the most elite warriors in Adunian society were offered this position.\n\nInitiate: The recruit rank of Rangers, most never made it\n\npast this rank. \n\nAuthor's note:\n\nI myself attained the rank of First Ranger, in the time of Elysium.\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al-Nur Menu!", "§bAmin Al-Sham", "Al-Nur Spring Bakery & Inn§0\n§0-------------------           Menu§0\n§0-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Owner: Amin Al-Sham§0\n§0Location: Al-Khaleed, Haria, Isle Of Asul.§0\n§0-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Baked Goods 2-5 Pg§0\n§0Meals 6-9 Pg§0\n§0Drinks 10-11 Pg§0\n§0-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n\n      Baked Goods§0\n§0-------------------Bread 0.5 Minas§0\n§0baguette 1 Minas each§0\n§0Croissant 1 Minas each§0\n§0Pancake .5 Minas each§0\n§0Toast .2 Minas each§0\n§0Caramel Bread .5 Minas each§0\n§0Honey Bread .5 Minas each§0\n§0Chocolate Pancake 1 Minas each\n\nCream Pancake 1 Minas each§0\n§0Butter pancake 1 Minas each§0\n§0Maple Pancake 1 Minas each§0\n§0Honey Pancake 1 Minas each§0\n§0Cake 15 Minas each§0\n§0Cheese Cake is 15 Minas§0\n§0Chocolate Cake 20 Minas\n\nSweet Cake 20 Minas§0\n§0Pumpkin pie 15 Minas§0\n§0Chocolate Pie 15 Minas§0\n§0Cream Pie 15 Minas§0\n§0Mushroom Pie 15 Minas§0\n§0Cannoli 15 Minas§0\n§0Plain Cookie .5 Minas§0\n§0Butter Biscuits .5 Minas§0\n§0Chocolate Cookie .5 Minas§0\n§0Triple Chocolate Cookie 1 Minas§0\n§0Brownie .5 Minas\n\nCaramel Cookie .5 Minas§0\n§0Ma'amouls 1 Minas§0\n§0Fortune Cookie 1 Minas§0\n§0-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0------------------>\n\n-------------------          Meals§0\n§0-------------------Sandwich 1 Minas§0\n§0Potato Chowder 1 Minas§0\n§0Mashed Potatoes and cheese is 3 Minas§0\n§0Mushroom Stew 1 Minas§0\n§0Pumpkin Soup 1 Minas§0\n§0Fondue 1 Minas§0\n§0Chicken Soup 1 Minas§0\n§0Mutton Soup 1 Minas\n\nRabbit soup 1 Minas§0\n§0Vegetable Soup 1 Minas§0\n§0Beef Soup 1 Minas§0\n§0Chicken Stew 2 Minas§0\n§0Beef Stew 2 Minas§0\n§0Mutton Stew 2 Minas§0\n§0Rabbit Stew 2 Minas§0\n§0Chicken Noodle Soup 2 Minas§0\n§0Mutton Noodle Soup 2 Minas§0\n§0Rabbit Noodle Soup 2 Minas\n\nVegetable Noodle Soup 2 Minas§0\n§0Beef Noodle Soup 2 Minas§0\n§0Cooked Chicken 1 Minas§0\n§0Fried Chicken 2 Minas§0\n§0Stuffed Chicken 3 Minas§0\n§0Steak 1 Minas§0\n§0Prime ribs (beef) 2 Minas§0\n§0Meatloaf 3 Minas§0\n