        StaticBook("The Matriarch", "§bThurak'Yar", "THE MATRIARCH   \n\nThe tale of the daughter of Dragur.\n\n\n\nRe-Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 21'st of The First Seed, 1489.\n\nFirst born of the brood of Dragur, a female, molded in his image, and adopting his unquenchable thirst of sheer knowledge. \n\"The sun will awaken each new day, followed by the rise of the moon, that will light the seemingly endless nights, and during\n\nthese nights it will be the Stars which will guide you. This land in which you were born in will teach you many things. And as you come to learn, you will share the knowledge which you have come to acquire in the hopes that the ones you come to\n\nshare with learn from it. This is my dream.\"\n\nAnd so the Daemon fell into a seemingly eternal slumber. Many centuries have come to pass since that day, and he collection continued to grow. Unfortunately, some had used bits of knowledge she had\n\nshared with them for their own greedy purposes. They didn’t believe in her ways of “Shared knowledge for knowledge”, and wanted it without giving anything in return. They found the place in which she kept all her books, scrolls and scrawlings, and began\n\nto steal whatever they thought would bring them wealth and power. Upon returning, she felt a sense of violation and mistrust, but knew and understood that time itself would heal those feelings. She began to scrawl everything she could remember from what\n\nwas stolen from her, but they were merely tattered fragments compared to what she once had. Hope had reached her a few years later when she found one of her books amongst some ruins and rubble. She began to hope that the others\n\nwill come to reveal themselves once more.\n\nThus, the Matriarch wanders the land, in search of the items that were taken from her, but also still learning what she can from her travels and from the land. By merely observing and keeping scrawls of what she has come to witness, to finding\n\nbooks, novels and scrolls from past and present civilizations of the land. This is her passion... And her only purpose.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "§bDiane Farsight", "=+-+=\n    The Monster\n       Manual\n       =+-+=\n        \n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Diane Farsight\n\n       Foreword\nThe world is a dark place, and it's filled with dark things. This book, and others like it, will hopefully inform you of what is out there, and how to deal with them. After all, Ignorance is a most insidious killer.\n\n      The Blob\n================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: Blobs are generally docile animals shaped like big piles of goo. Their size can vary greatly, but they tend not to surpass 6 feet in height. Their color varies, but will usually be\n\nbe the color of the enviornment they live in. Furthermore, they are covered in an outer layer of dry skin that protects them from extreme heat. Because of this, they are often found in hot climates. If enveloped by a blob, suffocation is the only way it\n\nkill you, as their bodies have no acidic properties.\nWeaknesses: Blobs are quite susceptable to cold, making Thanium a perfect weapon against them.\nCreation: Blobs can create more blobs by splitting themselves apart, creating two, smaller blobs.\n\n     The Ooze\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Oozes are the volitile cousin of blobs. They have the same shape and color, but can be much larger and territorial than their counterpart. Their size can become a staggering 5\n\nmeters in height, and their body produces a potent acid capable of dissolving flesh and metal alike. Also unlike blobs, Oozes prefer the cold, and lack the outer skin that blobs possess. If you ever need to tell an Ooze apart from a blob quickly, use your\n\nnose. Oozes will smell much more acrid.\nWeaknesses: Oozes are slow and notably flammable. The best way to deal with one is to set them alight, then run while they burn.\nCreation: Oozes can split themselves into more oozes, just like blobs.\n\n  The Giant Ooze\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: On occasion, there will be a sighting of a Gargantuan Ooze. Often they come from forgotten cave systems opened by earthquakes, or humanoids digging too deep. They are like\n\nOozes, but much larger- usually over 10 meters in size and capable of dissolving massive castle gates in a matter of minutes. Weaknesses: Fire will still kill gargantuan Oozes, but it is imperitave that you do not attempt to hide from them- there is\n\nalmost no stopping one if it begins chasing you.\nCreation: Unknown. Normal Oozes should split into smaller Oozes before reaching this size. It is hypothesized that extended time in cramped conditions underground allows an ooze to grow to this size.\n\n  The Flesh Worm\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: The tunnel worm is a subterranian monster of epic proportions. It's full length is unknown, but it is easily several meters in diameter. Most of it's life is spent boring\n\nholes in the earth for it to travel in, often straight through stone. A cave created by a Tunnel worm recently will always be perfectly circular, and ribbed to allow the tunnel worm to maneuver within it easily. It is hypothesized that the Underdark\n\nbeneath the dwarven lands of Anthos was sculpted by the errant burrowing of tunnel worms.\nWeaknesses: Any place that isn't perfectly fitted for it's body, such as large caverns or the surface.\nCreation: Unknown.\n\n     The Drake\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: A Drake is, in essence, a corrupted dragon, like those spoken of in legend. Unlike their bretheren, Drakes are much smaller in size and easier to defeat. Despite this, they\n\nare still capable of flying and breathing fire, and as a result require a large body of able men to be killed safely. When killed, a drake's body will dissolve entirely, but if one can manage to retrieve some of its scales without killing the beast, they\n\ncan be used to great effect in alchemy.\nWeaknesses: None.\nCreation: Legend has it that drakes are born when a dragon is overcome with taint. This, however, has never been witnessed.\n\n   The Alchemical\n       Chimera\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: An alchemical chimera is a fusion of two animals. It is truely an unnatural beast, created by a devious use of alchemy. Chimera come in all shapes and sizes,\n\nbut all will resemble the combination of two  natural beasts. They are mindless beasts, virtually untamable, and gluttonous for flesh.\nWeaknesses: : Time. A well created Chimera will last, at max, for 2 to 3 years.\nCreation: Alchemy.\n\n The Dark Chimera ===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Through the use of drakkarian magic, the normal conditions for a chimera can be subverted, allowing for fully adult humans to be partially fused with parts hewn from\n\nanimals. The result is a fully intelligent, remarkably stable chimera. Many dark chimera are no more than victims of dark mages, but this is not always the case. Great care should be taken when dealing with one.\nWeaknesses: None\nCreation: Alchemy\n\nMixed with Drakkar Magic.\n\n    The Vodnik\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Vodnik are tiny, fish-like creatures that inhabit rivers and lakes. When vodnik encounter a corpse of any sort, they will begin filling and infesting it. The corpse will begin\n\nmoving of it's own accord, and begin dragging anything so foolish as to disturb it's water under with it, to become infested as well. Eventually, this process will crescendo until a small army of shambling corpses inhabit an area. This makes clearing\n\ndifficult.\nWeaknesses: Attacking the arms and legs of a vodnik-infested corpse is your best bet. Cutting off the head should have no effect.\nCreation: The Vodnik reproduce by laying eggs in the corpses they inhabit.\n\n  The Giant Crab\n===================Danger: High\nDescription: An enormous crab, about 15 meters across, 5 meters high, and chitin thicker than plate armor. If they see you, they will try to kill you. . They attack anything that moves,\n\nmembers of their own species included.\nWeaknesses: Their eyes are vulnerable, but should you lack for arrows you should try attacking their underbelly, or failing that, playing dead.\nCreation: Unknown. They certainly do not reproduce.\n\n    The Ghost\n===================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: A corporeal entity that is not yet ready to leave this world. Specters have several stages of 'unlife'. Stage one specters are always gray, and flit in and out of existance constantly.\n\nWhat seperates this stage from the others is the fact that, without fail, the spirit will not be able to come to terms with the fact that they are already dead. They usually need a large amount of persuasion and occaisonally hard evidence to make them\n\nrealize this. Stage two specters already realize that they are dead, and are able to begin learning to control their abilities more effectively. One of two things happen to stage three specters. They will either turn blue and become good, or turn red and\n\nbecome pure evil. This is usually in response to how well they were treated in their unlife, or how evil they were when they still lived. Powerful specters are capable of invisibility, minor manipulation of physical objects, and ejecting ectoplasm.\n\nWeaknesses: Spectres can be banished with a single swing of a weapon, especially holy and gold instruments. They can and will come back to life later, however. They are also unable to cross even the thinnest of gold lines.\nCreation: Spectres are\n\ncreated when someone dies, but cannot come to terms with their own passing. They become stuck betwixt.\n\n    The Graven\n===================\nDanger: High\nDescription: Graven are evil spirits who died carrying a great obsession in their hearts. As it drove them in life, so to  does it drive them in death.These spirits will wander the lands,\n\nendlessly pursuing their unattainable goal, and the pursuit of that goal itself becomes the very fuel that keeps them alive. Above all else, do not look a Graven in the eye. Their eyes are portals into their maddened soul, and will instill a lasting\n\nmadness into the hearts of those who see it.\nWeaknesses: A graven can be banished easily with any weapon, but is particularly susceptable to gold, and holy objects. Likewise, they are unable to cross any line made of gold. In special\n\ncircumstances, is also possible to banish them forever by completing the task that drives their madness.\nCreation: Gravens are created when a truely obsessed person meets an untimely demise.\n\n   The Apparition\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: An apparition is an amalgation of many, many lost spirits combined for one purpose, and that purpose is pure evil. Apparitions are malicious, and very dangerous to fight.\n\nThey are capable of incredible acts of telekinesis and illusion, beyond what any living mage could ever accomplish. Normally, apparitions are bound to a central pillar, marked by many skulls and skeletons littering the area around it. If you come across\n\none such pillar, is vitally important that you DO NOT DAMAGE THE PILLAR IN ANY WAY, SHAPE, OR FORM. Destroying the pillar will weaken the beast temporarily, but afterwards it will be able to roam the world at large, bringing great chaos in it's wake.\n\nWeaknesses: An apparition is significantly more powerful than a spirit. The use of gold weaponry can keep it at bay, but the banishment itself lasts only mere moments. Only a very thick ring of gold can contain it. The only way to kill them\n\npermanently is through the aid of a team of Clerics or Shamen\nCreation: The exact origin of Apparitions is murky. From what can be gathered, they are formed from the death of many individuals in one place, at the same time.\n\n  The Boogeyman\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Yes, the boogeyman is real. Well, was real. The only known boogieman is currently dead. Boogeyman are sentient collections of bugs that swarm around a central corpse. Based on\n\non the only known boogeyman's example, boogiemen are intelligent, and extremely murderous, taking pleasure in killing innocents. When endangered, the bugs inside the boogieman will scatter in all directions. Because of this, when hunting the Boogiemen it\n\nis imperative that you take him by suprise.\nWeaknesses: Boogeymen are weak to fire, and crushing implements. Gold hurts it, but a sword will not have much effect on the swarm.\nCreation: Unknown.\n\n     The Oolog\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: The Olog  is roughly twice the size of an orc, and  nearly three times as stupid. A product of large amounts of orcish inbreeding, Ologs were raised for having muscle and size,\n\nand their bodies show it. Still descendant of Orcs, they also are capable of bloodraging, making them twice as dangerous.\nWeaknesses: Ologs are stupid. I mean, really stupid. Use that to your advantage.\nCreation: These creatures are\n\n(loosely) considered Natural' beasts, and reproduce normally.\n\n    Conclusion\n\nThis book has merely scratched the surface of what lurks in the night. Expect more books in the furture.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Stay Alive, Atheria.", ""),
        StaticBook("V Veritatis 6", "§bJacob Chapel", "Verbo Veritatis\nSixth Edition\n23-3-1480\n\nIn this edition:\n*Knights Rebellion\n*City of Dwarves reclaimed\n*The Karovian Column\n*Words from the Emperor\nAnd much much more!\n\nReporters needed for the newspaper\nDear readers, as always we are in great need of reporters for our esteemed newspaper, especially now Ralph Riley has stepped down from his position because of his prolonged battle with illness. Since patronage has\n\nbeen secured, we are able to pay much better rates for articles. As a reporter you can expect up to 500 minas per article!\n\nThe work is freelance, and you are paid per article delivered. Please contact Jacob Chapel if you are interested.\n\n((Contact me (Pepernoot) ingame or on the forums!))\n\nThe Knights Rebellion\nIn one of the greatest moves of treachery in our time, Maric Varodyr, once Grand Knight of the realm, and part of the Order of the Red Dragon has taken up arms against the Empire. After word had reached the Emperor that Maric was\n\nconspiring against the integrity of the Empire, intending to break it up into pieces. Immediately the Emperor dismissed him from his position, but Maric fled to the Keep of Angren and barricaded himself in there, along with a few rebels.\n\nOur grand Emperor demanded Maric to leave the keep, but the traitor defied these orders and claimed the keep for his own. Hiding inside the keep he proclaimed himself King of Renatus, a claim so audacious and without any real claim to the title,\n\nhe must surely be absolutely mad drunk on power.\n\nAs of now the traitors are still hiding behind the walls of Angren, awaiting their certain and inevitable death. Quoting our Emperor: \"Do not recognise this traitor who has so aptly deemed fit to call\n\nhimself King without any form of legitimization from the Church or the faith. Fight back against the foreign tyrants who would dare infringe upon our sovereignty, despite their signing of various treaties intended to ensure such would not be so.\n\nYet do not fight because of who you are, Highlander, Heartlander or Farfolk. Fight because by the creator above, you will never allow such a spineless snake-tongued worm as Maric Varodyr to sit upon the throne of humanity”\n\nCarry on Carrion!\n\nThe City of the Dwarves reclaimed\nSince the reconquest of the dwarven capital, the dwarves have been very busy to rebuild and reclaim their old capital. Nearly all signs of the Undead occupation have been removed and a lot of work is being done to\n\nrebuild the homes of the dwarves, under the guidance of Lord Balek Ironguy and Thurland Grandaxe, the architects of the arts guild. The new city will be completely situated in the mountains, with farmland in the valley in front of the entrance to\n\n the mountain home.\n\nThe new city has been named Kal’Karaad, and it should be ready for habitation in 2 saints days ((11 November)). We of the Verbo Veritatis wish the dwarves happiness and prosperity in their new capital, and hope that it may last\n\n a thousand years. Sadly the dwarves have not returned our goodwill to help in the current rebellion of the knights, and have retracted their offer to come to our assistance.\n\nFormation of the House of Magnates\nThe Emperor has formed Oren's first legislative body! Known as the House of Magnates, it consists of representatives, or magnates, of all the nobles of the realm, along with the burghers of Petrus. The higher one's\n\n title is, the more representatives and votes, one gets. The body votes on appointing various ministers, akin to privy councillors, who make up the government. It is led by the Lord Chancellor who acts as virtually any under-king to the Emperor,\n\nworking on the day to day affairs of the realm. Currently the Chancellor is Joachim var Sarkoz, a learned barrister from the court of King Francis who has been appointed by the Emperor to help facilitate the establishment of the Magnates while the nobles\n\nand emperor focus on the military expenditures at hand. He shall rule for three years, before he is either voted in again by the various Magnates or a new Chancellor, or known more colloquially as the Prime Minister, is appointed by the Magnates.\n\nLet us hope Prime Minister Joachim can guide our country to glory!\n\nHoly ward over Petrus\nOn the 10th of The First Seed, mages have cast an undead weakening ward over our grand city of Petrus. The main effects of this is to dispel the effects of their magics. The mages creating the magic, one of them being the ancient\n\nwizard Blundermore, forged a magic crystal and lifted it up into the air, defying gravity. From the crystal lights and other magical effects originate, bringing a feeling of safety and calm over the city.\n\nThe populace can rejoice over this noble effort of the mages, and it is hoped that the ward will keep the undead away for a long time.\n\nThe Karovian Column\nA Tragic End\nOver to the news from Karovia this week, and it appears that her husband’s reluctance to give her a child has finally pushed poor Lynn Rovin over the edge. The other day, her body was found lying at the bottom of\n\na cliff face, her stomach punctured with knife wounds. Though it has not yet been confirmed, early evidence appears to suggest that the blows were self inflicted. What an unpleasant end to what could have surely been a most enduring marriage...\n\nThis newspaper would like to extend its deepest condolences to her widowed husband, the Imperial Prince, Aleksandr Carrion for his tragic loss.\n\nIn other news, yet more spook-filled sightings of the Imperial Prince’s late twin brother, Yakov Carrion!\n\nAs reported in Edition Five, little is known of Yakov’s decision to betray Oren to the Undead scourge, though recent events suggest he has returned to to seek vengeance against close members of his family. We can only hope that the guard remain viligant\n\n in these dark and dreary times. In brighter news however, Aleksandr is said to have found a new wife to replace his dearest beloved. Rumour has it that this is said to be Lynn’s very own sister! We suspect it shall not be long before we have another\n\nroyal wedding on our hands!\n\nSo dear readers, with his wife’s demise and his brother’s fall to the Undead, where will Aleksandr turn now? Find out next time in the Karovian Column of Verbo Veritatis, Edition Seven!\n-Our anonymous source in Karovia\n\nWords from the Emperor\nTo the loyal fellows of Orenia,\n\nThough some minor rebellion plagues our lands, a simple matter it will be to drive out the meager forces assembled under the traitor Maric Varodyr.\n\nSuch a petty uprising is of little consequence in the grand scheme of our Holy Empire, such writing on this day regards the welfare of our capital, Petrus.\n\nWhen I had first been elected by the Electorate to serve as Emperor,\n\nPetrus had been little more than a ghost town. Now I am happy to say Petrus is the single most populated city in not only our realm, but of the world itself. This cannot be attributed to I, but to the true heartlanders of Petrus who have graced this city\n\nwith life. Petrus stands as the jewel of our modern world, in not just the strong economy, but in terms of cultural regards, social mobility, and military might. \n\nNowhere else in Athera can one find a public library with such a vast array of knowledge\n\navailable to the public, nowhere else in Athera maintains our efficient system of free food, and nowhere else in Athera upholds a city guard as do our Wardens of the Imperial Watch, a Watch at current roster twenty-four men strong.\n\nThe average daily income to Petrus coffers is 5,000 minas. The average yearly budget for the Imperial Watch is 20,000 minas. Petrus maintains a budget of 44,000 minas for building improvements and public works. Average yearly tax income is 4,000 minas.\n\nPetrus holds 53 separate plots, of which only 8 are not filled at the time of this writing; 43 plots had paid taxes last tax cycle. Truly the economic structure of Petrus is unmatched by any city in the world, and this does not take into account the great\n\nndustrial capability of our Holy City. Within Petrus are produced the finest weapons and armor in the entire world, with the most efficient labor force in the world harvesting vast quantities of wheat, ores, stone, and wood everyday.\n\nUnlike the treasuries of many other nations, the majority of goods produced are not stashed away but sold as surplus to the citizens of Petrus, weapons and armor worthy of Kings can be found for open sale and in quantity, at a pittance compared to what\n\none may find at the cloud temple auctioneer.\n\nThough there is much more than just numbers to Petrus, I hope this has given some insight into our holy Capital and I am proud for all the fellows of Petrus who make our city the jewel of the world.\n\nCreator watch over us all,\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion\n\nReturn of the Order of Saint Amyas\nThe Order of Saint Amyas has been reformed, with Adrian de Bar as its new Grand Master. Shockingly though, Adrian quickly pledged his support to Maric’s traitorous cause and was convicted of treason.\n\nAfter persuasion by Oren, and a lot of mercy on the side of the Emperor, he was returned to the fold quickly though. Hopefully he is wise enough to not betray Oren again.\n\nWe hope that the Order will become a beacon of purity and righteousness, especially in these dark times, and that honest God-fearing men fight for its cause.\n\nPetrus tavern under new management\nAs the old Throdo has not been able to properly take care of the tavern at the central square in Petrus, the tavern has been granted to a new owner. The tavern has been renamed “the Drunken Dragon”,\n\nand it has been quite busy indeed.\nThe Verbo Veritatis wishes Sam good luck with running the tavern, and may many drinks be drunk!\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nWe hope you enjoyed the newspaper, and remember: Athera’s greatest bookstore, “Books of Oren”, is the publisher of this great paper. There are shelves upon shelves of amazing books for incredibly low prices. Visit us at Abbey Road 13, Petrus!", ""),
        StaticBook("Wolf Druids Tome", "§bThe Wolf Druid", "I- Power\n\nThe soul attracts that which it secretly harbors-that which it loves, and also that which it fears. Thus circumstances do not make the Druid; they only reveal him to himself. It means that blessedness, and not wealth, is the measure\n\nof right thought; misery, not poverty or lack of family is the measure of wrong thought. A Druid will find that as he alters his thoughts towards the Nature and the Aspects, Nature and Aspects will alter towards him. For you will always draw near toward\n\nthat which you, secretly, most love. The Races surge with uncontrolled passion, are tumultuous with ungoverned grief, and are blown about by anxiety, doubt, and the wars and wills of Aenguls and Daemons. Only the wise Druid, only he whose thoughts are\n\ncontrolled and purified, can make the winds and storms of the soul, and indeed the world, obey him. The greatest achievement was at first, and for a time only a dream. Just as the oak sleeps in the acorn, and the bird waits in the egg,\n\nso dreams are the seedlings of realities. Beware therefore of what you dream of. For some dreams are given by the Aspects to inspire us by what may yet be. Others are planted within us by others, foul seeds that we harvest to our destruction.\n\nII- Pride\n\nThere is but one way to truly gain mastery over nature, and that is to realize you cannot truly master it at all. It masters you. When one attempts to force it, compel it, command it, or otherwise exercise dominion over it-the\n\nover it-the power flees like a timid bird. This is because the Aspects know our innermost thoughts. They know how we intend to use Nature’s Gift. Man may deceive other men. But one simply does not deceive the Aspects.\nIf their will is sought,\nthey will\n\ncome. If we emulate the principals by which is thrives, they flourish in us. Pride is poison to them. In reality, there is perhaps not one of our natural passions so hard to subdue as our pride. Disguise it, struggle with it, beat it down, stifle it,\n\nmortify it as much as you please. It is still alive, and will every now and then peep out and show itself. You will see it perhaps, even with in the most sacred grottos of the realm. For even I, the Arch Druid, could conceive that I had completely\n\novercome it, I should probably be proud of my humility. A desire to be observed, considered, esteemed, praised, beloved, and admired by his fellows his one of the earliest, as well as the keenest dispositions discovered in the hearts of the Races.\n\nMy advice to new Dedicants is to squelch it all their days, for those desires lead to ruin.\n\nIII- Doubt\n\nMany Dedicants arrive at the Groves with passion already instilled in them. They yearn to learn, they carry drive, and zest, and youth, and curiosity.When they enter our great tree, they have nothing, and leave with everything.\n\nHowever, a few lose what they have. The rigorous trials of Dedicancy begin to take their toll on them, or they submit their thoughts to the subtle poison of doubt. Not even an Arch Druid’s power can cure it, for these students do harm to themselves.\n\nThe mind, like the body, can be moved from sunshine into shade. They submit themselves to the slews of myriad ways of Aenguls, Daemons, and the trickery of man, and they yield before this great power to sway one’s faith in the Aspects’ might. Those of you\n\nwho would stay and train inasmuch as you strip yourself from jealousies and fears, and humble yourself before the Aspects, for you are not sufficiently humble, the veil over your eyes shall be torn and you will see. See all their glory and power, and know\n\nyou are beloved. A servant of the earth, and wild. Having conceived of their attunement, a Druid should mentally mark out a straight pathway to service, looking neither to the right nor left. Doubts and fears should be zealously starved.\n\nThey are disintegrating elements which break up the straight path, rendering it crooked, ineffectual, and useless. Thoughts of doubt and fear can never accomplish anything. They always lead to failure. Purpose, energy, power to do, and all strong thoughts\n\ncease whenever doubt and fear creep in. The will to do springs from the knowledge that we can do. He who has conquered doubt and fear has conquered failure in all his endeavors, both as a Druid, and a person.\n\nIV- Blight\n\nIn every era there comes a moment when the collective thoughts, whims, and motivations of arcane delvers become so self-absorbed, so malignant, so unheeding that nature itself revolts. Man scars the land such that it-\n\nfinals rebels against him. Man scars the land such that it finals rebels against him. As thoughts can spread despair and death like seedlings of weeds strewn by the wind, so they must eventually draw the Druids to pluck them out. The vetches must be\n\npulled, roots and all. When this happens, the Aspects cease to bless, and instead they curse. Instead of healing, they spew poison. It happens so swiftly and terribly. The ancients of the Wayward’s time gave it a name, this culling process that blackens\n\nthe world. They named it after a wasting disease that occurs in once-healthy groves of trees. They called it the Blight, and the first of these, the Great War.\n\nI put this quill to paper here now so that others do not make the mistakes I did in my youth. Blinded by war and hate, my transgressions were many, and hard to earn penance for. Though I served the Aspects diligently for many lifetimes, I fear that in my\n\nheart, I have failed them. May the Aspects look kindly on me in the afterlife-\n\nXal ussta stath xunde mir dosst elamshinae, Nemmisae.\n\n-Wolf Druid Ouity, Retired Arch Druid of the Order, Elandriel Grove", ""),
        StaticBook("requiem for a g", "§bSlots", "white women\ndrugs in my truck\ngunning down afros", ""),
        StaticBook("~Wheat Poem~", "§bDedicant Renn", "Renn's Poem\n\n~~\n\nA golden glisten of summer sea,\nGraceful arms waving to and fro.\nA warm sensation runs through,\nA feeling of protect and peace bestow.\n\nSoft movements from a gentle breeze,\nGrace, prosperity is of Nature's own.\nThin straws of strength and vigor,\nA sense of light against the unknown.\n\nLand's children of grain,\nTreated as a gift that provides life.\n\nA gift of quelling formidable hunger,\nA might savior of times of strife.\n\nA life of giving, a seed to a stalk,\nO' Nature, grant me day and week.\nThat the grains retain their numbers,\nFor a life without wheat shows bleak.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro. Alchemist", "§bRosso", "Forward:\n\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities, and traditions.\n\nChapter I: \n\nThe Recipe for a Good Alchemist.\n\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist: a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions. For those who wish to follow the noble path of an Alchemist, you must first\n\nconsider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\n\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize that it is simply an effort to save you.\n\nIf you do not possess these qualities, dear reader it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself and others. Now, allow me to go more in-depth about what these traits mean, in order of their\n\nimportance to an Alchemist: Patience. Alchemy, I'm afraid, is not a fast nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time for their elembic to boil so that the extract of your ingredients may be collected for use, or simply\n\nwaiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time it takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my opinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital\n\nto an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula consisting of 25 \"parts\":\n\n>7 parts waiting (brewing, waiting for the elembic's water to boil.)\n\n>5 parts setting up, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n\n>5 parts testing (making sure your potion works.)\n\n>3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n\n>3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and collecting the condensation using an alembic.)\n\n>1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n\n>1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\n\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely dull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated\n\nand rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish. So, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\n\nCreativity. Please note that I am writing here to explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something completely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in\n\nthe art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There comes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more\n\nexplanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their own extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This\n\nis much more difficult that it may seem... but I shan't go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but rather, an introduction to the science.\n\nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone who is impulsive and stupid... 'overly' enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of enthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience.\n\nEnthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of the list instead of the top, is simply because by\n\nreading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\n\nChapter 2:\n\nThe Life of an Alchemist\n\nThe Lifestyle.\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guilds need Alchemists, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the\n\nmost fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one location whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them.\n\nIn my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one's options before taking a job. This is not to say that an Alchemist /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choose a life of reclusion and\n\nintroversion--preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency. As an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and\n\nwounded. These paths will play  large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one who makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who creates healing serums as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are\n\nof no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of a guild. This is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing\n\nmuch of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could have a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however--and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of\n\nthe science--think of it more as a specialization. I, for example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds… even research companies.\n\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\n\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\nMany jobs seem to have a set \"morality.\" Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trustworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and is, much like\n\none's business opportunities dictated by the Alchemist's specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more \"evil\" morality, as they would likely find their work\n\nwith small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a \"good\" morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people. There are not set rules, of course, a healing\n\nAlchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is neutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\n\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\nThis section will be somewhat small, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist's abode will generally have only one constant: a lab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain\n\nan Alchemist's supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement… Well… The earth seems to be a bit more resistant to explosions than wooden or cobblestone walls.\n\nFarewell:\nI thank you, reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.\n\nAn Introduction to the Alchemist\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Mariana Illianos", "§bKale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Mariana\n\nAge: 22\n\nRace: Human\n\nGender: Female\n\nCondition/Injury: Originally came in for a check up, but discovered a strange discoloration within the patient's mouth. Turned out to be a sexual disease.\n\nTreatment plan: Patient should place mint leaves on the tongue to ease the swelling around the otter wallks of her mouth. She will be taking in plenty of fluids watching carefully of what she touches to prevent spreading it around: Contagious\n\nIt is reccomended that she stay out of work for at least a month, and come back in two weeks.\n\nDoctor: Kale\n\nCost: Will be charged on next visit. About 15 minas and a extra five for the check-up\n\nDate: 14th of Malin's Welcome, 1523\n\nEnd result: Will determine the next step when patient returns in 2 - 5 weeks.\n\n*Doctor Kale's signature would be here*\n\n\n~ Doctor Kale", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul II", "§bMarch Ash", "I hate the City. It is the ultimate culmination of all our sins against nature, the greatest perversion of our brain. Be they made of corpses, or cobbles, they are evil, all the same. I will break them. This sandstone rises high, but even the greatest\n\nconstruction by Men cannot withstand the eternity of nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn IX", "§bMarch Ash", "Sitting here, watching the sunrise, it would be nice to lay back and let the light wash over me. To rest until nature comes to consume me. To die peacefully. To pass my mission onto another. And then I stand up, and turn away from the sun,\n\nbecause my resolve is not dead, yet. I must kill the City, and all those who would ever support it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Lover's Day.", "§bKili Al-Deen", "they shine brightly in the moon lit gaze,i have traveled near and far yet seen not such beauty as this\nlike a diamond strong and proud yet pretty and pleasing to the eye.their touch is of a gentil flower on a warm sunny day,their voice is soft and\n\ngentil that fills the heart with a warm reassurance and a aw that makes you feel as thuo you have been touched and carryed away by a cloud,you get lost in their gaze as one gets lost in a sunset and your mood rises like the sun in the dawn. you yearn\n\nto be around them with and want to see their smile and happyness you feel as if its your duty to make them smile and joyfull.thy are my warm sunrise and Beautiful jem.to rise before you and make you your favorite dish and bring you roses of compasi\n\nhonnor and love that goes to no one but you,My dear love.\n___________________\n\n         By:Kili Al-Deen\n      (ibraheemc2000)\n\nnotes from writer:\nI made this for the enjoyment of the read and the warmth of the heart-Kili Al-Deen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Moonlit Eyes", "§bKili Al-Deen", "In moon Lit Gaze I saw Her Eyes,in which made my heart fill with crys, if i would fall for you it would be my demise!\nbut can I live my life with out your eyes?\nin the nights i Lie adrift in thoughts of your silky hair,and in the days i have the\n\nstrangth to kill a bear! and when I see you my heart races like a hare. Yet I wish you can see me amongst the croud,I shall say hi,I shall not now,days go by i see her smile, if i say hi its like a mile! oh such agony if a day goes by it will feel like\n\napart of me will die.\nAlas Alas it canot be more i will do it tonight!\nwhere i saw her and her eyes i will walk that mile and spare the bear for this night! the moon lit glaze fills her eyes by the tree she stands on that night i make my walk up\n\nslowly feeling more and more alive,what will i say what will i do for years now and i have not thought it thruo. i stand with her face to face struck by her dazziling eyes and beautiful silky hair until she made a warm smile like none ive ever seen on her\n\nface,and to my amaze,\nher cheeks looked ablazed.she came closer,i didnt know what do to.then i told her\"I Love You.\"with a second of silence she smiles and turns around.I walk back home in the moon light with my head down until i hear a sound\n\nso I turn around as i hear a gentil voice say \"I Love you too.\"\n\n\n        By:Kili Al-Deen\n       (ibraheemc2000)\n-------------------\nI made this because I was bord,i hope you injoy it and one day say it to your love i also planed this\n\nto be a poem but toward the end of it i couldnt find ways i could make it rhyme Hehe.\n___________________", ""),
        StaticBook("How2KillMonsters", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Monsters\n        and\n   How to Defeat\n        Them\n\n    by Seth Calith\n\nMonsters roam our lands, and a good fighter has to know how to repel them as well as their strengths and weaknesses. In this book, the reader will find a guide on how to defeat each beast using either a bow or a sword.\n\nZombies\nZombies are creatures that, wanting to attack, follow you around. With that knowledge, a bow is a useful tool to defeat these monsters. The key to this fight is charging a shot in your bow while running. Once it is charged, shoot the arrow to\n\nhit it while still charging another arrow.\nIf it is of your preference to use a sword, you can take advantage of the Zombie’s low terrain-calculation properties. Try to stand higher than its head so that it is unable to strike you.\n\nSkeletons\nThe average skeleton is not as strong as the zombie, yet deadlier because of his fine use of the art of archery and bowmastery. It is recommended to use a sword against such creatures since they are bad in close combat and can only\n\nshoot at a determined rate.\nTo do such, circle around it fast enough so you can avoid its arrows, which is not recommended unless you are wearing good armor. When it fires, sprint towards it and slash him as hard as you can. With an average iron sword\n\nand a good reaction, you can defeat it while only taking one arrow, probably to the knee, due to its position upon death. If you can’t dispose of these requirements, you will have to study its rapidness of shot or withstand some more arrows, which is not\n\nrecommended unless you are wearing good armor.\nFor profficient bow-wielders, a duel can be had against one of these creatures. One should find a place to cover oneself and do so. When it shoots, wait for the sound of the arrow to crash against your\n\nhiding place and leave it. Shoot it once with a good aim and hide again. It will surrender sooner or later.\n\nBlazes\nThe blazes’s combat is not very different of the skeleton's, and with the blaze shooting fireballs instead of arrows, three at a time. If using a sword, follow the steps for the skeleton with a slight change. Wait for three shots to be fired,\n\nnot one, and make sure you don’t step on the fires set ablaze by the blaze itself. Do a similar thing with the bow. You can know when he is about to shoot because it fires up.\n\nSlimes\nSlimes come in various sizes, and upon death they divide into smaller ones. Use a bow to defeat all but the smallest, that are inoffensive and can be easily defeated with a sword.\n\nEnderbeings\nThese are strange beasts. They can move from a place to another in a blink, known as teleporting. When fighting one, the only tip I can give you is to jump in some water. Oddly, these beasts are hurt by it, so it will die in its chase.", ""),
        StaticBook("The All-Theory", "§bArchibald", "The Theory of Everything, by Archibald Vallero\n-------------------\n\n    In this tome, I wish to explain to all my beliefs on why things exist with direct connection to the realm known as the Void. At times, you might be confused. This is entirely\n\nunderstandable given just how abstract this idea of mine might be.\nIf any of this offends you, I will let you know right now that I did not intend to offend or undermine anyone's religious beliefs. If that is what you believe I intended to do by the\n\ntime you've finished reading this book, then sorry. \n\nNow, let's begin.\n\n       The Void\n-------------------\n\n    Many readers probably have no idea what the Void is, which is why I've decided to begin this with an explanation so that non-mages can be at the same level of understanding with mages as to what the Void i\n\n     The Void, in short is a dimension where everything exists simultaneously along with nothing. It is all that is and all that will ever be, but at the same time there is nothing there. One point I should emphasize while explaining this is that the Void\n\nIS another dimension. Implant this into your mind: the Void is a completely separate dimension to ours. Now, the use of the Void to mages is simply to draw the ability to create from it. Another keyword I'd like for you to remember is 'creation.' It will\n\nbe mentioned continually throughout this tome. As said before, voidal mages are able to create an array of elements and entities by exhausting their mana, which is essentially every living being's life force. Mana flows through our veins, and with it we\n\nare able to connect to the Void and bring about lightning, flesh, fire, water, air, earth, 'raw' energy (arcane energy), and the ability to alter the world or the people around us through different types of illusion or alteration. We use the Void to bring\n\nabout the CREATION of something or another that would otherwise be inaccessible to non-mages. Now, all of us have a mana anchor in the void, which is what it sounds like. Our mana, while in our bodies, is also connected to the Void, and this is what\n\nallows all non-mages to become mages. Now, with this explanation, I wish to bring up my theory.\n\n    The All-Theory \n-------------------\n\n    So, now you understand what the Void basically is. Good. Now, what if I told you that, since the Void is a dimension where anything is possible and, while it is in a constant state of balance and\n\nunbalance, it was still able to create /everything/. What if the dimension is the epicenter of ALL creations? What if it was even the creator of /our/ Creator? Think about it like this . . .  Mana can be found in all living, organic beings. This means\n\neven grass, trees, all abundances of animals, and us. This mana is what allows for there to be a mana anchor, weak or strong, to the Void for all beings. While the grass you stand on might have an extremely weak mana anchor, there is mana there\n\nnonetheless. Necromancers can drain the life from anything with mana in order to power themselves, meaning that, indeed, all things have mana. Even the stone of castles or the earth beneath us might have mana, though it might be in such an insignificant\n\namount that nothing can really be done with it. If we move up the chain and start with trees, there's more than likely more mana in them than both grass and stone, since Graven's are capable of manipulating their own mana to creator a connection or bond\n\nwith the tree that allows it to stay there. The tree is also involved in this process, though, by allowing for their to be a connection in the first place. Perhaps they have enough mana to have such a thing be done. Next is us Descendant races.\n\nWe are able to cast spells that closely resemble elements we can observe in modern day life, but with more manipulation involved. I won't go into specifics, but it requires the touch of our minds to create ice sculptures, fiery animals, and other such\n\nabnormal things. \n\n    Now, I did say that mana flows through our veins, but what if, just like stone, our skin, bones, and other bodily particles also contained mana? We are beings of mana, from the bottom up. All other things are made of mana,\n\neven if it is difficult for mages to tell. This leads me to believe that we were all created by the Void, but with middle-men inbetween the process of our creation. \n\n    Let's delve further into the nature of the Void for just a moment. We can use i\n\nto create a myriad of things. Here comes the confusing part of this theory, but I will try to summarize it as such first before explaining.\n\nInanimate materials have low mana, not able to create anything. We are animate along with animals, and some\n\nanimals are capable of being magical while us Descendant races can connect with the Void to create. Aengudaemons are powerful, capable of creating amazing and wondrous things, an example being the Arch-aengul Aeriel creating the Ascended, or Metzli\n\ncreating the entire race known as the Kharajyr. This type of creation is far beyond the Descendant races' abilities. Then there is the Creator, which many believe has created the aengudaemons and all of us. This could be true. But now, answer this for\n\nme: what created the Creator? The answer to this, I have deduced, is the only dimension capable of bringing about everything material and animate, or the Void itself. It is to my belief that the Creator is simply a powerful entity that has a immensely\n\npowerful connection to the void, allowing for this being to acquire a massive amount of mana and the ability to create the aengudaemons and us all. Essentially, the Void brought about the powerful being known to us as the Creator, which had a greater,\n\nintense mana anchor and mana pool, that this creator of ours was able to use everything available to it in the Void (which is everything conceivable) to create this world, and the aengudaemons. \n\n    There's also a pecking order, I've noticed. The\n\n Void is the creator of all, it is a dimension/entity/being capable of granting power and creating any and everything, and as it had created our Creator, since the Creator has such a close connection to this dimension, this being's powers closely\n\nresembled the Void's. Then there are the Aengudaemons, some ranking higher than others. They have an immense amount of power, but have physical restrictions. An example would be the fact that they can only shape our realm through us lower beings, as\n\nthe paladins resemble Xan's hand, or the clerics resemble Tahariae's hand, or the cultists of Ikuras resemble Ikuras's hand. Then there is us. We do have a connection to the Void, but at only at a great cost. The more we master arts that allow us to\n\ncreate wards, elements, or bring things back to life or even drain mana from other living beings, the more our muscle mass and sanity disappears. We are thinning out. We are losing ourselves as we continue. This leads me to my next theory.\n\n    The All-Pure\n-------------------\n\n    As said before, the more one attempts to bring something into this realm, the more mass, or particles of themselves, they lose. I've lost around twenty pounds while still maintaining a healthy diet as I\n\nattempted to master conjuration, but if I were to try and learn even more evocations or magicks of another kind, I would be even far more thin. Weak. Decrepit. We lose our corporeal selves as we delve into the power that allows us to create. This leads me\n\nto the other observation that the more closely connected one entity is to the almighty Void, the more of 'themselves' they lose, or, rather, the more they lose their body, the greater their ability to manipulate elements and, naturally, everthing else.\n\nWhy this occurs I'm not /entirely/ sure, but an idea that's come to my mind is that it's the cost, as everything has a cost. The cost for becoming more god-like in being is that you lose what we know as ourselves. We lose our body and our 'mind.' This can\n\npotentially explain why Aengudaemons are able to have such great power in their own realm, creating what they want at their own whim, but as soon as they enter an earthly vessel to interact with us, they only become the equivalent of a powerful mage,\n\nrather than some being with the capabilities to destroy and create. The cost for having a body like ours is that they lose some of the powers that makes them 'them.' At the same time, once they are killed in this world, they are still able to ascend back\n\nto their own and retain their original powers. All very interesting, indeed.\n\n    The real aspect of the All-Pure theory involves 'purity.' In my belief, the closer one is to obtaining the ultimate power that the Void grants, creation, the more\n\n'pure' they are. In this sense, non-mages are not as pure as voidal mages. Inanimate objects aren't entirely as pure either, and are on the bottom of the order. This does not mean that one being deserves to live and one to die. It is simply my outlook on\n\nthings. Now, with this new theory, it is fact that mages who are granted their power from an aengudaemonic force, such as paladins, clerics, and cultists, are not as pure as voidal mages. The purest one can be is when they are able to siphon\n\ntheir spells of creation from the Void, the dimension where, believe, all life truly originates! The reason why paladins and clerics are not as pure as voidal mages is due to the fact that they are drawing their power from a being lower than the Void,\n\nand rather from an aengudaemon which had been created by the Void. They are drawing their power from a weaker source. The Void is the most powerful, truly. This could also explain why they, the aengudaemonic siphoners, are able to retain some muscle\n\nmass and weight while us voidal mages are weakened. We're closer to reaching the nature of the 'nothing-yet-everything' Void, while they are granted their power from a lower and less powerful being which takes its power from the Void. If they were to cut\n\nout the middle-man in their magicks, they would end up being like the voidal sorcerers: able to create more elements and manipulate this world further, yet at the cost of them losing more and more of their bodily matter. \n\n    With this in considerat\n\nI do believe that there is a Creator. I believe, though, that our Creator is, frankly, a being who has such a powerful connection with the Void that it was capable of bringing our kind about along with the aengudaemons. But the true Creator is the voidal\n\ndimension. \n\n    With this, I conclude my novel. I hope you, brave scholar, found this piece of literature interesting and profound in its content. Thank you.\n\n         -Archibald V.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilven Monks", "§bMonk Argyll", "Principles\n       of being a\n           Monk\n\n          Part I\n     The  History\n\nKeldrith, Lord of the Sun, began his story like the rest of us mortals. He was the son of a king, King Celetiman of\n\nCelestrian, a kingdom in what now know as Asulon, the city of Arethor, and thereby prince and heir to the throne. At the time the story begins, Keldrith was but a 13 year old boy. Thouthsand of villagers dwelt in the kingdom, and all of them loved\n\nKeldrith, for he was simply a kind and charasmatic person. As time went on, despite his age Keldrith fell in love with a princess.\n\nKeldrith's love was the princess Rellenia of a small city-state outside the Kingdom. He noticed her one day,\n\nwhen she was not at a political debate, like his father was most hours, but at the markets, purchasing wheat form a poor farmer and paying him twice it's worth. He was enthralled a maiden that was so beautiful, yet so kind. He went to the king of the\n\nstate, Taron, and offered an arranged marriage between the two. Taron approved his proposition, and a marriage was planned between Rellenia and Kledrith. Now one might that Rellenia would be unhappy about an arranged marriage, but quite the contrary, she\n\nhad loved Keldrith from the moment she met him. They were happily wed, and when Celetiman passed on, Kledrith took over as king. When time saw fit, they went out into the world, leaving the general of the military in charge.\n\nTime went on, and Keldrith, twenty-six, and Rellenia, twenty-four, arrived at a small hamlet known as Flowershire. In Flowershire lived a young man known as Tariel,  a kind farmer who the two liked instantly.\n\n Keldrith, Relenia, and Tariel became the greatest of friends,and when they left the hamlet, Tariel came with them. They explored all of Asulon, cherishing each others’ friendship, and having many adventures.\n\nSadly, their joy could not last. It was said that they came to a wasteland in Asulon, nothing was there except for scorched rocky mountains. Not much is known about what occurred within the valley, except a farmer a few leagues\n\naway said he saw a bright flash of light from that direction soon after they entered. In truth, they were murdered in this place. Their bodies faded into the earth, as death does, and their belongings vanished as well, all except for one each.\n\nIt was said that, upon their deaths, the Creator took pity upon their souls and bound them to three minerals, Rellenia, a diamond, Keldrith, a bar of gold, and Tariel, a gem of Lapis Lazuli.  He then waited, for he knew what would\n\n happen to the three friends. The stones stayed upon the ground for centuries, and all around them, the wasteland transformed into a paradise, water flowing from the mountain peaks reformed the land into a valley of grass,\n\nforming a pool in the center, the stones laying on the shore. Such a paradise could not go unihabited, so the Creator chose a single woman and a single man to discover it.\n\nThe man, William Alerus, and the woman, Vera Alerus, set up a home their, not knowing the stones the lied upon the shore, until one day, their child went down and explored. Amanda Alerus, their child, discovered the stones, and called her parents.\n\n They admired them, but something prevented both William and Vera from touching the stones, so Amanda went up and gathered them in her arms. The second she touched them, bright lights shot out, the colors of the stones, and they flew into the sky,\n\nthe gold to the sun, the lapis to the stars, and the diamond to the moon.\n\nThe Creator admired the friendship of the original three,and left knowledge upon the new three mortals living upon the shore.\n\n He told them the story of the stones, and instructed them to build a Temple in their honor. They trained a messenger bird, sending him home to their friends and extended family, speaking of the paradise and the small price to pay.\n\n They brought with them all the materials they could carry and departed for the soon-to-be Temple of the Triumvirate. Work progressed quickly, an immense library going up and the Temple itself a sight to behold. These were the original\n\nMonks of the Triumvirate.\nThe Celestial Triumvirate, as Keldrith, Rellenia, and Tariel came to be called, became deities in their own right, demigods of the sun, moon, and stars. They granted their followers\n\nthe ability to heal those who needed it by invoking their name in prayer, but the most powerful monks were able to do it through sheer mental focus upon them. They blessed the Temple when it was complete,\n\nthat it would be forever void of any illnesses or disease of the outside world, and that it would ever be a safe haven.As time went on, the monks forgot the old ways, becoming lazy and not helping those other than themselves\n\nThe Triumvirate saw this and were angry, so angry in fact that they banished the monks from the Temple, magical wards preventing any from entering the paradise as long as they lived, and longer.\n\n In fact, they did not allow anyone through until the adventurer Wilven Adonan.\n\nWilven Adonan, a young human adventurer, was among the first to originally came to the land through the portal. Upon seeing the people become\n\n afflicted with the devastating curse, Wilven set out to find some way to cure or dispel it. He traveled long through swamps, mountains, and forests and eventually came to a grand mountain range.  At the base of the mountains, he found a partially\n\n collapsed tunnel that seemed to cut through the mountain, so he made his way through it. On the other side, he discovered a marvelous sight.\n\nThis place that he had found was not like the world outside it. It seemed the curse did not affect this pla\n\n Lush trees and vibrant grass covered the place and clear waterfalls streamed down the sides of the mountains. The structures, although collapsed in some places, were beautiful as well.  Another strange thing Wilven noticed about\n\nthis place is that he felt healthier while inside the valley. Exploring some more, Wilven came upon a large structure with several arches. He made his way inside and eventually came upon a hidden tunnel back behind a collapsed wall.\n\nHe made his way through hallways and down staircases and found himself inside a large library. Amazingly, the library was intact and untouched by nature. After looking over several tomes and manuscripts, Wilven discovered\n\nthat this place was built long ago in order to serve as a place of worship for three beings of power, Keldrith, Rellenia, and Tariel. Together, these three beings formed the Celestial Triumvirate which watched over the sky and all below.\n\nWilven wished to discover more, but he first had to bring others to this sacred place where the curse did not reside.\nBy the time he returned to the humans, many of them had fallen to the effects of the curse.\n\nHe collected those whom were still well enough to travel and brought them back to the sacred valley. Once they recovered enough,Wilven sent three messengers to send word to the Orcs, Elves, and Dwarfs that there was a place\n\nfree from the taint of the curse. When the messengers returned, however, they brought with them only a handfull of people. Unfortunately, many of the other races’ people had fallen to either the curse or other unfortunate circumstances.\n\nFeeling reinvigorated by the day, the few remaining people set to work making for themselves a new home in this sacred place.\n\nFor many years, the survivors worked hard to restore the sacred valley to its original form.\n\nWhen Wilven was very old, he called the people together and told them all that he had learned of the Celestial Triumvirate. The people consecrated themselves to the Celestial Triumvirate and constructed a shrine to allow worship to all three beings.\n\nThey formed themselves into monastic order and cloistered themselves from the rest of the world. They chose Wilven as their Abbott and, together, the monks continued to live on in peace taking care of the sacred valley,\n\n giving praise to the Triumvirate, and praying for the curse to be cleansed from all the land. Upon Abbott Wilven’s death, the monks wished to pay honor to his life by naming the sacred valley after him.\n\nFrom that day forward, the place was known as Wilven Sanctuary.\n\n           Part II\n    Laws of being a\n            Monk\n\nI. A Monk must remain neutral. This is for the smallest of argument to that of war.\n\nII. Monks are to remain a kind and gleeful mood, even when angered.\n\nIII. Monk are to not add acessories to their robes unless it is the trimming of the robes- and then it must be one of the colours of the three Triumvirate.\n\nIV. A Monk is free to furnish ones room, but is forbiden to touch anothers.\n\nV. A Monk may never sell goods for profit and personal gain. If under special circumstances, the minas go to the Sanctuary and not the individual.\n\nVI. Monks are obliged to give bread, clothing and shelter to all in need.\n\nVII. If in a situation of which none can come to an agreement, the word of the Elder Monk stands.\n\nVIII. If one acts out of these laws his robes may be taken and released from all duties within the sanctuary.\n\n          Part III\n          Healing\n\nOur healing is done through the Triumvirate. If you do not belive in the Triumvirate, you will be unable to perform any acts of healing. The easiest act of invokeing power from the Triumvirate is\n\nthrough prayer. The more lengthy and the more praise given tends to give off more power. Another way to gain power is to chant the Triumvirate's name in sucsession, though this invoked less power. The hardest way is to invoke through silence, though that\n\nis the hardest to master. Healing works through the power of a selected Triumvirate to represent the caster. If a Monk is a follow of Keldrith, his healing usualy would give of a gold glow, though a Monk of Tariel's healing would be the colour of purple.\n\nResurection is a very obscure branch of healing, but is what makes the Monks so important. Resurection is very difficult to master, and requires the most concentration of all. Once a Monk has mastered silent healing, would he be able to sence the floating\n\nsouls around the temple. With practise, a Monk can revive these souls. Outside of the temple ressurection is much more difficult, and require a vast amount of energy. It usualy requires multiple sessions.\n\nPassive healing is one of the not as well known arts of healing. Around the time a Monk achieves ressurection and silent healing a Monk may unpurposly begin to heal himself, sometimes without one not even noticing, unless it's a grevious wound in which\n\nsparks of the chosed Triumvirates hue will begin bubble out of the Monk's wounds.\n\nChoosing a Triumvirate is one of the hardest decisions of a monk. As know, Keldrith's colour is a deep gold. Tariel is a Lapis purple, and Rellinia is a diamond blue.\n\nthough this makes little diffrence to a Monks healing it often shows off a Monk's personality.\n\nFinaly, we talk about achieving ones robes and becoming a Monk. To become a Monk one has to spend time as an Initiate, in which the Initiates mostly study\n\nbooks such as these as well as farm. Once an Initiate seems ready the Elder Monk tests him on his knowledge. If they pass they are given their robes and become a full monk. \n\nBook Writen by Monk Argyll.", ""),
        StaticBook("Staves", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "The\n          Wizard\n             &\n        The  Staff\n```~~~~~`\\I/'~~~~~'''\n\n\n            By\n Gallidron   Elindrow\n\nThe staff. This iconic piece of equipment is placed firmly in the minds of individuals everywhere as the tool of every wizard and mage. We all can imagine an elderly and bearded wizard, swathed in robes and leaning upon a gnarled staff.\n\nMost of us tend to think that the staff or even the rod and wand are an indispensable part of the mage’s arsenal. while it is in fact useful to a mage and can help to focus their arcane might, staves are, in fact, ultimately unnecessary.\n\nThe staff is a crutch in a literal and figurative sense. They help the often frail, physically weak, or aged mage to stand or to walk long distances. In this way they are of basic utility.\n\nIn the figurative sense these implements are useful in helping a mage focus their powers on a physical point in the world, the end of their staff. This simply makes it easier for a mage’s mind to form the spell\n\nand choose a place to bring it into the world. Magic after all is developed wholly in the mind before it becomes a reality. A veteran mage may have no need whatsoever for such a focus or aid.\n\nAnother use for the staff is to store a spell or spells within it to be cast when certain criteria are met. For example, an evocationist stores the spell, that summons a fireball, within their staff. The spell is set to go off when the mage\n\npoints the staff forward and says the command word or words. This can be incredibly useful, though also potentially dangerous. Make the command word to obvious or likely to be said, and a bystander could accidently set off your stored\n\nspell while you're having afternoon tea. Of course, make the criteria too complicated and you might not be able to get the spell to work when you really need it.\n\nThis of course, doesn’t even go into the possibility of a misfire. At this point you are not casting the spell with the same level of control you would have, had you drawn it straight from the void. The fireball could be set offin any given direction,\n\neven back at you.It is for this reason that a many mages will use a focusing crystal which has the ability to funnel your spell in the right direction.\n\nI, myself, am practiced in the trade of carpentry. As such I have made a few staves in my time. The experienced woodworker or the astute buyer of such things will note that some staves are of better make than others.\n\nThis, to my knowledge, affects nothing that the staff does magically. This is merely a statement of finery and fashion. A finer carved staff is simply nicer to look at and perhaps more comfortable to hold.\n\nOnce again, it is my hope that this book has been both interesting and informative. It is my sincere desire that you are left the better for having read it.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\npublishing date  10th of Deep Cold, 1519\n\nPlease read my guide to arcane magic!\n\n\"An Encylopedic Arcanum\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Melunis the Mad", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Melunis the Mad\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\nI was travelling to a place called Geedin in search of a philosopher called Melunis. This man was said to be the wisest in the land, according to my friend who went there a while back. So I figured I would see what wisdom he could offer me.\n\nI arrived in the town and walked up to a guard. I said,\n\n“Excuse me sir, could you direct me to the man named Melunis?” The guard just laughed and said,\n\n“The only Melunis I know is a madman, you can find him over by the alley.” I thought to myself, this madman couldn’t be the one that my friend was talking about. My friend was a very smart person and wouldn’t confuse a wise man with a madman.\n\nSo to satisfy my knowing of whether or not this was the correct man, I went to the alleyway and saw an old man in rags. I said to the man.\n\n“Are you the man known as Melunis?” to which he looked at me, smiled, and said,\n\n“Indeed so! How can I help you this fine day!” The day was overcast, and cold. I couldn’t see how it was fine.\n\n“Would you happen to know my friend, James Linson?”  The man looked overjoyed at the name and said,\n\n“Why yes! I remember the lad. I do hope he is doing well.”\n\n“Well he told me you were the wisest in the land…” I said, to which Melunis replied with a frown,\n\n\n“Wise? No I’m not wise. I am just a ragged old man in an alleyway. Do I look like I’m Wise?”\n\n“No you don’t.” I said. “You don’t look wise at all.” The man then got a sparkle in his eyes.\n\n”Not wise at all?” said the man. “Well I must agree. You being very well off must know what it means to be wise, as you are in a far better place then I.” The man thought for a second, then said, “Tell me, what does it mean to be wise.”\n\n“Well it means that you know a lot about things.” I said, “Like a smith knows how to smith well, he is wise in smithing.”\n\n“Ah..” said the man. “ So in a sense, being wise is having knowledge.”\n\n“Yes.” I said.\n\n“ Alright, well what is knowledge.” Said Melunis. “As in how would I be able to obtain it to become more wise.” I thought for a second, then said,\n\n“Knowledge is knowing something, and obtained by learning.”\n\n“I see!” Said the man. “But… how do I know I know something.” At this I was a bit perplexed. I said,\n\n“Could you explain what you mean?” The man nodded and said,\n\n“In other words, How do you know what you know is true.”\n\n“Because you know it works when applied to things.” I said.\n\n“Alright.” Said the man. “So knowledge is what you know works when applied to things, but how does that make it true?”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said.\n\n“I mean for example, we could see an abstract painting.” Said Melunis. “You could think it’s one thing, I could think its another. Both works when applied, at least to the individual, but who is right?”\n\n“I guess we would both be right.” I said. “It would be up to the individual.”\n\n“Ah I see now!” Said the man. “So knowledge is what works with the individual. But still, how do we know it is true? Because isn’t the truth universal?”\n\n I began to get frustrated. But… Then I came to a realization.\n\n“I guess the truth is up to the person.” The man looked at me and said,\n\n“So there is no real truth? But what about common knowledge?” I thought for a second and said,\n\n“The common knowledge is what people have a common belief in.” Melunis nodded, seeming to understand.\n\n“But then what is the real truth?” The man said.\n\n“The real truth…” I began, “The real truth is… unknowable. Even if we got to it, people still would have different opinions. And those opinions might have more people believing in it than the real truth.” Melunis smiled at me and said,\n\n“Thank you, I think I understand now what it means to have knowledge.”\n\nSoon after this conversation, I left. Slightly confused, but more understanding.\n\n\n Though now I realized what my friend meant by him being the wisest in the land.\n\nThe End\n\n\"Everything you think you know has to do with what you believe.\"\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser Quotes", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Heil Valdoria===\n\nExcerpts from the speech made by the glorious Kaisereich Decimus Rovin.\n\n\"...racial species must preserve the purity of the blood which Gott has given it!\"\n\n  ====Page One====\n\n  ===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"It is not for men to discuss the question of why Providence created different races, but rather to recognize the fact that it punishes those who disregard its work of creation.\"\n\n  ====Page Two====\n\n  ===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"...revolutionary change in our knowledge and therewith a radical reconstruction of the picture which human history gives us of the past and will also change the course of that history in the future.\"\n   ===Page Three==\n\n\n\n\n     And remember, \n       If you see a glorious member of the Kaisereich, yell\n\n   \"HEIL VALDORIA\"\n   \"HEIL THE KAISER\"\n   \"HEIL DECIMUS\"\n\n ===Approved By===\n\nThe Reich Ministry of Public Enlightenment and Propoganda.\n\n-Goseph Joebbelstein.", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "§bKristoff Herrick", "Wound healing\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet's start by steps\nStep 1- Cleaning the wound. \nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or\n\ndeeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. (ofcourse you need to take the dirt off first if it has dirt in it). \nStep 2- Suttering the wound. \nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread.Sounds§\n\nright? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these...Let's called them sub steps.\nSub Step I Heat up the needle. You need to do that incase of the needle carring any illness.\nSub Step II Clean the thread.You\n\nit beacause you don't want dirt on your wound.\n \nSun Step III-Suttering You start at well the start of the gash or deep wound (Warning this does NOT apply for small wounds.) \nYou'll then sutter like your sewing a rag, a messy and bloody rag\n\nthat screams like a little girl, non the less a rag. \n\nStep 3-Bandaging\nA bandage can be almost anything, a old rag (As long as it's clean) A bed sheet (As long as it's clean) etc. Then you just wrap it around the wound. Done\n\nNote: If there's any sign of infection after or  before you done this process you'll be better off cuting off the leg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Artificial Eye", "§bLillith Winterleaf", "((The book seems to contain page after page of concept drawings and schematics related to an artificial eye, some of the diagrams being extraordinarily complex. There are several notes in\n\nthe margins, as well as a list of materials beside some of the component schematics.))\n\nOuter Casing:\n-Pure Aurum\n-Fine Ferrum Wires\n-Redstone\n\nCare must be taken to form a perfect sphere, impurities of the shape can damage eye socket. Ferrum wires must be as fine as a maiden's hairs. Redstone must be free of impurities, the\n\nlense must be thin, no thicker than a flake of skin, and polished until translucent.\n\nInner Wiring and Circuits:\n-Pure Aurum Dust\n-Blessed Living Slime\n-Enchanted Ender Pearl\n-Ferrum Dust\n-Redstone Dust\n-Avanite Lense\n\nEnder pearl must be flawless, any impurities will cause the enchantment to become flawed. Must be enchanted with a Power rune composed from carbarum for maximum effectiveness.\n\nLiving slime must be carefully filtered and purified. Enhance it with druidic healing several times, use a fairy ring to enhance the effects. Focus on imbuing the slime with healing energy, do not rush the process,\n\ndo it carefully over several weeks, ask the slime to help the eye function and grant you vision. The slime alone will not do this, but it will guide the power from the pearl and facilitate this function.\n\nThe inner casing needs space for the pearl and a coating of slime. Form casing by melting down and combining the pure Aurum dust, Ferrum dust, and the Redstone dust to form a highly conductive alloy.\n\nThe casing must be no thicker than a millimeter, form the front to hold the avanite lense. Avanite lense is a component of light sensors, and  will enhance the quality of vision.\n\nOnce the inner casing is completed, close it within the outer casing, filling the interior with slime, taking diligent care to ensure all air is removed from the artificial eye before sealing the casing.\n\nTo prepare for insertion of the eye, I must remove the blinded eye completely, I will need someone to do this for me, I cannot imagine doing it myself safely. I will cleanse the socket, then coat the eye in living slime and carefully insert it as\n\nas I focus mending energy upon the socket, repairing the natural muscle and nerve connections, causing them to connect to the artificial eye as they did my natural eye, and if everything has been\n\ndone correctly, I should regain my sight through that eye for the first time in over 150 years.", ""),
        StaticBook("V Veritatis 6", "§bJacob Chapel", "Verbo Veritatis\nSixth Edition\n23-3-1480\n\nIn this edition:\n*Knights Rebellion\n*City of Dwarves reclaimed\n*The Karovian Column\n*Words from the Emperor\nAnd much much more!\n\nReporters needed for the newspaper\nDear readers, as always we are in great need of reporters for our esteemed newspaper, especially now Ralph Riley has stepped down from his position because of his prolonged battle with illness. Since patronage has\n\nbeen secured, we are able to pay much better rates for articles. As a reporter you can expect up to 500 minas per article!\n\nThe work is freelance, and you are paid per article delivered. Please contact Jacob Chapel if you are interested.\n\n((Contact me (Pepernoot) ingame or on the forums!))\n\nThe Knights Rebellion\nIn one of the greatest moves of treachery in our time, Maric Varodyr, once Grand Knight of the realm, and part of the Order of the Red Dragon has taken up arms against the Empire. After word had reached the Emperor that Maric wa\n\nconspiring against the integrity of the Empire, intending to break it up into pieces. Immediately the Emperor dismissed him from his position, but Maric fled to the Keep of Angren and barricaded himself in there, along with a few rebels.\n\nOur grand Emperor demanded Maric to leave the keep, but the traitor defied these orders and claimed the keep for his own. Hiding inside the keep he proclaimed himself King of Renatus, a claim so audacious and without any real claim to the title,\n\nhe must surely be absolutely mad drunk on power.\n\nAs of now the traitors are still hiding behind the walls of Angren, awaiting their certain and inevitable death. Quoting our Emperor: \"Do not recognise this traitor who has so aptly deemed fit to\n\nhimself King without any form of legitimization from the Church or the faith. Fight back against the foreign tyrants who would dare infringe upon our sovereignty, despite their signing of various treaties intended to ensure such would not be so.\n\nYet do not fight because of who you are, Highlander, Heartlander or Farfolk. Fight because by the creator above, you will never allow such a spineless snake-tongued worm as Maric Varodyr to sit upon the throne of humanity”\n\nCarry on Carrion!\n\nThe City of the Dwarves reclaimed\nSince the reconquest of the dwarven capital, the dwarves have been very busy to rebuild and reclaim their old capital. Nearly all signs of the Undead occupation have been removed and a lot of work is being done to\n\nrebuild the homes of the dwarves, under the guidance of Lord Balek Ironguy and Thurland Grandaxe, the architects of the arts guild. The new city will be completely situated in the mountains, with farmland in the valley in front of the entrance to\n\n the mountain home.\n\nThe new city has been named Kal’Karaad, and it should be ready for habitation in 2 saints days ((11 November)). We of the Verbo Veritatis wish the dwarves happiness and prosperity in their new capital, and hope that it may last\n\n a thousand years. Sadly the dwarves have not returned our goodwill to help in the current rebellion of the knights, and have retracted their offer to come to our assistance.\n\nFormation of the House of Magnates\nThe Emperor has formed Oren's first legislative body! Known as the House of Magnates, it consists of representatives, or magnates, of all the nobles of the realm, along with the burghers of Petrus. The higher one's\n\n title is, the more representatives and votes, one gets. The body votes on appointing various ministers, akin to privy councillors, who make up the government. It is led by the Lord Chancellor who acts as virtually any under-king to the Emperor,\n\nworking on the day to day affairs of the realm. Currently the Chancellor is Joachim var Sarkoz, a learned barrister from the court of King Francis who has been appointed by the Emperor to help facilitate the establishment of the Magnates while the nobles\n\nand emperor focus on the military expenditures at hand. He shall rule for three years, before he is either voted in again by the various Magnates or a new Chancellor, or known more colloquially as the Prime Minister, is appointed by the Magnates.\n\nLet us hope Prime Minister Joachim can guide our country to glory!\n\nHoly ward over Petrus\nOn the 10th of The First Seed, mages have cast an undead weakening ward over our grand city of Petrus. The main effects of this is to dispel the effects of their magics. The mages creating the magic, one of them being the ancien\n\nwizard Blundermore, forged a magic crystal and lifted it up into the air, defying gravity. From the crystal lights and other magical effects originate, bringing a feeling of safety and calm over the city.\n\nThe populace can rejoice over this noble effort of the mages, and it is hoped that the ward will keep the undead away for a long time.\n\nThe Karovian Column\nA Tragic End\nOver to the news from Karovia this week, and it appears that her husband’s reluctance to give her a child has finally pushed poor Lynn Rovin over the edge. The other day, her body was found lying at the bottom\n\na cliff face, her stomach punctured with knife wounds. Though it has not yet been confirmed, early evidence appears to suggest that the blows were self inflicted. What an unpleasant end to what could have surely been a most enduring marriage...\n\nThis newspaper would like to extend its deepest condolences to her widowed husband, the Imperial Prince, Aleksandr Carrion for his tragic loss.\n\nIn other news, yet more spook-filled sightings of the Imperial Prince’s late twin brother, Yakov Carrion!\n\nAs reported in Edition Five, little is known of Yakov’s decision to betray Oren to the Undead scourge, though recent events suggest he has returned to to seek vengeance against close members of his family. We can only hope that the guard remain viligant\n\n in these dark and dreary times. In brighter news however, Aleksandr is said to have found a new wife to replace his dearest beloved. Rumour has it that this is said to be Lynn’s very own sister! We suspect it shall not be long before we have another\n\nroyal wedding on our hands!\n\nSo dear readers, with his wife’s demise and his brother’s fall to the Undead, where will Aleksandr turn now? Find out next time in the Karovian Column of Verbo Veritatis, Edition Seven!\n-Our anonymous source in Karo\n\nWords from the Emperor\nTo the loyal fellows of Orenia,\n\nThough some minor rebellion plagues our lands, a simple matter it will be to drive out the meager forces assembled under the traitor Maric Varodyr.\n\nSuch a petty uprising is of little consequence in the grand scheme of our Holy Empire, such writing on this day regards the welfare of our capital, Petrus.\n\nWhen I had first been elected by the Electorate to serve as Emperor,\n\nPetrus had been little more than a ghost town. Now I am happy to say Petrus is the single most populated city in not only our realm, but of the world itself. This cannot be attributed to I, but to the true heartlanders of Petrus who have graced this city\n\nwith life. Petrus stands as the jewel of our modern world, in not just the strong economy, but in terms of cultural regards, social mobility, and military might. \n\nNowhere else in Athera can one find a public library with such a vast array of knowled\n\navailable to the public, nowhere else in Athera maintains our efficient system of free food, and nowhere else in Athera upholds a city guard as do our Wardens of the Imperial Watch, a Watch at current roster twenty-four men strong.\n\nThe average daily income to Petrus coffers is 5,000 minas. The average yearly budget for the Imperial Watch is 20,000 minas. Petrus maintains a budget of 44,000 minas for building improvements and public works. Average yearly tax income is 4,000 minas.\n\nPetrus holds 53 separate plots, of which only 8 are not filled at the time of this writing; 43 plots had paid taxes last tax cycle. Truly the economic structure of Petrus is unmatched by any city in the world, and this does not take into account the great\n\nndustrial capability of our Holy City. Within Petrus are produced the finest weapons and armor in the entire world, with the most efficient labor force in the world harvesting vast quantities of wheat, ores, stone, and wood everyday.\n\nUnlike the treasuries of many other nations, the majority of goods produced are not stashed away but sold as surplus to the citizens of Petrus, weapons and armor worthy of Kings can be found for open sale and in quantity, at a pittance compared to what\n\none may find at the cloud temple auctioneer.\n\nThough there is much more than just numbers to Petrus, I hope this has given some insight into our holy Capital and I am proud for all the fellows of Petrus who make our city the jewel of the world.\n\nCreator watch over us all,\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion\n\nReturn of the Order of Saint Amyas\nThe Order of Saint Amyas has been reformed, with Adrian de Bar as its new Grand Master. Shockingly though, Adrian quickly pledged his support to Maric’s traitorous cause and was convicted of treason.\n\nAfter persuasion by Oren, and a lot of mercy on the side of the Emperor, he was returned to the fold quickly though. Hopefully he is wise enough to not betray Oren again.\n\nWe hope that the Order will become a beacon of purity and righteousness, especially in these dark times, and that honest God-fearing men fight for its cause.\n\nPetrus tavern under new management\nAs the old Throdo has not been able to properly take care of the tavern at the central square in Petrus, the tavern has been granted to a new owner. The tavern has been renamed “the Drunken Dragon”,\n\nand it has been quite busy indeed.\nThe Verbo Veritatis wishes Sam good luck with running the tavern, and may many drinks be drunk!\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nWe hope you enjoyed the newspaper, and remember: Athera’s greatest bookstore, “Books of Oren”, is the publisher of this great paper. There are shelves upon shelves of amazing books for incredibly low prices. Visit us at Abbey Road 13, Petrus!", ""),
        StaticBook("IHBH:SA", "§bSer Paul Ryan", "- - - - - - - - - - - -         It's Hard\n    Being Handsome:\n\n  How to survive in \n  Athera, and other\n        life tips\n- - - - - - - - - - - - \n   By: Ser Pavl Ryan\nWith special foreword         by Emperor \n   Tuvya Car\n\n TABLE OF CONTENTS: \n\n- Foreword\n- Authors Note\n- Chapters I-V\n- About the Author\n\n        FOREWORD\n-------------------\n\nMeeting Ser Paul Ryan, much less becoming good personal friends with him, will most certainly be one of the most defining moments of my life. I've seen much in my time as the Emperor of Athera's greatest nati\n\nnever have I seen such strict dedication to greatness as I have in Paul. Whether it was making him part of my privy council, calling upon him to lead a heroic charge in times of war, or simply asking the favor of his attendance to my young daughters\n\nnameday party, I knew I could count on a man as loyal and reliable as Paul. Reading his first book, as well as getting a sneak peak at his upcoming biography, granted me a different outlook on life, and how I live it. Never before have I experienced such\n\na thrilling page turner as I have when reading \"It's Hard Being Handsome\". I recommend this fantastic encyclopedia of majesty to all men and women, regardless of age, race or gender, who one day wish to become sucessful.\n\n     AUTHORS NOTE\n-------------------In my times of travel around the land of Athera, I've come to learn a great deal of things, both through speaking to some of the oldest and wisest masters of \nmany skills, and trial and error as I blundered\n\nmy way through city after city, town after town. I've learnt how to fight great mythical beast, how to drink a \ndwarf under the table, how to hide from halflings, sell my legitimate wares to all kinds of illigitimate folk, and a great deal of other ski\n\n. But if there's \none thing I've learned above all else, it's this; \nIt's hard \nbeing handsome. \n\nHi, I'm Ser Paul Ryan, and this is my book.\n\nMany times through the years, I've been approached by great kings and lowly merchants, all desperate for my advice. I've been the honored guest in many foriegn \ncourts, and handed out justice in my own lands.\n\n I recieved many great awards, both for my continued service to House Carrion and Oren as a whole, and for helping\nout the distressed through all kinds of situations. Yet I soon found out that, no matter how great I was (and trust me, I was great),\n\n my life always seemed....\nempty. By the time I had done all of these great things and achieved knighthood and gentry status, all at the ripe old age of 18, I decided to write down my \nadventures, and, more importantly,\n\nthe rules with which I've come to live life. In the following pages, you too will learn to live by these rules. Good luck, friend,\nand I hope you enjoy it!\n\nCHAPTER ONE (I)\n-------------------Find friends:\nOne of the earliest lessons I learned in life was this; EVERYTHING'S better with friends, friend. Becoming close acquaintance to esteemed men and women like the \nruling class of Oren,\n\nor simply the pal of the local drunk and homeless, friends help you through all sorts of trouble. Need a place to stay? Fine a friend. Need\na loan? Find a friend. Need help breaking Goldsteins' stinking knees, because he still hasn't paid you back\n\nfor that time in the brothel? Find a friend. No matter\nwhere I go in all of Athera, I can always count on finding room and board, courtesy of my good pals. If you really think you're a step above the rest, you can even\ntry to become one of MY frien\n\nand join Paul's Pals™, my adventuring group of heroes. For better or for worse, helping out someone in need of a hand can result \nin some good luck coming your way down the road. Remember my original and trademarked saying:\n\n A friend in need is a friend indeed, who, in the future, will owe you™. \n\nCHAPTER TWO (II)\n-------------------Find fortune\n\nOne of the greatest assets any man has in lifes' adventure is his coin purse.\n\nMany a schlub can be bribed, and it never hurts to have the pocket coinage to buy that\nfancy new automatic crossbow, or perhaps donate to your favorite local political party. But how does one obtain such vast, impressive wealth like that owned by\n\nthe plutocrats of our age, such as Emperor Tuvya, or Ser Paul Ryan? Well, friend, let me tell you; hard work, creativity, and a good bit of honest borrowing can go far. I myself made my first fortune when I founded CapCo™, Oren's premier\n\nentreprenuerial company, which now is valued at roughly 500,000 minas. By working hard to achieve\nyour dream, and marketing your products correctly, you'll soon build the capital needed to further your endeavors, like\n\nperhaps launching a new, better company. Good\nbusiness partners are a must have, and I myself continue to hold close correspondance with my good friend and investor, Jacob Goldstein, of Goldstein & Company. After I safely handed over CapCo™\n\nto the care of my board of directors, my next startup companies, Paul's Pawn & Picking™, Paul's Tonics & Powders™, Paul's Ghost Hunting™, \nand Paul's Travelling Stall™all quickly flourished under my careful experience. Need some help starting down the\n\npath to vast wealth? Try finding a local investor\nto give you a startup fee, and bleed that sucker dry! If you need some immediate cash, perhaps to pay back the loan shark who threatened to break your fabulous \ncheekbones, consider\nborrwing som\n\nsomeone elses valuables and using those to pay. Remember, friends: It's not illegal if you're not caught. \n\nCHAPTER THREE (III)\n-------------------Find your talents\n\nIt never helps to have good qualities, friend.\n\n I myself am incredibly handsome and creative, and possess a myriad of skills that would make a jack of all trades cry\nuncle. But how can you exploit the talents you have? Simple; by deceptively manipulating others. Are you a heavy hitter? Consider\n\nstrong arming your way into the \nlocal tavern, and borrowing some of his ale to sell later at a profit. Small and sneaky? Deceptively sneak into a store after hours, and help yourself to the register. \nOr perhaps you're like me,\n\na reknown inventor throughout the lands, sought after for his political savviness and charm. Remember that in this life, NOTHINGS free. Make\nsure you charge the right amount to give that little girl the location you saw her lost dog in, or to hide that\n\nhalfling running from some hungry orcs. If you don't \ncapitalize on all of your chances to make yourself more marketable, you'll never make it in our dog-eat-dog world.\n\nCHAPTER FOUR (IV)\n-------------------Find adventure\n\nSure, friend, you may be able to talk the talk, but can you walk the walk? It doesn't matter if you've accomplished all of these other steps to becoming great, if you don't USE them! Go out on\n\nroad, and venture into lands previously uncharted. Have a drink at that edgy tavern, or consider stopping by your good dwarf friends\nto see what they've been up to lately. Seeing the world is its own lesson, one that anyone can take, and for free.\n\n Learn how to fight or talk your way out of \nany situation by haggling with the Vanirs over the price of a fish, or wrestling with Orcs in their sand pits. Awe the local milkmaid with tales of your completely\nlegitimate exploits, or spend a night s\n\nat a tavern to cover your room and board. Life in our world is uncertain, friend, but it's always worth checking around the \ncorner to see what kind of trouble you can get into. Fall down and break a leg, or wake up without memory in the temple of thos\n\nmonks who definitly enchanted this\nholy water I can sell you at a discount price? Get back up, and try again. If you're ever torn between relative safety, or a possible adventure, ask yourself one \nthing: What would Paul do?\n\nCHAPTER FIVE (V)\n-------------------Putting it all together, and surviving the process\n\nYes, friend, it's challening to learn how to be as great as me, and even more challenging to try, but the results will always pay off. By combining\n\nmy advice with\na little salt-of-experience you gain on your own, you'll quickly find yourself developing into the man or woman you only dreamed of becoming. Go out there, learn\nyour good qualities, get rid of your bad ones, and make\n\nsome good memories while you're at it. Work your way from the gutter to a palace, and go from using that\nrusty dagger to defend yourself to summoning the most powerful of magics. You will fail at first, friend. After all, no one is perfect.\n\n(well, actually, speak for yourself, bub)\nbut the lessons you learn in your failure will help you in years to come. Inevtiably, the great success you'll achieve will make the lesser peons\nof this great realm jealous of you. They'll wish they had yo\n\ncreativity, your work ethic, and above all, your dashing good looks. There's a great deal I've learned\nmyself in my many adventures, most of all I've found that, yes, it really IS hard, being handsome. But would I ever give it up?\n\nNot for anything in this world, friend. \n\n- Ser Paul Ryan\n\nSome Quick Tips! \n\nWant to get better at those strange moments of your life, when everyone suddenly has magical symbols above their heads, and people start hitting each other? Try \npracticing in your free time with some pals and a wooden\n\nsparring sword, or, if worse comes to worse, learn how to flee effectively! To fight another day, of course.\n\nDon't try so hard to win all of the time, friend! In gambling, tussling, or even a friendly debate, losing can often yield more than winning.\n\nIf you see Paul or one of his many friends throughout the land, consider stopping for a chat or challenge with them, rather than strangely running and jumping by.\n\nPick a skill or service, become talented in it, and learn how to make a living through it. Sell your paintings or swords in a stall, or on the road, like me! Get a job as a petty laborer to garner experience, before ultimately starting a rival\n\ncompany up with stolen secrets, and crush your former boss!\n\nGo outside every once in a while, friend. And I don't just mean leaving your hovel in Athera.\n\n\nHave fun, friend. What else are we here for?\n\n - About the Author - -------------------Ser Paul Ryan is a successful warrior, statesman, and inventor of great reknown. Founder and CEO of CapCo™, and a number of other popular brands, such as \nPaul's Pawn & Picking™,\n\n Paul's Travelling Stall™, Paul's Pals™, and Paul's World Fair™, he was born in the small village of Wesconsen, before squiring under Boris Carrion III. \nKnighted by the late Emperor Peter Chivay for valor extraordinare in the field of battle.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Frost Witch", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "An Encounter with Frost Witches\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\n\nRevised edition\n\nI first learned about the dreaded creatures, known as frost witches, from one of the tomes in the libraries of old Haelunor. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways.\n\nThough as an adult of more mature understanding and greater constitution, I revisited the subject of “monsters” and relearned the available details of the frost witch. They are exclusively women so far as any adventurer who has survived an encounter\n\nwith them can tell.\n\nThey are horrid to look upon in their natural state. Grey skinned with eyes like ice, but it is not so easy to spot one of these slippery creatures for an ice witch is a master of disguise.\n\nThey employ illusion to mask their true selves, that they may, with more subtlety, intrude upon our societies and seek out their prey.\n\nIn fact, as the story goes, a frost witch will adopt the guise of a young woman and sit, crying, in the midst of\n\nsnowy glade. This is done to attract young and hapless men. The clever frost witch will then transform into her hideous self and dispatch the unwitting male then and there, or she will lure him back to her coven to become a grisly meal for her sisters.\n\nThey are, without exception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a “Witch Mother” who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee, she will build her nest\n\nand gather workers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent.\n\nWhen another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience, she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or saddened.\n\nThe frost witch will then “mark” the woman with a curse. Should she succumb to her sorrow she will become a frost witch herself, and thus do their numbers swell.\nIt is reportedly a favorite tactic of the frost witches to seek out a married man\n\nand devour him, then they will curse his grieving widow. In this fashion do they gain both a meal and a prospective member of their coven.\nNot much is known about the curse, and there is no known way to remove it. It has been said, however,\n\nthat if the woman resists her sadness and sorrow that she may endure the curse and not become on of these fiends. Though she will likely live with the curse for the rest of her days.\n\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must seek out and destroy the witch mother. In some cases this is enough to cause the coven to wither and die. In others, however, if a witch who is powerful enough survives, she may assume the role\n\nof witch mother and allow the coven to limp on. In any case, the most foolproof method of destroying a coven is just that, destroy the coven. All of it.\n\nIf one seeks to harm a frost witch I would give them this advice. Strike fast and strike true for you shall not likely receive a second chance. Also, a sellsword of types once told me that gold is good for killing all kinds of unnatural monsters,\n\nperhaps it applies here as well, though I do not know for certain.\n\nIt is important to note that  a frost witch is not a rabid animal, and they can be reasoned with. They are also possessed of terrible cunning and one should not expect the blind fury of mindless monster when dealing with them.\n\nIt is possible to treat with them and in fact they could exist within your own city, your very neighborhood and most would be unaware. They humor of a frost witch is quite changeable and every moment you stand in their presence you are in grave danger.\n\nThe truth is that they are fickle creatures, and there is no telling what a frost witch might do.\n\nIt is said that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them on it that the witch will be bound by her curse to do the clever mortal one favor. Though this is only rumor and would prove both difficult and dangerous to study.\n\nIn closing, frost witches are a dangerous fascination and one should not seek them lightly. They are elusive and hide among the peoples of the world, it is for this reason that we must be ever watchful lest we become their next meal.\n\nI hope that this book has been useful to you, the reader. And that this information will help you, should you ever have….\n\nAn encounter, with frost witches.\n\nBy Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date 8th of Deep Cold, 1516\n\nRevised 18th of Amber Cold, 1520", ""),
        StaticBook("CH Handbook", "§bSaithor", "Introduction\n___________________\nThe Crimson Heart is a guild of Spellswords, Sellswords, Mages, and Scholars all alike, all seeking the same goal, knowledge, power, wealth, and fame.\nThe Hearts of this guild are brothers and sisters by oath.\n\nPaths\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are divided into 3 categories. Knights, Mages, and Mechanists. No matter what path you pick, your brothers and sisters will protect you. And no matter what they pick, you will too.\n\nPeople of Honor\n-------------------Sonoren Klaren: He is the Ace of Hearts, our leader\nTalimeracahe: He is the Red Joker, second in command\nEdwyn: He is the maker of the Crimson Hearth, the guild hall of the Crimson Hearts\n\nTrainers o' the Paths\n-------------------Olympus: Trainer of the sword \nLelien: Trainer of the magic\nVirgo: Trainer of the Mechanists\nSaithor: Trainer of the Bow & Trainer of the Realm\n\nRules\n-------------------1) Ye will protect your brothers and sisters\n2) Knights will remain loyal\n3) Mages will heed and heal\n4) Mechanists will procede and prosper\n5) Obey orders\n\nPath o' Knight\n-------------------The path of the Knight consists of the noble warriors of the Heart. They are the men and women who seek to be armed with a sword, and of those who know how to use a sword, or wish to know. They are loyal to the hearts.\n\nPath o' Mage\n-------------------The path of the mage consists the arcanic people of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the arts of magic. They heed to heal each of us, and will continue to do so.\n\nPath o' Mechanist\n-------------------The path of the mechanist consists of the artisans and merchants of the Hearts. These are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the most money and fame they can get. They will procede to proper throughout life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Side Dishes:§0\n§0\n§0baked potatoes§0\n§0\n§0steamed carrots§0\n§0\n§0rolls§0\n§0\n§0salad\n\nmain dishes:§0\n§0\n§0roasts§0\n§0soup§0\n§0it will most likely be beef or pork sence it is the most abundant animals ive seen in the area\n\nDessert:§0\n§0cookies§0\n§0pies§0\n§0sometimes cakes§0\n§0\n§0it depends on what we have on hand at the current time§0\n§0it would be advised to import food from other lands", ""),
        StaticBook("Zil' Dictionary", "§bgaiusmarius8", "The Magnus Opus\n     of Linguistics\n\nA study on the dialect of Sabunani, the language of the Zyl'Mxktlmy [Zil'Maktumi] \n\nCompiled by:\nYyl'Mxndxbh Xndxlls\n[Yil'Mandabh Andalus]\n\nThe language of the Zil'Maktumi is an intriguing feat of linguistic and scriptology. The Zil'Maktumi have gone through two phases of the development of their own language - Elder Maktumi and Sabunani scripts. The Elder Maktumi is remarkably different\n\nin that the written language does not represent vowels. Sabunani uses certain symbols to represent vowel pronunciation.\n\nA translation device is included to aid the fledgling linguist.\n\nCommon - Sabunani\n1. a/an - x\n2. and - sxw\n3. at - syr\n4. able/capable - txt\n5. before - sxzyd\n6. after - sxzym\n7. allow - yxk\n8. as much as - Rxl'\n9. much - rxm\n10. feed/eat - mlj\n11. seek/search/find - lxm\n\n12. irritate/scratch - gyd\n13. see/view - aytxn\n14. Perspective - Altgxp\n15. mirror - Aytgxb\n16. loose - nyj\n17. I/My - Hxt\n18. are - xy\n19. the - zxm\n20. you/your - xntx\n21. crawl - rlsxm\n22. begin - yxmln\n\n23. We/us/our/them - hxq\n24. he/son - nyv\n25. she/daughter - nyw\n26. few - qyw\n27. conquer/command/control - tlkyg\n28. homage/honor/respect/praise - dxslw\n29. result - vlrxb\n\n30. interest/intrigue/amazing - hljyk\n31. normal - gxzys\n32. King - Mxlyk\n33. study/learn - zys\n34. head - rxs\n35. Deity - Ylxm\n36. soul/spirit - Lyn\n37. Time - Bxl\n38. jar/vessel - bxt\n39. memory - bxjlk\n40. holy - hlr\n\n41. Heaven/Seventh Sky - Skxy\n42. life - tlryw\n43. horizon/edge/shore - qyj\n44. cry - zld\n45. creature/creation/thing - glvyp\n46. animal - gxvlb\n47. heir/inheritor - Fydxtlr\n\n48. self-begot - Ghxr\n49. have - zxw\n50. degrade - glhxt\n51. strange/odd - ghxb\n52. bond/group - pxrmyn\n53. in - hxw\n54. heart -kxlyb\n55. mourn - lymxb\n56. ancestor - gxjlb\n57. enter - cxtyn\n58. sand - rxf\n\n59. portal - slmt\n60. movement - flgyp\n61. up - qxd\n62. word - rxd\n63. action - gyn\n64. level/plane - rygxt\n65. move/travel - vlg\n66. on - ylb\n67. lack of/not/nothing - qxtlg\n68. than - tlg\n69. above - lxk\n\n70. under/below - jxk\n71. plant - frxr\n72. desert - sxhxrx\n73. name - lxmx\n74. peace - hxlxl\n75. table - txwyl\n76. wound/scar - glvyg\n77. every - fxw\n78. possible/liable - qlwxs\n79. guide - nxtlg\n80. ignorance - lxryf\n\n81. ability/skill - glbxl\n82. big/large - ryp\n83. small/mere - tlp\n84. good - nxm\n85. population - hyjxf\n86. situation/condition - qlrxg\n87. clean/polish - wld\n88. bad - mxl\n89. back - txv\n90. is - tx\n91. it - txz\n92. there - tlt\n\n93. their - txk\n94. those - tld\n95. know/known - vlt\n96. that - tyc\n97. cover/shealth/bath - hlrxv\n98. wind - wyhxd\n99. often/accustom/used to - pxl\n100. but/while - vlh\n101. history - wlryt\n\n102. wing - txlyn\n103. rational/intelligent/objective - clvyh\n104. part/aspect - rlg\n105. light - ylyln\n106. happen/take place - rxh\n107. withdraw - hxbyv\n108. then/thus - txqyr\n109. they - txwxt\n110. this - txxyp\n111. these - tlgyq\n\n112. if - vln\n113. with - fld\n114. desire/want/intent - rlflfm\n115. intend/wish - rltlm\n116. rub/smear - qlc\n117. gather/collect - pxrym\n118. kindness - sxtlr\n119. human/man - hxmx\n120. woman - nysx\n121. think/thought - fxvyl\n\n122. yes - gxb\n123. no - nxb\n124. don't - gxpnxb\n125. war/attack - byr\n126. naked/rip/tore - rlvyg\n127. reward - jybxv\n128. through - jxw\n129. warn - dlrys\n130. some - hxn\n131. clay - pywxt\n132. mud - mxd\n133. give - fyv\n\n134. between - rxkyj\n135. highest/ultimate - gxdlrxw\n136. goal/point - gxlxp\n137. since - wls\n138. North - Nlrxt\n139. South - Hlrxt\n140. touch - pxyg\n141. again - pxw\n142. bank/land/drop - ghxl\n143. near - pxv\n144. far/long - qyq\n\n145. native - flgys\n146. be - lyj\n147. resource/item - flk\n148. wise/smart - vxryl\n149. many/alot - wyjx\n150. organize - jxhr\n151. against - fyp\n152. invader - bxhyt\n153. nature - hljxt\n154. blind - gxbyv\n155. groan - fywyk\n\n156. to crack - blnxm\n157. apart - gxsyh\n158. hold - blc\n159. so - xl\n160. what - kxk\n161. where - txn\n162. when - klk\n163. who/whose - kxl\n164. how - mxn\n165. to - hxk\n166. put - mlv\n167. of - xp\n168. frolic/play - byw\n\n169. sun - yly\n170. fertile/healthy/growth - yljyn\n171. raid/steal/theft - rydxr\n172. damn/curse - Yxksyty\n173. from - gxm\n174. follow/stalk - ylc\n175. Federation/Civilization - Fyryrxtln\n\n176. Federator - Fyrxryt\n177. would - fxllt\n178. forget - fxpyn\n179. rise/gain - pys\n180. different - pylxh\n181. city - Mxdynxt\n182. thrive/live - jxklt\n183. yearn - dytxp\n184. for - dxs\n185. argue - gxvyl\n186. split - rybyn\n187 weigh - txj\n\n188. chaos - shlt\n189. child/youth - vxblm\n190. people - zxglk\n191. do/act - gxp\n192. serve/provide - qyn\n193. year - hljxn\n194. continent - ayq\n195. land/earth/ground - axg\n196. stand - gypxn\n\n197. death/stop - jlqxr\n198. power - gryvpxnvxr\n199. poet - dltxf\n200. tall - pyd\n\nGrammatical\n    Indicators\n\n1. prefix 'im/un' is noted with prefix Pyl\n2. Plurality is noted with a symbol '*' at the end of the word\n3. Zyl [Common: Zil] is used to refer to a group of people adjectivally.\n\n4. Adverbs are created with the symbol '/' at the end of words\n5. Past tense is created by the symbol '+' at the end of words\n6. To create gerunds or the -tion suffix, the symbol used is '=' at the end of words\n\nCommon Phrases\n1. How are you?\nMxn xy xntx\n2. Where are you from?\nTxn xy xntx gxm\n3. Hello!\nGxlymyk\n4. To each their own\nHxk hyglm txk yxn\n\n[[OOC: Those who possess this can contact gaiusmarius8 for a fuller dictionary.]]", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Studies", "§bAria Lanyathir", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Ariadni Lanyathir's\nDruid Studies.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n=-=-=- Index -=-=-=\n\nCh 1: Aspects\nCh 2: Blessings\nCh 3: Balance\nCh 4: Cycle of Life\nCh 5: The Order\nCh 6: Totems\nCh 7: Powers\nCh 8: Responsibilities\nCh 9: Ranks\n\n=-=-=-Aspects-=-=-=\n\nCerridwen: Mother of the Harvest.\n\nCernunnos: Father of the Hunt.\n\nCerridwen is the Mother of the Harvest, the Green Lady and the Woman of Morn.\n\nCernunnos is the Father of the Hunt and the Great Huntsman.\n\n=-=-=Blessings=-=-=\n\nCerridwen's blessings cover all harvests and marriages. Newly-weds may also receive the blessing of many children.\n\nCernunnos' blessings are used upon armies and honourable fighters.\n\n=-=-=Balance=-=-=\n\nThe balance of nature is one in which every life that lives is fair and just. None shall perish, both plants and animals, without a natural end. If their end is not natural, then a Druid is able to interfere to save the nature and\n\nwildlife from their unfateful end. However, is a forest is alite due to a natural storm or weather, then a Druid musn't interfere, but rather let nature run its course. This promotes the natural life cycle of all organisms.\n\n=-= Cycle of Life =-=\n\nThe Cycle of Life has 4 phases. Birth, Maturity-Growth, Reproduction and Death.\n\nBirth:\nBeginning of a New Life.\n\nMaturity-Growth:\nGrowth Stages into Adulthood.\n\nReproduction:\nFinding a Mate to create a new life.\n\nDeath:\nLoss of life.\n\nThe Food Chain is the order in which animals eat one another; the\n\n'Chain'.\nDecendants don't have a place in this chain, but would be near the Top, otherwise.\n\n=-=- The Order -=-=\n\nThe Druids are dedicated to preserving the balance of nature. Druids undergo learning and studying in order to establish a strong link with nature; a bond.\nThe Order is open to all races.\n\n=-=-= Totems =-=-=\n\nA Totem is a title that defines and identifies who a Druid is, representing their history, personality and approach to life. Only one Druid may possess a specific totem at one time.\n\n=-=-= Powers =-=-=\n\nThe extent of a Druid's powers are unknown, though they are some of the best healers and are deeply connected with nature. They serve nature, often using their powers in the form of favours.\n\n=- Responsibilities -=\n\nA Druid is a keeper and protector of nature. A Druid works to maintain the balance and peace of nature, possibly allowing the removal of a tree of forest, but expect each tree to be replanted elsewhere in return; balance.\n\n=-=-=- Ranks -=-=-=\n\nDedicants:\nThe students and learners of Druidism, under a Druid Guide.\n\nDruids:\nThe main rank, the middle position of the Order after Dedicants and before the Inner Circle.\n\nDruid Guides:\nThe teachers and 'newbies' of the Inner Circle.\n\nArch-Druids:\nThe heads of the Inner Circle. They maintain all affairs and have direct contact with the Aspects themselves. This is how most orders from the Asoects are\n\nconveyed.\n\nGrand-Druids:\nMiddleman for if a split were to occur.\n\nHierophants:\nRetired Inner Circle members, though still extremely strong. Respectable Druids.\n\nNotable Druids:\nUsually deceased\n\nDruids who have made such an impact on the Order and nature that they're kept on record as High Status Druids.\n\nDemi-Aspects:\nDeceased Druids who have passed on to join the Aspects; One of the highest honours the Order can bestow.\n\nSeekers:\nThe first rank amongst Druidism; People that have taken an interest in the Aspects, the Druids, and their practices.\n\nAcolyte:\nOne who is learning Druidism outside of the Order.\n\nLost Druids:\nDruids that have disappeared without a trace of explanation. Their return may result in punishment.\n\nForgotten Druids:\nDruids that have been removed from the Order, whether it's by death or unattunement, but despite being 'Forgotten', many of\n\nthese Druids are unforgotten due to their accomplishments.\n\nShunned Druids:\nDruids that have been shunned by an Arch Druid, due to their actions that have threatened the protection or peace of the Order. No Druid of the Order is peritted to speak with\n\none, but if a Shunned approached them, they must only say:\n\"Much wind pours from your mouth\".\nIf the Shunned persists, Druids should either ignore them or warn them that defensive action may be taken. This action should be carried out if the Shunned does\n\nnot heed the warning. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=By:\n    Ariadni Lanyathir", ""),
        StaticBook("Medical Std. V1", "§bThe Scribe.", "A Study of Medicine. \nPossibly Volume 1,\nAnatomy.\n\nAssisted by Salazar the Mali'Aheral.\n\n'One learns to figure out the limits of one's body as one travels.' ~Salazar.\n\nThe cadavers of less fortunate travelers make for good study; \nTheir bodies can be found suffering from illnesses or ailments,\n\nand studying them was an urge that could not be repressed.\n\nChapter 1: Circulation of Blood.\n\nThe circulatory system runs throughout the body. It provides blood to various muscles and organs, replenishing them with every beat of the heart. Blood provides Anima to the body, which is the life\n\nforce that drives us all, and gives us energy. Anima may possibly contain a variety of elements that we require to function in life. As one works more strenuously, the circulatory system does as well. This may be because as the body\n\nuses energy, it requires more anima to function at the previous levels.\n\nAilments of the Circulatory System;\n\nA disease of the circulatory system causes the blood to not coagulate where it may normally do so. This causes the patient afflicted with such a disorder to bleed profusely, until magic is introduced.\n\nThis disease is highly rare.\n\nAnother disease is caused by the blood vessels themselves being left open to the air or to water for a long time. This causes blood-poisoning, an infection of the blood itself.\n\nThis can be treated a variety of ways, though none of which are easy. Amputation is the most rudimentary form of this. The next is quick cleansing of the wound with pure water and alchemically based healing potions. The third is to use clerical magic, but\n\nsuch can be considered a panacea.\n\nThis condition is uncommon, as most open wounds are wrapped.\n\nChapter Two; Digestive.\n\nThe digestive system consists of the stomach, smaller intestine, large intestive, and the excrementory system. \n\nThe stomach contains within it a large amount of naturally produced\n\nacid which dissolves food that is consumed through the mouth. After the food is broken down, it seems to be passed through both intestines, where it is absorbed into the body. Of course, these broken down materials most likely filter into the blood system\n\nwhere the blood and the body converts the food to anima. This is why death by starvation can take place. However, the body itself can overstock these necessary nutrients, and cause fatness and obesity.\n\nDigestive diseases. \n\nThe stomach acid can become too concentrated and can break down the lining of the stomach. This can cause severe pain. The most common cure for this is the direct consumption of tippens root, as it brings the pH of\n\nthe stomach acid down to natural levels. \n\nAnother digestive issue is an illness that causes constant vomiting, or constant bowel movements. While vomitting is the bodies natural defense against bad food, this vomit is\n\nvery common even with high quality food. The best way to deal with this sickness is to consume mass quantites of salted water, as such replenishes the bodies well-being after their body exterts it. Sugar should also be added to the water.\n\nThis disease can be common or rare depending on its severity. \n\nOne may also vomit if they exert themselves to a point of exhaustion.\n\nChapter 3; Respiratory.\n\nThe Respiratory system contains the lungs and the windpipe. The windpipe is located behind the thick protective cover at the front of the throat. The lungs suction air from the environment\n\ninto them through use of a muscle underneath the lungs called the diaphragm. The lungs expand to hold the inhaled air, and then the air is pushed out. However, the body somehow utilizes the gas, most likely to produce more efficient anima.\n\nIf blood is deprived of the air, it turns purple and sickly looking. When re-exposed to the air, it turns bright red. My belief is that blood uses one of the gases that comprises air to convert nutrients into anima.\n\nBetween both of our knowledge, no diseases or ailments of the respiratory system were known, but the respiratory system can be damaged through the inhalation of coal fumes, causing 'Black-Breath'. This cannot be cured except by\n\nthe magic of the monks.\n\nChapter 4; Muscular.\n\nThe muscles are connected to the bones by tendons, stretchy bits of yellow 'flesh' that allows for the full range of motion. The muscles of the body tend to work in groups of two, one to push, and the other to pull.\n\nThe larger the muscle, the greater the force exerted by the movement of the muscle. As muscles are damaged through use, they heal and grow larger, thusly more powerful. This is why one is sore after strenuous exercize.\n\nNo ailment of the muscle is cureable. The degrading of muscle is either through use of magic, or by some ailment. Both of these result in the eventual loss of the majority of muscle.\n\nThere appear to be three types of muscle, involuntary, mixed, and voluntary. Involuntary muscles can not be controlled at all, such as the heart or the digestive muscles. \n\nMixed can be controlled some of the time, but for the\n\nmost part, operate on their own. This includes breathing, blinking, and swallowing. \n\nVoluntary muscles are only able to be used with input, such as the arms or the legs.\n\nChapter Five; Bones.\n\nThe bones are the structure of the body. They also offer protection. Bones are incredibly dense, most are stronger than steel. The amount of bones in a body is 206, with six tiny, tiny bones in the ears that some\n\nhow are linked directly to balance. The bones can heal themselves if set correctly, though clerical magic allows this process to finish faster.\n\nThere are no known ailments of the bone.\n\nAddendums; \nBruises are the pooling of blood from broken blood vessels.\n\nThe heart is an involuntary muscle.\n\nThe circulatory system involves vessels that take blood to the heart to replenish in anima,\n\nand arteries that take anima-enriched blood away from the heart to the muscles and other parts of the body.", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis: 1", "§bRalph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nFirst Edition         \nIn this edition:\n* A new emperor!\n\n* Fishing up relics\n\n* Greedy dwarves harras chef\n\n* “The Farmer”, by W. von Bran, reviewed.\n\nRecent News.\n\nA new emperor for our nation.\nOn the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1471. A new emperor was elected to rule over the Empire, listen to people and keep the nation safe from threats.\n\nTuvya of House Carrion has sworn to our creator to represent our nation in good or bad times, keeping the innocent safe from harm.\nIn the ceremony, Emperor-Elect Tuvya kneeled before the Lorraine and the High Pontiff, Daniel I.  He recited his oaths to\n\nchurch and state. Afterwards, he received the onyx Crown of the Exalted and the Blade of St Amyas.\nThe new emperor will surely bring better times for the empire and we will prosper more than what any other nation could.\n\nFishing a relic.\nFishing on the river outside Furstenburg, Phillip Krasline, a skilled fisher and part-time guard of our Majesty the Emperor, found a strange rock after a tug on his line. The rock appears to be an old knife carved out of a stone.\n\nHe said \"You can see it for yourself, it's crealy older than even the ruins here in Athera\".\nFor now the carved stone knife will be kept by Phillip until the Imperial Museum is finished.\n\nPhillip will return in the next issue to tell us all about the capture of the Fishlord.\n\nReports.\nClan Irongut harasses Oren’s greatest chef.\nThe Bada Bing Inn just outside of Petrus, owned by Oren's greatest chef known as Vinnie, is in the process of being stolen by the greedy dwarves of the Irongut clan.\n\nThe clan seems to believe that the land the Bada Bing Inn is built on belongs to them, and not to Vinnie. To them, this means the inn belongs to them as well. Shortly after leaving, I was able to ask him what the Clan father of Irongut, Balek\n\nwas going to do next. He replied with, \"Don't worry about them, I will be back and have them handled...\" This seems to be very foreboding for Vinnie.\nI joined the group of men and women headed towards the Bada Bing Inn\n\n as they feverishly sprinted to Vinnie's aid.  Once we got there, clan father Balek Irongut refused to open the doors, and threatened those that were there. After a short period of arguing, the door was broken down, and people rushed in from the back\n\nAfter a brief moment of thick intensity, Balek agreed to leave.\n \nWhat will become of the Bada Bing Inn? Will Vinnie get to keep his restaurant, or will the Irongut clan be back to take him down? Find out more next week, when all of this gets resolved.\n\nA report by Cain Vir Miles.\n\nBooks & Reviews.\nThe Farmer, by Wilhelm von Bran.\n\n“The Farmer & The Witch, or The Defeat of the Conjurer”, a two part series, is a captivating and well written story about events in an unnamed village in the Waldenian forests.\n\n It’s focussed on a man’s struggles and foes he has to deal with. Mainly in the second part is an elevating use of rhyme, making the books a joy to read.\nA must read!\n\n-Jacob Chapel.\n\nWords of the emperor.\n\nTo many of our fledgling state, the customs and traditions of my people of the Raev come off as foreign, queer, or outright disagreeable. Though predecessors of mine who shared\n\nmy blood desired to make Oren a Raevir state all-and-all, such outlandish desires my Reign shall bring an end to. I may be the eldest of living Crows and patriarch of my House, yet I was not born amongst the people of Raev. My childhood home was\n\nthe orphanage of Old Abresi, where I was warded until I was old enough to strike out on my own. Heartlander traditions and speech come more naturally  to I than my blood of Raev, and I simply wish to reassure all who remain loyal to our Realm that there\n\nshall be no pushing of Raev culture or language amongst our denizens, that Raev will largely be isolated from the affairs of our realm, and that my Reign is not that of Raev, but that of Man.\n\nCreator’s blessings to all subjects of Oren.\n\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion.\n\nLetters to the editor.\n\nIn future releases, you can send a letter to Ralph of Riley ((PM to nachotp, on forums)) to our offices on Abbey Road 13 next to the Cathedral of St. Sigismund, in Petrus.\n\nAll your letters will be published here for you to express your feelings about the current state of the society, economy or maybe denounce a villainous act. We expect your letters for the current releases, they can be anonymous if you wish to.\n\n-Ralph Riley\nEditor of the Verbo Veritatis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kha Dictionary", "§bRi'Zeriko", "~ Greetings/Courtesy Words ~\n\nSa'vi - Hello/Goodbye\nMul'ta - Thank you\nTra'kul - You're welcome\n\n~ Pronouns ~\n\nPatta - Father\nMuuna - Mother\nMetz'al - Life Mate or Spouse\nBunn - Wife\nMunn - Husband\nPer - Son\nMaut - Daughter\nPer'ta - Brother\nMau'na - Sister\n\n~The Karakatuan Government~\n\nTlatlanni - A Kharajyr blessed with white fur from Metztli herself, the Tlatlanni is perfection and divinity amongst the Kharajyr. The role of the Tlatlanni is to lead the Kharajyr for Metztli.\n\nTultelkos - Aelkos of war. He/she deals with political or militaristic efforts, and leader of the Moonblades.\n\nTruluk - Aelkos of Crafts. He/she is director of the economy and building.\n\nVarkolu - Aelkos of Faith. The leader of the Ja’ priesthood.\n\n Sostelos - The Social Aelkos. This Aelkos is responsible in providing happiness to the Kharajyr.\n\nThe titles of the Kharajyr are bestowed upon them according to their place in society.  Every Kharajyr will have a title (Excluding kittens/cubs) that forms the prefix next to their name. \n\nTla' - Tlatlannti\nRi' - Aelkos\nDri' - Tultelkos\nDra' - Moonblade\n\nJa' - Priest of Metztli\nYhl' - Elder of the Kharajyr\nQi' - Hunter\nKo', Ki' - Merchants/traders\nS', Sa', So',Si' - Unemployed\n\n~The Wildlife~\n\nTykkan  - Alligator\n\nVena-vi - Fireflies\n\nZisban - Monkey\n\nTuark - Hyenas\n\nNehpu - Colourful breed of birds found on the kha island.\n\nCehkan - Blue parrots\n\nCayda - Sharks\n\nGy'Waka - The Gy’Waka are a breed of colossal majestic birds that inhabit the islandthey protect the homeland as if it were their own and are by far the lead predators of the island.", ""),
        StaticBook("Auvergne Dialect", "ski_king3", "A Guide to the\n  Auvergnian Dialect\n\n\n   -by Rose Valois\n\n\n\n       Volume One:\n       The Basics\n\n  Table of Contents:\n\n\nThe Basics - Pg. 3\nGreetings - Pg. 5\nParting - Pg. 7\nPeople - Pg. 8\nRacial Terms - Pg. 10\nTitles - Pg. 12\n\nMessage from the Author - Pg. 16\n\n       The Basics\n\n\nOui - Yes\n\nNon - No\n\nS’il vous plait - please\n\nMerci - Thank You\n\nPas de problem - not a problem\n\nDe rien - You’re welcome\n\n        Greetings\n\n\nBon Matin - Good Morning\n\nBon soir - Good Evening\n\nBonne nuit - Good Night\n\nBonjour - Hello [Formal]\n\nSalut - Hail [Informal]\n\nEnchante - Pleased to meet you\n\n         Parting\n\n\nÀ bientôt - Until Next Time\n\nAu revoir - Good-bye\n\nAdieu - Good-bye\n\n          People\n\n\nMon seigneur - My lord\n\nMa dame - My lady\n\nMonsieur - Sir\n\nMadame - Misses [Married]\n\nMadamoiselle - Miss [Not Married]\n\n      Racial Terms\n\n\nHumain - Human\n\nElfe - Elf\n\nNain - Dwarf\n\nVerdâtre - Orc (literally means ‘Greeny’)\n\nSubalterne - Underling (can be used to substitute Nain, more derogatory)\n\nSouffrant - ill, unwell (often used to make racial term derogatory)\n\n          Titles\n\n\nDuc - Duke\n\nDuchesse - Duchess\n\nComte - Count\n\nComtesse - Countess\n\nBaron - Baron\n\nBaronesse - Baroness\n\nChevalier - Knight\n\nArchevêque - Archbishop\n\nDame - Lady\n\nSeigneur - Lord\n\nMaître - Master\n\nMaîtresse - Mistress\n\nVicomte - Viscount\n\nVicomtesse - Viscountess\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n   I hope that those of you who read through this book make use of it. Auvergnian is a very unique dialect dissimilar to any other dialect of Common present in Anthos. If you have any suggestions for words which should be in the next volume, please\n\nfeel free to visit me in Auvergne, or another member of the Valois family, to make reccomendations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Translations", "RogueSpectr3", "{t, ƒ:ªº£ ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, ñ.nü| ƒ'ª t, u':ô .nô t, ,ñö£:n,ºº d,i'û t, u':ô û,ª, e:º £' c'ññ.nô]\n\n[t,ü û,ª, ô\"º£ .nô e, û.º .º . º\"nd,.ñ| ô,ƒ:n:nø .£ i.º£ t,:ª ê.ö,]\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ'ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, .ø.:n| û:t t, º'ªª'û 'ƒ º\"ni:øe£ ª,ñ.:n:nø \"n£ª,.£,ô .nô \"nû,ic'ñ, £' t, ô,,ö c\"ªª,n£º 'ƒ t, º,.]\n\n[º\"ç ô:ª,c£:'ni,ººn,ºº :º .n.t,ñ. £' e:ñ| ûe' :º i:n,.ª]\n\n[t,º, .ª, £' d, E:º £ª:\"ñöeº .nô E:º ƒ.:i:nøº| ñ.nü £:ñ,º 'u,ª]\n\nThe first mathic age\n\nThat which is he made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were his to command\n\nThey were dust and he was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape\n\nAs was before, that which is he made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea\n\nSuch directionlessness is anathema to him, who is linear\n\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over\n\n{t, º,c‘nô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.c£:‘nº ‘ƒ t.£ ûe:ç :º e, .ª, d.ªª,ô ƒª‘ñ ,n£ªü]\n\n[t, ‘t,ªº e.u, t,:ª ô,u:c,º ‘ƒ û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n| ô,ƒ:n:æ t,ñ .º ûe.£ t,ü .iû.üº e.u, d,,n| t, c.ª,£.S,ªº ‘ƒ t,:ª ƒ.£,]\n\n[t,ü ê‘“£ .nô öi,.ô .nô ‘ƒƒ,ª t,:ª u‘:c,º £‘ t, e,.u,nº| d“£ t,ü .ª, .º t, ô,,ö c.u,º d,øø:æ ƒ‘ª º“ni:øe£]\n\n[t, û.ü :º ê“£]\n\nThe second mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry\n\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate\n\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight\n\nThe way is shut\n\n{t, t:ªô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[. ‘n, £,.ªº ƒª,, t, di:nôƒ‘iô ‘ƒ t, .düºº ƒª‘ñ t, ,ü,º ‘ƒ t, ö.ª£º]\n\n[:£ :º .º :£ û.º]\n\n[t, i:øe£ .nô i:øe£º .nô i:øe£:æ ‘ƒ t,:ª êª:n,º ƒª,, t,:ª º:øe£| t.£ t,ü ñ.ü di:nô ‘t,ªº]\n\n[û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n .ø.:n º“øø,º£º :£º,iƒ| .nô t, i:n, :º ñ.ô, .º .n “nc‘“n£.di, º,ª:,º ‘ƒ ö‘:n£º| .ii :n c‘nƒi:c£ û:t t,:ª ƒ,ii‘ûº]\n\n[.ii û:,iô:æ t,:ª i.û]\n\nThe third mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts\n\nIt is as it was\n\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others\n\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows\n\nAll wielding their law", ""),
