        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day 562: I am the only one left. All others are gone. My dear brother Sarrion is no where to be found. Am I mad? Or is the world not spinning?", ""),
        StaticBook("Transfiguration", "§bSarrion", "Transfiguration\n---------------->\n\"And so we learn to change the world around us, as if gods played with toys.\"\n-Sarrion\n----------------<\nWritten by:\nSarrion Zytiaear\n\n Transfiguration is under the school of Arcane Alteration, an art widely known for it’s use of Transmutation. This magic is known to have it’s user have the hands of one who match those of higher power,\n\nallowing them to shift properties of materials in which they had intently studied to their very will following the simple but so complex law of Equivalent Exchange. An art used by those who have minds that match brilliant scholars of old,\n\nthey are tasked with solving intense equations in their head in order to transmute their desired effect on the material, knowing the mass of the quantity transmuted as well as the alchemical make up, to those who witness such events just see it\n\nas a glow of aura, and the object magically changes. Transfiguration breaks down into three lesser schools of spells, the first would be Transmutation.\n\nTransmutation is the art of changing a material's properties to the users will following the art of Equivalent Exchange, as explained before, one cannot turn Ferrum to Gold, or make a blade out of a nugget of Ferrum,\n\n and matter cannot be destroyed, only broken down in the art of Deconstructive Transmutation, breaking a material down to a smaller form. The next school would be Enchanting, a mystical art that has intrigued the descendants for ages.\n\nEnchanting is the art of shaping mana crystals for use, as well as enspelling these crystals with a desired command, or in complex situations, entrap even other spells into the crystals captivity, encasing it to the command of the enchanter.\n\nThey say these crystals of old have always held high power in this art, for ages enchantments have been used for devices that only one could dream of, or artifacts of destruction such as weapons imbued with spells.\n\n Only the enchanter may understand the enchantment that he has created, another would take many years of time to even remotely understand the complexity of another mages work. Finally, the last school of this art is Warding,\n\n another mystical and complex art that allows it’s user to, the naked eye, completely neutralize spells. Warding comes in two main ways to cast, Wards themselves can be casted as an area of effect\n\n that neutralizes the magic that the mage is casting against from being ever casted, this kind of ward can be enchanted into gems, in elven culture these gems would very commonly be integrated into beautiful jewelry.\n\nThe second commonly used ward is an Abjuration, a quick spell casted by the mage to ‘destroy’ another mages spell mid-cast. In order to actually ward a spell\n\nyou must entirely understand the magic that you are warding, which takes years of study for that specific school of magic. The common red lines of this magic are as follows, You must /always/ follow equivalent exchange,\n\n You must entirely know the magic you are warding against, and you can only transmute a realistic proportion that you can handle, and of course as always with any Alteration one cannot transmute organic material.\n---------------\nEnd.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcana & Oddity", "§bAudrey Caillot", "~Arcana & Oddities!~\nThis shop is dedicated to bringing those who value items with stories just that! Items with stories.\n  We have put forth the energy to find items from those before and those past, and we have made ourselves focused to-\n\ntaking the utmost of care of the artifacts and relics we have collected over the years, and now we would like to share them.\n  We have two locations currently, one permanent home in Aethermoore where we have been allowed\n\nto originate, and a stall in the Monk Market, where you have probably recieved this booklet.\n\nOn top of items we have collected, we carry enchantments and the like, and support the community of mages and the arts.\n\nIt is with the greatest of pleasures we share our collections with you, and we hope you enjoy your stay!\n\n-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-2", "§bDaniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 2/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Fire Symbols\n\n           Weak\n\nName: Desert Berry Bush\nRepresentations: Empowerment, Overwhelming\nDescription: The Desert Berry Bush's appearance is that of a withered rose bush, long brown/grey stalks with big pointy\n\nthorns, yet without any leaves. It doesn't appear to grow higher than four feet, but most of the thorns are longer than an inch. It grows inside cactus forests, as in, where there is great concentration of cactus.Never has one been alone in the desert’s\n\nsands without a cactus near it. The Desert Bush Berries are the berries given by the Desert Berry Bush. The bush gives Berries of a strong red color every full moon. These don't last long, as animals of the desert appear to enjoy it's taste quite dearly.\n\nThe berries are extremely sweet, something very strange to find in the desert, so no wonder the animals enjoy it. The use of the berries are mostly in culinary, serving as treats, in jams and to bake. As for alchemy uses, it behaves as a fire symbol, as\n\nis custom to red ingredients. In this case not because of the color, but because of the strong flavor it has, almost overwhelming. On the other hand, it doesn't appear all that useful nor seems to give great use in equivalent exchange. Great to be used\n\nby new alchemists in their training, as it quite safe.\nLocation: Desert Cactus forests in Full moon days.\n\n        Moderate\n\nName: Flametongue’s roots\nRepresentation: Heat, Anger, Destruction\nDescription: Flametongue’s roots is a difficult reagent to collect. It’s location of growth already makes the task hard,\n\nhaving to find it extremely sunny locations in forests, either in burnt areas of it, or on hillsides. If you’re not lucky to find a spot which has burnt down, and if you don’t burnt the forest down to gather this reagent, then most likely you will have\n\nto climb a cliff or hold yourself in one’s edge to gather it. The second great problem with it, is that it’s sharp brambles release spores which with contact with the skin cause hypersensitivity to pain. Gloves have to be used when harvesting,\n\nand I would suggest a face mask as well. If you know where to look, it is not so hard to notice the reagent, as it has an almost rose like appearance. The roots are the part of the plant to use, being  bright red colored, which when used on wounds\n\ncauses coagulation. So to harvest it, one has to sometimes dig into the side of a hillside. Use it only when in a life or death situation, as the pain you will fill when using it, will most likely be far worse than waiting for the wound to heal naturally.\n\nSuch strong traits bring this plant representations of Heat and Anger.\nLocation: Forest’s hillsides and burnt forests.\n\nName: Dwarf’s Pumpkin\nRepresentation: Rage, Envy, Bitterness, Power, Strength\nDescription: Although it is called Dwarf’s Pumpkin, this plant is an odious orange-leafed shrub, and one of the most prominent feature of Swamp botany.\n\nQuite potent and atrocious smelling, it is easy to find at a distance, when it exists. It has it’s name from the it’s orange color, and the smell quite fits with the description of dwarves, or perhaps because of the brew which is made by them with this\n\nherb. They grow around the muddy waters and while they are not dangerous to gather, you may get your foot stuck and perhaps even fall into the disgusting mud, and unless some boots are used, your shoes will become horrible smelling. The whole plant may\n\nbe used for the brew made by the dwarves, yet only the brightest of orange leaves need to be collected for the alchemic use.\nLocation: Swamplands next to muddy waters.\n\nName: Blood Lotus\nRepresentation: Hope, Courage\nDescription: This vine of the deserts is one of my personal favorites to use outside of alchemy reactions. Perhaps a weird trait of mine considering what it’s properties are. The plant is of a\n\nrusty color, growing on the fresher entrances of caves in the desert. They fall from the ceiling and become like a red curtain that separates the cave from the hot exterior. These vines are easily harvested, and it’s main use outside of alchemy is mostly\n\nin culinary and brewing arts. A diet with consumption of Blood Lotus is one quite nutritious. The plant itself has a peculiar taste, one of iron, making the broths and stews created to appear to have been done with blood of an animal. Blood Lotus can\n\nalso be fermented to create strong alcohols of red color. It’s representation as a fire symbol comes down to the emotions spectral. It is a plant that grows in a hot climate and finds the perfect ideal place of freshness and light. As such, it represents\n\nhope, but as well courage.\nLocation: Entrance of caves in the hot desert lands.\n\nName: Elrow Berries\nRepresentations: Rage, anger, burning\nDescription: It isn’t common to find a fire symbol in cold climates, Elrow berries are of the few that exist. Elrow berries was named after an alchemist, probably in mockery, as it is\n\nalso known to some as the Hellfire fruit. It grows in bushes and has a great red color to it, easy to spot sometimes in the white wastelands of the arctics. The properties which make it a fire symbol are achieved when one is unfortunate enough to eat it.\n\nUnless for a single child and her mother with a great taste for spicy food, I have not met a single person which did not feel like their throat was on fire after tasting it. It starts as a spicy feeling in the mouth that spreads through the throat, where\n\na soreness starts coming with it. From there, the whole body starts to heat up, and even in the most cold days, the whole body starts to sweat, and the body starts aching. It lasts for a few minutes, many grabbing hands of snow and placing them in their\n\nmouth, others stripping almost down to their loincloths, and a few even faint. I don’t recommend eating Elrow berries unless perhaps you are dying of cold frost, or teaching an alchemist class and want a laugh. It’s normal uses are in poisons, especially\n\nthose that work with emotions, and it represents the more destructive side of Fire. It has been added to brews on some occasions as well, perhaps to heat up the body in cold winters.\nLocation: Bushes in cold climates.\n\n          Strong\n\nName: Crimson Vase\nRepresentation: Heat, Warmth, Love, Passion, Compassion\nDescription: In my opinion, this flower is the most beautiful that can be found in the forests. As it names suggests it has a strong red color,\n\ncrimson. This is the color that the large petals of the flower have, and the form of which they take is of an elegant vase. It’s beauty is also enhanced by it’s rarity, as finding one in a forest is an extreme delight. It appears at the base of young\n\ntrees, growing almost clinging to them. When the sun is high up, the plant starts almost glowing, as a beam of light passes through the small leaves and shines on it. Such combination of sunlight and protection can not be found on older trees. The plant\n\nsplendor does not end here, as my favorite trait is that the flower is warm to the touch, lovingly so. There are not many fire symbols which have representations of the ‘good’ side of fire, yet this one seems to have most of them. Warmth, Love, Passion,\n\nCompassion, this plant can be used for most emotion changing concoctions. Of course it’s very important to fire based potions as well, such as Alchemist’s fire, but with it poisons of envy and rage, and potions which bring focus, courage, and warmth\n\ncan as well.\nLocation: At the base of young trees in forests.\n\nName: Drake’s Tail\nRepresentations: Heat, Destruction, Chaos\nDescription: Of the herbs and plants of which I speak of in this volume, Drake’s Tail is the strongest and probably the rarest symbol of Fire. A rare sight in the deserts, almost\n\na legend sometimes, this plant is probably the best you may find without having to slay a beast of mythical stories. It grows in the deserts, but even in them the conditions needed for it to grow are quite scarce and hard to find. This plant’s growth is\n\nvery dependant on the moisture and temperature in the air, which means in the hot desert wastelands you will not find one growing. Only near Oasis, yet not too close does it grow. It needs the moisture that exists in the air because of the Oasis, and the\n\nhotness of the desert, so it becomes an area which one might find Drake’s Tail. It seeks shade as well, embarrassing it’s thin and long vines filled with thorns around a rock. With a red dusky color it’s easy to spot, when there is one around. To harvest\n\nit one has to remove the whole plant, as both the thorns and the roots are the necessary bits that are used by the alchemists in their concoctions. The harvesting is not only hard, but also dangerous. If one is struck by one of the thorns, he will gain\n\na strong fever and have a high chance of passing out in the middle of a hot desert, to be food to the coyote’s. It’s characteristics make Drake’s Tail one of the best in the fire eccentric representations.\n\nLocation: In deserts close to oasis.\n\nContinues in part 3\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-3", "§bDaniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 3/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    Water Symbols\n\n           Weak\n\nName: Blissfoil\nRepresentation: Calmness\nDescription: Blissfoil is a plant which has more applications in healing medicine than in alchemical healing potions. While it has been found to have weak potency in\n\nalchemy, it’s effects are quite used in healing. I do not believe many good doctors exist which have not heard of the use of this plant, for it is one of the best numbing agents out there. The greatest problem with it, is the fact that overuse of it\n\ncauses permanent numbing to an area, and with the power it holds, it happening by someone who does not know of it’s effects is quite possible. The plant itself looks like a combination of many small blue flowers with a thick and flimsy stalk.\n\nIt’s harvesting is as easy as collecting a flower, and it is born and grows under birch trees near grassy areas.\nLocation: Under birch trees in grassy areas.\n\n         Moderate\n\nName: Serpent's Stalk\nRepresentations: Life, Rebirth, Calmness, Fluity\nDescription: This plant is one of the easiest to find in the forest of the realm. If one knows where there are small ponds and perhaps streams of\n\nwater, they would find the Serpent's Stalks. Long Emerald hued stalks, with stripes and ridges of a lighter green and brown along its length, almost like a serpent. Sometimes simple mistaken by normal sugar canes by those unknown of this plant, and to\n\ncollect it is the same as well, cutting it at the bottom. Another attribute it holds similar to a serpent’s it’s the poisonous nature it has. Specific insects that come in contact with it are normally found dead all around them, yet from all it’s use, no\n\nother creatures seem to die from it. It is actually used many times as a healing agent, specifically to heal and treat burn wounds. A normal oinkment from simply crushing the plant and mixing it with some water may smooth the pain and keep the wound\n\nsafe. It is as such a good water symbol that can be used for antidotes, oils, balms, healing potions and potions of calmness, as well as fire extinguishing potions. Those are good to have when preparing alchemist fire.\n\nLocation: Grows near small bodies of water in forests.\n\nName: Mandragora\nRepresentation: Rejuvenation, Life, Rebirth, Regrowth\nDescription: This is one of the reagents most alchemists use when creating more powerful healing potions. It’s meat rejuvenating traits makes it so that it’s very well\n\nsought by many alchemists. No good ingredient comes without its dangers thought, and Mandragora is one that can bring a collector to a very humiliating death. It is observed growing into the shallow waters of swamp lands, with thick green leaves flowing\n\nout of the water. Such leaves are quite delicious as garnish for soups and to make a quite rejuvenating tea. It is highly nutritious as well, filled with nutrients. It is not the leaves that one uses as a reagent thought, but the “meat” of the plant.\n\nThe part of the plant normally underwater is shaped like a parsnip. It is this “meat” that needs to be collected and prepared to use by the alchemists. Collecting it it’s not as easy as it sounds. This plant creates highly narcotic and paralyzing spores\n\nwhich are released quite easily when the plant is moved. Inhaling them brings the humiliating death of drowning in a foot high water level, as you simply fall on it and are unable to move any further. As such, one has to known when the spores are fully\n\nreleased, and only then retrieve them. Normally simply a group of at least two set out to find them, and one pulls the other from death if the spores are still with the plant.\nLocation: Low waters in wetlands.\n\nName: Zawabate\nRepresentations: Life, Calmness, Rebirth\nDescription: Zawabate is the only reagent I know of water representation in the desert lands. Of course it does not grow in the middle of the sand, it grows in the rare oasis one might\n\nfind. There is it protected from the strong heat and low humidity, in the fertile grounds around the waters. It is identified by it’s prominent colors of green and yellow, with short curvy petals in a long stalk. For those that live near them, especially\n\nthe orcish shamans, it is a plant which brings a higher connection with the spirits and out of body experiences. To say more simply, Zawabate is a hallucinogen, creating great comfort and sensations, which are further enhanced if made into a stong tea.\n\nThese flowers are certainly an amazing addition to potions designed to numb pain or heal because of their home in such a lush landscape among a wasteland of aridity. The amount to use however, should be greatly controlled, due to its hallucinogenic\n\nproperties. Too much, and the healing potion might cause delusions and mental problems, which means it can also be used for to create those same poison effects if wanted.\nLocation: In the fertile lands of an oasis\n\nName: Frost Vine\nRepresentation: Life, Calmness, Ice\nDescription: Frost vine is a blue vine which grows in very cold climates. It seems to have a need for shade, the most common of places being around trees, leaving long blue spirals in their\n\ntrunks and falling from their branches. The plant is a very good numbing agent, one which can easily be made into a sticky clear substance which numbs pain and loosens stiff muscles. Too much of it and it may affect the limbs, making them completely numb\n\nfor some time. One must always be sure to wash the area after applying the substance. It is by some considered a good alternative to a stronger but also more dangerous rubbing agent, Blissfoil, and with some other good qualities in the mix.\n\nThe vine is quite cold to the touch, which means it may also be further used to better the effect of numbing and treating wounds and pains. With these traits, it is no wonder that this plant represents life, calmness and cold.\n\nLocation: Shaded areas in cold climates.\n\n          Strong\n\nName: Athin\nSymbol: Freezing, Ice, Life, Balance\nDescription: Athin is quite a potent Water Symbol that one finds in ice lakes and rivers of fresh water, which are normally frozen. It is a blue algae, sometimes quite hard\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nto find if the ice is too thick or the snow stops vision to the unfrozen water under the ice. One particular difficult to harvest plant, not due to the how you take it, but because of the danger associated with it. It is taught to all alchemists that it\n\ntakes two people to harvest Athin. This is because it grows under ice, on very cold water. The ice breaking and someone getting stuck is a high probability, but either way you will have to get into the water to collect it. Sometimes people get stuck\n\nunder the ice, not knowing where the hole they did was, sometimes they do not take precautions with heating before entering the water and freeze in the cold wind when out. Such dangers do come with reward, as Athin is one of the materials there are that\n\nare fireproof. It has a great representation of ice and freezing, and an alchemist that carries around alchemist fire, or simply makes it, always have some athin around with them as well.\n\nLocation: Under the ice of frozen lakes and rivers.\n\nContinues in part 4\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-4", "§bDaniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 4/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       Air Symbols\n\n          Weak\n\nName: Jailer’s moss\nRepresentations: Travel, Movement\nDescription: Quite an annoying plant in many cases, the Jailer’s Moss seems to stick to everything it touches. It is found the caves near or in swamps,\n\ngrowing in water streams from the walls, and sometimes even in small currents of water. It has a very light yellow color making it easily noticeable in the dark caves. It’s main property is the stickiness it has, just a touch and it never seems to\n\nlet go. Of course it doesn’t hold much force, so no one but the small fishes and insects it feeds on get stuck to it, it normally breaks or the whole plant gets dragged with the animal or person. It is from this that the ingredient is considered an air\n\nsymbol, representing the motion of travelling with the other animals, this way spreading. A weak symbol which is great for new alchemists to use and try out.\nLocation: Caves in swamps\n\n         Moderate\n\nName: Swamp’s blossom\nRepresentations: Quickness, speed, Travel\nDescription: This is the flower that would be considered the most beautiful in the awful looking lands of swamp and wetlands. A purplish\n\ngreen flower that grows through the branches of the trees, with a short and thick stem. One might feel bad for removing the little beauty one might find in the swamplands, which is quite understandable. After collecting this flower, you can remove the\n\nnectar which has a very peculiar reaction. This nectar is a clear liquid, but one that acts like quicksilver. Extracting a bit of it and pouring it over your hand, and it will dance gracefully until finding a way to the floor between your fingers.\n\nIt is this nectar that is used in the concoctions of the alchemists, one that represents a clear symbol of air.\nLocation: Growing through the branches of swamp trees\n\n         Strong\n\nlName: Crouching Feather\nRepresentations: Speed, Travel, Gracefulness\nDescription: A graceful and rare sight of the forest and plains. This quite potent reagent can be recognized by it’s\n\nlong three white petals that sweep in a downwards curve to the point where they touch the ground, appearing like feathers. Like the name it has, they are found “crouching” under large fauna, such as big bushes and shrubs. The harvesting of this peticular\n\nplant is one that is quite hard. The flower only blooms at night and a strong wind will blow the petals right off. When finding one, the alchemist or botanist must carefully remove the petals from the stalk, and keep them safe from being blown away, and\n\nfrom being crushed. When finally harvested, this plant is quite a strong symbol of air. The extract of the petals much be collected first, and doing so to a graceful petal is quite hard. It’s use it’s mostly for potions of celerity and when the\n\nrepresentation of speed is quite desired. Yet gracefulness and travel also represent these long petals.\nLocation: Under big bushes and shrubs of forests and plains.\n\nName: Elf’s hair vine\nRepresentations: Travel, Gracefulness, Speed, Flight\nDescription: One of the most beautiful plants of which I speak of in this volume, Elf’s Hair vine is a rare sight in the top of cold mountains. Like the elegant hair\n\nof the nibble elves, the plant has a extreme lightness to it, flowing softly even in the most minute of breezes. The vine is thin and white, seeming to float in the air. Normally protected from the wind, when a stronger gust of air finds it, the small\n\nblossoms that grow from the vines are broken off, and start flying with the wind, travelling together. They have many pure small white petals which gracefully come together to create the flower. These flowers is what an alchemist uses in his concoctions,\n\nwhich makes the collection quite difficult. If a simple breeze can take it away, picking it up or moving it around is an very timely task. The alchemist has to be slow and gentle, as not only would harsh movements send the graceful flower flying away, it\n\nmight also damage the petals of this fragile plant. With a representation of grace of the flower, it’s petals have to be in perfect condition when used, a tear or a part of it damaged, and most of the use is lost. This reagent serves with great use for\n\nconcoctions centered around speed and grace.\nLocation: Covered from the wind at the top of cold mountains.\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("Shifting.", "§bHelio", "Take note that I have frail information about this, the source from where I've learned being rather demented. By all means, may this book find itself to the worthy owner.\n\nVoidal shifting is the art of teleporting one from a place to another by the aid of the void. The process of voidal shifting is a simplistic one as it is complicated in practice. We'll start with mana-anchors. Mana-anchors is the connection from the void-\n\n-to the spell, this anchor's literally made of the mana that fuels the spell. Although, if the cast is not fueled with mana it will disperse, or by other means. This, isn't the case with alterationists, as they use their ability of manipulating what is --\n\n--already there with the connection of the void, and thus, mana-anchors. Frankly, when you project mana in a solid chunk further away is known as a mana-anchor. Now, how I understand a shifter uses their anchors to shift from a place to another, you --\n\n--project your mana to a space of area. Take note that this area must be on the same level as you, neither could  one shift oneself higher in the air or lower in the ground. In order to shift the anchor must be placed a distance away, with the most range-\n\n-of 30 feet. Here comes the uncomfortable part, if you wish to shift from the location you posess to another, you simply let your body pass through the Void and stop at the mana-anchor. Imagine the body being metal whilst the mana-anchor is a magnet, --\n\n--and the Void as an ocean, you simply drop the metal into the ocean and let it be attracted to the magnet. Take note that I've never tried this, and this is probably extremly dangerous to do without guidance, as you can be lost into the void. Sadly, this\n\n-\n\n-is about all the knowledge I contain of the subject, perhaps I will continue this work later on, farewell for now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "§bElluna Koortova", "Electric \n         Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  By Gauldrim Irongut\n\n\nChapter 1, Uses of Electromancy:\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, is just as likely to veer off it’s course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force, electromancy is a formidable tool. Slow to conjure\n\nand is a lifelong commitment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is  the extreme attraction\n\nto large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit plate of armour, or a large iron gate can cause the electricity to be attracted towards it and then channeled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt or burnt\n\nas the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjure, though fast once released, electric\n\nevocation is one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full plate mail in a single bolt, if large enough this just lends perspective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability to summon forth\n\nlightning from the heavens in the event of a storm with very good accuracy.\n\n\n\nChapter 2, Properties of Electromancy:\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water. Electromancy is as versatile as it is powerful. Electric\n\ncurrents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of plate mail when the electric current is sent towards the bearer\n\nthey will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricity as well. The current of the electricity will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent\n\nhurtling towards the stone, resulting in flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock, Electromancy can set wood, paper, and any other flammable materials alight causing fire and burns.\n\n\n\nChapter 3, Conclusion: \n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range.\n\nIt is advised that when in combat against such a mage, that large amounts of metal and or armour are unadvised to have and even steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer\n\nand to regard the raw power and wisdom of those that wield it.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "§bElluna Koortova", "Treating Wounds\n  \n    By Anonymous\n\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet’s start using steps,\n\n\nStep I - Cleaning the Wound\n\nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or deeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. Of course you need to wash the dirt out\n\nfirst should it have dirt in it. Remember to clean thoroughly!\n\n\nStep II -  Suturing the Wound\n\nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread. Sounds easy right? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these.. Let’s call them sub steps.\n\n\nSub Step I - Heating the Needle\n\nYou need to do that to burn away any remaining illness covering the needle, should it have had any.\n\nSub Step II - Clean the Thread\n\nYou surely need to do so, as you do not want a single speck dirt in your wound!\n\nSub Step III - Starting the Suture\n\nYou start at, well, the start of the gash or deep wound. (Warning! this does NOT apply for small wounds!)\n\nYou then sew it closed like you’re sewing a tear in a rag, a messy and bloody rag that screams like a little girl. Nonetheless, a rag. \n\nSub Step IV - Bandaging the Wound\n\nA bandage could be just about anything,\n\nan old rag (As long as it's clean, obviously!), bed sheets, anything of cloth material. Then you simply wrap it around the wound. Done!\n\nNote: If there's any sign of infection before or after you’ve gone through this process you'll be\n\nbetter off cutting off the leg.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "haha weed", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VIII", "§bMarch Ash", "Even at the top of the world, my sight from these two eyes only goes on until the horizon. But, my sight from my thousand eyes, that seems to go on forever.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VI", "§bMarch Ash", "The swamps have always been a place for reclusive druids to go and meditate. The muck holds thousands of years within it, an ancient story of the land. Corpses of ancient men and women, who will tell me more about the history of this place\n\nthan books ever could.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pain", "§bThe Inquisitor", "I do not know the name of the god to who Irri'aye pledged herself. Only that this sword has been pledged in its service, and that whoever wields it, must also wield that black voice. Just as the blade rends flesh, so too must it scar the spirit.\n\nWhoever that god was, they had the strength to hold onto Irri'aye, even despite the strongest efforts on part of Aureus.\n\nIt is not recorded whether she first became a champion of the glade, and then was taken by the temptations of this distant god, or whether she was allowed to become the glade's champion despite her prior commitments.\n\nShe served the glade and her god together, for a time. Times were peaceful, and the world was calm. She was one of the few champions whose ferocity matched that of the glade itself, sharp-witted and with a fiery spirit.\n\nShe pushed the boundaries of the glade, expanding its domain.  This made her well-respected and feared. It was wise to stay in her good graces. Unfortunately, it was not to last.\n\nA time came when there was conflict, and she was forced to choose between the glade, and her dark god. She chose her god, and so Aureus cast her out of the glade for all time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VII", "§bMarch Ash", "Taken by the hunt, everything else fades away. We fail to listen. Not to other people, but to the World. Here, in the black, damp, heat -- nature's voice comes in its purest form. Nothing is hidden. It is naked. It is as easy as fucking.\n\nIt whispers to me so quietly: kill them all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru I", "§bMarch Ash", "It is visceral. I smell the dry earth, the rind of the roots, the bitter air of tangled moss. The shade is cool. But then I exhale, and I am pulled back. I think I would be just as happy were I born a tidal wave or a breeze.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VII", "§bMarch Ash", "Not far from here, the Holy Orenian Empire's death throes tore apart the world. One of the greatest acts of sacrilege of all time. It cannot go unpunished. I will not stop until every shred of the old empire is turned to ash,\n\nuntil every person who was a part of this atrocity is dead. I will restore balance where it has been taken.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XVII", "§bMarch Ash", "And in the sand, respite.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "{!}§0\n§0\n§0---Kaia Kharadeen---§0\n§0\n§0On the cover of this journal is eched floral and flame designs. In the mid-drift of it to be the name of the Emiress Kaia Kharadeen's  name in§0\n§0cursive golden writing.§0\n\n      _Voidal Fire_§0\n§0\n§0~ It beams in the palm of his hand. Like a glow of light spewing from the Mali's very soul. §0\n§0\n§0~ It's very scent to be.. nothing. It held no§0\n§0impartial scent to anything that is imagined to be.\n\n-3. Voidal Fire.§0\n§0\n§0~The touch. Sears and burns like the fires of§0\n§0hell. Barely managable just to touch with a finger. Almost as if the skin was melting off of her muscular bone. §0\n§0\n§0      *Note Taken*§0\n§0\n§0Do NOT touch with the bare hand.\n\n-4. Voidal Fire.§0\n§0\n§0~If one were to lean over and listen to the crackling flame, it sounded like a pit of leafs rubbing together§0\n§0as the bright colors crossed paths repeatedly.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day one§0\n§0I write this the elven day after the incident of which I fealt quite sad for no reason. This was shortly after seeing a long time friend for the first time in these new lands. I don't know how to explain what I feel, But it worrys me terribly.\n\nDay two§0\n§0This feeling, It won't go away, I find myself on the outskirts of places... attempting to avoid human contact except from those I trust most.\n\nDay three§0\n§0Honestly, Given up on trying to make myself happy. Only my wife or Hazel or even Hannah could do that.. maybe my childs smiles'll do aswell... but otherwise my thoughts are occupied with the feeling. Today a topic came up and it reminded me of-\n\nmy son, Wonder if he died out in the forest in Vailor or is now strolling around in Axios... how I miss him§0\n§0\n§0[!] Some tear stains are laid across this page. All dried up and wrinkly.\n\nDay five§0\n§0I forgot to write the other day, Kinda glad I didn't though. because the pain of it all has collapsed. Still there in the backround, It's quite annoying really. Dunno what to do about it really. It hurts... I tried to kill myself before-\n\nrealizing I still had some things and people to take care of. Till next time, if there is to be.\n\nDay six. (The writing starts becoming erratic)§0\n§0\n§0My mind is starting to swirl in stress, worry, fear, guilt and confusion once more... my mind is snapping slowly again... I must leave the dreadlands in hopes to run across my wife.-\n\nI do hope that I live through my travels.§0\n§0End of day six\n\nDay Seven§0\n§0I took my baby and left the dreadlands after taking some rations to feed us. I traveled north into the forest and just stayed there for a few days listening to the sounds of the forest, Water gushing out of the falls. Leaves brustling in the-\n\nwinds.\n\nDay eight§0\n§0I am losing hope that my wife is alive or no longer faithful to me.. I had sent out a bird to find her a few days, or months as some people call them, prior to this entry.§0\n§0I just hope it'll all be over soon. one way or the other,\n\nDay Nine§0\n§0I had left the forest to go gather some supplies from the dreadlands, I had found almost all the tents to be missing for some reason. I hadn't gone back to the forest and just started pacing around the lands. I was en route to Oren's Capital-\n\nwhen my bird had returned after so long.. I was so happy when I saw her writing.\n\nDay Ten.§0\n§0For now I've no more need to relieve my stress this way, I've reunited with my love.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Warhawkes guide§0\n§0to Spirituality§0\n§0\n§0Prayers for the spirits-§0\n§0\n§0One that hunts must help guiding the animals spirit back to the stars. If to many souls gets lost, the animals will react and won't let them selfs being hunted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "what is a melody§0\n§0without its instrument§0\n§0\n§0The choir will sing again§0\n§0\n§0fruits of life do beg my pardon§0\n§0\n§0roaming astray my endless garden§0\n\nmy ill sees metal turn to rust§0\n§0\n§0and men grow tall from all but dust§0\n§0\n§0for i am the breath and life of home§0\n§0\n§0forge noble beasts and kings that reign§0\n§0\n§0i do this time and time again", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspect Studies", "§bTever Softfoot", "I was walking along the river near my home when I spotted a very nice spot to sit and take a nap. It was quiet, sunny and warm.\nI lay down and closed my eys. I felt the sun warming me. Felt the wind blowing and the life all around.\n\nI began to meditate. I felt a peace that I hadn't felt before. I eventually fell asleep. I dreamed I was bathed in light. The air tasted sweet. There was music in the air that sounded like an orchestra of nature. When I awoke I was reminded of my\n\nteachings. Of Cerridwen and the light and life she brings. I looked up into the tree, upon rising from my resting place, and saw a honey comb dripping with beautiful golden honey. Like it was a gift from Cerridwen meant for me.\n\nThe honey represents\n\nCerridwen because not only is it golden, it is life sustaining, warm, sweet,and the labor of creatures of life. Nothing would be living without Cerridwens blessing of bees to pollinate things.\n\nAs a lumberjack I find myself in search of exotic woods deep in mysterious places. I heard of a source of dark oak deep within the forests of the Mali. As I traveled through the ancient forest I felt the presence of the trees watching me.\n\nIt was a welcoming feeling however. I made my way to the location of the trees and made camp. Later that night a terrible storm came upon me. My camp was blown away and I lost my way. Three days I wandered the forest with no hope.\n\nI was hungry and cold. Hope had fled from me. I finally fell to my knees and yelled defiantly at anything that could hear me. \"I will no' die tis way!\" I thought of my love. Of the future that would never be.\n\nAs I kneeled there in the damp leaves, the quiet of the forest settled around me. The stillness was tangible. There was not a sound to be heard. As I stood up and looked around I saw a pure white deer looking at me. As I slowly backed away I tripped over\n\nwhat I thought was a fallen branch. On closer examination the branch turned out to be a moss covered bow. The string was made of vines. There were also a few moss covered arrows wrapped in a sheet of old leather.\n\nAs I picked up the bow the deer bolted away through the underbrush. Being on the verge of starving, I shrugged off the despair. This was my only chance to survive. I needed food. I grabbed the Bow and arrows and started after the deer.\n\nI tracked the deer through valleys, over hills, through fields and forests for what seemed like an eternity. As i crested a small hill I came upon the deer once more. The wind was blowing torwards me. The grass was soft and silent.\n\nIt was the perfect chance and my only one. I had not the strength to track this quarry any longer. I slowly nocked an arrow and raised the bow. I thought the mossy wood would creak and give as I pulled it, but it remained silent. I held my breath.\n\nThe only sounds were the wind and the fast beating of my heart. The thrill of the hunt running through my veins. The arrow flies true and hits it's mark. A clean kill. I went to the deer and sat by his side.\n\nCrying at my salvation I began to dress the deer.I built a fire and ate my fill all the while praising my luck. As I ate I was reminded of my teachings. Of Cernunnos the great huntsman. I believe the deer and the bow where gifts from him.\n\nI sat near the fire and began to meditate on what I had learned and thanks the Horned God for his generosity and for saving my life. \nThis moss covered bow reperesents Cernunnos. It is the tool of the true hunter.\n\nOf his dedication and prowess. Of the thrill of the chase and of the taking of your prey. And of the thankfulness for a life given to save another life.\n\nI was in the far north. Conscripted to a group of explorers as repayment of a debt. After trudging the snow for several days we came upon twin mountains. Very unusual looking with they were. We decided to make camp at the base of the second with plans to\n\nexplore them the next day.\nAfter a hot meal and a few tunes from a pipe we turned in for the night. As I lay there I heard someone crying out past the ring of light made by the campfire. I rose from my bed and walked the the edge of the camp.\n\nI could make out the shape of what looked like a small child. I paused and looked back at the others still sleeping. They would be fine, and so would I as long as I kept the fire in sight.\n\nAs I stepped out into the cold dark of the night, four other figures appeared. I turned to run back into the camp when a numbing coldness came over me. I couldn't move. Last thing I saw was the ground coming at me, then darkness...\n\nWhen I awoke I was in a lightless place bound in iron. I could hear muffled voices nearby. The ground was hard and cold. Luckily they did not take my jacket or any of my things. I fished a lockpick from my boot and began to fumble in the dark to unlock\n\nthe shackels around my feet. It was very difficult to pick the locks without making a sound and alerting my captors. My previous title as Borrower helped in the task of breaking free. I finally freed my feet and began trying to free my arms.\n\nLuckily for me being a halfling meant that the chains were far to big for my small arms and with a little effort I slipped my hands right through them.\nI crept towards the voices, grasping in the dark so as not to bump into anything.\n\nThe voices grew louder and louder as I crept in the dark, until finally I could understand what they were saying. It was three females talking about what to do with me. It seemed like the consensus was to toss me down a deep hole.\n\nI began to panic and flail around in the dark for an escape but only ended up tripping and banging my head. Bright light filled my vision as I was lifted from the ground. I was carried for some distance and then wind. Nothing but darkness and wind.\n\nI fell for ages it seemed then splash. I fell into an underground lake. The darkness was so thick I could not see my hands in front of my face. I picked a direction and began to swim. Eventually I found what seemed like a bank.\n\nI was so afraid. What was I going to do? I was miles underground with no light, no food, and no hope. I sat and cried for a while. Such was my despair that I decided that if I was going to die that it would be my way,\n\nNot eaten by some unknown creature of the dark. I rose from the place I was sitting and began to wander in the dark, tripping and fumbling as I went. As I was scrambling through the dark I tripped over a loose stone and fell down a hill.\n\nI rolled and rolled and fell off of a small cliff, breaking my leg as I hit the bottom. I screamed out in pain as I pulled my leg out from under me, bone protruding from the skin.\nAll I could do was lay there in despair.\n\nAs i sat there writhing in pain my heart sunk. I was not alone here in the dark. I heard small pebbles shifting in the dark. Something grabbed my broken leg and began to drag me.\n\nPain shot through my body as the creature sank it's teeth sank into my body. \n\nI sat up from my bedroll with a scream. The pain still wracking my body as I came to terms with what had happened. Everyone looked at me in bewilderment,\n\nwondering what was going on. As I sat there the pain faded and the realization that it was just a dream dawned on me. The horror and helplessness I felt was still there.\n\nI shudder even now as I write this. The feeling of that dream will haunt me to the end of my days. I think that dream was from Niimasae. Showing me that I I should find my own light, that, like in the caverns I am helpless without it.\n\nThe object I think represents Niimasae is the enchanted stone I had made so that I would never be without my own source of light. I will not be left alone in the darkness again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "§bRespiren", "~Druidology~\n\nDruids are the druii, the dryw, the druwid.\n\nNature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n\nFor those that know the oak, the trēow is both the tree and the truth.\n\n\n\nMysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning master of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender of unspoiled Nature.\n\n\n\nThe Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements.\n\nAll druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos devoted to protecting the wilderness and maintaining natural cycles and a balance between good and evil.\n\n~Scribed by Wayward\nDruid Respiren", ""),
        StaticBook("Recipies", "§bVlad Shade", "Alchemist Fire\nMandragora\nSerpents stalk\ndwarf pumpkin\nDrakes tail\nflame tngue\ncrimson vase\ncrouching feather\n\nStone skin\nMandragora\nSerpents\nDwarf pumpkin\nDrakes tail\nFlame tongue\nCrouching feather\nalabaster leaf\nclutchers straw\nmetzils tangle\nalabaster leaf\n\nGreater healing\nAthin\nFrost vine\ncrouching feather\nElfs hair\nTippens\n\nVirulent Slime\nMandragora\nSerpents stalk\ndwarf pumpkin\ncrimson vase\n\nPoisoned inferno\nMandragora\nserpents stalk\ndwarf\nflamtongue\ncrimson vase\n\nBoggy concoction\nMandragora serpents\n\nHermits concoction\nMandragora \ntippen\n\nTaste of sewers\nMandragora\nserpents \ndwarf pumpkin\n\nAll greaters require\nAqua vitae base\n\nlessers distilled water\n\nRegenerative are blood based\n\nFrost oil\nSerpents stalk\nAthin \nFrost vine\nCrouching feather\nElfs hair vine\nTippen\n\nMinor healing\nTippen\n\nSmoke wispers\nBlood lotus\ndrakes tail \nFingers\nCrouching feather\n\nChill blain\nAthing \nFrost vine\n\nGreater chill blain\nAthin \nFrost vine\nCrouching feather\n\nWinters blod\nAthin\nFrost vine\nSerpents stalk\n\nParalising venom\nClutchers straw-potent\n\nOr mandragora-Weak", ""),
        StaticBook("Informer Issue 2", "underwhereknight", "The Informer\n        Issue #2\n\n        Edited By:\n\n           Adam\n16th of the First Seed         Year 1564\n\nContents-\n--------\nThe Feslen Housing Scandal           pg3\n\nCannibals in Feslen? \n                      pg9\nThe Guard Moves into the Old Palace\n                     pg13\nUpdate on the Lorraine Killings\n                     pg15\nThe Grand Vailorian Tournament   \n                     pg19\nMurder Locations\npg25\n\n The Feslen Housing\n         Scandal\n\n   An anonymous source let me in on what is going on in Feslen behind the scenes, here it is. Past Feslen mayor Piero Gradic has been abusing his power as mayor for personal gain. To start the long list he\n\nhas been overturning houses in Feslen at an incredible rate to turn a profit at the expense of those being evicted. Gradic has also sold houses far under value to secure votes for mayor before. As well Gradic never paid his stewards for their hard work,\n\nowing over three thousand minas to one steward. Most astonishing of all he falsely tampered with the city ledger to do this and it has been years since taxes have actually been checked or logged! Many properties in Feslen are owned and unused by goverment\n\nofficals- likey from the corruption of Gradic. Feslen has three banks- only one open. My source claims Piero Gradic did not run for re election because he could not win and now that Gradic is head Steward he will likely keep overselling houses unless\n\nmayor Markese de Rolle sets prices for houses so they can't be overpriced.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   Come Drink and Eat\nat the Cracked Tankard Inn! The best place to get a drink in Feslen!\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n Cannibals in Felsen?\n\n   From the Lorraine Cross murders we thought things in Feslen couldn't get much worse but an unamed source let me in on something the Guard is hiding. An unknown group of cannibals have been killing and eating their victims.\n\nSome of the victims of this unholy act are already dead victims of the lorraine killings and devoured anyways. Another though had their door chopped down and house broken into and has eaten. It was truly horrible I hear. Are these cannibals the cultist in\n\nthe sewers? In league with the lorraine killer? The work of the undead? Rebel practices? It is unknown as of now. Be safe Feslen.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   The Feslen Informer needs writers! Contact Adam by bird and turn in an Artical for a mina payment and have your work seen!\n\nFor articals that are excepted.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n The Guard Moves into      the Old Palace\n\n   The ever growing Feslen guard has claimed the old royal palace once untouched it is now for the guards use. Although commandant Markese said the old garrison for the guard may be sold with the approval of a\n\ncouncil it seem as it will remain under the guards control. The old palace was to be the site of the new guild halls, one a magic school after the end of the war. Where will the guilds of Feslen move into now is unknown.\n\n     Update on the\n    Lorraine Killings\n\n   The unknown lorraine killer is still on the loose and among Feslen. The killer carving the lorraine's cross into the victims chest's and has been known to kill guards who witness them. A couple was brought into\n\nquestioning from the guard about the killings. Thoramir, a dwarf and Sue a human women with a baby child, Daren. They at first claimed at doing it but then broke their statement saying they did it all for the baby. Neither could decide who did it both\n\ntaking full responsibility for the crimes. In the end the guard released them on probation, taking on all their weapons and book that could connect them with a cult. For all of the known locations of lorraine killings see the back of the paper. The only\n\nlead in who could be the true killer is a man in a light brown cloak ran from the scene of a murder.\n\n The Grand Vailorian \n      Tournament\n\n   On the 11th of the Grand Harvest 1563 a grand and mysterious tournament was held in the middle of a desert in a grand area. The fighters fought for glory and prizes. In the end there were three prizes. And the\n\nthree remaining fighters fought a free for all to see who could win the grand prize. It pitted an orc, dwarf and undead ghoul agaisnt each other. In a fury of blades the dwarf and orc fought. After a drawn out battle the orc left walking, but was soon\n\nambushed by the ghoul, falling to it. The ghoul named Valdren won the main prize of tourney. I interviewed a man who got fifth place in the tournament, besting an orc to get there. I asked this Maximillion Dwanstead, a rugged man with a scar down his eye\n\nhow he bested the orc. Growing up sparing as a child in his spare time while being in the Golden Crozier he learned the art of fighting. he says \"Besting an orc feels good, though challenging. One can find it simple. When you ue their length and weight\n\nagaisnt them. Time your movements and strikes and they should fall before you relatively easily.\" He also said \"Any Orenian like myself can do what I've done. Just trust your feelings it's not as hard as it seems.\" There you have a good honest man to lend\n\nhis wisdom.\n\n   Locations of the\n    Lorraine Killings\n\n   Here is the list of the location of known spots of the lorraine killings.\n\n-1 Garin Road\n-5 Ganford Road\n-Infront of the Feslen Garrison\n-Falling from the church ceiling\n\n-Ross Road\n-The courtyard by the back gate\n-By the Feslen Auction house\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n   Buy Ad Space in the Feslen Informer for\n        50 Minas\n      Contact Adam!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I serve to Lady Ceona and House Vertilla.§0\n§0I serve to Gonzallo de Castro and the King Himself as well.§0\n§0Jonnathan may be a traitor.§0\n§0Leo Salb is a King§0\n§0Ceona might be cheating on Gonzallo§0\n§0Sir Rowen is a Steward§0\n§0Lord Thomas is a coward\n\nLord John is a friend§0\n§0Ser Edward has an Orden§0\n§0Ser Lion made one as well.§0\n§0William is new Recruit. Friend of mine.§0\n§0We're allied with Keints now.", ""),
