        StaticBook("Ravens Order", "§bPo'l MacCarthaigh", "One Claymore by order\nof Raven Armas\n\nNote: She is a good friend\nMake her something nice\n\nPrice: 60 minas (Paid)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Inn", "§b[Bartender] Arthur Caulfrield", "True Stories\n      Made Fiction\n\n       By Arthur\n        Caulfield\n\nIt was a quiet day at the tavern. The bartender had just served the last of the ale to an odd gentleman in a mask and was beginning to pack up when A man came through the doors. \n   He said nothing. Going straight to a table in the back he\n\nwas soon followed by a young girl, no older than nine. \n   The man had a serious expression on his face while the girl had quite the opposite. She wore a bright smile that had not been seen in a tavern for years.\n\nThe bartender could see by the shape of their ears that they were elves. They were obviously not ashamed of it, wearing the sign so openly in a place so close to Oren. \n   This scared the bartender. It had been quite a common occurence to cut the tips of\n\nelven ears a while back and he was not sure whether the practice still continued. \n    After a while, the drinks hit the gentleman in the mask. The bartender was just cleaning out his fifth empty mug when the gentleman spoke up.\n\n\"Shouldn't bring a kid to a place like this,\" He said turning around in his stool to face the man, his back leaning against the bar. \"Could get hurt.\"\n   The elven man did not respond for what seemed like an eternity, but what could have only been seconds\n\n\"Don't talk about my child.\" And believing it was over, he turns back to face the table.\n   \"I'll talk 'bout ooever I bloody well want\" The gentleman in the mask responded. \n    The bartender sighed. This was all too common an occurence. Each night a\n\nbrawl broke out for one reason or another. Tonight it had been over a child's safety. \n   There was little time to react, while the masked gentleman was drunk, he was also very agile and moved with quickness no drunk could even comprehend.\n\nJumping from the bar stool, the masked man approached the table and waited for the elven man to react. \n   No words were spoken. The elven man simply got up and pushed the man aside as he walked over to the bar. The bartender smiled\n\npolitely and served him some ale. The masked man did not like this response. At a sprint, he crossed the room and hit the elf in the nose just as he turned to register the noise.\n   The elf stumbled back and closed both hands around the nose\n\nwhich had already began to seep blood that stained his colorful blue robes.\n    The bartender, having recoiled in shock, now tried to dissolve the bar fight not realising it was already too late.\n\nThe girl still sat on the table at the far corner of the bar. Watching in horror. \n    The father, after controlling the bleeding, turned to his daughter and demand she stay there.\n    The little girl did not say a word, just simply nodded along to his\n\norders.\n   Both men had the same mindset. Both men remained silent, knowing what was going to happen. Both men left the bar and stood on the grass outside, still wet from that mornings rain. \n    The daughter, knowing her father could no longer see,\n\nran to the nearest window and stared out, both hands and face smooshed against the glass in anticipation.\n   However, the father saw this as he looked back, causing him to point and shout something muted by the double doors which were now closed.\n\nThe bartender felt sorry for her. To have a father so easily led into brawls could not have been easy. \n   \"Do you like orange juice?\" He asked her in a friendly tone. She turned away from the window to look at him with some level of confusion.\n\n\"Did you know that oranges are guarded by dragons?\" He asked in a conversational tone, walking over to a chest full of fruit. \n   It had always seemed like a waste to have this chest, he though, seeing as no one ever came to a bar to order freshly\n\nsqueezed lemon juice.     \"Dragons?\" The girl asked, mystified. Her eyes widened, not in fear this time, but in amazement. \"But why would dragons want to guard oranges?\" She asked a moment later, as the bartender brought out a mug and oranges.\n\n\"Well, oranges are the most delicious fruit, and the dragons know it. So in order to get the oranges, we need to defeat the dragons!\" The bartender explained, using his imagination for the first time in a while.\n\n\"Wow\" The girl replied, now trying to balance herself on one of the bar stools. When the orange juice was placed in front of her, she eagerly drank it, respecting the brave knights who allowed her to have it.\n\nThe bartender chuckled softly, knowing no other child would eagerly drink bitter orange juice like she did. \n   The fight outside has escalated, the bartender could see this through the window to his right. They had begun to draw swords and the\n\nshouting had intensified. \n    But in the bar, the child looked up at him with innocent eyes. Forgetting the danger her father could be  in and instead, entranced in a story of dragons and oranges.\n\nOf course, the mug had a bottom. And she soon found it. Her attention was lost almost instantly and she began to turn towards the window once again. \n   Quickly thinking, the bartender grabbed a pumpkin from the chest of fruits and plopped it onto his\n\nhead. Cutting off every sense he had. \n   \"Mmmffmfmfm\" he tried to mumble in order to get her attention. Thankfully she looked around and giggled at the sight of him. \n   Despite his embarassment, the bartender was glad he drew her\n\nattention away for just a moment. \n   For it was in that moment that her father snapped the masked mans neck and left him lifeless on the ground. \n   It was an image the child would never have to see, and that was worth the pumpkin becoming stuck to his\n\nhead.\n   Once the fight was over, and the father had rummaged through the corpse's possessions, he came to collect her. \n   She sat on the bar stool looking up at the man with the pumpkin head. Giggling to herself even as her father\n\nwalked in with a bloody nose and battle scars all across his arm and legs.\n   \"You think this is funny?\" He asked angrily, walking up to her and pulling her off of the bar stool. \n   She had little time to explain as he picked her up and took her out.\n\nThe bartender waved her goodbye, and she waved back. The father just carried on walking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tulatha's Diary", "§bTeerz", "Tulatha's Diary\n\nVolume 10\n\nDay 1\n\nI went hunting with Lan today, we ended up finding a huge cavern within was a book it was locked in a chest, I barely managed to avoid setting it ablaze, luckly Lan was there and saved the book from the fire.  I wonder whats inside.\n\nDay 2\n\nApparently we found a magic book!  I have lan out gathering the materials, we need a wolf, blood from myself and lan, as well as a bone for carving.  I plan on getting the girls together to help with this.  As we are a cult.\n\nDay 3\n\nTurns out we had to skin the wolf alive, the blood was astounding, however Lan quickly tanned it for me.  I wish the wolf had been dead for the ritual, but it wasn't allowed.  Now we must wait for the hide to finish tanning.\n\nDay 5\n\nUgh, there we go its finally done!  Lan's carving a symbol inside the corner of the hide.  *A symbol lies here*  We have to go through the book to see what we must do now.  It seems we need other symbols.  We have a choice of\n\nthese  *Several symbols sit here with descriptions*  I chose the one of lovers.  Lan agreed to it.  Julia and her lover are coming over to do their own ritual, they have their own wolf skin they made sure they did it when they where alive.\n\nDay 6\n\nAlright, we have everything ready, we must make the symbol, in our blood, we then need to write our own names in our own blood and I must channel mana into the middle symbol.  *A diagram is showed here*\n\nWish us luck.\n\nDay 10\n\nI was out for a few days, I can sense Lan, its amazing!  I can tell what he's feeling, he can sense me!\n\nIf I hurt myself he jumps slightly and glares at me once in a while, its funny.\n\nDay 11\n\nLan went out today, didn't tell me why.  My friend was silly and tried to go bind two Okars...thats what my Lan is, to herself, it failed, apparently you can only have one.\n\nDay 15 \n\nLan finally came back, he's wounded badly, his wound's don't seem to be healing...I don't understand.  I'm going to store you away for a while.  I'll use you as a note book dealing with Okars.\n\nDay 300\n\nIts been nearly a year since I bound Lan to me as my Okar, he's overly careful, he never goes out to cause trouble with me, his wound's don't heal proper.  He can barely taste, and feel.  But he can still hear, see, and smell better than\n\nI can, I don't know why fate has handed me these cards.  We got in a fight with some people, he kept them off of me, being faster as well and a skilled swordsman.  He kept me safe, however when he was hurt it hurt me just not as much, he got mad later\n\nafter the bodies lay fallen across the floor.\n\nHe saw how his pain had hurt me as well, and he left.  \n\nBack to the box you go.\n\nDay 421 \n\nToday, I woke up, dread filled me, I didn't know what was going on, then the pain hit me.  Its still there, I can't find Lan, it feels like my soul has been ripped out.\n\nDay 434\n\nIts been a while, I foud out what happened, Lan killed hims....it was my fault.  The monks won't return him.  Why, do they hate me?  He should be returned to me....hush little baby, everything will be ok.\n\n*The pages are filled with a madwomans ramblings.*\n\nDay 500,\n\nI write this, Okar's are a curse, don't meddle in what you think you know...this is my final Entry....goodbye.  I will go the way Lan went' and drink a posion.  Goodbye cruel world.\n\nSincerly \nTulatha", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser Quotes", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Heil Valdoria===\n\nExcerpts from the speech made by the glorious Kaisereich Decimus Rovin.\n\n\"...racial species must preserve the purity of the blood which Gott has given it!\"\n\n  ====Page One====\n\n  ===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"It is not for men to discuss the question of why Providence created different races, but rather to recognize the fact that it punishes those who disregard its work of creation.\"\n\n  ====Page Two====\n\n  ===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"...revolutionary change in our knowledge and therewith a radical reconstruction of the picture which human history gives us of the past and will also change the course of that history in the future.\"\n   ===Page Three===\n\n\n\n\n     And remember, \n       If you see a glorious member of the Kaisereich, yell\n\n   \"HEIL VALDORIA\"\n   \"HEIL THE KAISER\"\n   \"HEIL DECIMUS\"\n\n ===Approved By===\n\nThe Reich Ministry of Public Enlightenment and Propoganda.\n\n-Goseph Joebbelstein.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kaedreni", "§bThe Bloody Baron", "22nd of Malin's Welcome,\n                              1519\n\n\n         THE STATE\n             OF THE\n           KAEDRENI\n\n\n       by Titus de Sola\n\nDust scatters on the horizon.  Hooves on valley upon valley thunder to a halt, beasts glaring across to the other, obeying their rider's whims.  Carrion birds dare defy the scorching heat and incandescence of the regal\nWhite Sun.  A scene is painted for\n\nyou that will set the stage for generations to come. But no matter the turmoil nor the degeneracy of either side I find my conscience bothered greatly by the fact that the blood of Kaedrin and Rhoswen turns against eachother under both banners of the war.\n\nThe Kaedreni have opted to let their luster become a finely honed weapon, a greatsword, to be used at the whims of Savoie and Sarkozic alike, though disrespected moreso on behalf of the latter.\n\nBut only the Kaedreni allowance of such be at fault.\n\nAnd it is a weapon, forged inside the lungs of hell, wrought by tens of thousands of the strongest men of our Kaedreni race, that we do now let the others, who have forgotten their place as our vassals, use freely and improperly against eachother,\n\nlike children who can scarcely pick up a fork.  That weapon is our martial mastery and sheer superiority in waging conflicts, gained by our diligence in carrying out the will of God and His first, the line of Horen, and then of Chivay.  No other Race\n\namongst Men can maintain aggression nor offensive nor conviction in the way that the Kaedreni man can; it is simply impossible.  They cry as they attempt to emulate our finest military traditions that they have inherited our place as the finest amongst\n\nmankind, but like all others their walls crumble, their people degenerate, they turn to banditry and villainy, and they destroy themselves from the inside.\n\nThey frequently seek our service as their officers, but they will never be heirs to Kaedrin.\n\nThe free men of the Rose have turned on eachother, instead of their proper enemies: those who envy all we Kaedreni have done.\nPeter must weep, if the dead weep, at the state of our people, our Kaedreni race.\n\nI would weep in his place, but I\n\nwould also hope.\n\nI would not see the blood of Kaedrin wither into nothing in the same way that the Horens did.  Even the common Kaedreni man, at this stage, is more bloodworthy than your mainstay Orenian lord, and no doubt far more\n\nthan those savages of color out of the Duchy of Adria whom want to eat us alive. I would not see our people fall to that fate. I would endeavor to stop it.\n\nI, De Sola, would fight to the death if need be for our people, so long as it granted my\n\ncountrymen victory.\n\nAnd though when fighting we are naturally greater, fight, we must not always.\n\nWe need consolidation.  Ties of marriage between our Kaedreni Houses.  Living space, territories, slaves.  We cannot forget what it means to bear\n\nour name.  We were made to militarily administrate the world, and everyone else living in it are either ourselves, our allies, or they are rebels.  There is no other alternative.\n\nWhich of the three are you, friendo?\n\nMy love and my strongest wishes to those whom this letter concerns.  May it find you in good health, and in the mind for a change of the course of our history.  Hear out this message, brothers, hear out this message and bring Creeping Death to them all.\n\n\nBy Owyn's guidance, we will prevail.\n\nAve, true to Kaedrin!\n\n                         T.d.S", ""),
        StaticBook("These Words", "§bGriffith du Mont", "These Words,\n      My Love\n\n  by Griffith du Mont\n\n\nThis song was written for my beloved wife, Kyra. Though we will never have children... It matters not. We are rich in happiness. Words are my children and you my inspiration.\n\nMy pen pierces the page and\nImpregnates her with my thoughts.\nShe nurtures my mind in\nA womb of poetry,\nKept deep inside her,\nThose memories I'd long forgot.\nA preservation of distant,\nYet vivid imagery,\n\nNested within the warmth\nOf her embrace,\nAre the comforts of\nMelancholic, younger days\nThe wind on my back,\nThe sun in my face,\nRereading my past in\nNew yet nostalgic ways,\nThe precious moments that I can't replace,\n\nThese words, my children,\nBring me back, to that special place.\n\n         Griffith du Mont,           Grand Maestro\n               & Husband\n\nThis book was found in the Bard's College Library on the Isle of ArmaLuna in Asulon. I was brought over and transcribed by Elorna Avern.", ""),
        StaticBook("Man and Beast", "§b12igon6", "In the Land of Dragons and Lore, Where hope was no more...\n\nThere was a wandering man, sitting upon a lamb.  Striding across fields of ash and decay, filled with the smell of death and dismay.\n\nSoon he came across a desolate town.  Black and burning, making no sound.\n\nSoot clouded the air, everything was covered in flames.  With fire consuming the houses, or at least, what remained.\n\nThe sky black with smoke, his eyes teared, throat choked.  Salvation was lost, the man was distraught.  \"What could have brought such a pain, and for what gain?\"\n\nHe traveled through the deserted town a bit more, 'till he came across the resting\n\nplace for the poor.\n\nThe Man trembled as the sight of the lost lives were brought to light.  T'was a small boy, just a lad, laying with his Mom and his Dad.\n\nTears streaming down his face, The Man had to leave this place.\n\nBut as he turned, he faced a great shadow moving with grace.\n\nHe halted as the shape began to loom, the man's fate, it seemed doomed.  The blackness, shrouded in dust, came closer and closer \"Move Sheep!  You Must!\"\n\nToo frightened to run, the sheep, stood still.  For the sheep knew, the beasts intent, was to kill!\n\nThe man dismounted his steed and withdrew his sword from its sheath!  Wielding it with all his power, knowing this could be his last day, or even hour!\n\nComing into view, was the beast's large clawed feet.\n\nThe sound of its weight on the earth was immense, the rocks shook, and it rattled a nearby fence.\n\nThe Man squinted forward, and aimed his steel toward, the\n\ngiant's smooth underbelly.\n\nIn an instant he ran, without fear, or a plan, and he plunged the sword into its belly!\n\nThe monster let out a terrifying scream, as it red blood streamed!\n\nIt kicked the man back, crushing his arms, it made his ribs crack.  His face turned pale, as the serpent kicked and flailed.\n\nIn an ear shattering roar, the Thing spat fire and gore.\n\nThen as it fell to the ground, with an earth\n\nshattering sound, It collapsed its wings.  With its last breath, it clings.  Then let go, yet another, final yell of thunder!\n\nThe scorched land was silent, in awe.\n\nSwiftly a quiet rain began to fall.  The blackness of the\n\nearth began to wash away.  The sun started to warm the day.\n\nAmidst the new mud and dew, the man came into view.\n\nHe was propped up against a charred stump, but soon, softly, his heart began to pump.\n\nHe slowly opened his soot encrusted eyes, smiling, he could see where, in death, his enemy lies.\n\nHe fetched his sword from the beast, before hobbling his way to his sheep.\n\nThe sheep greeting his rider with a soft lick,\n\njust enough to brighten the man's face, just a bit.\n\nHe smiled and mounted his steed.  Broken, battered, and a legender since.\n\nThe Time of Dragons and Lore.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fishing Song", "§bMelodystar", "Katie's Fishing Song\n\nOne, Two, Three, Four, Five!\n\nOnce I caught a fish alive!\n\nSix, Seven, Eight, Nine, Ten!\n\nThen I let it go again!\n\nWhy did you let it go?\n\nBecause it bit my finger so!\n\nWhich finger did it bite?\n\nThis little finger on my right!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Jayan C2", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "The Jayan\n\nA fictional adventure series.\n\n           ~By Sofetios\n                 Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n         The King\n\nWe were approaching Northenway’s front gates. It appeared to be a very large city looking from the outside. As soon as the guards spotted us they came running.\n\nWhen they got to us, one of them said, “Lord Jedway! What happened to you? You’ve been missing for a week!” Henry raised a hand and said, \n\n“I was kidnapped by two bandits, and this young man saved me.”\n\nHe pointed to me. The guards looked at me and seemed a bit unbelieving, but then said, \n\n“Well its good you are back, you had better get back in the city. It isn’t safe out here.”\n\nThe guards led us in the city, I was amazed at the size of the city. I had never been in one so big, at least I didn’t think I had. We passed people in tents and damaged buildings and went through another gate inside the city.\n\nThrough this gate there was much nicer housing and no tents. After a bit longer we passed through yet another gate. Here there were large houses and manors, and finally went through one last gate.\n\nOn the other side of this gate was a path that led to a castle. It troubled me that the first part we went through as in such poor condition. When we got to the castle, the guards opened the doors.\n\nWe were led  up to the throne room, I stayed behind Henry, not sure what to expect.  At the front was what appeared to be the queen, the king, and a prince. When we got to the throne, the king stood up and went to Henry.\n\n He said in a stern voice, “Henry, where have you been! The castle has been in dismay without you around.” Henry looked at the king and said,\n\n“My coach was attacked by bandits on my way to Sadzten. I was held captive for a week. I wouldn’t be here right now if it wasn’t for my friend here.” He got out of the way and pointed to me.\n\nAs soon as he got out of the way the queen looked at me and her mouth slowly dropped and she got up. The prince looked at me with strange eyes. The king said,\n\n“Well thank you very much young man for your se-“\n\nAll of the sudden,  the queen was at the kings side. The king turned to her and said “Sofia, is everything all right?” The queen looked at me with strange eyes and said, \n\n“I’m sorry… It’s just he looks so much like…”\n\nhe king raised a brow then looked at me. Suddenly a expression of shock came over his face. \n\n“Boy what is your name?” I said,\n\n“James… Clark?” As if I was unsure if it was true, which I was coincidently.\n\n“Its just, you have the same eyes, hair, and face as our lost son who disappeared five years ago…” said the king. “Does the name Cire mean anything to you?” Right as he said the name I felt a large pulse in my head.\n\nI fell to the floor in pain as I yelled. “ARG!” The queen and Henry stepped back, but the king did not. He said under his breath. “My word, that cult must have…” The King knelt down to me. A guard said,\n\n“My Lord, get away from him, he may be dangerous!” \n\nThe King looked up to the guard and said,\n\n“You fool, this… this is my son.”\n\nThe king said to me, “Cire.” My head throbbed hard again at the name. “Look at me.” I forced myself to look at him. I found myself recognizing him and not recognizing him at the same time. It made my head hurt worse.\n\nI think the king saw the recognition in my face and stood up and said, “Get my son to a bed, and get a doctor!” Two guards came up and helped support me as I tried to stand up.\n\nThey half helped half carried me to  a room and I laid on the bed clutching my head. After a few minutes my vision was hazy and I wasn’t hearing right. I think I saw a old, rich looking man came in the room with the king.\n\nThe old man said, “This had better be important, I was just having tea!” The old man looked to me and said. “So what is wrong with him?” The king closed the door and said,\n\n“The Arimo cult.”\n\nThe old man jumped back and said in a hushed tone.\n\n“What!? Are you sure he’s even stable enough to be around? And how did he escape?” The king just said,\n\n“You need to counter act the drug.”\n\n I thought, how did the king know about the drug? The old man said,\n\n“You think I even know where to begin? The complexity that I’ve heard is in that drug is incomprehensible, even to me. your better off putting him down.”\n\nThe king angrily responded,\n\n“This is my son you fool! I would rather die than do that.”  The old man shook his head.\n\n “ Look, I wouldn’t know where to start.”\n\nThe old man seemed to get something out of a small pouch he carried. “Put this powder in water and have him drink it, It’s an all around cure I’ve been working on. Though I doubt it will counter act the drug.”\n\nThe King grunted in frustration and said,\n\n“Fine. Thank you, you are no longer needed.” The old man then turned and went to the door, looked at me one last time, and left.\n\nThe king left the room and after a moment came back in with a mug and an empty pouch. By now I was starting to lose conciseness. The King held my head up and I barely made out him saying the word “Drink”\n\nI drank the water slowly but surely, at the end the king let my head down and everything went black.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 4", "§bFenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: The action begins in part four of \"Double Dragon!\" I hope you enjoy, and as always, Onto the story!\n\nChapter Eleven: Moonlit Melee\nAfter helping to clean up the large meal, I asked if it would be any trouble if I slept somewhere in their home. \"Follow me! I gotcha covered!” Natalie said, then led me to her room. She rubbed the back of her head\n\nSheepishly when we arrived \"Eheh, we don't really have a guest room, but I have two beds in mine so uh, guess where you're sleeping tonight!\" She said with a sly smile. I looked in the room with a grin on my face, \"Thank you so much for everything\n\nNatalie; I don't know how I could repay you.\" I said. Natalie waved her hand at me \"Forget about it! We're friends now right?\" She replied,walking into her room and throwing open a chest in front of the bed to the right. She rummaged around in it before\n\nPulling out a big net, exactly like the one that I was trapped in previously. She began to head back out of the room \"I just gotta go put this up, be back in a second!\" She said as she dashed down the hallway and out the front door. I giggled softly,\n\nLooking out the window to watch. She glowed slightly in the light of the full moon, giving a peaceful aura about her. She unhooked the cut net, before attaching the new one, standing back and resetting her trap. I saw some movement out of the corner of my\n\nEye, and when I looked over to the source, I saw the glint of a metal blade cut through the darkness. Bandits! I pounded on the window, desperately trying to get Natalie’s attention, but my racket making must not have been loud enough. The bandit was\n\nGetting closer, and now there were two! I sprinted out of the room, throwing my hat off “Shamone wake up! We need to save Natalie!\" I shouted at the parasite. He startled awake,before my hair grew out in thick cords, now reaching my lower back. Long hair\n\nHovered up and down my back, as I burst out the front door, \"Natalie! Watch out!\" I called out, warning her of the bandits. She looked to me, then around her, jumping back as she spotted the bigger of the two bandits already bringing his arming sword\n\nForward diagonally, aiming for her neck. She wasn't fast enough. The blade cut straight through her, cleanly decapitating her head from her body. I watched as her head flew through the air, landing on the ground, her body collapsing beside it. The clunky\n\nMan laughed \"I gotcha bitch!\" He shouted. I stopped dead in my tracks, holding my hand to my mouth to stop me from screaming. Sudden anger and sadness filled me to the brim, fueling my drive to take these guys out. I dropped my hand into a fist, stomping\n\nTowards him loudly as he laughed \"What are you gonna do little girl, kill me?\" He said amused, raising his bloody sword. I grimaced and bared my teeth, \"I'm not gonna kill you... I'm just gonna beat the shit out of you!\" I yelled, before charging at the\n\nMan, reaching into my hair and grabbing Shamones jaw, flinging it forward. His mouth shot outwards in my right hand, covering my arm in hair, forming the gaping maw of an alligator's mouth at my hand, outwards. The action took both of the men by suprise\n\nAnd the one that struck down Natalie swung at the hair, only to have his sword bounce off the thick cord back towards him, smacking his muscled chest but not cutting into him. Shamone bit the bandits left arm fiercely, piercing through his clothing and\n\nTearing at his flesh with his gruesome teeth. He cried out in pain, twisting his body, trying to escape the wicked bite. I swung my left fist as hard as I could, lengths of hair covering it up and spinning rapidly as tiny blades of hair grew on the now\n\nSpinning drill of a punch. He brought up his sword with his right arm, his left being disabled by Shamones teeth, attempting to block the powered up punch. My fist slammed into the flat of the blade, pressing it hard against his chest. I roared in pure\n\nUnadulterated rage at the man and the drill punch sped up while the sword starting glowing orange with heat from the intense friction acting against it. The man grunted and struggled with the blade, barely staying in place as his feet began to drag\n\nAgainst the dirt. \"Behind us!\" Warned Shamone. I shouted in fury, retracting the drilling arm and alligators bite, swinging my head forward, while a loud buzzing played in my ears. \"Gotcha!\" Shamone said as he responded to my actions, and thick cords of\n\nHair shot out with the headbutt like action. The hair ensnared the bandit in front of me as I lifted my head along with the bandit, and flung him behind me. The bigger bandit landed on the small frail one behind me, being crushed by his comrade. I turned\n\nTo face them, my hair flowing in thick swaths behind me “This is for Natalie you bastards!” I screamed and proceeded to kick the living hell out of both of them until they were poor, sniveling excuses of men. They moaned in pain and agony, as I looked at\n\nThem to make sure the bandits were down for the count. \"Don't you dare try to escape.\" I said in the most threatening voice I could muster. They coughed in response, writhing on the ground. I looked back to where I thought Natalie's body was and... It\n\nWasn't there. I looked around frantically, a panicked look on my face. Who would steal a body?! Then I heard something that made me believe I was going insane. I heard Natalie’s laughter. I looked to the source of the laughter and very nearly fainted.\n\nThere stood Natalie’s headless body, but she held her head at her side like a helmet. \"I didn't know you had a parasite! That's awesome!\" Her head said with a smile. Tears brimmed at my eyes and my knees grew weak \"This can't be real, you were killed!\" I\n\nSaid, not believing what I was seeing. She laughed again \"Haven't you heard that cats have nine lives? Well, I guess you could say this cat has quite a few more lives than nine, but the puns still there.\" She said, raising her head up over her exposed\n\nNeck. She plunked her head back down where it belonged, twisting it left then right. She smiled and spread her arms wide, as if it was no big deal that her head had come off. It was at that moment that the night had become too much for me to handle.\n\nI fell onto my knees, as my vision quickly went dark, and I blacked out.\n\nChapter Twelve: So That Really Did Happen?\nI woke up in a bed, still fully clothed from the feel of it. I was laying on my right side, with Shamone facing the rest of the room. The bed smelled of fresh laundry and, not surprisingly, cat hair. The\n\nEvents of last night came crashing down on me, as I sat up quickly and threw the covers off myself. I looked around the room to find that Natalie was nowhere to be found. I got out of the bed and grabbed my hat which was sitting on the bedside table,\n\nSlamming it over Shamone, right as he was greeting me with a \"Morn-\" Poomf. Covered. I heard his teeth clicking together in annoyance. \"Kid, take it easy, your friends fine. She said she was gonna get a small catnap in then go make breakfast... Speaking\n\nOf which! It's food time!\" Shamone said greedily. Even after hearing this reassuring news from Shamone, I rushed out the bedroom and to the kitchen. There I saw Sixis and Roger, weeping over dramatically \"Oh whatever shall we do! Our one and only\n\nDaughter was slain last night! Oh woe is we!\" Roger said, trying to hide a grin, while Sixis just started laughing. \"You-you’re laughing about your daughter dying!?\" I exclaimed in disbelief. Roger waved his hand \"She didn't die Fuqua! She has a parasite\n\nTo. Although from what we know from our chat with Shamone (\"He was still awake when you passed out by the way\" added Sixis.), Fishtail is a much different type of parasite.\" Robert said, as Sixis picked up where he left off \"Shamone helps you in combat a\n\nLot more than Fishtail, and can talk, but he can't grant you the ability to remain alive even after having your limbs cut off!\" Sixis explains. I eventually caught on to what they were saying \"So you mean to say that she's-\" I asked, before being\n\nInterrupted by Natalie herself \"Indestructible! Pretty much!\" She said, bursting into the dining room with huge stacks of pancakes on platters in both hands, balancing a bottle of syrup on her head between her long cat ears. She set the platters of\n\nPancakes on the table, then snatching the syrup off her head and placing it in between the fat stacks. I ran forward and grabbed Natalie in a hug \"You scared me half to death!\" I thought when your head got cut off, you were done for!\" I exlaimed, being\n\nVery upset. \"Eheh, sorry about that, probably should have mentioned that sooner. But for now, why don't you sit down and we can have an eat off again. I won't let you beat me this time!\" Natalie replied with grin, hugging me back briefly, before gently\n\nPrying me off. I nodded my head, “What about the bandits? What happened to them?” I asked. “Oh, them, I took care of it, told them that if they came back, their head would be the one on the ground. Then they just ran off.\" Natalie responded, sitting down\n\nAt the table.  \"Stop messing around babe and get ta eatin! I'm starvin up here!\" Shamone yelled, vibrating my skull. I took the hat off my head, letting my short hair free. Now that the family knew of Shamone there was no real reason to hide him \"Fine you\n\nGreedy hog!\" I shouted back, then sliding into the seat next to Natalie. The rest of the family chuckled at our bickering, as we all began to eat. It looked like a return to normalcy for me... Wait, wasn't I supposed to train for something?\n\n\n\n\n================End Of Part Four\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCharacter Info-->\n\nNatalie FoRune: Age: 17 1/3. Height: 5'8\". Weight: 127 lbs. Likes: Making friends, Sunlit naps, Bowling, Golf, Parkour, Subjecting others to terrible puns, Robbing from the rich, Giving to the poor, Potatoes.\nDislikes: The mob, Feliz, Sushi, Guards,\n\nBullies, Marsupials, Loud noises, Lemonade, Getting caught.\nA feline feral, Natalie FoRune is an excelent thief and swordswoman. She makes use of her ability to not die of mortal wounds to her advantage, often stopping large groups of bandits from robbing\n\nA singular person. She is the mix between a human and a kharajyr, and has the traits of both. Her parasite, Fishtail, is her primary weapon of choice, her second being her claws. Her playfulness while fighting is a key signature of hers, often throwing\n\nOff enemys at how she laughs in the face of certain doom and death. She has been known for taking off her own head and placing it in random places, either to spy on people, or scare them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Double Dragon 1", "§bFenexo Freely", "\"Double Dragon!\"\nBy Fenexo Freely\nForward: I thank you dearly for reading the first four chapters of \"Double Dragon!\" I wish to specially thank Valeria Yule for all her support. Now, onto the story!\n\n\n\n\n================Amnesia Can Be A Bite In, Fuqua, And The Demon In Her           Hair.\n================\n\nChapter One: \nNew Folsom. Not a bad place to live. But then again, it wasn't exactly a good place either. Crime ran amok and the guards were crooked. The Mob ran this town and everyone in it… but it's practically the only place left to live.\n\nMy name is Fuqua, at least thats what Shamone says it is. I can’t remember anything besides him and his… Somewhat rude entry into my life. Everythings still blurry about him, but from what I can gather, Shamone and I are connected permanently.\n\nLiterally. I’m hiding him under my hat right now. He says he’s a parasite and that he’ll just be taking some of my food every now and then. Theres only one problem with that. His mouth is on the back of my head and he’s using my hair as his arms and legs…\n\nI guess you could say that ever since he’s latched onto me, its just been one big, long, bad hair day… Well… Heres my story…\n\nChapter Two: A Rude Awakening.\nI woke up in a room in New Folsom’s Tavern, The Rusty Nail, with a skull splitting headache. I lazily sat up, rubbing my face and then scratching the back of my head. “Hey! Watch the hands Kid!” A brutish voice said.\n\nI screamed in surprise, leaping out of the bed and turning around to find… Nothing… There was no one be found… I stood there, extremely confused. Where had that voice come from?\n\nAs I pondered this thought, the voice called out again “Hey babe, when can we get some food, I’m starvin up here!” I yelped and spun around, now for sure that someone was here. “W-who’s there!?” I asked worriedly. My heart was beating a mile a minute.\n\n“I’m right behind you, can’t you see?” The voice said. I slowly turned, scanning the room for any signs of life, but all I saw was a pile of clothes next to the bed. “Are you invisible?” I asked, still looking around carefully.\n\nThe voice laughed in a deep gruff tone, being easily identifiable as male. “I wish! But hey, its fun messin with ya! I’m on the back of your head!” The voice said. I froze, as I reached my hands up to my hair,\n\n“The… Back of my head?” I asked, more than worried. He responds “You bet! Be careful reachin around back there; don’t want ya puttin my eyes out!” The tough sounding voice laughed heartily, deeply amused by this.\n\n As my hands slowly trailed up the back of my head, they glided against… A tongue!? I pulled my hands back terrified and disgusted, hopping around the room and shaking the slimy saliva off of my hands “EWEWEWEWEW!” I exclaimed in a frightened voice.\n\nThe monster spat, like he was trying to get a bad taste out of his mouth. “Ew yourself! You taste as if you haven’t washed in days! Which makes sense, I was wondering when you’d wake up.” The monster retorted. I paused at this last piece of news,\n\nnot jumping around anymore. “What do you mean by that?” I asked, now more worried than scared. “Well… When I formed a symbiosis with you, ya just kinda conked out. Sorry about that, but a parasites gotta eat ya know!” The beast replied.\n\nI tried to remember what had happened, but the further back I went, the less there seemed to be. In fact… There was almost nothing. My head was empty and devoid of memories! I couldn't even remember what I was wearing before that monster was put me under!\n\nI rushed over to the pile of clothes, picking them up and examining them. They appeared to be some type of uniform for girls. The full uniform consisted of a white, long sleeved button up shirt with breast pockets and sleeve cuffs,\n\na black skirt that reached my lower thighs, a pair of high black stockings, reaching about 3 ½ inches away from the bottom of the skirt. Underneath the clothing there was also a pair of dark brown leather loafers.\n\nI pulled the clothes over my underwear covered body, before angrily asking the thing on my head “Just who are you anyways!” The monster snorted and said “The names Shamone. Nice ta meet ya Ms. Fuqua.”\n\nChapter Three: My Hair Eats Weird.\nAt that time, I was pissed. I mean, I had some kind of demon thing in my hair! It was just so… Gross. I growled in anger, trying to pull the parasite off of my scalp, but to no avail.\n\nI sighed and decided it would be best to try and just cope with the thing. I made my way to the bedroom door to exit, when a flash of white on the coat rack caught my eye. It was a hat! A white bowler hat with a black ribbon around it to be precise.\n\nI snatched up the hat and slipped it on over my head and Shamone. “Hey! I can’t see!” He shouted out in protest. I hushed him promptly, punching the hat in on my head, knocking against Shamones large crooked teeth.\n\n“I’m not giving out food for free. The least you could do is lay low and not make me look like a freak.” I said, to Shamone. The parasite mumbled to himself before going silent under the hat. I nodded my head, before heading out the door,\n\npast the empty hallway to the stairs heading down. It was a normal bar scene for midday… Unoccupied and desolate. Except for the massive rusted spike sticking out of the ground. It took center stage of the bar and was about 4 ½ feet tall.\n\nI thought to myself 'That is one serious accident waiting to happen.'  Before heading to the bar counter “What do you have for food?” I asked the bartender. The man looks up from cleaning a glass out with a rag.\n\n“We got some steak and some bread leftover from chefs last cooking session. If ya want that, it’ll be 20 Dollops and 15 Schments.” Said the bartender. I held a hand up, about to ask what that means,\n\nand then figured it must be the money that this place uses… Or even that I used to use. I digged in my breast pockets, pulling out a couple of paper folds with numbers on them and a few coins. The numbers on the coins read 25 and the bill read 50.\n\nI handed everything to the man, hoping he would sort out what he needs and give me back my change. The bartender nods his head, taking a portion of the coins, and going to get the plate of food from the slightly heated oven.\n\nThe aroma of warm steak and bread wafted over to me and my recently acquired demon. Shamone squirmed under my hat as the smell came his way. I pulled the bowler down tight, slightly smothering Shamone, as he gnashed his teeth in complaint.\n\nI coughed loudly to try and cover the noise he was making, going to take the wooden platter of food from the man. “Thank you sir.” I said as I made my way over to the corner of the bar as fast as I could.\n\nI sat down at a corner table and immediately began to dig into the bread, tearing hungrily at it, having not eaten for at least a day I knew I would probably regret eating all this food in one sitting at some point and not saving any for later.\n\nShamone growls lightly and says “Kid… I’m gettin impatient with my food. I can steal from your stomach when I want, but that takes longer.” I sighed deeply, leaning against the table, not really wanting to feed the monstrosity on my head.\n\n“Fine… Here, quick.” I said as I grabbed up the steak with a knife and fork, cutting it in half and holding up the piece of meat behind me, then swiftly tilting up the hat. Shamone darted forward,\n\nchomping up the steak and slinking back under the hat, chewing sloppily. I looked around the room to see if anyone had noticed, and thankfully the bar was still deserted.\n\nI continued to eat my food, as a man walked in, heavily armed and armored, going to talk to the bartender.\n\nChapter Four: Milk Goes Good With Murder.\nI finished my food, getting up to give back the wooden platter to the bartender. I sat down at one of the stools next to the counter, “Got any anything to drink? I asked curiously.\n\nThe bartender nods his head “We have beers, whiskeys, wines, you name it, we probably have it.\" The bartender said, examining the large stock behind him. \"Hmm... Do you have any milk?\" I asked, seeing if they really did have everything a bar could have.\n\n \"You're in luck, got our last pint in stock. That’ll be 10 Dollops.” He said as he went into the back to get the milk. I retrieved the money from my breast pocket, setting it on the counter and relaxing a little.\n\nThe heavily armored man who entered earlier scooted closer to me, as the bartender returned with the glass of milk, a straw sticking out of it. I latched onto the straw, holding the glass in both hands, as I drank deeply from it.\n\nThe taste of it was wondrous! It must have been a favorite of mine from before… Well I suppose since before I met Shamone. As I was about half way done with my milk, the armored man, for some reason, decided it would be a good idea to try and hit on me,\n\nand slung an arm around my shoulder. “Hey pretty lady, how about I get you a real drink for a real good time?” He says with a smug grin. “Uh, no thanks, we already have a drink.” Shamone said for me. The armored man just smiled and said “Deep voice huh?\n\nI can dig it...\" I was about to speak up, before Shamone acted up again “THATS IT, HE HAD HIS CHANCE!” The parasite shouted. My hair exploded upwards, Shamones maw stretching wide, his two yellow glowing eyes staring hatred at the armored man.\n\nThe man stumbled back, “A p-parasite!?” He was barely able to get that out, before spikes and arrows of hair grew from my naturally short black hair, going to slam into him at an upwards angle, tossing him into the air. I turned around in surprise,\n\nKnocking the rest of the milk over, the glass shattering onto the floor. Time seemed to slow, as I saw the man land on the spike, and soon afterwards impale himself upon it. His chest bursted outward, as the huge spike impaled him, bits of gore flying\n\nHere and there. He grabbed at the big spike in his body, struggling briefly, before the life in his eyes faded to nothingness. I stood there, shocked at what had just happened, as my hat floated back down onto my head. I quickly pulled it on over the\n\nParasite. \"Guards! We have a monster in here!\" The barkeep shouted, alerting the nearby populace. I ran out of the bar and into the crowded streets full of staring eyes. Tears sprung to my own eyes as I passed the still bleeding corpse on the rusty nail\n\nIn the floor. This day had gone from bad to worse...\n\n\n\n\n================-End Of Part One-\n================\n\n\n\n\n\n\nArt: ----------->\n\n======Character Art\n((http://i.imgur.com/rn780uy.png?))\nFuqua, our main protagonist in Double Dragon!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Jayan C1", "§bSofetios", "The Jayan\n\n A fictional adventure series.\n\n           ~By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\n\n        Chapter One\n         Who am I?\n\nIn the distance I heard someone say,\n\n“Wake him up…” Suddenly I felt my face get slapped, Hard. I burst into conciseness and opened my eyes. I was in small room.\n\nI was tied to a chair, my head was held firmly in place by something that felt metal. There were three people in there not including me.\n\nThe one to my left had blue robes on and a hood that covered his eyes, the one to the right was closest to me and apparently the one who had slapped me, he had plate armor on and a longsword.\n\nThe last person in the middle had black robes on but his hood was off. The one in the black robes came up to me and said,\n\n“alright, first of all, what is your name.” to which I replied,\n\n“Where am I, what-“ I was interrupted by another slap by the armored man. The man in black said,\n\n“ Only speak when asked to. Now I’ll ask again, What is your name.”\n\n I thought for a few seconds then realized I didn’t remember my name.\n\n“I..Don’t know.” The man in the black robes seemed pleased at this. He said,\n\n“Good, then the drug must have worked.” To which I said,\n\n“Drug? What dr-“ I was slapped again by the man in plate armor. The man in black then said,\n\n“Alright, from now on your name is James Clark.”\n\nHe waited a moment to see if I would say anything, but I remained silent.\n\n“Ah good, your learning.” Said the man in black.\n\n“I do hope your comfortable. As we are about to give you a gift. You see, every person’s head has a… section that is left locked. We only wish to unlock it, and of course use it. ” He smiled and looked to the man in blue.\n\n“Do it.” The man in blue stepped forward and placed a hand on both sides of my head. I felt a pulse hit my head, then everything went black.\n\nI slowly regained consciousness again. I was laying on the ground and slowly got up and coughed. I looked around. I was in the middle of a huge crater. There were bits of wood and stone everywhere.\n\nI remembered the three people, the pulse, and the name they gave me, but nothing before that. I started to make my way to the edge of the crater. After a good minute or two, I reached the edge.\n\n I climbed over the lip and then saw the body of the man in black, crumpled on the ground. His face had a look of horror on it. I wondered what just happened. I walked onwards, hoping to find civilization.\n\nI walked through what was now a forest until I came across a small camp. Before I got into the clearing, I saw that there were two thuggish looking guys around a fire. Nearby them was a well dressed looking man tied to a post.\n\nHis clothes though were beaten and worn. One of the thuggish men said,\n\n“What are you going to do with the money you get for him?” to which the other responded,\n\n“Not sure, but we’ll live like kings for ransoming Henry Jedway.” He said looking to the well dressed man.\n\n“Not so high and mighty now are you Henry. You know you sentenced my cousin to death about a year ago. I’m wondering why I don’t just kill you now.”\n\nI didn’t want to get mixed up in this, so I was about to find another way around when one of the men looked toward my direction and said,\n\n“Hey! Who are you!”\n\n I began to step back slowly when the bandits got up and started running at me with weapons pulled.  I was about to run when I tripped on a root and fell on my bottom.\n\nThe thuggish men were about to swing at me when I extended my arms toward them and turned my head in fright. I heard a ‘Woosh’ two crashes and two thuds.\n\nNoticing I wasn’t yet dead, I looked up and saw that the two men were about 25 feet away from me on their backs. I quickly got up as they did also. One of them said,\n\n“What the heck was that!?” To which the other said towards me,\n\n“I’ve heard of your kind, you’re a Jayan!” The one talking turned to the other thug and said pointing to me. “Let’s get out of here! We can’t fight that!”\n\nThe other thug looked toward the well dressed man and said,\n\n“But-“ the original thug then said,\n\n“I don’t want to die! Let’s GO!”\n\nThe Thug started running and the other one looked at me and then followed his friend. Confused, I looked towards the well dressed man, who had observed the whole scene and said, “Are you…Ok?”\n\nThe well dressed man just stared at me. I went over to him and untied his bonds. When he was released, he said, “What are you, and how did you just do what you did?” I replied,\n\n“I’m not exactly sure what I did.” To which he said,\n\n“You extended your arms and sent those two brutish thugs flying, without making contact.” \n\n“I did?” I replied.\n\n“Yes.” said the man. After a moment he shook his head and said, “Either way, thank you for saving me. I am in your debt. What is your name?” After a moment I said,\n\n“James Clark.” The man then said, “I am Henry Jedway. Noble of Northenway. We should head to Northenway now. I know the way.” .” He stopped for a moment then said,\n\n “Also, you should keep… whatever it is that you did a secret. Wouldn’t want to give people the wrong impression.”\n\n I nodded, not sure what else I could do other then follow him, and set off.\n\nEnd of Chapter One\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this. I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing please let me know by bird or in person!\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("JayasJourney C2", "§bSofetios", "Jaya's\n        Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n\n         Linink\n\nAs I woke up the next morning I couldn’t help but feel a bit afraid. Linink was one of the most important people in town and he was never really free.\n\nAlso, why was my Mom so worried last night? I stepped out of bed. Instead of the usual hardwood floor I was used to I was stepped on something lumpy and cold. I looked down and jumped back on my bed.\n\nThe weapons from last night where on the floor right next to my bed. \n\n“Jaya what’s all the racket?” Said my mom’s voice. It sounded like she was coming to my room. Quickly, I covered the weapons with my blanket.\n\nLike that would do anything, but it was worth a shot. My mom came in the door and said,\n\n“Jaya why is your blanket on the floor?” \n\n“Bad dream.” I Lied.\n\nMy mom frowned, bent over, and was about to pick up the blanket. I closed my eyes and cringed from what was about to happen. \n\n“Jaya are you ok?” Said my Mom concerned.\n\nOpening my eyes I saw my mom had folded the blanket and on the floor was nothing.\n\n“Uh, yea.” I said scratching my head. “I think I just must have hit my head.”\n\n“Well it’s a good thing your going to see Linink today.” My mom said. “Come on, breakfast is ready.”\n\nI ate very little breakfast this morning. The taste of it as usual was great, but the stress of what I thought was to come overcame my hunger. After breakfast my mom took me straight to The Adventurers Guild.\n\nAs I approached the massive building I started to get nervous. My mom opened the doors, led me past staring students, rooms that where full of weapons, and many more things.\n\n Finally we reached Linink’s Office. The large green door looked inviting enough but as to what was to happen behind it still worried me.\n\nWithout knocking a voice said, “Come in.” My mom and I entered the triangle shaped room. I saw Linink sitting a table in the middle, but beside the table on both sides where my friends Sofetios and Sofia.\n\nI relaxed a little. At least they would be here with me. “Jaya, would you please take a seat.” Said Linink coolly.  I took a seat, looked back at my mom, and Linink then said,  “I need to speak to Jaya and his friends alone Madam.”\n\nMy mom nodded and left the room quietly. Everyone was quite for a bit until I said, \n\n“What am I here for?” \n\n“I’d like to know that too.” Sofetios added.\n\n“Same here.” Said Sofia. After a moment Linink said,\n\n“We are here to discuss a recent series of events.”\n\n“Like what?” said Sofia. “Other then the Melonko Festival being today all that’s really happened was that Rainstorm last night.\n\n“Exactly my point” said Linink. “A rainstorm now? In the middle of summer? I just don’t really see that as natural. There is also the Prophecy.”\n\n“You mean that old tale everyone listens to at the festival?” Said Sofetios inquiringly.\n\n“Just that.” Said Linink seriously. “From what I’ve seen happening in the last two days I’m inferring that it may be coming true.” At this Sofia laughed and said,\n\n“Like that would happen now. I mean the rain was probably coincidence and it’s not like the weapons have been found.” At this I felt the blood drain from my face.\n\n“Well from what I heard from Jaya’s Mother last night, I think they may have been found.” Said Linink. Sofia and Sofetios look right at me and Sofetios said, “You didn’t really… I mean you couldn’t have…”\n\n“He probably didn’t” Said Sofia, Otherwise he would be wearing them right now. It’s not like he would leave them at his house or something if he found them. Right?” I looked slightly down at this comment.\n\n“The weapons only appear if the owner wants them to.” Said Linink. Sofetios turns to me and said. “Well Jaya? Did you actually find the weapons?” I tell them the whole story of what happened last night and this morning.\n\nWhen I finish, Sofia is staring at me in disbelief, Sofetios is too, and Linink looks the same as he did before. No one said anything for a while until Linink said,\n\n“Well I guess the prophecy is coming true.”\n\n“Should we tell everyone?” Said Sofia.\n\n“No.” said Linink. “That would only raise panic. We should just tell whoever really needs to be told then you three set off after the festival.”\n\n“Us three?” I said.\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink “You know both Sofia and Sofetios pretty well. Except for what each they specialize in.” I didn’t actually know what Linink taught Sofetios and Sofia in the Guild and they had never shown me.\n\nI gave an odd face to all three of them then Linink said, “To put it bluntly Sofetios is a magician and Sofia is a fighter, in class terms that is.” \n\n“A magician?” I repeated while looking at Sofetios.\n\n“Intermediate magician.” Said Sofetios. “Sorry but Linink said we couldn’t tell anyone outside the guild.” \n\n“Wait so what can you do?” I said. “Levitate stuff or something?” Sofetios looked at Linink and Linink nodded.\n\nAll of the sudden everything small in the room started to slowly floated upwards.  I froze and looked around.  Then the things in the air floated down to their original places.\n\n“You see Jaya, Everything we teach at this guild more or less has to do with Lin.”  Said Linink.\n\n“Lin?” I said curiously.\n\n“Yes, it is something that is in everything around us.” Said Linink. “Kind of like a fifth element so to speak. Sofetios will be teaching you about this on your travels.”\n\n“Wait.” I said. “There’s a whole Fifth element?”\n\n“Yes.” Said Linink simply. “Sofetios, Sofia, please get ready for your departure.”\n\n“But sir.” Said Sofetios. “We still-“\n\n“Come on Sofetios.” Said Sofia as he grabbed Sofetios on the shoulder and had him follow her. When they closed the door, Linink turned to me and Said. \n\n“You have a long journey ahead of you.”\n\n“Yes sir…” I said tentatively.\n\n“I just need to make sure you really have the weapons.” Said Linink concerned.\n\n“I would sir but I don’t know how to get them to appear.” I said.\n\n“Just hold your hand as you would your sword and try to will them there.” Said Linink. I did so and in a second a white sword materialized there. It felt warm in my hand. Linink seemed was taken aback a little, so I asked,\n\n“Sir, why me?” Linink seemed back as himself and said after a moment,\n\n“Because He chose you. At least that’s what the Prophecy sais.” Linink got up and went to his bookshelf.\n\nHe picked up two books and put them both on the desk. He opened one and the inside of it was hollowed out. All there was, was a semi-clear sphere about an inch long.\n\nHe handed it to me and said. “This is something I’ve been working on for a long time. Use it well.”  I sheathed the sword and took the sphere and said,\n\n“Sir, what is this?”\n\n“Don’t you recognize it?” Linink said surprised. “It is object from part of the lore they tell at the Melonko festival. Well, my version of it anyway.”\n\n“I’m sorry sir, I don’t really listen to the tales they tell.” I said a little embaraced.\n\n“Well then I should probably tell you.” Said Linink. “It is my version of a water sphere. This one I would say holds about 1 week worth of water for 3 people.” Unbelieving, I stared at the sphere.\n\n“All you need to do is heat it in something and water will come out.”\n\n“Sir?” I said. “What did you mean by ‘your version’?”\n\n“You’ll find out soon enough.” Said Linink. Suddenly there was music outside. “The festival is starting.”\n\n“Sir, what now?” I said.\n\n“Now, you go enjoy the festival.” Said Linink. “But before you go,” Linink picked up the other book and handed it to me. “This is a book on lore of Edrot. You may want to study it.”\n\n I turned to leave when Linink said, “and Jaya, two words of advice. First, with the powers you will soon possess, Make sure you use them the right way.\n\nSecondly, I need you to will away that sword for now. The people in town don’t need to see it.”\n\n“Is that all sir?” I said.\n\n“That’s all” Said Linink.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Governor Chivay", "§bLaethis Izalith", "Your Excellency,\n\nI write to inform you that I have requested a meeting with Praetor Tristin Tresery. This meeting is meant in hopes that I can apologize for much of the wrongdoing of my predecessors.\n\nThough I do not anticipate your\n\ndesire to attend this meeting, I thought it prudent to inform you my intentions so as not to circumvent your authority.\n\nIf you do wish to attend this meeting, you are more than welcome. The Praetor should have the details for such.\n\nSincerely,\nLaethis Izalith, Sohaer of Haelun'or", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Brotherhood", "§bJistuma", "Introduction:\nMany Aegeans now are sheltered. They know nothing of this world and what is happening. For instance, today I saw the Temple of Aegis in trouble. Slimes had started a siege on recently resurrected player, and sending them back to the\n\nCrypt. It was mayhem. And what troubles me even more, as a traveler, is that very few people know about the Dark Brotherhood. This evil guild is intent on the destruction of this world’s inhabitants. And needs to be stopped at all costs. This is why I\n\nwrite this book, so that you may learn to defend yourself against this, this taint… Let me begin on the history of the guild.\n\nThe History of the Brotherhood.\nIt is said they started off as… well… assasins with perfectly harmless intentions. This soon changed with the arrival of one known only as “The Stranger”. This “Stranger” as he is known, is responsible\n\nfor the deaths of many, and is rumored to be the Grand Master of the guild. It has been this way for many years now. If his true identity is found, report it to me immediately! It must be shared!\n\nThe Guild Itself.\nThe Guild is mostly assasins, with a few bandits mixed in. This makes it hard to track down members, commonly referred to as “Danalus’”. These appear to be the average rank, with half the guild seemingly comprised of it…\n\nThere is also the recruit variety of Danalus it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached this rank so far to my knowledge. This is the final rank. Only higher is the “unique” ranks. These ranks are only availible to those who\n\nThere is also the recruit variety of Danalus it seems. Koloth is apparently the next rank. Only two have reached this rank so far to my knowledge. This is the final rank. Only higher is the “unique” ranks. These ranks are only availible to those who\n\nhave proven their worth to the Grand Master, lesser councel and High Councillor. This is the Silencer rank. This rank is only available to those select few, and it is limited space. How it works is each high ranking member has one or two silencers, who\n\ncarry out personal contracts for the high ranking members. There is one more rank within the Brotherhood, and it is by far the most terrifying of the assassin ranks. It is “Iblees Champion”, a seemingly obscure term used to describe the best member.\n\nIt terrifies me, but thankfully, there is not a Champion yet.\n\nHigh Ranks\nThe highest ranks available are now closed it seems. These are namely the Lesser councel, High Councillor and Grand Master.\n\nThe Dark Brotherhood\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Ho", "§bSammy \"Mungo\"", "How to be a Silvertongued Devil- By Mungo the Bandit.\n\nIn life you may come upon times where reaching for your sword may not be the most ideal way to go, you may not be the best fighter, or you simply can't speak for your life, hopefully, this guide of\n\nsorts may assist you in swindling, lying, persuading and overall being a great talker. Now, me being me, I was born with the natural talent of making people absolutely adore me, whether this was being brought up in a tevern or my mother being\n\nquite a social escort, I cannot say, but what I can say is that this skill of mine has gotten me out of many  tight situations and into many fair maidens' dreams. But, enough of me glamourizing myself, I'll try to keep this book short and to the point.\n\n1.\nBe as polite as can be without seeming as if you want to kiss someone's backside, being polite leads to people liking you, and even giving you free things such as minas and food.\n\n2.\nBe eccentric and posh with your words. This of course excludes Orcs, they will most likely cave your face in if you use anything more complicated than six letter words. Use words such as indeed, gent, gentleman, kind, fine and so on, this\n\nmay lead to some thinking you a pompous whoreson, but to others you will seem a much more upper class gent or lady than you actually are, helping you achieve your goals whether it be getting that promosion, lying, succesfully conning,\n\nor simply being all the talk at spiffing Balls.\n\n3.\nSeem lighthearted, relaxed and calm, the calmer and more lighthearted you are, the more it will rub off on whoever you're trying to swindle, leading them to dropping their guard, taking a liking of you, or simply another way to seem that\n\nyou have no idea why there's a dead body infront of you while you hold a bloody knife, you just found it there of course.\n\n4.\nBe kind, even if it might not be in your nature, seeming like a kind person will help you in many ways, tricking people, this will lead to you making unlikely allies, you'll have more sway to your word, and if it comes to a tavern brawl\n\neveryone will believe you when you say you didn't start it.\n\n5.\nLast, but not least, be charismatic, even if you're quite the reserved person, this will inspire those around you, and lead to people believing your word over others.\n\nAnd so, that ends my short guide to being a charming and cunning criminal such as myself, whether you use it for good or evil, is your choice, I was just bored in the corner of a tavern waiting for someone to play some blackjack.\n\n-Signed, Mungo, the Charming Bandit.", ""),
        StaticBook("<3", "§bElayne", "It's sweet like nectar of the garden flower,\n\nIt's soothing like the buzzing of bumble bee.\n\nIt's warm like the rays of the morning sun,\n\nIt's the search of love so pure which keeps me on the run.\n\nIt's the pulse in my vein,\n\nThe thoughts in my brain,\n\nIn every breath that I take,\n\nThe smile my lips make,\n\nIt's in the twinkle of my eye, till the day I die.\n\nIt's my dreams in my sleep,\n\nIt's springs freshest leaf;\n\nA love so rare like this will always be with me for keeps.\n\nIt's warmth of my blood,\n\nAs my feelings flood,\n\nAs says my heart's beat,\n\nIts depth touches the ocean's feet.\n\nEven if its heart searing pain,\n\nWith nothing to gain,\n\nI will feel it as the tear on my cheek,\n\nAnd without words my soul will speak.\n\nA feeling so sincere,\n\nA bond so strong,\n\nI know my soul will never guide me wrong.\n\nI would wait till my last sunset,\n\nTill my heart slows down with dull ache,\n\nTill my eyes are wet,\n\nDak, you are my soul's mate.\n\n-=Lain=-", ""),
        StaticBook("S.G. Translation", "§bTaeleh Elibar'acal", "A Translated Text\n===================\n\nHail, one who keeps this book. \n\nThis book shall tell all you souls how to control the soul -- dark magic -- the dark fruit.\n\nTo get mortal blood. \n\nA soul bond within a gold vessel.\n\nYou must master this magic.\n\nA mortal's will is in a prison in a small corpse, a good master molds a gold soul.\n\nBut how, do you ask? -- I will tell you.\n\nYou get mage gold (arcaurum).\n\nYou make a vessel out of the gold and magically enchant it.\n\nYou make it look like the mortal. \n\nFor example, we have a Kharajyr.\n\nSoul bond within a vessel.\n\nYou drown it in a fire-like water.\n\nAnd then the vessel will lose shape and become the mortal.\n\n\nAuthor's Note: A very rough translation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Infinity", "§bGeedin Jayamen", "A Theory of Infinity\n       \n               -By Geedin\n                  Jayamen\n\nPlease note that this is simply my opinion. You can believe it or not believe it.\n\nLately I have begun to think about how things are connected. Take a rug for example. We see it as just one rug, but that one rug is made up of smaller things. Wool or string, which in turn is made of smaller fibers.\n\n I think that things probably get even smaller, maybe even infinitely. Just as things can be made of smaller things, so can smaller things make up one big thing. Again with the rug example. All of those fibers make up wool or string, which make the rug.\n\nYou may think it stops there, but what is the difference between fibers to a rug then to a rug being a part of a house?\n\nThe rug isn’t physically sewn into the house, yet it is part of it, the same as the fibers not being part of a rug until it is sewn into one. This begins a theory of Infinity. Let me give another example. Apples and oranges.\n\nThey are different, right? Well that is all a matter of perspective. Apples may be different then oranges, but they can still be grouped into what we call fruits.\n\nEven everything in the world, with its infinite different parts and pieces, can be grouped into what we call, well, the world. We may seem to think of the smaller things as making more sense when we should really be looking towards the bigger.\n\nNow let’s get a bit deeper. What is the difference between yourself and someone else? Well, there are differences, but there are also similarities. Well let’s think, what would make you two the same?\n\nWell the thing is, you are part of something that doesn’t make you the same, but groups you into one thing. Now for the trick. Say we are seeking all knowledge of things.\n\nWe learn more and more, yet never are satisfied with what we know, because there is always more to know. Well we are probably looking for some way or some knowledge that can make us content. I think I may have realized what that something is.\n\nIt is something complex, yet simple at the same time. It is everything, and it is also one thing. Imagine everything, every thought, every physical and non-physical thing connected into one, single, thing. That is Infinity.\n\nYou may be asking, how are we connected? I may ask you the opposite, how are we disconnected? As a rug is made up of fibers, so are you made up of flesh and bone.\n\nIf everything can be made up of infinitely smaller things and infinitely bigger things can be made of those smaller things, what does that leave, but the fact of infinity?\n\nNow to go into time. Time in my opinion is Infinite as well. The litteral sense of ‘Now’ is infinite. I think that there is no Past, nor future. There is literally only now.\n\nYou may say that you are able to think of the future or the past, but what is the future and past but theory and memory? There is no actual substance to it. Therefore I can only conclude that there is only, now.\n\nLet me delve into what we know as nothing. Nothing is completely a made up thing. There can never be nothing in any way. So you might ask, what made the something that is here now?\n\nWell, who says it ever had to be made. What if everything that is here simply was, is, and will be? That is all I have to write at the moment. Please know that this is only my opinion. Believing it or not is up to you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Boundwise Brews", "Pepernoot", "The Boundwise homebrews are all made with great care by the halflings of the Vale. The hops and herbs are selected with great care from the lush and fertile farms of Lenfarthing.\n\nCurrently two brews are available;\n\nBounderale\n----------\nA strong lightly coloured ale with a high proof, with a light fruity and sweet taste. Not recommended for the younguns.\n\nBounderbeer\n-----------\nA light beer with a hint of herbs, perfect drink with a meal or after a long hot day.\n\nTo order one of the brews, send a bird to Dudo Boundwise or Pansy Boundwise, Lenfarthing.\n\n((Pepernoot/fbPatty))", ""),
        StaticBook("Defunct Writing.", "§bThe Scribe.", "Why Poetry is Defunct.\n\nPoetry is the most useless form of writing. It seeks to convey a message in the form of a both a riddle and a rhyme. This is highly inefficient, as the message is deluded by the ornamentation used to create it in the\n\nfirst place. How can the message originally intended to be read keep its integrity when it is laden with unnecessary words that mean to weave into song? \n\nA song is perhaps a poem, but it is a preformance,\n\nnot an arrogant rendition of a message that is to be translated. Songs are set to music, and are designed to be entertainment, but poetry is just mindless babble with no point.\n\nA painting and a paper are very much comparable. Both try to convey a point or image, and do so by being as detailed and well set up as possible. However, a painting is not layed upon another painting, and then glued together with interweaving locks.\n\nThis would be the pinnacle of madness. This is what poetry is to sensible writing.\n\nPoetry is defunct.", ""),
        StaticBook("Untitled", "§bRuth", "I've found it. I've found the ruin. Something is in there, its in the library! I'm going down furth\n\n*The letter is scorched beyond this point. The writing was made in a hurry. A manuscript is stapled to the back of the note.*\n\nImperial Manuscript, mandated by the new Lord Kaldor Wicce. The note was found near the ruin of Azgoth, the Arith Keep. A dead bird was found near the note with intentions to fly to our aviary. Further investigation pending.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "§bValmir", "Mundane Healing\nBy Unknown\n\nMatron’s Foreword:\nWhen I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange Dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the treatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien.\n\nOne or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with nothing but rose thorns and petals.\n\nIn the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one of two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n\nMinor Cut (Matron)\nSimply apply a dose of deceased sentient slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it. The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n\nHeadache (Aleya)\nBoil milk, Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n\nStomach Ache (Matron)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full boil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber colour. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n\nSoreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax he muscles, and rest a lot.\n\nBurns (Matron)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere. The important thing about burns is\n\nto keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check the burn wound daily until\n\nthe skin can finally reform.\n\nFever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("I.E's Journal", "§bIaria Elervathar", "*The cover of this journal seems to be cladded with blue and purple water paint, along with vague drawings that got eventually ruined. On the first page, there's a beautiful night sky drawn. The owner's initials are written in the middle.*\n\n-I. Elervathar\n\n[!] The pages are filled with massive walls of text. At times, a small drawing that relates to the topic is seen at the side.\n\n(PM Halsi if you're interested to see the entries!)", ""),
        StaticBook("Baked Goods", "§bLilliana", "-=+=-Fruit Salad-=+=-\nA beautiful blend of apples and watermelon. This salad is cool on a warm day and fills up the stomach beautifully. A full helping of a small watermellon and two apples.\n\nPrice :: 5 minas per serving\n\n-=+=-Veggie Soup-=+=-\nA stew made of carrots in an apple broth. It helps cool the fever and warm the soul. Perfect for a rainy day. With three full carrots and the use of two juicy apples, this will fill you up.\n\nPrice :: 5 minas per bowl\n\n-=+=-Cheesey Bread-=+=-\nA garlic seasoned grilled cheese sandwich with rosemary and zesty cheese. A spread of sliced smoked ham or chicken is put in depending on your desire.\n\nPrice :: 8 minas per sandwich (2 bread)\n\n-=+=-Fruity Pancakes-=+=-\nPancakes made with various home grown fruits. The fluffy exterior holds the juicy fruit in place with each succulant bite. Your choice of berry, apple, or plain pancakes.\n\nPrice :: 4 minas per two pancakes\n\n-=+=-Plain Sugar Cookie-=+=-\nThe power of a pure sugar cookie sends shocks up your spine as you bite into this delicacy. With each tender chew, you find yourself pleading for more.\n\nPrice :: 4 minas for half a dozen\n\n-=+=-Fruity Cookie-=+=-\nThese cookies take a sweet turn for the healthy. Each of these pack a powerful flash of flavor of apple chunks in the dough.\n\nPrice :: 5 minas for half a dozen\n\n-=+=-Catch of the Day-=+=-\nWith a family of fishers, we catch a variety of fish we cook fry. Each fish is cooked fully to pull out its full flavor.\n\nPrice :: 6 minas per full fish\n\n-=+=-Fish Stew-=+=-\nThe fish are cooked and simmered into a steamy broth that takes the edge off any cold. A delectible taste and full flavor leaves you craving for more.\n\nPrice :: 5 minas per bowl\n\n-=+=-Pumpkin Pie-=+=-\nA creemy pie freshly baked and pulled from the oven. These delectible slices are enough to make you desire another slice.\n\nPrice :: 10 minas a pie\n\n-=+=-Apple Pie-=+=-\nA tastey treat perfect for any day. Servable both hot and cold this pie makes the mouth water. Made with fresh apples, this pie will bring you happiness.\n\nPrice :: 10 minas a pie", ""),
        StaticBook("A Parchment Roll", "§bThe Soothsayer of Argul", "I COME TO FOREWARN OF DEATH, FOR IT IS IMPENDING. [*The words are scratched into the parchment, the non-specific threat crudely scrawled.*]", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Squid", "Valmir_", "Tales of Squid\n\nBy Unknown\n\nOne of the most common creatures, squid are known to have existed in early Aegis and clear to modern day. They live among fish in water sources, including rivers, seas, oceans , ponds and even swimming pools.  This makes squid among the most adaptable\n\naquatic animals.\n\nSquid are very peaceful and do not attack back if struck. The only real danger they pose is drowning, should one hunt them underwater for too long.\n\nThe ink sacs found in quid are very useful, as the thick black ink is used for writing,\n\nas a dye, in alchemy and other uses. This makes squid hunting a potentially lucrative business.\n\nThere are numerous types of squid. Apart from the everyday common squid, some are thought to perhaps only be myths.\n\nIt is said that the Halfling Petyr Brandybuck once raised an army of Battle Squid in combat against the Undead. Their large teerth and overwhelming numbers are thought to have played a part in victory.\n\nAlso sometimes is seen are Flying Squid. Frequently\n\nmocked as a fairy tale, reports of them were quite common in Aegis.\n\nLastly, there have been reports for over a thousand years of Giant Squids that live in the deepest parts of the oceans. Although not often documented, some swear they have been\n\nresponsible for shipwrecks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cernunnos's Gaze", "§bAndor Abys", "Andor's Bardit Rite\n\"To Cernunnos may he keep the balance.\"\n\nhttp://i.imgur.com/C0gXhDd.png?1", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great North", "§bAptrotta", "The birthplace of the scourge… The final resting place of an ancient civilization… A land without hope… A land filled with beauty… Death hides everywhere… Life reveals itself everywhere… This land.. This ancient land… This land is The North.\n\nI, Cyrenn Yuln’Taynei, ventured into this dangerous territory with no respect to my own life all for one purpose. To discover. Discover what was lost. Discover what was hidden. Discover the unknown. The following pages you are about to read are written\n\nfrom using the notes I took on my expedition into The North.\n\nThe taint. The corruption. Its everywhere it seems. Even the entrance to The North is blocked by a large gate erected by the corrupt hands of the scourge. The air is foul with the stench of\n\ndeath. The snow stained crimson. Blood has been shed here recently. But, I must continue…\n\nJust after passing the gates I am greeted by an ancient ruin and the icy face of a cliff towards my front and to my left. With a quick glance to my right I notice a\n\na path revealed in the snow. The paw prints of some native animal leading me towards an unknown world.\n\nAfter about an hour of following the tracks I finally reach what I was looking for.  The path which shall lead me into the secret region of The North.\n\nA chasm lays before me. It twists and turns as my eyes follow it.Large stone tendrils reach out from the sides of the cliffs and the bottom like arms trying to reach for the sky. Luckily, these stone formations form perfect land bridges for I to walk\n\nupon. Without a thought of giving up, I continue forth.\n\nMy first night I spent still inside the chasm. I pitched my tent on a flat spot near the edge of a cliff. It was impossible to keep a fire going. The harsh wind that blew throuh the chasm smothered\n\nmy fire, stung my skin, and tried to blast my tent away from the cliff. Every hour the temptature dropped. This night was becoming a nightmare. Finally, my eyes gave into sleep.\n\nI awoke to a scream at the crack of dawn. A scream of terror. A scream of\n\npain. A scream signifying their final moments in life. The scourge was near. I had to go. With great haste I packed my tent and left.\n\nNothingness… All I encountered for miles was nothingness… Bare land stretched out before me for miles covered in snow\n\nand nothingness… This can’t be it… This wasteland can’t be all that The North is. My journey must go on.\n\nThere it is. The first sign of a past civilization. Standing before me was a towering ruin of a kingdom lost from time. Thewalls have fallen, stone\n\nlaying around the snow, while the supports stand tall holding up this ancient structure. A closer work would reveal the history of the ancient people who lived here before us. We could finally see how life really was for the previous inhabitants of our\n\nworld. This kingdom. This ancient Kingdom held secrets that could change our view on life forever. It was my duty to take a peek into the past.\n\nI stomped forward through the snow over fallen structures, over relics, over bones. The bones...\n\nThey were everywhere. Perfect skeletons resting against stone walls, skeletons laying down in the middle of the path, skeletons sitting in chairs, skeletons hunched over counters. The farther I went into the city the more I saw. Each skeletal corpse\n\nresting in a position one would do during life. Something hit this city… Something purged the city of its population. But what?\n\nWith that I leave this forgotten kingdom. I leave its people behind. The mystery to what wiped away its people will stay that,\n\na mystery.  I don’t dare to take anything with me in worry that whatever killed these poor citizens may still be lurking the ruined streets.\n\nThe day is still young when I came across a small white tent and a fire pit. Excited, I set of in a run towards\n\nit. Laid out before me was a horrific scene. A decaying body was left in the snow, the campground covered in blood leading towards a small tunnel. I decided to follow the trail, my curiosity getting the best of me.\n\n\nThe tunnel was small and cramped. Sunlight shone down through cracks in the ceiling. When I reached the end of the blood trail, a skeletal women stood hunched over a small lever as if she was guarding it from someone. Next to her sat a large basket\n\nconnected by rope. It hung over a large hole. The rope stretched upwards curled around a wooden beam. It hit me. A lift.\n\nThe lift shook slightly as I stepped into the basket. I reached out towards the women, my fingers splayed. Carefully, I knocked the\n\nlever the other direction, the bones falling over into a heap. With a creak, the basket started lowering itself downward. I was plunged into a darkness as the basket passed through the stick thone.\n\nMinutes passed before I was able to see light. The stone\n\ntunnel finally opened up and it came to my attention that I was placed inside a large cavern, the floor flooded with molten lava except for few places.  A bridge made of dark stone, the color of blood, stretched across the lake of lava. Blood shards\n\nfloated over the molten liquid. Across the lake sat a strange looking ruin.\n\nThe basket, only five feet away from the floor, plummeted towards the ground as the rope snapped above. I hit the ground hard, the basket landing on its side. Slowly I crawled\n\nout from the basket unharmed. I swiveled my head to the left, already making my way towards the bridge. Bubbles formed on the surface of the lake, popping every few seconds sending droplets of lava upwards at an alarming speed while I crossed the bridge.\n\nThe ruin was a mess. It appeared as if someone tried to get out quickly. From what it looked like, the place had once been a workshop for some sort of engineer.  There was faded blueprints laying on a desk to the front of me, a tool table to my left, and\n\nan oddly placed track to my left which rounded a corner. The tunnel in which it disappeared gave off a dim glow. My interest having peaked, I set off to follow the track.\n\nThe tunnel twists and turns as I walk through, a faint clicking sound audible. The\n\n room suddenly opens up to a large cavern, a weird iron device hanging from the ceiling nearing the floor. A few feet in front of it rests a mound of stone with a keyhole in the center. Soon I discovered I am sitting atop a gaint cage. Could whatever it\n\nheld be what killed the population? Scared, I dart back towards the lava lake quickly crossing the bridge only to remember the basket had fallen. \n\nMy eyes dart around the cavern desperately searching for a way out. A stroke of luck hit me as I noticed\n\nvines hanging down from a rock edge above, daylight shining down. My feet moved towards the vines before my brain could think. I curled my fingers up around one of them and slowly pulled myself up, panting by the time I reached the surface.\n\nThe endless\n\nwalk began again. Tall pine trees have begun to appear more frequently. Every once in a while I would come across a deer or some other animal…\n\nAfter a few days of nothingness, I finally gave up on the expedition... Food supplies were running low and so\n\nwas my patience... I knew The North had to hold more, but my life sources were dwindling...\n\nThe Northern Expedition was a great intellectual experience for myself. I hope my efforts to discover have affected some of you to venture out into this vast land by yourself. As usual, I wish you farewell.\n\n*A large, fancy signature rests on the bottom of the page*\n\n\n<()>Cyrenn Yuln’taynei<()>", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Moon Fest", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Black Moon Festival\n\nBy Unknown\n\nThe day of a lunar eclipse in Anthos. Once night falls, you won’t feel the warmth of the sun for many hours to come. Although a rare event, it occurred a few times in Asulon.\n\nSome denizens of the word took it as a sign of the end of everything while\n\n others celebrated the strange event. During this time the rates of crime increased dramatically as criminals took advantage of the unexpected darkness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy.", "§bMuildir", "Second Extract of Prophecy From the Kha.\n\nThe priests gain a prophecy not of prophecy of images, but of words. The shamans do as well.\n\nThe first cryptic message is as follows: \nOrigins are all but absolute.\n\nWe've not past my own dispute. \n\nStrands of fate now do entwine, both minds and soul are my design. \n\nSafeguard not my children near, mine is the vessel of love and fear.\n\nPity not the weight of strain, I do this time and time again.\"\n\nEnd first message.\n\nBegin second message:\n\nFruits of life do beg my pardon, roaming astray my endless garden.\n\nMy will sees metal turn to rest, and grow tall from all but dust.\n\nFind me not in book nor tome, for I'm the breath of life and home.\n\nForge noble beasts and kinds that reign. I do this time and time again.\n\nEnd second message", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Man's Dream", "§bMerekM", "'There once was a dream,\nIn this man's heart,\nThat life was never sullied,\nInstead was cherished,\nWould not be perished,\nAnd brought to eternal flame.'\n\n\n'A keep they built,\nSo it was felt,\nA burden they all could carry,\nBut darkness fell,\nIt did compel,\nA burden for none to bury.'\n\n\n'New burden made,\nSo lightness fade,\nAnd the man was who to blame.'\n\n\n\n\n-Poem rewritten by Merek Moonstrike. Original creator: Gladius Moonstrike.", ""),
        StaticBook("Red Rose Day", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Red Rose Day\n\nBy Unknown\n\nRed Rose Day is a celebration of affection towards a special someone in your life As signified by its name, participation simply dictates that you five a Red Rose to a person of significant importance, whether it be a sign of love, or a simple greeting to\n\na dear friend. It is one of the most commonly celebrated occasion. Humans, Elves and Kharajyr are most likely to participate in these festivities, while many Dwarves prefer to give gifts such as ale.", ""),
        StaticBook("A life..........", "§bLurk", "His body lay there with his guts torn out, I stand at the back watching our leader as he tears bits of his skin off and eats them.\n\nHe pulled out a slimy liver of the man and slurped it down his throat!\n\n\"T'ats what yer get fer tryin' ter assassinate me'h yer focks\"\nhe said with bits of kidney spewing out his mouth!\n\"A'h loike ter eat me hostages alive,\" he smiled a creepy grin.\n\n\"He chewed into the mans face tearing away the muscle and cheek bones.\nThe man screamed for his life, his voice boomed over the forest.\n\nOur leader dug his nails into his face ripping it open a bit more, He started to swallow the flesh until we heard footsteps nearby.\nThe leader rubbed some blood over his chest and pretended to be dead, the rest of us fled behind the trees.\n\n Orcs came out grunting, \"Oooh look at t'at we got ourselves a'h dinner.\"\nI took my bow off my back and aimed it at one of the Orcs, I slowly put the arrow on and Fired at the Orcs head.\n\nThe orc fell down with a loud slam.\nThe rest of us jumped out killing the other 2 Orcs.\nOur leader got up and thanked me then kicked the Orcs bodies to see if they were really dead.\n\nWe walked back to Petrus and our leader went into the Tavern, his blood stained outfit caused some curiosity, so people were\nasking if he was stabbed.\n\nHe didn't reply to none of them who asked, but instead slurped his Ale, I guess to get the taste of Internal Organs out of his\nmouth.\nI wandered out of Petrus and headed to the streets to the Temple.\n\nA man named Arthur stopped me and guided me into his Tavern, owned by Vinnie The Chef.\n I brought a couple of Ale's and stayed there writing, until I noticed a little girl\nwalk through.\n\nI decided to make a joke \"Yer 'ere fer Ale?\" I said, unfortunatley the father didn't take it Swell he told to the daughter to go\nplay outside onto the porch.\n\nHe started to get angry so before he could punch me I decided to punch him straight in the nose, blood dripped down from nostrils\nas he stood there holding it, tilting his head back.\n\nHe told me to get outside so I withdrawed my sword and was ready for a fight.\nI looked at him angrily, A women poked me with her sword and I can't remember much after that apart from he put his hands onto my neck behind me.\n\nArthur told me the story later on.\nI decided to walk back to Petrus and go to my Leader, but 6 Elves stopped me they wanted my swords, my bow and everything I had\nin my bag.\n\nLuckily for me, my group wasn't far behind the Elves and they came out of the trees chopping off the Elves heads, blood squirted\neverywhere.\n((Okay that is the first part of my Journal I will make the second one soon))", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy Cracked", "§bEllir'siol", "Setherien will rise above his voi[sic] dominion, with the remains of those he burnt waking from the rifts. And amongst his army, there will be four of his dark lieutenants. Not the Harbingers but the ones before them.\n\nTanreez the Dhadow[sic],\n\nSkidrow the Dreaded,\n\nMalghourn the Drake,\n\nBalrog the Demon.\n\nThey will break into the Fringe, and they will force the obsidian portal to open.\n\nSetherian has always wanted to conquer a[sic] ancient land, and with the moon rising the time is nigh. \n\nOnly when his Dark Lieutenants are killed, will the golden lance be able to kill the Black Wyrm.\n\nStop him, before he opens a path to the world where a Daemon holds hostage.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C1", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n      Chapter One\n\n  A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\n\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\n\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\n\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\n\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\n\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\n\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\n\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped.\n\nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen.\n\nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll.\n\n It had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones.\n\nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said.\n\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\n\nThen looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again.\n\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\n\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow.\n\n I then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\n\n As I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house.\n\nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.”\n\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\n\nEnd of Chapter One\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Nativitas", "§bShady_Tales", "There were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either,but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\n\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity. Truly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\n\nthe seven skies. With his intent and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. THe rolling seas, the proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God. The World was\n\nnot created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what?Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how  hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and\n\ngood our actions be. The first mortal being to be created was a man.This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see.The Aengul and the Daemon, the two spirits created\n\nbefore the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.God then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell  and the Man lived. God then took the\n\nman and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman.These simple beings could not talk, nor talk, nor\n\ndid they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis. Malin was the first of\n\ntheir sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh\n\nmeadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nWe do not know how they fathered sons and how their lines continued but perhaps God created a partner for\n\neach Son to continue their lines? Soon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken\n\nwith grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks\n\nand traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis. At this\n\ntime, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for\n\neach other and each others people.Urguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of\n\nAegis, and Horen began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace.Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the void, kin spirits\n\nto the Aengul, defected.Iblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things\n\ndelicate, he was quickly befriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's\n\nplan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\n\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content.\n Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy\n\nthe barren forests.To Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him. Horen, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased\n\nHe needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality. Krug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The\n\nbeast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror. In Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in\n\nflame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time.\n\nHe stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the strength of Krug as they fought\n\nthe beast.Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.For the thirty years the Descendants\n\nfought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw\n\nup their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast.Urguan grew greedy, he fought\n\nvalourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day. One\n\nday where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers. An army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty\n\nand beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\nIblees' soldiers\n\nburned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed\n\napparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark\n\nsoul would be forever trapped in torment. But..Before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time. “You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it\n\nshall forever be part of the souls that inhabit it. Malin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of\n\nyour own. Even you have done my work, if you realize it or not.Urguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in\n\nthe deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied. Horen, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and\n\ndie before you ever taste the fruits of your pointless labors. And you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your\n\nlust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.\"As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\n\nThe Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to\n\ncorrupt their souls, the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason. The robed figure stood before the four brothers. \"There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to\n\nbless you. Malin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived. Urguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind. Krug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist. And Horen, may your people\n\none day explore the Seven Skies. I can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.\" And with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into\n\nthin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations I", "§bLorar Minskin", "Observations and Their Benefits\n-------------------Written by Lorar Min.\n-------------------  As you look around do you notice the fate of the people around you? The tick tock of the clockwork and the innerworkings of the life they live is set in stone.\n\nIt is to the point of which it seems that even the biggest actions seem to have no effect in pulling people out of this loop. Now, It'd be safe for me to say that you are probably one of those people who dilly-dally around and are stuck in one preset path\n\nin which you feel that you have no control over. Infact It'd also be safe for me to say that you, yourself, the person that is reading this is so clueless that they don't even realize that they're stuck in this loop. You need help, fast.\n Unlike others\n\nbefore you, these events don't need to happen. They don't need to be one event piling on another and another to the point of no return. You, yes you have a chance to stop this. At this point I'd say you're quite confused on what I'm talking about. I'm\n\n talking about your old friend who is predetermined every single, every single day I tell you to do the same exact thing in which he does the same exact tasks until the point of no return. That no returning point being death. I'm talking about changing\n\nwhat you're doing. For better or worse, for the danger, for the fun, for the neverending amazement of not knowing what is going to happen next. Unlike your ancestors you can change what your future may hold. Perhaps your grandfather was a carpenter and\n\nyour father was also a carpenter and by golly-gee you better be a carpenter. That, that itself is what I'm talking about. Do not follow what is preset for you, stand out.\n You've got one life and you better make it worth living because who knows what\n\ntommorrow may hold. Take that last step, eat that extra roll, ask to court that special lady, do whatever you feel like you may never have another chance to do. Because who knows, you might not be there the next day to do it.\n\n-My First Book, Lorar", ""),
        StaticBook("Report on Kha", "§bViaiel", "Report on Kha kitten\n------------------\n24th of The Deep Cold 1521\n------------------\nBy Viaiel Elsinael - Evarir\n-------------------Kha was found wandering elcihi. Apprehended by Evarir Viaiel. Cause: Suspicious activity.\n\nKha was to be let out by Evarir Viaiel. Kha stole everythingit could before making a run for it. Kha's life was ended by Evarir Viaiel, using a bow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Common Knowledge", "§bRinaline Sirius", "Preface:\nIf you're new to this world or just completely oblivious to everything, this book is for you.\n\nChapter 1: Conversation\n\nConversation must always be prim and proper. Cussing is an absolute no-no.\n\nPersonally, I have accidently done this and I still feel impure to this day because of it.\n\nRemember, arguing and violence solve nothing. So don't get into a fight with another 'aheral.\n\nYou are no more superior than the common mali'aheral, unless you are of higher status or speaking to a mali'ata.\n\nMali'ata are not posionous but it certainly is plausible to stay away from them. If they try to seduce you, don't fall for it.\n\nChapter 2: Love\n\nAs tempting as love sounds, it is forbidden until you come of age. It is fairly disgusting to see two people showing affection in public is degrading and immoral. You will get judged and perhaps even put on trial.\n\nIf you really wish to pursue someone you MUST be more than 50 years of age.\n\nIf a mali'thill is seen trying to court another mali'thill and this mali'thill is younger than 50. This mali'thill is too child-ish to understand what \"love\" is.\n\nSo if the other mali'thill agrees. . . this mali'thill is revolting.\nIt is NOT okay to pursue sexual relations with mali'thill of under 50 years of age.\n\nSexual relations with a race that is not mali'aheral is considered impure. You will be labeled as a\n\nmali'ata and your 'lover' will be dunked in acid. It is disgraceful to have a child with another race. Even another race of Mali. (eg:Mali'ker, Mali'ame.)\n\nHowever, if you do not get caught, have fun living a wretched life of impurity.\n\nChapter 3: Knowledge\n\nKnowledge is power, and only the mali'aheral can achieve this state of being pure.\n\nOther races make too many mistakes, lack the common sense that is necessary to survive, or are just incompetent.\n\nThis is not 'racist' , it is a known fact by all except those who truly want to be ignorant.\n\n\n------------------\nThat was the end of this book, if you have any corrections or need any tips, be sure to talk to me.\n\nThis was written by Rinaline Sirius, on the 16th of First Seed, 1589.\n\n\nThank you for reading.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Reason", "§bGrigor Grandaxe", "A Guide to Reason. A Philisophical Bestseller by Grigor Grandaxe.\n\nHey you.\nYeah You.\nWhat do you know about Philsophy? Here in this book I will give you statements to help you to reson with yourself, to think and\n\nto reflect on actions based on the Philosophical premises that I will give to you.\n\nInstustions for use of this book:\n1. Open this book\n2. Follow the guidelines of each statement\n3. Keep it to one statement a day\n\nso that you may have the designed, 10 day reading period here, weather you read this at church, at work, in bed or at home.\n\nOn the next page your journey through Philoposphy will begin.\n---->\n\nDay One, Statement One.\n\"Progress just means bad things happen faster.\" - Grigor Grandax.\n\nConsider the connotations of this statement and its effect on you and your life, are bad things happening to you?\n\nDay Two, Statement Two.\n\"I think therefore I am.\"\n\nWHat do you want to be? HAve you tried to be this? Mabye you are all you want to be, and if so have you considered how you got there?\n\nDay Three, Statement Three.\n\"I can't go back to yesterday, because I was a different person then.\"\n\nHow much have you changed since yesterday? since last week? last year?\n\nDay 4, Statement 4.\n\"Don't bitw off more than you can chew because nobody looks attractive spitting it out\"\n\nWho has strived for something so far out of their reach they injure themselves whilst striving for it?\n\nDay 5, Statement 5.\n\"All is fair in love and war.\"\n\nThink on this statement for yourself and apply its Philosophy to your life. It has important conotations.\n\nDay 6-10\nPlease purchase Part Two of the Grigor Grandaxe Philosophy\nReading Plan for the added statements, remeber you will become a better persons if you apply the Philosophies of this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("~~Haelun'or~~", "§bThallan Tal'iheiuh", "~~Haelun'or: The Motherland~~\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Thallan Tal'iheiuh\n\n~~Introduction~~\nSince early Asulon, the Mali'aheral, sometimes simply referred to as `High Elves` (although their name literally means `Blessed Elf` in the language of common), have lived in seclusion, away from the other children of Malin: the\n\nMali'ame (Wood Elves) and the Mali'ker (Dark Elves). This isolated land, reserved only for pure Mali'aheral (a Mali with a completely High Elven background, meaning marriages to only other\n\nAheral and certainly no offspring with an Elf of a different sub-race), was known as Haelun'or, translated from Ancient Elven as, like in the title of this work, `motherland`. Haelun'or has, since its founding in Asulon, existed in all of the realms,\n\nwhere the Mali'aheral lived in cities of different titles. As strict the High Elves are with who they let into elcihi (the city), on several occasions their nation has been a home of refuge for the other sub-races, and also the Kharajyr (often called the\n\nKha), a feline race, found already living on Asulon upon the descendants' arrival there, have stayed there on several occasions.\nIn this book, all of the cities which the Mali'aheral have resided in shall be listed, and a few words will be written about\n\neach, starting from Aegis and finishing in the land of Thales.\n\n~~Aegis~~\nIn the first realm that Malin, his brothers, and their descendants explored, the Mali'aheral lived at peace (mostly) in the nation of Malinor, dwelling within its leafy cities, such as its capital, Laurelin. Under the rule of High Prince Native,\n\n the first of the High Princes of Malinor, a group known as the High Council was formed, so as to aid Native in governing and protecting Malinor. This council was predominantly made up of Wood Elves, yet one High Elf, Prince Toren, was a part of it.\n\nPrince Toren is well known for his idea for the creation of a large and fruitful farm which was built within Laurelin, keeping the Princedom of Malinor fed and happy. This happiness was, of course, before the arrival of Iblees, a powerful Daemon.\n\n~~Asulon~~\nAfter leaving the Verge, an island used to recuperate on following the destruction of Aegis to the bane of Iblees, and sailing to Asulon, the Mali'aheral, led by Dio Astoré and Ellir'siol, felt it time to detatch from the other Mali, setting\n\noff to build a city of their own. Said city was built upon one of the many ruins found across the land; the ruins used as the foundations for the city were that of an Ancient Elven civilisation. It took several years to construct the grand city (the\n\nlayout and design of which was just how the old cihi, now just rubble and stone, would have looked) and, upon its finishing, it flourished as the new home of the Mali'aheral. It was named Haelun'or, the same title as the nation known today - it was\n\nelcihi'thilln: the Silver City.\nJust after its building, Haelun'or was a part of the Princedom, under the rule of High Prince Kolyat Alfakyn. However, this, to the Mali'aheral, was not seen as a chance for open borders between elcihi and the rest of\n\nMalinor: large iron gates (more often than not seen closed and locked) at the end of a large bridge, branching out over a ravine, a natural split between the High Elves and their fellow Mali. No Mali'ame/ker/fenn were allowed through the gates; it was\n\nproperty reserved for the Aheral.\nAs the city grew in both size and population, the Silver Council, Haelun'or's equivalent of a government, led by elsohaer, the leader and ruler of the nation, negeotiated with the Princedom and, as a result, Haelun'or\n\ngained autonomy. From this point on, the Silver City ceased to be a part of Malinor, and instead the Mali'aheral began ruling themselves as an independant people.\n\n~~Anthos~~\nFollowing the great surge of natural disasters that rendered Asulon uninhabitable, the races travelled, stopping at two islands known as Elysium and Kalos, to Anthos, a new and unexplored land. For a short while, the Mali'aheral lived within\n\nMalinor once again, but this was short lived, as feuds and arguments between the Aheral and other sub-races caused the Blessed ones to leave, building their own city, called Lin'evaral. It was the most western city in the mainland and could be accessed in\n\n two ways. They remained happy in their home for many long and prosperous years before the Black Scourge (led by Setherien, last of the Drakaar, part Daemon, part dragon beings) and many large earthquakes forced them to flee the ruined cihi.\nWhile the\n\n destruction of the city was ongoing, a camp, known as New Malinor, was set up outside the capital of Luminaire. It acted as a kind of refugee camp, giving Elves shelter as the war between the Elves and the Scourge drew on. The High Elves, distraught by\n\nthe loss of Lin'evaral, came to New Malinor, seeking help. They quickly set up a camp and began to live alongside other Mali once more. There was, for a short time, peace in New Malinor. However, some non-Aheral Mali were displeased with the treatment\n\nthat the High Council were providing and began to revolt. This revolt was successful without any bloodshed. The Conclave of Malin, a city built upon Lake Lake, then took control of ruling the Elves. Unlike the Mali'ame and Mali'ker, the High Elves were\n\ndisgusted by the Conclave, saying that the terms for purity were not popularising equality and that this new rule was promoting what they referred to as Mali'valah, Elves acting like Humans. The Mali'aheral then moved to a secret unerground home, entitled\n\n the Tomb. Nearly 30,000 High Elves stayed there, a similar size population to the Conclave.\nThe Tomb contained several gates and gardens with four main sections, known as branches: a multi-floored library, with vast amounts of books. Another branch was a\n\n scientific area, used for research and experimentation. A housing branch, many levels deep,\nhoused all of the Tomb's residents and a final branch was for Elsillumiran, Haelun'or's guard force (the nation has never\nhad a recognised army). This area was\n\nused for training and was, by many, considered insiginificant to the rest of their home.\nOutside of the Tomb, the people who knew about its whereabouts were scarce, and it was never discovered, by another race (or sub-race, for that matter).\n\n~~The Fringe~~\nAfter Setherien was defeated, his icy realm in the North began to melt, flooding all of Anthos, causing its\nabandonment, as the races went through the portal into The Fringe. Here, the Mali'aheral built a city, Tahn'siol, meaning `lonely\n\npeak`hich was constructed on a large hill, with a great source of water that could supply the whole land.\nDuring the time spent on The Fringe, which was constructed on a large hill, with a great source of water that could supply the whole land. During the\n\n time spent on The Fringe, concordats between the High Elves and the other sub-races were created so as to\nprotect the surrounding districts of Ker'lomi and Lin'ame (this should be simple to distinguish the homes of the different sub-races).\n\n under the laws of Haelun'or. The Kharajyr also had a district within the walls of Tahn'siol.\n\n~~Thales~~\nUpon arriving in Thales, the High Elves built the city of Celi'ante. The concordats between the sub-races were destroyed, as\nthe Wood Elves and Dark Elves did not agree with the treatment they recieved in Tahn'siol, and they decided to build\n\nsettlements of their own. For a short while, Haelun'or went through a period of bitterness toward the newly created Council of Splinters. However, these arguments did not last long and againg the other Mali came under the protection of Haelun'or.\n\n~~Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya~~", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunai: Rangers", "§bArnorian", "Origins\n\nDuring the Reign of Braen Elendil, the Adunian Lord came to see that with the ever rising population of their race, he would soon need a military to keep order instead of just relying in the good will of his citizens. And so, he asked his\n\nbrother Cirimas to gather the most Elite and loyal soldiers he could find and bring them before him. The names of these four men were never recorded, but it is known that one was of house 'Lorsmor' and another of house Loyola. The four men stood before\n\nBraen, all were well trained in the arts of stealth, the longsword, the shortsword, dagger and longbow, learning from their fathers, and father's fathers, who had to outrun and hide from the Rhodir and other men of Owyn Godwinson during their Exodus.\n\nBraen decided that based on their traits, these four men would be known as the Adunian Rangers, and that they would serve as their race's first personal military force. Over time, Cirimas and the four rangers slowly built traditions, and organization\n\nthroughout the order, and gained more men along the way.\n\nUniform\n\nTraditionally the rangers had no official uniform, but they were told to stick to a certain code to do with what items they wore; the rangers would wear\n\nleather boots, fingerless leather gloves, a leather belt, a large coat and a cloak over the top. The Coat of Cirimas was passed from captain to Captain, as was occasionally his clock. All of this would be over any other clothes they wished to wear.\n\nFort Arendil.\n\nThe rangers lived in a large cave system under the hill which Al'Ildic stood upon, though the caves had been renovated to be more like an underground fortress. Said fortress was named after Arendil, the last\n\nKing of Idunia, and was meant to be used as a fallback point if Ildon ever came under a siege it was unable to hold off. Sadly, in the final battle of Ildon in which it fell to the undead, few managed to get to the fortress before its gates had to be shut\n\nto save those inside.\n\nWatchtowers.\n\nAs the Adunian Kingdom spread over the land, the rangers decided that they could only keep order in Ildon itself from fort Arendil, and would have to find a way to do so in the towns, farms and\n\nestates that surrounded it. And so the watchtowers were built all over the kingdom. In each watchtower, a single ranger would live along with up to 15 initiates whom he would use to keep order in the surrounding area. The garrison of each watchtower was\n\nrotated every fortnight.\n\nTraditions.\n\nThe final initiation for a ranger was for him to be taken out into the woods where he would swear an oath of service to the Adunian race.\n\nNo men of non-Adunian blood were permitted to join the rangers.\nAn heir to the Adunian throne would have to spend five years in the service of the rangers before he could become the lord.\n\nIt is often thought that it was tradition that all young men\n\njoined the rangers for several years after they turned seventeen, though in reality seventeen was simply the age where one was permitted entrance into the order, and over time, it became a popular trend to join the rangers as soon as one was allowed.\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 4 : Adunai", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Religion ~*~\n\nWhen Fai O'Thuaid was founded, Orthodox Creationism was the official faith enforced by Harren and his descendants. Though they were isolated from the church and took no efforts to maintain contact, they were still devout Creationists who\n\nkept true to their beliefs and traditions. After landing in Al'Ildic however, many Adunians lost their faith in the Creator, pondering why he allowed the brutal Ulgaard Rebellion to occur, and the Adunians to be cast out of Aegis. In the early 400's,\n\nBraen Elin'sehn, son of Elendil began preaching a new belief; that the Creator had abandonded them, leaving the spirits of their ancestors behind to take on the role as their guide. The belief was quick to catch on in Al'Ildic society, giving rise to\n\nAdunian Creationism.\n\nAdunian Creationism centers around the belief that a single Creator build the world, but then abandoned his people after they disapointed him. This called for the spirits of the dead to step in and take up the Creator's role as\n\nthe guiding hand for the living. A Century later, the religion had evolved and built itself upon three main figures - Elendi the father, Maria the mother, and Braen, the son and chosen prophet of\n\nCreator. Followrs of the religion would pray to these three figures, as well as their own personal ancestors.\n\nAs the centuries went on, more patrons were added to the original three. Cirimas Elendil became the patron of protection and justice, Garth\n\nHaryn the patron of war and triumph, Falcryn Delmar, patron of politics and negotiation, Reman Elendil patron for vengance and loyalty, Rymeul Elendil, patron of exploration, and so on and so on. Other lesser patrons also existed, though they were not as\n\nwidely worshipped and were generally confined to provinces in Al'Ildic.\n\nVarious shrines were erected across Al'Ildic, most notably a shrine to both Elendil and Maria in Ildon, a shrine to Cirimas in the north of Ar'Norian, a shrine to Braen high in\n\nMaria's peaks, and a shrine to Garth Haryn in Del Kaev. The shrines took the form of large stone statues representing their chosen figure, and a stone altar at the feet where offerings of gold, food and other valubles would be left. Pilgrims would often\n\nleave relevant offerings to their patricular patron at each shrine. Another important part of Adunian Creationism is the connection between the people and the Sea. This importance was derived from the sea having been where the Mali'Dun disappeared, where\n\nHarren's remains were cast by Owyn Ulgaard's rebels, and the place where Elendil had chosen to take his last voyage.\n\nThis method of worship went undisturbed for around six hundred years before the Canonist faith was brought to Al'Ildic.\n\nWhen Lord Rymeul Elendil reopened trade with mainland Aegis in 1001, the faith of Oren was soon to follow and began spreading it's influence on the smaller continent. This was not very effective, as for three centuries the Canonist church struggled to\n\ngain a foothold, only having only converted around five percent of the population by the Realm's fall in 1309.\n\nWhen the Adunians eventually resettled in new Ildon under Lord Artorus Elendil the future of the Adunian religion was reshaped again.\n\nArtorus had been raised for the most part in Renatus, and had been brought up with the Canonist faith from a young age. When his time to lead came, he made sure to spread his beliefs amoung his followers as to assure they were fully accepted as members of\n\nGodfrey's Holy Oren Empire. Artorus's son and heir, Harrion was himself extremely devout, to the point of founding a holy organization known as the 'Monastic Order', making him another driving force behind the Canonization of the Adunians.\n\nDuring Artorus's reign there was a massive shift away from Adunian Creationism, almost wiping out it's existence. The majourity of Adunians converted to Canonism, while the vast remainder merged Adunian Creationism and Canonism together, forming what is\n\nknown as New Adunian Creationism.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 5 : Adunai", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Customs ~*~\n\nThere are an array of traditions and customs that have shaped Adunian society over the ages and many continue to practice to this day. Many clans have their down traditions specific to themselves, some provinces have a similiar system\n\nsuch as the Nivinese connection to bowie culture, while the most important customs are those that apply to the realm and race as a whole.\n\nSuccession laws in Adunian society differ from those of most other races. While a man in Oren will leave his lands\n\nand titles to his eldest son, an Adunian would leave his simply to the youngest. This system was put into place to assure a landowner could spend the longest time possible in his position, and quell the threat of political instability from provinces\n\nchanging hands. It also took away the issue of sons killing their fathers to take their positions ahead of time, as most heirs were to young to even consider such a cource of action. In spite of this, the law did cause unnecessary hostility within\n\nfamilies as a young boy could grow up thinking he was his father's her, only for said father to bear another child and force the first to relinquish their claim. It was a testing dilemma for many young Adunians, but also a fitting method for them to prove\n\ntheir honour and dedication to their family above all else. The Adunian succession laws have been in place since Braen Elin'sehn, who left his position to his youngest son Farwil rather then his eldest Cirimas, who had been absent for many years living as\n\na ranger.\n\nAdulthood in Adunian culture begins for a man when he has lived through seventeen winters. At this point, a large celebration of drinking, dancing and music will be held in honour of the man, the extent of the festivities varying\n\ndepending on his clan's wealth. The celebration can last from one day, to an entire month. When the festivities and hangovers have cleared, the now adult man sets out on a trek. A man from a common clan may only explore his native province, when a member\n\nof a greater clan might also visit his neighboring regions and important sites around the realm. An Elendil however, is expected to visit each of the realm's provinces, their main towns and cities, along with the major shrines to the patron saints.\n\nWhen the man returns, he can take on political or military roles in society, or elevate his position in whatever sect of the workforce he was being trained in beforehand. Adunian women have a very different experience in thier transition to adulthood.\n\nThe largest discrepancy, is the age at which they are considered adult, which is twenty winters past. Festivities are held, although not public; more closer family affairs. When she turns twenty, she gains the ability to marry.\n\nWomen have a strange place in Adunian culture. They don't face the same extreme control they are subjected to in societies like Oren, but it is frowned upon if they seek certain careers. When they reach adulthood, they gain the same freedoms as men; they\n\ncan enter the workforce, choose their own husband without the interference of other family members (though they were often threatened or pressured into heeding the judgement of their father or clan Elder), travel, or in rare cases, enter the Military.\n\nWhile the 'ARC' (Adunian Ranger Company) and Ildician order were male dominated, occasionally a woman could rise to command a squad or company. For the most part, women were known to stay home, tend to the household, raise children and contribute to the\n\nwellbeing of their town or city. Like men, they were expected to uphold dress standards, covering themselves from the head down, only exposing their hands and head.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 4 'Adunai'", "§bArnorian", "Artorus eventually left the care of the monks and slowly made his way in the world as a military man. By the time Aegis was destroyed and it's citizens had voyaged to Asulon, Artorus was an esteemed military captain of the Phoenix Guard, which was the\n\nprimary military force of the Kingdom of Renatus. By chance, Halboron saw a notice in the cloud temple that had been placed by Artorus, claiming he was looking for his long lost uncle. Halboron traveled as fast as he could to Renatus where he was reunited\n\nwith his nephew. Together, they planned to reunite their race and rebuild what they once had.\n\nAfter many years of tireless work, Artorus and Halboron completed building a new Ildon in Western Renatus, by which time their family had grown\n\nimmensely. (Authors note: I was born at this time.) Many years after the time when it was acknowledged officially complete, Halboron met the end of his days due to an infected wound he had sustained serving Westfall as Lord Commander of the Westwatch.\n\nThe years pressed on, and Ildon continued to grow, eventually becoming one of the largest cities in Oren. As with all good things, they must come to an end - The Order of the Mongoose came to three figures - Artorus Elendil, Jon Norsem and Eze'kiel Tarus.\n\nThere, they convinced the three of a plot that in the House of Horen, lay the blood of Demons and the next undead uprising. Sold by the stout and trustworthy wizarding order, the three immidiatly rose in revolt in what they believed was for the greater\n\ngood, and were swiftly put down in a three day siege and battle in Ildon. Artorus and Eze'kiel were executed by Lancel Hightower (Who then forced marriage upon Eze'kiels Widow), and Norsem fell in combat. \nIn pity of Artorus's son Torrhen (My brother) the\n\nEmperor gifted him with the dukedom of Westfall in a successful attempt to sway Torrhen from wanting to rebel agaisnt Oren Himself. The Elendil family and the Adunian race continued to live in Ildon under Torrhen's rule, until the final days of Asulon.\n\nFrom there, the Adunians moved to the Isle of Elysium, where complex politics and a severe lack of land led to a terribly ugly bout of infighting amoungst the three young Elendils (I was a child at the time, too young to be concerned with said politics.)\n\nIsabella Elendil (My sister, age 17), Torrhen Elendil, aged 25, and Harrion Elendil, aged 35. It was during this time a near civil conflict broke out, and the two sides remained seperate well into the time of Anthos.\n\nWritten and Annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 3 : Adunai", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Appearance ~*~\n\nAdunians take traits from both their Harrenite and Mali'Dun ancestors. Brown or black hair are the only two colours found, though like other races it goes grey with age. It is not uncommon for an Adunian's hair to go grey at ages as\n\nyoung as fifteen, a trait inherited from the Mali'Dun. Their skin is pale, but generally no paler than the average Heartlander. An Adunian's eyes are either grey from the Mali'Dun, brown from the Harrenites (A rare trait), or green, which appears to have\n\ncome from a mix of both, the most common eye colour. Adunians generally grow to heights of about 5\"11', and have a lean build. Tradition has the Adunians keep their hair shoulder length, and grow beards that keep close to the face.\n\n~*~ Clothing ~*~\n\nThe general climate of Al'Ildic was quite cold. Though it's landscape was only coated in snow during the winter months, the chill of the northern wind was present year round. As a result of this climate, Adunians came to dress in a\n\nparticular way. Men would wear heavy coats and cloaks, lined with furs and warm skins, thick leather boots and warm wool breeches. Women wore long-sleeved dresses, often accompanied with furs draped over their shoulders, light cloaks and some form of\n\ntrousers to keep their legs warm. Over time it became considered 'rude' or 'Socially unacceptable' for more than the hands or head to be unclothed. This way of thinking has stuck over the ages, and Adunians true to tradition always cover themselves from\n\nthe neck down before presenting themselves publically.\n\n~*~ Weaponry ~*~\n\nDue to factors such as their slender build, Al'Ildic's snowy climate and the influence of their Mali'Dun ancestors, Adunians tend to avoid heavier or blunt weapons.\n\nArming swords, Bastard swords, Long swords, dirks and a variety of other smaller bladed weapons make up the majority of an Adunian army's weaponry. Unique to the Adunians however is the Bowie knife. Named after the Bowie nomads (named for their lifestyle\n\nreliance on the bow) who created it, the bowie knife was meant to bridge the gap between a tool and a weapon. A large blade with a clip point and sweeping belly, generally around nine inches in length. The wielders hand would be protected by a wide metal\n\ncrossguard that could be used to parry an incomming blow. Despite this connection to smaller arms like the bowie knives, an Adunian's favourite weapon is always his bow. The legacy of the Mali'Dun stayed strong with their descendants and bow making became\n\none of the most respectable trades of Al'Ildic. All sorts of bows were utilized by the ARC (Adunian Ranger Corp), the bowies, the Ildician order and the general common folk of Al'Ildic, from longbows to composite bows. The bow that left the greatest\n\nlegacy of all was the double recurve warbow.\n\nOnly the greatest Adunian bowyers could craft the weapon, using four prods rather than two for additional power, though not so much that it would break the bow. Generally made\n\nfrom the yew that grew in the forests of Ar'Norian, crafting a double-recurve warbow was more about finding the balance of power than anything else, maximising it's ability to shoot with strength, but not so much as to splinter the wood. An accomplished\n\nbowyer might only ever craft two or three in his lifetime, and it is unknown if any today possess the skill to even make one.\n\nThe last of the three weaponry innovations unique to Al'Ildic is a material known as 'Eldar steel.' Called Eldion steel by some,\n\nthe material was forged in a grand fortified cavern to the south of Ekvol in Al'Ildic's Irthgard mountain range. Smiths from around the small continent would go there to study the art of crafting blades, and over the centuries they were able to create\n\ntheir own unique style of blacksmithing. In a lengthy process the smiths would craft weapons by layering steel for a sharper edge and a more ornate appearance.\n\nAt first, the blades were brittle and could shatter if used extensively, but the Eldar smiths\n\nhoned their ability over many generations, and eventually their weapons were as strong as any other. The time it took to craft such a weapon meant they were rarely made and far more expensive than a regular steel sword which could do the same job just as\n\nwell. As a result of this, only the richest and most influential clans of Al'Ildic ever owned an Eldar steel weapon, and they were usually passed down through the generations as a family heirloom. In modern times, weapons of Eldar steel are in fewer\n\nnumbers than the endangered Adunians whose ancestors made them, and like the double-recurve bow, it is unknown if anyone yet has the skill to recreate it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 2 'Adunai'", "§bArnorian", "This blade became the official blade of house Elendil, and was passed down to the heir of the Adunian crown when he turned seventeen. No one is quite sure which Lord had the blade forged, but it is known that it happened around the reigns of the Lords\n\n'Dranan', 'Rymeul' and 'Anmas.' During Braen's (Dranan's father) reign, he commisioned a group of his finest archers and swordsmen to form an order of Elites, known as the Adunian Rangers - the sole military force of the Kingdom. This order would serve\n\nthe Kingdom for many years to come, under the command of several legendary Ranger Captains.\n\nDranan started another Adunian tradition, of burying each member of the Elendil family with a crown, each made out of a single Material with a gem on the\n\nfront. To have a steel crown meant that you were a brave and courageous warrior, whilst a gold one meant you were more diplomatically minded. A Silver crown would be a balance of both. A Diamond on the front of the crown would mean that you were an\n\nAdunian Lord, an emerald would mean you were a military man (Most commonly an Adunian Ranger), a ruby would mean you were a gifted Artisan, and a sapphire would mean you never found a calling, but were always willing to help others.\n\nWhen Rymeul came to the throne, he led an expedition back to the sea which his ancestor had crossed generations ago. He discovered a land bridge had connected the two realms, of Adunia and Aegis. Rymeul's grandson, Bethrol would then go on an expedition\n\nof his own across the land bridge and back into Aegis, where he discovered Idunia had long since been destroyed, and a new kingdom had arisen - The city, \"Al'Khazzar' and the Kingdom, 'Oren'. Bethrol came to arrange trade agreements with the Orenians\n\nwhilst on the expedition, and trade routes were formed. This was the first contact the Adunians had had with the outside world since the three hundred odd years of exile. \n\nOver the years, the Adunian settlement of Ildon turned from\n\nan Isolated village into a hefty city, then into a small Kingdom. By 'Rydel's' rule, the Adunian rangers were no longer sufficient to keep law and order in the Kingdom. He had his brother 'Thorenir' disband the Rangers, and start a larger force called the\n\nAdunian Legion. This decision, which was seen as foolish by some may have saved the entire Adunian race from destruction, as soon after this choice was made, Rydel's steward 'Icarian Delmar' turned agaisnt him, and attempted to ursurp the throne.\n\nThis marked the beginning of what would be reffered to in history books (such as this one) as the 'Great Adunian War'.\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol 2 : Adunai", "§bArnorian", "In the year 333 a massive populist rebellion led by Owyn Ulgaard, a common Highlander and the son of a miner succeeded in removing the Adunians from power. Starting in 332, one by one the Kingdom's settlements fell to the Rebels, their Adunian Earls\n\neither being put to the sword, or forced to flee to the Capital. By the following year only Idunia remained under King Arendil's control. Though Idunia did not stand for much longer, as it was the ancestors of the Highlanders who had built the cities\n\nwalls, and so it's secrets had been passed down to them. Rebels were able to penetrate the fortifications and open the gates for the Highlander hordes to rush in and sack the city. Owyn confronted Arendil, and cut him down in single combat ending the\n\nthree century long rule of Adunians over Fai O'Thuaid. \n\nDuring the sack of Idunia, rebels pulled Harren's remains from his mausoleum and cast them off the cliffs into the sea, never to be recovered. With Highlander victory\n\nsecured, Owyn Ulgaard had the remaining Adunians rounded up, and placed on ships at a small unnamed fishing town two days south walk of Idunia. Here, the newly crowned King proclaimed Adunians banished from Aegis as retribution for their unjust\n\nenslavement of the Highlander people, vowing to annihilate them completely should they ever return. Elendil, Son of Arendil and last of Harren's line took command of the Adunian fleet and lead them northeast across the sea, following in the wake of their\n\nMali'Dun ancestors in the hope of finding them. \n\nInstead, the Adunians found Al'Ildic, a large isle almost four months voyage across the ocean. Landing on cape Gelbor, the Adunian people settled the Island starting with the Western coast. Elendil\n\nproclaimed the settled lands 'The Adunian Realm of Al'Ildic' and himself as the 'Lord of the Adunian Realm and People., establishing a new capital at the foot of Maria's seven white marble peaks, a set of towering mountains named after his wife that stood\n\nat the centre of the Great Forest of Ar'Norian. The town was called Ildon, and grew to become an impressive city in the time that followed.\n\nOver the centuries, the Adunians began to spread east across the island, establishing new independant\n\nprovinces and realms. In the year 626, the Second Unification War drew to a close with Al'Ildic triumphing over the independant Realm of Eldion. From 334 to 1309, Adunian culture grew and developed on their isolated contintent, traditions evolving, clan's\n\nrising and falling, wars being lost and won. In the end, the Realm's end came and went in a day, taken by the undead scourge like the rest of Aegis.\n\nSince then, the Adunian people have failed to recover to a position anywhere near as grand, their\n\nhighest points being in the Duchy of Westfall under Godfrey Horen's H.O.E, and again as the Kingdom of Adunia in Kaedrin. In Modern times, Adunians are spread few and far between, wandering the world as Rangers, or integrating with various other societies\n\nand organizations. Through it all, most Adunians remain true to their ancestry and traditions, it's importance having been drilled into them over the generations since Al'Ildic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Volume 1: Adunai", "§bArnorian", "In the years of ancient Aegis, there were no Kingdoms or cities, there were tribes and clans of Men, Elves, Dwarves, and Orcs. One of mankind's greatest tribes were the Harenites, a group of strong hearted warriors led by Harren, the First born of Horen,\n\nand one of his favourites. Soon the Harenites clashed with a tribe of Elves led by Princess Sarai of Malinor. The Two people fought for fifty years, until one day they finally made peace with one another. Weapons were thrown down, and soon the peoples of\n\neach tribe began to marry each other. The Blood from the Elves and the Human's mixed, and soon the first of a new race were born. \nThe descendants of the two tribes called themselves 'Adunian' and as one, they created the kingdom of 'Idunia' - one of\n\nthe first civilized settlements in Aegis, where they would rule over normal men for many years. During the rule of an Adunian called 'Arendil', the grandson of Haren, one of the pure-blooded humans living in Idunia called 'Owyn Godwinson' began a\n\nrebellion agaisnt the Adunians, sick of them ruling over his race. Sparing the gritty and long details, he succeeded and took Idunia for himself. Arendil was killed, and all Adunians were henceforth banished.\n\nArendil's son, 'Elendil' (Later to be\n\nknown as 'Elendil the Exiled') led the remaining Adunians to the far north of Aegis to get away from Godwinson and his forces, whom he feared would decide to chase after them and exterminate the scattered Adunians. The Adunians went as far north as\n\npossible, until they came to a large sea, (creatively named the Adunian Sea, by Lord 'Rymuel Elendil'.) Stretched out far before them. Elendil has his people build two boats, Salvation and Haren's Voyager. After months of labour, the Adunians completed\n\nthe boats and set sail across the sea, hoping to find a Haven for them to settle in peace on the other side.\n\nAfter a two month journey, the Adunians anchored their ships on the coast of a then foriegn land, and set off to find a fine place to settle. For\n\nanother week Elendil led the Adunians across an area of large open plains, and then into a thick forest of pine and spruce. It was within this area Elendil decided to settle, and put his people to work on building the town that would eventually be named\n\n'Ildon', meaning 'Haven.' The castle that sat on the hill nearby would be called 'Al'Ildic', meaning 'The Invincible.'\n\nThe Adunian race flourished in it's new Home, and under the rule of Elendil's descendants who\n\nbecame known as the House of Elendil. Elendil's only son, Braen Elendil became leader of the Adunian race, taking the title of 'Adunian Lord', and started the tradition of passing his title down to the youngest son, to give himself the longest reign\n\npossible. The Adunian Lord also wore a circlet called 'The circlet of Horen' which the Adunians believed to have belonged to Horen himself, before it was given to his son Haren, and passed down the line. Somewhere in the comming years, one of the Adunian\n\nLords had a blade forged, and specially enchanted, dubbing it 'Durendal.'\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 1 : Adunai", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Introduction ~*~\n\nFive years after the world was supposedly built by an almighty 'Creator', Horen, the first King of men was given a son by his wife Julia, whom they named Harren. The child grew up in a time of conflict, and before long was commanding\n\nsoldiers in his father's army. Through all this time however, Harren never felt entitled to his father's holdings and believed that he should instead forge his own kingdom to leave a legacy worthy of his Father. At thirty years of age, Harren was granted\n\nhis Father's permission to take his men and go north beyond the borders of his lands. The men trekked into the vast unknown wilderness for many weeks, eventually comming across a towering mountain range on the northeast coast of the Aegisean continent,\n\nthe Thuaid mountains. Here Harren decided he would build his kingdom, and set about conqeuring the Highland tribes that dwelled there. Little did he know that another tribe was already at work attempting to dominate the region; a tribe of elves who called\n\nthemselves the Mali'Dun, lead by a woman named Sarai. They were tall and elegant, had pale skin like snow, hair black as night, and hollow grey eyes, arming themselves with mainly bows and spears.\n\nAs they moved through the mountains from the North, the\n\nMali'Dun conquered the Highland tribes that lived there, enslaving them and forcing them to fight in their army. Eventually the Harrenites and the Mali'Dun clashed in the battle of Grumder Hill, with the frormer being vastly outnumbered. Harren was forced\n\nto retreat and avoid further confrontation with the elves for a time, focusing his efforts on the Highlander tribes once again. The Harrenites changed their tactics after the battle to mimic those of their enemy, forcing the survivors from each conqoured\n\ntribe to join their force, practically enslaving them as a lower class of soldier. The playing field was leveled, and the two armies clashed a numer of times in the following seven years during their individual conquest of the mountains. Sarai comming\n\nfrom the North, and Harren from the South. In the year 42 (Adunian Calendar) each side took heavy casualties in the second battle of Hrak's field, prompting the leaders of each army to meet and negotiate a conclusion to the war for the Thuaid Mountains.\n\nThe result of the meeting was a political marriage between Harren and Sarai, and the unification of their armies. Before long, Sarai was pregnant with Harren's child, and the son of Horen issued a command to his people; each Harrenite must marry a\n\nMali'dun, and that their children would be the first of a new, superior race. The Highlanders remained a lower class throughout this and were forbidden to lie with either of their overlord races. With the end of the 42nd year, Harren proclaimed the\n\nKingdom of Fai O'Thuaid, encompassing the entire mountain range with himself as King and his wife as Queen. What was formerly two armies became a single society and settled on the cliffs above the northeastern coast, naming their township 'Idunia'.\n\nIn the year 43 Harren's son 'Baren' was born, the first 'Adunian' with many more like him following. Gradually more settlements spring up throughout the kingdom, and in the year 104 Baren succeeded his father. Six years later, the remaining Mali'Dun\n\ndeparted for Mainland Aegis, the last of their human partners having died from one cause or another, leaving the Kingdom in the hands of their descendants, the new Half-breed race, Adunians. For three centuries the kingdom of Fai O'Thuaid\n\nflourished in the northern isolation, the Adunians living as an upper clase of noble Earls among the vast amount of Highlanders beneath them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Progenitor Is: 1", "§bTaenost Ihnsil'dionn", "\\The Progenitor/\n\nThe Progenitor is a publication that stands to represent an unbiased report accompanied by historical accounts recorded by Taenost Ihnsil'dionn. These historical accounts are classified as primary, through the eyes,\n\nhands, and participation of the recorder hisself. What you will read within is as accurate of accounts as an 'aheral may achieve, no spin - no adjective to spice nor distract from the history wrought between peoples of the Fringe.\n\nThe Voice of the Alrasians\n\nThe High King Syrio has attested that the start of his expeditionary camp's involvement in the Zionist War came when Valesmark merchants were attacked by human bandits. Dwarven details protected the merchants and\n\nrebuked the attempted highwaymen attempts, allowing the Valesmark to deliver their goods to the Cloud Temple of Anthos. Thereafter, High King Syrio explained that he felt drawn towards the Zionist treaty to deter further highwaymen attempts on his own.\n\nHigh King Syrio remained unfidgeting with concerns of the proposed treaty from High Chancellor Wilfriche Buron of the Orenites, not revealing what he nor his council members felt or decided. \n\nThe Alrasians bound themselves to secrecy in that they did not\n\ndetail or reveal any of their future hopes as to their participation in the theatre of war. All that could be ascertained was that the Alrasians insist that their perch atop the karst of Kal'Arkon was temporary and that they have land speculations\n\nunderway. \n\nHigh King Syrio attested lastly to an attack that the Orenites committed that led the camp to be slaughtered mostly. His description bore witness that men, women, and children were put to the sword by the Orenites.\n\nInterviewed High King Syrio\n -2nd of Malin's Welcome, 1456\n\nTemple of Vallendar Accosted\n\nThe Temple of Vallendar currently stands along the grounds of an old, yet ruined settlement named Montefleur. A clericess by the name of Lenia Ith'ael\n\nbore witness to an accosting from a supposed Ruskan named Harrison de Silvarois and a polemic from Lucienists which concluded the temple to be of a heretical nature.\n\nThe Clericess has confirmed that besides those two isolated incidents, no other\n\nconfrontations have occurred despite the Temple being in the current theatre of the Zionist War. Lenia Ith'ael confirmed that the temple is monastic in nature, adherents of Tahariae as the Archangel of Purity and patron of the Clerical Order farm produce\n\non Vallendar's grounds.\n\nInterviewed Lenia Ith'ael\n -5th of Malin's Welcome, 1456\n\nThe Dwarven Casus Bellum\n\nBalek Irongut detailed the reason for their involvement in the Zionist War. A summoned emissary dispatch arrived at Vekaro from\n\nKal'Arkon consisting of Lords Dizzy and Zahrer along with dwarfish legionnaires. \n\nThe Orenites examined the relation between the Orkish Warnation and Dwarfish Kingdom by relating that the Warnation attacked Vekaro in the near past, date untold, and asked\n\nthe Dwarves to allow them to return the same treatment without intervention. The Dwarfish emissaries requested evidence of such an event and the Orenites failed to produce. Balek Irongut described the confrontation as ending with Wilfriche cursing the\n\nDwarfish dispatch and besetting his soldiers of Vekaro on them in which all Dwarves successfully escaped except for Lord Dizzy who was injured by a pikeman.\n\nBalek Irongut described this instance as the casus bellum that King Wulfgar acquired which led\n\nDwarfish Kingdom to the current Zionist War.\n\nInterviewed Balek Irongut\n -15th of Malin's Welcome, 1456\n\nAn Attempt on Wilfriche Buron\n\nUpon winning a battle at dusk against the Dwarfish, Alrasian, and Orkish forces, the Orenites sent a\n\ndetail along with their High Chancellor to confront Syrio on what they perceived as a betrayal of expectations as they had given a truce to the Alrasians which Syrio had to confirm with his council. Upon arriving in their expeditionary camp, Wilfriche\n\nbegan his warnings to High King Syrio before having an axe crash down upon hisself. An assassin of Mali'ker ethnicity informed those around of his militant dislike for the Orenites before being slain by Wilfriche's detail.\n\nThe Orenites immediately drew\n\nsuspicions that High King Syrio had organized the plot as they escorted Wilfriche away from Kal'Akron as legionnaires attempted to rally for what gave the Orenites fear as being a further attack on the High Chancellor.\n\nAccosting of the Mali'aheral\n\nThe elcihi of the Mali'aheral, Tahn'siol have been accosted and accused of taking a political stance in the Zionist War. The Mali'aheral have a reverence for neutrality, as insisted by the Sohaer himself. An issue of\n\nanother publication known as The Flagship has been countered by the 'aheral as being libellous and request that the publisher remove any content that attempts to tie a neutral political entity into a war. \n\nBounty on High King Syrio\n\nA bounty\n\nissued by the Orenites, specifically High Chancellor Wilfriche Buron has been announced on High King Syrio Forel. The current paying price for his head stands at 2,000 minas.\n\nPok'Ugluk Alive?\n\nAn infamous and key figure in Uruk culture and history\n\nhas been reported to being found in the Fringe. Whether reports are true could not be confirmed, although the reports reveal that Pok'Ugluk stated a disdain for the ruling Azog clan of the Warnation and a desire to remove them for their seat of power.\n\nScourge at Kal'Akron\n\nThis subject matter remains to being very controversial with differing narratives. The Zionists upon being capitulated and slaughtered as they fled into Kal'Akron brought about an unsubstantiated accusation that the Scourge aided\n\nthe Orenites. The Progenitor\nshares a statement of a witness who corrects this narrative by explaining the following: The Zionists insist that they were struck by frostfire along the fields north of Kal'Akron, but failed to remember that they had\n\nfailed to hold position to be struck - the Orenites had already pushed, killed, and defeated the Zionist army. In fact, it was the Orenites who had been assaulted by Harbingers in which the trajectories of their frost-fire led to some of the Orenites\n\nidentifying the distinct, grim appearances of Harbingers who sat along the karst of Kal'Akron nearest the Alrasian Expeditionary Camp.\n\nAn 'aheral historian recommends the following statement: When you study events in history, your best evidence\n\nare primary sources. Primary sources are accounts from those who lived and witnessed the particular event in person and were typically affected by said event in some way and has emotions, thoughts, and experiences to recount. The Orenites had succeeded\n\nin the battle whilst most, if not all of the Zionist forces had been felled. The best judgement to make in this case would be to take the Orenites' accounts as solid while the Zionist accounts are mythic explanation as to their failure in the battle at\n\nKal'Akron. It is typical for  collective memory to weave up an explanation of either realistic or mythical proportions to define the moments in which those people had gone through a hardship.\n\nThe Progenitor, in the next issue, welcomes editorial and\n\nopinionated content that will be clearly and visually separated from our journalism. The Progenitor in and of itself remains separated from the conflict and those who write for the Progenitor uphold a standard of refusing any attempts to persuasively or\n\nforcibly put forth libellous, flowery, and scandallous content. \n\nThank You for Reading\n\nProgenitor\n Issue I\n  Printed on:\nThe 20th of Malin's Welcome\n                      1456", ""),
        StaticBook("Orlanden's Three", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Orlanden’s Three Visions\n\ndictated by Prince Orlanden\ntranscribed by Elorna Avern\n\nIt all started our first night on Elysium as I was sleeping by a cozy little campfire where the Dwarves had begun mining out their Hold.\n\n I have many theories of what might have triggered these visions; it may have been the burning of the Elder Tree in\n\nAsulon before we left.\n\nFor the first of the three visions thus far, I found myself seemingly flying through a large, very high canopy, high above the thick forest's floor.\n\nThere was a bright light directly over what I would think would be the Mother\n\nTree of the forest.\n\n I was drawn to it, but just before I could reach it, I woke up.\n\nThis dream, along with the other two I've yet to speak of, I see nearly every night. \nIt's as if they're developing into a story.\n\nThe second one, which happened on the second night here in Elysium, began with me standing at the tree line of this tall, tall forest.\n\nThe outline of the forest was made up of very large trees the likes of which I've never seen before.\n\n I know not what they are called, but they towered over everything else. \n\nAs I wandered inward, there was a smaller forest of normal looking oaken trees that greeted me. \n\nThrough their canopy you could see the canopy of the large trees, barely allowing\n\nany light through except for one opening in the center.\n\nAs I walked amongst these giants I saw flora that is completely foreign to Asulon and even Aegis.\n\nThere were streams that ran throughout the forest, crystal clear spring water, perhaps runoff from\n\na nearby mountain. \n\n It was a sight so many will wish to behold, I am sure of that.\n\nThe third dream began, sure enough, on the third night. \n\n In this one I found myself in an enclosed space, but to my rear was a triangular opening with bright,\n\nnatural light shining through. In front of my seemed to be what I can only think of as a pillar or beacon. \n\nIt was removable, so me with my curious nature, removed it from its resting place.\n\nIt felt so... wrong.\n\nSo wrong that I had removed it, the feelings it gave me were dark and grim.\n\n Immediately I replaced it, and just as quickly the feelings of warmth and love rushed back to me.\n\nAs I let go of the pillar and stepped back, I awoke, concluding the third\n\nvision. \n\nIt must mean something.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Crown-Prince", "§bJacob Chapel", "\"The Basis of the Perfect State\" was written by Edward Winter II as gift to Ostromir Sarkozic Carrion upon the conquest of Renatus.\n\nThis book has been transcribed and copied by and under guidance of Jacob Chapel.\n\n((Original by AiiM))\n\nThe Basis of the Perfect State\nTo the Crown-Prince,\n\nThe governance of a state must be just. To be a just state, the governing body must execute their duties and powers efficiently with the will of the people and the good of the state held\n\nas supreme.\n\nThe judicious and firm-handed monarch can in his own right control the state. A monarchy is far more efficient, effective, and has a lesser potential for corruption than the republican system of councils, voting, and election. The downfall\n\nof the just monarch is his heir. The spoiled child corrupts the state, the weak-willed monarch relinquishes the power of the royal family. The royal heir must be established as the supremely noble and knowledgeable steward of the state, whose governance\n\nis just and his decisions well-made.\n\nThe ill-fit heir has, in the past, been rectified by extensive counsel, where the royal extends to his advisors the powers of the state. The function of the government in this state does deteriorate, as the\n\nabsolutism of the monarch is sullied by the extended powers and corruptions of the monarch's counselors, whose motives and intellects are unknown and unverified.\n\nSo one must establish the basis by which a just monarch can be ensured by the generations.\n\nElection of the most just by the common people is a flawed system, as the uneducated and ignoble masses know not of justice nor righteousness. The thieves and beggars in the charity of the state should not be tasked with the selection of a\n\nrepublican heir. The whims of the people to favour a man do not establish him as the most effective steward and leader to his people.\n\nElection by the masses of nobility is too a flawed system, as the nobles delight in their pleasures without properly\n\nknowing of management or governance. Their corruptions of sin diminish their efficacy as a just constituency.\n\nThe solution then, is to look for the most just of a collective of just monarchs in a collective of states, and to choose from them a supreme\n\nmonarch, who should steward the constituent monarchs in his wisdom and with a firm-hand.\n\nWere the Kingdoms of humanity to with each other combine, and the monarchs together of varying levels of aptitude to their position were to choose from amongst\n\nthemselves the most well fit to the supreme crown over the constituent monarchs, then a just monarch could be established. The unity of the Kingdoms should  strengthen the military and economic state of function, and further serve to demilitarize and\n\nfocus supplies on economic pursuits, by allowing for the each of the states to contribute to a military to a lesser degree, which shall together equal a force unrivaled by any modern monarch.\n\nThe human Kingdoms of Salvus, Ruska, Herendul, and Oren,\n\nwere they to unite, could each contribute but 25,000 men to a combined force, and still manage to afford their borders greater protection than if they alone attempted to muster 90,000 each for their own interests, an impossible feat regardless.\n\nThe unified states would be able to pass and enforce legislation and regulation, and efficiently and effectively steward their states with the guidance of an emperor-steward and his leadership in their governance.\n\nFurthermore, the borders and futures\n\nof the human states would be secured by the stabilizing force of the constitutional empire and her emperor-steward, who would be elected by the constituent Kings to be the most just of all men to govern humanity. The states would together validate their\n\nclaims and legislature, and their combined military force would both strengthen the defense of their borders and allow for each of the constituent Kingdoms to turn focus upon their domestic affairs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Northal, Hanseti", "Aetosion", "The Lands of Northal in Anthos, A Compendium of Environmental and Historical Information\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\nby The Rt. Hon. Edward, second of his name, of the noble House Winter of the lands herein writ.\n\nNorthal --- A History\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\n       Chapter I\n\nNorthal, previously within the demesne of the Kingdom of Hanseti, was never properly settled. In fact, the past human habitation of Northal is so entirely unremarkable that the writer isn't even sure the purpose of this passage. Previously unsettled, and\n\nonly recognized as arctic wasteland \"Wall-Adjacent\", it was unused by its lords, left as ice and stone. It was not until the modern lords and ladies of House Winter, and their hardy bannermen and vassals approached the steep and snowy cliffs, and said,\n\n\"Yes, this is land. It can be tamed like any other,\" and so it was. The tundras remained just as glacial, but the indomitable human spirit prevailed against the elements. The County of Northal was chartered by his grace, the Duke Codrik Green, for his new\n\nfound vassal, the Rt. Hon. Lord Robert Winter, son of Harold.\n\nNorthal --- A Land\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\n       Chapter II\n\nThe lands of Northal stretch from the old Teuton bridge due east of the Castle Greywyn, to the open seas of Valence off the eastern coast of the Kingdom of Oren. Defining the Southward border is the sharp shift in flora and fauna notable where snow begins\n\nto fall south of the wall. The northern border is, of course, the North Icewall. Built by whatever force for whatever reason, no human who has dared summit it has come back entirely intact. These borders, effective by edict of his grace, the Duke Codrik\n\nGreen, determine the bounds of the land.\n\nNorthal --- A Climate\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\n      Chapter III\n\nThe climate of Northal is the most entirely inhospitable south of the Wall. Any man, elf, or dwarf idiotic enough to build their home within these lands comes out a member of a hardened folk. The lands are infertile and barren, a layer of permafrost rests\n\njust beneath the soil, requiring intensive labour to render what sparse deposits of nutrient poor soil there are in Northal, usable for planting. However, it is still somehow managed, but what magics of a massed peasantry it cannot be fathomed. The\n\navailable land to be built upon is rocky and irregular. To traverse it is difficult, and to establish is even moreso. Excluding the pockets of flatland within Northal (namely, Ice Lake, Snowy Pass, and Bridge Gully), all other locales must be mined into\n\nwith a strong iron pick to break through the frozen stone and ice. It is postulated that these rare pockets are the result of glacial movements centuries past, which carved out basins into the terrain, and later melted to water the fields of Ager. The\n\nhigh temperatures of the land are rivaled only by the peaks of the Silver Mountains of Furnestock, and at only at one month during the year in the height of summer does the temperature rise above freezing, enough so for the ice of Northal to sweat and run\n\nthin streams down the cliffs into Ager, the Greymarsh, the Raev, and Norfolk. Lower down the mountains these streams gather into stillwater pools, which will continue to provide irrigation for southward farmlands, even when the water in the high up lands\n\nof Northal remains frozen. It is said that if you piss towards the Castle Greywyn in the dead of night, from any peak in Northal, that the ghost of the Hochmeister Mirtok will freeze your piss into a spear and the winds will blow it back into you, running\n\nyou through with your own piss. A nastier death a man could never fathom. The mountains of Northal are home to the frozen corpses of hermits, and the bundled men of the Winter, and none other.\n\nAn Author's Note.\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~~Father, why didn't you move us to Salvus. There is a complete lack of immoral Southeron noblewomen. Send help.\n-The Rt. Hon. Edward Winter II\n\n*The Snowflake Sigil\nof House Winter*", ""),
        StaticBook("Aegian History", "§bThe Pine Druid", "Aegian History\n\nThe Age of Founding and the Before Times\n\nDuring this time, Druids were brought together and the Druidic Order was founded by Wayward Druid Respiren Knox. The records of these times may never be fully\n\ndeciphered, however. Although we know of some of the first Druids in Malinor, such as Respiren, Swifthide, and Native, very few details are known. Perhaps someday the past regarding these times will be revealed.\n\nThe First Age of Reconstruction\n\nThe First Age of Reconstruction was ushered in by the initiation of Dragon Druid Apollan into the Order. Apollan was the first to express interest in joining the Order after reading\n\nthe \"Myth of the Great War\" and spent long hours in the Druid grotto after he was famously murdered outside the gates of Laurelin by a bandit. Apollan quickly moved up the ranks. Meanwhile, the Order gew. After initiating Apollan, Respiren expressed\n\ninterest in 'rebuilding the Order'. Everyday, new citizens of Aegis would show up in the grove wanting to become Druids. Most were immediately innitiated. As the Order grew, so did a number of things including property and knowledge. During this time the\n\nOrder gained a lodge in Ravenhold, as well as one in the Laurelin docks. Additionally, two stalls were bought at the Laurelin Marketplace and hundreds of books were added to the Order's library.\n\nThe Age of Abandonment\n\nUnfortunately, due to extremely casual and non-uniform rites of the Wayward Druid, people were joining the Circle, only to wander into the wilderness never to be seen again. With no established Hierarchy\n\nthe Order lacked organisation and purpose. This was made apparent when an Elf named Rowan arrived. Archdruid Rowan, arrived from a far off forest, seeking to re-establish his lost Circle, the Druids of Mother Aegis. Rowan is likely the only citizen to\n\nhave argued with the Order's ways. His only backing for title of Druid was that he 'had a love of nature'. When Rowan became annoyed by the fact that he had to be initiated in order to be allowed into the inner library he stormed off claiming he would\n\nstart his own order somewhere else. Rowan was last seen entering the wilds outside his home in the Ravenlodge, and was never heard from or seen again. Fortunately the dark Age of Abandonment was brought to an end by the light of the Dawn Druid Maiavel.\n\nThe Age of Reformation\n\nThe Age of Reformation was brought on by the ideas and drive of one Maiavel. With her determination, she was able to rally the remaining Druids to create an official lore, hierarchy, rules and sense of order.\n\nThe Second Age of Reconstruction\n\nDuring the second age of Reconstruction many more books were written and a Grand Tree in the Laurelin Grove was planted. New Dedicants were brought in but less frequently than in the first age, and the\n\ninitiation process was more careful and uniform. During this age, the current Hierarchy was established with Apollan as Archdruid.\n\nThe Age of Knowledge\n\nThe Age of Knowledge was ushered in by Petyr, the Salmon Druid. His creation of the \"Dedicant's Vow\" and the \"Attunement Ceremony\" greatly helped the Order as did his other ideas, including spearheading the wiki.\n\nThe Age of Mushroom Transgressions\n\nThis age was brought about by the conflict caused by the deffering ideals in the Order. Some Druids were becoming increasingly annoyed at the restriction that came with having a grove in the\n\ncity (where trees/mushrooms could or could not be planted and the structure of the Druid tree). Other Druids argued that it was their duty to promote balance, and that the runway growth of mushrooms flowing from the grove was nowhere near\n\nnatural. Some Druids wanted a new grove to be created outside the city and far away. Others wanted the grove to be close. Still others did not want a new grove at all. However, it is important to note that most of these arguments were caused by\n\nmisunderstandings, which is why this age is sometimes called the Age of Misunderstandings or the Age of Confusion.\n\nThe Age of Renovation\n\nIn the end, most mushrooms were removed from the grove when Maiavel stamped her foot and the mushrooms instantly broke (but were unthoughtfully left on the ground, only to be swept up by Deltaro). A new,\n\nsecret grove was set up in the wilderness outside Ravenhold, (notable work from Mahten and Aeaira whom spent days working on the road leading to civilization). The Laurelin Grove continued to be renovated and improved on, with notable work\n\ncontributed by Lunar Druid Bircalin and Dedicant Deltaro.", ""),
        StaticBook("The First's Word", "§bUnknown", "It is on this day, lliran, we were declared no longer Mali. Some may gasp and scorn me for writing in the tongue we had for so long cast of as part of our duty to guard the talareh'sirame-- But no longer is it just the Okarir'ame who have cast off our\n\nancient tongue. No, it is the will of the council that all elves within Malinor, if it can even be called that at this point, forget the mother tongue which was once spoken by all of the noble descendants of Malin. I seek not to speak these words aloud\n\nnot for shyness, but for practicality. It is clear we may not allow our greatest cultural artefact to be simply destroyed by the now mad council. It is clear that those who lead us must not know of our impending betrayal for the sake of Malin.\n\nWe must prevent what is to come. We must preserve the Word Altar.\n\n- Eloem", ""),
        StaticBook("The Plaque", "§bUnknown", "elmahnih'vallei biloke el iheiuhii'ame-- oem tayna ito haler tayna'ame ito elefer. ito puer'sae dionne'ne, indor'ne. heya'maehr'sae ito Eliheiuhii'ame. san'thill indor into Eliheiuhii'ame ehier elindor'lin'Malinor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aheral Hst. V1", "§bThe Scribe.", "Mali'aheral means blessed Elves. The Mali'aheral ancestors bathed in a golden pool. This is how they gained their appearance and conciousness that is kept today. The Mali'aheral have a tendency to dislike the other races. Many\n\nbelieve this is a burning hatred, and that the Mali'aheral seek to rid the world of the other races. However, this is not true. The Aheral merely are annoyed at the chaos and lack of intelligence of the others.\n\nIn Aegis, elmaliaheral resided in the leafy cities of Laurelin. Upon the High Council, only one Mali'aheral sat, Prince Toren. He alone stood as a bastion of order against the chaos that was seeping in from the rest of Malinor. However,\n\nit can be assumed he may have actually been impure, as the strict and just laws of purity had not been established as of time he lived in. \n\nPrince Toren was tasked to feed all of the Elves of Malinor. As such,\n\nhe grew one of the largest farms to ever be seen in the lands og Aegis. He named it the Laurelin farm. That is, one is afraid, all that is known of the people in Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("On \"Racism\"", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "On \"Racism\"\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nDuring my initial days of Haelun'or, I took great care in writing a treatise upon the more common questions critical of Mali'aheral society. This book contained rebuttals to these questions for the sake of education, and the sake of the ignorant\n\npeoples beyond our community. This is a reprint of sorts (though not truly, as the original manuscript was lost in Asulon) that contains more ignorant questions, extended arguments, and superior literacy. That said, this introduction is long enough.\n\nLet us begin.\n\nA human once told me,\n\"Purity is of the heart, not of the mind and body.\"\n\nLet us ignore the obvious conclusion that a heart is merely a muscle that pumps blood through the body, with no importance to purity other than filling its\n\nmandatory biological role. The human presumably refers to the heart as the beholder of an abstract concept of \"goodness,\" so we shall argue that point. \n\n\"Goodness,\" the act of being \"good,\" is a fundamentally flawed concept. There are\n\nthings that are innately evil, such as the dread-demon Iblees, profligates of Dark Magics, and other varying monsters who tout goals of domination and destruction. These are certainly cruel. But what can truly be considered \"good?\". Good (and at times\n\n\"evil\") are subjective in their very nature. Even the words of the much-revered Aenguls are only a matter of perspective. Let us say that in a Valah village, a family is taxed heavily by their local Lord. This lord treats them the same as any other\n\nfamily, but this one is particularly poor, and can barely survive the long winters. One day, the father in desperation robs a nobleman, and kills him. The pauper did not take pleasure in the act, and had not intended the nobleman to die. This allows him\n\nto feed his long-suffering children. Would this act be good, or evil? If one situation can be skewed in such a way, then, logically, others must also be flawed. \n\nThe maehr'sae hiylun'ehya teaches that purity is a combination of mind,\n\nand body. It is something only mali'aheral are capable of, and can never be allowed to fester beneath the guidance of the ignorant. To advance our people, Mali'aheral must enhance and strengthen their minds. To understand nature's workings is\n\nto understand our existence and its natural place in the true-world. To this end, our people are gifted with extraordinary intelligence, and it allows us a greater capacity to absorb information, and create our own.\n\nIn advancing our people, we complete the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. The heart has no purpose in true purity.\n\nA wood elf once asked me, \n\"If you are not racist, why do you not allow intermarriage between your people and other races?\"\n\nThe other races are, as commonly said, \"lesser\" than true, pure mali'aheral. This is not a malicious slur\n\naimed at them for amusement or as an emotion-fueled outburst of hatred. This is simply observable fact. Traits that commonly bring the ruin of other societies, for example; greed and violence, are barely prevalent within our community. Furthermore, our\n\naforementioned heightened mental faculties make such traits almost non-existent. Our blood ensures this superiority, and every muddying of our family lines with inferior specimens dulls preferred Mali'aheral traits. This makes the completion of the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya more difficult with every corrupted generation. Were we to allow rampant, foolish breeding, then the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya would never be completed, and our kind would languish in the mediocrity of the other Mali.\n\nA Dwarf once asked me,\n\"If you have no prejudices, why do you allow so few outsiders within your society?\"\n\nOutsiders are difficult to trust. There are a worthy few of them accepted into our numbers, but these have proven their\n\ncompliance and worthiness to our people. To why we bar outsiders in general, will be answered in an allegory--one that will be far simpler to grasp for those not of our people. \n\nImagine yourself the owner of a fabulous dwelling, filled with\n\ndelights unknown to your envious neighbours. You enjoy your life amongst the trinkets and comfort items that you gathered, and rest in a fine wicker chair in the sitting room. Suddenly, a person you have never met walks through your door, without so much\n\nas a knock, and begins to walk about \"Ooh\"ing and \"Ahh\"ing at the many delights and placing her dirty fingers upon your property. Confused and concerned, you ask the obvious question of \"What are you doing?\" The stranger, with a smile, explains that she\n\nthinks your home beautiful, and is looking around. You, in turn, explain to her that you don't want unannounced people in your home. With that, she becomes angered, and declares that you're \"greedy\" for keeping your property to yourself. Such things\n\nshould be for everyone to see! You explain to her that she is free to do as she pleases with her own home, but that you prefer your privacy, thank you very much. \n\nThe stranger disappears, and begins spreading  rumours amongst your fellow\n\nneigbours of your greed, and how you \"hate people.\" Suddenly these neighbours also begin to barge their way in, and look about. Sometimes, things go missing. You in turn build a high wall around your home, and though they continue to voice their anger\n\nat your actions, they are no longer a nuisance. It should not be a necessity to do this, but the nature of your neighbours makes it so.\n\nA dark elf once asked me, \n\"Your people insult ours so viciously! Why would you be so cruel?\"\n\nMisinterpretation on the part of those whom we \"insult.\" If this occurs so commonly, why have these victims not re-evaluated the\n\nreasons behind our words? What we say always has merit. This is what they do not understand. They choose defensiveness over recognising their faults, and therefore never adapt and improve themselves. Thusly, our people will \"insult\" them again, and will\n\nlikely continue to do so until their missteps are recognised. Such is only befitting a proper Mali, and for their own good.\n\nA Goblin once asked me (version interpreted from orcish babble),\n\"If you are superior, how is it we orcs have slaughtered you in battle countless times?\"\n\nActs of combat and physical strength do not imply superiority. Violence is one of the\n\nbasest and most simplistic natural urges that any animal is capable. It can stem from any dark emotional outburst, and those that practice them commonly cannot be fully trusted. To use yet another example -- were a giant spider to attack and kill an Uruk,\n\nwould the spider therefore be superior to the orc?\n\nSuch as it is, these questions irk me so, especially when my associates cannot answer them. May you be further enlightened, my reader.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("What is Love?", "§bThe Eternal Library", "What is Love?\nby Unknown\n\nLove?\nWhat is love?\nMerely an entertaining hobby?\nOr just something to produce the next generation?\n\nOh how?\nHow do you love?\nHow do you get\nThat tender\nPassionate\nThumping\nSpeeding\nHeartbeat?\n\nFrom the long told fairy tales.\nWhat of the intense burning inside?\nThat were told by old couples.\nDoes love deserve your undivided attention?\n\nWhat is love?\nWhen one has not yet experienced?\nOr is it a simple personal journey\nThat everyone will pass one day?", ""),
        StaticBook("Barbuthulith", "§bVellulaei'thill Vul'athri", "A study of\n     Barbuthulith\n\nPreface\n\nMetal and rock have both long been an integral part of every civilization. Even the barbaric bipedal creature labelled 'Uruk' has used them to build a vaguely organized agglomeration of primitive clans.\n\nIt is a common belief outside the silver walls of Tahn'siol that the greedy bortu are the greatest masters of metalworking in existence. \nThis is both comedic and ridiculous. While the stunted ones have certainly achieved great skill in burrowing into the\n\nground like rats, their knowledge is greatly lacking in the finer arts.\n\nMetalworking is a skill obtained through the centuries, perfected by dozens and dozens of Mali'Aheral for years untold. We have truly achieved perfection in this.\n\nFew are the secrets that stay hidden from us now.\n\nDiscovery\n\nHowever, these mysteries still remain, for this art holds secrets kept withing the earth itself, hidden from our ever observant eyes. One such secret was discovered while cleansing steel in preparation for a\n\ntask.\n\nAt first glance, t'was but a harmless piece of rock, to be removed and cast into the flames.\nHowever, as I picked it up with my clamps, I was shocked to find that it would simply not be shaken free from the aformentioned\n\ntool. Realizing that there was something most strange at work, I pulled it out of the flames and let the clamps and rock cool.\n\nDescription\n\nFirstly, a visual description. This rock has no outstanding features like Orichalcum. It is plain and black. Running water over it has not removed this dark sheen, which has lead me to deduce that it is not the product\n\nof ash from the forge.\n\nThis rock is most peculiar. Analysis shows that it is attracted to one thing and that is iron. Whith any other material it will act like a vulgar pebble and slide off. But with iron it will stick. When removing it, a small feeling\n\nof attraction can be felt by the person. As if a sticky substance kept the rock attached to iron.\n\nIt has no reaction to copper, bronze or gold.\n\nPotential uses\n\nBarbuthulith as I will now call it, was tested in water as well. The unclean water of the forge. It was plunged into a beaker of the dirty liquid and the results were most satisfying. It was almost as if it had purified it, the water\n\nhad cleared a few shades and once the rock was brushed off and plunged in again, the same reaction could be observed.\n\nMost interesting, a purifying rock would be of enormous use when facing a plague or simply a sullied well.\n\nAfter expirementation it has been proven that it removes sickness from water. Sullied water was taken from a small village and brought to the two test subjects. One was given the water as such, while the second ones water was purifies beforehand.\n\n-The purificatin process consists of running the water through a small sieve with the rock at the bottom and repeating this manoeuvre a dozen times over.\n\nAfter a week, subject one was in a dire state and displayed the typical plague\n\nsymptoms. It was thus purged in flames. However, subject two was very much alive and well. Of course, this subject was killed and dissected to verify that the inside was as healthy as the outside. Analysis proved that it was in perfect health.\n\nNote:\n\nBoth subjects were valah.\n\n\nI conclude that this rock, barbuthulith has enormous potential and I will certainly inspect it's attractive properties in details.\n\naddendum:\n\nBreaking the rock into smaller pieces diminishes it's attractive capabilities. It seems that it relies on mass and is probably not a magical object.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sillumir Conduct", "§bAndria Ith'ael", "Sillumiran Conduct and Regulations\n\n\n              \nBy the Maheral\nAndria Ith'ael\n\n          Index\nPage hael (3)\n  Preface\nPage kulin (5)\n  Cooperation\nPage esun (8)\n  Valah \nPage telu'oem (11)\n  Mali'aheral\nPage telu'esun (18)\n  Kharajyr\nPage niut'telu (20)\n  Avernan\n\n       Preface\n  Our situation within the new citadel is very different from the times of Annil'sul. We are now within a new land with our allies. Due to this, the Sillumiran are in need of new regulatons to allow us to continue to\n\nprogress. The children of Larihei shall be safe.\n\n  These regulations shall take affect on the 1st day (oem) of the Deep Cold, in the year 1475. \n\n \n ~Maheral\n\n     Cooperation\n  As per our new agreement with House Savoie of Aldersberg, who are the owners of the land we currently reside on. We are to provide milltary assistance if they request it.\n\n  If there is trouble\n\nwithin their town or land, it is your duty to assist them in the removal of the trouble maker - or threat. \n  You are to cooperate with the guards of the town if required, if you do not trust them, then consider the fact that they gave us\n\n a home.\n\n  However unlikely, in the event of a war, we be obliged to provide to help House Savoie (and House Carrion) in their battles. The Maheral is of the opinion that assistance will not be required often.\n\n         Valah\n  As we now live within the lands of the Holy Oren Empire, more specifically the land known as Aldersberg, it is going to be a common occurence to see a Valah approach the gate. Members of both House Savoie and Carrion are to be\n\ngranted entry if requested.  This also applies to any other member of governence within Aldersberg or Oren.\n\n  The typical proceedure for allowing a Valah entry to the citadel is simple. Simply inquire as to what their\n\nname is, what their business and/or reason for entering the city, and what weaponry they are carrying. If they seem suspicous or a resident of another nation other than the Holy Oren Empire, further questioning may be needed.\n\n      Mali'aheral\n  The Maheral wishes that only the uttermost pure Mali'aheral enter the citadel. The proceedure to allow them entry is similar to that for the Valah, however additonal questions are required.\n\n  Upon the new arrival approaching the gate, one should examine them for strange eye or hair colours, excessive jewelry, or tatoos.\n\n  Examples of 'impure' traits or signs of Mali'ata include dark coloured hair, red or black coloured\n\neyes, golden jewlery or a severe amount of tatoos. \n\n  It is recommened you do not kill such beings, for we are not on our own land. Instead, let them be unless they continue to approach the gate after being denied.\n\n  If they are indeed physically pure, you may begin the mental purity test on them. The first question to ask is simply 'Thill ito kae'leh?' or 'Are you pure?' You may provide a translation of the question in Common if they are not influent in the\n\nElven language. \n\n  After they have sucessfully answered the afforementioned question, you may begin to ask about our society, questions such as 'Who is Larihei Lohmanih?' or 'What does the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya mean to you?' are adquate questions to provide to the new comer.  \n\n   You may also ask them of their skills or occupation to allow for easier intergration into the citadel.\n\n  If they sucessfully pass, you may grant them entry. Though let it be known that the Maheral may overturn your judegement at their will.\n\n        Kharajyr\n  Kharajyr, much like our allies in the Holy Oren Empire, have not betrayed us. Therefore, as they once lived with us, they are to be granted entry as the Valah are.\n\n  They shall be\n\nsubject to the same regulations as Valah, though they may need to be protected better due to potential dislike of Kharajyr displayed by the Valah.\n\n        Avernan\n  Avernan - simply meaning 'wanderer' or 'confused person' in our language, refers to those who are not permitted the citadel without the permission of the Maheral or are banished from our blessed society.\n\n  Avernan include Mali'ame, Mali'ker, Bortu and Uruk. All of which, with the exception of some of the Mali'ker and Mali'ame, are to not be granted at any time. Not even the Maheral may grant an Uruk entry.\n\n  If one of the\n\nafforementioned beings requests entry, you may contact the Maheral for judgement of the situation or check if their name is the list of permitted Avernan, for there are few who are not associated with the nation of Laureh'lin.\n\nay'Haelun'or Larihei'ehya\nay'maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n  Sillumiran, always remember your sacifice and your vows. Protect the children of Larihei.\n\n~Andria Ith'ael, Maheral of the Mali'thill", ""),
        StaticBook("Law and Progress", "§bThe Scribe.", "The Importance of Law.\n\nMany are opposed to the laws of the Mali'aheral. They decree them horrendous or barbaric. \n\nMany are opposed to the laws of the other races as well. Every individual seems to believe with a burning\n\npassion that only their laws are conducive to the most prosperous nation. However, I believe that law itself is prosperous to a nation or goal. How can progression exist without rules or order? The Mali'aheral are my first example of this.\n\nTheir laws are strict and very pointed. They are designed to weed out chaos from the state of Malinor. In doing so, science has been able to thrive within their community, and drives them towards success and prosperity.\n\nThe next example are the Orcs of the Rexdom. Their laws are much looser, but still maintain some integrity. The Orcs are a very violent race, but their goals are accomplished step by step. However, they progress slower than the Humans, Dwarves, and Elves\n\ndo. The Valah have a very stringent code of honor, and it allows them to progress quickly and militaristically. The Bortu have less stringent laws, and progress at a slower pace than the Valah do.\n\nLaws are conducive to progress. Without personal code, without the code of state, without the code of the realm, progress cannot be plentiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Origins of Magic", "§bValmuel Elibar'acal", "In a normal perspective, energy is taken from the void and projected into anything the caster may like. Take it be a Fireball or a wall of solid ice! Of course, there are many ways one could direct this energy from the void. However, we will be delving on\n\nhow exactly it works! Now, to begin, we must remember that all magic is of void origin, and it all must return to the void. \n\nThere are a few exceptions to this rule, such as the Druids, of which they're magic leaves\na lasting effect\n\non the world. This can be done by using the energy granted by such forces to move the objects appropiate to the magic they are using. This would pertain to nature, obviously. So it is not the magic that stays in the world, but rather the object\n\ninfluenced by the magic. With this being said, after a spell is cast and the connection to the spell is lost, it will return to the void. This is a quick and natural practice, however those who have trained to utilize this process can be\n\nknown as users of Fi\nhiiran'tanya. The entire idea of this, is that one would open up an immediate \"portal\" of which the mana returns instantly, to the caster's will or not. Only mana can pass through this portal.\nThe entire explanation of this shall be\n\ncovered shortly. THe reason I am bringing this up is because I wish to explain a large concept, and perhaps, truth. All magic comes from the void, even Deity/Source magic. The reason this is, is because we as mortals have difficulty drawing from the void.\n\nAlthough as powerful as we may conceive ourselves to be, our access over the void is somewhat limited. That is why some turn to Deities/Source Users, who have much more power.\n\nPower brings ability. These have the ability to draw upon\n\nthe void in ways we cannot imagine. That is where holy magic, and perhaps dark magic, may originate. In a basic sense, it is casted in a sense to \"smite\" the mana, to return it to the void swiftly.\n\nOne could argue that is exactly the conflict\n\nof which these users face. Whether it is holy or dark is not the question, but perhaps different ways of expelling the magic to the void? \n\nAs I was saying, Deities/Source Users can cast in ways we cannot do. It brings in possibilities\n\nof Druid Magic, Holy Magic, Dark Magic, Kha Magic, and other forms. However, all of it is drawn from the void. With the immense power of these beings, one could mold and shape the mana in different ways we could never do.\n\nIn recent events,\n\nwe have witnessed some interesting things happen to the progression of magic. The Dark Lord Setherien, the Leader of the Scourge, fuels his servants with his power. Now, this may seem normal as other Aenguls or Daemons might do. However, there is one key\n\npoint. Setherien is mortal! Atleast, he is a physical form. The potential knowledge from this is unlimited. If one could give another magic, if powerful enough, in the physical plane, why can't others do it?\n\nThis is a pure concept, and not to be taken\n\nentirely serious just yet. However, the possibilities are endless, if there is no restriction in the physical plane. Could one possibly amass enough power to give another his/her abilties? Again, I do not know the answer to this. It is all speculation.\n\nIn conclusion to this small essay, magic in of itself is highly peculiar, and much of it we still do not know about. However, I hope you have had a stronger grasp of it's origins and capabilities, even though I personally do not recommend it.\n\n- Valmuel Elibar'acal", ""),
        StaticBook("Ways2DealWImpure", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Liberals,\n  Dissidents and\n   the Impure:\n The Ways to Deal        with Them\n    Accordingly\n\n      by Nelecar\n\n       Foreword\nAs steadfast upholders of the mali’aheral ways, we must recognize the threats caused by these three subgroups to our blessed way of life. There are key differences between them, and factors about them vital for\n\nthe average citizen of Haelun’or to know - in this text, I do so hope to explain such.\n\n   Chapter One:\n      Liberals \nA liberal is a fellow Mali’aheral such as you or I who has fallen prey to the hedonistic and frivolous ways of the wood elves. They believe incorrectly and immaturely that we as a whole are wrong and they are right -\n\nthat our discrimination has ‘no basis’ and we should be equals with the vile orcs.\n\nThey are blatantly wrong in this regard; if you see or think you may have had any knowledge of a liberal, report it to the officials as soon as possible.\n\nFrom my studies and research, I have recognized that there are two main subgroups inside the liberal circle. These are:\n\nThe Dormant Liberal\nDormant Liberals disagree with our ideals, however they do not plan on taking\n\naction against them currently, and remain very silent about their opinions. While they may not seem to be, they can be potential threats to the government and the Mali’aheral way of life. They are essentially a seed stage, and dormant liberals can\n\nprogress into volatile liberals.\n\nThe Volatile Liberal\nThe volatile liberal disagrees with our ideals, and takes or plans to take action (albeit from the shadows) against them.  They try to recruit others to their cause subtly. While they are\n\nmuch more dangerous, they are far less subtle than dormant liberals are- dormant liberals, of course, keeping their opinions entirely to themselves.\n\nLiberals are perhaps the hardest of all to quell, and their punishment varies on severity, however\n\nideal course of events is to have an agent identify the liberal and zone in on him. A warning will be given most of the time, however in extreme cases (such as a desire to overthrow the government) a more permanent measure will be needed.\n\n   Chapter Two:\n     Dissidents\nThey are always sympathizers of the lesser races.\n\nDissidents tend to be easier to deal with in most cases - however sometimes they take refuge in other nations, particularly in nations where free\n\nspeech is permitted. In these cases they may be protected by law. The appropriate punishment is imprisonment (as exile wouldn’t work due to the previous statement), however in medium-to-high cases execution may be needed to prevent further offenses.\n\n  Chapter Three:\n    The Impure\nPerhaps the most heinous of the three groups is the unclean. An impure is one born of a Mali’aheral and a non-mali’aheral. Breeding with a member of the lesser races is perhaps the worst crime in our society, far\n\nsurpassing murder and thievery. They are often belligerent, troublesome, and corrupt, and would see us in ruin. They have many supporters despite their nature. Exile is the appropriate punishment for being an unclean and having intimate relations with\n\na non-Mali’aheral, whereas execution is the appropriate punishment for procreating with one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Refreshments", "§bLilliana", "-=+=-Cool Milk-=+=-\nFreshly cooled milk that stays frosty in its glass. This milk will throw you back into the days of your youth and fill you with soothing joy.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Calming Tea-=+=-\nMade with fresh Chamomile leaves and set to relax you. This tea will help sooth the nerves and make you feel calm. Perfect before meditation or a test.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Nightly Tea-=+=-\nTea made with Jasmine and small amounts of Nightshade, this safe tea is tested with our youngest patrons to give you the perfect drink to help sooth you to sleep.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Sweet Tea-=+=-\nA burst of sugar and tea leaves, this tea is meant to give a short burst of energy and sooth that sweet tooth.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Honey Tea-=+=-\nA honey based tea meant to help sooth muscles and sooth damaged throats. This is perfect to drink after a cold or illness.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Black Tea-=+=-\nFor a stronger and more intense burst of energy, this tea is made with you in mind. This will help give you the necessary burst of engery to fill your day up.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Ice Cool Water-=+=-\nA tall soothing glass of water, this will help quench any thirst. Fetched directly from a deep spring, its guranteed to be cool and refreshing.\n\nPrice :: Free\n\n-=+=-Apple Juice-=+=-\nFresh squeezed apples mixed in with the cool spring water makes this sweet juice all the more desireable to drink.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass\n\n-=+=-Berry Juice-=+=-\nMade with a variety of berries, this cool juice will make you content to sit and sip away like a carefree child.\n\nPrice :: 2 minas per glass", ""),
        StaticBook("Slight bleeding.", "§b[Ghost hiding] Irelia Fenn'asul", "Alternative ways to stop bleeding.\n\nWhen treating a victim, the primary sources which help stop bleeding may not be available. However, there are alternative sources. \n\nSugar, for example, when poured onto a\n\nwound will help with the clotting process and reduce the risk on infection, but only slightly, and is a good secondary method.\n\nIce can also slow blood flow and provide pain assists due to numbing.\n\nMixing salt with water\n\nand poured over an open wound can aid in disinfecting and bleeding cessation.\n\nThese methods work best for small cuts and wounds. Do not waste time finding these things if proper equiptment is available!", ""),
        StaticBook("Defining Purity", "§bAzorella Coulissante", "As is often the case with such things as mutable as language, definitions and connotations can often become confused over the passage of time and the turnover from generation to generation. This particular treatise will attempt to clarify\n\nsome of these definitions, namely those regarding Mali'aheral purity.\n\nFirstly, it must be noted that this treatise will not attempt to explain how the lesser races may try to define their own standards for purity,\n\nshould they have any standards at all. Since a pure Mali'aheral would never breed with such lesser stock, such definitions are generally irrelevant for practical use and will not be addressed in this document. For the purposes of this document, the terms\n\n'pure' and 'impure' will refer only to those who have some form of Mali'aheral heritage. The term 'lesser' refers to any of those without a Mali'aheral heritage.\n\nPurity, like the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, typically relies on\n\ntwo main pillars: mental purity and physical purity. The first pillar, mental purity, is more difficult to define and is dependent on a Mali'aheral's actions and intentions. This will be covered in more depth later in this document. However,\n\nthe second pillar, physical purity, is considerably more straightforward as it relies strictly on bloodlines.\n\nPhysical purity is dependent entirely on a Mali'aheral's heritage. A pure Mali'aheral can only\n\nbe born of physically pure parentage and therefore cannot have any of the lesser races marring their bloodline. By contrast, a physically impure Mali'aheral (also known as an acaln due to the severity of this impurity) will have a\n\nlesser amongst their ancestors. There is no way to remedy this kind of impurity aside from termination, hence, extreme care must always be taken in regards to producing offspring.\n\nMental purity is less simple to define and\n\nis reliant on a Mali'aheral's actions and intentions. A mentally pure Mali'aheral will often adhere to the tenants of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, although this kind of definition is bound to evoke confusion since each Mali'aheral likely has\n\na slightly different interpretation of Larihei's teachings. These different interpretations ought be embraced as they help weave a lush and rich environment ripe for debate and learning; however, in defining purity, these interpretations often\n\nbring with them ample confusion.\n\nInstead, it may be simpler to try and define the actions and intentions of a mentally impure Mali'aheral. The greatest offenses to mental purity lie in the murder of other pure Mali'aheral\n\nand in breeding with lessers. However, care must be taken to note the intention of such actions. For instance, a Haelun who accidentally smothers her infant in their slumber may remain mentally pure depending on the circumstances, but\n\na disgruntled guard arbitrarily murdering fellow pure Mali'aheral ought serve a capital punishment for their capital impure offense.\n\nSome lesser, but still troubling, offenses may include violent assault on another Mali'aheral or\n\nphysically intimate fraternization with a lesser, even if this does not lead to expected or unexpected offspring. These kinds of mental impurities may be recoverable by a strict reeducation, but are nonetheless a grave insult to the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya and should not be taken lightly.\n\nAs a final word of warning--to accuse another Mali'aheral of impurity is a matter that should be handled with grave care. To do so falsely would be akin to trampling on\n\ngenerations of careful breeding and centuries of tradition with intense ramifications for the accused should the innocent walk guilty. By the same measure, however, it is equally dangerous to allow impures to scourge society should the\n\nguilty walk innocent. Take care with your judgement, lliran, for the future of the Mali'aheral rests upon it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity and Order", "§bIcarus Adil", "Purity and Order\n\n        Haelun'or,\n           Axios\n\n     Published 1589\n\n\n\n     by Icarus Adil\n\nChapter 1: Introduction\n-------------------     There have been a great many works written about purity and the importance of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, each of which provides a compelling account on the importance of purity to the mali’aheral of\n\nHaelun’or. Yet to my knowledge, there is no literature on the importance of purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya in their preservation of order within Haelun’or and among the mali’aheral.\n     If all the reader seeks is knowledge about the nature of\n\npurity and its appointment or attainment, then I encourage them to pursue other pieces of writing. “On Racism” and “Purity,” both by Lucion Sullas, prove valuably informative, or alternatively the more contemporary work of Iaria Elervathar, “Our Purity.”\n\n     Each makes an invaluable case for purity and its importance, and will undoubtedly aid the reader in understanding the ways of the mali’aheral. Yet if the reader remains unconvinced, or otherwise seeks a prescriptive understanding on how the maehr'sae\n\nhiylun’ehya maintains order wtihin Haelun’or, I implore the reader to read further. This may prove a particularly valuable tome for those not of mali’aheral birth who have chosen Haelun’or as their home, so they can understand why they too must pursue the\n\ncourse of the pure.\n\nChapter 2:\nSystems of Order\n-------------------     Before we consider purity as a means of maintaining order within Haelun’or, one must consider how systems for promoting order work within a society. Though I expect most readers to be pure mali'aheral of\n\nHaelun’or, perhaps some reading have earned the right to live within Haelun’or in spite of their birth, and originate from beyond these walls. Regardless, systems of order in other societies will serve as adequate allegories for our purposes.\n\n     First, let us consider the Holy Oren Empire. Ignoring their frequently shifting regional variance, there are many consistencies which promote order within their society. For example, the Empire maintains a system of nobility, informing each person\n\nwithin the Empire of their place in society at their birth. This position determines each individual’s rights and responsibilities, how they must conduct themselves publicly, who it is appropriate to marry and produce offspring with, and this is only the\n\nstart. Likewise, through the relationship of vassal and liege, every individual can trace the line of authority from themselves to the Emperor, a central figure from whom all authority comes.\n     There is no question that this system has its faults, yet\n\nthat is only when this system of order is ignored. At times, vassals will believe themselves capable of ousting their liege and forcing themselves into power, or liege lords will provoke rebellion through ill-treatment of a vassal, and in short order we\n\nfind a system of chaos. Yet it is almost always certain that, had these individuals opted for maintaining the existing system, they would have found themselves better off. No matter its issues, the Holy Oren Empire maintains a fairly effective system of\n\norder.\n     Next, we shall consider the Dominion of Malin, more specifically the Principality of Laureh’lin. The mali’ame have a far newer system of order, existing in earnest for less than a century, yet it has proven exceptionally effective in\n\nestablishing order through dogma. In a strategic move, a single individual managed to establish a false history for the mali’ame, reframing the already familiar and respected Aspects as  gods of the mali’ame. Through effective proselytizing, many were\n\nindoctrinated into this faith at a time when the mali’ame faced unprecedented strength and security.\n     The results of this have proven particularly exceptional. With the authority granted by these newly established gods, the Prince of the mali'ame can\n\njustify his every action and force order upon his people. Whether it be intrusive internal measures to maintain security or gross external violence, in the name of these Aspects he can do as he pleases. Not even the Holy Oren Empire has based its society\n\nso heavily on zeal and dogma, differentiating it as a thoroughly different yet similarly effective system despite seeming political equivalences.\n\nChapter 3:\nPurity and Order\n-------------------     It is my hope that these two examinations, though cursory in nature, have proven helpful in understanding what is meant by the term ‘system of order.’ Now it is time to consider purity through a\n\nsimilar lens.\n     Purity is particularly prescriptive through the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, for it demands a great deal of those seeking to be pure. Most simply, it demands physical purity, the fervent refusal to muddle mali'aheral blood with that of other\n\nraces, even fellow mali. Those who ascribe to purity recognize superior traits found more consistently among mali’aheral bloodlines, and as such each must do their part to ensure they go unsullied.\n     Equally important are the components of\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya, more contemporarily considered ‘progress and health.’ The first gives each pure mali’aheral purpose, for each mali’aheral must actively pursue progress. Each must provide some work, typically of the mind, to add to their society.\n\nThe goal of this imperative is to constantly improve upon itself, to add more and in turn encourage others to add more. Through progress, we provide each mali’aheral with purpose.\n     Yet on its own, progress could be pursued recklessly. This can mean an\n\nofficial believing he knows best and resorting to progress at the tip of a sword, a scientist deciding progress comes through sacrifice and garnering it through deathly experiments, or a madman bastardizing progress as justification for other atrocities.\n\nThis is the importance of the imperative of health, for it requires that all pursuit of progress must not come at the expense of our fellow mali’aheral. Each is equally important if Haelun’or is to exist as a society rife only with order, and thus the two\n\nmust be pursued strictly.\n     Of course, purity requires all to behave in accordance with a series of intricate rules. There are rules of how one can and cannot treat their body, how courtship is to be performed, specific manners through which disputes\n\ncan be adjudicated, among countless others. Though some who decry the mali'aheral way treat them as needlessly restrictive, in fact they are no different from the rules of any other society. Each and every society has rules for socialization and\n\nappropriate behavior, yet Haelun’or has chosen to codify them and enforce them strictly. This is merely a means of removing ambiguity, and thusly is not strict, but instead merely ordered.\n\nChapter 4: Systematic\nFailing and Change\n-------------------     Despite the fact that purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya are clearly exceptionally ordered, none but the most stubborn would assert Haelun’or has not faced a great many failings over the\n\npast century. This is not due to some failure of purity as a system, but instead the decisions of citizens and leaders alike ignoring it.\n     We have seen periods of leadership where needless aggression and warfare have given strength to the wielders of\n\nblades rather than pens. We have seen periods where citizens care little for the collection of knowledge and pursuit of progress, but instead their mere existence with brief recital of maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. We have seen those who pursue twisted progress\n\nat the sacrifice of health. When we find disorder in Haelun’or, it is not due to a failure of this system, but instead a decision, conscious or inadvertent, to ignore it for some other end.\n     Each system of order has means to create change; for\n\nHaelun’or, the means of change is open discussion and decision by the consensus of mali’aheral. Yet too frequently, change has been pursued by open rejection of purity or the implicit bypassing of it. For purity and maehr'sae hiylun'ehya to prove a\n\nsuccessful system of order, the principal aspects of purity, progress and health must always be pursued, and change must be considered within these boundaries and through the systems for change we deem legitimate.\n     Though this has been meant primarily\n\nas an informative account of how purity promotes order within Haelun’or, it is also a cautionary one. To maintain our system of order and to protect purity, we must maintain a society with open discussion rather than censure, and commit Haelun'or to\n\nholding its purity with the utmost reverence.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Death, & Life", "§bElindor", "Introduction\n\nSection 1:\nMental Scarring\n\nSection 2:\nAccepting Death\n\nSection 3:\nGenerational Cycles\n\nIt would be beneficial to begin with by outlining common knowledge before traversing any further. We mortals have been granted a most precious gift since the first Iblees war in that the Temple Monks are capable of cheating mortality.\n\nRegardless of the fatal nature of our injuries we are able to be revived and restored as though such a thing had never happenned. And thus the actuality of our mortal beings comes only at a time when our soul no longer grasps on to whatever fate it was\n\nthat kept our body here. Either by admitting defeat or realising success. These are the only two options for a soul that no longer returns to this realm for its body. And the dream of all mortal beings is that we can discover the latter, and in doing so,\n\nfind our eternal peace. But for many, it is the former that defeats us; a wounded soul desiring to escape the cage of this mortal flesh.\n\nSection 1:\nPsychological Scarring\n\nIt would be only a fool who attributes physical scarring to a lack of skill on the part of our Temple Monks. Capable of re-grafting burnt flesh and attaching severed limbs (or growing new ones)\n\nthere is really no place upon these bodies for scarring. For a Monk is able to heal with the divine Triumvirates powers to restore a body to the juvenile untouched form of a babe. In those experiences where ressurrection is not required and a fleshwound\n\nis the result, would not their hands be able to rejuvenate such an imperfection of the skin?\nSurely it is only by acceptance of the wound that our soul attributes it as an integral part of self.\n\nIf the one soul were able to be bound to two identical bodies (if it were the same soul one would assume the bodies to be the same as it is a common belief that our physical appearance is manifest from our central 'being') that then lived independant,\n\nif after the lifetime of a human they were brought back together to be compared, would they not be considered so very different from eachother? Forgetting the earlier talk of physical scars, their personalities would have taken shape under the outcome\n\nof their personal experience. One may be a romantic fool while the other is defensively paranoid. And this because their experiences have shaped them more than the soul from which they came. So then, any scarring that may further differentiate them is not\n\nmerely a defect, but a signet. That darkened patch of skin or red line of flesh serves as a reminder of the lessons that this individual has endured. Thus for all of us, the scars that are upon our body are only those that our soul has developed an\n\ninseparable attachment to, in the knowledge that what came with that scarring is an alteration upon the individualism of that being.\nThe result: countless visits to the Temple Monks will still bring back the bruises of a past life. Long after\n\nthe physical effect would have reason to remain. It is only when the psychological association with a scar is lifted (or fades with time) thatthe body can be observed as healing.\nUnless one can avoid trips to the Monks altogether.\n\nSection 2\nRealising Mortality\nAs was alluded to in the preface: fatality does not come (with rare exception) when brutality of wounds overcomes the skill of the Monks. Instead the soul chooses not to return for another month or another day. There is\n\nsome unnaccounted for resignation to the final rest that research has never successfully concluded why the circumstances of which are wholly individual to each case. As was also alluded in the preface; realisation of mortality is clearly connected\n\nto a soul's concept of fate.\nWhen time's expanse is objectively viewed outside of the portion of a lifetime, what becomes of the existence of one individual is not the occupation of their years, but the accomplishment of their fate.\n\nEach individual soul is tasked with a thing that it is their duty to discover and accomplish. And the eternal rest that comes to a soul that has aligned itself within the universe's jigsaw is a reward so much greater than a gardener's sense of\n\naccomplishment over the blooming of magnolias.\nYet we are surrounded by brokenness, failed purposes and vengeful cycles of hurt. Not all souls can accomplish their purpose. Many souls would not even have uncovered what that\n\n'thing' it is that is required of them before their time expires.\nThe observation, then, is that the soul is a more delicate entity than perhaps we credit it. When our innermost being (whose connection to the divine/spiritual we've no comprehension of)\n\nabandons this vessel before its purpose is actualised, there must have been a monumental resignation. The continual numbing of repeated defeats, or the mindless wandering of undiscovered purpose, or the accepting of a rival too great to overcome.\n\nWhen a soul permanently abandons its vessel, it too abandons the purpose for which it needed that body in the first instance.\nWhat unbearable sadness did forsake the fallen.\n\nSection 3:\nCyclical Beings\nHas not it been observed that the attributes of a known figure in history can personify another whose purpose is the same? Was not High Prince Native considered the reincarnation of Malin himself? even\n\namongst Elves old enough to have known both within their lifetime. The of presence of Xan, an Aengul of ol', joined these mortals to fulfil an action set in motion millennia previous. And lesser examples too of the reappearance of the Arcane Mage,\n\nas well as others whose striking semblance of another from the past (not so in physicality but in characteristics and drivenness towards a same purpose) is haunting yet undeniably required.\n\nHow many times has this entity previously existed? How many other vessels has this soul occupied? And does it return because the purpose has not been fulfilled, or because it /has/ yet similar cirumstances arise in which the same purpose repeats?\n\nFate is a tricky thing to pinpoint. Undeiniably there are important figures who shape the way the world functions. But what of the smaller ones who, over their lifetime, have made a mark that is (at least for a time) irreversible?\nAre we all cycling\n\nendlessly? Or is it only the few who do? Perhaps the soul has some interaction with the Aenguls who no longer walk amongst us. They have always been so desirous of interacting with the mortals, and mayhaps it is these cyclical beings through which\n\nthey can. Perhaps (at more of a stretch) these /are/ the Aenguls incarnate with the mortals.\nThere are many questions that yet remain, and perhaps I, the author, should have answered more of them before writing this.\nNext time.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spear", "§bThe Forgotten Scribe", "\"Brev was the first man ever to strike down an Aengul, and when it’s patron of Age screamed from the heavens, ‘what have you done’, Brev could not hide his discrepancy, for the proof of the Aengul of Youth’s death blazed bright from the height of the\n\nsky.”\n~-~\nThe legend of Godslayer Brev is one not often noticed amongst the archives of the Temple Monks, whom covet the knowledge of the known planes upon their sandstone shelves. It is a tale of regret, of fury\n\nand sadness, and within it’s weathered text lies a lesson for both man and goldblooded -- to never pass the boundaries that the Creator set for them.\nBut the legend it not mere falsehoods; it is truth, bound upon layers and\n\nleather and scribed from men of ancient origin; from the time when holy fire raged in the sky, and from the time the same fire scorched Krug’s pure kin to the bone. The time of such event dates back even before the known times of Iblees’\n\nwarmongering, when the four races established themselves in their four corners uncorrupted but sparse. They prospered and they settled brief peace; it was a time known not for wars, but for curiosity and expansion, and\n\nknowing that their four fathers already took claim to the whole of the Aegisian plane, they sought what was beyond it -- what they could reach, but could not grasp. The sky.\nTheir attempts at claiming the heavens often fell to dust; enacted by\n\nover-ambitious humans and haughty Elves with towers that either did not reach high enough or simply toppled because of their reach. Ironically, it was not the mortals that reached the immortals first, but the otherway around; for the\n\nraces held no means of reaching their godly masters whereas the masters could reach them -- and reach them they did, in those old times, when all were naive and thought nothing of conceit and budding violence.\nAll mortal men were jealous of the\n\nbirds of the sky, whom could sail the wind and reach the borders of the heavens with but draws of their wings, and the shadow these creatures cast were like salt upon the wounds that were carved into the early history of red-blooded\n\nfailures. Shadows were a sign of irritation, and the sun’s rays were favored over the darkness of physical mass-- thus, understandable emotions derived from these mocking shadows. Human men spat upon the shade of flighted\n\ncreatures, Elves scoffed at them and Dwarves grumbled and retreated into their mines, seeking comfort amongst earth’s treasures. The Old Orcs, smooth of skin and monstrous naught, however, saw the shadows of winged beasts as\n\nchallenges and insults, and sought to snuff them from the sky in which they were projected. One such example would be of the Legend of Brev, whom mistook an Aengul for a bird in the face of the glaring sun.\nWandering the planes of Krug’s\n\nbirthplace, the descendant Brev, who was famed for his great strength and fortitude, was in the process of a grand hunt with the intent to return to Krug’s children with enough game to feed them all for weeks -- a feat that would surely be remembered\n\neven when worn from the passage of time. However, prey was sparse, and Brev’s effort in the chase was languish in the face of demanded speed. What he had caught was drawn from his impressive ability to throw spears of iron that cut through the\n\nair like a giant’s arrows.\nThe sun’s smile was bright and it’s rays were harsh on this day of the hunt, and it was only into the late afternoon that the towering, tan-skinned son of Krug found himself at a loss; unwilling to trek further into the\n\nexpanse of his homeland in search of prey that refused to challenge him. But lo’ and behold -- a great shadow was cast upon the earth from a creature of mighty size, far larger than a bird, that circled Brev upon the waves of the sky. Staggered by\n\nhis findings, Brev drew his eyes to the sky -- and beheld but silhouette of an assumed bird of great size alone; unable to make shape of it’s features on behalf of the sun’s blinding light. Knowing his spears were not enough to fell this creature, Brev\n\nsought a nearby mountainous range, and from the side of the mountain he grafted a massive spear of sturdy stone; unable to be hefted by none but himself and his kin in the manner which he planned for it.\nSo he returned to the circling\n\ncreature, which was unbeknownst to his plots, and with squinting aim and the tense of muscles, he flung the great spear forth -- into the sky and into the heavens which the beast lingered; an arrow, a lightning bolt of earth that shot from the\n\nground instead of the clouds, and in a spectacle and show of godly skill, the spear impaled the creature; but it did not draw blood.\nCuriousity was a scourge to those of heavenly blood -- it was a sign of degeneracy and ignorance, for all\n\nAenguls and Daemons knew most of the inner-workings of the world thus far - with the exception of their own experiences - and the trivialities of exploration and - Creator forbid it - the interaction of the mortal and the immortal. But some\n\ndisregarded this ideal of isolation and sought to bless the four races with their presence. One such individual was the unnamed Aengul of Youth, whom favored sailing the vast skies of Aegis, much to his patron’s displeasure and concern -- the Aengul of\n\nAge, whose name is also unknown.\nThe Aengul of Youth was naive and sought to explore all there was to see, and his journey led him to Krug’s birthplace, whence Brev roamed in feverous hunt. But his search for glorious knowledge led to Brev’s\n\ninescapable fury; a decimation carved from the very earth. Flighted in the sky with wings not unlike a hawk’s the Aengul of Youth bathed in the gross incandescence of sunlight-- blind to the one that mistakenly targeted him. In one fatal\n\nswoop, however, the Aengul’s heavenly being was collided against and impaled with Brev’s Stone Spear; and the event of the Aengul’s violent death was so great, that gold blood was not drawn, but fire -- the spear scorched by golden flame, plummeting\n\ndownward, as the very sky ignited in destructive reaction to the Aengul of Youth’s cataclysmic demise.\nThe seven heavens felt this death, this disparity -- and it’s Aengul of Age, who fathered the Aengul of Youth since it’s creation, cried\n\nout in horror; he cried out and his voice was so furious and abask in agony that it cracked through the sky and shook it’s very foundations -- “What have you done?!”\nAnd Brev, who stood awed and horrified by his own mistake, his worst sin, could\n\nnot move from the place that he threw the spear which lingered steps from him, buried point-first in the sand - he could not close his eyes despite the bright volumes of the plummeting golden fire. Without even the notion to raise his\n\narms to protect himself from the charging storm, Brev the Strong was engulfed in the fire of heavenly demise; roasted to the bone and decimated by it’s otherworldly power almost immediately.\nThe Monks of the Old Cloud Temple were the first to take\n\nnotice to this tragedy, and with hurried pace they sought the scene now riddled with ash and golden fire that still cracked and burned upon the ground; the black scorch-marks focused upon the still-standing skeleton of Brev and his spear - coined\n\nthe Stone Transgression - to form a most unusual display. The kin of God expressed his horror and his dejection from the skies, and thus, these old Monks sought to honor him by damning Brev’s soul to a limbo, and his spear to a grave.\n\n\nSealing his soul to a single large rib, Brev’s skeleton was buried with his godslaying spear within the depths of Krug’s homeland with his soul, trapped within the severed, surprisingly heavy bone locked within a jailed chamber of steel and earth;\n\ndamning Brev’s soul to a fate of ungained peace, trapped in a limbo and locked within but a peace of his own scorched structure.\n~-~", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity", "§bLucion Sullas", "Returning to Purity\n\n\n\n\n\n\nby L. Sullas\n\nThere is to be a new number of standardised regulations regarding those who have fraternized/taken on disingenuous traits that any and all impure mali’ata of pure birth may undertake. As the mali’ata has wronged the venerated race,\nthus they must seek\n\nredemption in the eyes of all who would call themselves mali’thill. As such, they must gain the forgiveness of all who dwell within the pure lands.\n\nThe “purifying” shall be conducted in stages.\n\n1. The Drawing of the Curtain--\n\nThe mali’ata must be sincere in their desire to become a part of the glorious nation, and be willing to perform all the tasks asked of them. They must be willing to shed all childish egalitarian\nbeleifs pushed upon\n\nthem by the hedonists of the outer-world.\nShould they not conform to this ideal, they shall not be allowed to return.\n\n2. Righteous Revulsion--\n\nShould the mali’ata be sincere, and willing, they will be allowed to enter the city. Here, they must seek out every citizen within its walls, and tell them individually of the crimes they have committed towards\n\nmali’aheral. They will then, after informing each individual of the crimes, ask for forgiveness from each citizen. The citizen may ask the mali’ata of anything, and the mali’ata will do as they ask with great vigour and a calm disposition in a manner\n\nbefitting any true mali’aheral. The labours the mali’ata provided are but a pittance in exchange for the attacks on purity they have performed.\n\nAs a citizen, standards of good judgement are expected and a request which calls\n\nto question the logic of itself will reflect negatively upon themselves if inadequately explained. Should a pure citizen request a task that clashes with the laws of the city, the citizen shall be punished according to the crimes they\n\nrequested to be committed.\n\nThe mali’ata may not advance to the next stage unless every citizen gives their forgiveness.\n\n3. Learning the Way--\n\nAll mali’ata must understand and revere the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, as it is the very phrase that defines our people, our culture, and our civilisation. Those that lack an understanding, an interpretation, or true, unbridled zest\n\nfor the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya will find themselves shortly more unwelcome than they had been previously.\n\nThe mali’ata shall be assigned a teacher from the ranks of citizens, the duty of whom it will be to teach the mali'ata\n\nthe maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. During this stage, any citizen may approach the mali’ata with a task, and as before, they must complete it.  \n\nAt the end of this process, they will be tested by a select group of citizens of their knowledge\n\nregarding the blessed phrase.\n\n4. Meagre Acceptance-- \n\nThe mali’ata, after gaining the forgiveness of the others, and understanding the apex of our culture, will be called to an assembly of all pure citizens. Here it will be decided by the\n\nmajority whether the mali’ata may become a part of the exalted society and resume their title of mali’aheral. However, they will not be considered a full citizen unless they undertake the final responsibility of their race.\n\n5. True Acceptance--\n\nThe reformed mali’aheral may now look to the city, and consider it their home. But they will not be known as “citizen” until they find a citizen of pure blood to be bonded with, and propagate the mali’aheral race.\n\nAt the birth of the first child, they shall be entirely forgiven of their crimes in any fashion, as they have returned all that they have stolen from the mali’aheral people.\n\nWith this act, they should rejoice--as they have obtained citizenship.\n\nby L. Sullas\n\nCopied from the Law of the Mali'aheral\n\n*a pile of paper has been stacked neatly*", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Purity", "§bIaria Elervathar", "The Prominence\n          Of Purity\n\nA special thanks to:\n\nMy maln and haelun,\n\nIatrilemar and Ariana Elervathar\n\nMy tutors and lliran,\n\nAcaele Lazul and Nyna Norval\n\nIntrocution:\n\nKarin’ayla everyone. Although you are probably moreso interested in the topic regarding purity, I cannot let you escape this brief introduction. My name is Iaria Elervathar, malii’lari ito Iatrilemar eyha Ariana Elervathar.\n\nI was both raised and lectured in The Silver City of Axios, eager to learn more about our desire for purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. Albeit I have yet much to learn, I consider myself quite adept in the ways of our culture regarding our most --\n\npriced possession, our purity. I wish to lecture you further upon the matter, or merely give more knowledge for you to enjoy.\n\nChapter 1:\nPurity\n\nPurity comes in many different ways. You have physical purity, but also mental purity. Both are priced possessions that us, the Mali’thill, would not want to trade for anything in the world.\n\n Our purity is defined by how closely we follow the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. an ancient phrase that the Mali'thill have carried for centuries from the old books originally left in the College of Haelun’or. It roughly translates to --\n\n\"The pursuit of wisdom and health\".\n\nNow let me explain to you, dearest reader, what mental and physical purity actually means.\n\n--\n\nPhysical Purity:\n\nA matter regarding your lineage and appearance. We cannot take you seriously if you’re a mixed breed. Your maln and haelun, both probably mentally ill, had the sick idea of pursuing a romance that spits onto the work --\n\n that us, the Mali’thill, have protected and worked on for centuries. You are certainly not welcome in our blessed city.\n\nMental Purity:\n\nThis involves moreso your determination to the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. --\n\nYou may look pure and come from a Mali’thill lineage, yet that does not necessarily mean that you’re the face of purity. It’s about your personal demeanour. If anything of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya is violated by you, we consider you as mentally impure. -\n\nYou’re in luck however, since we grant you the courtesy of being lectured again by one of our blessed Mali’thill. You’re welcome, impuritan.\n\nChapter 2:\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya\n\nNow that I’ve explained the matter of purity to you, dear reader, I must certainly inform you about the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya I’ve been writing about. --\n\nAs I’ve mentioned before, this ancient phrase in the Elven tongue is roughly translated to \"Wisdom and health\". Wisdom, and health. Both factors we value dearly. Let me thoroughly explain to you these two factors.\n\n--\n\nMaehr'sae \n(Work/Progress)\n\nThis refers to our expanded development of our knowledge and wisdom that we gain throughout our years in life. The life of a Mali’thill must be commonly filled with the eager to learn and gain more --\n\nknowledge and wisdom. This revolves around the topics of science, arts or magic.\n\nHiylun\n(Health)\n\nThis regards our purity, both physically and mentally. It is important for us to hold dignity --\n\nin our lineage and physical appearance, as we are blessed with this glorious race that stands above all. I myself am very proud of my heritage, especially about the prestations of both my maln and haelun.\n\nChapter 3:\nPurity, why is it so important?\n\nAs my last chapter, I’d like to explain why we value the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya and our purity so much. That our life can be determined from these two factors may seem absurd to you, --\n\nbut then again you may obviously still not understand after reading this tome.\n\nWe are proud of what we are. Yes- again, absurd to you perhaps. We do not wish to taint this work we’ve been providing for over centuries now, --\n\nespecially not with impuritans and mentally ill parents who provide us with mixed breeds. We presumably have more knowledge than any other race existant due to our years of experience and the information we are granted from our unique Eternal library. --\n\nI personally pity you, although not all living mortal could be like the Mali’thill.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Arithi", "§bRuth", "House Wicce and House Arith were the only ones to survive when we crashed upon this new land. Everyone else we had ever known sunk to the bottom of the Frozen Sea. And now, House Arith has been eradicated. They were a Southern house, ruled by the Imperium\n\nof Man. They did not fare well in the cold. The last of their kin died when their keep collapsed some leagues north of us. We settled back when we saw the blizzards that consumed the north. They were never less clueless. The secrets they lost\n\nin that quaint little keep of Azgoth! It is said they kept a massive compendium of knowledge that they fiercely protected. Some say they tended to it more than their own hearth. But these are only rumors. The truth lies in the north, in their keep.\n\nOne of our own riders reported that the keep was smouldering and crumbling, admist a heavy snow storm that settled on the ruined castle minute by minute. Perhaps a thunderstorm. Would lightning melt through stone and steel so quickly? Who are we to know?\n\nThe Arithi are gone, and the Wicce's have plenty to worry about. Me? I'm thinking about finding whats really happening up North. Something is behind all of this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bio Theories", "§bLeyu", "Contrary to the magic theory of life being so diverse due to magic, I have observed something quite different. The following will be my notes and observation on reality.\n\nThe offspring seem to have traits dirived from their parents. The calf of a piebald doe and a solid coat stag had approximately half the spots its mother had. The following is a sketch:\n*a sketch of a spotted doe, a solid color stag, and half of each calf\n\nI thought that maybe that if one was to build on one specific trait, it would become more pronounced. I took 50 mice from the wilderness, each of more or less the same physical appearance, and caged them in my room. I selected the most approachable of the\n\nmice, being the ones that did not instantly recoil from my presense. I took those mice and bred them together. After a few weeks, I selected the most approachable of the babies. These too, I bred. I continued this for five generations.\n\nGeneration 1: These mice did not instantly recoil when I approached them. They also accepted food I gave them. I deemed these mice, out of the original batch, to be the more approchable of the batch.\n\nGeneration 2: The more approachable mice out of this generation were as follows: They were less hesitant to accept food from me, they did not scurry away from my hand, and they were unphased by my presence.\n\nGenereation 3:\nThese mice were astoundingly strange. They seemed to be joyous when I arrived to check on them, and they did not recoil at all. They did not hesitate to accept my food.\n\nGeneration 4:\nThese mice were very different. They were extremely overjoyed to see me, and they were like dogs. They snuggled agaisnt my finger, and kept to me for warmth. When I touched them, they were in ecstacy. These were tame.\n\nGeneration 5:\nThese mice are as tame as any household pet! They scamper towards me and attempt to cuddle with my hand. They seek my presence and are saddened by my absense. I believe I have successfully produced a pet, and tamed mice.\n\nI decided to test if the obverse was true. Out of the original batch I captured from the forest, I bred the most unruly ones. The results are as follows.\n\nGeneration 1:\nThese mice were the unruly ones I selected. They ran away from my finger faster than the rest, they did not sniff the food I offered, and they seemed a bit afraid.\n\nGeneration 2:\nThese mice were even scarder. They took less time to run away from my finger, they did not even go near the food I offered, and they occasionally got defensive.\n\nGeneration 3:\nThese mice were even more defensive. When I put my finger near, they hissed and ran away. They ran away from the offered food and did not even attempt to reconcile with me.\n\nGeneration 4: \nThese mice were even more ferocios. When they saw me, they got defensive, and attempted to bite my finger several times. They snarled at the food I presented.\n\nGeneration 5:\nThese mice were as aggresive as a mother bear! They actively attacked my finger when I put it in there, and I have the scars to prove it. They hissed and snarled at the food, and they were alerted by my presence and were violent.\n\nThe results of the Mice experiment were very fruitful! It proved that if one were to exploit the traits and capitilize on particular traits, in this case, tameness and aggression, one could change the entire race of animal! We have proven that traits are\n\ndependant on parental traits and that they can be artificially manipulated and be used to make new races of animals, with different behaviors and physical descriptions.\n\nI have developed an extraordinary theory! The results of the mice experiment proved that traits can be artificially manipulated and selected, but could nature do this as well!? It may go against everything that we are taught, but perhaps the diversity of\n\nlife in the wild is a product of nature, not magic! Could nature dictate that the creatures with the better traits more suited to its environment survive to pass their traits to their kin, thus making that trait prominent in the race. Eventually, this\n\nwould accumulate and become a new race! This could explain the diversity of life far better than magic ever could! I dub this theory Draug's Theory of Natural Manipulation of Traits.\n\nDraug's Theory of Natural Manipulation:\nMany people would object to the past statement, announcing it as heresy and idiocy, but there is enough proof to atleast make an argument for it. I realize that I have not really explained the Theory of Natural Man-\n\n-ipulation. Basically, nature plays the role I play. The beasts with the desirable traits, ones better suited to the land they live in, will be able to reproduce, thus passing the trait that allowed them to survive to their kin. Nature weeds out the unde-\n\n-sirable traits through illness, predation, food accessability, and famine. The beasts that have the better traits will pass the trait to the kin, and so on. Eventually this will manifest into new beasts, with distinctly different traits than its\n\nancestors. Overtime, these beasts become specialized to their environment, and have developed specific traits for their lands. For example, creatures of the desert have ways to conserve fluids and keep cool, like larger extremities and needing less water\n\nto survive. I bet that these started out as, a beast needed slightly less water to survive, and it survived, with its water consuming peers dying of thirst. Eventually the trait would become prominent. We have not yet discovered how these changes come-\n\nabout, but we know they exist. Given enough time, a beast will become specially accustomed to its land, eventually thriving in its habitat. Life will prevail and overcome obstacles through Natural Manipulation.\n\nThe Theory of Dominance:\nWith each generation traits are passed down from parent to offspring. It seems that some traits mask other traits. The red petals of flowers are more dominant than white. Yet in the next generation,\n\nthe plants were red and white. It seems the trait was not destroyed, yet hidden away. Such stands the theory of specific traits being dominant over other traits.\n\n-Xanthur Altraza\n\nPlant Luminescense Theory:\n\nAfter planting flower cultures and observing their growth, I noticed a strange phenomenon. When I first planted the flowers, some were planted, accidentally, on a hump in the dirt, making them face more horizontally then\n\nverically, like the others. However, after three more days of observations I noticed that these plants has started to tilt. They eventually, throughout another week of my spectating them, aligned themselves with the original vertical plants, making now\n\nboth groups face vertically, albeit one group's bases are planted horizontally. I concluded from this discovery that plants require something from the Sun, (Through Artificial Manipulation they achieved this characteristic/ability, since a plant which is\n\nable to tilt itself towards its source of nourishment, the sun as I concluded, would be more efficient than one which could not, making it more likely to thrive and prosper, thus through nature the plant has been manipulated so as now the whole species\n\nshares this ability), This something required by the plants could either be the sun's warmth or the light it emits. So as to test this, I created a new experiment. I planted a few flowers under the shadow of a tree, thus making them not at all exposed to\n\nsun's light.  I planted a few more flowers next to the trees shadow, where it was exposed to light. After two weeks, the leaves of the plants, under the tree, began to shrivel and yellow. After about another week, the plants completely died. On the other\n\nhand, the plants exposed to light were green and healthy, prospering. After several retrials of this test, I can safely say that plants in fact, do require light to survive, as well, plants have developed a method of adjusting themselves so as to be\n\nexposed to light, this through Artificial Manipulation.\n\n- Sil Iyat\n\nWhales\nThis may be something different from the rest in this journal, but I believe it is necessary. I will observe the habits of whalers. I can see what can drive a beast to threatening status.", ""),
        StaticBook("Delivery Birds.", "§bThe Scribe.", "DELIVERY BIRDS.\n\nHow is it that birds are able to find the recipients of letters without knowledge of who they are needed to visit? My theory is that birds can be trained to detect the soulstones of those who need letters delivered to them. If this is true, can\n\nall animals sense soulstones?\n\nAll musings of course.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Odd Wish - SB", "§bSam", "\"I wish that I my hair becomes dark blonde, my eyes bright blue, and my skin a lighter color.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("One Wish..", "§bAbigail M. Eumelia", "My wish is to leave a legacy on the world. To be remembered as a great mali'aheral.\nI just want to make everyone..happy...living in peace.\n\nPeace between the races, and to leave my legacy on the world, being remembered as a Great Mali'Aheral.\n\nPeace...\n\nRememberance...\n\n\n\n\n\n         Abigail\n         Eumelia.", ""),
