        StaticBook("Secret Hunt (V2)", "§b[Masked] Talen Broclaw", "Renenkai Benevere\nCaitlyn Hightower\n\n40 dwarves, only two survivors against Undead. \n\nUndead pushed advantage, then vanishes.\n\nSpiders and Zombies rose from the ground\n\nOther nations not notified yet.\n\n\"Naieri\" Friend of Renenkai\n\nOrdanach = Spider Matriarch. Servant of Iblees\n\nSlavers:: Operating outside CLoud Temple\nAppearance: Scars.\n\nDark Elf, \n\nCaitlyn is sailor\n\nKing of Oren: Heinrick Carrion\n\nA little summary of what you're doing. For now, head to this location ((PM when you're there))\n\nABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\n\n24: -854.5 26: -742", ""),
        StaticBook("Arlen's Wish", "§bArlen Kharadeen", "Sultan Arlen Kharadeen's Wish:\n\nAsides from wishing for more wishes, I aspire to become exalted among men through minas... So aye, about 10,000 minas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elad's Wish", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "Dear mighty and powerful good of LoTCWeen, \n\nIt would be with great if I could recieve a fancy magical relic or item in return for my hardships in this maze.\n\nLove, Elad\n(Haadi Mubdee)", ""),
        StaticBook("Pyromancy,AGuide", "§b[In Costume] Archibald Cyrion", "Pyromancy, A Guide.\n\nFire Evocation, otherwise known as pyromancy, is the art of creating flames from the  very essence of the Void itself.\n\nGetting Started:\n\nKnow you may ask\"How do I even get to the Void?!\"\n\nWell ask no further.\n\nA simple week or two of meditation will hopefull get you along the lines of connecting to the void.\n\nImagine the void as a\n\nwindow within your mind, and through that window is energy (of sorts). To keep that window open there needs to be something holding it open, in other words: your energy, call it mana if you will.\n\nAfter connecting to the Void:\n\nAfter managing to connect to the void, a mage simply has to get better, through the means of meditation and practice. \n\nOnce a mage has formed a sort of \"bond\" with the void, they may now begin to summon flames.\n\nHow do you\n\nask? Well all you need to do is know how a flame is, how it is made, how it not only destroys but purify, how it burns, basically BE THE FLAME.\n\nOkay, I Managed With the Void and How Fire Works, Now What?\n\nNow you get to the fun part.\nWith the connection of the void and the knowing of how fire works, you probably know how to do it, somehow.\n\nAt first a mage in there first week or two will barely\n\nmanage to get a spark going, much less a ball of fire. However after continues effort and meditation, a mage can achieve their goal of mastering fire evocation over the course of around five elven months.\n\nFire:\n\nNow you may be asking how are you going to actually use it in the terms of combat. Well obviously you, with some practice, mold the flame into that of a sphere and condense it. The stronger larger the flame, the greater the energy. \n\nAs of this,\n\nyou can also cause an explosion of the fire as it contact with a surface, the size of the explosion depending on the strength of the mage.\n\nNow after reading this, you may or may not want to be a mage. But good luck!\n\n- Archibald Cyrion, Head of the Cyrion Bloodline", ""),
        StaticBook("HarbTale Vol.II", "§bOrithur", "A Harbinger's Tale\n\nVolume II\n-------------------\n\nWe went under many names. Harbingers, Dark Leuitenants, Hiishtgul, but no matter what we were called, our reputation for hideous destruction,\nmutilation and fear\n\nwas known universally. Our first major target was the Druidic Grove of Anthos, were the Nine Harbingers gathered with the corrupted footsoldiers to slay the peaceful tree-folk. Needless to say, it was a slaughter. And we loved every moment\n\nof it. The acts of evil we performed were bliss to us.\n\nWe resided in Setherien's distant corrupted lands where I, the keeper of his knowledge and his library, constructed a mighty spire where it might be stored. Despite my corruption\n\nit seems my love for books remained untouched. It was here that I endlessly studied the races, and even the Order of the Golden Lance. Those seeds of doubt within my ashen mind grew small sprouts upon discovering so much about the world we sought to\n\nvanquish. Nothing made sense to me, and I at first voiced my concerns to my brothers. They spoke of treachery and it was then I saw that I was the only one, the only one to not be entirely mindless to the whim of Setherien.\n\nMany moons passed,\n\nand many more acts of slaughter proceeded. Continually villages and cities fell, more and more innocent victims of the Drakaar would fall, their bodies rising as twisted, distorted versions of their previous selves.\n\nI initially watched with a sense of\n\nglee, but this glee faded as those seeds of doubt stretched into long vines, and the realisation of what was occuring continued to gradually dawn upon me.\n\nI decided action needed to be done, and I summoned my library spire to the\n\nfallen elven capital where I had told Setherien I'd be expanding the library's knowledge. Although a Drakaar, Setherien's lust for knowledge as all dragons do lust for was also untouched, and he willingly accepted my quest. In truth, I had wanted\n\nto contact the elves in a nearby settlement, as often adventurers would venture to my corrupted spire, where I would speak and discuss things endlessly with them. Needless to say I was threatened and often attacked, but despite this, I continued to learn.\n\n\nAs my painful release from Setherien's corrupted began to reach its close, I was attacked. The elves only saw that I was a Harbinger, the creature that had destroyed their home and loved ones, so I do not blame them for felling my spire.\n\nSetherien however, did begin to see what was becomming of me. I sensed his eyes watching me always, his distrust of me would be my undoing and I knew this. So I escaped. I latched my lifeforce to one of his Bloodshards and fled from Anthos. Alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seed of Laurelin", "§bTristanm1", "The High Prince of Malinor and The Seed of Laurelin\n\nScribed by Zevandir\nTold by High Prince Native\n\nA powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities came to Aegis to help us with the erecting of Laurelin's trees. I met him at the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple.  We set off on foot to a mountain gorge I had come across that\n\nwould act as a natural barrier to our foes. Once we arrived, the Druid wandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch at his hip every so often. He showed me the seeds in said pouch and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them, with a shine\n\nvery similiar to glowstone. Whilst my brigade of builders were creating the city's defensive wall, trees began to grow exponentially! It seemed as though the trees grew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above us. It\n\nwas a wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similiar glowstone sheen, and sprinkles of metallic dust swirled down from the tree tops.\nThere was still, however, a large clearing in the centre of the city. This of course\n\nwas for the mother tree. A tree to harbour them all. He grabbed a bit of parchment from his satchel and look over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid then walked to the centre of the clearing, and began to cast a powerful spell upon one of the seeds.\n\nleaves suddenly spun around him wildly, and a wonderful green color radiated from him like an aura.\nThe tree' trunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. I was rather frightened when I saw this, hoping he hadn't cast the spell incorrectly. As\n\nthe Mother Tree grew to its ultimate height, I saw a small opening half way up the tree. Low and behold, the Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming \"This is where the stone alter shall lie.\"\nOnce the trees seemed to stop growing, we climbed up the\n\ntrees with packs of wooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become of the finest city's of Malinor, and to think it had all begun with just a pouch of seeds and a pinch of Druid Magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ", "§bTuvya", "By writ of His Imperial Majesty those creatures known as Ascended may put their wards over Petrusia.\n\nTrickery, curses, or decievery will be met with the execution of\nperepetrator and\naffiliates.\n\n~Tuvya", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Demons", "§bBruta Thersist", "Frost Demons\n                                  \n\nThese creatures typically take the form of a woman. Typically only Elven or Human. The Creatures are pale skinned, clawed and sharp toothed. A true abomination to the...\n\nCreator's design.\n\nArmed with Evocation and typically assisted by whatever fool they've seduced into their bidding. \n\nIt should be noted that these women are also Illusion mages. Hiding their true forms.\n\n       Counter Measures\n                                        \n\nExposure to open flame, typically close to the skin, disrupts the illusion magic at play.\n\nThe Creatures are deathly cold to the touch.\n\nThe Women have abnormally sharp teeth.\n\nSimply check a woman for all the standard signs associated with these creatures and there should be no issue.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish...", "§bElijah Everest", "I wish to be a great builder of nations and to own an architecture business and an archery shop.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Trapped Boy", "Viper3X", "Day 1\n\nThe ruins collapsed in behind me. I haven't been able to find a way out. I have no tools or weapons, and the rubble is too heavy. I'm almost out of food. No clean water, only a small stream that travels underground. I can hear creepy sounds nearby.\n\nDay 4\n\nI'm so tired. So, so tired. I haven't eaten anything in 2 days, and my stomach feels empty. The water... the water had something in it... My stomach... it hurts...\n\nDay 6\n\nMy skin! I don't know what is happening to me. I can't feel the lower half of my body. I can barely crawl to the water. Is this the end?\n\nDay 7\n\n*Stains of dark blood litter the page*\n\nI... I can barely move my fingers to write. I don't... I don't know what is happening to me. I hear sounds everywhere. It's like a spider is crawling around in my head. Creator, save me.\n\n*The next pages are torn out or missing.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Dohvi's wish :)", "§bDelonna", "I wish for a matching pair of silver necklaces, both adorned with the purest Whitestone Gem pendants.\n- Delonna.", ""),
        StaticBook("Silent Thanks", "Mririshboys", "Silent Thanks. \n\n-------------------\n\nFor even as our mouths stay shut\n\nThank her,\n\nEven as our words are silent\n\nThank her,\n\nThrough ways voices cannot express\n\nThank her,\n\nGive thanks in actions, silently, gracefully but\n\nThank her.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electrical Evo", "§bLelien", "Electrical\n     Evocation\n\n   §\n\n*Once you flip to the second page, a current, about the strength of a electrical fence, would jolt through you. Most likely rendering you unconcious.*\n\nWith magical love,\nSilvos and Lelien.\n*A small heart is drawn at the bottom*", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Ethics", "§bGlacio Nereus", "Motivism, Deontological, and Consequence theories of ethics.\n\nFirst, the consequence theory dictates that an action is either right or wrong based on the consequences of any given action. An example is if a man kills another man.\n\nman. The action would be right if the consequences were good, such as saving the lives of five good people, or bad, such as if the man who was killed were to have saved the world. Utilitarianism is based off of consequentialism,\n\nand the basic point of utilitarianism is an action is good if it brings about the greatest amount of pleasure, and the least amount of pain, for the largest number of people. Issues with this type of utilitarianism though are that one can not see the\n\nthe consequences of the future until they have occured, and one can commit heinous evils if others were to be pleasured by the action. An example of the first argument would be if a man is in a comatose state, and others work to keep him alive,\n\nalive, killing him would be what a utilitarian \nof this type would argue to be the good action. However, the effort that is no longer keeping him alive \ncan be used to aid others, but this condones murder of of the comatose person. The other argument\n\nis the \nsoldier analogy. A soldier fighting in a war decides to spare a fleeing enemy since the enemy is \nunarmed, wounded, and in no state to fight back. However, this soldier later kills fifty innocent men. \nAlthough the motive for sparing\n\nsparing the man was a good motive, the consequence in the long run was ill, \ndespite being unable to foretell such a result. This would make the soldier who spared the enemy guilty of what he could not foretell.  Another type of utilitarianism is rule\n\nRule utilitarianism. Rule utilitarianism is different in how it attempts to reconcile consequentialism and deontology. This formsays an action is morally justified if an act conforms to a rule, and leads to the greatest good.\n\nFor example, if a man follows a rule of to not murder, then his act is good, even if one he may have murdered will do so himself. So, two forms of consequentialism are utilitarianism and rule utilitarianism.\n\nContinuing the discussion of ethical theories is deontology. The deontological theory states an action's is based not on the consequences or the motives of an action, but rather the action in it of itself. An example would be if a man were to fight\n\ncriminals. criminals. This man's actions may be fighting for good, but he is bad due to the act of fighting being morally wrong. An example of a good action would be being charitable. charitable. If a man were to donate money to a man who uses money for\n\nhedonistic acts, it would still be a good action, and the man a good man. This is because deontology states that the act, \ncharity, is good, so the man doing the act is good. There are more nuances within this theory however, but they will not be\n\ndiscussed in this book. Finally, motivism is the theory that an action is either morally permissable or morally wrong based on the motives of an action. An example would be if the previously mentioned soldier spared his foe. The action would be considered\n\nconsidered morally permissable since the act of not killing him, and the reason for it, is good. A good. A more direct way to follow motivism is the idea to universalize a given maxim, and see if it can be ordered as a universal law. An example would be\n\nif the soldier spared the enemy once more. The action would be considered morally permissable since the act of not killing him, and the reason for it, is good. A more direct way to follow motivism is the idea to universalize a given maxim, and see if it\n\ncan be universalized as a universal law. law. An example would be the action of stealing. The maxim would be 'I should steal.' If one universalized the law, then everybody should steal. If everyone were to steal, the idea of stealing itself collapses,\n\nfor stealing is the act of taking something that is not rightfully yours. Now, there is no object or thing that is rightfully anyone's since all is being stolen, and all is gained by stealing. Therefore, this view of motivism states\n\nstealing is never morally permissable. Other actions with this include murder, lieing, suicide, and many more. An example of a morally permissable act by this view of motivism would be any action that does not defeat itself when universalized.\n\nFor instance, the soldier that spared his foe is doing the right thing since the idea of not killing does not defeat itself, and it can be universalized. However, a flaw in this argument would be conflicting duties.\n\nFor example, if a general ordered the soldier to kill the surrendered foe, the man's two duties would be conflicting. He has the moral obligation to not kill the man, and the moral obligation to obey his superiors due to the idea that\n\nboth maxims can be universalized. This argument is against this type of motivism.\n\nIn conclusion, the three types of moral theories include consequentialism, deontology, and motivism. All\n\nthree have their independent benefits, and their independent flaws.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wish", "§bProfessor Beros Oathcast", "*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n\nThis Pumpkin Day, I Beros Oathcast wish for another alchemical creation involving pumpkins... It would be useful with all these excess pumpkins laying around.\n\nMay this wish come true. ~ Beros\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*", ""),
        StaticBook("Rivenza's Wish", "§bRivenza Acosta", "I wish for my granddaughter Beatrice to grow wealthy, powerful, and happy.", ""),
        StaticBook("My wish!", "§bIyath the Toymaker", "I wish to become a veteran at tinkering, please !\n\n-Iyath, the toymaker (a little\nheart has been drawn) <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "hex37", "__Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nMatron’s Foreword: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients\n\nfor the treatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery\n\nor internal organs with nothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n\n-Minor Cut (Matron)\nSimply apply a dose of  deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it.  The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n\n-Stomach Ache (Matron)\n\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n\n-Soreness (Aleya)\n\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n\n-Burns (Matron)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere.\n\nThe important thing about burns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist, and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check the burn wound\n\n daily until the skin can finally reform.\n\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Snowy Hearts", "§bKailon Grandaxe", "Snowy Hearts\n------------\n\nMountain lays cold,\nClouds of hail,\nThe harsh wind north\nThe land assailed.\n\nUpon eyes of men\nIt drives them away\nYet to a dwed\nWelcomes their stay.\n\nFor our kind observe\nPast the cold sky\nInto the heart\nOf the mountain side.\n\nThrough the mists\nInto the vale\nA lush land appears\nWhere most do pale.\n\nMighty strong pine,\nStanding with pride\nAncient wood souls\nTo which all confide\n\nThe calls of ravens\nHarsh to most ears\nSweet winter sonets\nIs all we dwed hear.\n\nThe hares that dart\nAnd nestle in holes\nAs the snow parts\nSee the Mount's soul.\n\nThe land in the north\nHarsh and so cruel?\nDwell there like dwed.\nAnd be shown a fool.", ""),
        StaticBook("Final Journal", "§bArchMage Bell", "Scribe's Notes\nThis is the last journal recovered signed by Archmage Bell. There are several other books that may be attributed to her writing from a later date; however this journal is her last entry in full faculty.\n\nI have not been as diligent with keeping writings as I once was. This is disappointing on my part, but...circumstances prevented it. What is there to say now, really? I have given up. I have been...captured, tortured by the\n\nundead many times now. I have removed the spells which cause the Monks to retrieve my body with ease, even within such a tainted place as the Undead Keep. Why they...he...wants me to join him, so badly, I do not know. Nor do I care to know.\n\nBut, before I go into that, I should clarify what I have been doing. The Arcane Mage graciously offered me a position as an Arch Mage a few years ago. I was happy then. I was expecting to be able to find a way to save Aegis, to protect it...\n\nI failed, obviously. But I am sure now, more than ever, that the disturbance in the Balance has been caused not by a fail ure on the part of any of the Four Races, but on the failure of those this \"test\" was administered to.\n\nI believe more than ever that this all was a test for the children of the Aenguls. A test which they failed. The Undead were never meant to have the massive effect on the world that they have. The Veil is falling apart.\n\nWith it, Iblees is gaining more power. Yet, ironically, the further weakening of the Veil is the only thing which could grant us the use of magic! How the world laughs at us. The Veil must be sealed. This has gone on long enough. Magic is not worth the\n\ninsanity that the unde ad bring, the chaos and destruction and pain.\n\nBut I have not the power to do so. I have been fighting the undead in my own way. Defending the places they attack... And turning their own followers against them. Latsi, I truly hope you are happy. I...truly hope you do not allow them to get to you,\n\neither physically or mentally. Do not fall, my would-be apprentice. I realize you will likely never read this. If worst comes to worst, I will have to either end my own life...or have someone end it for me. I will not allow myself to be turned.\n\nAnd this book will likely rot on the shelves of the Library...which is fine by me. There is no need for the world to read words from a traitor like myself, who...has many times nearly given in to the temptation, just to make the pain stop. Latsi at least\n\nmust stay a bastion of truth. An example of what you can become... Though it would have been better if he had not joined the Ascended, though if he stayed with me he surely would be being tortured also. Regardless, it would be selfish of me to try\n\nand attempt to change his mind. He is free. Let him do as he pleases. And I...am free for the time being, as well. Hence I write this missive quickly lest they find me again.\n\nUnfortunately a side effect of the....things that have been happening to me is the return of numerou s memories. Some from long ago, long forgotten...these hurt the  I care not to get into them, but I...I ca nnot believe I forgot them in the first place.\n\n All of them hurt, really. I recall meeting the first Prophet. I recall the offer he gave me, the things...that happened then. How I almost fell to my temptations. The current Prophet simply loves brining those memories up, the ruddy...\n\nI believe he was upset when he lost me the first time. The fact that I rose back to fight against him again made it  worse. That, and the fact that I turned Latsi against them angered them as well. I failed at changing Kevin, though at first I thought I\n\nsuceeded. I failed at convincing Algor otherwise. In truth, my failures outweight my successes. And the betrayals that I have faced have made me bitter, angry, paranoid. They belittle the trust I place in people and the friendships that I keep.\n\n I fear death....but I fear rising from it more. If I can survive this trial...I will write again. More frequently than I have been. If I do not...I apologize in advance. If I somehow falter and become tainted, please.  Please kill me.\n\nDo not let me hurt my compatriots, my friends, the people that I hold dear. Killing me would be the greatest favor one could grant me. I need to finish this now. I do not want to lure them back to the Mage's Tower in their hunt for me.\n\n I...there isn't much to say. The Ascended and the Undead were put on this earth as a test, a test which was failed. The Veil needs to be strengthened, not weakened, even if it costs us magic. That...is all there is to say.\n\nStay strong in the face of these circumstances. \n\nSigned,\n\nThe Arch Mage, Lady *a longer name is written here, then scratched out beyond recognition* Bell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Attunement", "§bTristanm1", "The Attunement Ceremony\nForging the Link\n\nBy Salmon Druid Petyr\n\nFor a Dedicant, the attunement ceremony is the final step of initiation. This forges a link between nature, the rest of the Druidic Order, and themselves. The guide leading the ceremony must be careful to do such properly.\nI personally choose to do this\n\nceremony by the Birch Pond. I have them close their eyes, and I begin to coax their minds into accepting the spirits of nature around them. At first, I merely whisper to their minds, hoping to soften their natural defenses. Once their mind is unshielded,\n\nit is possible for enlightenment occur. It is different for everyone, but most report vivid images of the forest talking to them. In my opinion, the visions should not necessarily be told to everyone. They reveal something true about a person's inner\n\n being which should only be known to them. Of course, later, they may choose to use this information when choosing a title or totem.\nThe correct chanting must be performed and not stopped until you have internally communicated with the Dedicant\n\nafterwards. Be wary of pushing on the Dedicants to forcefully, for the mind is a fragile thing. Make sure that while forging the link, they do not react negatively, harming your mind as well as their own.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry: Volume 1", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Poetry\n        Volume One\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n     The Dreamer\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs your dreams you try to tame.\n\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\n\nUnawakened, the Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds paper he jots.\n\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.\n\n       The Cobbler\n           and\n         The Crow\n\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nto finish before the morning dew.\n\nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\n\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n\"Don't you know I have work to do?\"\nThough I know it didn't understand.\n\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\n\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing,\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\n\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn't find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\n\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\n\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nand my situation was quite tight.\n\n\"I must have dropped it,\nOn the way back from the store!\"\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\n\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\n\"Where was the tapping I couldn't bare?\"\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn't there.\n\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\n\nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\n\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe.\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\n\nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.\n\n         Imprint\n\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never do fall,\nAt least that's what I like to tell.\n\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nUsually in the day,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favorite toy.\n\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\n\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.\n\n   An Uncommon Sight\n\nI go about my day,\nDoing the same things as before,\nThe same old road,\nFrom my humble abode,\nNot realizing it is a bore.\n\nI walk ever onward,\nKnowing all my tasks by heart,\nA straight narrow trail,\nWith nothing new to avail,\nAll I do is my part.\n\nThen one day as I'm going past,\nA park once again,\nI see a boy,\nwithout even a toy,\nwho couldn't be past ten.\n\nThe boy was doing something abnormal,\nsomething I hadn't seen before,\nHe was looking in the sky,\nNot even blinking an eye,\nthey didn't even seem sore.\n\nI wondered if there was a hawk,\nOr something in the sky,\nI didn't hear a thing,\nOnly the birds that always sing,\nSo I did wonder why.\n\nI looked over,\nto the boy sitting by,\nHe was being bullied by his peers,\nAnd was starting to go in tears,\nJust for looking in the sky.\n\nI was about to go over,\nTo try to help if I could,\nbut the parents went first,\nBefore I feared the worst,\nTo help as they should.\n\nI walked on my way home,\nWondering why what I saw came to pass,\nI had a thought why,\nso I looked to the sky,\nand saw it in it's great mass,\n\nAs I looked to the sky,\nI was transfixed,\nI hadn't done this in a while,\nAnd it did make me smile,\nAs past and current memories mixed.\n\nI saw the vast expanse,\nIn all its mystery,\nI watched the clouds in the sky,\nAs they changed shape and passed by,\nAs they had for all of history.\n\nSuddenly someone laughed to my left,\nEven thought it was mild,\nSomeone looking at me,\nLaughing at what I appeared to be,\nJust as the others had done to the child.\n\n         Friend\n            or\n          Enemy?\n\nEverywhere I am\nI hide from your sight,\nIf it's in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\n\nI am one of sleep's worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear's best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\n\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when its hot and I'm in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI'm sure to give you a fright.\n\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\n\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Sorcery", "§bAmbros_", "FORWARD\nIn this book you will find a very simple guide on being a proper mage, this would include  your supplies you need as well as the proper training you need to become a decent mage.\n\nCHAPTER 1\nWhat is Arcane Magic?\nAll magic uses the smae power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often\n\nconsidered to be a more modern version of magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation.\n\nCHAPTER 2 \nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic \nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect\n\neffect of your spell to be. Some scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done. Many mages claim  that their\n\npowers are akin to keys (necessary to unlcok the final effect of a spell) another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting\n\nthat even the most learned of arcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that\n\nno one today questions their utility is anyone's guess.\n\nCHAPTER 3\nDiffrent Types Of Magic\nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.  Although they can often\n\nachieve a number of other magical feats that the other ,agical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then most often than not you will see a mage locking a door with a spell, shooting fire\n\nfrom his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any so any form of \"spiritual\" type attributes about it are gone.  A healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is\n\na form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire or easing pain with a numbing spell. Whatever the case is\n\narcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jasper's Diaries", "§bDomainoft", "Jasper's Diaries\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\nWondrous Writings\nVaerhaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((9/9/13))\n\n((These are 3 diaries of a man named Jasper. It follows 20 years of the mans life. As you read you concentrate on the important moments)) The marrige is finally today! I can't wait to move in with my wife to our new house in Al'Khazar.... Our stay in\n\nthis town has been well accepted.... A weird fellow came to our house today speaking of prophecy, looked a little crazy, but appeared to be a nice person.... so we decided to invite the prophet to lunch today. We learned he is Afonse.... His\n\nstories are full of life, death and adventure, we don't know if they are true.... Great story teller, but seems like he can't read or write.... Mr. Wilcons doesn't talk to us anymore, the town seems to have started resenting us since we\n\nbefriended Afonse.... Anna is pregnant! The joy to finally have a son or daughter to call my own.... The undeath have been on my mind of the town folk, they are becoming agitated.... Why, why..why would they kidnap a pregnant woman. Just because\n\nthey hate Afonse... why Anna? She did nothing wrong!.... She is safe... After I came home after looking for her, she was there... The relief...but Afonse was in bed next to her, gravely wounded. Seems he attacked the kidnapers... all\n\ndied, Afonse was left with injuries. .... We do not know how long he'll last, he has been weaker each day.... Our son has been named today, Jistuma. Named by his late godfather Afonse, who died today. Named after Afonse's god of judgment, to give\n\nblessing to our son and to himself recieve good fortune in death. Haven't seen Anna cry since the death of his brother. Her tears seemed green like her eyes. Rest in peace Afonse.... the king came to our house today, the treats from the town are\n\nbig, and they want us death. They take the kidnapers side, how dare they? The king decided to exile us, as to please the town, and to save our lives.... we were given the belongings of Afonse.... They said he had a will..... The king was good, sent a\n\nhealer to our home in the wild to give birth to our son..... I found a book in Afonse's belongings, seems to be about his religion. ..... It talks about sacrifices and death to pleast their masters. I don't know if Afonse knew about this.... But then I\n\ntalked to the king about it. He told me Afonse was an orphan, picked up by an evil man that showed himself as a father to him. Started teaching him his religion. but as something good, to ease the transition into evil... But as a criminal he died\n\nsoon, and left Afonse with an evil religion. That he taught was good..... As I read the book, I found out that Jistuma was an elf from the past, a former disciple, that carried the task of judging the souls of the believers.... Today is Jistuma's 10th\n\nbirthday, I can't believe how happy he is in the wilds. befriends animals from the forest, and all the traders from all races seem to like him, even the orcs for some reason.... He got angrier and attacked his mother. I do not know why. Now he is crying\n\nand remembers the events differantly. What has happened? .... Anna died... The boy cried a lot... It isn't his fault.... The druids can't figure out why Jistuma has been so angry and attacking everything. I fear he might be possessed. A more powreful\n\ndruid will come. Freight and anger make my son lose control. He is possessed by a demon, and the demon is wise. After taking control and attacking, he gives my son new memories. The druid taught me how to make a potion to ease the\n\ndemon, but even with this, If his feelings get really strong, the demon might take control... What will I do?..... Jistuma makes 18 years of age today! I can't believe how good he is at catching animals and monsters, and I'm very hapy that he sees all\n\nraces the same. He even sees all man the same. good and evil... I don't like that much, I deal with the black market for ingrediants for his potion. And sometimes they come to my house... I can still remember the time an undeath came. I was frighten to\n\ndeath, but Jistuma started casually talking to him like he was any other person.... he has been bugging me to let him travel..... I need to tell him about the demon. I think I'll take him to the druid so he can tell him with more detail. This way, he\n\ncan start to shut up about the travels... ((The last written pages of the diary are written in blood, the words get messy sometimes and drops of blood are everywhere. but its still understandable.)) We were attacked outside of\n\nAl'Khazar. We didn't noticed we wer surroudned by monsters. I got close to getting hurt by them, but Jistuma saved me. Oly to slash my stomach in the next second. HIs eyes were yellow! He quickly regained control, but he was apologizing on how\n\nhe couldn't stop the monsters in time. His eyes were losing the green from this mother and are gaining some red. He's taken me to Al'Khazar, but when someone tries to help me. He doesn't let them pass and shouts and screams. 'Why do you want to kill\n\nhim, that was so long ago, just hekp him please just help him'. The demon is distorting his reality. ((This is the last page of the diary. It's also written in blood, and there are marks that seem to be from tears, but the color on the spots are\n\ngreen.)) I am approaching death. My son left me for a bit so I could be alone to pray for Anna. Son, if you learn to read and see this, please know that I don't blame Al'Khazar, I do not blame Afonse, and I do not blame you. And remember, your\n\nmother Anna loved you, and I Jasper, love you as well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "§bArchmage Crumena", "When the murder and attacks upon the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind -- many claimed it was the work of surfacers, others believed\n\nthat such things were only possible by those within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menorcress: behind these stragglers to return the\n\nhorror unfolded, each path and passage they journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their\n\ntaint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became quickly enraged,\n\nspitting in the faces of the priestess' whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged, the devote and the rebels.\nBeneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding damnation of suns\n\nlight, the Caverns of Menorcress. Its streets littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded -- the one marvelled city now rots with death and destruction... crumbling under civil war. Bathed in life blood of their kith\n\nand kin, the rebellion breach upon the Yathrins' sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble born and\n\ntheir ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and mori alike stand in un-ease union against the treat of taint of its own city -- this seeded by those turned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed 1473.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventus Adeptus", "§bgaiusmarius8", "The days of victory has come to an end.\nWhen the armies of men pretend.\nThat one can handle the might of the Wyrm.\nThey will witness a most tenacious storm.\nArcs of lightning shall splinter stone.\nPlumes of ash shall expose bone.\nThe Days of Parting shall\n\nbegin.\nWhen mother and child will be separate.\nWhen companionship will end as disparate.\nNo friend shall you find upon fleeing.\nNo new dawn will grace you upon leaving.\nNo soothing element shall you be seeing.\nTo those who call themselves believers.\n\nAnd the agents of the Ultimate Judgement heathens.\nKnow you to be afraid, yet dull deceivers.\nOnto yourselves do yourselves do you fool with poor reasons.\nYou will say, \"I believe in the Creator,\" and be content.\nYet the very fact that you fight against\n\nyour own Rapture.\nLeaves the truth being that you reject your own sentence.\nTo be brought forth to your Creator enraptured.\nFor deep within, you know your sins prominent.\nThe Supreme will look down upon you in shame.\nEvoke his name when you are taken by\n\nthe Dominence.\nWhen the Crow's feeding hand is split asunder.\nWhen the capital is captured by surprise.\nWhen the agents of the End of Days plunder.\nTo find the churches empty of worthy prize.\nO' nobles, truly you are of the faithful,\nWhen your convents\n\nlay unadorned and empty.\nRather you parlay in daillances and bellies full.\nWhere is your monies o' gentry.\nThe agents of your Reckoning will not be impeded.\nBy petty guards and cloistering walls.\nWhen we come to inform you of your deeds o' conceited.\n\nYou will rest on knee by His will and laws.\nHe is all-Powerful and you will learn this well.\nWhen the Crow's nest is struck down by the Wyrm.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desc. Leaves", "§bCallax", "-=-=-=-=-=-\n          Descending\n              Leaves\n           =-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nAs the tree grows older, its roots wither and from the lack of nutrient the tree, too, withers. The tree, stiff and hollow, is parched and barren. Its leaves descend, becoming fewer and fewer. Like the leaf, I descend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Misfortune Hunt", "§bThe Misfortune Teller", "Down, down, down you go, gently down to the Grand Tree Inn!\n\n\nUp, Up, Up you go, gently up to the land of beards!\n\nStop now, criminal scum! Behold the almighty stone dwarf!\n\nOver the mountains! Down to the tall forest dwarf tree.\n\nSwim, swim! Follow the water up towards the waterfall with a path behind it!\n\nSwim, Swim! Follow the path, the cave of old.\n\nThe road, the bridge! You see them both, follow the road to the icey land.\n\nBehold! It's cold!\n\nThrough the icey land into the land of hot long vines and tall buildings with green hats.\n\nSTOP! Before you enter the land of green. Turn to the right and follow the path straight, don't move away!\n\nInto the land of strong green people.\n\nFollow the path towards the Holy Temple.\n\nOh No! Prepare to move back to the elven lands.\n\nYou may now meet the weird creature.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fjarriauga", "§bThe Veiled Scribe", "Legends of the Volsung - The Fjarriauga\n\nOf all the tales and legends of the Volsungs, the Fjarriauga are the darkest. In Skjoldier, homeland of the Volsung family, stories of the Fjarriauga are told to scare misbehaving children into submission at night.\n\nThey are said to be wicked ice spirits, taking on the guise of fair and innocent maidens to draw their prey to them. Young boys and girls alike are warned against venturing into the forests where they dwell, lest they are never to be seen again.\n\nIt is said that Kriemhild, the first Fjarriauga, was a woman abandoned at the altar by her betrothed. Broken-hearted she stumbled out into a snowstorm, collapsing amidst the swirling snow and frozen drifts. As she waited for death, Old Father Winter, one\n\nof the Volsung gods, discovered and took pity upon her. He leaned in and gave her the wedding kiss she longed for, transforming her into a vengeful - and powerful - ice spirit.\n\nWhile Fjarriauga are malicious creatures, they are also cunning, powerful and ageless. Many of the greatest seers and fortune-tellers in Skjoldier were Fjarriauga, and were both feared and respected by all. Brave or foolhardy men would often seek them\n\nout, seeking to make use of their talents, powers or insight; although rarely without cost.\n\nHowever, those with a sharp eye who identify a Fjarriauga even through her maiden disguise may secure her aid. Although fickle and cunning creatures, a Fjarriauga is bound to aid those who discover her with a single favour - no more and no less. Such a\n\ntoken should not be squandered nor taken lightly, as although she may be bound to fulfil the favour, it is unwise to earn the ire or wrath of a Fjarriauga.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarf Babies", "§bRosso", "Where do dwarf babies come from?\n\nHave you ever wondered how the dwarven numbers rise? Of course you have, you look at them and think so. The truth is, there are baby dwarves. Quite a statement I know, just think of how a dwarven baby would look like. IIIIUUUUUU, it sounds hairy!!! And\n\nyes... it is very very hairy.\n\nNormal babies come when a man and a woman mate, and after pregnancy a baby is born. Well, if you notice, there are almost no woman dwarves, but I will state why this is further in. The true\n\nways are far more disgusting and frightening than mating can ever be, it is a mixture of ale and hair.\n\nDeep inside the mountains of the dwarven towns, deep underground, are special and greatly guarded rooms. It is in these hidden rooms\n\nthat the baby dwarves are born. I was quite lucky that I found such a room when the guards were fully drunk and had knocked each other out. So I entered the room and by the creator! It smelled worse than the drunks just outside!\n\nIn a room which\n\nseemed filled with puke and ale, there were chunks of what looked like hair. Some of the hair like chunks were even moving. At that time I heard talking just outside the room, and in fear of being discovered, hid myself behind a rock. A dwarf came in,\n\ncompletely drunk and with a knife in his hand. “By Yakemar, ay s’all ‘ave a son!” he shouted before he cut part of his beard.\n\nI watched stunned as this happened, I could never believe a dwarf had cut his own beard, but soon I would know why the dwarves\n\ntreasure their beards so much. Releasing the knife he fell on his knees and coddled the beard near his chest. “Ya will be named Grikot” he said, and that is when it came to me, all those other hair chunks, were in fact part of the beards of other dwarves.\n\nThe dwarf placed the beard chunk down, and picking a bottle, tilted ale over the beard before leaving. So you see dear readers, the dwarves treasure their beard because it is from it that their children will be born from. So where do the small amount of\n\nfemale dwarves come from? As I walked out I realized that one of the chunks was very small, and that the baby could be seen. A female dwarf is born when a dwarf, being far too drunk, doesn’t cut enough of his beard, and as such, the dwarf is born\n\nbeardless, becoming this way, a woman.\n\nNow, onto the types of Dwarves, as you should know, there are cave dwarves, mountain dwarves and forest dwarves. After discovering such intriguing ways of conceiving a child, I searched further\n\nand found out the reasons. Cave dwarves are the ones where the room in inside a deep cave. Mountain dwarves, the cave is dug inside a mountain but it does not go very deep. Both of these type of dwarves, as they were born inside a room by willing\n\ndrunkenness, Forest dwarves are born on the outside, from when the drunkenness is so great, they couldn’t find the room. That is the reason the Forest dwarves are looked down upon from the others, they were not born in the rooms for the beards to be\n\nplaced.\n\nI hope this text has helped the leader to understand the hairy way of dwarf birth.\n\nWhere do Dwarf babies come from\n\nOriginal author unknown\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Moss", "§bDolan Velethen", "Cave Walls moist.\nTorches burning hoist.\n\nThe group traveled\ninnto the unknown?\n\nThis, however, was\nnot an aadventure as\nyou would imagine\n\nThese men were of five year\n\nHumans traversing through school.\n\nThe education was like\nblack moss.\n\nGrowing until mature", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Recipes", "§bRosso", "Sleeping Draught\n\n==================\nWild Lettuce\nWater\n\n>Break leaves from plant\n>Steep leaves 1 hr. in hot water.\n\nBurn/Rash Oiuntment*\n\n==================\nWild Lettuce\n\n>Break leaves from plant\n>Grind leaves into poultice\n>Add water and a whole Wild Lettuce\n*Helps with dry skin\n\nRespitation Potion\n\n==================\nWater\nCaterpillar Fungus\n\n>Grind up fungus\n>Add fungus to heated water, and mix well\n\nHealing Water I\n\n==================\nWater\nLily pad\n\n>Heat up water\n>Cut up Lily Pad and mix with water\n>Pour some in wound\nWARNING:\n    Stings slightly\n\nHealing Water II\n\n==================\nRose\nSpider Eye\nBone\nWater\n\n>Gring up Rose, Spider Eye, and Bone\n>Mix with water that was once snow\n\nHealing water II\n                (Cont’d)\n==================\nLily Pad\nHealing Water II\n\n>Place a few drops in wound\n>Place Lily Pad on wound and bandage\n-If Lily Pad turns brown, it’s healing\n\nPoison\n\n==================\n3 Spider Eyes\n2 Bones\nWater\n\n>Grind up all 3 Spider Eyes\n>Grind up both bones into bonemeal\n>Add both to heated water\n\nPoison II\n\n==================\nPoison I\n2 Spider Eyes\nBone\nRose\nDead Lily Pad\n\n>Grind up Bone, Rose, Spider Eyes, and Lily Pad\n>Mix with Poison I\n\nBone Pain Reliever\n\n==================\nShroom of Immortality\nWater\nLily Pad\n\n>Grind up Shroom of Immortality\n>Gring up Lily Pad\n>Mix together, then add heated water\n\nStomach Pain Reliever\n\n==================\nJelly Ear\nWater\nSugarcane\n\n>Grin up Jelly Ear and mix with heated water\n>Extract sugar from sugarcane, and add to mixture\n\nDraught of Thought\n\n==================\n2 Magic Shrooms\nWater\nWild Lettuce\n\n>Grind Wild Lettuce into a poultice\n>Grind up Magic Shrooms\n>Mix together, then add water, and heat\n\nLimb Pain Reliever\n\n==================\n……. Shroom\nWater\nLily Pad\n\n>Grind up Lily Pad\n>Grind up ……. Shroom\n>Mix together, then add to heated water\n\nEnergy Potion\n\n==================\n2 Cocoa Beans\nSugarcane\nWater\n\n>Grind up Cocoa beans\n>Extract Sugar from Sugarcane\n>Mix together, then add to heated water\n\nEnergy Potion II\n\n==================\n3 Cocoa Beans\n2 Sugarcane\nWater\n\n>Steep Sugarcane in water half an hour\n>Grind up Cocoa beans\n>Get rid of sugarcane, and add Cocoa Beans, ground, to water\n\nPain Reliever\n\n===================\nTippens Root\n\nCopiers note: The book ends here, it is unfinished.\n\nAlchemy Recipes\n\nUnknown Author\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Harbtale Vol.I", "§bOrithur", "A Harbinger's Tale\n\nVolume I\n-------------------\n\nBlessed we were, the brothers and sisters of the Order of the Golden Lance. Our spirits were mighty, our friendship like no other. We served proudly under the\n\nAengul, Xan, and it was our divine duty to seek out the dark creatures of the world that threatened the order and sanctity that we lived to protect.\n\nOne such creature, was the Drakaar known as Setherien. A Drakaar is the\n\ncorrupted version of a Dragaar, a greater dragon. These dragons are capable of thought, speech and extreme power... As we were soon to learn.\n\nSetherien had a sister, and the pair of them resided quietly in a Dwarven ruin. When the dwarves of Asulon\n\nreleased the pair, they managed to slay the sister, but Setherien himself, as a fledgling, escaped. Our Order recognised the threat and sought to end it before the corrupted greater dragon could bring further harm to the world.\n\nNine. Nine of the Order were chosen to track down the beast. One of these nine being myself. We hunted the creature across many lands and encountered many struggles along the way, years passed before we finally discovered the hiding place of the Drakaar\n\nin the frozen North of the land soon to be known as 'Anthos'. We waited, observed, and planned carefully, we could not feel more prepared to attack, and so we did...\n\nThe Drakaar slew us all within minutes. I watched the determination fade\n\nfrom the dying faces of my brothers and sisters as the unholy creature laughed over our bloodied bodies. Our long journey seemed over with such a hopeless anticlimax, and if we could have known what was to come, we would all have gladly fallen upon our\n\nown swords before the search for Setherien even began.\n\nFor you see, Setherien did not kill us. He enslaved the Nine of us as his immortal servants. We became Setherien's Harbingers... And soon the mortal races found Anthos, and\n\nSetherien's revenge was to be dealt through us, the people that had sought to protect them.\n\nUpon the corruption of our bodies and minds, we became imbued with a power over dragonfire and frost, as well as the ability to corrupt the\n\nfallen into withering, charred skeletons to act as Setherien's footsoldiers, and we his Dark Leuitenants.\n\nBut we did not see ourselves as slaves. The Harbingers gladly obeyed their master, and all memory of our past lives became but a distant dream,\n\nblurred and unclear. We were taught to ignore it, but I didn't. I became obsessed with these memories that didn't seem to belong to me. I served loyally under Setherien, but the doubt was planted.\n\nEach of us bore the same black and blue robes of a\n\nfreezing aura, with only our differing helms and visors to identify us as individuals.\n\nWe became willing icons of fear, and the more we served under Setherien, the more distant our past selves seemed to become...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Charred Book", "§bUnknown", "10th of the Grand Harvest:\n\n I have returned to Sarrowglek from the Lone Mountain to gather some supplies. I shall be traveling back shortly.\n\n11th of the Grand Harvest:\n\n We are sharing an encampment with the Uruks. They are surprisingly courteous, allowing us to share this place with them for now. \n Now, as I am settled in, I shall\n\ntake the time to describe my settings. \n Our encampment is on the edge of a forest, near several great trees. The Orcs have set up wooden pallisades around a small encampment.\nOutside the wall lies several tents\n\nand a campfire.\n To our west lies a great door, carved into a mountain. There, most of the action is, however the Dwarves have disallowed anyone to near the door. Plus, a quiet area to settle in is nay a bad idea.\n Down the road\n\nlies two great Dwarven Statues, of two dwarves holding a shield and a torch. They are magnificent to behold.\n\n11th of the Grand Harvest Part 2:\n\n Rumors have spread of the Dwarves attacking the Orc Encampment, however I doubt they are true.\n In the meantime, both Waldenians and Uruks alike\n\nshare tales around the campfire, /this/ is what Mar's end goal is, I know this for sure now. A world where this is not an uncommon occurence, and where it applies to /all/ races, not just the Orcs and Waldenians.\n\n11th of the Grand Harvest Part 3:\n\n The rest of Mar has arrived, including the Valkelm. Nothing much else to record.\n\n11th of the Grand Harvest Part 4:\n\n The Dwarves claim Khorvad, or Iblees, lies behind the doors. I fear this is true.\n\n11th of the Grand Harvest Part 5:\n\n Doors remain close, however I sense this shall not be so for long. Creator help us if the rumors are true.\n\n12th of the Grand Harvest:\n\n Much has happened since I last wrote. The door opened, revealing an ancient Magi, possibly from Rivel...? The mage warned of Harvesters, beasts that would slay us\n\nall. Right on queue, a pair of Harvester Golems dove out of the rubble, and began slaughtering us. Many died to them, but some did survive long enough to fell the monstrosities.\n We discovered a passageway which the Harvesters\n\nmust have come from. Hardly a passage though, it was a river of lava with stalagmites reaching above.\n After much climbing and scrambling, we reached what seemed to be a Dwarven city. The spirit of Magnis Goldhand warned\n\nus not to enter, but, of course, we ignored him. If only we had heeded his words. \n We searched the city for a key to open a great door in the northern wing of the city. After much searching, we found out.\n\n On the other side lay a witch of Rivel. She put up quite the fight, proving more devastating than the Harvester Golems. However, I survived her onslaught. Now, outside the door to what I hope to be the final room, I write this.\n\n13th of the Grand Harvest:\n\n The door has been opened, in front of us lays a great puzzle. The Dwarves are working to decipher it.\n\n14th of the Grand Harvest:\n\n We have been fools, we have been such stupid fools. The Dwarves activated the mechanism, only to wish they hadn't. Now, we are locked in here indefinitely.  Wait, something is\n\nhappening... Creator save us, it's him! The Betrayor has retur-\n\n*The book seems to suddenly end here, blood spattered all over the page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lesson 1", "TwilightWolf9012", "Elven lesson one: History\nIn the days of old, the ancient elves, our ancestors, spoke a language that is rumored to have been veiled in mystery and magic. Some tell tales of the tongue of elves having the power to control certain aspects of nature\n\nitself like guiding the growth of trees and triggering the migration of animals.\nAlthough it is mostly unknown why our language disappeared so quickly, it is speculated that a tabboo was placed on it, and is slowly vanished from our culture. Elven\n\nscholars, however, have begun to unearth the fragments of our language, and have begun to piece them together. It is our hope that by educating the elven people with what has been recovered of our tongue, that we may revive what has been lost by time.\n\nAs you read on, eager student, be wary that the language takes much time and effort to master. \nLesson 1: Greetings\n\nIf you have lived in Malinor for a while, the common elven greetings are used very frequently. The two most common are\n\nKarin'ayla and Ker'ayla. When translated into common, Karin'ayla means 'good day' and Ker'ayla means 'good evening' or 'good night'. However, one may notice that when these greetings are translated directly into common, they are structured\n\ndifferently. For example, Karin'ayla literally means 'day good'. This is because in the elven language, modifiers of the word are placed /after/ the word being described and seperated with an apostrophe. The same concept applies to the greeting Ker'ayla,\n\nwhich would literally mean 'evening good' or 'night good'.\nOur most common farewell in elven is Van'ayla, which means 'farewell'.\nWhen pronouncing these greetings and farewells, it is important that the apostrophe indicates just a slight pause in\n\nspeech. The words, with much practice, should roll of the tongue with ease.\nFor review, the words listed in this lesson are...\nKarin'ayla-Good day\nKer'ayla-Good evening\nVan'ayla-Farewell\n\nPractice these with patience, and study\n\nthe word structure carefully, as both pronunciation and understanding of sentence and word structure is an absolute staple when learning the language.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blockades", "§bJerry_Man", "Mental Defence\n\n\nInformation not for public consumption\n\nTo begin with you must recognise when an unwelcomed presence has taken residence within your mind. Those who delve in minds know well how to go undetected, so you must recognise the signs. Firstly comes the subtle feeling that you are not alone.\n\nSuch feelings tend to come in the night, when the candles have worked their way to snuff and the distant sounds of rustling cooperating with the dancing shadows to create ghostly apparitions within your imaginings. That sensitivity to space that rises in\n\nsituations most troubling in which your skin seems able to feel the open air, bringing with it the confidence that you are indeed alone, and that sleep should no longer evade you. It is such sensitivity to your physical surroundings that arises when your\n\nthoughts are occupied by more than yourself. Secondly is recognising thoughts that seem unfamiliar to you. One's own mind works in certain patterns that are as unique to them as a language is to a race. Familiarising yourself with the way that you\n\nthink can prove neccessary in determining the invasive thoughts of others. Not just in moments of cerebral invasion, but also in the morbid agreement with the doubts of others. Such concepts that are outside your own considering are a\n\nvirus upon your positive imaginings. But such is a digression. Thirdly is the most obvious, the experiencing of visions and the hearing of voices that are not the product of your own consciousness. If the invasive mind has gotten so far as for\n\nyou to witness such things, it may already be too late to resist them.\n\nResistance is a purposeful action. At any moment of awareness that your mind may no longer be a place of solitude, one should employ a simple avoidance technique. Preoccupy your thoughts upon one thing. Prepare this thing within your mind during\n\npersonal meditation so that it can be called upon at a moments notice. If a secondary presence exists within your mind, you should experience their attempts to work around this barrier. Most likely they will attempt purely to distract you so that\n\nyour purposeful thought slips away, if even for a moment, that they might continue unimpeded.\n\nYou may attempt to rehearse this simple barrier such that it become impenetrable even to emotional blackmail or physical distraction. But do not expect to keep out all intruders with a simple fence. For they are like the fox that seeks out a hole,\n\nthat they might have their feast upon the innocent poultry of your thoughts.\n\nThe Best Defence that one can have is trickery. If you are sure that your thoughts are not solitary, and the other party is indeed working to belittle your wall, you must protect that which is most sacred. Do NOT think upon the thoughts or memories\n\nthat you old most secretly. Keep them far from your mind, and instead, lead your mind through a series of thoughts that you beleive the other party most wanting to see. If needs be, invent the image that they seek as though you were dreaming.\n\nFabricate the vision, re-invent the thought. Lead your mind through patterns that are safe, and all the while fein defeat.\n\nThere are some skilled minds in our world that know well how to push the consciousness. If they remain convinced that no foul play\n\nis in action, they may be appeased at their own ability to search through your mind, and release their attachment with your consciousness. Never knowing that your trickery has left you guarded.", ""),
        StaticBook("Whitestorm Ck.Bk", "SapphireShard", "Baking with The\n      Whitestorms\n\n\n  Some of the family's\n   favorite recipes.\n\n\n\n         James\n      Whitestorm\n\n\n\n\nVolume One:\n               Cakes\n\nBasic Cake \n----------\nServes an entire party. Prepare long in advance, and douse in brandy to prevent mold.\n\nIngredients\n-----------\n1 lb Oat Flour\n1 lb Egg\n1 lb Sugar\n\nIngredients Contd.\n-----------------\n1 lb Butter\n1/2 Cup Candied Orange Peel\n1/2 Cup Candied Lemon Peel\n1/2 Cup Candied Citron\n1/3 Cup Currants\n1/2 Cup Almond Flour\n1 Tsp Nutmeg\n1 Tsp Mace\n1 1/2 Tsp Cinnamon\n\nIngredients Contd.\n-----------------\n1 Tsp Ginger\n1 Tsp Cloves\n1/4 Cup Sherry\n1/4 Cup Brandy\n\nDirections\n---------\n1. Heat stove to adequate temperature. Grease a 10 inch pan in preparation.\n\nDirections Contd.\n---------------\n2. Beat the butter in a bowl until creamy. Add the sugar and beat until fluffy. Stir at a medium speed while gradually adding in egg, until thoroughly combined.\n3. Sift the Oat Flour in a seperate bowl. -\n\nDirections Contd.\n---------------\n3. - Add the spices and almond flour. Add the mixture gradually to the butter, sugar, and eggs, while stirring. Continue stirring until thoroughly mixed.\n4. Add the brandy and sherry to the batter and mix.\n\nDirections Contd.\n---------------\n5. Pour the batter into the pan, and spread it evenly. Bake until a knife can come out clean. Allow cooling for half an hour.\n6. Invert the pan onto a plate, then onto a cooling rack. Allow even more cooling.\n\n*The rest of the pages contain dozens more recipes, for almost every type of cake one would need.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Karma", "§bIsengar Brockfall", "The breeze flew into the deserted inn.\nThe doors slammed shut every minute, whilst the inn keeper kept his elbow onto the counter and his hand pushed onto his face people were looking in and running off.\n\n\"COM' 'N 'ERE\" he would shout.\nBut they got too scared and ran off into the distance.\n\nHe would glance out the dirty window, looking at the sky until it fades dark.\nHe would then blow out the candles, put on his brown coat and walk\n\nhome.\nHe would always hide the key under the inn mat.\n\n\"'Lo Isengar\" they would say when he stumbled into Gimblewood.\nIsengar was never the social person so he often grumbled or moaned and kept to\n\nhimself.\nAs he jammed in his silver key into his burrow he would sit down on his hand made wooden chair.\nYou could count his personal items in a matter of seconds.t\n\n1) 2 wooden spoons\none for eating and the other one for stiring stew.\n\n2) A small handmade wooden chair with a tied on cotton pillow.\n\n3) A dusty desk with old books on it stacked Alphebetically.\n\n4) An old mattress that has yellow stains on it.\n\n5) A bucket full of dirty water with old socks in it.\n\n6) A small wardrobe\n\n7) Knives and forks\n\nAs much as Isengar seemed like he was poor from the way his house was, he was actually very rich.\nHe was very tight with his money.\n\nHe always seemed to have money in his pockets or in the bank.\nPeople teased him saying \"Yer go' 'ny dust 'n t'em notes?\"\n\nHe would sit on his chair smoking a pipe looking out his window.\nHe would then prepare his favourite food:\n\nA roast pork stew with some seasoning.\nHe would stir the stew until it is brown, thick and gooey.\nWhere the meat is soft and tender.\nAfter his large meal he would wash it down with some Carrot juice that he squishes with a circular cutted log.\n\nThen he would go straight to his wardrobe and pull out his Light blue PJ's.\n\nThen he would go bed.\n\nOne day Isengar got up at about 5:30 which gives him time to prepare the meals for his inn.\n\nAs Isengar slowly got out his bed stretching his arms and yawning with a glum look on his face he would get changed into his coffe stained shirt.\n\nHe would then then put on his black trousers and head to work.\n\nIsengar glanced out\n\nhis window, and noticed it was pouring with rain.\n\"Hmph\" he grumbled.\n\nHe would slip on his coat and wander outside.\nHe would take a right to head out of Gimblewood.\n\n\"Mornin' Mr Brockfall\" one of the Halflings smiled.\nIsengar gave him a fake smile and headed out.\n\"Feckin' humbug\" he whispered as he passed him.\n\nHe arrived at the inn at last the rain started to quieten down Isengar started to relax.\nHe made himself a mug of Vincenzo Ale slurping at every sip.\n\nSoon an odd man walked in with a red robe and had a strange look on his\n\nface.\n\n\"What ca' a'h get yer?\"\n\n\"Nothing\" he replied\n\nIsengar looked at him with a confused and solid look on his face.\n\n\"T'en ge' out yer stuped feck\" he shouted.\n\n\"Now. Now no need to get feisty little one\" he smirked.\n\nIsengar started to calm.\n\n\"Yer obviously 'ave a'h reason ter com' 'ere a'h s'pose?\"\n\n\"Aye\" the man said.\n\n\"T'en tell me'h or ah'll...\"\nIsengar threatened but was interupted by the man.\n\n\"You should learn to give your money away young man!\"\nhe smiled.\n\n\"A'h can do what a'h w'unt wit' me money yer cunt\" arthur growled.\n\n\"Aye, you can but perhaps you should learn to give some away to your fellow Halflings.\"\n\n\"'o do yer t'ink ye ar' tellin' me wot ter do wit' me mon'eh?\"\n\nI am Karma\n\nIsengar ignored his pathetic speech, and carried on cleaning his counter with a ragged cloth.\n\nLater on when Isengar finished work he noticed a man sitting on the side of the road.\nWhen Isengar passed the man gripped his\n\ntrousers and asked for money, Isengar refused to give his money away to a peasant.\n\n\"Ge'h a'h job yer pesant\" he shouted.\n\nThe man looked down at the dirty pavement in sorrow.\n\nIsengar walked off to Gimblewood.\nAs he came in he noticed his house had a big sign out front, as he read the sign aloud it said:\n\n\"Dear Mr.Isengar, a'hm afrai' we'h kickin' yer out. Yer see Gimblewood 's a'h community, we'h shar'\n\nour stoof, so be packed by tomorro'.\"\n\nIsengar was furious, he kicked the sign over in rage.\nAnd went over to Milo's house.\n\"Yer feckin' cunt, yer can't kic' ma'h out!!!\"\n\nMilo chuckled \n\"Isengar calm dow'\" he said in a calm voice.\n\"CALM DOW' EY? YER FECKIN' KICKIN' MA'H OU'!!!!\"\n\"A'h can see why yer angr'eh, but unti' yer learn ter shar' yer shite t'en yer ain't comin' back!\"\n\nAs Isengar stomped back into his house grabbing and throwing things about.\nHe packed anything important like food etc.\n\nSo as Isengar was knocking things off the shelf into his small handmade bag he panicked of where he was going to stay.\n\n\"'n inn perhaps\" he muttered.\nIsengar peeked under his chair and grabbed his bag of 200 minas.\n\nIsengar opened his burrow door and slung his bag's over his shoulder.\nHe took the silver key out his pocket and looked at it for a\n\nmoment, then he extended his arm back and threw it forward letting go of the key it plopped into the lake and sunk into the soil.\n\nIsengar had his head down with a glum look on his face, the other Halflings giggled as he stumbled out of Gimblewood.\n\nIsengar walked down the road to Petrus.\nHe was blinded by the light when he was out of the trees.\nSquinting his eyes he made out a figure on the end of the bridge.\nIsengar Huffed realising who it was!\n\nIt was the Old man, he smiled at Isengar laughing.\nA sudden voice came to Isengar's head.\n\"Had enough yet, small one?\" The voice giggled.\nIsengar did not reply but instead shook his head.\n\nThe man smiled with an evil grin.\n\nSuddenly the rain started to fall from the clouds!\n\n\"'S t'is Karma too yer cunt!?\"\nThe man started to chuckle.\n\n\"No, That's just the weather\" he says politley.\n\n((PART 2 WILL COME OUT SOON))", ""),
        StaticBook("Whitestorm Ck.Bk", "§bRosso", "Baking with the\n      Whitestorms\n  Some of\nThe family’s\n    Favorite recipes.\n             James\n\n       Whitestorm\n\n\n\nVolume One:\n               Cakes\n\nBasic Cake\n----------\nServes an entire party. Prepare long in advance, and douse in brandy to prevent mold.\n\nIngredients\n----------\n1 lb Oat Flour\n1 lb Egg\n1 lb Sugar\n1 lb butter\n½ cup Candied OrangePeel\n½ cup Candied Lemon Peel\n½ cup Candied Citron\n1/3 Cup Currants\n\nIngredients Contd.\n----------\n½ Cup Almond Flour\n1 Tsp Nutmeg\n1 Tsp Mace\n1 ½ Tsp Cinnamon\n1 Tsp Ginger\n1 Tsp Cloves\n¼ Cup Sherry\n¼ Cup Brandy\n\nDirections\n----------\n1. Heat stove to adequate temperature. Grease a 10 inch pan in preparation.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n2. Beat the butter in a bowl until creamy. Add sugar and beat until fluffy. Stir at a medium speed while gradually adding in egg, until thoroughly combined.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n3. Sift the Oat Flour in a separate bowl. Add the spices and almond flour. Add the mixture gradually to the butter, sugar, and eggs, while stirring. Continue stirring until thoroughly mixed.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n4. Add the brandy and sherry to the batter and mix.\n5. Pour the batter into the pan, and spread it evenly. Bake until a knife can come out clean. Allow cooling for half an hour.\n\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n6- Invert the pan onto a plate, then onto a cooling rack. Allow even more cooling.\n\nWhitestorm cook book\n\nWritten by James Whitestorm\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_ASUL_5(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("My Wish", "§bPhaedrus'Yar", "I wish for a metal to work with. One not known to any smith before me. More powerful than any metal known.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Affliction", "§bInforum Populi", "The Affliction\n\n\n   \"Eyes and ears\n      everywhere.\"\n\nThe contents of this book are not fiction, but facts we have to face.\n\nDuring a stay in Malinor I came across something rather unusual. There was a deranged man who stabbed a guard locked away. Another man, not sure the name but he was bearing a black robe. Under this robe he wore chainmail.\n\nThis robed man tried talking the guards into releasing the man for an unknow reason. I later learn this imprisoned man is named 'Fyre'. As I grow curious so do the guards, attempting to search this robed man asking questions.\n\nHe revealed the his\n\nchainmail and when asked to remove it, he left the city. As he did this I trailed.\n\nHe noticed a man on the road leading away from Malinor, he stopped to talk to him. He said Fyre had sent him, the man seemed angry.\n\nIt sounded like the robed man addresed his 'friend' by /Corvo/. The man denys the accusation, claiming how Corvo is a varsele to these lands (Is this man Corvo in disguise?). The robed man looks confused, asking him \"Why would Fyre lie to me?\"\n\nThe one claimed to be Corvo got angered further, saying that he test the patience of a 'demi god'. \n\n- I remained hidden in the trees, making sure to make not a noise.-\n\nThe robed man swears his life to the 'demi god.' The man claiming\n\nthat it was a dark art and asking why he wish it upon himself. \n\nAnother man approaches seeming to know the 'demi god.' He asks who the robed man is. The 'demi god' tells the robed man to provide him death telling him to draw his sword.\n\nHe orders a deathmatch between the two, and the fighting goes on. Both fighters showing great prowess with a sword. \n\nThe fight ends as the robed man is stabbed in the shoulder, forced to back off. The other, providing mercy and telling him\n\nto leave and seek aid. The 'demi god' orders him to stay, as so he does. He slithered over to the winner, placing his hand on the back of his neck. He proceeds to tell him how he had provided his use, and that he had done well with the tasks he was given.\n\nThe 'demi god' AKA corvo AKA the man approached by the robed man said, \"Sadly, the lords do not want you to become apart of us.\" and with that he sent a jolt of electricity through the winner.\n\nThe 'demi god' then approaches the\n\nwounded, robed man. Offering a hand of aid. He brings the injured man close and whispers some things in his ear before releasing him and striding off towards Malinor. \n\nThe robed man approaches the corpse, raising his\n\nsword as high as he can, he brings it down in a mighty swing, severing the mans head from his body. He clenches the bloody head by the hair and chased after the 'demi god.'\n\nI then called it a day, packing up and heading off to bring\n\nyou this story of something that is plaguing our world as we know it.\n\nCheck around for more valuable information from the Inforum Populi. \n\n((None of this info is meta'd. If you'd like proof contact --\n\nBenben582))", ""),
        StaticBook("Shaman and Uruk", "§bVulnir Velulaei", "Spirit - A manifestation used by Shamans. Not always Uruk. Some might be captured Aengul or Daemons.\n\nA spirit's personality can affect its physical form. Example: Elphaba's earth spirit takes on the form of a fox. Probably a sign of slyness.\n\nUruk height - Depends on type of Uruk. Gobo, Uruk, Olog.\n\nGoblins are the size of humans. \n\nUruk are roughly 8-9ft tall.\n\nOlog - Giant, very strong but very, very stupid.\n\nUruk who live with outsiders are considered whitewash.\n\nThese Uruk disgrace their ancestors and are generally weaker than the average Uruk.\n\nSize means nothing if they fight like a big Uruk.\n\nEnhrok - Spirit of blood.\n\nAnkrus - Spirit of the sea.\n\n(Note: Shaman interviewed turned his staff into a red snake.)", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "Eenhoornheid", "§+§+§\n   Introduction     to Hydromancy\n\n    by Ev Ar'ahern\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nW§§§§§§§§§§§§ater: seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of live, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike.ust as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbinger of eradication.\n\nDespite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromance yearns to wield.\n\n A hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from the ability to\n\ncontrol \"mana,\" but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is difficult\n\nto put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it become more simpler tasks.\n\nMany mages use a staff when evoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for instance, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of of some of the\n\n properties that is possesses, and also because it has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from.When the water is pulled forth, it forms a stream from\n\n the end of my staff that maintains itself midair. From here, I can move it, project is somewhere, or allow it to dissipate.\n\nO§gne thing about water evocation that differs from the other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world.  Novice water evocationists begin with controlling pure water in its liquid form.\n\nAs a hydromancer becomes more skilled ((approximately late tier 3)), he is able to change the water into ice. ce is much more suited for battle and defence than liquid water is, as it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block oncoming\n\nprojectiles, as a form of short-distance defense, and as a method of harming others. I have personally mastered a technique of blasting an enemy with water, and then freezing them in their tracks should they be hit.\n\nMagical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from the heat of the sun or a torch. To break void ice, the hydromance must either completely lose concentration, or another magemust do something to break the ice\n\n(i.e. a pyromancer melts the ice with magical flames). Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as the wisps of steam are too difficult for even the most trained evocationists to control.\n\nW§ ater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin", "Eenhoornheid", "The High Prince\n     of Malinor\n      and the\n Story of Laurelin\n\n by Anonymous Druid\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin'evaral, the Enclave of Haelun'or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir'Indor Lelien\n\nA powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities in the First Age came to Aegis to help the Monks of the Cloud Temple and a few surviving families at the coming of the Second Age. An aspirational Wood Elf referred to as Native was amoung the\n\nsurviving colony of Wood Elves during this time and he sought to use his knowledge of creating homes within treetops to protect those who were hoped to return to their soulstones at the Aegis Temple after freat war.\n\nThe Wood Elf sought the Druid, and found him near the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple. They set off on foot to a mountain gorge he had come across that would act as a natural barrier to potential foe's. Once they arrived, the Druid\n\nwandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch on his hip every so often and scratching at his head before dropping a seed. He showed Native the seeds within the pouch which have a very similar shine to glowstone.\n\nWhilst Native's guild of builders were creating the city's wall and pathways, the old Druid continued to walk along and casually drop the seeds in areas with his gnarled brook in-hand. In a matter of moments, trees begun to grow exponentially!\n\nIt seemed as though the trees grew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above them. A wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similar glowstone glow. Bits of dust swirled down from\n\nthe treetops and faded away near the forest floor.\n\nThere was still however, a large clearing in the center of the grove.\n\"This, of course, is for the Mother Tree.\",\nthe Druid exclaimed. He then grabbed a bit of parchment from his\n\nsatchel and looked over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid walked to the center of the clearing, and began to cast a powerful spell upon one of the seeds. Leaves suddenly whirled around him for short moment and fell to the ground. The tree's\n\ntrunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. Native was rather frightened when he saw this, hoping the Druid hadn't casted the spell incorrectly. As the Mother Tree grew to its final height, he saw a small opening halfway up the tree.\n\nLow and behold, the Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming, \"This is where a stone altar shall lay.\".\n\nOnce the rest of the smaller trees were done growing the builders guild and Native climbed up the trees with packs of\n\nwooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become one of the Finest Cities of Malinor and to think it had all begun with just a pouch of seeds and a pinch of Druid Magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Order", "§bRespirin", "The Druidic Order\n     Volume 1\n\n     By Wayward\n    Druid Respirin\n\n\n Druids divide Aegis into domains, defined by the mountains the rivers, the sea and the land.\n\n- The Circles -\nAll Druids within a domain are within a circle, named for the area the domain occupies, or sometimes it's founder or the druid's worship.\nThe members of a circle hold themselves responsible for the well-being of the\n\nwilderness and the continuation of the orderly cycles of Nature within their domain.\n\nA few traditions chapter have grown up to govern the harmonious workings of a circle: initiations, the challenge, the ban, the moot, and selection of acolytes. All druids, from the humblest initiate to the great druid,\n\nmay freely follow their own interpretation of druidic beliefs and act however they believe best serves Nature.\n\n- Circles and Branches-\nThere are often different branches of druid's in a circle forest druids, plains, mountain, desert and arctic druids...etc.\n\n-Initiates-\nThe cornerstones of the druidic order faith. faith. They normally live in stone, wood, or mud-brick cottages and act as the protectors of a tract of wilderness or a sacred grove.\n\n-The Inner Circle-\nThe inner circle contains nine of druid rank, three archdruids, and a single great druid. To enter the inner circle one must be experienced, a vacancy must open up,\n\nor the rising druid must be victorious over another in the druidic challenge .\n\n- Druids -\nA circle never has more than nine druids, though Initiates are often known as Druids too. Using druidic resources they agressively root out emergent threats to the wilderness within a domain. Druids attend the High Council of the Moot, and act\n\nbased on the needs of the circle as a whole. Serving as a mentor takes up much of druid's time, too. It is their responsibility to initiate new druids into the Order.\n\n- Archdruids -\nEach circle can have only three archdruids and, as with the druid rank, advancement requires either filling a vacancy or winning a challenge against a seated archdruid. An archdruids role resembles that of a druid, with two differences.\n\nArchdruids concern themselves more with maintaining the balance of Nature, making sure no one alignment or ethos comes to utterly dominate the domain. Also, archdruids spend time training to step into the role of the great druid.\n\nTo accomplish both these goals, they devote much time to travel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Zeviars Wish ;)", "§bZevíar Frøydís", "\"My most wanted thing has always been a flame book!\" \n\n-Zeviar Froydis", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "§bLori Oathcast", "Long Range Translocation Device Investigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from Archmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockets within the void to place objects and a --->\n\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the void, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the original void translocationist present. The void translocationist must --->\n\n- then re-locate himself and in the area he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stay open when powered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Recipes", "§bconnor428", "Table of Contents:\n\nPg. 2: Mending Potion\nPg. 3: Strength Potion\nPg. 4: Potion of Night V.\nPg. 5: Poison\nPg. 6: Nausea Poison\n\nMending Potion:\n\n1x Serpent's Stalk\n1x Tippen's Root\n1x Water\n\nThis potion heals minor cuts of the user. Can be poured into small wounds or consumed. After consumption, the user felt a slight bit weak.\n\nStrength Potion:\n\n1x Miner's Helmet\n1x Flame Tongue\n1x Goblin's Ivy\n1x Water\n\nPotion gives the user strength for a very short amount of time. WARNING: This thing kicks like a mule!!!\n\nPotion of Night Vision\n\n1x Egg\n1x Swamp Blossom\n1x Water\n\nAllows user to see in almost pitch black. However, he may find that he has trouble when mining minerals as he will have a bit of fatigue.\n\nPoison:\n\n1x Spider Eye\n\nIt's poison. Does anything else even need to be said?\n\nNausea Poison:\n\n1x Rotten Flesh\n1x Goblin's Ivy\n1x Water\n\nIt's like poison. But it makes you hungry and nauseaus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Limerick", "§bMonk Scribe", "There once was a halfling named Fime\nWho could cook a stew worth a dime\nAn orc came one night\nAnd paid for the sight\nOf Fime in a pot with some thyme\n\n- Author unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mukars wish.", "§bSage Ju'Mukar", "----------------------------------------Ju'Mukar wish to Metztli\n----------------------------------------=========================----------------------------------------Mukar is not one to make demands from the holy mother, but if Metztli you recieve\n\nthis. Mukar wishes for a nice new elegant staff to be made. A long wooden one with many pointy edges along the shaft of it to attach many oddities, then a large lapis crystal at the tip.\n\nMul'ta Metztli awnd Sa'vi.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bastion of Light", "§bGungnir", "Above the land that screams damnation\n\n   Lies a temple of holy salvation\n\n   I remain dormant, peaceful sleeping\n\n   For one to take my piece for keeping", ""),
        StaticBook("Homework", "§bIndra Tresery", "\"I will walk the forest with my new kin.\"\n\nMy new kin, the rest of the Druid Order. A recognition of the those within the Order becoming apart of me and myself apart of them.\n\n\"I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me.\"\n\nI believe this just means that I promise to never withhold any truths.\n\n\nAs the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need.\"\n\n<The Aspects watch over us (The Order) so I pledge to do the same to thos in need.>\n\n\"I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk approaches.\"\n\n<A promise to uphold the Orders duties despite how bleak the outcome may seem.>\n\n\"I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\"\n\n<Straightforward, a promise to keep loyal to their duties and the order.>", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Magic", "AxMaynard", "A book of research into Arcane Magic. It's useless for teaching. but it contains lots of notes of research into how the Void worls, how the Voide can be damaged, and the side-effects of channeling power. It may be of interest to a powerful wizard.\n\nThe text looks to be written recently and along the pages are some ink smudges.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Falling...", "§bMonk Scribe", "The Falling of our World\n\nIn Aegis, all across the lands,\nThe Undead are making a stand.\nTheir power shown, the taint comes forth,\nit started spreading from the north.\n\nIn Al'Khazar they\n\nshowed it first,\nUndead power at its worst.\nThe city wrecked, many struck dead,\nThe King kidnapped, the people fled.\n\nThe northern cities also gone,\nCelestine and New Alstion,\nCrimson Vale, last\n\nWinterfell,\nThey stand now as empty shells.\n\nThe gaze of the Undead then turned,\nTo Alras, as we quickly learned.\nAgain a long and bloody fight,\nThe Undead try to prove their might.\n\nAlras fell to gas and flame,\nDefenders should not feel ashamed.\nTheir fight back was long and brave,\nBut Alras just could not be saved.\n\nThe Gauntlet struck, the lava flowed,\nA portal from the taint arose,\n\nLaurelin, attacked by Ghasts,\nDefenders stop their fires fast.\n\nThe taint transforms New Terriko,\nThe Undead strikes a mighty blow.\nBut defenders inflict pain,\nThe Undead there is quickly slain.\n\nIn Galahar, they strike as well,\nBut the monsters are quickly felled.\nThere is no overwhelming taint,\nNo gas that makes the people faint.\n\nResistance to the Undead grows,\nIn each attack it clearly shows.\n\nAegeans all protect their land,\nAre they gaining the upper hand?\n\nThough Human cities fall to Blight,\nThey have not given up the fight.\nThe Elves too are still full of strength,\nFighting the Undead to great lengths.\n\nThe Dwarves stand strong from underground,\nTheir defences are most sound.\nThe Orcs shout 'skah you' to Undead,\nPutting on pikes their rotten heads.\n\nDifferent, but still much the same,\nAll races share each\n\nother pain.\nIf Aegis can all fight as one,\nThe Undead surely will be done.\n\nBut if... if we fail to unite...\nWe will surely lost this fight.\n\n- Written by Josef Timothee in Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 2", "§bArinislia", "Elven Lessons 2\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\n\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in Elven are as follows:\n\nKae-Me\nNae-You\nLae-He/Him\nHae- She/Her\nLye-We\n(used to speak of Elves, people, or\n\nworld)\n\nfor example, the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (he fared well).\n\nIn addition to this, other good languages supplements to\n\nanyone learning Elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail of form critical grammatical structures in a sentence. The dash denotes location of a seed word. Affixes and seed words are seperated by an apostrophe.\n\nac-(aca-) - Honorific for accursedness\n\nah-(ahe-) Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholar.\nEx.: Ah'Lucion\n\nfi- New or anew\n\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) -Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. Ex. : Cer'Silir\n\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n\n-ento (-nto) - Next\n\n-onn - from or born\n\nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive\n\n-ir -purpose\n\n-sae - The spreading, development, or management\n\n-ii - deminuitive form\n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Khodvra's Wishes", "§bLucien Dreden Tundrak", "60-70% Carbarum Battleaxe,Sharpness 1, Unbreaking 2, Thorns 2.\n\nAny Carabum weapon really...", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "§bJistuma", "Is this what the druid college is like…? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I’m a druid for some reason… It’s as if they’re brainwashed.\n\nThey think I’m an elf, too! I’m a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She’s also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe…? I’m just jotting down notes… And my thoughts… And why is this\n\n happening!? So, what do write now. I don’t even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I’ve been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact… It’s a magical artifact from\n\nWinterfall that the undead want. Now it’s in the hands of one named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It’s from the Kar’Lani tribe, and is hidden in the “fake father of Al’Kazaar”. It’s cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books\n\nwritten by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact.\n\nI’ve been living in Al’Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al’Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went to Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while.\n\nBut then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of course. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me\n\nenough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us or something. He kept on saying we were elven and druids, which neither of us were.\n\nBell’s human and I’m a dwarf. And I don’t think either of us would want to study druidism after this… Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it.Er, not it. Us. He tried to break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house.\n\n We found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I’ll go back to Al’Khazaar… but I’ll write about the next adventure.\n\nI went to go to Al’Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell’s help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell disappeared. I still don’t know where she is. We continued on the path, along with\n\n an orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and died.\n\nA while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fin at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits. The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil bandit.\n\nIt’s obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al’Khazaar didn’t even notice. He, along with the rest of the human royalty,\n\nis just STUPID. There’s no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn’t even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point…no. Untrue. Just untrue.\n\nAnyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. Everyone thought he was a pale orc, even thought he’s admitted to be undead many times. The fools… the idiots, the fools… I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead came.\n\nHe even used the same tequique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponents. The fools… no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on…\n\nI would write more about my life, but I realize I just don’t know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can’t let people know of my feelings or all my thoughts. That’s pretty much all of my life so far that I\n\ncare to share.\n\nDruidism\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("True Prosperity", "Terafir", "There was once a town, a peaceful one, led by a grand leader, strong and wise. He used his power to bring prosperity to his town, through both freedom and oppression.\nOne day, a man walked through the town, for he believed that only he knew the secret to\n\ntrue, everlasting prosperity. He requested to see the leader, many, many times. Eventually, the leader submitted to the man's request.\nThe man gave the leader a speech, upon how if he was such a great leader, and such a knowledgeable man, why not take\n\ncontrol of the town, show them all how it is done, and give the profits back to the people?\nThe leader thought this made sense, as everyone did tell him he was an excellent judge of character.\nHe took control of the city's housing and working buildings,\n\nshowing them all how to work more efficiently, work longer, and in the end, he promised to them that they would get their worth back.\nThe workers thought this was a bit odd, after all, he did seize their homes as well. But, they trusted in him, and\n\nbelieved that he knew what was best for all of them.\nSoon after, the people, tired and angry from working with no profits, turned upon their leader, as he was using the money to fund himself.\nThe leader, recognizing what he had done, listened to\n\nthe people.\nThe people demanded that he succeed all power to them, the entire decision making process. He accepted, with one condition: he wanted to keep his previous money and house.\nThe people agreed, and he willingly handed over power to them.\n\nBut as time went on, it became apparent that something else was wrong now. \nNothing ever got done. The townspeople bickered over every tiny detail, all disagreeing with each other and trying to beat their fellows and friends.\nOne day another man\n\ncame through the town, and saw what was happening. He knew something was amiss, and after a little bit of investigation, he got the entire story. This man was wiser than most, realizing that neither form of rule was going to work.\nHe went before the\n\npeople in the dirty and musty square, it dried up from all the constant disagreements.\n\"People of this once-great town, listen to my spirit. I come not from within you, but from outside, where I can truthfully judge what is right and wrong.\"\n\nA few shook their heads at this statement, but many others agreed. This man did not know them, so he could not have any bias between everyone.\n\"You were all once great and prosperous, trade and happiness was alight in this great city.\"\n\n\"But alas, it has now deserted us. Your profits have been squandered, your dissagreements abound. Yet, I have your salvation.\"\nThe people yelled at him angrily, \"The last man spoke of this too, was he not wrong and ruined us all?\"\nThe man raised his\n\nhands and waited for relative silence before speaking. \"I am not going to take away your power. I am going to change the direction it goes.\"\nThe people were understandably curious at this. What does this man mean, changing the way it\n\ngoes?\nThe man spoke.\n\"We cannot effectively decide on our own where our fair town should go. Which is why we need someone who does know.\"\nThe man guestures, and the once great leader steps up, and stands for a few seconds, listening to\n\nthe murmur of the crowd, and the blowing of the wind.\n\"Once, I ruled this town with a fair hand, trying my hardest to make this town right. And then one man showed me how much power I had, and I grew corrupted. But then, the unthinkable happened.\"\n\nThe leader guestures his arms to the now assembled crowd.\n\"You all showed me what I had become. One who did not care for his people. You took this power away from me, and I was humbled. You showed me the path.\"\nThe man steps forward.\n\n\"I cannot force you to take your great leader back. I can only plead. Please, he knows what he is doing. He knows what needs to be done. And he is ready.\"\nA few cheers went up from the crowd, and before long, the whole square was alight with joy and\n\nlaughter. \nThe town was more prosperous than ever that day, and to anyone's knowledge it is still there, filled with light and sound, the cheers from the taverns, the smiles from the children, and the shaking of hands for business.\n\nLittle did anyone realize that it was all set up from the beginning by one man. He was the one who promised prosperity to the people, showing them that their leader was not so bad after all. This man knew balance, and above all, a need for it. He left the\n\ntown that night, slipping out in the cover of darkness, moving away from the sounds of merry laughter and happiness. The man set out, and to all that anyone knows, is still travelling the world to this day.", ""),
        StaticBook("My wish!", "§bBjorn The Black", "My one wish is for just a bit of land for my tribe in the deep woods!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lone Tree", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "=======()======\n ===-=- ========\n ======/\\ ===-=-\n =====/__\\ =====\n =====/   \\ =====\n ====/____\\ ====\n ===== _U_======\n ===,_/     \\_====\n ==/_______ \\===\n “The Lone Tree” \n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Ikuras", "§bwatyll", "Ikuras, Daemon of Fear and Insanity\n\"And so it was that (Ikuras) was imprisoned, entombed by his brothers in fire and earth.\" -Diary of Grigory Adeveci\n\nThere are few things in Ancient History more mysterious, more dark, than the tale of\n\nIkuras, the Daemon of Fear. What little we know is written in the Diary of Grigory Adeveci, a monk who was by all accounts insane. However, it is the belief of some that Ikuras is very real, and that his story is true. The following is an analysis of\n\nGrigory's writing.\n\nThe journal begins fairly ordinary.\n\n\"Greetings, my name is Grigory Adeveci. I am writing this in my little room in the abbey. All is quiet now here at night and I believe it is safe to bring the artifact out. Allow me\n\nto describe this artifact to you, it is a small key, appearing as a dagger. It appears to be forged of a crystal material, and shimmers darkly when I turn it towards the light. Tomorrow I will study it more.\"\n\nRecords suggest that Grigory was a part of\n\nthe abbey's archaeological studies, and collected this artifact, this key, on a dig. The next passage is where Grigory begins experiencing odd dreams. \n\n\"Last night I had a vision. The world was drenched in a shadow. It looked like a damp,\n\nheavy shadow. I could not see through it, only hear the mad laughter from underneath. I do not think the artifact is safe to show anyone else. I will have to see what happens upon my sleep tonight.\"\n\nThe next day the journal goes on.\n\n\"My nightmares last night were nothing short of disturbing. I was the land, and I could not see. But I felt things, crawling on my back. Hairy, gaunt, rotting. I must destroy the artifact or I will be unable to sleep.\"\n\nThere are varying arguments\n\naddressing why Grigory did not simply remove the artifact from his presence. The most prevalent belief is that he was already turning mad. This is Grigory's last sane entry. \n\n\"My dreams were good, heavenly last night. I dreamed that a\n\nthousand lights came down from the heavens and sucked away the darkness. I do not know where they imprisoned it, but the darkness was locked away somewhere. The fear was locked away.\"\n\nHere Grigory appears to have gone completely mad. This is\n\nseveral weeks after his sane entry. His writings get longer and longer periods of time between them. \n\n\"I don't know why I tried to break myself. He told me it was bad but I did it anyway. I had to try and escape from myself. I should have known I should\n\nhave known I should have known I would shatter. The fear is eating me now. I see my blood on its teeth teeth teeth.\"\n\nThe repeating of phrases is very prevalent in the insanity writings. Always he repeats something three times.\n\nThe second line in this next entry is so oddly out of place, it is assumed that this obscure prophecy came to him in a bout of sanity.\n\n\"The fear fear fear is eating me I don't know why the lights made it gone the light made HIM gone gone gone. And\n\nso it was that he was imprisoned, entombed by his brothers in fire and earth. Ikuras. From the same divine spark as Iblees and Aeriel. Creator preserve me it said the name it said the name name name it must never say the name.\"\n\nAt this point Grigory\n\nconstantly refers to himself as \"it.\" This next entry is the final one, written one month after the last. \n\n\"They crawl all over it. The wolf, the spider, the corpse. It is the First Continent, and it feels them on its back back back. Now it is the Second\n\nLand, and it is free free free of the fear fear fear. But now it is the Third Place, and it is back back back. It is feeling the wolf the spider the corpse again again again. The key is the prison. The key is the prison. The key is the prison.\"\n\nDisturbingly, the last three sentences, the repeating of \"The key is the prison\" is written in Grigory's own blood. Records show that he committed suicide after this last entry. ((Contact watyll for any questions.))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Oath", "§bAdeon of Rhoswen", "I,___, accept the burdens to follow the marking. I will act as expected of me and risk my life for the innocent mundane, to protect them from the dangers of the supernatural and monstrosities alike, should I fail, creator help me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Report 07/23/15", "§bTaynuel", "Guide: Taynuel\nDate: 07/23/15\nDedicants: 8\nIGN: KibagoKid\n\nDedicant: Terreni\nDate accepted: 05/12/15\nTasks: 13 (working on GT)\n\nHaven't heard from her yet. Beginning to think she is giving up. Hasn't responded to birds.\n\nDedicant: Sul'irrin\nDate accepted: 07/02/15\nTasks: 2\n\nCurrently dealing with personal issues, which explains absence of dedicant. Said he'd be back an Elven week ago, though. Not sure what's going on.\n\nDedicant: Faenor\nDate accepted: 07/09/15\nTasks: 6\n\nHave not heard from this dedicant in a long time. Not sure why. Should've completed this task by now. Doesn't take a week to read the history of the Order. Considering\n\nremoving him from dedicancy if I don't hear from him soon.\n\nDedicant: Echo\nDate accepted: 07/13/15\nTasks: 8\n\nRecently turned into a plant person, was given a couple days to get used to the changes. Had some trouble convincing her to do her next task. I understand the risk that the transformation\n\ngives her, but if we all gave reasons we couldn't leave the Grove I'd have books on books of excuses for everyone in the Grove. Needs to buck up and be willing to take a risk or two.\n\nDedicant: Muildir\nDate accepted: 07/11/15\nTasks: 11\n\nMaking excellent progress. I'd say one or two more tasks and this one is ready for evaluation. One of my favorites of this batch.\n\nDedicant: Za'Kabar\nDate accepted: 07/13/15\nTasks: 11\n\nMy other favorite of this group. Excellent learner, very devoted, looks into his tasks, has an answer for every question. Same condition as Muildir. Maybe another\n\ntask or two and this one will be ready for evaluation. Might have him and Muildir do a review with me before they start their Grand Tasks after evaluation.\n\nDedicant: Rukdug\nDate accepted: 07/23/15\nTasks: 2\n\nNot so sure accepting this one was a good idea. He's on thin ice already and its only been one day. Heavily monitoring his actions ((both ic and ooc)).\n\nDedicant: Katelynn\nDate accepted: 07/23/15\nTasks: 1\n\nDaughter of Bee Druid and Orchid Druid. Thank the Aspects she takes after her mother. Still, best to be safe rather than sorry. Keep under careful surveillance.\n\nSummary\n\nTerreni (Lanterensangel): MIA\nSul'irrin (ZeedusFrostBlood): MIA\nFaenor (GoboHobo): MIA\nEcho (Restless_S0ul): needs more time\n\nMuildir (Jax129): Ready for Eval\nZa'Kabar (Lord_Durza): Ready for Eval\nRukdug (Dragonslayerelf): Thin ice\nKatelynn (KawaiiGamerGirl_): Under careful surveillance", ""),
        StaticBook("Ardol Tome #24", "Erveris", "All that is written in this book is:\n\n\"SKIPPEH BE FAT\"\n\"ALGRIM BE WHALE\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 5", "§bArinislia", "Elven Lessons 5\n\nOriginally by: Kalenz Uradir. Rescribed by: [Ghost] The Eternal Librarian.\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\n\nIn elven. In order to denote affiliation, the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and means\n\nin such a case 'spirit'. this also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaenan'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\".\n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in\n\nword 'evareh'. In elven, it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh -operative sing.\n-erih-operative pl.\n(-arih if the verb ends in -ar)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Living Blade", "§bCorvo", "The living sword. Something that even I can not explain so fully in detail. Such a thing can only be made with the help of others or that of an alterationist. From how I see it, Flesh is placed all around the blade, Allowing me to control said blade's\n\nMovements remotely. Such a blade will be able to bend itself and extend in diffrent ways. A very strong blade in terms of thought battle like structures. This blade will have to made from iron, Strong enough to cut others. As well it will need that of a\n\nStrong type of flesh and skin, Something that will not break itself so easily. But at the same time allow me to control it. An octipus's body of sorts will possible allow me to place tenticals all around the blade and allow me to move the tenticals in\n\nOrder to bend the blade in diffrent ways. Heh... But now I must gain that of an enchanter in order to make the blade bendable and allow me to do things much simpler. However the only one I know that will be able to do such a thing will most likely be that\n\nOf Crumena. Hmm... Well in anycase now all that is left is to create said blade and gain the items needed. This book shall become a guideline for said obeject.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Destructi...", "§bMonk Scribe", "The Destruction of the Cloud Temple\n\nAnd so it was, that the events near the end of Aegis had unfolded. First Al'Khazar, lost to the taint of the Undead and deadly miasma. Then the north, once the greatest defense of the Undead, also fell. Soon thereafter\n\nit was the great cities of Alras, New Terriko, Galahar and Kal'Urguan. These were terrible times, with the Undead attacking daily and smaller villages and buildings going up in flames daily. Corpses lined the streets and refugees tried to find shelter\n\nwherever they could.\n\nAnd so it was that one last attempt was made to save Aegis, and send the Undead scum back to the Nether. After years of strife and violence, with the Great War a recent memory, it is amazing that the nations managed to join\n\ntogether so quickly. Of course, the threat of Undead domination served as motivation. \n\nAnd so it was that finally, all peoples of Aegis joined together. Champions from each nation were chosen, equipped with what could be salvaged from the wreckage\n\nand sent to Laurelin. There stood a portal, raised by the Undead Vardak. It was here that the Champions of the nations prepared themselves for the final assault on the Nether.\n\nFor those who did not enter that cursed place, there are only\n\nstories. Tales of the heat, and the sickening gas, the hordes of monsters and explosions. It was the Dwarf Urir Ireheart who made it first to the Nexus and destroyed the Axe of Krug, sacrificing himself in the process. In doing so, the Nether began to\n\ncollapse.\n\nFor those waiting outside the portal, gathered in Laurelin and the surrounding areas, this was a pivotal moment. Should the Champions succeed, the Undead would be vanquished. If they failed, Iblees would be free to\n\ncontinue his tyranny upon Aegis. As it turned out...\n\nWe knew that something had gone awry when, instead of the Champions emerging victorious, Dragons suddenly appeared. Massive, black winged beasts, they seemed to strike out of nowhere.\n\nAnd they were not alone. Having seen the destruction in the Nether caused by the Champions, and knowing that his Undead were now to be trapped in the Nether, Iblees unleashed his final fury. \n\nDragons. Fireballs. Monsters. The\n\nsame tools of the Undead that had so ravaged Aegis for decades now struck again. Laurelin burned, nearly the entire city falling to flames. The Cloud Temple, the last safe place for the Descendent Races, was blown to pieces. Even across Aegis, in places\n\nthat had already been conquered by the Undead, and those that hadn't, anything that remained was torn to pieces. The fury of Iblees was remarkable to behold.\n\nStanding on the steps of the Cloud Temple, I was lucky to make it out alive. Having no\n\nnotice of the impending doom, I was saved only by chance. When the Temple exploded under my feet, I happened to land in a puddle. It was pure chaos from that point. I flung arrows into monsters, trying to seek a good vantage point. It seemed in vain, as\n\ntheir numbers quickly overwhelemed those who battled for Aegis. Many were dead instantly, others after a battle. More still retreated from fear or terrible wounds. \n\nAfter running out of arrows I turned to a sword, slashing and hacking. While a\n\nprimitive weapon, it served the purpose well. Zombies, Skeletons and Spiders fell in droves as the sky was lit up with the flames of explosions.\n\nIt was quickly clear that there was no saving the Temple. I fled south on the King's Road, hoping at\n\nleast to try and contain the violence.\n\nI shall never forget that day... the screams, the blood, the endless suffering. In the moment the Undead were gone, it would appear that Iblees had won. The Descendents had no Aegis left, it was\n\ndestroyed beyond measure. We would be forced to flee our lands, escaping through the Verge to Asulon. And yet, Iblees lost as well. His servants the Undead were sealed away in the Nether for all time, useless to him. \n\nPerhaps this is the\n\nmost important lesson of all. There were no winners at the end of Aegis. At best it is a draw, with the Descendents forced to flee and Iblees without his minions. At worst, he secured a victory paid for with the blood of untold numbers, who all died\n\nin the name of Aegis. Although the Undead are seemingly gone, we must be constantly aware of the possibility that they might rise again. Given all that has been endured, one hopes they remain sealed away...\n\n- By Lunia in Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("ProtectiveCharms", "§bNitholiak VonSchlichten", "ARCANE POWER\n  Protective Charms\n\n\n\nBy      Nitholiak\n     VonSchlichten\n\nMagic comes in many forms and types.  Many seems to overlook the usefullness of protective charm s in their everyday lives. From charms that deflect dark energy to simple locking charms, they effect most citizens of Aegis.\n\nProtective charms can be split into two categories: Spell and Runic. \nRunic charms are used for to protect doors, chests and other property from theft or destruction. Only those experienced enough in rune enchanting can master this ability.\n\nBut for those who do possess it, it makes for a very profitable source of magical revenue from the Dwarven Rune Magic.\n\nProtective Spells are different from the runic charms. Protective spells can protect vast areas from disturbance. Most cities in Aegis have powerful protective spells cast over them. This means nobody can destroy parts of the cities.\n\nThe only exception is dark magic. Protective spells can also be cast on a much smaller scale. Forming magical barriers to small areas that protect against magic spells cast by another.\n\nBoth types of Protective Charms require much study and practice. Do not get discouraged if you fail repeatedly.  Practice must be done for months.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blood of Many", "§bRosso", "With great might and ideals men have raised themselves to fight. Throughout the sands of time we have seen gigantic armies fall and tyrant kings still stand. And yet, where do these ideals, these admittedly impressive albeit unsuccessful ventures lead?\n\nDeath and destruction. The decay of rebellions, and the downfall of freedom. And yet where many have failed, it takes but one to succeed. Need one be reminded of any of the ancient kings and rules who have come to an, shall we say abrupt end? Indeed,\n\nAssassins shape the tide of history more than you know. And here you arem reading, seeking, learning. What is it that you wish to know I wonder?\nIt is true that we have our governments, it is true that they are what hold us together- And yet! It is also\n\nthat we have the power to sway the tide! Move the battlefield to our advantage! And even, end the rule of the horrendous” The power in the minority is greater than we think. And it is why today we live in a world DEFINED by the assassinations of\n\nyesterday! And were these the greatest historic decisions? Perhaps not. But while some were not the best, others changed history for the better, bringing Aegis to the place it is today-or was yesterday rather. Grand armies once again amass in a hopeless\n\neffort to combat the Undead forces.\nIt makes one question where the world will be left, with such meek enemies yet so strong.\nIt is high time we accept our history’s motive and ally ourselves with Iblees to bring salvation to our world. This is where our\n\npowers are tested. We must remain resolute in the times to come if we are to become united. Otherwise we might as well let our blood spatter against the stone.\n\nThe Blood of Many, the Heart of One\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("CMask Guidebook", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Anti-Contagion\n  Filtration Mask\n     Guidebook\n\n       by Mirtok\n\nThank you for accepting your very own anti-contagion filtration mask, through this handbook you will learn all the important functions and procedures for operating and effectively using your mask. By the order of the Hochmeister in hopes to combat the\n\nrising infectious ailments, every Hanseti citizen is issued their own filtration mask for safety.\n\nSafety Tips\n1.) Never misplace or lose your mask, though the Hochmeister cares deeply for your safety, he will not be able to give out spare masks to careless people. \n\n2.) Never share your mask, to prevent the spread of the illness\n\nthe Hochmeister urges all mask users to stay with their own mask no matter the circumstances.\n\n3.) Maintain your mask, keeping your mask in proper order at full upkeep will prevent incidences of break or breaches in your mask's special\n\nprotective filtration and sealant systems.\n\n4.) Use filters to their fullest, each few years the Hochmeister will distribute new filters for your masks but until then you must ration off what you have, this will not only test your ability to be\n\nresponsible for your life but to prove you have what it takes to survive in a hazardous world.\n\nPreparing your Mask\nUpon receiving your mask, it is a good idea to become acquainted with how it works and how to properly use it to fend off infective agents of death.\n\nFirstly, it is a good idea to make sure your filters are in place\n\nand secure along both sides of the mask.\n\nUnder the eye sockets of the masks should be two metal containers with 3 clip secure locks located on the circumference of each capsule. Inside you can see the several layers of filters and spinning mechanism\n\nthat make up the filtration system. Do refrain from tinkering with the delicate parts and only manipulate the filters. Once assured that the filters fit snuggly in their respective areas we can make to making sure there are no cracks in the mask. We are\n\nunsure as to how the infection is spread and therefore it is important to count for all possible biological entries into the body. First examine the two large eye sockets and lenses on the front of the mask. Also can along the main folds and seams of the\n\nmask to make sure no loose strings or openings are present. Finally, make sure the center piece where each tube leading from the two filter capsules is not loose or emitting a rattling noise when shook. Be sure to be extra careful when checking for\n\nbreaches as a single hole can mean the difference between life or death.\n\nReplacing Filters\nTo replace a filter, you must first unlatch the lid to the two filtration capsules. Once the interior is exposed, carefully turn the filter pads until a hard click is heard above the smaller clicking during turning. When heard, the\n\nthe pads should slightly elevate themselves into a popping motion and then should be ready for removal. Replacement works in the opposite fashion, place the new ones in the direction of the painted arrows and turn when the resistance is felt.\n\nSeveral clicks should be heard until a final snap indicates its in place. Close the capsule and move to the next one.\n\nUsing your Mask\nWhen your situation calls for you to use your mask, you must follow a few simple steps to ensure your maximum safety in the face of an infective area. First loosen all of the straps along the back and front of the mask. Then place the\n\nloose mask over your head and position the eye sockets for your preferred viewing.\n\nWhen ready, slowly tighten each strap until the strapped area feels tight and snug over your head. It is very important to maintain a tight fit but also to keep the mask\n\nfrom cutting off blood flow to your mask and face as such will prompt discomfort and compel you to adjust the mask. When all straps have been secured, turn the small dial located on the front of your mask where the capsule tubes meet until you hear a\n\nsmall rush of air., When all these are done, you should have achieved maximum anti-contagion safety.\n\nBreaching/Cracks\nIn the event of a breach or crack in your mask, it is advised by the Hochmeister to quickly remove yourself from the jeopardizing area and seek cover and solitude from any other contact with others. The Hochmeister then\n\nurges you to remove the filter pads from your filtration capsules and attempt to apply them over your nose and mouth if no other repair methods are successful on the damaged mask.\n\nGood luck out there and may Celestia keep this tragedy from our frozen lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Plague", "§bVeldryn Uuthlini", "The Plague is a disease that spreads quickly, strikes without discrimination, and has a high fatality rate. It refers both to the disease itself as well as the time it struck Asulon resulting in widespread deaths and chaos.\n\n\nThe plague was first recorded in year 37 in Asulon, when it broke in the lands of Seventis. Immediately the infected began to die in mass numbers, resulting in the near collapse of Seventis.\n\nSpread by travelers and other creatures, the plague quickly spread to other settlements including Skravia and the Cloud Temple Sanctuary.\n\nAll attempts to find a cure or prevent the spread of the infection initially failed. The monks of the Cloud Temple who would usually take the injured and sick to their lands for healing, -\n\nbecame overwhelmed by the deaths and started to burn the bodies. Attempted cures such as magic and alchemy did not help halt the spread or aid the sick, but in some cases only increased the severity.\n\nReactions were varied. Some nations and settlements such as Holm and Ildon implemented lockdown policies to prevent themselves getting infected. Others were badly struck, -\n\nsuch as Seventis and Skravia. Initially closed off, the plague infected the lands of Renatus and struck the peasants of Arethor and Ager with particular vengeance.\n\nThe Subudai were rarely struck down with the disease, leading to claims that they were immune. Having a stronger immune system, Orcs caught the disease with less frequency, -\n\nbut the effects were still as severe. Kharajyr as well managed to avoid getting sick as often, having better tuned senses and being exposed to more diseases in their jungle homes.\n\nSymptoms\n\nWhen the first outbreak of plague occurred in Seventis, several symptoms were common. Over time the initial symptoms became less common as those infected died, and a new variation of the disease became more common.\n\nGreen-Spot Variation\n\n- Green dots on the skin causing itching.\n- Numbness in the digits and limbs.\n- Weakness.\n- Memory loss and mood swings.\n- Vomiting.\n- Coughing up blood.\n\nBlack-Spot Variation\n\n- Shivers.\n- Paranoia.\n- Coughing of blood.\n- Fear of blood itself.\n- Internal hemorrhage, resulting in bleeding through mouth.\n\nOther Effects\n\n - Wheat could also suffer from the plague disease and would wither in the field. Eating bread or other goods made with infected wheat could result in infection.\n\n- Beasts of all kind could also be struck by the disease and displayed similar symptoms to the sentient life forms. The disease passed freely between them.\n\nResults\n\n- Death usually occurred within one Elven day.\n\n- Among those who survived, many were scarred for life from the green or black dots.\n\n- Many initial survivors were killed by other diseases because of a weakened immune system, or from monsters that could attack them more easily.\n\n- Many small settlements were made completely devoid of life, as the plague killed all who lived in them.\n\nPrevention\n\nThe plague was the deadliest, fastest spreading and most contagious disease ever recorded. Prevention methods were initially limited to avoidance of those already infected, often by leaving civilized areas.\n\n Some nations and settlements issued lockdowns to prevent the plague from entering their borders. In time other methods were developed, such as masks that helped prevent the catching of the plague.\n\nBut a cure has been found and cured the great plague and the people affected.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish", "§bWykem Evenheart", "I wish that I had enough Minas to buy a charter for our guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic: Vol. 2", "§bRatemenatorz59", "Void Magic is the art of extracting elements from the void, and commanding the elements.\nThe Void is an endless space, in which elements reside in. Those who delve in the arts of the arcane are able to pull these elements from this 'endless space' and\n\nare able to command it to do their will.\nIt is not 'creating things out of nothing', however. To command these elements at will, and to extract them from the void, you will need mana.\nThe exhaustion of mana varies upon the magnitude of your spell.\n\nFor example, though you won't succeed, trying to mold fire as a beginner may exhaust an incredible amount of mana. Don't try this, it may kill you.\nTo be able to use void magicks, you require a connection to the void, but that is a story for another day.", ""),
        StaticBook("another wish", "§bIyath the Toymaker", "I wish I'd fall and love and get married with someone WHO ISN'T BORING\n\n-Iyath", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Magic", "§bAmbros_", "PROLOGUE\n This book was recovered from Aegis is dated around 1356 of the last age of Aegis. They are early writings from the wizard Ambros that remained in secret for a century.\n\nHave you ever seen a scribe readying a page to copy a piece of text? The scribe scrapes the sheet clean, then carefully traces out perfectly straight lines to contain the text and set it in order. Finally, the scribe sharpens a quill and carefully forms\n\neach letter in the text, stringing the characters together to form words, paragraphs, and finally the whole page. Preparing a spell is like that. I have my spellbooks, the original manuscript. I begin the processes by resting my mind and body, erasing the\n\ndetritus from the previous day. Sleep wipes my mental parchment clean. When I awake, a focus for a while. I cast off the details left over from my dreams and set my thoughts in order, just like a scribe setting the rules and margins on a page.\n\nWhen I finish, I have built a mental structure for my spells. This is the essence of magic. As I have continued to hone my magical art, I find I can create more and more mental pages to contain my spells. When I have created as many blank\n\npages as my mind can hold, I turn to my spellbook and copy the spells I need. I don't use pen and ink, of course, I carefully review the arcane formulae recorded in the book and fill the empty structures in my mind with magical power. There's no\n\nfeeling quite like finishing preparation for a spell. Thoughts swirl like autumn leaves through my mind. By sheer force of training and will, I force those mental leaves into motes of arcane power. The motes collect on the framework like beads of dew\n\non a spider's web. The final result is a thing of stunning and sublime beauty. With every breath I take, I can feel the structure thrum with power.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant's Vow", "§b12werbles12", "~*~\n  The Dedicant's Vow\n\nI now walk the forests with my new kin. I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me. As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need. I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk\n\n approaches. I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\n\n   by:\n   Salmon Druid Petyr\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will walk the forest with my new kin.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges his or her official ties to be with the Druids of the Druidic Order.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges loyalty to the Order and thereby promises to speak the truth and never with deception.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need.\"\n\nWhile under the guidance of the Aspects and the elder Druids, the Dedicant pledges to return the favor of respect and service.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk approaches.\"\n\nThe Dedicant pledges devout service, no matter the time nor obstacle he or she may face.\n\n           ~*~\n\n\"I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\"\n\nThe Dedicant does just that; he or she vows to uphold his or her duties and their pledge as a Dedicant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elements of Mind", "§bFarley III Stafyr", "Elements of Mind\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\n\nUpon the writing of the Theorem of Wisdom, my very own mind came to the conclusion that there must be more to it. Every person knows of elements such as fire, earth, water, wind or air and lightning.  But aside from external elements which we\n\ncan feel and use, there are also other elements, in a completely different range, of which we unknowingly make use and into which we tap, without realizing it.\n\nThe Elements of Mind.\n\nThe mind is a strange fabric, giving us the ability to think, to consider, to act, react, to learn, to remember and many things more. But the mind itself, such as the outer world we experience, has its own elements. To underline this, an example will be\n\ngiven.\n\nFeelings. Feelings, such as love, guilt, hate, happiness and many more. This is one of the elements of the mind, we are able to use it, express ourselves with it, to tap into the power of this element.\n\nFurther explanation is not necessary, I presume, as everyone has at least one feeling within him.\n\nOther elements do exist. Wisdom is one of them, as I aforementioned. Also knowledge and experience are\n\nelements of the mind. But there are more!\n\nConcentration, Purity, Peace and Balance, and Common Sense.\n\nHow each of these work, will be explained in further, upcoming books. e\n\nFor the element of wisdom, I refer myself to my work “Theorem of Wisdom” for further information. The book “Knowledge and Experience – Elaborated” may give additional hints about two further elements.\n-: Primary Edition :-", ""),
        StaticBook("The False Vision", "§bRyn", "I spoke at great length on the subject of Gazadriel with the High Prophet of the Dwarven nation, Hogarth last evening with Za'Kabar. During our chat, we gained information that may be useful in the coming days. I make this record for the future generation\n\nof decendants, so they may know our plight. \n\nAll of this started a few Elven days ago, when I had taken some nightsap with my sister Illithri, in an attempt to finally get some sleep. As I dreamed of camping in the Fringe, my rest was interrupted by a\n\nvision of a rainbow colored fairy ring. Once I stepped inside of it, I awoke.\n\nAn emergency moot was called a few hours later. A second vision had been already viewed by many who chose to step into a fairy ring.\n\nThey stated that this second vision told them of a coming harvest of souls, and that the one reaping them must be preserved.\n\nThis went against everything I had ever been taught of being a Druid. We are neutral, we preserve the balance of\n\nnature. To take a life like this reaper is cannot be part of the balance. A few people agreed with me and together, we set out to prove this vision as false.\n\nAmong those who came were Henry and Barry Winterleaf, Illitri, Eloh'ra, Aeras, Za'Kabar, and\n\nOliver. Together, we set off from the Grove and made a bunker in which to hide and research who could have made a false vision to us. \n\nAs time went on, Aeras went to see the vision for himself. When he returned, he convinced Eloh'ra that the\n\nreaper must indeed be preserved and they left our numbers. \n\nAfter this happened, it became clear that I needed to see the vision for myself. Za'Kabar and I left the bunker together and travelled to the fairy ring within the Grove. Together, we stepped\n\ninside of the ring and instantly passed out.\n\nThe vision that I saw was as follows. I was standing within a field of wheat, watching a harvester reap the grain. As I watched, the stalks of wheat turned into decendants: Humans, Elves, ect.\n\nAs the harvester reaped the decendant stalks of wheat, it's scythe seemed to draw the very souls from them.\n\nThe vision continued and someone appeared in the field. They slayed the reaper with a golden sword. As the reaper died, a mighty storm appeared,\n\ndestroying the field of wheat. A voice spoke and said the harvest must continue, the reaper must be preserved.\n\nI awoke with Za'Kabar and we both agreed in that moment that this vision could not be from the Aspects. It was then we set off in two different\n\ndirections. Za'Kabar travelled to the Stream Circle, to see if there were others who felt the way we did.\n\nOliver and I departed the Grove and travelled to the Cloud Temple to seek wisdom from the books there. \n\nThere, we ran into my nephew,\n\nYohei, one of the Elder Monks at the temple. When I told him of the vision and my belief, he said he would help all he could and began his own research.\n\nWe settled down for the evening, reading every book that we could find. The book about Aenguls\n\nhad an interesting name inside of it. The name of Gazadriel. He is the Aengul of curiostiy, new beginnings and the one most involved in mortal affairs. \n\nI moved on to another book, one on the group known as the Ascended.\n\nThe first mention of Gazadriel was in the death of Sage Martin Benedict. He had a Golden Staff in his possession, and as he decended into madness, he clutched it.\n\nWhen the time of his death came, he cursed the staff and\n\nthrough it away from him. He warned the Acolytes that it was the Golden Staff of Gazadriel. That it was imbued with Gazadriel's intent to 'renew' the world, to destory it and build it again as he saw.\n\nMore mention of Gazadriel's name came a little\n\nfurther into the next part. Gazadriel had appeared from the staff to the Ascended in Anthos. The events were confusing that I read about, but continued on down the page.\n\nOnce finished with that book, it was decided between Oliver, Za'Kabar, and\n\nmyself that we would need a lot more information to determine if Gazadriel truly was the cause of the false vision.\n\nThe hour was growing late at this point, and having no where to go, Za'Kabar and I left Oliver at the temple to rest and moved on to\n\nspeak with our next hope for help: Hogarth. \n\nDuring this time, rumors began that people were hunting Druids, because of the vision. Many people had beleived the false vision and sworn to protect the reaper. The reaper that we knew of at the time\n\nhappened to be a Frost Witch. That was another... thing... that pushed me over the edge of not believing in the vision. But anyway, Za and I made our way to Hogarth's home. He took us in and we told him of our plight. He gave us a room for the night and\n\npromised any assistance he could give, and that he would keep his eyes and ears open for more information. \n\nA couple of Elven days passed. Yohei found no new information and I began reading more indepth into the texts I had found.\n\nI received a bird from Hogarth asking to meet up again. Za'Kabar and I travelled to his home again and the three of us spoke at length about the current situation.\n\nThe first reaper, the frost witch, had been destroyed. With her death, a storm occured,\n\nbut not the world ending type of storm that we were expecting if the vision were true. \nThat is the moment I truly knew that the vision was false. Hogarth reveiled that he believed there were other reapers as well. I agreed with the thought. I had\n\nspoken with Barry earlier in the day about the same subject... and that one of our fellow Druids may be a reaper. For protection of the person, I will not put their name in this tome, incase I am wrong about who they are.\n\nOn to why I think that\n\nGazadriel is 100% behind all of this. As we spoke to Hogarth, he told us a story from Athera and a place the Dwarves found called Rivel. It was a mystical floating city, completely abandoned.\n\nWhen they had looked into it more, they found out that it\n\nwas an ancient High Elven city, where the High Elves had enslaved other races to do their bidding. One record they found was of a 'Radient Man' that appeared in the city.\n\nHe used his powers against them and everyone turned on eachother. The\n\ncity was abandoned, everyone dead or fled the distruction. Hogarth and now I, believe that this 'radiant man' was indeed Gazadriel. \n\nThe only permenant solution to the situation is going to be the death of Gazadriel. The only way to do so is by\n\nrunesmithing a weapon that can fight an Aengul.\n\nThe only clan who possibily could have helped is now gone. Lori Oathcast died... My heart is a little saddened by this. But we have to push foreward. Hogarth is learning to runesmith and soon,\n\nI hope soon anyway, he will be able to forge the weapons that we need to kill Gazardiel.\n\nWhile we wait for these weapons. the only thing we can do is kill the reapers, to try and buy us time.\n\nMay the Aspects ever guide us...", ""),
        StaticBook("Assorted Writing", "§bArcane Mage", "Writings of the\n     Arcane Mage\nThis book contains a collection of compiled writings by the Arcane Mage.\n\n     OF MAGIC\nThere are two sides of magic.\nNeither evil; Neither good... \nIt is only the choices and actions of the weilder which will shape the fate of all man.\nWe can only say... \nChoose wisely.\n\n  SLAYER'S JOURNAL\nThis is the first entry of my search, what will become indubitably a long and trecherous journey. This is the search for a arcane, ancient power, with its roots within the very depths of Ageis. This is my search for that power, so\n\nthat I may better myself and the greater world. The magic is said to consume the soul... But for the chance to create life... I would do anything. \nThere is little that we know about this power, it is too ancient. Only a few have ever tapped into\n\nits infinite depths. Here I refer to Availer, the wandering wizard, the most powerful being in Ageis. Who has waded deeper into the mystic magic that any other. He has retained his self... For now.\n\nSECRET OF THE MAGES\nAway in lands far lies an ancient secret, buried in history, shrouded in mystery. The keepsake of the mages; past and present... \nWithheld in a deceptive case, ancient and ruined...\n\nHolds within its perilous depths a power  beyond measure, deep in the womb of the world you will find it... \nIt holds the knowlege of the world, ancient to modern, evil and good... all dengerous...\n\nIt holds the power of life and death, none who enter leave the same. At the end of the road, under lighted sky and deepest dark lies the power. The choice the keep it within or destroy it will change the fate of all man for ever...\n\nBeware the tower! The deceptive case, in it awaits the power, but left not to take, but to win. The greedy will fall, the cautious will cower, there are only a chosen few who have the will to claim the power; others will bow to their will.\n\nThe journey only begins here; it is but a start to the end of all ends, power beyond power... This journey begins where your journey began...\n\n     THE UNIVERSE\nThere once was a man, this man lived on a hill. \nOn this hill there was a home, in this home there is a cat.\nIn this cat there was a worm, in the worm there was a cell.\nIn this cell there is a universe...\n\n   POEMS OF ACEERI\nScribed by the Arcane Mage\n 1. The Land is ours\n\n 2. Falling into the depths\n\n 3. The Creation\n\nTHE LAND IS OURS\nCome now my soldiers,\nThere is land just ahead.\nFertile soil, and our enemies no where to be seen. \nCome now my soldiers, we can settle here. \nThere is land to build on and land to farm on.\nCome now my soldiers\n\nFALLING INTO THE DEPTHS\nI see the world in my eyes,\nfalling into the skies,\nbeholding those in the mines,\nfinding those in the trees,\n\nI see the world in my eyes,\ndemons, creepers, skeletons,\nall trying to destroy,\nI see the world in my eyes,\nfearing those who seek the gods,\novercoming those who disobey the laws,\n\nI see the world in my eyes,\nfeeling the water so cold and deep,\nstaring into the lava so hot and dangerous,\nI see the world in my eyes,\ndestruction and deceit,\nfalling into chaos,\nthe never ending depth.\n\nTHE CREATION\nNothing to be seen,\nbut the endless void\ngods churning to make a new world,\nNothing to be seen,\nbut monster's souls waiting to be released into the world,\nseeking destruction at every point,\n\nNothing to be seen,\nbut an stranded man's land,\ntrying to survive in the deserted wasteland,\nNothing to be seen,\nbut an explosion of great magnitude,\ncaused by the creepers of the night,\nNothing to be seen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunian Poems", "§bHamish", "Open your eyes and watch the sky,\nto see the blue and the white,\nand view the stars that roam up above\nand watch the birds in flight.\nTo see the seasons change with time\nand the people grow and age,\n\nto see the kindness in their hearts\nand their dark eyes that hold their rage.\nOpen your eyes to notice the difference\nbetween the rumours and praise,\nfrom the people who honestly care\nto those that could not be more blasé.\n\nTo notice the change from black to grey\nfrom purple to blue, orange to red,\nand see green turn to yellow,\nthe rich comforted and the hungry get fed.\nOpen your eyes to watch the pain\nthat others hide from the rest.\n\nThey might be the man on the street\nor the masquerade, best dressed. \nNotice the seasons wash the air new\nto make room for their colours, \nand make the people change their clothes\nas well as watch out for others.\n\nOpen your eyes to their lives going by,\nto their hopes flickering and fading,\nthe things they want most leaving\nand their dreams gone from trading.\nWatch out for a puddle of tears\nnear a gravestone of the loved,\n\nand see those who longed to be touched\nas they keep their fingers gloved.\nOpen your eyes to see the compassion\nthat seems to flow in this realm,\nfrom the caring and the kindness\nto the comfort that can overwhelm.\n\nBut also take note of the depression\nthat sits at the bottoms of the lakes, \nthat rots on the tree branches\nand in the corners of the crates.\nOpen your eyes to see what I see, \nthe final realisation;\n\nthat with every new begining\ncomes yet another civilisation.\nBut just rest and take it all in,\nwith your eyes wide open\nand see this shattered realm like me,\nwith my heart completely broken.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nShattered,\nThe fact that I am broken,\nBroken,\nEven with what I said;\nTattered, \nMy heart is thankful for use,\nSmashed,\nEven though all out my heart bled.\nHalting,\n\nMy world, but seems to keep spinning,\nCrushed,\nAs my mind searches for support;\nImperfect, \nHe is gone forever as they said,\nUneven, \nAnd I did not have the energy to retort.\nDisturbed,\n\nThey told me, when I asked what happened,\nSnapped,\nThey said, when he fell with my heart,\nDefeated,\nHe was, as he was carried outside,\nCracked,\nThey described he was not that smart.\n\nStopped, \nas I cannot hear it anymore,\nDestoryed,\nmy heart to the very core,\nAltered, \nas I think its beat has changed,\nDefective,\n\nand it has made me beyond poor. \nIs,\nwhat a time that this has been,\nWhat,\nI have been through is too much,\nI,\nonly wanted to see him again,\nFeel,\n\nhis heart and his touch.\nMy,\nThree, dear Three, bless him,\nElton,\nfor he was my net under the ledge,\nIs,\nhe really, truly with you now?\n\nDead,\nand gone, straight over the edge?\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nHis green eyes never leave my gaze\nand his beard will always be brown,\nhis kilt never lost its colour\nas he kept not a trace of a frown.\nHis high stature has yet to be forgotten\nwhat with his boom laughter and grin,\n\nand his highspirits not only with his family\nbut also in the tavern with his gin.\nHis comforting words kept me going\nas his form took shape in my mind,\nfor it was I who kepts his memories,\nit was I that he never left behind.\n\nI cannot say I enjoyed all of it\nfor that man saw too many wars,\nbut he also had his moments of triumph,\nand those he loved dearly of course.\nHe kept his mind straight and level\neven under the most pressure,\n\nhe always knew where his place was\nand respected those who were lesser.\nSometimes he forgot right from wrong,\nbut then again, we all to at some point,\nand yet he knew how to keep people motivatied\neven though he was hard to dissapoint.\n\nAnd though I miss him still to this day,\nwith years gone since he passed,\nI still wish Hanrahan was here with me,\nbut for now his memories will stay glassed.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nI tried to paint you with the finest paints,\nto bring your green eyes and brown hair,\nbut the picture simply slipped from my mind,\nand on the canvas you were not there.\nI had the colours perfectly mixed,\nmy brush poised and ready,\n\nbut when it came to shaping your face,\nI could not keep my hand steady.\nI ended up painting a landscape;\nit was one that I knew all too well,\nit had trees in the back and buildings around,\nbut little did I know that I fell.\n\nI watched my hand with curiosity,\nnot knowing what it was doing, \nand suddenly I forgot where I was,\nand even the tea I had brewing.\nI forgot my life and all my memories,\nI forgot who I had lost,\n\nI only knew about the place at hand,\nand I could not see the lines I crossed.\nI backed into my own painting\nof the trees and of the buildings,\nand backed right into the old Clinic of ours\nand I found the stash of old kindlings.\n\nI relit the fire just behind the counter,\nand leaned on it as I looked towards the door,\nI had washed the floors and that silver bell,\nand waited for your arrival once more.\nAs I stood in the Clinic of Memories\n\nI seemed to trick myself,\nbut at the time I could not see you\nas I restocked the shelf.\nYou walked in quietly as you always did,\nand I hung my coat on a hook.\nBut I could tell that I was not alone\n\nas you stood in that corner and looked.\nI turned around to see your expression,\nthose green eyes sunked into your face,\nand when you told me simple words that calmed me,\nthey helped me find my place.\nYou stepped closer and hugged me,\n\nyour words were soft and kind,\n\"You will be all right, I promise,\" you whispered,\nand suddenly it was I who was hard to find.\n\"Can't I just go back to the Clinic?\"\nI almost cried as you came near,\n\n\"Yes, anything you want, I promise,\nbut for now, Arial, you must stay here.\"\nSomething happened just then, \t\nwhen you promised I would be okay.\nI knew that the person I was then\nwould not be the person I am today.\n\nFor now I know that Arial\nwas the one who you wanted to protect,\nso she took her things and kept them safe,\nleast she be the one I forget.\nAnd now your dreams can come true,\nfor your daughter now walks these lands,\n\nand I can assure that Arial will be all right, \nbecause she is in your own hands.\nShe may call herself Annabelle,\nbut that is only for your sake,\nbecause she knows your daughter is in her\nand her soul was always yours to take.\n\nBut I did lose myself in the Clinic that day,\neven though it was just a painting.\nAnd even though it was all in my mind,\nI know it was real and Arial is still waiting.\nShe will wait for you until the end of time,\nuntil the brush is steady,\n\nuntil your face can be painted again\nand until you think she is ready.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nPostscript.\n\nA collection of poems\nwritten by a famous Adunian poet in the late Anthosian period.\n\nLet her memory be charished by all those who read her delightful words.\n\n-Hanrahan Brae", ""),
        StaticBook("Strange Code", "Jistuma", "From a note written by a friend in code, of many pages, she had no memory of writing it, or what it did mean.\n\nI decided to try and decipher it as if it were a secret note between armies, and I came with results. The code is copied first, then the\n\nmeaning of the code is told, then the translation.\n\nCode\n\n{t, ƒ:ªº£ ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, ñ.nü| ƒ'ª t, u':ô .nô t, ,ñö£:n,ºº d,i'û t, u':ô û,ª, e:º £' c'ññ.nô]\n[t,ü û,ª, ô\"º£ .nô e, û.º .º . º\"nd,.ñ| ô,ƒ:n:nø .£ i.º£ t,:ª ê.ö,]\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ'ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, .ø.:n| û:t t, º'ªª'û 'ƒ º\"ni:øe£ ª,ñ.:n:nø \"n£ª,.£,ô .nô \"nû,ic'ñ, £' t, ô,,ö c\"ªª,n£º 'ƒ t, º,.]\n[º\"ç ô:ª,c£:'ni,ººn,ºº :º .n.t,ñ. £' e:ñ| ûe' :º i:n,.ª]\n[t,º, .ª, £' d, E:º £ª:\"ñöeº .nô E:º ƒ.:i:nøº| ñ.nü £:ñ,º 'u,ª]\n\n{t, º,c‘nô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.c£:‘nº ‘ƒ t.£ ûe:ç :º e, .ª, d.ªª,ô ƒª‘ñ ,n£ªü]\n[t, ‘t,ªº e.u, t,:ª ô,u:c,º ‘ƒ û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n| ô,ƒ:n:æ t,ñ .º ûe.£ t,ü .iû.üº e.u, d,,n| t, c.ª,£.*,ªº ‘ƒ t,:ª ƒ.£,]\n\n[t,ü ê‘“£ .nô öi,.ô .nô ‘ƒƒ,ª t,:ª u‘:c,º £‘ t, e,.u,nº| d“£ t,ü .ª, .º t, ô,,ö c.u,º d,øø:æ ƒ‘ª º“ni:øe£]\n[t, û.ü :º ê“£]\n\n{t, t:ªô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[. ‘n, £,.ªº ƒª,, t, di:nôƒ‘iô ‘ƒ t, .düºº ƒª‘ñ t, ,ü,º ‘ƒ t, ö.ª£º]\n[:£ :º .º :£ û.º]\n[t, i:øe£ .nô i:øe£º .nô i:øe£:æ ‘ƒ t,:ª êª:n,º ƒª,, t,:ª º:øe£| t.£ t,ü ñ.ü di:nô ‘t,ªº]\n\n[û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n .ø.:n º“øø,º£º :£º,iƒ| .nô t, i:n, :º ñ.ô, .º .n “nc‘“n£.di, º,ª:,º ‘ƒ ö‘:n£º| .ii :n c‘nƒi:c£ û:t t,:ª ƒ,ii‘ûº]\n[.ii û:,iô:æ t,:ª i.û]\n\n{t, ƒ‘“ªt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t,:ª i.û :º t, ö‘û,ª ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[ºi‘ûiü t, i:øe£º .ª, ,æª.u,ô û:t t, ºüñd‘iº ‘ƒ t, ,nº,ñdi,º ‘ƒ t, ñ.nü]\n[t, º:øe£º ‘ƒ n,û ç.:nº .ª, ƒ.ñ:i:.ª]\n\n{t, ƒ:ƒt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.øñ,n£º .ª, ñ.ô, .º £‘ø,t,ª .º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n[t, ñ.nü ç‘‘º, t,:ª ö.t| £‘ t, ª,ö,£:£:‘n .º t, º“n ª:º,º .nô ƒ.iiº ‘ª £‘ t, dª,.*:æ ‘ƒ :£| t.£ t, º“n ê.ii º£.nô º£:ii]\n\n{t, º:xt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ñ.nü d,c‘ñ, .º ‘n, .º û.º t.£ ûe:ç :º e,]\n\n{t, º,u,nt ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[.º û.º d,ƒ‘ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º ñ.nü ñ.ô, .ø.:n]\n\nMeaning\n\n. - a\n, - e\n: - i\n‘ - o\n“ - u\n\nt - th\nƒ - f\nª - r\nº - s\n£ - t\nñ - m\nc - c\n\nø - g\nû - w\ne - h\nç - ch\nô - d\nn - n\nü - y\nu - v\nö - p\nd - b\ni - l\nê - sh\n* - k\n\næ - ng\n\n| - ,\n\n[] - sentance\n{} - title\n\nTranslation\n\nThe first mathic age.\nThat which is He made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were His to command.\nThey were dust and He was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape.\n\nAs was before, that which is He made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea.\nSuch directionless is anathema to Him, who is linear.\n\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over.\n\nThe second Mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry.\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate.\n\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight.\nThe way is shut.\n\nThe third Mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts.\nIt is as it was.\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others.\n\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows.\nAll wielding their law.\n\nThe Fourth Mathic Age\n\nTheir law is the power of the many.\nSlowly the lights are engraved with the symbols of the ensembles of the many.\nThe sights of new chains are familiar\n\nThe Fifth Mathic Age\n\nThe fragments are made as together as was before, that which is he.\nThe many choose their path, to the repetition as the sun rises and falls or to the breaking of it, the sun shall stand still.\n\nThe Sixth Mathic Age\n\nThe many become as one as was that which is he.\n\nThe Seventh Mathic Age\n\nAs was before, that which is he many made again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sins", "§bKyral Rilann", "The following are the Sins of the Acolyte.\n\nMurder, many many counts of murder. Including\nMurder of a Child\nMurder of a relative\nMurder of ELWEN\n*the page is wet here*\nThe sacking of The Salvus Grove, murdering Druids to-\n\nobtain a simple book.\n\nConsorting with a Frost Witch on numerous occasions\n\nConsorting with Murderers of all types (Dark Brotherhood, Frozen Thorns, The Flays)\n\nDisloyalty to my late-\n\nhusband King James Hightower twice.\n\nCausing chaos and disorder within Asulon, with many deaths not done by myself, but because of my actions\n\nThe continued practice of Void magic.\n\nThe becoming of a cultist in Athera\n\nThe assault of many druids within Athera.\n\nAgain I will repeat, the Betrayal of the Clerics and ascended, the betrayal of my Wife Elwen, I murdered her in my trance.\n\nThese are my sins, I carry them heavy.\n\n-Acolyte Kyral", ""),
        StaticBook("TheWitchsMarsh", "Domainoft", "The Witches Marsh, Told by Nienna Calm\nNienna: Have you ever heard of a place called \"The Witches Marsh\"?\nIt's a small swampland outside near Malinor. It's dark and gloomy place. I paid\nit a visit one evening, Looking for some more Mandragora\n\nLeaf. Though, when I\nfirst came to it the only thing I could find was a warning of the dangers\ninside.\nI ignored the warnings, Unfortunently. I thought it was just the nearby\nhalflings trying to ward people away\n\nfrom there vale. I was very very wrong. I\ngot lost almost immediatly as I entered the marsh. It was dark, the trees\nclouded the path ahead, and the ground made it hard to walk at all. I tried to\nmake it to the base of a nearby moutain, but as I\n\nreached the base I slipped\nand fell into a cave littered with webs. I was covered by them almost\ninstantly. Webs seemed to cling to the walls, the ground, everywhere. You would\nthink that walking back up looked like\n\nmore trouble than it was worth.\nSo I tried to look further in, to see if it was a through passage. I took no\nmore than two steps before I found myself in the middle of a large Cavern. The\ncavern was Punctuated by a single, slanted\n\nspike in the center. It was of a\nmaterial I'd never seen before. It was odd and slightly pale. I cut my way\nthrough more of the webs, and dropped into the room. I checked the material and\ntook a sample or two as well, but then I\n\n...heard something behind me. it was a\nsqueltch. Coming from a smaller alcove attached to the room I was in. I hadn't\nmuch in the way of weapons at the time. So i drew my crude stone axe annd tried\nto find the source. As soon as I was inside the\n\nsecond cavern though I heard a\nhiss. It's liek what the spiders make but lower..deeper. The sound came from\ndirectly above me, and as I looked up to see it. I found that i'd walked\nbeneath a spider as tall as that wall ovre there is high\n\n\"20ft\".\nAs soon as I heard it, it was on me. It attacked me as soon as I saw it. It\nhunched down, and tried to pin me beneath it while tring to stick it's fangs\ninto me. I was fast enough to jump away, but the spider sliced my lower\n\narm\nopen with one of it's fangs. I looked around the room and found that I was in\nthe larger atrium with the slanted spike in the center. I hadn't time to climb\nout of the room again, so I made for the spike. It had a flat area on the top\n\n\nof it and I managed to make my wau up it. Though unfortunently the spider was\nstill on my heels. I ran to the tip of it as fast as I could, lept, aiming for\nthe entrance to the room. Thankfully, Since I'm still here speaking to you I\n\nmade it. Then I rummaged through my bag for my last vial of alchemist flame,\nand threw it on the ground.\nAs soon as I got out, I fell over again. The sider was poisonous. I did what I\ncould to apply a tournoquet, and wandered back\n\ninto the Witch Marsh. What I\nfound was a house. I passed out immediately as I entered. To my luck, I woke up\nwith Savictus the Druid, looking down at me. Apparently he lives in those\ncursed marshes because of the\n\ntaint present there. He saved my life, and\nremoved the posion. And that is how I lived through a giant spider attack.\n\n-Leyu'Maehr\nVaelhaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((3/3/13)", ""),
        StaticBook("Laurelin", "§bArinislia", "Children of Laurelin\n\nI hear the song of Laurelin;\nThe children’s laugher singing;\nOf trees, and leaves of many things,\nTo many, the sound of bells ringing;\n\nI hear the song of  Laurelin,\nNow lost in the burning flames;\nThe echos whisper in our hearts,\nNow most don’t seem the same;\n\nI heard the song of Laurelin,\nof purity and rings;\nOf ones who mix of blood,\nAre met with acid that stings.\n\nI seek the song of  Laurelin,\nOf children’s laughter and song;\n The sound almost lost to me now,\nThough somehow I continue on.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ents", "§bUnknown", "Ents\n\nEnts are massive tree-beings that protect the forests. They make their presence known in times of great peril, or when they feel their charges are in the utmost danger, or threatened.\n\nThere have been several sightings of Ents in world history, and these beings were revered by the Druids as being the most sacred of guardians, and their actions regarded as will of the Druidic “Aspects”, or ancient Spirits; incarnations of nature.\n\n Appearance\n\nEnts are generally very tall beings, made of wood and moss, leaves and branches. They have unique facial features, and two “trunks” for legs.\n\nEnts resemble trees that have stepped out of the ground and became lords of the forest.\n\nThey tend to have beady eyes, and no visible ears (though they can hear).\n\nEnts are diverse, and have interests dependent on the land that they are serving. And while they seek to protect all natural life, they regard their own territory in highest priority.\n\nThey can display a wide range of emotions and intelligence, if anyone could stand to listen to an entire conversation for long enough!\n\nEnts are wise, and slow to speak. A single sentence uttered by an Ent can last up to ten minutes.\n\n Most instances of decision making by Ents have taken years before they have made them, which could be perhaps a gaping weakness. They do not believe in hastiness.\n\nEnts, while having differing personality traits, seem to all be quiet creatures naturally. They spend time they aren’t roaming the forests pondering and philosophizing  as ancient minds tend to wander to greater questions that lesser beings\n\ncannot yet hope to comprehend.\n\nMany times Ents are mistaken for trees in the forest, as they are simply distracted by thought.\n\nAnother great weakness of an Ent is that grabbing its attention is quite difficult. Unless the forest cries out in pain, it tends to stand still and entertain its thoughts.\n\nThose in connection with nature have been known to coax two\n\nor three out of their ponderings though.\n\n Language\n\nEnts can commune between one another through the language of the Ents, which is a throaty mumbling that also involves rustling their leaves.\n\nBeing so massive that they can tower at fifty feet (and even higher), they have massive brute strength. A single being attacking an Ent would be utterly doomed.\n\nEnts in Asulon have torn down entire gates, in Anthos they have tossed Dwarves like skipping stones and ancient texts even describe an Ent fighting a Dragon!\n\nHowever winter is a terrible foe for an Ent; only a Pine ent could survive in it.\n\n Creation\n\nIt is rumoured that Ents are born from Elder trees, as they usually protect the forests that surround one, taking upon some of the visual traits of that tree.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 1", "§bArinislia", "Elven Lessons\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\n\nIn Elven, grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one, instead of placing an adjective before a noun, it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\n\nKarin’alya-Goodday\nKer’ayla – Goodnight\nVan’ayla –Goodbye\n\nEach places the time of day before the adjectives describing it. Noun adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\nOther important words of the beginner in Elven include race names:\n\nMali-Elf\nUruk- Orc\nValah-Human\nBortu-Dwarf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of Elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\n\nWood Elf-Mali’ame\nHigh Elf-Mali’aheral\nDark Elf-Mali’ker\n\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures, the suffix tali- may be used. This word directly means ‘part of’.\n\nGoblin-Tali’uruk (Lit: Part Orc)\nHalfing-Tali’valah (Lit: Part Human)\n\nOther basic phrases include exclamations, including:\n\nGood-Ayla\nBrilliant-Sul’leyun (Lit: Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("Moonlight Dance", "§bKlaudia Crast", "[!] The story was given by a anonymous man. Though if one must know- he roams the streets of Oren daily.\n-------------------\n\n    Moonlight Dance\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n------------------\n\n~ 1.\n\nThe sun submerged itself beneath the dimming salmon mountaintop to the sight of a harmonic moonlight beginning its climb from the darkened Earth.\n\nThe air was amongst a thinning moisture that\n\n~ 2\n\ntingled the aromatic smell of lingering fern.\nPerfectly placed fingers were present among the warmth of the grass pressed palm. \n\nHer teal eyes pierced the skin to which she glanced, lustfully.\n\n~ 3\n\nEnticing my very being.\nThe charming aura surrounding such a woman pulled me closer to her ever so slightly.\n\nReturning the gaze I then pulled my lips closer to hers, watching the dimming sight of her illuminated -\n\n~ 4\n\nlips under the moonlight.\n\nI found my eyes closing, furthering my body towards hers. The warming sensation of her lips became that of a snug hearth\nbeneath a wood burning stove top.\n\n~ 5\n\nHis mind soon became detained in cadence of her soft lips against his. A joyful ache overtook me as her arms found home upon my shoulders.\n\nNow they were wrapped around my neck.\n\n~ 6\n\nThe slight tug of her arms took me onto the ground alongside her torso. The swing of her affection brought me amongst a trance of cherishment.\n\nThe trance, this trance was soon broken by the inevitable. Pulling my\n\n~ 7\n\nfrom my lips. My adoring eyes opened in a graceful haste to look upon a warming smile within her eyes.\n\nAlmost as if it was a pleasant virus; I too felt a smile manifesting at my mouth.\n\n~ 8\n\nThe beating of our breath was only so slightly shadowed by the delicate rushing water of the creek.\n\nI could only take a moment of admiration towards her before I felt the forward pulling of her weakend hands against my -\n\n~ 9\n\nshirt. The scene fading into an aengulic light as I was pulled down against her chest.\n-------------------\n\nThis story hides the identity of the pair. Although there is more and more descretion upon us.", ""),
        StaticBook("South Laurien", "§bUnknown", "The Battle of\n      South Laurien\n\nThe sky shook as magic carved it's way from the heavens to the treetops of Laurien. Me an Lex'Lur ran throught the city, trying to get to the source of the attack. Climbing the trees, we avoided the fireballs that were thrown at us.\n\n Finally getting past the flames that were eating away at the city, we saw her standing on the highest tree. It was her, Cassandra. \"It is Cassandra herself, there is no hope!\" came a cry from the crowd.\n\n But lo, Prince Native himself appeared, and he rallied us against our attackers. \"Slay the ghouls that claw at our feet!\" he cried. So with sword in hand, I joined the soldiers in their tasks. As soon as we dealt with them another threat arose.\n\n\"The sky!, look at sky!\" Looking up, I shouted in fear. The sky swarmed with ghasts, raining death upon us. Scrambling to mount a defense, many allies died in the resulting attack. We finally managed to take them down, one brought down by my own arrow.\n\nIblees's power waned, and his curse of night was lifted. Weakened, Cassandra left, and we set to work putting out the fires. In the aftermath many lifes were lost, and Prince Native was wounded. But we had defended Laurien,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-and the trees would live to see another day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Two Doors", "§bDolan Velethen", "Two doors, both opaque in feature, stood in front of two staggly men. On the left stoff Veren, a human whose life was reached half. To his right stood Hijol, a wood elf younger than a fox out of season.\n\nIn between them was a sign that read \"Choose carfully\". Hijol inspected the sign and claimed that the sign was closer to the right door than the left one.\n\nAfter some long discussion the two decided that they must both choose the same door. They felt tired and rested.\n\nThe next marrow Hijol woke to fine two sleeping children. Both girls of unrecognizable race. He awoke one and quickly told her his tale. \"The right door is correct\" He notes that the sign has dissappeared. \"There was a sign that read 'There must be only\n\none right door'\".\n\nMeanwhile Veren awoke to find the other girl. Afyer he told her she must not trust Hijol, the two groups conjoined.\n\nFighting words came out. In one corner stood anger and spite.\n\nThe other stoff curriosity and fear. The winner, only the one brave enough to turn a knob,\n\nThey grew weary and slept another night. The next marrow Hijol's girl and Veren's girl awoke to find themselves alone and, adults.\n\nIn Hojol's girl's mind she had two facts, she must choose a door with Veren's girl, and it has to be  the right one. Veren's girl was to scared to speak to Hijol's girl.\n\nHijol's girl only had one option, in her mind, she must take out veren's girl to\n\ncontinue...\n\nHer fists hit her face. Her blood tained her tunic. Fist meet fist, and death was quick.\n\nHijol's girl turned the right knob slowly. On the other side was horrer. Both doors went to the same place. A small\n\nbedrock room with a sign that read \"Life isn't going to bend it'self to your perceptions.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Cold Defiance", "§bTelperian Faroar", "Death abounds cold unwavering frozen to the hands of the murders who stalk the lands seeking revenge for a crime gone uspoken from the mouths of the innocent.\n\nHard cold despair rains from the skys striking the ground with the heavy beads of blood falling from the heavens to the mortals who stand high and mighty upon their throwns of lies and unbroken unchanging laws that are over looked.\n\nLife is the essence to all the breath flowing throughout the veins of all giving light to the dark breaking the bridges between mortal and immortal it cross's all boundaries untouched.\n\nCold senseless murder a force diriven from madness and spite at all truth and light in the little array of life displayed upon the land, hard to play a act with blood upon your hands and life staining your soul\n\nGreen lusturous life flowing from the streams of the cloudy abyss that stems roots of happiness and growth into the grounds of warm abundant free flowing wings of light spread out like a blanket over the land\n\nWaves crashing breaking upon the unseen landscapes hidden underneath the watery depths unopened is the book that lies underneath the sands of time hidden in a library at the heart of knowledge locked under the men sworn to oath\n\nTorn broken and shaking the man stands upon the corner drifting into the smoke flowing from the cracks between life and death steadily growing heavier and entangling him forcing upon him a choice between death and life\n\nThe moon a silent sentinal upon the deep blue ocean sprawled across the night sky a beacon of hope for travelers weary of the heat of day fading from the rising darkness consuming the nights oblique deceptive heart beat\n\nTime holds all things but change is woven into it seemless hand and hand they move fluently unbroken unchanging never stopping the two must race for a end that is non existant for as long as they continue all life follows\n\nThe light colorful leafs fall through the air drifting upon a breeze unseen by the eyes splaying across the ground slowly moving away as if attempting to hold on yet wishing to go somewhere new\n\nTaken and broken is the man who has been enslaved and forced upon to work the lands of others and breath the air of servants ever wanting never loving anyone truelly forgetting the meaning to live\n\nA expanse a demension locked from those who seek to use it all but a handful fall into the little space that sits between the books upon the dusty shelf it defines the borders between mortal and immortal\n\nCloudy is the sky that drifts past dimming all light that floods in draining the darkness from the earth bleeding it out from the breaking cracking ground under foot to leave behind all else\n\nA mist floats over the dense forested path leading through the patches of ferns and tall grass to the center of the beast a forest spanning leagues into the hills heading for a clearing hidden from sight underneath a dense covering of leafs and branchs\n\nDrifting fading leaving behind all that seemed whole and real in a world so clouded with ideas opinions and dreams that could consume everything that comes underneath the clouds of a revolution a new beginning the start of something great\n\nInspiration dedication and undeniable faith in the unknown holding onto things unseen not displayed beneath a case held beneath your peering eyes to lock away the heart of a man within the heart of a tyrant hide from fear and be opressed by the truth\n\nLife solid and whole its a beacon for inspiration and great works of art yet we praise the very thing that is our demise it gives us hope to keep breathing we live to keep life to make life to know that when we leave life will continue moving on\n\nSteadfast untrue believable these words could lead us to believe to lie to contain the ignorance of words contained within the mouths of foolish mens hearts bearing thoughts and deeds that show truth that are born from fear, fear of what is to come", ""),
        StaticBook("Zpirit Buuk", "§bShreck", "DUH ZPIRIT BUUK\n\n   rulg tew awl ub duh shomoz whu halped mi ryte diz buuk.\n\n  ELEMENTUL ZPIRITZ\n\n*Skathach-Zpirit ub fiya\n\n*Akathro-Zpirit ub watur\n\n*Bregthar-Zpirit ub earth\n\n*Fiarza-Zpirit ub wind agh air\n\n*Kulthark-Zpirit ub metul\n\n*Neizdark-Zpirit ub sturm\n\n*Binazdar-Zpirit ub lite\n\n*Radzanib-Zpirit ub darknuzz\n\n*Fanzra-Zpirit ub chaoz\n\n*Arznaf-Zpirit ub ordur\n\n*Ringat-Zpirit ub lief\n\n*Tagnir-Zpirit ub death\n\n*Omnizan-Zpirit ub zpace, intertwindud wif etz partnur, Sandru\n\n*Sandru-Zpirit ub tyme\n\n  IMMORTUL ZPIRITZ\n\n*Votar-Zpirit ub duh hunt\n\n*Enrohk-Zpirit ub bluudluzt, zavagery agh war\n\n*Shezept-Zpirit ub revunge, plotz agh stelth\n\n*Jevex-Zpirit ub ordur, hard wurk, agh zelf zakrifize\n\n*Ixli-Zpirit ub forbidun knowludge, truuf agh judgemunt\n\n*Ogrol-Zpirit ub dezpair, zapped strength agh entrapmunt\n\n*Kor-Zpirit ub duh flat\n\n*Ankrus-Zpirit ub duh zea, fishurmen agh zafe travulz\n\n*Arwa-Zpirit ub furtiluti, harvuzt agh farmun\n\n*Anyhuluz-Zpirit ub deztruction, malishush intunt, internul stryfe\n\n*Akezo-Zpirit ub helth, vitality agh heelun\n\n*Paxahru-Zpirit ub stewpudity agh arroganze\n\n*Ublulhar-Zpirit ub hope agh new beginunz\n\n*Ghorza-Zpirit ub travul\n\n*Rolfizh-Zpirit ub azzazzinashuns agh poizun\n\n*Trokorl-Zpirit ub engineerun, mashinery agh buldun\n\n*Luara-Zpirit ub duh moon\n\n*Ramakhet-Zpirit ub duh dezurt agh zand\n\n*Krathol-Zpirit ub payn zuffern agh ztarvashun\n\n*Veist-Zpirit ub illushun, trikz agh theivury\n\n*Freygoth-Zpirit ub duh wild agh wild animulz\n\n*Glutros-Zpirit ub greed agh beun phat\n\n*Thulezia-Zpirit ub luzt, plezure agh beautifulnuzz\n\n*Isuz-Zpirit ub lub, carun agh tranquiliti\n\n*Orgon-Zpirit ub dezease, pestilence agh failur\n\n*Urin-Zpirit ub rain agh hail\n\n*Kesaroth-Zpirit ub envi agh beun jelluz\n\n*Leyd-Zpirit ub dominanze agh strength\n\n*Scorthuz-Zpirit ub kleansing agh purgin\n\n*Theruz-Zpirit ub intelligunze agh lernun\n\n*Gentharuz-Zpirit ub zmithun, smeltun, induztry agh forgin\n\n*Ikuras-Zpirit ub fear agh inzanity\n\n*Drelthok-Zpirit ub zleepun agh dreemz\n\n*Eathruz-Zpirit ub dawn agh duzk\n\n*Kotrestruu-Zpirit ub memury agh duh rekordun uf knowludge\n\n*Lethrothak-Zpirit ub hindzite agh excuzuz\n\n*BETHARUZ-ZPIRIT UB BEER, GRIIN AGH CELEBRASHUN!!!!!!!\n\n   ANZESTRAL ZPIRITZ\n\n*Krug-Duh firzt shomo evur agh duh hozhuzt ork tew evur lib. Hi iz duh hozhuzt zpirit\n\n*Lur-Hozhuzt hunter en hiztury\n\n*Rax-Hozhuzt warriur ub awl tyme\n\n*Gorkil-Duh hozhiezt militari stratiguzt agh tactishun\n\n*Braduk-Ah faymed hozh chieftun\n\n*Dom-Duh zecund hozhezt shomo\n\n*Ugluk-A kub ub Gorkil, hozh warriur\n\n*Azog-Duh hozhezt smif en hiztory\n\n*Kurak-Alzo grukd az duh howlur ub Lur, wen zummond et kauzuz duh shomo tew tranzform intew ah half ork, half howlur, dey luze der mynd wile dey ar tranzfurmd\n\n*Tor-Knewn fur hiz kalm, kollective intellekt agh stronkth\n\n*Trickster-Knewn fur hiz zubterfuge\n\n*Bralkor-Knwen fur hiz rezuztunze tew physikul damag\n\n*Jarkun-Knewn fur hiz dexterity agh zpeed\n\n*Yar-Knewn fur hiz hozh wizdum agh zpirituality\n\n*Yaggo-Duh hozhezt ridur ub awl tyme\n\n*Dregort-Duh hozhezt boat buldur agh kaptun tew evur lib\n\n*Grumbah-Ah hozh buildur\n\n*Vargo-Knewn az beun ah veri hozh alchemizt\n\n  HOZH URUKZ\n\nShreck-Wun ub duh hozhiezt urukz tew lib, hi iz blu agh stronk agh zmart agh handzum agh kewl agh stronk\n\nReynuh-Ah hozhie peepun uruk whu iz veri stronk agh zmart\n\n*Wun-Ah veri stronk ogre\n\n*Glumpuzz-Ah nub'hozh uruk whu iz rehd", ""),
        StaticBook("Aging Potion", "Pinsir99", "Aging Potion\n==================\nStill being worked out, \nthis potion increases the aging process by twenty five percent per day, everyday. \n===================Ingredients:\n1 Cup Savvil, Crushed\n1 Cup Aqua Vitae\n\n¼ Cup Swamp Blossom Nectar\n⅓ Cup Tippin’s Root, Crushed\n===================Method:\n1.Bring Aqua Vitae to a simmer in a cauldron\n2. Place Saffvil and Tippen’s in a woven spider string pouch, common to those\n\nused in tea making.\n3. Infuse into Aqua Vitae until mixture is a sickly pink color.\n4. Slowly add Swamp Blossom Nectar, drop by drop, making sure each is properly infused before adding the next one.\n5.Leave at simmering head for one to two hours\n\n6.Remove from the cauldron, bottle quickly.\n\nNote- Adding Elrow Berries, Drake’s Tail, Or Dwarvern Pumpkin increases how long the effects last, not the potency.\n\n(Original recipie by the deceased Laerny Marrows. Copied and restored by Aerius Adurond.)", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorely Mistaken", "BadPumkin987", "Ugly man with a fat cat, why is it he got so fat? Was it fish, or cream, or milk? Or perhaps the cat's food being filled!\nUgly man, why are you so? Is it age, your body old? Was it wrinkles, withered hands? Ancient smiles, gone away.\nThey call them old,\n\nugly, fat but do they truely see just that?\nIf that is so, they are sorely mistaken.", ""),
        StaticBook("Simon's Mind", "§bJistuma", "So I randomly found one of the clerics making a group to go investigate a chapel. I decided to join in. Two clerics, someone in mask and robes that would be killed on sight in Abresi, the Doctor, The blueberry elf (or at least one of them), and then\n\nanother one was with me as well.\n\nWe were lead to a volcano, near it actually. To a broken stairway, I had to climb up some vines since all the others were in armor, and attach a rope for them. Up the staircase was a chapel, where we\n\nwould meet Simon. Thought he didn't show up at the entrance. So we went inside into the dungeon.\n\nThe chapel was empty, but the people noticed the arrow pointing down. They thought something was under there and there was, a passage down to\n\na dungeon of sorts.\n\nDown there we found what appeared to be a riddle.\n\nMind over Matter\n\nDoth thy mindless hands wish for wisdom or material, brawn or brains?\n\nInside that room, two chests, seems like a trap.\n\nAlso a hole in the wall. The chests were empty and safe, and the hole was the answer. One of the mechanims that existed in Silva Insula, where you had to place something in. It opened a door down\n\nto tombs.\n\nIn them it spoke of the Lance, Guardians.\n\nThe Lances path they never strayed.\nFoward unto dawn, they did, marching to his demise, only to find death waiting. With open arms they greeted death like true, old\n\nfriends. Xan, protects.\n\nThat was what was fully written.\n\nWe seem to have found Simon there, in the library. The Cleric started making talk to him.\n\nSimon spoke of Xan, a guardian of\n\nInnocence. A deity. There seems to have been a whole group that worshiped Xan.\n\nIt appears the cleric drugged him... then performed some magic on him, and then we were transported into another realm? I don't know what to write about this.\n\nThere is a chest board in from of us, a big one.\n\nSo I played against Simon, and won. He went all green afterwards. The cleric then did his magic and we went into another realm.\n\nThis realm is pretty weird. the stone\n\nunder our feet is yellow, and there is a giant floating clock, with a few many smaller ones around. There are also giant black towers.\n\nNothing too big was done in that realm, the cleric continued to heal Simon or something of the kind.\n\nSoon we were in another. This one had willow trees with a white bark and glowing leaves. Then I turn and there is a walkway up, supported by nothing. Fully white stone, it's trully magical.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry: Volume 2", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Poetry\n      Volume Two\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n        Courage\n\nIt is a thing you use\nWhen you can't go to the end,\nWhen all seems lost\nAnd you can't defend.\n\nYou use it as\nIt combines with your will,\nAll you need to do is\nLet it give its fill.\n\nThe choice is yours,\nGive in or go,\nThough in the end\nOnly you will know.\n\nSee with your spirit\nAnd not with fear,\nfor then you will know\nThat courage is here.\n\n        The Path\n\nI come again,\nTo a place I know well.\nOne that I always,\nSeem to dwell.\n\nA place where,\nThings do not change.\nNor do I attempt,\nTo rearrange.\n\nA ghost appears,\nThat I do not know.\nI know his name,\nYet my memory doesn't show.\n\nIn his eyes I see,\nThings I have lost.\nThings that have happened,\nAt a dearly cost.\n\nAs I get up to leave,\nThe ghost comes too.\nDown the path,\nThat I always knew.\n\nSuddenly I forget,\nWhere I am to go.\nThe ghost then leads,\nAs if it does know.\n\nBut then something,\nGets in the way.\nBlocking our path,\nThe path I wish to stay.\n\nI look at this animal,\nLike it should not be.\nThe animal looks back,\nStraight at me.\n\nIt's vaporous shape,\nAnd looks not kind.\nIt twists and turns,\nAs if it's in my mind.\n\nIt attacks with fear,\nAnd poisons with doubt.\nI then manage,\nTo give a shout.\n\nThe ghost comes forth,\nAnd the animal backs away.\nAnd I run back to the place,\nWhere the animal wants me to stay.\n\nThe ghost comes with me,\nAnd reminds me again.\nOf why I go up the path,\nOver and over again.\n\nI walk the path again,\nAnd see the animal come.\nThe fear comes again,\nThough I do not run.\n\nIt attacks and lashes,\nBut now I only pass through.\nThe ghost nods in approval,\nAs I do what I was meant to do.\n\nTime crawls by,\nAnd my will wears small.\nBut the ghost keeps me going,\nAnd I try to stand tall.\n\nThe end of the path,\nDraws near by the sight.\nThe animal is now transparent,\nWhich I know to be right.\n\nI finally come,\nTo the end of my path.\nAnd I do give,\nA slightly small laugh.\n\nThe cost now gone,\nKnowing that I did my best.\nFinally at last,\nMy memory is at rest.\n\n       The Lake\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening's yawn.\n\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed.\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don't seem to last.\n\nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes smaller still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\n\nIt has become ten times smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven though it has not changed.\nTo other people it might be normal,\nbut to me it is considered strange.\n\n         Ideas\n\nI walk in a city,\nOne false and true.\nOne in which buildings grow,\nAnd keep coming up anew.\n\nSome outsides are nice,\nWith insides rotten,\nOthers opposite,\nBut soon forgotten.\n\nI walk through some,\nAlways remaining the same,\nYet others I go through,\nThat just aren't tame.\n\nSome are giants,\nYet smaller ones are more.\nSome have large openings,\nAnd others a small door.\n\nSome are designed well,\nOutside and through,\nOthers need work,\nMaybe to start anew.\n\nWhen a building is finished,\nIt does relax fast,\nAnd people move in,\nIt done at last.\n\nTHE END\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Followed", "§bUnknown", "*The  pages appear old and it's writting hardly legible as the author seems to have written hastily.*\n\n\n       The Followed\n\nThe first thing that hits you, is the dark. The never-ending darkness laid out before you. They say it drives men crazy, oh the screams. The screams of tainted souls all stuck in a realm of neither life or death, Forever doomed just waiting...\n\nWaiting for what you may ask? Nor you or me knows the answer,but sometimes traveller i can hear them,hear them whisper my name.. In the darkness they call out to me,tring to eat my very flesh and bone, chewing feasting.\n\nI can feel them long for my soul! I know it is only a matter of time.. Blood.. blood is what they hunger for..\"We are not living nor dead. We are the chosen, The breed of eternity.\" Those cursed words they.. they repeat and repeat inside my mind!\n\nI’m not sure..I..the tunnels,they seems to never end! Tunnels of pure madness and evil . They call me the \"walker\" for what reason i do not know. A wanderer, some stranger to all that I meet. The spirits, they call to me, one by one...\n\nThere walls..the terrible walls.. The darkness is a blinding sight  yet it makes me feel enlightned far more than before. And the silence,the silence who tears the very sense out of your mind. I was a man once, a mortal just like you traveller...\n\nWith a family, friends, I had it all.. but that was before that night. \"That night\" I tell you was the day I lost it all.. my home burned.. my people massacred.. Well, some where lucky, and were able to survive for a little while..\n\nMy family did not have that fortune. My wife was first, Torn apart by some sort of device, it tore her limb after limb,i could do nothing more than to watch in pain and silence.\n\n*After the odd read, you question the sanity and legitimacy of the author.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilds Task", "§bArinislia", "For this simple task, I left from my Guide Lillith's Grove and set off into the southern wilds nearby. I ventured here before with another task of collecting the different plants and found this area quite enjoyable to walk through.\n\nDay 1\n\nI found a suitable clearing where I quickly set up camp. I find it humorous that my guide think I would find this unpleasant to do. She seem to forget that I had been travelling for a time and although I do find this quite demeaning,\n\nI am rather used to it now. I laid out the items she has given me. Three jungle saplings, 3 seeds, 8 bonemeal, 6 dough, the tent set up behind me of course, 1 dandelion, 4 empty bottles, and one water bottle. Given how much bonemeal I was given, I assumed\n\nit was meant for the seeds rather than the saplings itself. \n\nDay 2\n\nI set about planting the seeds into the ground near the tent and moved alittle further out to plant the jungle saplings. I am not familiar with\n\nthis plant so I have given it as much space as possible. Keeping them watered, I preceded to plant the dandelion into the ground just outside the flap of my tent. The dough provided is serving well, only making small amounts of bread and taking little\n\n bites as possible while filling the bottles up with water at a nearby stream. \n\nDay 3 \n\nIt is quite peaceful out here. I always found nature to be so. Though I do love the magical structures and buildings of my\n\nkind more, this will do as well. I am been pondering this Grand Task for awhile. I have a few ideas and will take them in motion once I am done here. The seeds have started to spout, showing life within the plant as it grows. I sprinkled just a small\n\namount of bonemeal on the plants, helping them along while I went to tend to the saplings. The saplings themselves seemingly larger now as well. \n\nDay 4\n\nI awoke to find the seeds turned into small strands of wheat.\n\nThey are still quite green and not yet ready to be harvested, though I think I shall leave them be and let them stay grown. The saplings have grown larger as well, already taller than my own form with a few branches sprouted here and there. This task\n\nseems simple enough, doing what I already do, observe. I do recall standing in the fairy ring, feeling the life around me. I heard the song once more, I seek to hear it again. \n\nDay 5\n\nI bathe in the nearby spring to make my\n\nappearance presentable to a passerby that happens to come across me. The saplings now turned into small jungle trees. I sprinkled some bonemeal on them so they can grow alittle more faster. The wheat now fully grown and quite full of life.\n\nI feel that my time here is coming to an end. I have already packed up the tent and put away the supplies that was given to me. The trees now grown even more than when I have last seen them. The dandelion's petals bloomed fully and resting near where I\n\nhave slept. Prehaps I shall return here after I am attuned. Though I do think there are more tasks ahead.", ""),
        StaticBook("TF: Vol. XII", "VonEbs", "The Flagship\nVolume XII  (9/30/13)\n\n===================\nContents:\nA Rex Unites the Uruks\nThe Ac’telarah Patrimony\nA New Construction in Luminaire\nAdunia Abandons the Westerlands\nRegency in Salvus\n\nThe Goldman-Horen Edicts\nLand Grants offered in Ruska and the Trog\nHeralding a New Kingdom\n==================\nA Rex Unites the Uruks\n\nThe Uruks of the Trog have of late become more and more involved in daily life\n\nin Anthos. Reversing the trend the previous decade of isolation, orcs can now commonly be found in Luminaire Plaza, outside the church in Salvus, and along the roads to the Cloud Temple. Spearheading this effort to bring the uruks into contact with the\n\nother races is the newly titled Rex Grool’Azog’Gorkil. Grool, formerly Wargoth of the Gorkil Clan, has served in many positions in the Uzg and Krugmar, from High Yazgurten to Wargoth. Some of his previous accomplishments include building the Trog,\n\nsetting up a new currency. the bone token, and leading a Waagh against Malinor.  \n\nGrool recently claimed the position of Rex, and so far has remained unchallenged. This is not the first time the pale orc has aspired to this title,\n\nhowever, in all previous Rex Klomps he was ultimately defeated. Only time will tell what path Grool will choose for Krugmar and the uruks.  \n~Ebs\n===================\nThe Ac’telerah Patrimony\n\nThe Magestate, headed by Artimec, has elected to rejoin with Malinor in the face of threats from the Kingdom of Ruska. Artimec, the current guild master of the Arcane Delvers, will become the governor of the province of Ac’telerah, including both the\n\nArcane Delver fort and the village of Lenniel. This comes after the Magestate had separated from Malinor in an act of defiance against the High Council for alleged dealings with the Dark Brotherhood, a shadowy organization filled with assassins.\n\nAc’telerah had then been formally recognized and allied with William Horen, the former King of Renatus, formerly known as Oren. This was announced with the posting of the Sapphire-Emerald Amalgamation, which has been coldly received by the\n\nresidents of Malinor, who by and large want nothing to do with the Talarans. Whether both sides will maintain their sides of the agreement is unknown, but this treaty indicates growing stability in a region plagued by shifting alliances and collapsing\n\nempires.\n===================\nA New Construction in Luminaire\n\nIf you have been in Luminaire in the past few elven weeks, you can not help but notice the looming building that has been constructed\n\non the west side of the main square. Only the Lower and High Councils have been permitted access, and with good reason. If you were to climb the newly finished stairs, you would be assaulted by a the bright light of magma shining from below what appears\n\nto be an impossible obstacle course in the form of the resurrected Gauntlet. \n\nThe Gauntlet is not new to Malinor, as there was an extremely popular version located in Laurelin during the Golden Age of Aegis. The general premise\n\nis that both Mali and other competitors attempt to complete the Gauntlet for a minas prize. It is perilous to say the least, but the prizes can become quite large. In Aegis, any Mali that completed it was awarded 5000 minas and a plaque on a wall\n\nlocated behind the obstacle course. Until it is determined exactly how difficult the current Gauntlet is, the prizes will be predictably smaller, but the accumulating pot could grow large. The entry fee will be 50 minas, half of which will go towards a\n\njackpot to be won by the next person to complete it. After nine competitors complete the course, it will be redesigned.\n\nThe Gauntlet will be opening soon, so be prepared to test your agility and endurance like never before.\n==================\n\nAdunia Abandons the Westerlands\n\nThe Kingdom of Adunia, a vassal state of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, has moved to the south, within the contemporary borders of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. There were clashes reported along the border,\n\nas well as raids by the Flays against the various settlements in Adunia. The land that the Adunians left behind is slowly being transformed by the strelts of Kralta, who are restoring much of its natural beauty. A large wall has also been constructed,\n\nhowever there is no sign that Ruska will be attempting to cut off Malinor from the rest of the human lands as was attempted in the past by the White Roses and the Kingdom of Kaedrin. \n\nThis is just another chapter in the history of the Adunians,\n\nwho have been moving from place to place for decades, attempting to find a permanent home to settle down in. Their stay in the Westerlands was just one stop, with other stops in Cal Dais, Vaerhaven, and even the War Uzg for a time.\n\nDespite the constant shifting of their population, they have managed to resist dispersing like the Subudai did in Asulon. With its exit from the region, Adunia has also departed the Northern Coalition, which is now dominated by King Seigmund Carrion of\n\nRuska. A further report will be filed next week detailing the conditions in the new Kingdom of Adunia in the south.\n===================\nRegency in Salvus\n\nWith the unexpected death of King Aron Bedevere, Salvus has been left with an heir\n\nnot yet eligible to take the throne. Lord-Regent Nigel Therving has been serving as the Regent of Salvus, and is holding the reins while Aron’s son, King-Infante Relenkai, matures into adulthood. Salvus is currently facing possible threats from\n\nthe other human kingdoms, who wish to annex parts of Salvus’ fertile lands, and might use this moment of weakness to strike against it. The Lord-Regent has his work cut out for him ensuring that Relenkai will have a kingdom to inherit when he comes of\n\nage.\n===================\nThe Horen-Goldman Edicts\n\nGoldman, a familiar name to some, has been appearing at the top of several documents recently issued by the Treasury of Renatus. This relative, Tuv\n\nGoldman, of the famous, or perhaps infamous, Toveah Goldman,  has apparently been granted the position of treasurer of Oren previously held by now King Silus Horen. At one point, Toveah Goldman held the largest share of property owned\n\nby a commoner in Oren, and thus the world, owning completely the towns of Baile and Aldersburg, as well as large chunks of the Westerlands and Abresi. \n\nThe Horen-Goldman Edicts seem to be targeting business in Abresi and the rest\n\nof what is left of Renatus, and have so far resulted in the threatening of closure of several shops in Abresi. Taverns are having to register with the government, and stricted taxes are being put in place, Already there are rumors of a black market\n\ndeveloping, though these rumors could not be confirmed. These are bold steps for Renatus, the economy of which has been faltering in recent years much like that of the other nations of Anthos.\n===================\nLand Grants offered\n\nin Ruska and the Trog\n\nFor the enterprising poor in Anthos, new options have opening in both Orcish and Human lands. In the former, the Trog is offering small farming plots and houses to “Pinkies” willing to pay a small amount of their crops.\n\nA similar program has been set up in Ruska, with a 10% tithe in place. Aimed at attracting new residents in Anthos, the Trog system, which has been operating for longer than the Ruska program and benefits from close proximity to the Cloud Temple, is\n\nproving quite successful. It was started by the current Rex, Grool’Azog’Gorkil, and has been considered a success by observers. Similar programs are reportedly being considered by other nations, though it is argued that the current\n\npopulation of Anthos, which has been in decline for a number of years, can only support so many farmers. Food is already extremely cheap due to Aron Bedevere driving down the prices in Salvus at the beginning of Anthos to undercut his competitors,\n\nand there is more than enough to feed everyone. The life of a farmer in Anthos tends to be comfortable, but routes for elevation in society are few outside of military circles. It is not known how this new group of farmers will affect the economy of\n\nAnthos, but food prices are expected to remain low for the foreseeable future. \n~Ebs\n===================\nHeralding a New Kingdom\n\nIn an edict issued by the Kingdoms of Ruska and Renatus,\n\nthe Kingdom of Herendul has been formally recognized. Ruled by House Winter, it is the northernmost Human nation, and consists of the Duchy of Hanseti, along with a few other northern counties. Crops do not grow well in the North, so the new kingdom might\n\nhave to import food to some extent in order to feed its growing population. It is currently forming a military from the remnants of House Winter’s personal guard, but some question how effective it will be fighting the forces in the North\n\nif they ever return in strength. Certainly King Winter has much work to do, and now has the authority to do what needs to be done to secure the North against ever threatening Chaos.\n~Ebs\n===================\n\nEditor’s Note\n\nA monthly subscription of the Flagship can be purchased for the small sum of 50 minas, with a guarantee of 4 issues an ((rl)) month. If you would like to be a journalist, or write reports for the Flagship, please contact Editor\n\nEbs Telrunya via messenger pigeon, as there is always room for more journalists on the Flagship Team.\n\nMany thanks, \n~Ebs Telrunya, Editor of the Flagship", ""),
        StaticBook("A Book", "Anonymous", "It was the raw and wild duo of earth and natural growth: the Aenguls Cernunnos and Cerridwen. These two incorporeal beings are the patrons and deities of which Druids call upon for influence over nature. With the elven\n\npenchant for similar ideals as the Druidic Aspects, the two factions frequently blend. In this, the Druids exist.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apparitions", "§bVeldryn Uuthlini", "Apparitions are formed when a large group of souls die in a particularly horrific way in a single location. Examples of this may be being burnt alive, sailors drowning on a sinking ship or simply a massacre.\n\nThis however is not to say that all mass-deaths will cause the formation of an apparition.\n\nFor an apparition to form a particularly dark soul or group of dark souls with their mind set on malevolent behavior must have perished with this large group of souls.\n\nUpon death this dark soul binds all the other souls together to form an evil manifestation known as an Apparition. Apparitions gradually grow more powerful as they age.\n\nOnly a few Apparitions were ever found. Three existed in the realm of Anthos. \n\nThey owned no Names, but were described as the following.\n\nApparition of 10 Souls\nThe weakest from the three.\n\nApprition of 50 Souls\nThe one, founded in the base of the Delvers\n\nApparition of 100 Souls\nThe most powerfull one recorded.\n\nThe Apparition of one hundred souls appeard in it's spectre form like a woman. This might be happening, because the dominant soul could be the one of a woman. This Apparition was also known to be the most dangerous of all.\n\nIt was also known that the Black Scourge summoned it's powers and made a contract with it.\n\nAfter the fall of the Black Scourge and Anthos, this Apparition became a \"Wandering\" Apparition. The most dangerous of all Spiritual beings.\n\nIt losed it's pillar, but a myth tells about that this being closed itself into a prison. Waiting to be released once again upon the world.\n\nThe only way to stop this being to destroy a town, is with the help of Clerics and other holy magical users.\n\nAfter the races arrived on Athera, the Apparition of hundred souls might aswell passed the portal.\n\nIt was recorded that this being was able to disguise itself as someone, but obvious signs like red eyes showed the truth behind the disguise.\n\nA demonic being, called Vangron. Found out on how to summon a Apparition and used his new founded ritual to doom the races multiple times in Anthos. How to summon one is unknown, only the person called Vangron would know, even if it is known to be the -\n\n- most dangerous ritual in existence. Since you never knew wich Apparition would appear...\n\nNo more informations were found.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Veldryn Uuthlini-", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish", "§bArtemis", "I wish that I could find an amazing ring unlike any other to present to one I may marry one day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wishes", "§bAmadeus \"Balorien\" Glaciem", "Dear Headless horseman.\n\nI want your skeleton horse for halloween thank you!\n\n\n\n       Sincerly Amadeus", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish", "§bJudas Windsor", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n\nJudas Windsor's wish:\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nMy wish is to have 2500 minas, I will use this for good cause by sparing some of it away has an act of kindness and to buy myself some luxuries.", ""),
        StaticBook("'The Balrog'", "§bArinislia", "'The Taint'\n\n7th of The Grand Harvest, 1475\n\n       The day was calm and gentle. The sun was high, shining its rays down upon the Father Tree as the druids went about their day. One of the druid children suddenly runs up, gasping for breath as she appeared to have been running.\n\nShe looked panicked, saying that she ran into a Dread Lord summoning something in the nearby woods. Suddenly a loud shriek was heard. . All look up the natural carved stairs of the Father Tree to see the Dread Lord stand before them.\n\n. A ghoul standing next to him along with some followers, the Dread Lord unleashed the ghoul down upon the druids, commanded to kill them all. During this, the Dread Lord then turned and advanced up the tree,\n\n, telling his followers to block all that dare move up. The ghoul was quickly defeated, but not before spreading its taint on all that it bit along with ones that were near when it exploded.\n\nIt appeared that if something wasn’t done quickly to cleanse, they perished.\n\n       The druids now advancing further up the tree, the followers were quickly removed before advancing further up.\n\n. Again the druids were blocked and met with a horrible abomination. The Dread Lord cackled down at them, before unleashing a balrog upon the druids, charging down full force.\n\nSeveral that were in the way were easily knocked off the tree to their deaths.  The druids seemed unorganized, yet with some coordination from a few within the order, they quickly rooted the balrog and threw it off the tree.\n\nThe Dread Lord far gone by then yet the top of the tree tainted. The druids advance upward, circling around the taint and focused, using their healing magic to remove the corruption of the tree.\n\nBelow where the balrog  fell off the tree, several came from different nations and organizations and struck down the abomination where it stood.  With the Father Tree healed once more, the druids descended down and helped cleanse and heal the wounded.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fear and Misund.", "§bLillith Winterleaf", "Fear and Misunderstanding;\nThe Wihuns from a survivor's perspective.\n\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\n\nI was taken from my home.\n\n\nIt was the middle of a perfectly normal day on Asulon, there was a light rain in the early hours that left the air clean and fresh, and the birds were singing happily outside my Inn. I ran an Inn about a '\n\nday's horse ride from Skravia. My husband had built a large Fortress there and I built my Inn within the upper courtyard next to the stables,  overhanging the cliffs above our farmlands. It was a popular stopover for travelers from\n\nSkravia heading out into the wilds to hunt, gather lumber, fish, or simply travelling. Some, including a few of my fellow Druids, and members of Skravia's royal family, enjoyed coming to my Inn for liesure, to get away and relax, so we were accustomed to\n\nhaving people stop by frequently.\n\nOn this day, the Inn was empty, which was unusual, but I was taking the opportunity to sweep and clean the inn, and as I began wiping down the bar,\n\na man came in holding a piece of paper and wearing a friendly smile. He came over and sat on a stool at the bar, ordering a mug of ale and placing a gold coin on the counter.  I gave him his ale and we began talking.\n\nHe asked about the Inn, if there was anyone else there, then if I knew a Druid named Lillith Whisperblade, me, and I was beginning to grow wary from the rigid way he was speaking, so I said she was not around. But he looked back at his paper,\n\nthen slid it over to me, it had my name, a physical description, and the word DRUID written on it, and he told me there would be 'no more games' and that I was coming with him.\n\nI backed away but I was trapped behind the counter, and he stood and came around, pulling out his blade. As I spoke to try and talk reason with him, he backhanded me, telling me to be silent and come with him,\n\nor else.  I refused, and he slashed at me suddenly, cutting off half my left ear.  I jumped over the counter and reached the door as one of the guards from Skravia came in for his regular drink.\n\nHe saw my ear and tried to defend me, but my attacker yelled after me as I ran, calling me a witch and stabbing my would-be rescuer, leaving him to bleed out as he caught me.\n\nHe knocked me out and I awoke in a cage, built on a raised platform in a room designed like a chapel, pews facing the cage. My attacker was next to me, laying out tools of torture on a small table. He introduced himself as Tyret Wolfgank Farfor,\n\nand asked if I knew why I was taken.  I knew the name, my friend and teacher, Jena, had been tortured by the same man before escaping him. The discussion was calling me a heretic and a witch because I wielded 'magic' as he called,\n\nand would not listen when I tried to explain the difference between nature's gift and void magics. He and his followers all cursed me and any other wielder of ant sort of powers, even the temple monks,\n\nof being the cause of Aegis' destruction, and that they would 'cleanse' us.\n\nThe torture began by slicing and peeling away small portions of skin on my arms and legs, then using a red hot poker to burn the wounds and cauterize them.\n\nHe took a small pocket blade and had one of his men grab my head and force me to look upwards as he pushed the knife through my lower left eyelid and behind my eye, seeking to pry it out intact, but his hand slipped\n\nand I saw a black line spread through my vision as his blade sliced through my eye, blinding it.\n\nHis hand slipped because of a commotion upstairs, he dropped the knife and left one of his younger followers to watch me while he\n\ndealt with it, and I later found out that it was my sister and the King and High King of Skravia with a few if their men. The guard at my inn had survived and reported what happened and me being called a witch,\n\nso they had little doubt who had taken me. The Wihuns had more men, but apparently Tyret said he had not taken their Druid, and they had never mentioned exactly who was taken, so they departed to get more men.\n\nWhile this all happened without my knowledge, the young man I had been left with had come beside me, telling me that all the pain could be over if I renounced my druidic path and joined their cause, that I wad too beautiful to suffer like this,\n\nand I should be with him, he would make them stop and protect me if I would only turn away from my mistakes. I looked him in the eyes and held my kindest smile as I told him my husband would come for me,\n\nand long after the Wihuns were made to answer for their crimes, I would live happily with my husband and our children as a Druid.\n\nThe young man frowned deeply at my response and walked over to the brazier,\n\ntaking a poker right from the heart of the coals, the tip white hot. He came back and held it in front of my face, I could feel the heat and I was terrified, but not nearly expecting what came next.\n\nHe lowered it towards my waist, telling me \"No, there will be no children for you, witch.\" then stabbing me just above the thigh, pressing it through my womb and moving it in circles, I screamed.\n\nI could feel the fire burning me from inside, and he poured a healing potion down my mouth and held his hand over it, making me choke it down through my screams to keep it from killing me,\n\nholding the hot iron within me for what seemed an eternity of pain, but must have been only a minute, then removed it right as the healing potion's effects wore off.\n\nI screamed and cried as Tyret returned down the stairs, asking what was wrong, the young man saying he had simply continued.  They continued on as before, my body going numb on me, my mind crying out for my husband.\n\nAfter another few hours of physical and mental torture, the base shook from a violent explosion, men screaming the front wall had been breached.  They closed their inner gates and grabbed their weapons as a second explosion shook us,\n\nmuch closer, sending rubble down the stairs, and I heard my husband shouting commands to his men as they rushed down the stairs. The fight held at the final gate for many minutes, but my husband and his men broke through\n\nand slew many, though Tyret escaped out a tunnel with many others.  I was released into my husband's arms, only managing a weak smile before finally succumbing to my agony, passing out.\n\nThe rest is history, I awoke at home, a temple monk beside my bed trying to mend me, but he could not, their powers were at the time greatly weakened, and he could not save my womb.\n\nI believe the Wihuns could have been a force of good, but they allowed fear, prejudice, and misunderstanding to rule their actions and became a force of great evil in the world, harming many innocents and few of the 'dark mages' they claimed to target.\n\nI did recently however meet the son of Tyret, and learned the group had disbanded upon his father's death, and he did not agree with the targeting of druids, among others.  I have lived with the injuries and mental\n\ntorment of that dark, horrible day for over a century, never able to bear another child, but blessed with my only son before that terrible day. I devoted myself to the druids, turning my past into my reason, my drive.\n\nI want to bring love and peace and balance back to the world, and let others see that any pain can be endured and still work towards a better tomorrow for everyone. Prejudice only divides and weakens\n\nus against the darkness that follows us from land to land, and now, more divided than ever, we stand prepared to fall for the last time if anything threatens our world with peril once more.\n\nDo not let anger and pain from the past ruin our chances to make this a better world for our children, our grandchildren. We must unite and set our differences aside so we may stand against the darkness and prevail,\n\nlest Iblees the Betrayer prevail over the descendants.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "Jistuma", "Water: seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of live, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbinger of eradication.\n\nDespite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromance yearns to wield.\n\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from the ability\n\nto control \"mana,\" but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is\n\ndifficult to put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it become more simpler tasks.\n\nMany mages use a staff when evoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for instance, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties\n\nthat is possesses, and also because it has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it forms a stream from the end of my\n\nstaff that maintains itself midair. From here, I can move it, project is somewhere, or allow it to dissipate.\n\nOne thing about water evocation that differs from the other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice\n\nwater evocationists begin with controlling pure water in its liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled ((approximately late tier 3)), he is able to change the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defence than liquid water is,\n\nas it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block oncoming projectiles, as a form of short-distance defense, and as a method of harming others. I have personally mastered a technique of blasting an enemy with water, and then freezing\n\nthem in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from the heat of the sun or a torch. To break void ice, the hydromance must either completely lose concentration, or another\n\nmage must do something to break the ice (i.e. a pyromancer melts the ice with magical flames). Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as the wisps of steam are too difficult for even the most trained evocationists to control.\n\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\n\nIntroduction to Hydromancy\n\nWritten by Ev Ar'ahern\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Adunian V.1", "§bJistuma", "-Ancient Adunian-\n\n           OOC:\nThis is an IC book teaching the reader how to read and speak the Ancient Adunian tongue. The book only teaches the very basics: Nouns, verbs, sentence structure and the like. The book\n\nlacks information on descriptive words and some adjectives. For a character to learn what this book offers would take 6-12 months as it is a complicated language. ((That’s 1-2 RL weeks))\nActually typing in Adunian is simple. You go into\n\nGoogle Translate and select Irish. You simply type in what you want to say, and copy-paste the translation into MC text. It’s courtesy to also put the English translation in OOC, making it easier for others to RP.\n\nHave fun learning Adunian!~\n\n            IC:\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll\n          ~=~\n      *200 pages\n       of writing\n       on Adunian\n       is here*\n\nOld Adunian V.1\n\nWritten by Monk Argyll\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wish!", "§bThane Andwise Peregrin", "I, Andwise Peregrin, wish for knowledge to a long forgotten secret.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kha Wish", "§bZhikar", "Sa'vi Metztil in the fountain. Ju'Mukar wishes for a nice new elegant ferrum staff, the staff would have many places to attach things onto it.\n\n\nMeanwhile Mukars kitten, Zhikar,  wishes for ======(the text is crossed and unreadable but a new fast\n\nwas wrote) \nZhikar wishes to know the truth about Mukar. What he really is and to be happy..", ""),
        StaticBook("Gardening Guide", "§b'Finek", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-          How to\n         Remove\n         Weeds\n         from\n         Crops\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nIt has long be tought that when you see a weed in your garden that you should pull it out at once.\n\nThis I say to you is not what you do, lest you rip up your crops with the weeds.\n\nWeeds at an early stage wrap themselves around the very roots of the crop for that is where they find a lot of water going, by doing so it takes away a little water from the crop though not very much.\n\nWhen the time of harvest comes you shall then harvest the crop along with the weeds. Place both the weeds and crops into a basket and throw them into the air, by doing the crops will fall down into the basket.\n\nThe weeds on the other hand are much lighter and would blow away even on a low wind.\n\nAfter repeating this for a good five minutes you should have mostly crops in your basket.\n\nIf you missed a couple you can simply go through it by hand.\n\n\nHere are the risks of what can happen if you do the opposite:\n\n1: The weed has wrapped itself mostly around the crops roots, so by pulling up the weed you risk pulling up the growing crop.\n\n2: Keep the crops well watered, if you don't the weeds will take almost all of it.\n\n3: You need at least a small wind blowing through the air for the weeds to be caried away on the wind, make sure it isn't very strong though or some of your crops might get away!\n\n\n\n          -=+=-\n        Written by\n\n          'Fenik\n     The Cervitaur\n          -=+=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Athera", "§bAzoth Hawksong", "The\nTraveler's\nGuide\nTo\nAthera\n\nThe Cloud Peninsula\nIn every land to which the Descendants have travelled there has been a Cloud Temple.Either the secretive Cloud Order that looks after the Descendant Races is either always one step ahead of the mortal races or the\n\n world truly is littered with empty sandstone monasteries waiting for mortal monks to move in. As is the case with all of the Cloud Temples, violence is both forbidden by law and magically prohibited within the sanctuary’s bounds.\n\nThe Abyss\nA pit of unfathomable depth and size, the Abyss is clearly no natural phenomenon. The fabric of the world itself seems torn there, with magical energies defying the laws of nature. At the edge of the Abyss islands\n\n float on nothing and water forever plunges into the depths without ever filling the Abyss or draining the seas. The Abyss seems impossible, yet there it is, its yawning depths visible to all who travel too far to the west.\n\nThe Shards\nThese colossal burned spikes of land jut out over the Great Abyss towards the west of Athera. Nothing grows upon these jagged fragments of whatever was there before the Abyss was formed. Most Atheran historians believe the shards to be\n\n the result of a cataclysm involving magics beyond the capabilities of mortal magi, although so far no indication has been found of how old the Shards, and by extension the Abyss, are.\n\n Above the shards, upon a floating isle lies what looks like an abandoned city, but it floats too high to be reached by explorers.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Guide on Mages", "§bLerin Hrak", "A rough guide to hunting mages, by Lerin Hrak\n\nForeword, This is only a rough guide and the first book I have written in many years, it will eventually be refined by me in the future.\n\nChapted One, Identifying mages\n\nWhile a mage can be just about anyone, they often will stick to light clothing and carry only basic weapons if any on them, they also tend to favor staffs both to help them focus on spells and to aid them\n\nin walking. Almost never will you see a mage wearing armor as it encumbers them too much and they need as much energy as possible to create their spells.\n\nChapter Two, A Overview of mages\n\nMages are indivduals who have spent many years in learning the ability to harness the void to create spells, which are in a way, altering the physical realm to create something, truthfully I am not learned in that\n\nparticular subject. In this pursuit their bodies are often left physically weaker then average members of their race and they have little time to learn much else to become skilled in it, such as swordsmanship. Mages also rely on their on energy and focus\n\nin order to create their spells, creating a weakness for if they can not focus, then they are next to helpless and only skilled mages can create magic that can actually kill instead of only wounding.\n\nChapter Three, Tactics against Mages\n\nIn my years of experience, I have figured out one of the best tactics to use against a mage is to disrupt their focus, pain is a excellent way to do this, and it is also wise to keep close to them so you can\n\ndisrupt their focus more so as they will not be able to focus without letting their guard down for you  to attack. Another favoured tactic of mine is stealth, for a mage can not attack with a spell if they can not see or hear you, and you can quickly kill\n\nor disable one with a single blow.\n\nChapter Four, A guide to types of mages.\n\nWhile for now the last chapter, this is also one of the most useful as you must be aware of the dangers the different types of mages present. The most basic and common would be a Evocation mage, one who can\n\ncreate things such as fireballs and spikes of ice to use as weapons, they can be deadly both up close and at range if they are skilled enough and clever enough. Next is the summoners, while slightly rare from what I've seen, they can be quite deadly as\n\nthey can summon or create creatures using their spells to fight for them, the beasts themselves are not real in a sense, but they can still injure and only persist while the mage can focus on it.\nNext is the Illusion mages, they are capable of using\n\nspells to confuse and muddle the mind by creating false images and other such things, in the end all they create is false, though they can still be dangerous as many illusions can still appear and feel to quite real.\n\nEpilogue\n\nFor now that is all I shall write of, though they are several other types of mages, I shall expand upon this book in other editions and other entire books, eventually I shall cover abominations aswell.\n\nUntil I get around to writing another, I wish you luck and may the Creator guide you against the Undead threat and others who go against him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 4", "Eenhoornheid", "New Elven Lessons:\n     Volume IV\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the composition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten the simple word in elven to use. To express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before.\n\n1 - oem \n2 - nuit \n3 - hael \n4 - vailu \n5 - kulin \n6 - banih \n7 - laier \n8 - esun \n9 - moiel \n10 - telu \n100 - matelu \n1000 - marmatelu\n\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words to form the names of handheld tools. Some such examples include those below. To those more advanced in Elven others may be thought up.\n\nFer'ame - Axe \nFer'thuln - Pickaxe \nFer'nor - Shovel \nFer'sul - Torch \nFer'bilok - Hammer \nFer'norsae - Hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("Golem Issues", "§bJared Blackfoot", "One of my Golems has become slightly sporadic. It seems my design is slightly flawed, they must be shut down or maintained regularly to prevent their logical functions from deteriorating to an unworkable state. Just another chore for Enas, I suppose.\n\nStill, I should keep an eye on him, things would be bad if they went rampant.\n\n-Jared Blackfoot", ""),
        StaticBook("TOTTA: Book I-2", "SapphireShard", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n-----------\nElements of Alchemy\n    \nVolume I-2 of V\n\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\n--\n\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.”\n\nBut what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is required before that question can be answered and in fact,\n\nif that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir, and concept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon.\n\nthey must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into each of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual,\n\nthey must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into each of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual,\n\nmay understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\n\nFire \n=== \nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\n\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal.\n\nFire can represent rage, anger, hatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will,\n\nand allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear at. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\n\n\n Actions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action of burning, consuming, and destroying.\n\nAlchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon,\n\nbut if one were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos.\n\nIt is true that Chaos is often something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized.\n\nChaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and powerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick,\n\ntwo completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or solely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used.\n\nThe teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\n\nEarth\n===\n\nThe Enduring, The Lifegiver, the Fortifying\n\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things,\n\nI will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength,\n\nthe notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance,\n\nor strength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion.\n\nProtecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also used in antidote potions, disease-curing potions,\n\nand, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders,\n\noften associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also required for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on.\n\nMany of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend,\n\nand using elements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation.\n\nNow, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon transmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals,\n\nfor metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\n\nWater\n===\n\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\n\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water.\n\nOften known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its name for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing,\n\nliquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on drinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid,\n\none must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\n\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life.\n\nBut one can also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic.\n\nThrough oils, one may reap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made\n\nwhich is best made by distilling wine or other liquors\n\nAir\n===\n\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\n\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception,\n\nand even flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes,\n\nthe ways in which to represent Air are quite obvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion,\n\nare rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite rarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather,\n\nwhich is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions centered around this element.\n\nAnother, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and Air intermingle.\n\nWith that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols,\n\nthe next chapter will explain herbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.", ""),
        StaticBook("May'ilu", "Wodehouse", "With a clinking and chiming of bracelets signalling the arrival of her lover, Velara could hardly keep a grin off of her face as she rested her elbows on the furnished wooden counter, hands delicately supporting her head as she watched Mayirr sway\n\ninto the shop, pink hair cascading elegantly down over her precious shoulders. The two stare at each other for a moment; A soft 'Karin'ayla' was all that needed saying. They lingered over each others frames for a moment before Mayirr broke the gaze,\n\nslipping lithely around the counter to cuddle Velara from behind. The pink haired elf's ears twitched sensitively as she held her may'ilu, her cheeks turning a similar colour as they stood there silently. Mere moments passed, and the door to the shop\n\nrattled open, breaking the two apart. \nWatching Velara abruptly disappear down to the basement with a look of utter embarassment, Mayirr smiles, her cheeks flushed with the same feeling as she looks back to greet the customer.", ""),
