        StaticBook("Book of Horen", "§bShady_Tales", "The years passed and went on and on, as time is wont to do. The Descendants, after being cursed by the Great Devil, adapted their lives to suit their new roles. There was, for some time, peace and prosperity amongst the original realms created by the\n\nCreator. One day, upon the cusp of which a red sun rose from the east, King Horen of humanity was approached by an Aengul, a divine messenger of God. This Aengul shone magnificently, illuminated by the light of God, its shades and colors twisting\n\naround one another as it addressed Horen. Its wings swathed in blinding white, it opened its mouth, and through it the Creator spoke. \n\n\"Horen of Man. God has chosen you as his divine prophet, as his mouthpiece on this world, until the day of\n\nyour ascent into the Seven Skies at his order. You are the almighty king, the Creator's chiefmost servant on this hallowed earth. Be jubilant, for you are second to none but me! Humanity is the holy, divine being of God, the human body remaining the most\n\nunadulterated, original form of the Creator's design, not possessing of neither corruption nor mutation. You are the chosen people, and you shall carry out my commands, and your people alone, not your brothers and their kin, shall swear to my commandments\n\nThey are as follows!\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the Creator and Guide of everything that has been created; He alone has made, does make, and will make all things.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Divine\n\nare the Creator's regents in this realm and that their obdience is worship to the Creator.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Aenguls and Daemons are the Creator’s servants.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator\n\nBlessed be His Name, is One, and that there is no unity in any manner like His, and that He alone is our God, who was, and is, and will be.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, has no body, and that He is free from all\n\nproperties of matter, and that they can be no comparison to Him whatsoever.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the first and the last.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name,\n\nand to Him alone, it is right to pray, and that it is not right to pray to any being besides Him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that all the words of the Divines are true.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the\n\nprophecy of Horen I our teacher, blessings be upon him, was true, and that he was the chief of the Divines, both those who preceded him and those who followed him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the entire scrolls that is now in our possession is the\n\nsame that was given to our Divines, blessings be upon them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Holy Scrolls can not be corrupted. \n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, knows all the deeds\n\nof beings and all their thoughts.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, rewards those who keep His commandments and punishes those that transgress them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that there will\n\nbe a revival of the dead at the time when it shall please the Creator, Blessed be His name, and His mention shall be exalted for ever and ever.”\n\nAnd so Horen listened, and he repeated the Creator’s words, and he carried the word\n\nof the Creator to his people, who listened as he did. They kneeled before Horen, first of the divine, and pledged the commandments and supremacy of humanity over all but God. The realm of man rallied underneath the Regent of Heaven, arming themselves and\n\nerecting great fortresses, beginning the golden age of the Horen dynasty. For truly, it was decreed that humanity was second to none but the Creator, and the chosen people would carry out his command until the end of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana Theory", "CaptainSheepy", "+~*~*~*~*+*~*~*~*~+            MANA\n          THEORY\n\nCh 1: What is Mana?\n\nCh 2: Limited Mana               Theory.\n\nCh 3: Seperation                Theory.\n\nCh 4: Use of Mana              Through                   Practices.\n\nCh 5: Closing                     Thoughts.\n\n\nBy Elwen Evaglno\n\nWritten by Ceruberr\nAsul'Ailer.\n\nChapter 1:\n\n     What Is Mana?\n\nMana is something that resides inside of everyone, no matter their experience in magic. Mana is what keeps us alive. It fuels life itself. Known to me, all living beings possess an equal\n\namount of mana. Mana is a pool of energy from which we draw on to do everything from the mundane to the magical.   Many people think that Mana is separate of our physical energy, like when we run. This, however, is far from the truth. Running uses your\n\nMana, which is in fact our physical energy. Losing our Mana is what makes us tired and fatigued and we must rest to restore, or recharge it. Mana and “Physical Energy” are one and the same. It is why a Mage cannot easily use magic after having ran a very\n\nlong distance. It is thought that using up all your Mana would result in death, as Mana is what keeps you alive. It is hard to do this mundanely though, so those who do not use their Mana for mystical means wouldn’t die easily of Mana loss. However, a\n\nmage accepts that overuse of their magic could end up killing them if they do not control their power. Abusing power comes with a price, which is why most Mages are intelligent and logical as they have to be in control of themselves,  lest they be their\n\nown undoing. Mana is what fuels a Mage’s spells and incantations, no matter what form of magic they practice, be it Arcane, Divine or anything else. A Mage learns to manipulate their Mana pool to perform feats that a normal person could never do, such as\n\nsummoning flames from the Void, moving an object with sheer force of will or healing injuries through mystical means.\n\nChapter 2:\n\n  Limited Mana Theory\n\nA part of my theory is that Mana is finite. You never “gain” more Mana. Your Mana has a fixed maximum capacity that cannot be naturally surpassed. I theorize that if you did somehow manage\n\nto surpass this limit, then your body would destroy itself from the inside out due to an oversaturation of Mana. Just as completely draining your Mana would kill you, so too can overcharging your Mana. Though, if this theory were true, how do Mages\n\nprogress? How do they grow more powerful and become able to cast much more before their tired? We can akin this to physical training. As you exercise, you train your body to use your Mana more efficiently for things like running, lifting or fighting.\n\nProgression is dependant upon learning to use your Mana efficiently rather than gaining more. The same is true for a Mage. The more they use their spells and practice their art, the better their bodies get at using their Mana efficiently for their magic.\n\nFor a Mage, casting spells and practicing their art is akin to physical exercise for a warrior. Your Mana is limited. However, you can train your body to make efficient use of that limited resource and get better at what you do, be it Magic or fighting.\n\nChapter 3:\n\n  Seperation Theory\n\n Building upon Chapter Two’s theory of training to use your Mana more efficiently, the next part of the Mana Theory explains why a Mage can’t use all Magic with equal ease as they train\n\nand why they can’t train physically to increase their Mana efficiency in Magic. This is the Separation theory. Simply stated, each Magic school and physical activities are all separate ways to use your Mana, and you must train your body in each way to be\n\nable to use your Mana efficiently in each activity. This theory explains why when a Mage has mastered one art - for sake of example, let’s say Illusion - that they can’t simply transfer over to a new art - Let’s say Flame Evocation - without extensive\n\ntraining in it first. This is because that they must train their bodies to use their Mana efficiently in this new way that is foreign to the body. This also extends to why high-profile Mages are not physically strong. Their bodies do not know how to use\n\nMana efficiently in physical activities, but their bodies can use their Mana efficiently for Magic.\n\nChapter 4:\n\nUse of Mana Through\n        Practices\n\nEach art of Magic uses Mana in a different way. Here, I will list some of the arts in which I know and theorize how that art uses it’s user’s Mana. Evocationists\n\nuse their Mana to pull matter into reality. Their Mana is used to form matter out of nothing and keep it in existence while the natural world tries to force it back out of existence. Their Mana is spent forming and maintaining what they evoke.\n\nAlterationists (From my own experience as a Telekinetic) use their Mana to alter or manipulate already existing objects, casting a sort of temporary enchantment on an object to achieve the desired results. Their Mana is spent forming and maintaining\n\nhe enchantments they weave. Illusionists use their Mana to alter the senses of others or pull ethereal creations from the Void, such as flashes of light, tricking others and falsifying senses. Their Mana is spent weaving and maintaining these illusory\n\neffects. Divine Casters (Druids, Clerics, Monks) gain power from their Deity whom helps form their Mana into a result, such as healing a wound or commanding something under their Deity’s domain, such as plants for Druids. Their Mana is spent through\n\nabilities granted by their Deity.\n  Warriors exert their Mana through physical activity and training. Their Mana is used by movement such as running or swinging a sword and it is also used to move while wearing armor due to difficulty in doing so.\n\nTheir Mana is drained through physical exertion. There may be arts unknown to me, but these are the ones that I have learned of, studied and theorized.\n\nChapter 5:\n\n   Closing Thoughts\n\nMana is a force we cannot see or fully study. While this tome may shed some light on the subject, we can never truly understand Mana. However, we can theorize and think of\n\nwhat it may be or how it truly works. For now, I close the book with a thank you for spending your time to study this tome. I hope you are better for it and that this insight into Mana may encourage you to study Magic yourself if you haven’t already.\n\nVan'ayla\n\nBy Elwen Evaglno\n\nWritten by Ceruberr\nAsul'Ailer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Copied Book", "§bMonk Scribe", "*Many parts of the book seem missing, but it appears to be a copy. Clearly the book it was coppied from was not complete.*\n\nWriten by the Third Elder Monk, in the year 109. Many pages are missing in the original.\n\n…..the female Aengul proceeded to leave, Aeriel and the Wizard were indeed distraught. The system collapsing before their own eyes…… Odion was called for guidance. It is reported that the Daemon’s stone halls spat flames like a baneslither when he heard\n\nof this dissent. They rushed to find that the portal had already closed, making it impossible to trace the followers of the Dark Lady, as Monk John was apt to call her.\n\nAeriel decreed that the ethereal spirits must refrain from the constant contact with\n\nthe Descendant Races as to avoid further mishaps such as this. Some of the Daemons who had befri…..d mortals were angered and left the realm as well, while the remaining Daemons and the majority of Aenguls decided to abide by thi….., each in their own way\n\nIt did seem that Aeriel, as well as the Wiz……………….which some did not……… ……and throughout Aegis, the monks destroyed all tomes other than……much to his dismay. The Wizard was quite upset with the actio………. though it was all for a grand cause, indeed.\n\nHe later came to be glad for Aeriel’s decision, for………… efforts were certainly successful for the most part, as is apparent in society, and the account o…………not fully untrue, naturally, yet th………… only to be preserved within this room by the Scarlet Monks", ""),
        StaticBook("A", "Rurikk", "*the journal in your hands is covered with tanned leather and tied shut with a leather chord, branded upon the cover is: \"A Huntsman's Guide to Surviving the Wilderness\"\n\nIntro:\n\nHello everyone, this book was written by an experienced survivalist in hopes that all who wish to venture out into the wilds will be prepared for the trials and hardships they may face along the way.\n\nAfter reading this booklet you will be able to\n\nsurvive on your own without any extra aid from outside sources. \n\nNow let us begin then.\n\nChapter One \"What You\nWill Need\":\n\nThe most important items that a survivalist needs to well... survive, are the tools that he/she either finds or brings with him/her on the way to their journey into the wilds.\n\nHere is a list of helpful items:\n\n1. Flint & Steel\n2. A Small Hatchet\n3. Preserving Salts\n4. Needle and Thread\n5. Skinning Knife\n6. Waterproofed Satchel\n7. Small Fishing Hook\n8. Sturdy Clothing\n9. Sufficient Rations\n10. Common Sense\n\nChapter Two \"What To Expect\":\n\nOnce you have acquired all the supplies listed in the previous chapter you are now ready to begin your journey.\n\nFirst things first, to survive in the wilds you need to know at least a basic background of the\n\nenvironment you plan on venturing into, such as weather patterns, what kinds of vegetation grows in the region, as well as the different beasts that make their home in the area.\n\nRemember to study maps and acquire as much information about the region if\n\npossible before you decide to make the trip. Failing to do so could result in dismemberment or even death.\n\nOnce you have done your research and acquired all of your supplies for the trek into the unknown, you will finally be ready to begin.\n\nChapter Three \"Setting Up Camp\"\n\nIn this chapter you will learn the basics of setting up a safe and reliable camp site to live in during your stay in the wilderness.\n\nOnce you have found a suitable place to set up camp, you need to make\n\nsure that the area you have picked is in fact a safe place to stay in. To do so, please check off everything on this list:\n\n1. Is it dry and warm?\n2. Does it protect you from the elements?\n3. Is it close to a source of water?\n4. Can you easily find it if\n\nlost?\n5. Does it protect you from unwanted visitors?\n\nIf all of the above checks off as okay, then you have done a great job in picking out a location for your campsite!\n\nChapter Four \"Exploring The Wilderness\"\n\nSo far so good, if you've gotten this far then that means you haven't killed yourself yet. Good job!\n\nIn this chapter we will be going over the basics of wilderness exploration.\n\nWhen an experienced survivalist arrives in uncharted lands, they usually do one or more of these things listed:\n\n1. Find a high place and survey the lands before you, taking notes of key land marks in the immediate area.\n\n2. Preparing themselves for long treks away from the safety of their camps, make sure to pack extra food, you may be away from home for a while!\n\n3. Preparing for all possible outcomes, make sure to think of everything that could happen while you are away\n\nfrom the camp; things such as being captured by jungle pigmy's to the occasional bear destroying your camp can easily be prevented if you just prepare ahead of time.\n\nCarrying out with at least one of these tips can make your life out in the wilderness\n\nmuch easier, and could possibly save your life.\n\nChapter Five \"Returning Home\":\n\nCongratulations, you've survived your trip and are ready to break camp and return home with a multitude of new stories from your trip.\n\nRemember that when you are ready to leave to make sure you try to leave\n\nthings just as they were when you first arrived at the location you chose for your camp.\n\nOnce you have finished returning things as they once were, you can then begin to journey back home. Make sure not to forget any trinkets or trophies that you might\n\nhave found while exploring the wilderness!\n\nThanks for reading\n\nA little bit about the Author:\n\nCharles Silverblade:\nCharles was born in the small farming town of Riven, where his cousin Uthor Silverblade helped to raise him and teach him to become a fine young man in terms of Oren society. When he turned 18 years of\n\nage, he enlisted in the Oren Military as a conscript and quickly ascended the ranks of hierarchy in the military until he finally acquired the title of Ser and received Knighthood in the Order of the Red Dragon. Charles now lives with his Wife and four\n\nchildren with the rest of the Silverblade family who reside in the Duchy of Furnestock.", ""),
        StaticBook("Opinion on Truth", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "An Opinion on Truth\n\n             -By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\nBefore I start, let me just emphasize that this is just my opinion. I want to share it with you and hear what you all think!\n\nThe truth can be a hard thing to know these days. With so many lies about various things in general flying about, it is hard to discern the truth from the false. Now I’m not here to tell anyone what the truth is in any situation.\n\n I just want to talk about and discuss what I feel the truth is in itself. To start out, I am going to go a bit off topic, to what I think about fear and doubt.\n\nSo what is fear? Fear in my own opinion is of course when you are afraid of something. Whether that be the outcome of a decision you have to make, or doing something you have never done for the first time.\n\nThe next question is what does it mean to be afraid of something? What causes it? I think that fear occurs the most often, though not all the time, in the absence of knowledge. Like when you aren’t sure about something.\n\nFear of the unknown is a very common thing, as the unknown can possibly do anything.\n\nNow, if someone had complete confidence that something will happen a certain way, then that person would likely have little to no fear about it unless it is something bad that is to happen.\n\nFor example, if I practiced day and night for a big test of some sort, and was sure I knew everything needed to pass the test and then some, I would hopefully and likely feel little fear.\n\nIf I was in a battle and had to get my leg amputated, I would likely fear that because I wouldn’t want to lose a limb.\n\nIn the second example I know what is going to happen, I know how it’s going to happen, but I will likely still fear that it will happen. As for the first example, if the person who studied day and night failed the test.\n\nThat would cause the next subject. Doubt.\n\nDoubt is something that I think causes a lot of fear. It ties in with the lack of knowledge in something. Doubt can be a very powerful thing. It changes or attempts to change your perspective on things, for better or worse, though usually for the worse.\n\nAn example of good doubt would be thinking about an outcome of a certain action like whether something is a good idea or not, and acting on that doubt.\n\nAn example of bad doubt would be something like thinking that you cannot do something due to a past experience.\n\nTo avoid doubt and fear, I think the best way to defeat both is to find out the whole topic of this. The truth. Truth in my opinion is very simple to ourselves, but hard to obtain from outside of ourselves.\n\nIf you know the truth about something that would mean that you have true knowledge in a certain part or most aspects of that something. This would defeat both doubt and fear, as fear is mainly caused by doubt, and doubt requires uncertainty in something.\n\nThe problem is that some outside sources do the next thing. Lie.\n\nLies in my opinion increase doubt and in turn fear. They corrupt the truth and make things harder to make out. A lot of things have the ability to lie. People, books, even our own memories can lie.\n\nI know that most people would say their memories are not faulty, and I agree that can be true for the most part. Everyone will have different interpretations of a thing that they all together witness, like an abstract painting.\n\nI am only saying that there is a possibility that a memory could be wrong.\n\nNow how to discern what is a lie and what is the truth. Well, that is quite the question isn’t it? We can usually lie at any time, so how to know what is true?\n\nThat brings me to something I call absolute truth, or in other words the real truth in something. The thing is, I think that we can never know the absolute truth. Don’t get me wrong. It is there, it is just usually unknowable.\n\nTake the abstract picture example. Both people would know what the picture looks like to them, but they would likely be two different interpretations. The object outside the two people’s minds is the absolute truth.\n\nWe just have interpretations of it through what we think and perceive.\n\nSo who would be right about what it the abstract painting is? I think they would both be right to a point. With the truth in most matters there isn’t a white or black scenario. It is usually some type of grey.\n\nNow, imagine white as truth, and black as false. We can get the grey a closer to white with the more truth we tell about the subject. We can also get the grey closer to black with the more lies we tell.\n\nNow it is certainly possible to get things to all white. This is based on both the question and the answer. If I asked, did you go to the store today, and you did and said yes. That would be a truthful statement.\n\nAs for the opposite with it getting to all black. That is a tricky thing. I think as soon as there is a falsehood in there, something is already not all true. Though it can get even darker the more lies are put into it.\n\nAs for how to get rid of all the black and grey. I see the only ways are to either be found out, or the better option which is to confess. In doing a total confession, you undo all the black and grey, leaving the truth as you know it to yourself, white.\n\nNow back to how to find out if something someone says or does is true or not. There is something that can help with that. Trust. Trust helps you believe what someone says is true. It both does that and helps you be more truthful to that person.\n\nI believe that in some cases it helps the other person be more truthful to you as well. Now when both people trust each other, that is where things get really interesting.\n\nI would think very plainly that when two people trust each other, the truth flows a lot more smoothly. Who should you trust? Well, that is up to you.\n\nAll in all, the truth is simple, yet easily diverged into a lie. I believe the more truth we tell, the clearer things will be to those we tell it to, the more trust we will gain, and the more likely people will tell ourselves the truth.\n\nIt is easy to tell the truth, Harder but more temporarily convenient to tell a lie, and even harder to own up to a lie. When and if all the lies are cleared up to yourself, well, what need would there be to lie again?\n\nIf you simply tell the truth from there onward you would be set on a much clearer path then in my opinion. \nThat is all I have to say. I hope you took something from this book, and remember. This is just my opinion.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Fund. Alchemy", "Jistuma", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nThe Fundamentals of Alchemy\n\nVolume I of V\n\nForeword:\nI have heard many a man ask why one, such as myself, would take such interest and dedication in the art of alchemy when there are ready-made spells that could do just the same, if not better, a job than an apothecary’s potion. My response to\n\nthis statement is rather simple, whereas one must have a certain gift for spell-slinging, rune-craft, and spirit-speaking, one mustn’t need these frivolous commodities to use a balm to mend a wound, shroud themselves in a nigh-invisible cloak\n\nwith the swig from a bitter bottle, or set someone ablaze with bottled flame. Alchemy is not merely reproducing a wizard’s spell, but it is shaping the spell in a way for the common man’s use. While magic still has its place in our world, Alchemy allows\n\nthose without the gift to reap the same benefits as any mage might.\n\nChapter 1: The Fundamentals of Alchemy\n------------\nThe Principle and Law of Equivalent Exchange:\n\nAs I was providing my services to a rather quaint hamlet, which also provided me information of the local flora and more of the same legends I always here of, I was approached by a man of common repute, and he produced a sarcastic, yet thought provoking,\n\nquestion. This question was, and I will attempt to reproduce the dialect as best as my phonetic ability will allow, “ ‘ow come, Mister, ‘hat ye’ can make all ‘dis ‘onderful stuff outta nothin’?” Now as shameful as his speech may be, the question remains\n\nthe same. How is it, that alchemists are capable or reshaping the spells of sorcerers for the common folk out of, seemingly, nothing? The answer to this question is simple to state, but fairly difficult to grasp, and this is the Principle of Equivalent\n\nExchange. Much like the money one gives to the merchant for the apple or slab of meat, one cannot have something for nothing. As the saying goes, “there is no such thing as a free brunch,” there is no such thing as a free potion. This fundamental rule\n\napplies to old alchemy, through the use of symbols and rituals, far more than what I call “Modern” alchemy. Although I will not get into ancient alchemy, I will state why this rule applies to Modern Alchemy. To craft a potion, for example a bottle of\n\nalchemist’s fire, one requires the materials. Much like a spell casted by a wizard, one cannot make something out of nothing. Know that to make a potion, and the possibilities are truly endless, one must take plants, objects, and other representations of\n\nwhat they wish to make. For example, alchemist’s fire could be best produced with an - -, a mixture of -  -, -  -, and a dash of -  -. Why would one need these items?\n\nThe - - provides the basic mixture of what we will make, and of course the better quality of the - - the better quality of the Alchemist’s Fire, but of course we will get further into this in a later chapter. The -  -, a -  -\n\nplant that grows most often in deserts, is often -  - and often associated with -  -. This provides an superb symbol for the element of -  -. The -  -, another powerful symbol of -  -, mixes well with the crushed -  -\n\nto produce something truly strong. The -  -, an optional portion, is another symbol of -  -, albeit both weaker than blaze -  - for both a -  - fire burns far greater than -  -.\n\nNow then, although you have these symbols of flame, rage, and warfare, one mustn’t simply toss objects into the metaphorical cauldron. Precision is necessary, as always. One must measure their mixture carefully, or they will give too much. And giving too\n\nmuch will tip the scales of Equivalent Exchange, causing unpredictable results. Why is this you might ask? When balance is achieved through Equivalent Exchanged, a mixture of the elements for the bottled spell of your desire, than all is well. But when\n\nyou disrupt this balance and push on the world, taking and forcing in too much of one or more element then the world will push back. Of course a word of caution is required, for one may think taking less is the best option when balance is not a certainty.\n\nThis is a common misconception for not providing enough of one element will result in the same conclusion, imbalance and chaos. This can be easily associated with cooking, too much of one ingredient will spoil the recipe, not enough of an ingredient will\n\nPreparation and You:\n\nNovice Alchemists often question me, what advice would you provide the budding alchemist, what sip of wisdom could you provide one who desires to tap your fountain of knowledge? The answer to this is rather simple, preparation is key to any potion. What\n\nis meant by this is that to mix a potion that you have not mixed before, or do not mix often, you must have all the facts and supplies before you begin. This is best provided in a short list of required procedures if one wishes to keep their eyebrows,\n\nfingers, and life.\n\n1. Have all the Facts\n2. Know the Recipe\n3. Clean and check all your instruments are in working order\n4. Ensure you have plenty of whatever ingredients you are using\n5. Keep and Calm Dispostion\n\nI believe the only topic that requires explanation is “Have all the Facts” and by this I mean that one should not mix a potion they know nothing about. Even having the recipe is not enough to craft a potion safely, but knowledge of its origins,\n\ningredients, and uses are crucial. Although budding alchemists often overlook this step, it may save your life one day.\n\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Bravery", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nBravery:\nThis is not a Task that is assigned, rather it is earned by the Dedicant. If an event occurs during their training, or at the grove, and the Dedicant shows an act of exceptional selflessness and bravery in defense of the Order,\n\nwhile maintaining admirable attitude and integrity, their Guide may deem to count this action as a completed Task, as they have proven that their heart is with the Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sorcerers: One", "SerahLove", "Sorcerers: Recognizing the\n        Various Varieties\n\n\nAmongst those who possess distinctly closer bonds to the void, a few different kinds have been recognized. This short excerpt will attempt to bring the reader through these varied distinctions, and\n\nhopefully provide aid in attaining some small measure of enlightenment in the subject matter.\n\n\n   The Common Robed Mage:\n\nSorcerer(ess)/Magician/Conjurer/Wizard/Robe.\n\nThe typical conjurer, often accompanied by a staff-\n\ndraped in long cloaks, adorned in all manner of strange markings- runes- and odd colours, is often depicted as an old man with a long, thick beard, and possessing a vast reservoir of knowledge esoteric.\n\nThere is no doubt that this variety is the most\n\nrenowned and favored. The common Mage is often the most well-versed in the forbidden art of magical combat- with more powerful spells and hexes, and (depending on the proficiency of the caster) all the more perilous.\n\nHowever, with these strengths, come\n\nweaknesses, for the common Mage is often, by tradition, frail and lacking in physical prowess- endurance, hardiness and such- due to the almost fanatical obsession that such ilk often possess with the endless search and acquisition of more knowledge, and\n\nin turn, more power of origins profane.\n\n\n\n     The Household Mage:\n\n\n   Witch Maid/Hearth Mage.\n\nThe common Mage's humbler counterpart of lesser renown, the Household Mage could\n\nvery well be the lowly servant a small measure too efficient at the crude task of sweeping the kitchen floors, or even the unassuming cook who heats the oven furnace a moment too quickly.\n\nThe subtlety of the magic these beings possess and put into\n\npractice makes them quite difficult to discern to those without the knack for spotting such things. One could, perhaps rightly, assume that such beings might hardly pose any considerable amont of threat, due to their lack of experience and utility in the\n\nfield of combat.\n\nHousehold Mages can be either shunned members of the secluded Mage's Guild or former, disgraced apprentices who, having in the past acknowledged their inferior ability or lack of talents, had decided to follow an entirely different path,\n\nseeking a livelihood in a different environment.\n\nTheir spells are most often simplistic in nature and effect, and pose very little danger- if any at all. These mages are seen as more benevolent than the common Mage, and physically more robust; though\n\nsuch things are quite difficult to confirm, given the elusive and subtle nature of the mages in question.\n\n\n          The Battle Mage:\n\n\nWarrior-Witch/Spellblade/Witchman/Mystic Knight.\n\nThe rarest and least liked of\n\nthe known types- The Battle Mage is seen as the bane of chivalry and honorable duels, with little regard for learning more of this art. The Battle Mage is most often spotted in places where war and conflict are as commonplace as frost on a cold winter's\n\nmorn. He is often the result of a fighter who, through rigorous and excruciating training, had learnt both the way of the blade and the art of the arcane- applying both theories and practices in harmonious synergy. The existence of such beings suggests\n\nexistence of some clandestine groups or knightly orders that had handpicked and set aside some select candidates to undertake the rigors required to achieve this balance of spell and blade.\n\nThe training of a would-be Battle Mage is the stuff of tales and\n\nlegends- often known to be one of- if not THE most dangerous path to the art of magic. Apprentices that had been found and deemed fit candidates were often rumored to have died of various accidents- including, but not limited to: Death by fire and cinders\n\n, of spell mishaps and eternal sleep, of ice and water, and of broken shards of marble and glass. The fortunate few- if one could even call them as such- that did somehow manage to live through the horrors of their training, and the ire and malice of the\n\ncommon folk, quite often found themselves unable to resume the lives they had once led, some distant time ago, now bent purely on suffering and death as heralds of doom and ruin.\n\nBattle Mages are often not as proficient in the art of magic as their more\n\nfocused counterpart: the common Sorcerer. However, their skill with and mastery of the sword may, at times, more than compensate for this lack of further magical prowess and potency. Hence, it would be most unwise for the regular mage to step within range\n\nof the Battle Mage, for the Battle Mage, neither frail nor unfit, could quite as easily close the distance, and deal a devastating blow.\n\n  Sorcerers: Recognizing the\n         Various Varieties\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        \n                - Arthur Versluis\n\n   Revisions by E.S. and A.F.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druids Grove", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Druid's Grove\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, The Solstice Druid\n\nThe Druids’ Grove is a place of Aspectial worship and peaceful congregation. It is a place where natural Druidic energies run deep and life flourishes in the glory and light of Cerridwen and Cernunnos. The Mother Grove, usually the most grand of all\n\ngroves on a given land mass, houses the Druidic Order and serves as their place of spreading the Druidic way through ancient teachings.\n\nNever should violence or anti-natural forces be issued within the grove; when these things are wrought on\n\nsuch sacred grounds, a Druid may do what he must to see the sanctity and peaceful aura restored. Furthermore, never should armor or weapon be donned in a grove for it is an area of peace and harmony with nature. When an individual holds armor and/or\n\nweapon, he anticipates violence and the need for said materials which only brings violent thought and meaning to the grove, thus disrupting the peaceful and harmonic aura.\n\nDruids’ groves have served throughout history as an\n\nimportant aspect of Druidic culture and Druid congregation. They’ve also served as elegant gardens, floral and faunal reserves, and places of knowledge. Drui’inder, take into account the purpose and sanctity of the Druids’ grove to better your\n\nunderstanding of Druidic culture and spread your wisdom to the generations to come so that they, too, may be enlightened by this cultural tradition. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elder Trees", "§bUnknown", "~~~Elder Trees~~\n\nAn Elder Tree is an ancient tree that is rumoured to have become sentient. They are powerful entities filled with Druidic Energies. Throughout time they have offered wisdom to Druids, and even housed Druid Groves.\n\nElder Trees are very old and usually extremely large; the tallest trees in the forest.\n\nThey are also usually the mother tree of the forest; the forest having grown from them.\n\nOne of the most notable features is their ability to create Ents, the powerful tree-like creatures that serve as guardians of the forest.\n\nEnts are usually known as the children of the Elder trees.\n\nThere are only a few Elder Trees in the lands; In Anthos Druids spoke of three: ~En'Leawyn of Luminaire\n~Elt’irigin of the West\nand,\n~Bouri’juin of the South\n\nThere are many more Elder Trees in the lands that the Descendants have inhabited, and in the lands to follow, discovered or still a secret...", ""),
        StaticBook("Traveler's Guide", "§bIllmori", "Nice and Bad Places\nGood=10\nNice=9\nPretty good=8\nPretty nice=7 \nOkay=6\nWell=5\nNot so Nice=4\nNot so good=3\nUgh=2\nEww=1\nWorse=0\n\nNerezza - 3\nPetrus - 8\nHaelun'or - 9\nCerulin - 9 \nDul'Sildure - 7\nAkovia - 5\nWerdenberg - 8 \nViridian Inn - 3\nDwarven City - 7\nCloud Temple - 7 \nUruk Lands - 6\nDwarven City with ships - 2\n\nConyon lands - 5\nBronze Elven Lands - 7\n\n-=-=-\n\nTourist's Guide : \n\nForest Walks : Cerulin, Haelun'or, Petrus, Nerezza, Akovia, Dwarven city with ships\nSwimming : Cerulin, Dul'Sildur, Dwarven city with ships, Bronze elven lands\n\nEarning Tan : \nUruk Lands, Dul'Sildur, Petrus\n\nParty and Events \n(One to Ten scale used) \nNerezza - 2\nPetrus - 10\nHaelun'or - 8\nCerulin - 4\nDul'Sildur - 7\nAkovia - 3\nWerdenberg - 5\nViridian Inn - 8\n\nDwarven City - 3\nCloud Temple - 7\nUruk Lands - 3\nDwarven City With Ships - 1\nConyon Lands - 3\nBronze Elven lands - 7\n\n-=-=-\n\nDescriptions : \nNerezza - Unpeaceful Cold Kingdom (Bad for elves) \nPetrus - Friendly Central\n\nKingdom. May have some problems there sometimes. \nHaelun'or - A beautiful, but spooky city, high racism rates\nCerulin - A Beautiful, but spooky city, high control rates\nDul'Sildur - Scary, but interesting castle. Good for walks or adventures. Have a lot\n\nof secrets\nAkovia - Small Kingdom, few citizens, not so fun\nWerdenberg - Small City, lots of citizens, pretty fun\nVirdinian inn - Inn with lots of things happening in it. Good for scandals or fights\nDwarven city - Absolutely boring place, but beautiful\n\nsomehow. \nCloud Temple - The. Center. Of. The. World. \nUruk Lands - Hot and dry places, bad peoples, lots of fights\nDwarven city with ships - What The Nether \nConyon lands - Pretty boring, but interesting too lands. \nbronze elven lands - ...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Simple Story", "§bUnknown Author", "*The old tome is worn and dusty, and the ink is partially faded.*\n\n=================== A Story\n===================\n\n\" Two chaste Temple Monks were walking down the road during a heavy downpour of rain. They came across a beautiful young woman who was taking shelter under a tree. She called out to the monks, requesting that they carry her across a small stream.\n\nThe first monk immediately moved to help the woman while the second silently protested. The first monk scooped the beautiful lady up in his arms, and he carried her across the stream. After crossing it, he promptly set her down and continued on his way.\n\nThe two began walking down the path once more, and the second monk remained silent for several minutes as the woman disappeared from view. Finally, he spoke to his brother.\n\n'As monks of the Cloud Temple, we are not supposed to have contact with woman!\n\nWhy did you pick that women up so casually and carry her across the stream?' \n\nThe first monk replied, \n\n'Brother, I set the woman down long ago. Why is it that you have not?' \"", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish.", "§bOsmond Swiftheart", "*The handwriting seems to be written in cursive, yet much more advanced*\n\nA wish.\nMy wish would be to become a strong cleric under the guidance of the blessed Tahariae.\nI wish to protect all that I love,\n\nAll whom I've befriended, and dispose of all the dark beings who wish on one's destruction or even the entire world. \nTo heal those who are in need. To make my mark on the world, make Hesh proud.\nThat is my wish.\n\n*On the final page is a name written as a signature*\n\nSincerely,\n\n        Osmond\n      Swiftheart", ""),
        StaticBook("Powers of Being", "§bFarley III Stafyr", "The Powers of Being\n\nWritten by Godwein Stafyr\n\nAs a theoretical study, my writings began about wisdom, leading me to the difference between knowledge and experience and their relation, furthermore bringing me to write a first draft of the elements of mind.\n\nBy now I have realized that there must be more. The mind is part of the being itself. A power within everyone of us. Logically though, the being consists of more than only the mind.\n\nPhysically we have the body as the second power of being. The body is one power we use every day, its elements are blood, organs, muscles and the resulting strength…  The elements belonging to the body shall be elaborated by me\n\nin further writings.\n\nTo note, that this is the point where my studies will go over into the studies of doctors and healers, likely to be seamless. For this I must also refer to a man of biological knowledge in the future.\n\nAs for the third and last power of being, I hereby mean the soul. The elements of soul are yet to be elaborated and studied by me, although I can definitely align an element to the soul. In another work of mine, I say that feelings are an element of\n\nmind. By now, I must correct myself and say, that feelings are a definite element of the soul. The same may go for purity as well. For this we will see further in the future, what my studies and writinggs bring up.\n\n-: Primary Edition :-", ""),
        StaticBook("Scourge Guide 1", "§bKnyghtfalcon", "Information on the\nScourge and Harbingers.\n\nTOC -\nMembers and Names\nTainted Creatures\nMagical Abilities and Combat Tactics\nCultist Names\nThe Use of Thanic Ore\n\nWithin the Scourge, there are many members of both Harbinger and other creatures alike. The list is as follows.\n\n Harbingers -\nShae'tan - Shaela\nFemale\nFavours Deception\n\nAbsolution\nMale\nFavours Combat\n\nXort\nMale\nFavours Combat\n\nNihil\nMale\nNeutal - Peaceful\nTreasures Knowledge\n\nDumamis\nMale\nFavours Combat\n\nKalgeryas\nMale\nExtremely Violent\n\nMarak\nMale\nSecluded and Devious\n\nMortum'Vherzix\nMale\nSecluded, EXTREMELY HOSTILE, DO NOT APPROACH.\n\nSitri'aim - Deceased\nMale\nFavoured Manipulation\n\nKav'Zoras - Deceased\nMale\nFavoured Violence\n\nEudihr - Kaos\nMale\nViolent and Deceitful\n\nCreatures -\n\nVithquar\nFemale\nViolent and Childish\n\nCreated by the Masked Judge - Rosso. A half-dragon female.\n\nIt is hostile, dangerous, and believes herself to be the wife of Iblees, queen over the nether realm. Advise approaching with caution, although she is easily manipulated.\n\nMittens\nApparition\nEXTREMELY DANGEROUS\n\nMittens is an apparition created from hundreds of tormented and damned souls, of those who have died in the harsh terrain of the north.\nIt is extremely violent and almost\n\ncompletely unstoppable without a strong dose of holy or spiritual magic. Advise not to approach, turn the other way if you see it. It is dangerous. It will not hesitate to kill you.\n\nKaar'thul the Snake\nUnknown\n\nThis being is a snake-like creature which can assume an almost completely invisible state, and possesses powers alike the Harbingers, with the ability to breath frostfire.\n\nIt is a long segmented serpent when visible, with blood red eyes and a shredded and torn body. It was created to serve the Harbingers although its current alignment is unknown. Advise caution when dealing with the beast, it is very deadly.\n\nCorrupted Drakes\n\nSetherien is in command of many drakes and other serpentine beasts of the north.  When dealing with these creatures, it is advised that you do not face them alone and stay out of tight groups.\n\nThey attack with fire, claws and biting, along with physically slamming their body down on structures and opponents. The best way to kill them is to hit the joints of their wings, strike their eyes, or strike in their mouth when they roar or breath fire.\n\nBohra\n\nLarge pig-like humanoid beings who used to inhabit the northern lands. These creatures are tainted to serve Setherien. They are brutes, yet stupid in most cases, the best course of action is to have someone distract\n\nthem while another attacks, or to simply take them out from a distance. A few arrows in their skull should end the beasts. Aim for the spine or eyes in the case of the corrupted ones, only severing the head or spinal cord can truly end them.\n\nServants of Setherien\n\nSkeletal creatures, the past mortals who have fought against Setherien. Every time a body is taken from the battlefield by Setherien's minions, these are created from the remains. Formerly known as Kambasors\n\nThey usually arrive in groups of two to five from the rifts created by Harbingers or other creatures. In groups they are quite deadly, but singled out are easy to remove. They inflict a sickness on contact, so beware hand to hand combat. The sickness is\n\nknown as taint poisoning, and will sap away your life force and weaken you severely. Aim for the spine or skull, as it is the only way to defeat the creatures.\n\nDrudges of Setherien\n\nThese creatures are the brutish and more armored version of the Servants. They usually possess better equipment and armor, and are slightly more strategic. They inflict a stronger form of the taint sickness.\n\nThey are killed in the same way, spine or skull. It is best to avoid these and remove them from a distance, they usually arrive through rifts in groups of three at a time.\n\nThe Riders of Setherien\n\nConquest\nWar\nFamine\nDeath\n\nThese creatures are spectral beings which ride on the backs of undead steeds.\n\nNot much is known about them by me at least, they were created close to my removal, and thus I had not much time to learn. They are deadly, swift, and masters at combat and war. They possess the ability to open rifts as the Harbingers do.\n\nCombat - \nThe Harbingers in combat are quite weak to melee abilities and require their distance and magic to compete. In order to vanquish one, you must severely damage its armor to force it away.\n\nThey are weak to lightning, and typically do not appreciate fire. They are cold beings, and attacks of ice have no affect. They can not suffer from sickness or wounds, burns nor freezing. They are spectral creatures, and only solid physical strikes will\n\ntruly affect their form. Harbingers can be sentenced to destruction and removed from the realm permenantly if enough clerics can focus holy magic on the creature. Holy magic is their ultimate weakness, use it to your advantage.\n\nAbilities -\nDrakaar's boon\n- This is the basic of magic for the spectral beings, and other dark creatures. This is the gift of the dark one, Setherien, which grants them their abilities and the skill of drawing power from him.\n\nThis is the key, and gives access to all other abilities one might possess. This is what powers the harbingers, keeps the alive. This allows them to hover, and use a specialized form of illusion which allows them to disguise themselves.\n\nFrost Fire, the Northern Breath.\nThis is a specific form of dark, unholy fire, which freezes instead of burns. It is very deadly, and gives highly painful and deadly frostbite on contact, and coats objects with ice. A single blast contains enough\n\nmagical energy to kill a man, and armor seems to have no affect against this.\n\nThe Taint of Setherien, Setherien's Wrath.\n\nA cloud of pure sickness cast out from the forms of the spectral beings, other creatures possess the ability to breathe this out as well. It infects those within the cloud with a\n\nhorrendous desiese which has the ability to spread between multiple hosts upon mere contact. It weakens the victim, induces sickness, vomiting, hallucinations and saps their life from them. Tainted Bohra also can spread this desiese.\n\nSetherien's Call, the Ballista of Drakes.\n\nA large, explosive ball of corruptive energy, cast out to cause mass destruction on an area. It is capable of destroying walls and other structures in a single condensed blast. Only Harbingers are capable of this\n\nThe Rift of the Drakaar Realm, Call of the Servants.\n\nUsable by the Horsemen and the Harbingers, as currently known, along with Corrupted Drakes. This magical rift through dimensions can call forth Servants and\n\nDrudges of Setherien into Combat. A dark ball of pure dark energy is cast to the ground, which begins to spread in a large wave of taint as a rift opens between worlds, dragging the beasts out to fight. Do not step in the rift, it is very toxic.\n\nThe Ritual, Summoner of the Damned.\n\nA ritual performed by the Harbingers, which calls down a large Skeletal Servant simply known as 'The Prophet' which takes the form of a large Drudge. It is extremely hostile, capable of taking down\n\nplatoons of soldiers on its own. It is not often used, as it takes much of their energy to summon. But beware, this creature is extremely deadly, fast, and possesses magical abilities beyond all others. Some believe it is Setherien himself in disguise.\n\nThe Summoning of the Tokens, Call of the Sword.\n\nThe Harbingers possess the ability to call forth their weapons from the same realm of the Kambasor creatures. They can do this at will, in mere moments. They are never unarmed.\n\nIn order to defeat the creatures, beyond their magical abilities, you must kill them as quickly as possible. The longer they exist, the more rituals they may perform and the more kambasors are brought forth. It is important they are dispatched as soon as\n\nyou can get within striking distance. Without their leaders, the rest of the creatures will panic, and they will fall. Just the same, the creatures are without hope if they do not have their servents to defend them. Get them seperated and kill them.\n\nCult Members Known -\nVithquar\nAsher 'Latue' Acosta\nRin\nHaadi Mumbdee\nKelsey Von Craw\nCombo'Breaka'lur\n(Descriptions match each name)\n\nThanic Ore -\nThanic ore is important to the scourge. All bloodshards are made of thanic ore, as are the Harbinger's weapons and armor. While poisonous to void magic users, theirs is enchanted and thus does not kill on contact. They possess large\n\nquantities. It is vital to them, as their armor can not be made of anything but the material.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ki'Kun's wish", "§bKi'Kun", "I wish ter wass a school ta al races couuld go too, too learn magic, diffrent crafts, an tings needed in life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adawulf's Wish", "§bAdawulf", "Allow Redstone Currents to go through regions.\n\nIf that's not possible then.\n\n7 stacks of gunpowder.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana: Lifeblood", "§bGerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\nMana:\nThe Lifeblood of Magic\n\nTranscribed by:\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\n\n===================To the ignorant and uninitiated, this energy is mistaken simply for something they name 'stamina.'\n\nThe beings that have been found to carry the most amount of Mana around them are those dubbed \"the magic users.\" Gleaned\n\n===================-from common research, mages learn to gather mana around them as they progress in their art. As they grow further in skill, they become able to carry more mana about them- enhancing the speed at which a mage casts, thus allowing the-\n\n===================release of more spells within a smaller period of time. \n\nMuch like a fire, if the fuel or mana has been completely consumed, the user will perish or, at the very least, find himself close to the gates of death. Such is why mages must-\n\n===================-be sure to take the necessary precautions- planning their every move, every attack, carefully, mindful of their limitations and current state. An improperly-timed spell may cause adverse effects for the caster- perhaps\n\n===================even bring his ruin in a hectic environment and situation. From this, the origin and conception of the old \"Wihun\" strategy can be glimpsed. The \"Baiting\" technique which the ancient group of witch-hunters once used involved the\n\n===================continued application of pressure upon the caster. The witch-hunter would harass the mage into expending his mana until exhaustion- frightening the caster enough to incite a barrage or volley of magical offense. And when the time had-\n\n===================come, the most opportune moment finally revealing itself, the clever hunter would spring forth- fangs bared at the worn down mage, closing in for the deathly blow.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem V1", "§bUnknown", "For Resia.\n\nWith warm, cleansing light,\n\nYou further the Cause that is right,\n\nDestroying that which plagues these lands; that unholy blight!\n\nAlways lending your aid to help those in need,\n\nNever stopping until those imprisoned are freed.\n\nEverything you set your mind to, you succeed.\n\nOne must ask, however, are you getting what you require?\n\nHow can one toil daily, without tire?\n\nSome around you take, while others help. I, for one, only wish to.. [A few words are\nscribbled out]\n\n..prevent you from expire.. -ing.\n\nSo as this poem reaches its end,\n\nOne hopes its message will send.\n\nEnjoy yourself every now and then, and never forget your helping friend.\n\n\n- P.S.\n\nI'm not the best at this! I hope you enjoyed it.\n\n[The poem is unsigned.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Homework 3", "§bIndra", "Erin Ibar'ker (ThymeLeviathan)\nDaughter to Gigarun and Arinislia. has been a druid for five elven months. Gryphon Druid.\n\nDwyn Tinuvial- Dedicant in Athera taught by Pine druid Gigarun. Favorite task was the staff task. Chose Deer as his totem\n\nto symbolize the protectiveness he has for his 'herd'. \n\nElswyen Deathbane\nTotem: Rose\nDruid for two elven years. Chose their totem because of the love and beauty symbol, but also because of their sharp thorns. Taught by Ouity and Izzy\n\nFavorite task was making a 'living' boat.\n\nArinislia Athna.\nTotem: Owl\nSeventy or eighty years. Was an archdruid and Guide, now a Heirophant. Favorite task: The tree task; go into the forest, grow a tree, nuture and protect it. During her -\n\ndedicancy, a white owl followed her and observed her and eventually became her companion by choice.\n\nArtimec Camoryn:\nDruid for 20 years.\nTotem: Hawk\nFavorite task was the poem task.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druid Code", "§bPine Druid Garun", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~    The Druidic Code\n         As Scribed\n     by the Dragon\n     Druid Apollan\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n\n\nTranscribe by the Pine Druid Garun.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~Section A: Druid Conduct\n\nGeneral Conduct\n\nA.) Never insult a fellow brother or sister in any way ((OOC or IC)).\n\nB.) Never kill a brother or sister ((for fun, etc.))\n\nC.) Never steal from the order or from a brother or sister.\n\nD.) Don't destroy property of the Order.\n\nE.) If you are below the rank of guide, it is not your place to make decisions that affect the order as a whole.\n\nF.) All Druids must conduct themselves in a mature and upright manner ((OOC & IC))\n\nG.) Never criticize a brother or sister in an overly negative way. ((OOC or IC))\n\nH.)Calm the heck down!\n\nI.) Always immediately contact a higher ranking Druid if you have a problem.\n\nJ.) Stay active ((On the forum.))\n\nK.) Never criticize someone ((OOC for actions done IC or vice versa.))\n\nL.) A Druid may use violent force if they or other Druids are in danger, it is self defence, or if it is in defense of nature or the balance.\n\nConduct around Shunned:\n\nA.) When a shunned person enters the grove immediately instruct them to leave. If they do not leave instruct them once that you will forcibly remove them if they do not leave. If they still stay a Druid is free to use any mean\n\npossible to remove a shunned from the grove and the surrounding area.\n\nB.) When a shunned person with a KOS designation enters the grove immediately instruct them that they will be killed if in the next ten seconds they do not leave. When the ten seconds\n\nhas expired a Druid is free to slay any non-obeying shunned.\n\nC.) When you see a shunned person (even with a KOS designation) somewhere other than a grove, continue on your way and do not try to make contact.\n\nD.) If a shunned tries to make contact with you somewhere outside a grove simply reply with the phrase \"Much Wind Pours from your mouth\" and move on. If they speak to you again repeat the phrase. If they try a third time inform them that if they\n\ntry to speak to you again you will reply with violent force.\n\nE.) If a shunned with a KOS designation tries to contact you somewhere other than a grove, inform them that they have ten seconds to move away from the present location before violence is used.\n\nF.) If at any time a shunned becomes aggressive or violent, refer to Section A, Subsection 1, Line L of the Druidic Code.\n\nSection B: Initiation and Ranking Up:\n\n1.) Outsider to Dedicant\nA.) Complete an extensive interview with a Guide.\n.) Recite the Dedicant's Vow.\n\n2.) Dedicant to Druid\nA.) Stay a member for at least two Elven weeks. If seen as unready by the guide or higher, shall stay until the guide deems you ready.\nB.) Complete a varying amount of Druidic Trials assigned successfully.\n\nC.) Complete a Grand Task.\nD.) Choose carefully what totem you will go under. This can only be changed once after becoming official.\nE.) Become attuned in the ceremony performed by an Arch Druid or Guide.\n\n3.) Druid to Guide\nA.) Stay a member for four Elven weeks (being a Dedicant does not count). If seen as unready by an Arch or higher, be patient and gain wisdom.\nB.)Once deemed as ready, take training underneath an Arch as an apprentice, and watch how\n\nthey are to Dedicants, how they assign tasks, how they handle the grove, etc.\nC.) Study up on the subject, as well as how to perform an attunement ceremony, what the tasks entail, what the interviews for Dedicants are meant to have, as well as other\n\nthings your teacher suggests you learn.\nD.) Practice giving a few Dedicants tasks under the supervision of your teacher.\nE.) Once you and your teacher both feel you are ready, the teacher will discuss with the other Arch's and you shall begin guideship.\n\nSection C: Punishments\n\n1.) The punishment for breaking a rule depends on person, severity, the rule broken and previous track record.\n\n2.) The punishment for breaking a rule includes but is not limited to: a warning, probation, a shun, a KOS (kill on sight) designation and banishment from Athera ((Server ban)).\n\nSection D: Clauses\n\n1.) All rules are subject to change.\n\n2.)Section B, Subsection 1, Line C is optional if the Dedicant does not plan on becoming a Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Punishment II", "§bArchmage Crumena", "The Punishment of Hubris II\n\nWhat Nemiisae did not realize was that the portal had only been closed to prevent their leaving. The portal within the Verge to this new land was still open to anyone who could discover it. And discovered it was. The Dwarves were first to uncover\n\nthe portal into the Verge, as the first group to find it mined into the cavern it had been hidden in. Seeing the notes left behind by Nemiisae, they sent one dwarf ahead to try and locate the portal inside the Verge. He returned shortly, proclaiming\n\nthe glory of the land he saw reflected in the portal’s visage! Mountains, gold, diamonds, as far as the eye could see! It was right there, a short walk away! A world of their own, which they could run as they like, without having to share it with\n\nanyone! The Dwarves quickly made a decision to gather their families and things and venture through. Within the day, they were ready to venture to the Verge and then towards their new land. Greedily, they decided they had to prevent others\n\nfrom discovering this mystical, resource rich land. Using good, old fashioned Dwarven ingenuity, they collapsed the tunnel they had accidentally discovered the portal via, then quickly passed through. They quickly found the portal\n\ninside the Verge leading to this mystical new land and pass through that as well. And again, another group had fallen for the trap. The portal was closed behind them, so there was no place left to go but forward. They ventured into the\n\nland, ready to settle it and hoping to thrive. But within the next half of a millenia, they had all perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors…creatures or otherwise. All they left behind was skeletons, of their homes and of themselves.\n\n\nAbove ground, as the tunnel to the cavern shifted and collapsed, a huge crevice formed in the landscape. It had not been there the day before and as a Human merchant group passed the area they began to wonder what had caused such a\n\ncrevice. One of them suggested it may have been a tomb, full of riches. Eager to investigate, the Humans spent the next month digging down into the ground, following the slant of the crevice and eventually discovering the cavern which\n\nhoused the portal to the Verge. The Humans too spied the notes and messages Nemiisae had left behind, promising them a land free from Iblees’ curse, free for the taking! Their short lifespans would be gone and they would be immortal like their cousins!\n\nThe merchants quickly climbed back to the surface, cutting down the branches of nearby trees to cover the entrance to the land. They all quickly traveled to their homes, to fetch their families and supplies in order to settle this new land. The came\n\nback less than a week later, descending into the Cavern, through the Verge and into the new world. But they too fell into the trap. The Portal was closed behind them and they had no place left to go but forward. They ventured out to settle these new\n\nlands with their families. But within the next half of a Millenia, the majority of them had perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors. They were not made immortal as they had hoped, but rather had even shorter lifespans than usual. They became\n\ninbred, sick, ill, and in the end all they left behind were shadows of their former selves, a slow, stupid race incapable of complex thought and cursed by maladies and deformities.\nAfter the Humans had placed tree branches to cover the entrance to\n\nthe Cavern, a group of Elves ventured into that area, hearing the call of the wounded trees. They discovered the branches and removed them, wondering what foul creature had despoiled the trees in such a way and for what cause. Into\n\nthe cavern they ventured, discovering the notes from Nemiisae and the portal to the Verge. This group did not go back for more, though more would come later, as they were immediately forced through. Running from a threat, they\n\nentered the Verge and discovered the portal to the new world. Fleeing still, they had no choice but to enter. They too fell into this trap, the portal closed behind them, no way back, though they would only find this out after returning later to\n\ninvestigate. For now, they still had running to do. Immortal though they were, this land was still rife with danger. Forced to settle in it, the Elves would follow in the footsteps of their cousins, perishing within this strange lands within half a\n\nMillenia. In these lands they were susceptible not just to the terrors, but also their own curse. Far more infertile than they were in their original lands, they died out merely due to a lack of numbers. While some of them eventually interbred with\n\nNemiisae’s children, those who refused would only gain numbers through other poor fools coming through the portal. In this way the Elves too, were trapped.\nWhen the Elves first found the broken and disturbed trees as well as the secret\n\nthey hid, they did not realize they were being hunted. Following them from Malinor had been an Orc hunting party, searching for slaves, meat, or just a bit of violent fun. The Orcs assaulted the Elves at the entrance to the crevice, and\n\nhaving no other way to go, the Elves immediately fled into the Crevice and down into the Cavern. The Orcs gave chase, of course, following them through the Verge and the next portal, into the new world. The Elves had gotten ahead, fleeing to the\n\nnearest forests they could find. In the thick cover, the Orcs lost sight of them. They began to investigate the land as their cousins had. They settled, adventured, and fought. Fighting was what they were good at and they were much better\n\nequipped for the trip into this new world, to face the terrors that haunted it. But their own aggression killed them in the end. They perished at the hands of beasts, monsters they should have known they would never defeat, at least not in totality.\n\nWithin a half of a Millenia, the Orcs too were extinct, leaving behind only the skeletal ruins of their previous homes and their old enemies they had died out battling.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed, 1473.\nTo be continued in the third volume.\n[Credit to TehLulu for the writing itself.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 5", "Eenhoornheid", "New Elven Lessons:\n     Volume V\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nIn elven in order to denote affiliation the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and\n\nmeans in such a case 'spirit'. This also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaean'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\".\n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in word 'evareh' . In elven it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh - Operative sing\n-erih - Operative pl", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeriel Question", "§bBael Tunnelsmasher", "THE AERIEL QUESTION\n-------------------\n\nA discussion on the worship of the diety\n    \" A E R I E L \"\n\n\n\n\n\n       Archbishop\n Bael Tunnelsmasher\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nFor the longest period of time, certain members of the Irongut clan; dwarves of otherwise good repute, have been accused of heresy.\n\nUpstanding individuals, such as Hiebe, Algrim and Phelrin have professed faith in Aeriel as a true God\n\nand have, by some twisted circumstance, suffered because of it.\n\nWith no historical evidence, whether in ruins, artefact or record, holding that Aeriel was ever worshipped by the early Dwarven societies, and the\n\nsignificant distaste for Aeriel was compounded further by the betrayal of the dwarves by the Ascended sages in the late-Aegis period.\n\nSave for a few faithful, Aeriel-belief is detested and even branded heretical by some factions of the\n\ndwarven people, most significantly found in the faction of Kjell and his clansmen.\n\nBut historical reasoning aside, is there any true founding for such distaste and hostility?  \nThe Sages were revealed in the end\n\nto have been corrupted by Iblees, so their motives were certainly not pure, but neither were they the orders of their patron. Which brings us to the \"Aeriel Question\".\n\nIs Aeriel-worship compatible with the dwarven faith?\n\nMany would say \"no\".\nFewer yet say \"yes\".\n\nMost care very little, but for the sake of religious stability, I will examine the similarities and attempt to reconcile the mainstream creed with that of the Aerielist faction in the faith.\n\nThe most common claim is that Aeriel is merely another name for the commonly accepted divinity named \"Anbella.\" A mistake to be sure.\n\nAeriel is best known for being the opponent to the fallen daemon Iblees as the other divinities stood\n\nstill and allowed him to rampage on the mortal realms, however, those informed few of us are aware that Aeriel is infact a guardian of the Dead.\n\nA sphere that is totally incompatible with the Godess of Life and Living: Anbella. Many would rejoice\n\nat hearing of this incompatibility; particuarly the Irehearts, however, the sphere of Aeriel is compatible with another divinity in the dwarven faiths:\n\nDUNGRIMM\n\nI suggest that Aeriel is infact an aspect of\n\nDungrimm. Now it is also knowledge to the learned that Aeriel is not a war-like diety, whereas Dungrimm is the embodiment of righteous war.\n\nMy suggestion is not that Dungrimm is Aeriel, but rather Aeriel is the personification of Dungrimm's more\n\nfeminine traits. The feminine aspects of a certain diety, while Dungrimm is the personification of the masculine traits of the same diety.\n\nOf course, even as I am the supreme shepherd and lord of the Dwarven faiths, it is not within my\n\nauthority to add or subtract from the established order as many others would do with impunity, but rather should I succeed in recalling the other remaining bishops, this matter of doctrine will be sealed in Synod and all will be bound by decree.\n\nSEALED BY\nHIS HOLINESS;\nBAEL TUNNELSMASHER\nIN THE REIGN OF\nHIS HIGHNESS;\nKING THORIK GRANDAXE\n\nSigned:\nAbsp. Bael T.\nBsp. Thrym I.\nBsp. Dominic I.", ""),
        StaticBook("Graven Laws", "§b'The Shrieking Knight'", "Orders of thy Graven\n-------------------Thou shall follow thou's task.\nThou shall honor thy master.\nThou shall honor thy Brethern.\nThou shall honor thy comrade.\nAmen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wishing a wish", "§bEsgäleth Vynatis", "Forbidden Books.\nLost books. \nPrefferably containing valuable knowledge. \n\n\n- Esgaleth Vynatis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edible Flowers", "Teerz", "Edible Flowers\n\n*Only eat petals if this sign is shown.\n\nAngelica\n\nGood with fish and steps are good candied.\n\nTaste like Celery.\n\nAnise Hyssop\n\nTastes sweet like licorice.\n\nApple\n\nDelicate floral flavor\n\nArugula\n\nNutty or spicey almost pepper flavor.\n\nBee Balm\n\nTastes like earl gray when made into tea.\n\nBorage and Burnet\n\nBoth taste like cucumbers.\n\nCalendule *\n\nTastes spicy, tangy and peppery.  Turns foods golden.\n\nCarnation\n\nApple like flavor, good for tea.\n\nChamomile *\n\nTastes similar to apple, good for tea.\n\nChrystanthemum *\n\nTastes slightly bitter with a pungent aroma.\n\nCoriander\n\nSoapy like flavor.\n\nCornflower * \n\nSweet and spicy, clover like flavor.\n\nDandelion *\n\nBuds are good fried in butter, tastes like mushrooms.   \n\nGood for wine.\n\nDay Lily\n\nTastes sweet like lettuce leaves, tastes slightly like chestnuts or beans.\n\nGladiolus*\n\nTastes like lettuce\n\nHibiscus\n\nStamens are bitter.\n\nTastes unique, makes a good drink when boiled.\n\nHollyhock\n\nTastes very bland.\n\nImpatiens\n\nBland flavor.\n\nJasmine\n\nDelicate sweet flavor, great for tea.\n\nJonny Jump up\n\nTastes sweet almost bland.\n\nLavender\n\nTastes floral, slightly perfumey.\n\nLilac\n\nLemony floral flavor.\n\nMallow\n\nSweet delicate flavor\n\nMiragold\n\nSpicy and even bitter.\n\nOkra\n\nTastes similar to Squash blossoms.\n\nPansy\n\nvery mild sweet and tart flavor.\n\nPinapple Guava\n\nSimilar to ripe fruit, flavorful.\n\nPrimrose\n\nSweet almost bland like flavor.\n\nRadish\n\nMild sweeter version of the radish plant.\n\nRedbud\n\nMildly sweet flavor.\n\nRose\n\nAromatic Flavor.\n\nRosemary\n\nPinelike flavor, sweet and savory.\n\nRunner Bean\n\nNectar, bean like flavor.\n\nScented Geranium\n\nTastes similar to lemon or mint.\n\nSnapdragon\n\nBland almost bitter flavor.\n\nSociety Garlic\n\nMild garlic flavor.\n\nSquash Blossom\n\nSweet nectar flavor.\n\nSunflower\n\nSlightly bitter flavor.\n\nThyme\n\nTastes like lemon.\n\nTuberous\n\nSour crisp almost lemon flavor.\n\nViolet\n\nNectar like flavor.\n\nYucca *\n\nCrunchy fresh flavor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Risen Journal", "§bArchMage Bell", "RISEN JOURNAL\nThis journal is dated around 1302 of the last era of Aegis.\n\nI've come across an interesting concept as of late. The premise of it is quite interesting. And it is quite in-depth for such a simple matter. To explain it initially is simple. The concept is that of equivalent exchange. The idea that you cannot have\n\nsomething, from nothing. You must first give up something of equal or greater value. But it is much more complex than that....and has a greater impact on the current situation than it appears. I will write more on this subject as I continue my studies.\n\nBut I believe it may be very useful against the undead... :: I have travelled quite a bit since my re-awakening as it were. I cannot help but take advantage of the fact that I feel well, and alive for once.\n\nI had the pleasure of speaking with Arcane Mage Slayer at Laurelin the other day. He's quite the gentleman, which was especially useful when that idiot Rinscher was buggering me. He was able to cast a spell on him to ward him off, which hopefully scared\n\nhim away from me. Which is good, considering were it not for the Monks of the Temple, Rinscher would have succeeded in killing both King Perea and High Prince Native, though I am more upset about the latter of the two.\n\nI've also travelled to Alkhazar again, take a...less travelled route, and met a group of travelling merchants who go by the names of various sins of man. I would have no trouble with them at all had one of them not sought fit to threaten me on the\n\nrooftops of Alkhazar. (I have become a bit enamored with running atop the roofs, I am embarrassed to admit.)\n\nParanoia is still at a dangerous high in Alkhazar. I can understand it, to an extent. I myself do not trust many people at all. Though I have been trying to judge people on their actions, not how I see them. Yet my instinctive judgements have usually been\n\ncorrect, so far.\n\nNow I have set out once more, to the Valve. I have passed throught before, but only now have been given a proper tour by the Grand Champion, Whurili. They seem to be well prepared in the event of an undead invasion. But when I first arrived, they and a\n\nfew orcs were discussing alliances namely the idea that orcs and dwarves would ally, and humans and elves...but against whom? Each other? I will have to find out as much about this as possible. But for now, I've decided to begin officially leaving my old\n\nlife behind. Or, atleast, the agony and bitterness I had because of it. In a symbolic gesture, I have decided to leave one of my journals hidden outside the Valve. I have all the valuable information from them written down elsewhere.\n\nBut there is no longer any need to try and recall the false memories which once plagued my mind. I leave part of my insanity here, behind me. And still, I look forward to the future and the seven skies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry ((1))", "Sofetios", "The Dreamer,\n                The Lake,\n          Friend or Enemy,\n              and Imprint.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                       -By Sofetios\n\n              The Dreamer\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs your dreams you try to tame.\n\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\n\nUnawakened, the Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds paper he jots.\n\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.\n\n                 The Lake\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening's yawn.\n\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed.\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don't seem to last.\n\nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes smaller still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\n\nIt has become ten times smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven thought it has not changed.\nTo other people it might be normal,\nbut to me it is considered strange.\n\n                 Friend\n                    or\n                 Enemy?\n\nEverywhere I am\nI hide from your sight,\nIf it's in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\n\nI am one of sleep's worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear's best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\n\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when its hot and I'm in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI'm sure to give you a fright.\n\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\n\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.\n\n                Imprint\n\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never do fall,\nAt least that's what I like to tell.\n\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nUsually in the day,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favorite toy.\n\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\n\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.\n\nThe End", ""),
        StaticBook("Flynn's Wish", "§bFlynn Terrance", "Flynn Terrance's\nBook of his wish.\n\nI wish to become honored by all others, not become rich, just honored.", ""),
        StaticBook("Everal", "§bLeyu", "The History of Everal, the First City of the Elves\n-Retold by Leyu'Maehr\nVaehaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((9/10/13))\n\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a Magikal power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantely there and in the surrounding\n\nareas. The sand there made glass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the First Race, later known as Elves, planted their magikal seeds... great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary Fyre could not scorch these\n\ntrees, for the magik embeded in them was still new. The Elves thrived in the new land along with the trees, spreading its seeds wherever they went, creating an Empire that Dwarfed all others previousely known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of\n\nthese towering trees, singing to them to help them grow. And all was peaceful. Then one day many centuries later, a Astronomical Strom swept across the land, Felling the Magikal Trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the\n\ngound and forming pools of lava. Great Fyre, fueled by the dark energys of the storm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometers remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning\n\nProtected in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the Magikal trees once more, but the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn't let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to\n\nreach for the sky! They trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the Atmosphere! And all was at peace one again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that rose with the\n\nStorm. And then a terrible thing happened. Some of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral, preferring the\n\nnew forests beyond its border. They spread out far accross the land, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually even they settled down and formed small villages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting\n\nwhat they left behind. By this time only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other Elves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left each family took with them a seed from the\n\nfirst tree, which happened to reside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes. And its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armor to\n\nhelp the remaining elves in their journeys. This armor now resides in the Tomb of Evaral, as the First Tree's spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in Evaral. However over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them.\n\nUntil one day, many centuries later, it came in the hands of a young druid. The great city of Evaral's location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still ou t there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it. And bring it to power\n\nonce again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vidar's Wish", "§b'The Bear'", "Vidar's Wish\n\n\"Ah wish t'at meh smit'ing skill would guh up. Ah've been workin' meh arse off an' et is takin' suh bloodeh long!\"\n\n- Vidar Frostbeard\n  Aslso known as 'The Bear'", ""),
        StaticBook("Coppied Book", "§b-", "*This book seems to be a recently made copy*\n\nPanacea, one of the Four great Myths of Alchemy. A concoction which is said to cure all, be it a cut, a broken bone, an illness or a curse. No matter what ails the user will be cured. I wonder if this is a good thing.\n\nThe only thing said that Panacea is not able to heal is death. Such is said to be a myth due to the nature of cure everything. It is said to cure even illnesses of the mind, have one thought what that is?\n\nAn illness of the mind might be as extreme as hearing voices that aren’t there, or phobias of all kinds, so those would be healed. Yet what of those which might be simple and might or not be an illness?\n\nThink of depression, would that be an illness of the mind, or simply a state of mind? Would one that drank it reach a state of full perfection of body and mind, perfect immunity of new illnesses, how would it be?\n\nThe matter that an alchemist can never know the full outcome of the myth is one of the parts that make it a myth. I spoke of immunity of illnesses and perhaps even poisons. That is one theory that Panacea can also bring.\n\nOther parts of the Panacea that are left undecided are of the speed it acts. Some say it’s instantaneous, others say it reacts in seconds, others say it takes hours or days depending on the severity.\n\nOne thing all say about it, it may heal all cuts, broken bones, physical ailments, and all types of poisons. Most of these things can already be done with powerful or greater potions of mending and healing.\n\nWhat makes Panacea so special is that it is said to cure all curses. Alchemy reaching into the realm of magic healing and taint healing is unheard of being successful. Such is the greatness of Panacea.\n\nThe greatest curse to heal is of course, the curse of Iblees. This separates it from the Elixir of Life, the myth of the creation of immortality, which is said makes one unable to die, but does not remove him of harm or curses.\n\nOne can imagine the outcome of a human taking the Elixir of Life without taking Panacea as well, as one that can not die having a curse of old age would not have a good result. Sometimes curing everything is better than being immortal.\n\nThoughts of Alchemy Myths - Panacea\n\nby Luteran Barkin", ""),
        StaticBook("i will yes", "§bKuro", "I wish I had the head of my ex-wife to wear as a lovely hat, Rivenza always did like collecting hats.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dark Wish", "§bAzaghal Doomforged", "A wish story;\n\nOnce upon a time, in a land far away, across the seas lived a horrible race of creatures called Harbingers. They were the most feared beings on that plagued continent known as Anthos, and rightfully so, weilding necrotic powers, and a\n\nseemingly godlike prowess for magical abilities. I wish for a race like this to come back to the lands, to put fear in the hearts of the mortal races again, we have grown to comfortable in our lives, in our plushy estates and manors, our stone casltes and\n\nwooden farms. I want a darkness to set upon these lands, perhaps one which we may not find the light in again.\n\ntl;dr ((pls antag pls. i wish for antag to happen.)\n\nThe book's words are written in a dark red ink, strange runes are doodled onto each page", ""),
        StaticBook("Ioannis' Wish", "§bIoannis Chalkidikeus", "I wish for a donkey. Or maybe two donkeys.\n\n*prays to the Aengul of Harvest!", ""),
        StaticBook("Lumen Liber", "§bAiwendil", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~        Lumen Liber\n         A Book \n            Of\n    oOo Aeriel oOo\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~Blessed are those who keep the words of this ancient prophecy. But beware to those who defile it, for the destruction written in this book shall be\n\nbrought upon the cursed tenfold.\n\n~+~+~ /oOo\\ ~+~+~\n\nThe world has become desolate and unkind. A starless midnight has fallen over the world. You are losing faith, and have allowed Iblees to become the god of this world.\n\nThereby, I, Aeriel, and my Father, the Creator, shall bring destruction when the time comes. We shall destroy the world creating a new era, a new age, and a new world. Heed this warning, for I am coming soon. \n\nIblees shall take power over a large\n\nmass of people. People who are smart, yet weak. They know who they are. In that group the seventh son of a seventh son shall be brought as a gift for Iblees, and he shall have power over him so he may do his will. He shall claim power over the world, and\n\nwill declare war against Iblees. Only those who's eyes have been opened by me will see that this brood of vipers is a liar! Sadly, one of the holy children shall join him, for he shall be a peace-maker. For half an elven generation, this wolf shall lead\n\nthe world, telling lies of the darkness. At the end of this period, I will choose a group who shall fight against the dark one, the one who is nameless. This group shall be led by a King and a Queen. They shall be called the Lord of the Wood and the Lady\n\nof the Light. These two may be of any descendant race, but must be betrothed! Together they shall lead against the darkness and they shail prevail. But then, in a desolate time, one shall die at the hands of Iblees himself, and therefore half of every\n\nliving thing shall turn to dust. That is when I, Aeriel, shall fall down from the seven skies like a dew drop from the tallest of trees. All shall see my beauty and despair. I shall not be a Dark Lord, but their Queen! Along with my brethren, the Aenguls,\n\nand our cousins, the Daemons, we shall destroy all that is tainted and shall make the world anew. However, we shall wage war on Iblees, but we are no match for him. This shall be when the All-Father, the Creator, descends upon the world.\n\nA great shadow shall fall across the sky and all the stars will fall upon the world to form his sword. And his sword shall be of pure light! Brighter than the brighest lights, and all that fear the Father shall be blinded until destroyed. Taking his sword\n\nhe shall slice Iblees into a thousand pieces and scatter him across the universe. When the time comes he shall come back and rise up once again, but he shall be but a mere mortal. And with this I shall take the holy spear and throw it through his heart,\n\ndestroying the one who has forsaken the world. When the evil one dies, a great snow shall fall unto the world and all will be silent. Even the beating of the heart won't be heard. Everyone living thing will freeze and die, and all things shall end.\n\nThe All-Father shall release his pet, the serpent and it shall swallow the world whole. And a world shall be born anew with prosperity. And the ones who have love and light in there hearts shall once more be resurrected up from the dust in which they were\n\ndestroyed, and all shall have everlasting life. \n\n Long Live the Light!", ""),
        StaticBook("A humble request", "§bDak'ir Des'Nox", "I wish merely for a shred of my people's past. A tome or an item from times long gone. Something pertaining to the history of the mali'ker.", ""),
        StaticBook("Darker Poetry", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Darker Poetry\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\nThe Sound of Memory\n\nI was wandering the hallway,\nIn my lonely abode.\nThinking of my once beloved son,\nThe memory that was poorly sewed.\n\nI went into his room,\nAlways just wanting to see.\nBut then I heard a sound,\nWait… could it be?\n\nI heard the sound of breathing,\nEver so slight.\nThough where was it from?\nI knew I had to be right!\n\n“John!” I said intensely,\nWaiting for a sound.\nThe breathing got even louder,\nAnd the stairs began to pound!\n\n“John come out!”,\nI cried in desperation.\nBut the breathing got louder still,\nI said, “Stop this evil sensation!”\n\nI ran to my room,\nAs fast as I could go.\nAnd got into my bed,\nWondering if I wanted to know.\n\nI lay shaking in my bed,\nMy head in the sheets.\nThe breathing continuing to get louder,\nAnd the stairs continuing to beat!\n\n“Be gone!” I yelled desperately,\nLooking at the door of my room.\nJust waiting for,\nSomething to loom.\n\n Then I ran to the door,\nAnd shut it tight.\nWondering if there would ever be,\nAn end to this eternal night.\n\nBut then I looked to my bed mantle,\nAnd saw a picture of John.\nThe breathing began to subside,\nAnd the beating didn’t carry on.\n\nI remembered then,\nWhat I should have long ago.\nMy dear john would never again,\nEver, ever, show.\n\n          Alone\n\nStanding alone,\nOn a seashore in the sky,\nHoping someone will come through,\nMaybe someone that's new,\nTo create a new tie.\n\nNever knowing one,\nExcept me,\nWishing to know more,\nNot knowing what for,\nJust knowing what is to be.\n\nSearching the sea,\nFor anything in sight,\nLooking for bliss,\nBut this I do miss,\nIn the darkness of the night.\n\nA feeling,\nSomething inside me,\nA feeling deep inside,\nTrying to hide,\nAs it grows harder to be.\n\nWaiting,\nFor anything for me to atone,\nGrowing old,\nAnd growing less bold,\nAs I slowly turn to stone.\n\nAlone,\nSitting in the dark night,\nTrying to see,\nBut nothing there to be,\nJust waiting for it to be light.\n\n         The Lane\n\nI wander away,\nOn a dusky lane,\nWondering if,\nI'll ever have a name.\n\nI have a name,\nBut it's not who I want to be,\nThe name I want,\nIs the name that is me.\n\nI wander down this lane,\nTogether but apart,\nWalking through an endless maze,\nWithout even a chart.\n\nI see a light,\nA light far away,\nBut it always seems to be,\nThat it never will stay.\n\nI wander down this lane,\nAnd many others at this time,\nHoping that they will come together,\nLike two words becoming one rhyme.\n\nI wander down this lane,\nThe same lanes again,\nSometimes stopping on some,\nOnly to start again.\n\nI wander away,\nOn a dusky lane,\nThings happening that are maddening,\nBut somehow I remain sane.\n\nI wander down these lanes,\nNever less, never more,\nDoing all the things,\nThat I had only done before.\n\n          Inside\n            and\n             Out\n\nI am sitting in my old stone box home,\nHappy and content,\nFor I go to this place many a time,\nWhen my will has bent.\n\nThe walls slowly are coming in,\nAs I wonder things aloud but silent,\nAnd of the things trying to get in the box,\nThe walls remain resilient.\n\nThe bird in the cage sings it's silent song,\nAs the walls become smaller still,\nThough on the outside it remains adamant,\nThe inside begins to fill.\n\nTime stalks me as the walls begin to collapse,\nAnd a dark murkiness shows through,\nI know of it's intentions well,\nNone of it to be new.\n\nIt tells me that it's different,\nI know it's not but doubt remains,\nAnd the closer it does creep,\nThe more it strains.\n\nThen again I trust it,\nAs the walls finally collapsed.\nBut alas all I see is darkness behind it,\nAnd memories from the past.\n\nSo I begin to build again,\nMy stone box of old,\nHoping the next time,\nMe and the bird will be bold.\n\nTHE END\n\nThis poetry was from my more... dark days. I hope you atleast enjoyed reading them.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))\n\nIf you were not sold this book by Sofetios Jayamen, it was done without his permission.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Shamanism.", "§bDato Miian", "[!] This books is very very old and muttered.\n\n\n\n       Orcish\n      Shamanism\n\nChapter 1: How it works.\n\nChapter 2: Influencing\n\nChapter 3: Forcing\n\nChapter 4: What happens!\n\nCHAPTER 1.\n\nDark Shamanism is a different way of getting Spirits to aid you. Instead of convincing them, you use set of different magics to negatively influence/force the Spirits to give it's true name and make the pact, giving you power over the spirit.\n\n It is then forced to do whatever you'd like as long as the dark magic keeps influencing it.\n\nDark Shamanism is not a different magic all on its own, but rather just a different method with severe side affects. Think of it as \"The Corruption\n\nof Magic\", however that is only affects Shamanism and its sub-types.\n\nFirst you must connect to the Spirit World. You must conserve as much energy as possible, so the usual method of candle lighting/cactus green and heavy meditation\n\n is needed. As your connect to the Spirit Plane/realm, you must then call upon your Dark Magics. For this to even work, you must be advanced/intermediate in whatever Shaman sub-type you are trying to darkly influence, because summoning the two\n\nmagics, even for a ritual, will be difficult. Once you have called upon your dark magics, you get the Spirit to come to you once connected.\n\nThen, the user use himself, his soul, as an anchor between the physical plane and spiritual plane.\n\n This process is difficult, and the magic will seep through you and into the spiritual plane. You must then apply it to the Spirit at hand, and use it to negatively decide their decisions. Their are two ways to go about this!\n\nCHAPTER 2.\n\nUsing your dark magic, you can influence the spirit at hand. You can use it barely enough so that the Spirit agrees to make the pact, even if there is a negative to it. Since the magic is subtle, the Spirit may realise a mistake and leave you entirely,\n\nand you must find a new Spirit to practice on. This is a risky way, but it is more subtle than forcing. Once the pact is made, and when magic is channeled into the Physical Plane, bits and pieces of the dark magic you originally used will show, but not as\n\nmuch as forcing someone. The side affects will be cut in half however still noticeable.\n\nCHAPTER 3.\n\nUsing your dark magic, you can completely and utterly force a spirit to do your will. Its like using your dark magic\n\nand slamming it's face onto the table it is aware you are negatively influencing it a lot, however it is completely powerless to do anything. Other spirits will take notice immediately if this evil magic and may \"Tell on you\" to others Shamans. Massive\n\namounts of dark magic will pour through the channeled magic, and will make your Shaman magic extremely noticeable.\n\nCHAPTER 4.\n\nYour dark magic does not corrupt the spirit, but rather the magic it sends out.\n\nThe Spirit is far to powerful for your magic to affect, but the power it sends out if affected. The dark magic will negatively influence the sub-types of Shamanism. These are the effects:\nElementalism: As tiers progess, fire will turn blacker, the earth\n\nwill be slightly tainted as you move it around. Water will become blackened and dusty, turning someone extremely sick if they were to drink it. Finally the air would have a nasty, blackened tinge to it.\nLuataman: As magic seeps into you, yourself, your\n\nskin turns blackened and shows a sign of age. Your blood turns a blacker color. However in the heat of bloodlust your power is heightened.\nWitchdoctor: Your blessings will become much less potent as the dark magic seeps through your power, and your curses\n\nand taints will become stronger. Your potions and lands affected have a musty, old, rotten smell to them.\nFarseer: The dark magic clouds your ability of sight, your sightings become darker. You frequently see more dark, sinister things in the future than\n\nhappy and pleasant ones. Even if it is happy, it is turned upside down as your point of view becomes negative.\n\nDo not use this book for bad. Use it intuitively!", ""),
        StaticBook("Prices of Potion", "RedBench", "Prices of Potions\nBy Gauldrim Irongut\n\nPotion 1: Potion of Swiftness\n- (2 minute Effect) 40 mina\n- (8 minute Effect) 60 mina\n\nPotion 2: Poison\n- (0.45 second effect) 50 mina\n\n-(2 minute effect) 70 mina\n\nPotion 3: Potion of Slowness\n\n-(1.30 minute) 40 mina\n-(4.00 minute) 50 mina\n\nPotion 4: Potion of Harming\n\n-Potion of Harming 50\n\n- Potion of Harming II\n60\n\nPotion 5: Potion of Weakness\n\n-(1.30 minute) 40 mina\n-(4 minute) 55 mina\n\n((More to be added))", ""),
        StaticBook("Brightest Day", "§bfirespirit44", "In the deepest dark, no moon, no light\n\nJust the neverending twilight, a starless sky\n\nThe wind howls, the mountain crumbles\n\nA single warrior stands straight, above the fallen eight.\n\nSoon the warrior is gone\n\nLeaving the eight to their fate\n\nTo be immolated in the black flames, their skins just like ash\n\nTheir eyes raging with hate and despair, crumbling to dust.\n\nLeaving me in the darkest of nights\n\nBut the darkest of knights\n\nCan only give way to the brightest of day.\n\n~Kote Gerrymyn", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 1", "§bLeyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 1\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun Kameki\n\nLeyun's Forward\nWhen I learned to use the gifts of nature to heal, Callax gave me his list of herbs. It is time to write this information down in a form that can be widely shared. Hopefully it'll be of use to anyone who heals using herbs.\n\nAthin\nAn herb with a blue visage. It grows at the bottom of almost frozen lakes.\nEffects: Athin works as a cooling balm, making an excellent lotion. It also can cause blue hued skin.\nOverdose: Mild Frostbite\n\nAlchemical Properties:\nAthin is a strong water symbol, good for use in colder potions.\nNotes: Generally requires at least two people to harvest due to freezing conditions.\n\nAlabaster Leaf\nAn herb of Alabaster hue. It grows in drier areas in forests, typcally near fallen trees.\nEffects: As a mild poison, Alabaster Leaf causes dizziness and nausea.\nOverdose: Extreme fatigue.\n\nAlchemical Properties: Alabaster Leaf is a moderate earth symbol.\nNotes: Often used as a dye/paint. Harvest by carefully cutting the leaves.\n\nAqua Nymph\nA small chain of fragile blue baubbles that grow underwater. It is often mistaken for frog or toad spawn.\nEffects: Severe hallucinations when ingested as an herb. Powerful burn remedy when boiled. Causes the throat to close up when\n\ningested in oil form.\nOverdose: Stronger Effects\nAlchemical Properties: Aqua Nymph is a strong water symbol.\nNotes: Aqua Nymph is extremely delicate and must not be touched by hands. A correct way to harvest the herb is to take the thin layer\n\nof sediment that it grows in and the whole plant, scooping it into a jar so that it doesn't touch the edges and it's roots remain intact. If done any other way, it will likely ruin the plant.\n\nThe plant can be made into a powerful burn remedy by pouring\n\nthe whole plant into into a cauldron and small pot. When boiled, the plant's buds will release a liquid that will make a thick oil that can be easily spread over burns.\n\nBeard Weed\nA shaggy green moss that grows hanging from rare trees in caves. A rare herb, but grows in plentiful groups.\nEffects: With water and blissfoil, it can aid in the healing of internal organ damage and ease pain. Beard weed famously\n\ncauses significant hair growth. Can be poisonous if not prepared properly.\nWhen toxic, it can cause bloating, nausea, diarrhea, internal bleeding, and even death.\nOverdose: Stiffness. Possible hairgrowth across the entire body, creating a\n\nbeast-like appearance. Alchemical Properties:\nBeard Weed is a moderate earth symbol. It works well in hair tonics.\n\nBlissfoil\nAn oily blue flower that grows in clumps under birch trees.\nEffects: Numbness where the oil is applied. It has been known to cause headaches.\nOverdose: Permanent loss of touch in the affected area.\n\nNotes: Oils are found near the petals and stalk.\n\nBread Mold\nA blue or green mold that grows on bread, cheese, and other food items.\nEffects: This particular mold only affects some individuals negatively. In these individuals, exposure can cause a rash or the throat to close up. The mold\n\nhas disease fighting properties that can be brought out by a skilled druid.\nOverdose: Too much can caue confusion, odd behavior, a severe rash, reduced urination, or seizures.\nNotes: A druid is required to bring out the disease fighting\n\nproperties, and care must be taken to reduce the effect of other types of mold growing with it.\n\nBlood Lotus\nA rust colored herb, found growing near entrances to caves in hot climates.\nEffects: Extremely nutritious, but extended use can turn the skin orange.\nOverdose: Kidney stones.\n\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate Fire Symbol\nNotes: Can be made into a strong, deep red alcohol.\n\nCrimson Vase\nA vase shaped plant with deep red petals that is commonly found in places with a mild amount of light. The herb grows on trees parasitically.\nEffects: Slight burning sensation if it's liquid is spilt. It'll cause rashes.\n\nOverdose: Will burn even more.\nAlchemical Properties: Crimson Vase is a strong fire symbol, typically used in love, rage, and envy potions, as well as Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: The petals are warm to the touch.\n\nCrouching Feather\nAn herb with three white, drooping petals. It only blooms at night under large bushes.\nEffects: Calming and clears the mind. Can cause light-headedness. With proper druidic preparation, it can be used as a sedative.\n\nOverdose: Coma\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It is typically used in clarity potions.\nNotes: Crouching Feather is highly fragile. Wind can damage the plant.\n\nDiddyfunkle\nA bright, purple flowered herb that tends to grow in jungles and plains.\nEffects: The purple stems cause extremely itchy rashes. The center ball's jucies can be used as a sedative or to clear the mind. Can cause unconciousness\n\nor death if not prepared correctly.\nOverdose: Death\nNotes: Tiny amounts can be a delicacy.\n\nDraugr Tongue\nAn aloe like, orange flowered plant that grows in grassy plains.\nEffects: The liquid in the plant makes for a good disinfectant, but stings.\nNotes: The stem is not useful.\n\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nA stinky, orange leafed shrub that grows by water, usually in swamps.\nEffects: Burning taste similar to ginger.\nOverdose: Burns!\nAlchemical Properties: Strong fire symbol, commonly used in Alchemist Fire.\n\nNotes: Easy to pick. Smells bad. It's named for it's use in dwarven brews. The brightest leaves are the most potent.\n\nElf's Hair Vine\nAn white blossomed herb with an icy white visage. It grows on high cliffs in frozen lands.\nEffects: It has a calming effect and can result in more fluid movements, but may cause someone to move too fast, in which case physical\n\nexhaustion could be an issue.\nOverdose: Rapid heart beat, burst blood vessels ad the like.\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It's used in grace and speed potions.\nNotes: The vine is extremely fragile, and the petals contain nectar.\n\nFlame Tongue Root\nA bright rust colored root with a rose-like flower. It can be found in heavily forested areas, burnt out forests, and areas with a lot of sun and water.\nEffects: The root can be used as a coagulant, though it can burn.\n\nBe warned that the spores can cause sensitivity to touch.\nOverdose: Too much blood cloting, strokes, etc.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate fire symbol\nNotes: Fairly hot to the touch. Watch out for those spores.\n\nFrost Vine\nA small, brittle blue vine that grows in frosty areas, usually on trees.\nEffects: Soothes pain and and numbs/relaxes muscles where applied. Full numbness of limbs can occur on prolonged exposure.\n\nOverdose: Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol.\n\nGoblin's Ivy\nA short brown or green vine that can be found clinging to buildings and rocks.\nEffects: Scentless, mild, nausea inducing poison that can also cause mild dehydration.\nOverdose: More nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\n\nAlchemical Properties: Weak to moderate earth symbol commonly used in resilience potions.\nNotes: Goblin's Ivy can survive in nearly moistureless areas.\n\nGrobsnopper\nA pink or yellow buld-like flower that grows on trees, typically found in moist forests.\nEffects: Potent healing effects. \"Soaks up\" disease.\nOverdose: Stomach aches.\n\nHabgobsnit\nA tall, pale-shaded grass that grows in forests and plains.\nEffects: Juices good for numbing. It can provide a sense of clarity... or just get you high.\nOverdose: Paralysis\n\nKing's Ivy\nAn ivy with golden flowers and a dark green stalk that grows on rocks, tree trunks, and old ruins.\nEffects: Can be taken as a stimulent, but can cause agitation.\nOverdose: Heart attacks, and in general too much energy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Conduct", "§bTaynuel", "~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n          The Druidic\n     Code of Conduct\n\n       As created by\n   Apollan in the wake\n    of the Age of Poor\n          Judgement\n\n Scribed by Hare Druid       Taynuel Viellsinch\n\n~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n\nSection A: Druid Conduct\n\nGeneral Conduct\n\nA) Never insult a fellow brother or sister in any way. ((ic or ooc))\n\nB) Never kill a brother or sister ((for fun, etc.))\n\nC) Never steal from the Order or from a brother or sister.\n\nD) Don't destroy property of the Order.\n\nE) If you are below the rank of guide, it is not your place to make decisions that affect the Order as a whole.\n\nF) All Druids must conduct themselves in a mature and upright manner. ((ic or ooc))\n\nG) Never criticize a brother or sister in an overly negative way. ((ic or ooc))\n\nH) Calm the heck down!\n\nI) Always immediately contact a higher ranking Druid if you have a problem.\n\nJ) Stay active. ((on the forum))\n\nK) Never criticize someone. ((ooc for actions done ic or vice versa.))\n\nL) A Druid may  use violent force if they or other Druids are in danger, it  is self defense, or if it is in defense of nature or the balance.\n\nConduct Around the Shunned.\n\nA) When a shunned person enters the Grove, immediately instruct them to leave. If they do not leave instruct them once that you will forcibly remove them if they do not leave. If they still stay a Druid is free to use\n\nany means possible to remove a shunned from the Grove and the surrounding area.\n\nB) When a shunned person with KOS designation enters the Grove, immediately instruct them that they will be killed in the next ten seconds if they do not leave. When ten\n\nseconds has expired a Druid is free to slay any non-obeying shunned.\n\nC) When you see a shunned person, even with a KOS designation, somewhere other than a Grove, continue on your way and do not try to make contact.\n\nD) If a shunned tries to make contact with you somewhere outside a Grove, simply reply with the phrase \"Much wind pours from your mouth\" and move on. If they try to speak with you again, repeat the phrase. If they try a third time inform them that if they\n\ntry to speak to you again you will reply with violent force.\n\nE) If a shunned with a KOS designation tries to contact you somewhere other than a Grove, inform them that they have ten seconds to move away from the present location before violent force is\n\nused.\n\nF) If at any time a shunned becomes aggressive or violent, refer to Section A, Subsection 1, Line L of the Druidic Code.\n\nSection B: Initiation and Ranking Up\n\n1) Outsider to Dedicant\na) Complete an extensive interview with a Guide.\nb) Recite the Dedicant's Vow.\n\n2) Dedicant to Druid\na) Stay a member for at least two Elven weeks. If seen as unready\n\nby the guide or higher, shall stay until the guide deems you ready.\nb) Complete a varying amount of Druidic Trials assigned successfully.\nc) Complete a Grand Task.\nd) Choose carefully what totem you will go under. This can only be changed once after\n\nbecoming official.\ne) Become attuned in the ceremony performed by an Archdruid or Guide.\n\n3) Druid to Guide\na) Stay a member for four Elven weeks (dedicancy not included). If seen as unready by an arch or higher, be patient and gain wisdom.\n\nb) Once deemed as ready, take training underneath the Head Teacher as an apprentice, and watch how they are to Dedicants, how they assign tasks, how they handle the Grove, etc.\nc) Study up on the subject, as well as how to perform an attunement ceremony,\n\nwhat the tasks entail, what the interviews for Dedicants are meant to have, as well as other things your Head Teacher suggests you learn.\nd) Practice giving a few Dedicants tasks under the supervision of your Head Teacher.\ne) Once you and your Head\n\nTeacher both feel that you are ready, the teacher will discuss with an Archdruid and you shall begin your Guideship.\n\nSection C: Punishments\n\n1) The punishment for breaking a rule depends on the person, severity, rule broken, and previous track record.\n\n2) The punishment for breaking a rule includes but is not limited to a warning, probation, a shun, a KOS designation,\n\nand banishment from Athera. ((server ban))\n\nSection D: Clauses\n\n1) All rules are subject to change.\n\n2) Section B, Subsection 1, Line C is optional if the Dedicant does not plan on becoming a Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sporan's Wish", "§bSporan Kyroc", "Sporan's Wish:\n\nI wish for my life span to extend, being able to live the same length as an elf, but age just as slowly, maintaining my features as a young man, until the final years of my life.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Truest Wish", "§bShiloh Ellis", "I wish that my art changes the world for the better.\n\n~*~Shiloh Ellis~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Atheran Uruks V1", "§bTemür Törs Ajedh'raq", "Betrayal of the             Uzg\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten and Recorded\nby\n\nTemür Törs Ajedhraq\nRider of the Subudai\n\nThe Uzg of the Uruks, centered in the Goi, San-Vitar, of the new world, Athera, had experienced a unity un-paralleled in recent history.  In the Goi, the clans Gorkil, Lur, Yar, Kog, Magra, and various others coexisted.  This unity is attributed to the\n\nRex Malog'Yar.  A wise and powerful Shaman, Malog'Yar enacted reform among Uruk culture to bring the Uzg into the forefront of the politics of Athera.  Under these reforms, stricter codes of honor were introduced, which elevated the Uruks from a looseknit\n\nculture of raiders to a unified culture based on code-of-law. These reforms, though, drew harsh criticism from some of the Uruks, especially from the Azog clan.  \n\nThe Azogs, already dissatisfied with the Uzg's hostility towards Raine Academy, was\n\npushed further from their brothers.  Tensions were heightened between the Uzg and the Azogs.\n\nAt this time, another perilous threat arose to challenge the Uzg.  An Uruk, by the name of Zogrocka, had risen to immense power through the wicked\n\nand vile means of Dark Shamanism (a topic I will fully explain in the Expanded History of the Uruks).  Under Zogrocka's leadership\nthe ancient and exiled clan Dom rose again.  The Doms were a clan dedicated to Dark Shamanism, that fell out of Krug's grace\n\ndue to their trickery and abuse of spirits and elementals.  They also offended the Uzgs and other nations through their abominable practice of cannibalism.  Justly, the Uzgs hunted down and executed the Doms in earlier times.\n\nThe rise of the Doms\n\ncoincided with the split of the Azogs and the Uzg.  In the Azogs, the Doms saw an army to enforce their corrupt ways.  In the Doms, the Azogs saw a means to achieve power and claim the Uzg for themselves.  \n\nDespite the Uzg offering complete\n\nand total amnesty to the Azogs upon their return to the Uzg, the Azogs forsook Krug and the Spirits in favor of the dreadful\nDoms.  Making a deal with the patron Spirit of the Dark Shamans, Ixli, the Azogs traded parts of their sanity for the corrupting\n\npower enjoyed by the Doms.\n\nNow combined, the Doms and the Azogs sacked San'Vitar, the Uruk's 'Old City'.  At first, the unholy alliance encountered little resistance and many Uruks of the Uzg were slaughtered.  A joint force of Uruks and\n\nHumans were unable to repel the assailants later on.  The Goi was left severely debilitated following the attack.\n\nAfter the attack, the desperate Uruks pleaded the spirits for guidance.  In an odd series of events, the Uruks were given\n\nassistance.  Following the shrieks of an injured scaddernack, the Uruks discovered a cave where the spirit Veist revealed itself to them.  Veist pledged its support against the Azogs and the Doms, but in return, the Uzg's High Shaman, Brunhyldir,\n\nwas morphed into a Goblin.\n\nIt was in this frail form that the High Shaman Brunhyldir confronted the Dark Shaman Zogrocka.  Alone, the two battled, drawing upon the Mojo that the Spirits granted them (whether that be honorably as\n\nin Brunhyldir's case, or dishonorable, in Zogrocka's).  The honor and the strength of the High Shaman prevailed, and the abhorrent and corrupt Zogrocka was defeated.\n\nLeft without a leader, the Doms were weakened.  The Azogs\n\nfollowing Zogrocka's defeat then attempted to gain power by their own means.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nOn the 6th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, I, Temür Törs Ajedh'raq, was witness to the following events that occurred in San'Vitar.\n\nThe Azogs, unable to gain power through the corruption of Ixli and the Doms, arrived\n\nat the Goi armed and armored.  They approached the Rex in his Blarg and demanded the Rexdom under threat of force.\n\nIt is notable that by Uruk custom, which has been observed for generations, the Rex may be challenged to an 'honor klomp', in\n\nwhich the Rex and the Challenger fight for the title and position of Rex.  These fights generally occur unarmed and unarmored.  With that said, it is also of worth to note that the Azogs, in no way, shape, or form, challenged the Rex honorably to such a\n\nfight.\n\nThe Azogs' justification for such demands were that the current Rex was weak, and the Uzg was crumbling.  They came to the Goi claiming they could make it strong again.\n\nTo justify their for-\n\n-saking Krug and the Spirits, they claimed that the dark powers of Zogrocka had made them servants of the Dark Shamans.  Despite there being a lack of Azog Shamans at the confrontation, the Azog clan claimed to have made amends with the Spirits.  This\n\nblatant lie is further discredited by the presence of Dom Shamans accompanying the Azog party.\n\nFor two days, the Azogs and their Dom Shamans held the Rex.\nTheir terms: the Rexdom and the Uzg, or war.  For two days the Rex held out and\n\nattempted to reason with the Uruks made unreasonable through\nIxli's Bargain.\n\nOn the 8th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, the Azogs departed the Goi as enemies of the Uzg.  With their coup-de-tat failed, they returned to\n\ntheir fort without the Uzg in their command.  Both sides, immediately following the encounter, started to strike alliances with other nations and factions.  The Uruks of the Uzg appealing to those who uphold honor, and who wish to maintain orderly law\n\nthroughout Athera.  And the splinter Azogs, appealing to those who would rather there be the vile corruption of chaos unleashed upon the land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Aspects", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\n Lesson on The Aspects:\nThis lesson teaches a Dedicant the core 'faith', if you will, of Druidism, The Aspects. While little precise information is known about them, through dreams and visions Druids have gleaned a little of the nature of our patrons.\n\nIt is important for the Dedicant to understand that without The Aspects, Druids would have almost none of their gifts, it is the blessing of The Aspects that we can attune to the currents and melodies of nature, the ebb and flow of life around us.\n\nHelp the Dedicant develop a respect and thankful attitude towards The Aspects, they should give thanks to them often. Use other tomes such as 'An Introduction to the Aspects' to aid your lesson.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 4", "§bArinislia", "Elven Lessons 4\n\nOriginally By :Kalenz Uradir. Rescribed by: [Ghost] The Eternal Librarien.\n\nRescribed once more after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\n\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the compostition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten, the simple word in elven to use. The express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before\n\na multiple of ten. For example: niut'matelu means 200.\n\n1- cem\n2-niut\n3-hael\n4-vailu\n5-kulin\n6-banih\n7-laier\n8-esun\n9-moiel\n\n10-telu\n100-matelu\n1000-marmatelu\n\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words for form the names of handheld tools.\n\nSome such examples include those below. However, to those more advanced in elven, others may be thought up. \n\nFer'ame- axe\nFer'thuln- pickaxe\nFer'nor- shovel\nFer'sul -torch\nFer'bilok- hammer\nFer'norsae- hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("Thirty to One", "§b\"Caroline Hightower\"", "C. Hightower:\n\"Thirty to One\"\n\nKey of A-dur | A maj\n\nSharp notes:\n\nF, C, G.\n\nTonic: A\nSub-Dominant: D\nDominant: E\n\nC#     E         D    C#\nBap- tised  in    batt-\n\nD      |   D         E      D\nle         thir-  ty     to\n\nF#- - -\none- - -\n\nRepeat F# / D / A / E\nuntil otherwise instructed.\n\n| - So silent before the storm - -\n\n| - Awaiting command\n\n| - A few has been\n| chosen to stand - -\nas | one outnumbered\nby | far - - -\n\n| - The orders from high command - -\n\n| - \"Fight back hold your | ground\" - - - \n\n| In early Snow's Mai | den it came - - a | war\nunkown to the | world - - -\n\n| - No army may | enter that land - - - that | is protected by\nD      C#      B\nO-    ren's hand\n\n| - Unless you are\n| thirty to one - your\n| force - will soon be un | done - - -\n\n        F\nun-  done - - -\n\n| Bap-tised in bat-tle\n| Thir-ty to one - \n| Victorious Oren\n| Just like al-ways\n\n| Sol-diers from Or-en\n| Se-cond to none -\n| Wrath of the Teutons\n| Brought - to a ha - - - lt.\n\n# Continue the chord sequence with new lyrics.\n\nThe third of Snow's Maiden it starts. Attacks Aesterwald.\n\nA barrage of arrows and fire. Stand fast. The city will hold.\n\nThe emperor has pledged his life. \"I'll face my fate here.\"\n\nThe sound of barbarians so fierce like thunder up high.\n\nSo come bring on all that you've got.\n\nUndead, magic and ba-lli-stas.\n\nUnless you are thirty to one, your lives will soon be undone. Undone.\n\n*** CHORUS. ALL SHALL SING. ***\n\nBap-tised in battle\nThir-ty to one\nVictorious Oren\nJust like always\n\nSoldiers from Oren\nSecond to none\nWrath of the Teutons\nBrought to a halt\n\n*** SING ONCE MORE, PLAYING OCTAVES. ***\n\n*** CODA: ***\n\nCadential 6-4\nChord V 2nd inversion\nChord I (sustain)", ""),
        StaticBook("Wildwyn Woods", "§bJacob Chapel", "The Wildwyn Woods\nThe Wildwyn Woods were a forest near Al'Khazar in Aegis' Oren. This play has been transcribed from an old scroll by Jacob Chapel.\n\nOriginal author:\nJon Evaglno ((Jon021))\n\nScene opens on clearing in the middle of Wildwyn Woods in the middle of the night\n\nRougon Wildwen enters\n\nBushes rustle\n\nRougon: Who's there?\n\nBushes rustle once more\n\nRougon turns to the bush\n\nRougon: Who are you? What do you want with me?\n\nSomething growls\n\nRougon yelps in terror and proceeds to exit\nAll that is heard is the sound of Rougon being mauled\n\nScene opens on small town in Wildwyn Woods\nTownsfolk are about their normal activities, IE buying bread, etc. \n\nOrgoron Wildwen enters\n\nOrgoron: Help! My brother's been murdered!\n\nAll the townsfolk gather around as Orgoron drags his brother's dead body to the center of town\n\nMarya: what happened to him?\n\nOrgoron: I don't know! I just found him in the woods, mangled as he is now.\n\nTownsfolk murmer about the strange event\n\nGnargnon: his wounds look like a beast mauled him!\n\nAryan: what kind of beast? A zombie? A hoard of pigmen? A spider?\n\nGnargnon: none of those. Nothing has claws that could do this. These are worse than a wolf's claws.\n\nAll the townsfolk murmer, shocked. The town elder, Hydragnon, enters \n\nHydragnon: people! People! What is it that brings you into this huddle?\n\nAryan: Rougon's been murdered! \n\nHydragnon examines Rougon's mangled body \n\nHydragnon looks up grimly\n\nHydragnon: this is like that- Nothing I've ever seen before!\n\nOrgoron: whatever it is, it's running free in the woods! That's where I found his body.\n \nHydragnon: nobody go out during the night! Ever!\n\nMarya: but Elder, why not?\n\nHydragnon: It's-er-whatever did this is out there! \n\nDragnon enters\n\nDragnon: Father, we obviously need to get rid of this thing. If we can't go out at night, we can't kill the beast. So, who will come to slay the beast with me?\n\nA hushed silence falls over the townsfolk\n\nOrgoron: I will! I need to avenge my father! The beast will be slain! We are the two best warriors in the village! the beast won't stand a chance!\n\nOrgoron and Dragnon leave the village at night, armored and armed\n\nIn the morning, Gnargnon is walking through the woods, and finds Orgoron dead and Dragnon barely alive.\n\nDragnon: Urg...\n\nGnargnon: Dragnon! It didn't kill you? What was it? \n\nDragnon: D-d-don't go into the w-woods at night.\n\nDragnon dies after delivering that message \n\nGnargnon: Dragnon! Help! I found them!\n\nGnargnon enters the village carrying Orgoron's dead body, and Aryan carrying Dragnon's.\n\nHydragnon: No! NO! My son! He should have never gone out there!\n\nGnargnon: those were his last words, \"Don't go into the woods at night.\"\n\nHyrdragnon weeps over his dead son's body\n\nHydragnon: why did you have to go out there? Why? Why?\n\nGnargnon: Elder.. Do you know what the beast is?\n\nHydragnon: How should I? You think I've been out there? Of course not!\n\nHydragnon marches off, taking his son's body\n\nNight falls over the village\n\nAryan, Marya, and Gnargnon all meet in the town square\n\nGnargnon: something is strange with the Elder. He always seems to know what the beast is.\n\nAryan: maybe we be should leave it alone. After all, he just lost his son.\n\nMarya: if we don't get rid of the beast, we'll lose many more than them\n\nGnargnon: We best investigate then. Let's pay the Elder a visit.\n\nThe three enter Hydragnon's house to find it empty\n\nAryan: where could he be? I doubt he went into the woods.\n\nGnargnon: he might have. But we can't go, because we'll likely be killed.\n\nMarya: we can ask him in the morning.\n\nThe three leave the elder's house\n\nThe sun rises over the town, and the elder is loitering in the town square\n\nGnargnon approaches the elder\n\nGnargnon: Elder? Where were you last night? You weren't at home.\n\nHydragnon: I-I was out burying Dragnon\n\nGnargnon: In the woods?\n\nHydragnon: the woods? of course not!\n\nGnargnon: do you know something about the beast, Elder?\n\nHydragnon: Y-yes.\n\nGnargnon: What? Spit it out!\n\nHydragnon: It's a man and a wolf.. One by day, the other by night.\n\nGnargnon: so someone in town could be it...\n\nHydragnon: yes. I doubt they'd tell you who they are.\n\nGnargnon: we need to find out who it is, and quickly.\n\nGnargnon leaves Hydragnon's home and Hydragnon sighs with relief\n\nGnargnon meets Aryan and Marya to discuss the news\n\nGnargnon: the elder told me what the beast is. It's a man by day and a wolf by night\n\nAryan: so s-someone in the town is the beast?!\n\nMarya: I'm certainly not the beast!\n\nGnargnon: nor I!\n\nAryan: nor I!\n\nGnargnon: then who is it? \n\nAryan: wait... if they were the beast, they'd have to leave the village at night... and Hydragnon wasn't here that night...\n\nGnargnon: you aren't saying he's the beast!\n\nAryan: that is exactly what I'm saying.\n\nMarya: then we need to get rid of him!\n\nGnargnon: we need to pay the Elder another visit.\n\nAll three of them go the Hydragnon's house\n\nHydragnon: Aryan, Marya, and Gnargnon. How can I help you?\n\nGnargnon: we need you in the town square\n\nMarya, Aryan and Gnargnon drag Hyrdragnon into the town square and tye him by his hands and feet to the ground in chains", ""),
        StaticBook("Orichalcum", "Jistuma", "__Orichalcum__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: I found this little gem off of a dead spy named Devin Ryder. Yes, he was a bard and a spy, and he had quite a few things in-between. I’m pretty sure he stole this book. Actually, I’m sure of it.\n\nOrichalcum is a precious metal that is made out of white gold and silver. It can hold powerful and magical energies and is a great material for Magical items such as staves, swords, and magical Tiaras.\n\nIt is used by mages to store spells so that they can release those at the right moment. When using Orichalcum, be aware of its powerful magical properties. Don’t mess around with it - it can become dangerous at the wrong moments.\n\n==How to make==\n\n==Orichalcum==\n\n1- Melt the white gold and silver.\n\n2- Let flow energies of white magic into the metal while forcing it together.\n\n3-Make one metal bar of the combined metals\n\n4- Bend the bar to the shape of the power-rune\n\n5- Power the rune\n\n6- Reshape the rune to the symbol of resistance\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n7- Reshape the rune to the symbol of capacity\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n8- Now create the object you want to make\n\n9-Bury your Orichalcum at a place where it can absorb energies of nature, such as a forest or grove\n\n10- After 5 days your  metal is ready and you can recover it.\n\nThe process is complete now, but don’t expect it to go perfectly smooth the first time. This is a process that needs experience.\n\n-Contact Aurea in Haelun’or if you have questions-\n\nOrichalcum\n\nWritten by Nienna\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((21/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Immortal", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Immortal\n\n          ~By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\n\nThere is a man in the town,\nWho knows that Power is the source of good,\nHe controls the town,\nBut his people do frown,\nBut the man doesn’t notice and never would.\n\nAs he goes through the town,\nAnd buys with a word,\nThe people do stray away,\nAnd for their company he cannot pay,\nBut to him that thought is absurd.\n\nAs the man drinks his wealth,\nEven to him none was dealt,\nThe man gets word one day,\nThat someone had passed away,\nAnd there came a new feeling he’d never felt.\n\nHe traveled very far,\nAnd as he walked to the place,\nHe couldn’t bear to look,\nAt this grave by the brook,\nWhere his life had been another case.\n\nAs he returned home,\nThe Home that never was,\nHe looked into the clouds,\nHe sought an answer he knew he wasn’t allowed.\nAs nearly every person does.\n\nHe walked into the town,\nSure the answer was there,\nWith his wealth here but gone,\nTo other people he was drawn,\nBut he realized the connection he did tear.\n\nAlone in a crowd,\nHe then sat down,\nEveryone just passed by,\nAnd the man began to sigh,\nUntil a small boy came around.\n\nThe boy looked around,\nAnd saw him alone,\nThe boy sat next to him,\nAgainst the man’s own whim,\nAnd said in an easy tone.\n\n“Sorry to bug you now,\nBut you look a bit sad,\nI’ve been following a while,\nAnd you never seem to smile,\nSo I brought something that might help a tad.”\n\nThe boy reached in a bag,\nAnd he pulled out a small ball,\nHe gave it to the man,\nThe man took it in his hand,\nHe dropped it and it bounced tall.\n\nThe man began to smile,\nAs his heart felt sore,\nFor the man’s answer was clear,\nThe very thing he did fear,\nThe immortal things in life you can’t pay for. \n\nThe End\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this.\nI'll be writing more in the future.\n\nIf you like my writing please send me a bird or tell me in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro To Aspects", "§bTristanm1", "Introduction to the Aspects\n\nBy Sunshine Druid Verden\n\nThe Mother of the Harvest, the Goddess of Change, the Green Lady. Cerridwen has many names, but all of them stem from her warm and caring demeanor toward the world. She is the matron Aspect of farmers and gardeners everywhere, and it is\n\nher divine radiance that blesses the crops and flora upon the world. The fragile, but beautiful flowers and the delicious fruits of the land are her domain. The seasons are gifts from her.\n\nThe Father of the Hunt, the King of Forests, the Green Man. Cernunnos also has many names, but all of them reflect upon who this Aspect truly is; a hunter. It was he who brought about the existence of wolves and bears -- of tigers and hawks. The predators\n\nof the land are his apprentices, and the thorny plants his traps. He is the patron Aspect of huntsmen and warriors everywhere, and it is his divine strength that blesses the worthy. The steadfastness of nature comes from him.\n\nThrough their grace, the world and all who dwell upon it came into existence. What we refer to as \"Nature\" is the combined efforts of these two infinitely powerful beings, and it was them that saved the sentient mortal races from utter destruction during\n\nthe Great War. It is our duty as their children to respect and aid Nature whenever possible, and by doing so give praise to their greatness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Knowledge", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nBroader Knowledge:\nThis Task is given in order to teach the Dedicant that knowledge is perhaps the most important thing in the world. Ignorance can easily get you killed, and misunderstanding can easily cause offense where there should not have been.\n\nGenerally this task involves going out and finding two books or tomes that contain knowledge or teachings from outside the Order, it is important they are not Druidic in content, as the entire point of this lesson is to understand\n\nsomething else and fill gaps in their knowledge so they can be more successful in their future dealings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aura", "Eenhoornheid", "Aura\n\n§i    by Salamandra\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nAura, is a gaseous substance that lies dormant within every living being until awakened, and once is awakened, allows the being to cast magic. One who learns to control this aura within their bodies and out, could be known as a 'Mage'.\n\nWhen a spell is casted, a certain amount of aura is drained from the caster, which also affects their physical stamina. If one completely runs out of aura, the result is usually fainting, but some have been known to die from the overuse of magic.\n\nTo replenish one's aura, they must simply not use magic for a long period of time, or to restore aura more quickly, one can meditate.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gray Bard's Song", "§bGrungron Irongut", "The Grey Bards\n           Song\n-------------------The father journeys far away\n\nThe children left behind\n\nThe children now to rule themselves\n\nNo father there to mind\n\nThe child of light creates the stars\n\nHis countless friends to tend him\n\nThe child of fire creates the sun\n\nTo drive away night time sin\n\nThe child of night creates the moon\n\nIts lonely light his sign\n\nThe father comes from far away, his journey at its end\n\nThe children gather 'round his throne\n\nHis glory theirs to tend\n\nThe child of light approaches first\n\nHis father turns away\n\nThe child of fire sees his light, may he be now in dismay\n\nThe child of night there lingers on, the transgression his to mend\n\nThe father now yearns long for sleep, his heart filled with great sadness\n\nThe children flee to their creations, seeking comfort in their kindness\n\nThe child of light calls forth the stars, his company be aenguls\n\nThe child of fire divides the sun, its fragments called the Daemons\n\nThe child of night brings forth the moon to drive away the madness\n\nThe children three now lost to time\n\nTheir glory sealed onto their signs\n\nThe childrens children linger on \n\nThe children third compose their song\n\nThe father now sleeps, his rest sublime \n\nHe hopes to forgive his childrens crime\n\nThe father journeys far away\n\nThe children left behind\n-------------------Composed by the Gray Bard\n\nRecorded by\n\n-Grungron Irongut", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great War", "Saviordude", "The Myth of the Great War\n-------------------Thousands of years ago a terrible war broke out between two mighty guilds of mages - one good and one evil - that controlled great empires. Mages on both sides vowed to fight until they were utterly triumphant,\n\nseeking to purge their rivals from the earth. With fearsome magic and drake armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning a final victory.\nIn the proces of their warfare. the mages wrought vast devastation on the world. Forests caught fire and\n\nblazed till fone, islands sank into the sea, and entire races became extinct. Eventually the Aspects awakened from their slumber to witness the savage confict. Shocked by the destrucion, the Godess sent a vision to a single elf; the woman who would become\n\nthe first Arch Druid, Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a Druidic Order to preserver the fragile remains of her worlds ecology. With the guidance of the Aspects, the order grew in strength until it finally had the power to\n\nintervene in the mages's war. The force of young Druids pooled their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts.\nOnce the former mages - no longer caring about good\n\nversus evil - slither, bounded, loped and crwaled off into their ruined habitats the Order began to heal the world. Since then, the Druidic Order continually works to prevent such destruction from ever occuring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars\n\nof good and evil no longer mar the precious earth. But the order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the guilds of warring mages; those good and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows. Each guild claims it had been on the\n\nverge of victory and would have won, had the Druids not interfered.\n\n-Transcribed by Ol' Treehugger", ""),
        StaticBook("Punishment III", "§bArchmage Crumena", "The Punishment of Hubris III\n\nIn the course of the first two-hundred and fifty years, as Nemiisae searched for a way to open the portal and leave this place, Zanunder aged within his sleep, eventually dying. Bereaved of her husband she fell into a great remorse for having\n\naccidentally killed him. Her mind became clouded, muddled, perhaps even mad. Then her children came to her with reports of these strangers in their lands. She realized then what had happened…The portal only shut on their side. It must\n\nhave been an act of God, she believed. Then she realized, it was a test! As God had tested the Four Brothers, surely he was testing her and these others to become stronger. But her compassion would not allow her to let others fall victim to this trap\n\nshe had unwittingly played a part in. She could not reopen the portal, but she could close it from her side, sealing off both the portal to the Verge and the portal within it to the new world. Then she retreated back into her Caverns, encouraging her\n\nchildren to live, breath, fight, grow stronger. Punish and perish the weak and live for themselves and for her, for it was the only way to gain God’s favor. Then she left them to their own devices, her wishes for their future made clear.\nIt was in this\n\nway that hubris was punished, that the sins of those who came before was tested and they were proven guilty. Had these people physically gone to these lands, surely the curse would not have killed them all. But by passing through the\n\nportal of Hubris which Nemiisae had created, they doomed themselves and their kin. Other groups found the portals between the time Nemiisae realized what had happened and closed it off, but anyone who came through was doomed to suffer and die.\n\nThere was no hope for them as soon as they had passed through those portals into that world. But it is far enough removed that between the first settling of it and our time, no one has ever discovered it again. Beyond churning, whirling seas,\n\ndeadly islands, leagues and weeks away from the lands settled by the Four Brothers, it would be impossible to reach without the assistance of a very strong force indeed. But perhaps it is for the best, that these ruins remain ruins, and the skeletons\n\ngo undisturbed, lest we awaken old evils...", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic The Basics", "ventus2", "Magic The basics\n\nMagic is the art of using magical energies from the void and bringing them to life, forming them into what most people call spells or magic. Now this book shall state the very basics of magic. What the energy is and some other facts\n\n     Magical Energy\n\nMagical energy or in other words “Mana” is what mages use to perform their spells, How mana is found is through the void, the void is the realm that supports all mana inside, There is a everlasting amount of mana inside the void,\n\n         The Void\n\nThe void is everything and nothing at the same time, An everlasting is inside the void and is where mages connect to perform their spells, Connecting to the void is a process that is easy in a sense but at the –\n\nSame time extremely dangerous, and the reason for this is being that the mana inside the void is what we call stamina, or in other words life energy, The main way of connecting to the void is through one’s mind, And how to do this? One must find out for-\n\nThemselves, Also considering that mana is life energy there may or not be a way for a mage to use this in order to grant themselves eternal life, But I leave that to you as well as how to perform spells and use mana.\n\n-Corvo", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: The Void", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nDangers of the Void:\nThis lesson is the most vital for a Dedicant to understand. Void magic, ALL Void magic, is pure imbalance. If an attuned Druid casts Void magic of any sort, even a very simple spell, it damages their connection to the Aspects\n\nand their communion to nature. The Druid that attuned them will also feel when this occurs through the link they formed upon attuning the Dedicant, and Archdruids feel the Void casting as well and can sense the taint of it upon a Druid.\n\nIt is vitally important you explain this to every Dedicant so they understand the consequences of their actions and the damage they will do to their attunement. Furthermore, casting Void magic is grounds for immediate reprimand by the Order,\n\nand further offenses will lead to unattunement and removal from the order.  Void magic is a subject it pays to be knowledgeable about, ignorance can get you killed, but a Druid must never seek to use such\n\nunnatural and imbalancing magic. ((if you are a Druid and you use Void Magic of any sort, you MUST OOCly inform at least the Guide that attuned you and an Archdruid, how you approach telling them, or not, in RP is up to you.\n\nFailure to OOC inform is considered power gaming and if it is learned you have done this, you may have your attunement shattered without the chance to explain your actions. POWERGAMING IS NEVER OKAY!!!))", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Fairy Ring", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nFairy Ring Meditation:\nThis is an important lesson, and you should encourage the Dedicant to return to fairy rings on their own from time to time, even after their attunement. For this lesson, you should explain what they will experience\n\nonce they enter the ring. Once they understand, have them sit within the ring and give them the time they need to become used to the sensation, answer any questions they have. Then, have them meditate,\n\nhelp them find peace and balance, and let them meditate until either you feel they have succeeded, or the strain of the communion is causing them undue stress. Reinforce the experience with questions\n\nabout what they felt, what they saw, and if they have any questions themselves.", ""),
        StaticBook("R.Plants Vol. I", "§bAmfionas", "Rare Plants and their Properties\n------------------\nby Larky\n\nThere are numerous peculiar plants and vegitation that can be found in any realm.\n \nThis is but a small effort to document their properties.\n\n1.SilverLine\nThis plant is named silverline due to its unique silver lines that mark its leaves.\n\nIts height is equal to that of the tall grass and it usually grows in cold climates where its covered in snow.\n\nThe most remarkable\n\nthink regarding this plant is that when lit on fire it emits a silver light. The fire with this color (silverfire) can retain this state for a couple of minutes to a few hours depending on the number of leaves used. \n\nThe fire created despite its differe-\n\n-nce in colour, has no other peculiar properties.\n\nTemperature and size remain relatively the same.\n\nIf the leaves are left to dry under the hot sun, one will observe that they have longer effects.\n\n2.Dablaora\nThis plant is easily distinguisable due to its vivid orange colour. It grows mostly in the deserts.\n\nShould the dark red fruit it forms be consumed one would be able to mimic perfectly the sound of a squirel.\n\nThe reason the dabblefruit causes that is unknown. It is also unknown why the person still retains its ability to speak properly.\n\n3.Velteleafy\nVelteleafy is a mostly normal plant. What distinguishes from other is its fruit.\n\nThe plant forms fruits the size of a small melon.\n\nThe fruit is coloured purple with blue dots and is quite nutritious and filling.\n\nThe problem is that the saliva of the user becomes quite thick and sticky.\n\nHe soon begins to form large violet and blue bubbles that fly off whenever he tries to speak or breath with his mouth open.\n\nThe veltefruit does not appear to have any long term impacts on the health of an individual that consumes it.\n\nIt is also quite entertaining.\n\n4.Treledelti\nThis plant is distinguishable by its pale yellow leaves with red sybols that resemble flames.\n\nIt does not grow in a particular region set aside deserts and\n\ntundras. \n\nIt does not create any fruits and when its leaves are consumed the user is overwhelmed by a sense of hunger.\n\nHe is able to consume twice as much food than the normal ratio and the effect wares\n\noff only after an hour. \n\nOnly to be eaten at a party where there is an abundance of food and beverages.\n\nWritten by Larky at the 16th of Malin's Welcome, 1451\n\nVaerhaven", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragos", "§bkido122", "On Dragons\nThere Life and Death\n\n      By Sam King\n\n     Chapter 1: Birth\n\n Dragons are, known by most everyone, born by egg much like our domesticated and less dangerous, Chicken. Ounce the egg is laid it goes on a one month incubation period. The mother dragon will warm her eggs with her belly,\n\nlaying next to to it, gently mumuring away, like a loud rumbling purr, as she increases her internal heat. She would do this for hours at a time for about a month, until the time the eggs hatch, at which point the egg now begins its life as a hatchling.\n\n Chapter 2: Hatchling\n \n After the egg hatch's, the hatchling will, if all goes well, stand on its four legs, strecthing its wings for the first time. It is important to note that dragons are not yet able to fly at this young age, and won't be able to for\n\nquite some time. Dragons at this age are around the size of a wolf, and are thought to be relativly tame and kind, much like a puppy. For its first week a hatchling will wander around its nesting site, never traveling out of eye sight of its mother.\n\nIt is during the second week of a hatchlings life that is left alone, as the mother goes to hunt to provide both her and her hatchlings hunger. The Hatchling is then left to its own accord, and begins to hunt small rodents and animals. The Third month is\n\nwhen the hatchling is now able to hunt on its own, under normal circumstances, and is when the fires within begin to bubble up, though not able to breath its deadly fire, it is good to note, smoke can be seen from their nostrils and mouth. When the\n\nhatchling reaches a year of age, is when it is left alone and now considered a Drake, or \"Teenager\".\n\n\n\n  Chapter 3: Drake\n(Next Page)\n\nDrake are still unable to use its deadly fire, but its bow a fierce and dangerous hunter, around the size of horse and rather grumpy. This age is often considered to be their \"Awkward\" phase in their life., as they are prone to explore great distances for\n\nno appairent reason, which is why they where said to be the most commonly sighted age of a Dragon. They have also been said to have caused the most havoc, as they are for some reason, really agressive and proned to attack anyone who got to near to them.\n\n  Chapter 4: Adult\n\n Little is know about adult dragons, as they were rarely ever said to be sighted. What is known how ever is at this stage is whena dragon is now able to, 1-Breath Fire, 2-Fly, and 3-Mate. Adult dragons are thought to be rather\n\nunagressive, except for a few circumstance which I will get to soon, as they have been rarley sighted and don't attack often, if at all. Noe the mating rituals of dragons is, ofcourse, unknown, mostly likely lost in time. What is known is this, they\n\nbecome very agressive and is one of the few times they are said to be. During their mating season, time is also unkonw, is when they are said to attack towns, as when a Adult has its nesting site picked, nothing will stop it from nesting their, even if it\n\nis already occupied. It is also worthy to note that the legend and myth that dragons have a affinity to treasures, is neither proven or disproven, though most likely false. As to why and what purpose a dragon would horde treasure is unknown, except to\n\npossibly attract potential mates.\n\n\n\nChapter 5: Wyrm's\n\n Almost nothing is known about Wyrms, other then they are some of the oldesy and anciet dragons to ever \"Exist\". When an adult\n\nbecomes a wyrm is unknown, what is know though is that they are to be feared, extremly feared.\n\nChapter 6: Death\n\n Natural deaths hav enever been know or spoken of for dragons. The only few deaths of dragons\n\nspoken of is caused by few curagous knights/wizards, even then this legends and stories have no real reason to be thought of as fact in nearly all occasions.\n\n   Authors Note:\n \n This entire book is put together by a few years of researhc into myths and lengend s of these grand beast. Nothing written in this book is inherently fact, and should not be treated as such. This is just the most reasonable\n\npossibility's concerning \"Dragons\" few, if not no, facts on these beast exist. \n\nDedication is to all who enjoy the mysterious and unknown in the, as well as to those who enjoy our history, though this it not, per say \"History\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Wish", "§bLorn Aldilia", "Lorn's Wish\n    I wish to become the greatest Blacksmith. I want to out do the greatest of the great. Tis a lot to ask for but maybe one day\n\n Signed, \n     Lorn Aldilia", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wish", "§bKeovan Scarfen", "-------=[]=-------\n A Wish ay..\nTo be able to find a way to help friends in need for soo.. im not one fighter... A wish for a possible recipe of a potion, a teacher or medical.. anything that will help my friends stay alive\n~Keovan Scarfen\n((nanoninja23", ""),
