 their dooms by it.\n\nAs soon as Zanunder, Nemiisae and their children stepped through the portal, they realized it had slammed shut behind them; They could no longer return to the land they came from. At first, this was not a problem to them. They were confident\n\nthis land would be their Paradise, the savior of their children. But their children had spent decades cut off from the light of sun, while living and thriving within the Verge. They set out immediately for the thickest forest they could find, in hopes\n\nof slowly acclimating their children to the light. But this was not to be. This land was rife with dangers, of all shapes and sizes, lurking behind corners, within the trees, in the skies, the oceans, the rivers…There was no escaping it. The very least\n\nof these dangers were the skittering, venomous spiders of the caverns. Their children began dying off, one by one, then two by two, then five by five, then by the droves. Finally, Nemiisae chose the least of the threats of this world and blessed her\n\nchildren with that creature’s aspects. Her children became a mix of her blood, Zanunder’s, and that of the spiders that lurked the caverns. They migrated into these same caverns, living amongst and as the Spiders did, save from the beasts and terrors\n\nlurking on the surface. Vicious, cruel, the children shifted and changed into horrible beasts, preying and feeding upon one another.\nNemiisae knew she had to bless them in this way so that they may survive, yet still she grieved for their corruption.\n\nAs well, no matter how hard they tried, Nemiisae and Zanunder could no longer procreate. Horrified, they began to believe it had been a trap all along. A trick by God to punish them for acting out, perhaps?! Or was it just for His own amusement?!\n\nZanunder refused. They argued at length, until finally he threatened to take the children and go elsewhere. He firmly believed if they traveled far enough they could survive, thrive, beat God and the Curse. Frustrated and exhausted,\n\nNemiisae knew she had to stop him somehow, or their children would all perish. She remembered the blessing she had given her children and as Zanunder turned to leave, she changed her form to that of a giant Spider. She put him to sleep with her\n\nNemiisae knew she had to stop him somehow, or their children would all perish. She remembered the blessing she had given her children and as Zanunder turned to leave, she changed her form to that of a giant Spider. She put him to sleep with her\n\nvenom and wrapped him within a cocoon. Then, she bade the eldest and closest of her Daughters to watch over the others, before retreating into the deep with Zanunder, to try and find a way to force open the portal and escape this horrid place.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed, 1473.\nTo be continued in the second volume.\n[Credit to TehLulu for the writing itself.]", ""),
        StaticBook("The Navy of Oren", "SpamShok", "ORNE NAVY SHIPS:\n1st: Medium Cruiser\n-5 Ballista slots per side, second deck. All empty, ship unarmed.\n-58 meters long\n-Two masted ship\n-4 prison cells, no doors.\n\n2nd Ship: Small Cruiser\n-Two ballistas on deck, forward part.\n-Two small masts.\n-30 meter long ship\n-Strange, light weaponry under deck.\n\nN.B: Ship is barely a threat\n\nhttp://goo.gl/a8mhi\n\n3rd ship: War Galleon\n-74 meters long\n-4 Forward deck top ballistae\n-Officers: \n*Kais Ishikawa\n*Lancel (Hightower?)\n*Uthor (Silverblade?)\n-Privy council meeting room on board.\n-4 masts. 2 mid-deck main ones.\n-Large crew areas\n\n4th ship: Small Cruiser\n-No weaponry\n-3 small masts.\n\n*More intel unavailiable, unable to enter ship.*\n\n5th Ship: Small Interceptor \n-Black sails (???)\n-Two small masts\n-No weaponry\n-Small crew capacity", ""),
        StaticBook("Raserei's Ballad", "§bHagan \"Weird Eyes\" Raserei", "In the merry Autumn’s Cold, From me home I started,\nLeft the house of home, Nearly broken hearted,\nSaluted knowledge dear, Grabbed me darlin' notebook,\nDrank a pint of beer, Me grief and tears to smother,\n\nThen off to reap the scorn, Leave where I was born,\nGet a stack paper, To banish bounty hunters,\nA brand new pair of brogues, rattlin' o'er the bogs,\nFrightenin' all the dogs, On the mountain path to Malin’\n\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nIn Lenniel that night, I rested limbs so weary,\n\nStarted by daylight, Me spirits bright and airy,\nTook a drop of the pure, Keep me heart from sinkin',\nThat's the Weird Eyes cure, Whenever he's on for drinking.\nTo see the lassies smile, Laughing all the while,\n\nAt my curious style, 'Twould set your heart a-bubblin'.\nAnd asked if I was hired, Wages I required,\nTill I was nearly tired, Of the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\n\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nIn Malinor arrived, I thought it such a pity,\nTo be so soon deprived, A view of that fine city.\n\nWell then I took a stroll, All among the quality,\nBundle it was stole, All in the neat locality;\nSomething crossed my mind - When I looked behind,\nNo bundle could I find, Upon me stick a wobblin'.\n\nEnquirin' for the rogue, Said me small town brogue,\nWasn't much in vogue, On the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\n\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nFrom there I got away, me spirits never failin'\nLanded on the stead, Just as the elf was watchin';\nThe darky at me roared, Said that minas had me,\n\nWhen I grabbed about, A sentence found for Weird Eyes,\nIt was with the dame, played some sadist games,\nDanced some hearty jigs, The water round me bubblin',\nWhen off the job, Wished meself was dead,\n\nOr better far instead, On the mountain path to Malin’.\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra~.\n\nThe knights of Mistress here, When we safely landed,\nCalled meself a fool; I could no longer stand it;\nBlood began to boil, Temper I was losin',\nPoor old Stenar card’nal, They began abusin',\n\n\"Hurrah my soul,\" says I, My limbs that I let fly;\nWolfy boys were nigh, An' saw I was a hobblin,\nWith a loud hurray, They joined in the affray.\nWe quickly cleared the way, For the mountain path to Malin’.\n\nOne, two, three, four five,\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nGrab the miss and help her\nDown the mountain path\n\nAll the way to Malin’,\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra.\nWhack-fol-lul-lee-ra~.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poe Grace - Wish", "§bPoe Grace", "I wish of this well, for my body to never age.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scary Stories", "§bJasper", "A Compilation of Scary Short Stories\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       By: Jasper\n\n1~\nMy daughter won’t stop crying and screaming in the middle of the night. I visit her grave and ask her to stop, but it doesn’t help.\n\n2~\nI was having a pleasant dream when what sounded like hammering woke me. After that, I could barely hear the muffled sound of dirt covering the coffin over my own screams.\n\n3~\nThe longer I wore it the more it grew on me. She had such pretty skin.\n\n4~\nI can’t move, breathe, speak or hear and it’s so dark all the time. If I knew it would be this lonely, I would have been cremated instead.\n\n5~\nI put my hand on the wall to guide my way in the dark. Then I felt a heartbeat.\n\n6~\nMy wife woke me up last night to tell me there was an intruder in our house. She was murdered by an intruder 2 years ago.\n\n7~\nShe asked why I was breathing so heavily. I wasn’t.\n\n8~\nI begin tucking her into bed and she tells me, “Daddy check for monsters under my bed.” I look underneath for her amusement and see her, another her, under the bed, staring back at me quivering and whispering, “Daddy there’s somebody on my bed.”\n\n9~\n\"I can't sleep\" she whispered, crawling into bed with me. I woke up cold, clutching the dress she was buried in.\n\n10~\nThe grinning face stared at me from the darkness beyond my bedroom window. I live on the 13th floor.", ""),
        StaticBook("~+~Squid~+~", "§bTadmonster", "~+~On the Use of Squids~+~\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSir Rokkur\n\n1. A Basic Background\n2.A History\n3.Utilitarian Purposes\n4.On uses in War\n5.Taming the Squids\n\n      A Basic Background\nThe squid is one of the most tenacious creatures, capable of brute amounts of force and speed. It has long, strong tentacles with sharp suckers capable of puncturing and holding on to solid iron. The larger the squid, the larger\n\nthe tentacles, and the larger the object that can be grabbed by said squid. The squid is capable fo grabbing objects, and manipulating them with their strong dexterous tentacles. They have the capability to open a jar, and a large Nordic Squid can open a\n\nman's skull. The only more horrifyign thing than the barbed tentacles is the horrifying maw. Armed with a beak strong enough to clip iron into bits, the largest of the Nordic Grand Squids have been recorded biting the mast of a ship in half. This beak is\n\nhard, and usually black. The The squid has two large eyes, about 5x the relative size of the eyes of a human.  These eyes are capable of seeing in both the dark, and the water, and reflect light while fully open. Squids do not blink, and their eyes are\n\nusually pure black. These monsters are incredibly dangerous, and attack with vicious speed. The most remarkable point is the team work of several squids. They attack like a wolf pack, one by one weakening the enemy. A story tells of a group of smal squids\n\nthat were able to eat an entire ship that was about 100x their size. The team work of these squids is exceptional, and is very dangerous. \n\nOverall, squids are extremely dangerous, and shoudl be avoided at all costs.\n\n2. A Brief History\n\nThe Basic Squid was common across nearly all ocean areas, and would remain this way. However, in the Nordic seas, ice caps would  freeze over, sending squids further down. This would result in a process called deep-sea gigantism, which\n\nwould soon create squids of incredible size. They would remain low in the ocean, trapped underneath ice caps, until the warm winters that would stay for several years. Large, 15 foot squids would soon appear along Northern shrores, but were utilized by\n\ntribesmen for food. However, largerm squids would be found, and ships would be lost quickly. Within a decade, the first Nordic Giant Squid, a 50 foot monster, would be discovered. The ships sent to kill it returned victoriously, but in ruins. Several of\n\nNorse families fled south, leaving few to defend. In an attempt to end the problem, they sailed north, into the heart of the swarm. About 10 miles out, they encountered Nordic Grand Squids, about 100 feet long. About 5 miles out, they encountered Nordic\n\nMass Squids, about 200 feet in length. At he center of the swarn, fighting past tons of squids, and with a ship remaaining, four sailors would find a Kraken, a squid over 300 feet long. There were seven of these Krakens, as recorded in the log found\n\nfloating in the following months. These men would not survive.\n\nEventually, the norsemen fled south, and intermingled with human culture at a higher level. However, smaller squids would follow, making the common species found everywhere.\n\nNo records of Krakens further south than the far North oceans has been recorded. The largest squid in southern areas as of yet is only 22 feet long.\n\nFor now.\n\n3.Utilitarian Purposes\n\nThese squids can be used for a variety of things. The Nordic tribes orignally used them to haul small ships, and they carry powerful ink sacs. Their large beaks are good for removing barnacles if used, and\n\nmany of these squids can be used for food or research. They are large, and smaller breeds have been harnessed for aquatic transportation.\n\n4.Use in War\n\nThe smaller breeds of the squids, can in fact be used for aquatic transport. They can pull boats, increasing speed and mobility.\n\nBy utilizing their massiv maw, attackers can use them to bite holes on ships, sinking them easily.\n\nThe larger squids have the potential to be used to full fights, using their powerful tentacles and jaws to break warships. The largest recorded tamed squid was a measley 19.5 feet long. However, the possibility to tame a Kraken is very possible. That will\n\ncovered in the next section. If tamed, the Kraken can be used to easily sink even the largest of warships, and woudl be crushing to any Naval force. \n\nThe tactic best used is an underbelly attack. By driving the Krakens under the boats, then having them\n\ncome up from underneath may be the most successful tactic. They would be too hard to hit, and would be able to use the large tentacles and the maw to finish off the boat.\n\n5.Taming the Squid\n\nThe squid is quite easy to tame. By providing a large amount of fish, safety, and shelter, the squid will be quite easily tamed. However, to make the squid follow commands, the squid woudl require the consumption of a golden apple, as\n\nsquids have an affinity to shiny materials.\n\nA Kraken would require about one whale a day. It would also require an enormous lake, and complete safety for it to not maul any near it. To match its appetite for riches, several solid gold blocks are needed.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Challenge", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Challenge\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nAn Archdruid cannot be removed from position by a vote or by force. Only if he retires or dies may his position be claimed as empty. However, when an Archdruid becomes exceedingly inactive or loses sight in what's right for the Orderand refuses to retire,\n\nhis position may be challenged. The Challenge is and only ever should be issued in the most extreme and rare of cases.\n\nWhen all hope is lost and the Order is suffering because of an Archdruid, the Challenge may be instituted and may\n\nonly be instituted by a Druid Hierophant. The Hierophant who issues the Challenge shall create a difficult, and unbiased, trial that requires the challengers and the challenged to put many skills to the test such as exploration, investigation, wisdom, and\n\npiety. Furthermore, the existing Archdruids must all agree to the terms of the Challenge. This event could take anywhere from a few Seeds to a Year, and whoever returns to the Hierophant, first, with the required information, items, or knowledge will be\n\ndeemed the victor and shall take the seat of the challenged Archdruid.\n\nIf anyone is realized to have cheated or wronged the Challenge in some way, they will be disqualified. In the case that only two individuals, a challenger and the\n\nchallenged, take part in this vigorous trial and one cheats or wrongs it in some way, the other will be granted the victor even if he is the individual being challenged.\n\nAs aforementioned, the Challenge shall only ever happen as a\n\nlast resort. The Inner Circle, all except for the Archdruid being challenged, must deem it necessary as must a Hierophant to organize and oversee it. This rite should never and cannot be abused.  Those who try to see to its usage in improper context shall\n\nfeel not only the wrath of the Aspects, but that of the Order as well. Blessed be he who takes any and all proper precautions with a troubled Archdruid before seeing the institution of a Challenge.", ""),
        StaticBook("Meat Cuts", "§bJistuma", "Beef cuts:\n\nChunk (lower Neck)- Chuck Beef is located in the lower neck region of the animal. It is by far the best cut to be used in a stew or to be ground due  to its large amount of connective tissue\n\nBeef Rib (Ribs) – The Beef rib is part of the rib cage of the animal. It contains prime cuts such as the prime rib, as well as rib-eye. So far the best cooking methods I have found are cooking it on a grill or in an oven because of its tender nature.\n\nBrisket (lower front, underneath Chunk) – Brisket is another tough cut of beed, it is located directly under Chuck. It is best prepared as a pot roast, or covered in spices and smoked.\n\nPlate (Short Ribs) –The Plate is the part where both Short Ribs and Skirt Steak are made. Usually good for braising, they are also great if marinated and grilled. This cut also contains a lot of cartilage and care needs to be made cutting it.\n\nShank (Legs) – Shanks derive from the upper left portion of the animal. It is tough and not very edible unless braised and slow cooked.\n\nShort Loin (behind the Ribs)  – The Short Loin is a piece that is usually cut into steaks. It contains the Porterhouse, Tenderloin, and Strip Steak. All of them seem to be really tender and are derived from the rear part of the ribs.\n\nFlank (Utter Area)  – Flank is usually marinated before cooking and its preparation usually includes marinating and careful cooking. This cut is found near the utter and usually best when ground.\n\nRound (Rear end)  – Round is usually a tougher, but leaner piece of meat. It is best using moist heating methods such as stewing or pot roast. This part of the animal is where cubed meat traditionally derives from.\n\n\n\nPork Cuts\n\nPork Butt (shoulder)  – Despite the /unfortunate/ name, the Pork Butt is actually the upper shoulder. Although it is great for braising, it can also be made into sausages. Right above this is a fatty layer great for making lard.\n\nShoulder (Above the legs)  – The Shoulder is a pretty self explanatory name. This is another tough cut of meat however I find it good in making sausages as well. However it is usually cured or smoked.\n\nPork Loin (Ribcage)  – This part of the pig is mostly ribcage. It can be cut into Tenderloin located in the back and the whole Loin can be roasted or chopped into individual pieces. Like the Butt the Loin also has a fatty layer above for making lard.\n\nHam (actual Butt)  – The Ham is the part of the pig which is a deceptive name. This cut comes from the back of the pig and is saved for salted meats, and smoked ham. In addition the bottom portion, the Ham hock can be braised as opposed to curing.\n\nSide (Bottom)  – The side of a pig is where many can enjoy the simple breakfast treat of bacon. As well this part can be cut into steaks o made into pancetta, this is by far one of the tastiest parts of a pig and it takes much effort to avoid eating.\n\nSpare Rib (Under the Loin)  – The Spare rib is located where the breast connects to the ribs, it can be prepared by braising, slow cooking, or even grilling.\n\nJowl (Head)  – The Jowl is mostly used for sausages, as with any area this part is located. However it is not uncommon to see this part cured. Although not common it has been done.\n\nMeat Cuts\n\nUnknown author\nCoppied by Rosso\nCloud Temple of Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "§bAnonymous", "Fear the Old Dark as Ryder did.\n\nThis is only the beginning.\n\nThere shall be no end.\n\nGod is with us.", ""),
        StaticBook("Foul Play", "§bHileia'elr", "-----Foul Play-----\n\nWritten by Hileia'elr\n\nCan a simple man overcome his feelings for the most lovely creature he's ever met; Or will he have to express his true feelings?\n\nIt was a day like any other in the Caliphate. The sun was shining, there were few clouds to be seen, and there were plenty of travelers coming to Al- Wakhrah looking to make some coin, or buy some supplies.\n\nIn fact, for Larrion, it was the perfect day to run a shop. His store was flooded with customers, wanting to buy some goods from the man. Larrion would shout out, pleading with the sea of people in his tiny shop to make a single-file line.\n\nAfter about an hour of the alchemist selling to the large amount of travelers in his shop, a man in a red hat approached the counter. It was his friend, Keltran. \"Aye, Larrion, how you doing?\" Larrion simply groaned, wiping off the counter.\n\n\"What do you want?\" Larrion said with a neutral tone.\n\n\"Well...\" Beltran began, \"I felt somewhat sorry about what I did to you a while ago...\"\n\n\"Wait.\" Larrion started. \"What did you do now?\"\n\n\"Oh! S-So you don't know?!\" Keltran exclaimed.\n\n\"You fool... The hell did you do now?\"\n\n\"U-Uhm... Why don't you go for a nice walk while I watch your store?!?\" Keltran nervously stated.\n\nLarrion gave him a dead look. \"This isn't over... Here are the keys.\"\n\nAs Keltran watched the store, Larrion walked out of his shop, turning to the left to see the lines of small stores set up.\n\nHe walked pass the fountain, and made a sharp turn into his friend's store.\n\nAs he opened the doors to the small shop, he noticed a person behind the counter, sorting some books.\n\nIt was none other than Netiley the Vixen. She was sorting her collection of magic books, guides, and novels for sale.\n\n\"Ooh, hello, Larrion!\" she said. \"Have you come for your royalties today?\"\n\n\"Er, yes...\" Larrion replied. \"How many of my books have you sold?\"\n\nNetiley plopped a brown sack on the counter. \"See for yourself.\" she said.\n\nAs Larrion opened the pouch, about 85 minas shimmered with a sparkling flare. Larrion then dipped his nose inside the bag and took in a deep breath.\n\n\"Aah, minas...\"\n\n\"Thank you, Netily.\" Larrion said, as he placed the pouch into his bag. \"Yuuup! No problem.\" Netiley replied.\n\nAs Larrion was just about to leave, he noticed yet another figure over the counter...\n\nIt was a chicken. A small, white, chicken, sitting behind Netily on it's lap.\n\nLarrion stared for quite some time. \"Who is that?\"\n\nNetily pointed. \"Aye, that would be Hegory.\"\n\nLarrion stared at the bird for moments, when he finally asked, \"Can we go upstairs? I want to introduce myself to your friend.\"\n\nNetiley shrugged, and opened the door to the upstairs area for him and Hegory.\"\n\nAs Larrion and Hegory sat down at a table for two, they stared eachother in the center of their eyes for quite some time. It was only a minute or so, but to Larrion, it felt like hours.\n\nLarrion broke the iceberg.\n\n\"So... what is it you do in the shop?\"\n\nThe chicken made a clucking noise.\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nLarrion placed his elbows on the table, and rolled his eyes.\n\n\"Do you have any hobbies?\"\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nFamily?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nJob?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nAt this point, Larrion decided to talk about himself.\n\n\"Well, I am especially interested in alchemy. Aside from that, I run a small store.\"\n\n\"Cluck. Cluck cluck, cluck-- Cluck cluck cluck, cluck CLUCK!\"\n\nAt this point, Larrion was blushing. Never before had anyone shown such compassion, such sympathy, and such care for what Larrion went through everyday. He finally found someone who would listen to him.\n\nLarrion removed the goggles that rested on his eyes, and held Hegory's left wing in between his own two. Larrion bent down to kiss the top of his love interest's wing, and smiled. Hegory couldn't smile, but instead looked to the ceiling.\n\nThe very next day, no one could seem to find Hegory or Larrion. Any sign of the two ever being there in the first place had vanished. As everyone searched for them, little did they know that the two were already at the docks, planning their new lives.\n\nThe two decided to live out at sea on a house boat. For the next 15 years, the two lovers would survive off of fish and fried eggs. They met few people during their time at sea, and that's just how they liked it...\n\n\n-The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Sky Kingdom", "§bPrishe Mantisuku", "Journal entry 1:\n\nI found what it seems to be some floating land no way of support to keep these lands from staying up.  It seems to be a fallen kingdom. South west of Athera", ""),
        StaticBook("A simple wish.", "§bAdil", "What would I, Adil 'the Eagle Eyed' of Hallowvale Contracting wish for? Well. I'd wish for a new eye to replace my missing one, but I'm afraid thats long gone. I wish for the courage to fight against the monsters which torment me, the courage to fight\n\nagainst the creatures of darkness like Trolls, Wendigos, and the evil that looms over Ard Ghorrock! If those two can't be accomplished, a good supply of uh.. Quartz Dust, the snorting kind, or Shimmering RedSand, the snorting kind too, will do.\n\nSigned, Adil 'the Eagle Eyed', Vander of Hallowvale Contracting, Council to the Vandalore.", ""),
        StaticBook("The End of Hope", "§bXanivic", "The End of Hope\n             Xanivic\n\nIt struck us... struck us like a bolt of lightning. None of the folk in Aegis knew what had happened. With the Undeads proceeding from the northern lands, the inhabitants of Aegis had no escape. Nowhere to run. Nowhere to hide.\n\n The womens' screams, the childrens' cries... The darkened sky casted over the land, somber. Griefing in agony and hopelessness.  After a few days of the sudden destruction near Oren, silence conquered. Aegis didn't speak a single word.\n\nThe atmosphere was silent to the point where the only thing heard was the thoughts of a wanderer. He stood around 5'6. Bearded with leather rings choking the ends of his beard. He wore light brownish and beige armor.\n\n His face... his face had a distinctive scar that slithered diagnally from the left side to the right side of his beaten face. His right eye was a light green color. The color of the algae filled seas.\n\nAs he walked the road to the Cloud Temple from Kalurugan, his thoughts were flooded with horror. A single tear streaked down his cheek as he whispered  a forgein language, \"Aley bastia.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Crossing Poems", "§bDurandal Mefiez", "II\n II\n  III\n    IIII               I\n       IIII           II\n          III Poetry\n             IIIIIII\n                II III\n               II    III\n             II        II\n            I           I\n           I\n           I\n\nCan I call you yard to yet.\n\nAnd believe you too can fly.\n\nSadness of a humming bird's bet.\n\nIs that you both know why.\n\nLeast I not hate nor love too much.\n\nIf their meanings finds me lost.\n\nWhen as an evening showed me how.\n\nA sunset told me soft.\n\nMy love of you is a painful truth.\n\nAnd these are it's worst occasions.\n\nFor I could only give you everything.\n\nBut I can never give you persuasions.\n\nThis with bravery and secrecy wrote.\n\nAnd delivered in urgent times.\n\nDear friend please read then burn this note.\n\nMy memory has outlawed rhymes.\n\nThe meadow dreams of shadows.\n\nAnd a young bird dreams of air.\n\nWhere I am warmed by dreams of you.\n\nSnow in The First Seed holds my stare.\n\nI was standing where men must stand.\n\nAmong sunsets for those who stood.\n\nwWhile there I held one grain of sand.\n\nAnd heard you've done good.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nShort collection of poetry by:\n I)urandal Mefiez", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Moot\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nThe Moot is an assembly held for all Druids of a particular Circle to come together for discussion, debate, and decision making. It is a time to worship the Aspects, to make notice of the events of the world, to commit to projects, and much more.\n\nMany times a Moot might serve the sole purpose of voting for a new Archdruid or Druid Guide or to cast votes on shunning a particular individual who has wronged a Druid, Druids, or the Order. Seldomly, a Moot might be held to throw a party, host a\n\nwedding, or perform a funeral.\n\nOnly by the word of an Archdruid may a Moot be called. Druids, Dedicants, Druid Guides, and Hierophants all can, and should, present information of importance to the Archdruids, and anyone can request\n\na Moot be called. However, it is up to an Archdruid to decide if and when a Moot shall be held and for what topics it shall be held to discuss. Only shall the Inner Circle, the Archdruids and Druid Guides, make a definite decision, based on a vote count,\n\nfor the Order. No other Druids or Hierophants are permitted to make decisions for the Order, but their opinions and advice are taken seriously and with much consideration. When serving as a meeting, a Moot is held in the Moot Room of the\n\nhosting Grove. While a Moot is in session, often times the Archdruid who called it will take the floor to present topics. Out of respect, all who wish to speak should wait for a pause or go-ahead. Druids should request or stand to take the floor or\n\npresent a topic. Dedicants aren’t permitted to attend Moots, but accepts are often made. In the case that a Dedicant is permitted at a Moot, he or she shall not speak unless asked to.\n\nThe Moot is an ancient tradition of Druidic culture. Sometimes\n\nnon-Druids are even invited to Moots, such as when relations are being discussed between the Order and a Nation or other group. A Moot is versatile, able to serve the purpose for many different occasions. It is one of the most formal, serious, and\n\nimportant aspects of Druidic culture. When in attendance of a Moot, remember to respect the speaker and follow proper etiquette. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Peasant & Queen", "§bKlaudia Crast Warnek", "-------------------\n\n\nA Peasant & A Queen\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\nWarneck\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\n-------------------\n\n-\n\nMy heart was heavy in my chest, it pounded like smith's hammer. I closed my eyes and took a deep breath. Looking around me, regal figures stood. \n\nAll looking at me dumbfounded, astonished of what I had done.\n\n-\n\nGuards gripped their swords tightly awaiting an order. I looked up at the throne, where she sat.\n\nShe looked at me without the condescending glare the others showed me.\n\n-\n\nI could barely breathe as I waited for her response. Idle gossip chatted quietly throughout the room. Lords and Ladies talking behind my back.\n\n\"Did he say what I think he said?\", \"He's just a peasant is he not?\"\n\n-\n\nI did not listen, I looked upon her face and waited. Sweat beaded down my brow.\n\nI had just proclaimed my love of the Queen before her. From the first time I had laid my eyes on her, I felt myself drain of all thought.\n\n-\n\nThe only thing that entered my mind in that moment was the mere sight of her beauty.\n\nI looked up at her again, she looked as if in deep thought. I stood once more and prepared myself.\n\n\"Your Highness,\"\n\n-\n\nI paused and took a breath. \"I urge you to speak, it may not be my place but I grow impatient and yearn for an answer. I have looked upon your beauty without word for what seems like a lifetime.\"\n\n-\n\nShe leaned back in her throne and listened. \"I know you have had many suitors, many a man try and take your hand. And although I may not be rich, or handsome or even worthy a second glance of your gentle gaze. I'm wealthy in one way.\"\n\n-\n\nShe seemed to be pleased by this, a faint smile crossed her face. \"I am wealthy in my love, I may not have crossed your mind but you have crossed mine time and time again. Your elegant visage, your eyes, deep as the ocean and -\n\n-\n\nas lucid as the sky. Your hair as brilliant as the nights sky, even your silhouette is enough to leave me stricken.\"\n\nI heard a snide cackle of those present. I turned to the crowd then,\n\n-\n\n\"And I implore anyone here, to tell of their love. Did you marry for power? For wealth? Or for love? In my humble honesty it is my belief that it comes once in a lifetime for someone to find their true love. Far be it of me to know of your lives -\n\n-\n\nbut judged on your halting laughs and disheartened faces I am not far off.\" \n\nI turned back to the Queen and returned to my knee. \n\n\"Now I beseech you mi'lady. What is your riposte?\"\n\n-\n\nMy heart stopped as time seemed to do the same. I stood before her, a peasant before a queen. \n\nShe stood from her throne and descended to my level, she now stood before me with a wide smile.\n\n-\n\nShe put her hand on my shoulder, \"My good man please stand.\" I lifted myself up, now I looked down on the queen. \n\n\"I cannot say I am not surprised by your actions, and I would say if I were any other -\n\n-\n\nI'd have you brought to the block. On the other hand am impressed, and flattered.\" With a smile on her face she moved forward and kissed my sweet lips.\n\n\"Is this a reasonable answer?\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Deep Depression", "§bKlaudia Crast", "-------------------\n\n\n\n\n The Deep Depression\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\n\n\n\n\n\nYou meant so much to all of us\nYou were special and that's no lie\nYou brightened up the darkest day\nAnd the cloudiest sky\n\n\n\nYour smile alone warmed hearts\nYour laugh was like music to hear\nI would give absolutely anything\nTo have you well and standing near\n\n\n\nNot a second passes\nWhen you're not on our minds\nYour love we will never forget\nThe hurt will ease in time\n\nMany tears I have seen and cried\nThey have all poured out like rain\nI know that you are happy now\nAnd no longer in any pain.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Ground Logic", "§bJeth", "From my research, I've come to the conclusion that Thunder or more commonly called Lighting, is a powerful flow of uncontrollable energy. It is formed in the sky and once \"Charged\" enough, will strike anywhere it finds a conduit. A conduit can be anything\n\nbut some materials like iron and copper, seem to be better at conducting the intensity. The sound of explosion (Lighting hitting the ground and setting it on fire) always come after the visual peeking of the lighting. In other words, energy travels faster\n\nthan sound itself. That may not seem a lot, but it is quite a lot. \n-------------------After thinking about it, for hours and hours... I've come to the conclusion that I can prevent fires caused by lightning by setting a powerful device that would attract\n\nthe lightning toward itself (instead of our houses) and would neutralise the energy itself. If you think that the energy is moving at a... let's say \"A\" speed and it's power would be rated by \"P\" and without Power, there wouldn't be any intensity (A) then\n\none cannot be without the other. \n-------------------No, no, no, no! Something's no right. Power and intensity can't be working if there isn't something to transport the energy. A material, something to resist it. A resistance... Yes!\n\nA resistance could be called... \"R\". Therefore we know that the Power equals the amount of intensity moving inside a resistance. Which means... P(v)=I(A)xR(rl). With this simple formula, I should be able to control it.\n\n*DRAWING OF A PROTOTYPE*\n\n(((  http://imgur.com/4tpakIu  )))\n\n\n\n\n\n\nP(v)=I(A)x R(rl)", ""),
        StaticBook("Ascended-Unveil", "§bGranantar Fournier Ateus", "Seeking the Ascended is a daunting task. It requires mental fortitude that rivals that of the hardest steel, tempered by the most fiery inferno.\n\nOn the contrary, what may be home to the Ascended, resides in a harsh wintery, frozen land.\n\nWith Spikes of Ice skewering the chilled air, blade-like glass that sever one's legs and lenghty spires that seem like broken bridges.\n\nAmongst the frosty wrath, is a floating fortress. Gently hovering in the air-less sky. Peerless, but forgotten.\n\nThis frosty land can be found just South of Kal'Agnar, the home of the Dwarves. Beyond the peaked frosty mountains and slightly west of a large lake. But beware, only the dwarves can withstand the chill of this frozen hell.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beard", "§bZahrer Irongrinder", "-==-(The Beard)-==-\n\n-Chapter 1\n  -Anatomy of Beards\n\n-Chapter 2\n  -Household Uses\n\n-Chapter 3\n  -Famous Beards\n\n-Chapter 4\n  -The Future...\n\n-==(Chapter One)==-\nAnatomy of Beards\n\n      The beard is an apendage grown from the lower portion of the face and, when well kept, they may grow to glorious lengths. Aside from being pleasing in appearance, the beard has many uses which\n\n,if used properly, may create a funstioning and useful beard.\n\n-==(Chapter Two)==-\nSome Household Uses\n\n      The beard may be pleasing to the eye, but it is also as functional and useful as and arm or leg. The beard itself may be used by one experienced with beards to hold all manner of objects\n\nranging from small trinkets to large battleaxes. Those who actively grow and manage their beards may use them to carry larger and larger items, especially if oone is of dwarven blood. One who keeps things in his beard may become better and better at\n\nholding larger and larger things but the inexperienced may enter into a dangerous situation as the beard that is not managed well may become a fatal hazard.\n\n-=(Chapter Three)=-\nFamous Beards of Time\n\n      The following list is comprised of the famous dwarves and even some non-dwarves who have grown their beards to such length and splendor so as to be called famous.\n\n-Yemekar, he who creates beards\n\n-Urguan, the first dwarf\n\n-Native the Elf\n\n\n--More to be added in the next edition...\n\n-==(Chapter Four)==-\nThe Future of The Beard\n\nIn the next edition, more chapters are planned to be added including but not limited to:\n  -Military Uses\n  -Uncommon Uses\n  -Proper Management\n  -Arcane Uses", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir's Wish", "§bNemir", "I wish to be so much of a skilled lumberjack that others would call my skill supercalifragilistic.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Acerbus cult", "§bToby Williams", "Current known information about the Acerbus's and their cult.\n\n-Follow the Aengul / Daemon Aerkiath\n\n-Wish destruction on Aeriel, Iblees, the Undead, and the Ascended.\n\n-Wish for the god Aerkiath to become the Arch-Aengul / Arch-Daemon\n\n-Have automatons that are capable of Arcane Magic, suggesting the possibility of bound Souls similar to Heial\n\n-The masks is the source of power and corruption, hijacking control of the soul and mind.\n\n-Have Prohpets similar to Hosper. Last known prophet was named Aazar. Condition unknown.\n\n-Almost excusively use electric magic, colored red due to their connection to Aerikath.\n\n-Are able to taint normal mortals, causing them to hear whispers that try and break them and bend them to Aerkiaths will\n\n-Have an insignia very similar to the Eye of Iblees.\n\n-Masks possess people, forcing themselves on their mind and souls, bending them to Aerkiaths will.\n\n-Masks can be destroyed by Holy Magic, Arcane Magic, and Physical trauma.\n\n-Individuals who were possessed but had their masked destroyed will often be on the brink of insanity.\n\n-Insanity can be reversed with a great deal of time.\n\n-Contact Toby Williams of the Ascended ((tnoy23)) if more questions are had than are answered here.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning", "§bArcane Mage", "The Mage Chronicles \nThe Beginning\nIn the beginning there was nothing, only the Void. But in the Void there was a light, or as close to what we call a light, which was the one God. In Void he crafted the world, our world; Ageis. But this is the\n\nancient lore and you know it well... Now we diverge from ancient lore, to something somewhat missed, skiped over if you will. That of MAGIC\n\nThe power that is known as magic, was brethed into the very fabric of the world at the same time as he breathed his existence into Man. It was entwined into the world, and could not exist segmented. So it came to pass with the barrier erected\n\nbetween the worlds of the living and dead, that the power of magic ceased to exist, in all but the few most powerful...\n\nBut is was not to last. The evil power of Iblees broke the power of the barrier, and the worlds of the living and dead once more entwined... With the failing of the barrier magic once more seeped through the world, and the inhabitants of Ageis\n\nonce more felt a tingle in their blood...\n\nSo it was that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other darkness...\n\n They could only hope that with this new found power the right decision would be made...", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to Nature", "§bPine Druid Gi'Garun", "An Ode to Nature\n    by The Pine Druid\n\nWe walk upon her soil,\nWe gaze upon her trees.\n\nWe're surrounded by all kinds of things, \nThat sprouted from her seeds.\n\nWhen one steps out of one's front door,\nOne will see her work.\n\nHer prowess great and beautiful,\nNo dark or evil mirk.\n\nWhat is it that I speak about?\n\nWhat is it that I praise?\n\nThe lands we roam,\nThe streams that foam.\n\nThe trees so tall,\nThe rain that falls.\n\nAll of these are of her make, for they are her and her alone. The make of two of love and great.\n\nThat be Nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beginning", "§bJack", "\"Of the four elements, air, earth, water, and fire\nman stole only one from the gods. Fire. And \nwith it, man forged his will upon the world.\" \n\nJared Blackfoot", ""),
        StaticBook("Leo wish!", "§bLeonardo Gloop", "*The handwriting would be extremely scruffy and quite a few words would be spelt wrong*\n\nI want a biyg dogie tfat wil be my frend. I want to be ayble to wride on him! And he wil help me and stuf. \n\nAllso i want new clofos! But 1 wish is beter! So dogie!\n\n((In case you couldn't understand, with the spelling and that he wants a big dog that he can ride on and it will help.  Then he's just saying he wants new clothes but the first one is the wish.))", ""),
        StaticBook("We come as crows", "§bUnknown", "------------------- -------------------   We come as crows\n-------------------\n \n\n      _IIII\n     --IIIII\n         IIIIII\n         IIIIIIIII\n          IIIIIIIIIIII=-\n             IIIII\n              _I.\n\nIt was a quiet night in the city of Kralta. The never-ending, calming trickle of the murky riverwater was one of the few sounds that were heard through the night. Occasional caws of the crows echoed through the muddy pathways and alleywas of the city, as\n\na single woman walked in the night. Slutinyova, the most beautiful woman in the city, though, she hadn't managed to find any work in the city yet. On her way towards the inn, she heard an odd sound in the night. She gazed upwards to the sign.. \"Smithery\"\n\nThe name was carved on the sign. A quiet, steady banging could be heard inside. Her curiosity took over, and she snuck inside in quiet steps. The planks creaked under her foot as she was fully inside, and she attracted the smith's attention. He had been\n\nhammering a sword all alone in the night.\nThe smith quickly put the unfinished sword away as he noticed Slutinyova, ashamed of his work. Slutinyova, however, didn't mind. In fact, she thought the sword looked mighty.\nSurely the sword had thrusted through\n\nmany challenges and stretched even more wounds. \n\n\"Make leave, customer, smithery am closed!\"\nThe smith said.\n\n\"Worry not, am here to help! Sword looked like needs many grinding and polish.\" She claimed.\n\nThe blacksmith allowed a sigh escape his lips as he presented the his sword to her. She gently took the sword in her hands, examining it with a curious eyes.\nThe blade was great in size, yet it had its faults, it was curved to the side slightly.\n\nSlutinyova held the sword for a bit, before starting to work on it.\n\n\"I'm sure I know what I'm doing.\" Slutinyova said, as she brought the sword to the grindstone. The blade began getting in better shape with each swipe against the\n\ngrindstone. It would soon be finished. The sword started to look like it was done. The smith seemed very happy of the outcome, though she wasn't completely done with the sword.\n\n\"Slutinyova must make polish of sword!\" She said enthusiastically.\n\nShe took the banner in the colours of Carrion in her hand, rolling it around her palm before she rested it against the mighty fine blade. The unladylike manner she polished it was astonishing, furiosly she swiped against the sword up and down. Across the\n\nblade, until finally it looked like it was ready.\n\n\"Am done.\" she said, when she finished and the blade was finally done and it gleamed with victory and glory.\nThe smith smiled, as the most tedious part of creating merchandise was made\n\nin his stead.\n\n\"Many thanks, woman.\"\nhe said, continuing;\n\"But now must make way to fix creak-plank on floor, da?\"\nThe smith said, as he rested his sword. He moved over to the plank Slutinyova had stepped on, that let out a nasty creak\n\nas she stepped over it. He took the hammer he had been using earlier, beginning to nail the plank back to its place. It was unheard of to bang this loud in the night of Kralta, yet the plank was soon as good as new. \"Now all am ready for business, make\n\nstay for assistance?\"\nThe smith said.\n\"Da, da, da!\" She nodded in reply hastily, happy to finally find work..\n\nand so they made many swords together for the glory of Raevir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Prince", "§bGrand Prince Zane Drakon", "~The Undead Prince~\n\nI have been kidnapped and flayed. The undead turned me into one of them, trying to brainwash me into believing in Iblees, but the power of Wyrvun was too powerful for them to damage my mental ability. I will join them in their\n\ntakeover of the whole world.\n\n-The next few pages are written in a different language not commonly known.-\n\nVamos a prevalecer con la ayuda de Wyrvun . Nadie puede soportar nuestra ira , nuestro poder se mostrará a todos que somos algo a tener en cuenta . \n\n*A drawing of a dragon is painted at the bottom of the page.*\n\nCon el poder de los dragones , y el poder de los dioses , vamos a retroceder a nuestros enemigos y destruir cualquier cosa que se interponga en nuestro camino .\n\nSiempre vamos a ganar , siempre vamos a prevalecer ! Somos la raza superior !", ""),
        StaticBook("Favors of Nature", "§bElk Druid Danic", "Favors of Nature\n            And You\n___________________ \n  As one of the more well known talents of a Druid, Control of Nature can be and is a supremely useful subtype to delve into, whether the Druid desires to use it defensively,\n\noffensively, or for utility.\n\n  Of course, with being fairly well known, it also is accompanied by misinformation and ignorance. One misunderstood belief of this skill is how it relates to the rest of the Druidic powers. Favors of Nature,\n\nlike all gifts, is stemmed from the Druidic gift of Communion, and cannot be progressed without further strengthening your natural tether to the Aspects and Nature. Another misrepresented fact of control of Nature is in its very name; Control,\n\nmanipulation. Althought to those not apart of the Druidic Order, it may seem like the Druid is controlling the plant or animal. This is simply not true, and once again is involved with Communion. From here on out, we will use the more accurate term:\n\nFavors of Nature.\n\n  To continue our journey on knowing what this gift is, we must first understand Communion. Communion is the inherent gift bestowed upon the Druid once attuned to the Aspects. It is the ethereal tether that connects the Druid to Nature,\n\nand Nature, Druid. At first, this link is incredibly weak, and requires a great deal of effort on the Druid's part to maintain. Over time, as the Druid serves the Aspects, the link grows stronger and deepens. This can be accelerated through a common\n\npractice in the Order; Meditation. Meditation involves clearing the Druids mind completely, and focusing only on the Natural world around them, allowing it to envelop them (Become one, is a used phrase). This practice strengthens the Druids connection far\n\nfaster than the passage of time. Once a Druid has maintained a strong connecton, they may speak to animals, trees, plants, and the very earth.\n\n  This is where Favors of Nature comes in. As I partly addressed above, Favors of Nature is anything but\n\ncontrolling, but instead requesting. A Druid does not will a vine to come to his or her aid, s/he requests it to, and depending on his/her connection to the Natural world (See: Communion), it may or may not comply. A Druid with a stronger and deeper\n\nconnection will have no issues asking a plant or animal to do something, and will get a positive and compliant response. A Druid with a weaker connetion, such as one who was just attuned, will find it far more difficult to get anything to agree to assist\n\nhim or her, even in the more dire situations. This can lead to some unsavory predicaments.\n\n  One other variable is the type of Natural entity you are requesting assistance from; A simple poppy flower may be more than willing to do a little danice, but a\n\nlittle dance, but a mighty and old oak tree may scoff and reject anything you request of it. A frog might be perfectly happy to ribbit its dawn song, but a large grizzly bear not so much. Thus, one must be aware of their abilities before attempting to\n\nrequest anything of Nature. There's nothing worse than feeling a surge of confidence, and even arrogance might I say, only to be horribly disappointed and even embarrassed when the Natural world says 'No'.\n\n  In the end, there is no true way of training\n\nyourself in the typical sense in this gift. The most skilled in this art are always those with the strongest tether to Nature. So if you desire to grow your skill in this practice, I do hope I've set you on the correct path, cleared up a few misconception\n\nof this brilliant and most useful art, and that with a continued serving of the Blessed Aspects, and meditation, your next encounter with whatever obstable you come across is faced with confidence that the Natural world has your back.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thalia", "§bBarry Winterleaf", "Dedicant: Thalia\nDate: 04/09/2015\nGuide: Barry\n\nTask: Grow a tree\n\nNurture a tree to full health over the span of a few elven days", ""),
        StaticBook("Nobility.", "§bNapoleon Fournier d'Avenese", "NOBLE CUSTOMS AND A GREATER STATE\n_____________________________By Napoleon Fournier d'Avenese\n_____________________________Squire To His Lordship of Aldersburg\n_____________________________Hello, sires, of this nation. Clergy, gentry, nobility, and all\n\nothers interested. This book is to explain the concept of Fuedalism, and lay out edicts for the perfect fuedal monarchy. It is also to explain to nobles and higher clergly how to behave and interact with the lower orders and their respective lieges.\n\nI sincerly hope that you enjoy this book, for I am probably to print it and produce many at the store of Jacob Chapel. If any would wish to see me about this piece, I am usually in the Avenese Estate near Pibblebonk or #I Waterfall Avenue, Aldersburg.\n\nI.The Concept of Fuedalism___________________                                This chapter shall be short for it should be known to all. \n\nThere is no commonly accepted modern definition of feudalism, at least among scholars.\nIt is commonly, and simply\n\ndefined, as the nobility, in exchange for protection, swear fealty and provide labour and military power in exchange for counties and duchies. In some fuedalistic socities, kings and emperors were little more than grand dukes, with the meeting, the king\n\nand the nobles together having the power. However, fuedalism does seem to be on the decline, due to the absoulitist nature of the imperial monarchy. In fuedal society, the heirarchy could be described as:\n\nEmperor\nKing\nArchduke\nPrince\nGrand Duke\nDuke\nCount\nLord Mayor\nMayor\nGentry\nSmall Landowners\nFree Subjects\nPeasants\n\nII.Edicts of Nobility.\n\nI.He must be gregaroius and socially competant, and speak in a noble and \"posh\" manner (as some blackguards would call it)\n\nII.He must know the code of chivalry, save for the paragraph which says he must serve the welfare of all.\n\nHe is free to do as he wishes with his peasants and other subjects, mistreating them is discouraged but it is not an edict to not do so.\n\nIII.He must distrivute his land amoung the gentry and other landowners and delegate tasks to his courtiers.\n\nIV.He must mantain a full court, and hear the advice of his courtiers, for they are gentlemen and women, and their word should be respected. \n\nV.A nobleman must seek the consel of his liege before making a major decision, including marriages. However, if\n\na monarch would abuse their power, it is both their right and duty to fight against the tyranny and give more power to the nobility. Just as one delegates tasks and wealth to courtiers, a king must do so with his nobles. The monarch and his nobles must be\n\nin balance.\n\nVI.A noble must obey the head of house except in exceptional circumstances. \n\nVII.A noble must be an advocate for the fuedal system in every aspect, organizing his army in this way.\n\nVIII.He must not assosciate with peasantry or other men of the lower order.\n\nIX.The head of house should not occupy himself with martial prowess or entrance into the clergly-this is the duty of the younger sons.\n\nX.He must instead focous on his\n\nadministrative skills.\n\nXI.He must seek to be pious and faithful, for a noble should get to the fifth heaven at least.\n\nXII.As well as this, he must be able to attend mass and read the Holy Scriptures regularly, and teach it to his subjects, inspiring his\n\nlevies with such things.\n\nIII.Principles of A Stable State________________________\nI have read many books which stress the importance of absoloute monarchy. Of despots, and absoloute power. However, I think this not be true. I think it prudent that a\n\ntable of nobles, all the lords of the realm, decide together, with the ruler holding meeting regularly with noblemen. The reason absoloute monarhcy is bad is because it is brilliant if given to an able leader, an able emperor. But, if it falls under the\n\ncontrol of a usurper, his nobles are powerless and even then, if he is a mere bad monarch, and no usurper, the effect is much the same. The tyrant will abuse his power and inspire not with his wisdom but with his power and intimidation, many gallant\n\nnoblemen will be imprisoned.\n\nFurthermore, a noble should have a similar system with his gentry. He must seek their consel before making a move, and must build a good relationship with his gentry, who will then indeed serve their lieges gratefully and\n\nproesperity will come from the estates and martial prowess from the sons and brothers of these landed gentry. \n\nSuch a relationship should also be given to a noble's wife, who may be given administrative and diplomatic tasks. Of course, according to the\n\ncode of chivalry, we should not risk the lives of the ladies. \n\nHonour is an important aspect, and a duke or above should be able to call the crown out on matters of honour. Whilst not going so far as dueling, as a royal's death would cause instability,\n\nnoble must be a paragon of honour and hope, and must make sure his liege is. And vice versa. One should improve the other, with the monarch seeking the consel of the nobles and the nobles seeking the guidance and loyalty to their liege.\n\nIn order to keep\n\nfuedal order and keep the loyalty of the subjects, absoloute monarchy must stop. \n\nNo one but dukes and above should swear direct alligience to the emperor. The dukes and above must, with the counts swearing to them, the minor nobles doing to them, the\n\ngentry, the peasants etc. This also, suprisingly, helps the monarch, for he has no unworthy subjects unneedily wasting his time. An emperor must be in a high, distant place, the dukes closer, the counts closer and all the way down to the small landowners,\n\ndirectly taking responsability for serfs. This is the ideal fuedal government, the one which embodies fuedalism the most, and the greatest enforcement of fuedalism. \n\nBut you may ask, why would the monarch ever agree to this? Well, that is a simple\n\nquestion, sire, and for that, I have the answer.\n\nIn return for the greater power, the nobles must give a greater amount of troops, mostly levies, to the cause. If we focous on conscripting the levies in times of war, and follow this system in which\n\nvassals must provide more, perhaps we can double the size of our forces. \n\nI have also written a book documenting my principles on the organization of the army. \n\nIt is to be printed soon. If you enjoy this, please read that.\n\nAnd with that, sires, I bid you aideu.\n\n\n\n__________________________________________________________[!]A sketch of a miltiaman in a gambeson and with spear and shield is seen here[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Would - Prolouge", "§bDolan Velethen", "Long ago a princess, by the name of Alis, was in her tower alone. The quiet elf layed back on her bed, merely questioning her position in life.\n\nIt was a cold night and the moon shinned upon the ground like a glimmering diamond.\n\nHer dreams were not kempted and her love for adventure was tampered, for you see, in the morrow she was to be wed to a man who shall not be named. As she looked out into the woods an idea struck her skull.\n\nShe climbed down the vines of the walls slowly and quietly.\n\nWhen she touched the grounds Alis ran into the woods, never to be seen again.\n\nSome say that the princess died in the wood. Others say she\n\nlives in the wild alone.\n\nBut I know a different story, she became what we now know as the evil witch of the woods.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "Jistuma", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nElements of Alchemy\n\nVolume I-2 of V\n\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\n\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.” But what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is\n\nrequired before that question can be answered and in fact, if that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\n\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir, and\n\nconcept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon. An ignorant outlook on this statement is that what is meant is the physical, literal meaning behind these elements but one must look into the symbolism, they must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into\n\neach of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual, may understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\n\nFire\n===\nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\n\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal. Fire can represent rage, anger,\n\nhatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will, and allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear\n\nat. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\nActions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action\n\nof burning, consuming, and destroying. Alchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon, but if\n\none were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos. It is true that Chaos is\n\noften something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized. Chaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and\n\npowerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick, two completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or\n\nsolely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used. The teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\n\nEarth\n===\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\n\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things, I will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\n\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength, the notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance, or\n\nstrength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion. Protecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also\n\nused in antidote potions, disease-curing potions, and, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders, often associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also\n\nrequired for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on. Many of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend, and using\n\nelements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation. Now, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon\n\ntransmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals, for metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\n\nWater\n===\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\n\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water. Often known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its\n\nname for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing, liquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on\n\ndrinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid, one must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\n\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life. But one\n\ncan also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic. Through oils, one may\n\nreap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made by distilling wine or other liquors.\n\nAir\n===\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\n\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception, and\n\neven flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes, the ways in which to represent Air are quite\n\nobvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion, are rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite\n\nrarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather, which is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions\n\ncentered around this element. Another, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and\n\nAir intermingle. With that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols, the next chapter will explain\n\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\n\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-2\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Time Warping", "Minuscule_Evil", "Time Warping\n\n      by, Tahjeet\n   Asul'mira Mubdee\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nIf the theory of time as an illusion is correct then it is possible that time itself can be warped, molded or shaped, by the will of a person.\n\nTime, although a perception, an illusion is viewed as reality anymoment where the perception of time\n\nis changed, it is in the eyes of all, truly changed as a reality.\n\nBut to be able to learn to warp the perception of time, an illusion, a person must know how to create and mold illusions.This can be done with, perhaps, one’s mana alike how\n\nevocationists can create and change the arcane through the casting of mana.\n\nTo make a comparison, time is like a piece of iron and the one who can mold this piece of iron is the blacksmith, in this case an illusionist.\n\nTo shape and mold the iron, it requires the iron to be heated., the casting of ones mana, then to shape the piece of iron it requires a hammer, this will be the illusionist’s ability to mold and shape the illusion or perception.\n\nFor example, if the blacksmith hammers the iron flat it become elongated- lengthening time-if the blacksmith hammers the iron into a smaller length it becomes shorter – shortening time– if the blacksmith hammers the iron from a different angle,\n\n becomes bent - perhaps stopping time.\n\nWhat may be that separates simple illusions and the warping of the time illusion, which may be the reason no illusionist, is that time is an illusion seen by all and perceived as a reality.\n\nThis changes what that iron is. The piece of iron the blacksmith had been shaping was just a small piece of a large statue.\n\nThe illusion of time surrounds us, we are immersed in it, fragments of the illusion can be shaped, changing what we see and feel. It is impossible for anyone to truly see time as an illusion even though it is known to be so.\n\nLiving beings are designed to perceive time as a reality, to see old and new, growth and withering, life and death.\n\nTo understand time is to not see through its illusion.\n\nTo warp time is left in the hands of the curious.", ""),
        StaticBook("Horns of Ylmir", "§bUlmo Maehr", "The Horns of Ylmir\n\nAn extract from the song of the same name.\n\nI heard them wailing round me where the black cliffs towered \nAnd the old primeval starlight filckered palely in the sky.\nIn that dim and perilous region in\n\nwhose great tempestuous ways\nI heard no sound of men's voices, in those eldest of days,\nI sat on the ruinded margin of the deep-voiced echoing sea\nWhose roaring foaming music crashed in endless cadency\nOn the land besieged\n\nfor ever in an aeon of assualts\nAnd torn in towers and pinnacles and caverned in great vaults;\nAnd its arches shook with thunder and its feet were piled with shapes\nRiven in old sea-warfare from those crags and\n\nsable capes.\n\n-Verse 3 of 'The Horns of Ylmir' as recorded in 'The Fall of Gondolin'\n\n-A celebratory tale of the might of Ulmo, Lord of the Waters.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wish Sumary ->", "§bKeovan Scarfen", "-------=[]=-------\nA Wish Part 2\n\nNow when i think about\nit, it may be a bit over dramatic..\nIm.. just wishing for a teacher is all..\nAs.. of now im looking for a teacher in alchemy or/and a teacher in Arcane Shielding.. But theres many people wanting\n\nfor their wish to be taken.. So.. i guess this is just a dream for me\n\n~Keovan Scarfen\n(( nanoninja23 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Myths", "§bWayward Druid Respiren", "* The Myth of the *           Great War\nMany moons ago a terrible war broke out between the two mighty guilds of wizards -one good and one evil- that controlled great empires. Wizards on both sides vowed to fight until  utterly triumphant\n\n Seeking to purge their rivals from the land. With fearsome magic and dragon armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning final victory . Through their warfare, the wizards wrought vast devastation on the world,\n\nForests blazed up, islands sank into the sea, entire races became extinct. Eventually, the the great goddess of Nature awakened from her sleep to witness the savage conflict.\n\n Shocked by the destruction, the Goddess sent a vision to a single woman who would become the first Grand Druid. Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a druidic order to preserve the fragile remains of her world's ecology.\n\n\n\nWith the guidance of her goddess, the  Order grew in strength Until finally it had the power to intervene in the wizard war...\n\nThe force of young druids pooled  their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts.\n\nOnce the former wizards now unable to fathom the concept of good versus evil - slithered, bounded, loped and crawled off into their ruined habitats, the Order began to heal the lands.\n\nSince then, the druidic order  continually works to prevent such destruction from ever occurring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars of good  and evil no longer mar the precious land.\n\n But, the Order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the  guilds of warring wizards- those good and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows.\n\nEach guild claims it had been on the verge of victory and would have won, had druids not interfered. \n\n-As recounted by Hierophant Pulver, Master of Dungeons", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex Tahariae", "§bHeshakomeu Sohae", "[!] The brown leather cover of the small book bears only the embossed golden clerical eye: the symbol of the Clerical Order of Tahariae. Its white pages turn easily, and each is covered completely in smooth, flowing handwriting. [!]\n\n---------+---------\nCodex Tahariae\n---------+---------\n\nMay His Light be with you, servant of Tahariae.\n\nIt is through prayer and ritual that the priest of Tahariae calls upon His power. This tome contains the prayers and rituals held by the Sacred Priesthood of Tahariae that pertain to the arts of\n\nsanctification, healing, purging, and restoration, as remembered, developed, decided, and recorded by the High Priest Heshakomeu Sohae.\n\nNever again shall the ways of the priest be forgotten.\n\n---------+---------\nThe Hymn of the Promise and the Ritual of Sanctification\n---------+---------\n\nThe ritual of sanctification allows objects to be used as a conduit for Tahariae’s power while a cleric casts a spell. Every ritual uses sanctified items. Although without power outside of a ritual, they allow priests to form a stronger connection with\n\nconnection with Tahariae while summoning His power, easing the strain of healings and making them more efficient.\n\nThe process of sanctification one of the most basic forms of worship a servant of the Pure One, whether cleric or acolyte, can perform.\n\nDuring the forging or crafting of the item, the adherent shall pray the Hymn of the Promise.\n\n----------------------\n\nTahariae, oh Blessed One, Aengul and Lord of Purity,\nI bow before Thy glory.\nI am but mortal dust, yet You have chosen me to do Thy will,\n\nAnd I am honored to fulfill it.\n\nO Pure One, to You I promise my life,\nAnd pray that You would use it to bring glory to You.\nTo You I promise my soul,\nAnd pray Thy Five Tenets be upheld in all my actions.\n\nTo You I promise my loyalty,\nAnd pray that I shall serve no other lord before Thee.\nAnd to You I promise my heart,\nAnd pray that Thy Light may purify and make it just.\n\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nWith the finishing of the hymn, the adherent must then explain how the object shall bring glory to Tahariae. When the listing of its gifts is complete, the adherent shall end with: “May this be a testament to Thy Glory.”\n\nIf\n\nthe object is not complete by the ending of the hymn and listing, the adherent shall begin the hymn and listing again. They shall repeat them until they are satisfied with the quality of the object.\n\nThe sanctification of shrines is very similar the\n\nsanctification of ritual objects. The adherent proceeds around the perimeter of the shrine, anointing points around it with holy oil or water and circling it with burning sanctified candles whilst reciting the Hymn of the Promise. Once the perimeter has\n\nbeen fully anointed and encircled, the sanctifier may begin to extinguish each candle as they continue to recite the hymn.\n\nWhen preparing holy oil, the hymn is recited and the purposes listed whilst the oil is extracted or boiled from its source.\n\nWhen preparing holy water, a container is filled with water and taken to a sanctified shrine. The water is placed on a sanctified altar, the candles that adorn the altar are lit, and, as with all other items, the hymn is recited and the purposes listed.\n\n---------+---------\nThe Hymn of Restoration and the Ritual of Healing\n---------+---------\n\nThe most common use of a cleric’s power is the restoration of Descendants to remove bodily injury, whether through accident or assault, and it is the responsibility of a servant of Tahariae to show them the restorative Light of the Pure One.\n\nHealing\n\nusing Tahariae’s blessing, however, cannot be taught through a mere tome. It requires the personal guidance of a priest or experienced healer. Preserved here is the Ritual of Healing, a hymn and ritual used by those of the Sacred Priesthood to better\n\nfocus their spells and ease the strain they have on the cleric. It is not for untrained clerics to learn holy healing.\n\nThe ritual begins with the placement of four sanctified candles in a rectangular shape around the wounded individual. As each one is\n\nAs each one is lit, the beginning of each promise from the Hymn of the Promise is recited, also known as the Little Hymn of the Promise:\n\n----------------------\n\nO Pure One, to You I promise my life.\nTo You I promise my soul.\n\nTo You I promise my soul.\nTo You I promise my loyalty.\nAnd to You I promise my heart.\n\n----------------------\n\nAfter the candles are lit, thecleric should take hold of their staff or wand, focus on Tahariae, and recite\n\nthe beginning of the Hymn of Restoration:\n\n----------------------\n\nO Tahariae, Lord of Purity, I, Thy humble mortal servant, call upon You.\nGrant me Thy Light of grace and restoration.\nIgnore not the pain and suffering of the Descendants caused\n\nby the impurity of this realm.\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nWith the first stanza finished, the cleric summons Tahariae’s light. They must then reach out with the light to fully surround the body, using the\n\ncandles as a mental border for the aura. The candle flames will turn to the color of the light touching it. The cleric may then begin the healing process, using the light to restore the body to what it was before injury. As they work, the cleric shall\n\nbegin the second stanza of the hymn:\n\n----------------------\n\nReach down, O Lord, and wipe clean these wounds.\nAllow me to use Thy light to do Thy pure and holy work.\nRestore flesh and bone and blood and life with Thy holy light.\n\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nAs the cleric finishes the healing and releases Tahariae’s power, they may begin the third stanza of the hymn, otherwise known as the Sacred Acknowledgement:\n\n----------------------\n\nFor it is through Thy light that peace is found.\nIt is through Thy light that suffering ends.\nIt is through Thy light that purity is brought.\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nAnd so the ritual ends. Praise be to Tahariae.\n\n---------+---------\nThe Hymn of Life and the Ritual of Curing\n---------+---------\n\nDisease. If it gains a secure enough foothold, it quickly stretches its dark hand across the realm, poisoning and laying waste to everywhere it touches. Tahariae’s Light can be used purge illness from the body of the afflicted. Recorded here is the Ritual\n\nof Curing, a traditional hymn and ritual used by those of the Sacred Priesthood to cure disease.\n\nThe ritual begins with the placement of four sanctified candles in a rectangular shape around the ill individual and the preparation of holy water or oil. As\n\neach candle is lit, each promise from the Little Hymn of the Promise is recited.\n\nAfter the candles are lit, the cleric should take hold of their staff or wand, focus on Tahariae, and recite the beginning of the Hymn of Life:\n\n----------------------\n\nO Tahariae, Lord of Purity, I, Thy humble mortal servant, call upon You.\nGrant me Thy Light of purging and life.\nDescend upon this soul and purge the blight that torments its mortal body.\n\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nWith the first stanza finished, the cleric summons Tahariae’s light. They must then reach out with the light to fully surround the body, using the candles as a mental border for the aura.\n\nThe candle flames will turn to the color of the light touching it. The cleric shall anoint the sufferer’s forehead with holy oil or water while channeling their Light through it. They may then begin the healing process, using the Light to smother the\n\ndisease. As they work, the cleric shall begin the second stanza of the hymn:\n\n----------------------\n\nWipe away the suffering that coursing through these veins.\nBanish blood and bile and tears and pain.\n\nIt is only through Thy grace, O Lord, that such is possible.\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nAs the cleric finishes the healing and releases Tahariae’s power, they shall recite the Sacred Acknowledgement.\n\nAnd so the ritual ends. Praise be to Tahariae.\n\n---------+---------\nThe Hymn of Purity and the Ritual of Purging\n---------+---------\n\nTahariae’s greatest enemy is the evil and impurity that abounds throughout the realm. It is the duty of a war cleric to destroy the sources; it is the duty of a priest to destroy the taint they leave on the land and the Descendants.\n\nTaint is the physical\n\nmanifestation of darkness on our realm. It is one of the most difficult things to obliterate with Tahariae’s Light. Only incredibly experienced clerics have the skill and endurance to do so. A cleric with no prior experience should not attempt to purge\n\ntaint without an experienced cleric to supervise them.\n\nThe Ritual of Purging is designed to assist clerics in better focusing Tahariae’s Light on taint. May Tahariae be glorified through it.\n\nThe ritual begins with the placement of four\n\nsanctified candles in a rectangular shape around the tainted individual, the donning of a sanctified medallion, and the preparation of holy water or oil. As each candle is lit, each promise from the Little Hymn of the Promise is recited.\n\nAfter the\n\ncandles are lit, the cleric should take hold of their staff or wand, focus on Tahariae, and recite the beginning of the Hymn of Purity:\n\n----------------------\n\nO Tahariae, Lord of Purity, I, Thy humble mortal servant, call upon You.\nGrant me Thy sacred\n\nlight of purity and justice.\nObliterate the taint that has manifested on our realm with Thy holiness.\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\nWith the first stanza finished, the cleric summons Tahariae’s light. They must then\n\nreach out with the light to fully surround the body, using the candles as a mental border for the aura. The candle flames will turn to the color of the light touching it. Be warned: Tahariae’s light will cause great pain to the afflicted when it makes\n\ncontact with the taint. The battle between purity and impurity has begun in the Descendant.\n\nThe cleric may then begin the second stanza, anointing the site of the taint with holy water or oil as they recite:\n\n----------------------\n\nThy Will is just, O Lord.\nReach down Thy Light of Justice and banish this tormenting evil!\n\n----------------------\n\nWith the sight anointed, the cleric shall set down the holy oil, take the medallion in their hand, and hold it out\n\nover the sight of the taint. As the channel Tahariae’s Light through the medallion, they may finish the second stanza.\n\n----------------------\n\nSmite this impurity that threatens to overwhelm all it touches.\n\nMay this day be a testament to Thy Glory.\n\n----------------------\n\nAs the cleric finishes the healing and releases Tahariae’s power, they shall recite the Sacred Acknowledgement.\n\nAnd so the ritual ends. Praise be to Tahariae.", ""),
        StaticBook("ReturnedArchmage", "§bEdronos", "-  -  -  -  -  -  -  -\nThe Return of the\n        Archmage\n-  -  -  -  -  -  -  -\n\nHwaldar has found me again, speaking of troubles concerning the Guild. He mentioned the voidwalker, Whisperer. According to him, they are good friends, and Whisperer even proved useful as of late. Apparently, Hwalder has been tricked out of his\n\nposition, having to appoint Everard as Archmage in his place, things safe for Hwaldar.\n\n\nHe desires to usurp the Arcane Mage.\n\nWhen I asked what he needed, he said one thing: You are my new apprentice.\n\nI met him in the Tower, confused but nonetheless intrigued. He claimed influence over Guild matters, despite his recent expulsion, and while the invitation to apprenticeship honor s me and magic is the stuff of dreams,\n\nI have no aspirations for magehood. If I did, I believe this invitation would only serve to disappoint. Regardless, I let the curious mage speak.\n\nHe began by speaking to Golems and other such creatures touched or hitherto wrought by magics. Immediately, my mind shifted to Whisperer, the voidwalker, who has created quite the stir as of late.\n\nHwaldar continued, professing on the magics of \"entity creation\", with which entire beings can be born of the mind.\n\nThe conversation consistantly shifted to Whisperer from then on. Apparently, the voidwalker is one such \"mind-man\", possibly born insane and sent to the Void through use of unstable and young understood magic.\n\nSince then, Whisperer has returned, disoritented and furious. Then, Hwaldar touched on how to destroy one such entity.\n\nEarlier on in the conversation, Hwaldar spoke of \"bursts\" that occur when unstable  materials are used in entity creation. These bursts can affect the magician or the environment, but the results are always  undesirable.\n\nSomething similar can be used to \"overload\" a mind-man, who does not fear physical force. Apparently, any repeated use of magic upon one such entity, the ethereal voidwalker, will  cause the creature to burst themselves, as they absorb all magics\n\nthey come in contact with.\n\nIt's curious that the mage would reveal to me exactly how to destroy one such as Whisperer , whom he claims to be a close friend. It remains to be seen what Hwaldar is trying to get at.\n\nHe's made it quite clear that he has a scheme bubbling beneath his hood. How I fit into those plans, and what he intends for the Guild, I am not sure.", ""),
        StaticBook("Urban Myths V.1", "§bArthur Caulfield", "Urban Myths V.1\n\n\n\n\n\n        The Drowning\n            Soldier\n\nIf you have for any length of time stayed in Petrus, then you may have heard the rumour of the drowning soldier. \n   Such a myth was first talked about over forty years ago. It is believed to originate from an inn not far from Petrus and has now spread.\n\nThe myth has been widely regarded by locals as false. But many travellers still take caution and even the guards admit to jumping at sounds in the night. \n   While it may sound absurd, there has been no other way to explain the missing persons whom I\n\nwill describe to you over the course of this book.\n   Such missing person reports have been unawnsered to this very day, guards do not have an exclamation for it and even the extensive security put on Petrus in later months has not diminished the\n\nrate of kidnappings. \n  The figure I give you now may be shocking. But it is the truth, and in order to show you the true threat this myth holds, it must be told. \n   In the past forty years since the myth began, over twenty people, fifteen of whom were\n\ntravellers, have gone missing. Of course, with so few locals taken, the guards do not bother with extensive investigation. Leaving the myth unproven for so long.\n\nIt first started with an elf at an inn. He had supposedly told the bartender about a girl who had gone missing.     She had lived in Petrus for some time, the locals said each morning she would leave the city to visit the temple of monks.\n\nHowever, on one particular morning she left the city, never to return. \n   Her body was uncovered over twenty years later, it had been buried under the sand in the river.     If you have never been to Petrus before, let me explain.\n\nA bridge, going across a river will bring you to the cities front entrance. This river runs almost all the way across. It is in this river that all of the sightings and subsequent deaths occured.\n\nWhen the girl had been pulled out, she had expired. Almost unrecognisable. Her clothes were soaked and torn, her hair dissolved over such a long time, her skin was grey and held none of the beauty it had done in life.\n\nHer eyes bulged out from her skull, pushed from her head by the pressure. \n\nThis had been the first incident.\n\nOf course, I won't describe every single account for it would never leave you with a sense of safety again.    But I shall explain what should happen if you have the misfortune to see him.    Bear in mind no witness has ever survived to tell the tale, so\n\nI shall go from what I have heard of the many rumours. \n  Firstly, the myth is of a soldier, wearing the Petrus guard armour. He appears to be wearing the remains of a sword holster. \n  His hair is, or was, black. Knotted and left in clumps on his head.\n\nHis mouth is as grey as the worn uniform he wears.   \n   Some have even described him as having purple blothces on his skin, some sort of disease unheard of now.\n   But the frightening part is not his looks. But his voice.\n\nNo mortal being possess' the sound that this man makes when seen. \n   What can only be described as a piercing, hostile scream will escape his mouth. \n   The scream has been said to cause severe headaches and bleeding of the ear\n\ncanal. Stunning most which would give him time to attack. \n   Sadly, there is not much you can do once he begins to scream. No one has ever been able to block it out in enough time. \n   The fourth victim died wearing an iron helmet that completely\n\nsurrounded his head, making noise very muffled. Though this seemed to make no difference in his encounter and he was left as dead as all the others.\n   This is where many go wrong, for it is not the noise you need to escape. It is the sight.\n\nVictims were killed upon seeing the soldier. A blind man could never have been killed. \n   Of course it is ridiculous to tell people to wear blindfolds when walking in and out of Petrus, which is why nobody does it.\n\nThe scream is just the beginning. Once you have been stunned, or even paralysed, you will be dragged from the bridge and into the river. \n  Presumably buried under piles of sand so that you may not be discovered for years to come.\n\nSome of the bodies, discovered slightly earlier than twenty years, showed bruises around their throats and signs of struggle, torn clothes etc. \n   A rather odd thing to note is that the scream can only be heard by the spotter. Guards could stand just\n\ninches away and not hear a thing. It seems to only affect the person looking at the soldier.\n   The position of the soldier is also a point that changes with each telling of the story. Some say that the soldier is seen struggling and panicking in the\n\nriver, crying for help. The water around him will remain perfectly still and no splashing can be seen however it can be heard. \n   The soldier will cry out for help, go under a few times and sound rather convincing. It is only when the person runs down\n\nto help that he will leap out with inhuman speed. His arms raised, his hands open, ready to clutch at you're skin and pull you under.\n   Others may say differently. They may tell you that he is not seen drowning but is instead seen lying on the grass\n\nright besides the river, seemingly dead. Once approached, or in some stories looked at, he will sit up and stare at you.\n  This is usually when he will begin to scream.   Other stories are slightly more questionable. Such as one that suggests the soldier\n\nlurkes in a tree, waiting for a fisherman to go down by the river and cast his line in. \n  Others suggest he is not seen at all but has tremendously long arms that reach out of the river and pull you in.\n\nIn conclusion, if you see a soldier down by the river in Petrus, it is already too late.\n  Just stay away.\n\nYou have been warned", ""),
        StaticBook("Hubris Volume 2", "§bRosso", "Table of Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nBook Four: Page 2\nBook Five: Page 14\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Book 4\n\nAfter the Humans had placed tree branches to cover the entrance to the Cavern, a group of Elves ventured into that area, hearing the call of the wounded trees. They discovered the branches and removed them, wondering what foul creature had despoiled the\n\ntrees in such a way and for what cause. Into the cavern they ventured, discovering the notes from Nemiisae and the portal to the Verge. This group did not go back for more, though more would come later, as they were immediately forced through. Running\n\nfrom a threat, they entered the Verge and discovered the portal to the new world. Fleeing still, they had no choice but to enter. They too fell into this trap, the portal closed behind them, no way back, though they would only find this out after\n\nreturning later to investigate. For now, they still had running to do. Immortal though they were, this land was still rife with danger. Forced to settle in it, the Elves would follow in the footsteps of their cousins, perishing within this strange lands\n\nwithin half a Millenia. In these lands they were susceptible not just to the terrors, but also their own curse. Far more infertile than they were in their original lands, they died out merely due to a lack of numbers. While some of them eventually\n\ninterbred with Nemiisae’s children, those who refused would only gain numbers through other poor fools coming through the portal. In this way the Elves too, were trapped.\nWhen the Elves first found the broken and disturbed trees as well as the secret they\n\nhid, they did not realize they were being hunted. Following them from Malinor had been an Orc hunting party, searching for slaves, meat, or just a bit of violent fun. The Orcs assaulted the Elves at the entrance to the crevice, and having no other way to\n\ngo, the Elves immediately fled into the Crevice and down into the Cavern. The Orcs gave chase, of course, following them through the Verge and the next portal, into the new world. The Elves had gotten ahead, fleeing to the nearest forests they could find.\n\nIn the thick cover, the Orcs lost sight of them. They began to investigate the land as their cousins had. They settled, adventured, and fought. Fighting was what they were good at and they were much better equipped for the trip into this new world, to\n\nface the terrors that haunted it. But their own aggression killed them in the end. They perished at the hands of beasts, monsters they should have known they would never defeat, at least not in totality. Within a half of a Millenia, the Orcs too were\n\nextinct, leaving behind only the skeletal ruins of their previous homes and their old enemies they had died out battling.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Book 5\n\nIn the course of the first two-hundred and fifty years, as Nemiisae searched for a way to open the portal and leave this place, Zanunder aged within his sleep, eventually dying. Bereaved of her husband she fell into a great remorse for having\n\naccidentally killed him. Her mind became clouded, muddled, perhaps even mad. Then her children came to her with reports of these strangers in their lands. She realized then what had happened…The portal only shut on their side. It must have been an\n\naccidentally killed him. Her mind became clouded, muddled, perhaps even mad. Then her children came to her with reports of these strangers in their lands. She realized then what had happened…The portal only shut on their side. It must have been an\n\nunwittingly played a part in. She could not reopen the portal, but she could close it from her side, sealing off both the portal to the Verge and the portal within it to the new world. Then she retreated back into her Caverns, encouraging her children to\n\nlive, breath, fight, grow stronger. Punish and perish the weak and live for themselves and for her, for it was the only way to gain God’s favor. Then she left them to their own devices, her wishes for their future made clear.\n\nIt was in this way that hubris was punished, that the sins of those who came before was tested and they were proven guilty. Had these people physically gone to these lands, surely the curse would not have killed them all. But by passing through the portal\n\nof Hubris which Nemiisae had created, they doomed themselves and their kin. Other groups found the portals between the time Nemiisae realized what had happened and closed it off, but anyone who came through was doomed to suffer and die.\n\nThere was no hope for them as soon as they had passed through those portals into that world. But it is far enough removed that between the first settling of it and our time, no one has ever discovered it again. Beyond churning, whirling seas, deadly\n\nislands, leagues and weeks away from the lands settled by the Four Brothers, it would be impossible to reach without the assistance of a very strong force indeed. But perhaps it is for the best, that these ruins remain ruins, and the skeletons go\n\nundisturbed, lest we awaken old evils…\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Volume 2\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Gemstones", "§bcjmate8", "This book has been created in order to spread the cultural significance of gemstones. It is my hope that this book will lead to increased insight when crafting jewelry for a partner or friend.\n-------------------Ruby- Gives people increased wisdom.\n\nIt is particularly useful for rash, or less intelligent beings.\n\nEmerald- Increases the fertility of a person, both during conception and bearing. \n\nDiamond- The most powerful of all gems.\nIt amplifies all other\n\ntraits.\n\nAmethyst- Calms the nerves. Useful for study or meditation.\n\nSugilite- The healer's stone. It is used in the healing arts, both magic and item.\n\nCarnelian- Improves analytical skills.\n\nGarnet- The bloodstone. It is used to draw toxins from the body and aid in blood clot.\n\nOnyx- Used to obtain enlightenment.\n\nHematite- Reduces stress.\n\nJasper- Protects the\n\nwearer from mind invasion.\n\nSapphire- Invokes peace and happiness.\n\nTopaz- Increases both metal and physically stamina.\n\nTiger's eye- Destroys anxiety. It promotes non-reckless\n\ncourage.\n\nPeridot: Used for growth. Commonly given to small children to hasten or improve growth. It can also aid handicapped children who are recovering.\n\nPearl- Used in chakra. Improves the connection with both\n\nmind and body.\n\nSoladite: Absorbs negative thoughts from both the wearer and those around them. This negates the thoughts.\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Paladin of Xan", "§bAdorellan Sintel", "Xan:\n~~~\nA burning light in the\nunforgiving darkness.\nA sword and shield to\nthe order of the realm.\nXan is an Aengul, that which embodies the illuminating hope of Guardianship and Order. Xan was known for his war with a threat to the mortal -\n\n- realm. A Drakaar, one so strong and wise he was thought to be the herald of the Drakaar themselves. Xan's once powerful and strong order fought endlessly with Setherien. He bestowed his boons upon a line so ancient Xan 's blood mixes with theirs. The -\n\n- Athna's. Hilan Athna, the grandfather of the three siblings, Sarah Athna, Hilan Athna the II and his Guardian, Herun Athna now known as Xath. Hilan, the grandfather had his order convene and thus a might weapon of war had been forged. -\n\n- 'The Golden Lance.' A weapon so powerful that Hilan named their Order after it. This weapon was fueled with Aengulic power that of Xan's which gave it it's fierce, golden shine. Years passed and nine of HIlan'sd CHampions were slain and drafted into -\n\n- the dark side. Years passed and Hilan had passed away, bestowing his gifts and magics upon his grandchildren whilst Xan's bestowed the gifts of mind, strength and will to the three. By this time, Setherien had split the Lance in three which was -\n\n- was soon re-forged by Herun Athna with an immense amount of magic. Later, the Golden Lance was plunged into the depths of Setherien's chest, ending his reign of tyranny over Anthos & The Fringe.d Now, it is said Herun and Crumena were born anew as -\n\n- Xan's Guardianship and Order which were drawn together like brothers in arms.\n-------------------\n\n\nXan, however, fights a war of his own which only the likes of Aengul's and Daemon's can fight.", ""),
        StaticBook("See the Moonrise", "§bDamien Menrow", "Does thou want to see the Moonrise....watch the ending of the Day.\n\nThey have been working so very hard to move the Stars into a beautiful ray.\n\nYet it gets kind of lonely all the things they do, and no one seems to care...\n\nDoes thou want to see the Moonrise....I want to show you come with me.\n\nOrion's Stars are out and shining bright, it's such a gorgeous Night.\n\nOh wont you come and see....It's just that no one seems to notice all the things they do...\n\nIt's just that it gets so lonely....all sweet Night long. No one seems to want to see the ending of the Day.\n\nBut does thou want to see the Moonrise....or we can hang out till the Sunrise...*", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Balance", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nLesson on The Balance:\nThis is a very in-depth lesson to give your Dedicants, but a very important one. You may find the 'Neo-Druidism' tome to be especially helpful in this lesson, as it gives a most accurate description if positive\n\nand negative action towards preserving the Balance. This is sometimes a hard concept to grasp, but a very important one for every Druid. You must impress upon them that a Druid must recognize\n\nwhen action is required, and when observation or even lack of action is required, and understanding what these truly mean to a Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Talk with Undead", "§bDaniel Nodal", "*This paper has a mark of bloody fingerprints, as if the writer had bloody hands on the time of writing.*\n\nAsside from all the problems that were had from the point where I invited a dark robed person to my tavern until we arrived at a house chosen by a Xan paladin, we have finally started to speak with the undead. First impressions of it, it's not afraid to\n\ndie, but does not want to be destroyed. Says it would be a worse way to deliever a message by killing, so he perfers to talk. His name is Jinn, or so he says, he's body is extremelly light, almost as if he is made purely of a skeleton. Even his face made\n\na cracking sound when he was hit.\n\nHis body is made fully of bones, stripped of flesh by himself, or so he says. While being destroyed many times he still has a body, meaning he is reborn anew each time, by his own words.\n\nThe goals and motives of Iblees he does not answer mentioning to ask Iblees himself.\n\nHe asked of our thoughs of Iblees, after I stated that he appeared as a god to destroy us, he told that it would be like that, to birth a new world.\n\nA thought of the battle of good against evil, and of the once victory of good did not remove evil. To create a new world without evil. Stating that Iblees would not kill those that would not oppose him, and lead him to the new world. Hard to think of that\n\nconsidering the undead are his servants and they are dead.\n\nStating he is not controlled by his god, he then stated he would probably be doing more important things if he was, then said that the methods normally though of used by the\n\nundead, killing, destroying, were proving innefficient.\n\nThey kill to send a message, and they are failing at delievering it.\n\nStating that Iblees has changed from the times of Aegis, that before he only wished for destruction, now he\n\nwishes to create the new world.\n\nI sugested that Iblees removed the curse of us, to show us he means the words that the undead stated. He responded by saying that Iblees had placed the curses to show his power, and make the mortals know he is\n\none of greater powers.\n\nWhile stating that dark and light weren't really all that diferent, he stated that those of the Corruption sect could heal others.\n\nBeing injured I asked to be healed, as a demonstration. He\n\nsaid that Iblees would have to look upon those healed as something more than just decendents, something more worthy for it to work.\n\nIn the middle of trying to find something for him to heal, I mentioned perhaps an animal, and he afirmed that\n\nanimals were to kill, then it would not work.\n\nSo instead, he demonstrates it on himself. A Staff of the Betrayer was brought to him, he does not seem to have the power to create one. With his staff, the Xan Paladin was asked to swing and cut off one\n\nof his arms. In front of us he remade his bones, stating that this could not happen in Aegis. Proof that Iblees had changed he said.\n\nHe repeated many times that those that do not mess with the undead will not be harmed.\n\nSnow's Maidan 1481\n\n-Daniel Nodal", ""),
        StaticBook("TTOTWA: Book I", "SapphireShard", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist \n------------\nThe Fundamentals of Alchemy\n \nVolume I of V\n\nForeword\nI have heard many a man ask why one, such as myself, would take such interest in the art of alchemy when there are spells that could do just the same, if not better, a job than an apothecary’s potion.\n\na job than an apothecary’s potion.\nMy response to this statement is rather simple, whereas one must have a certain gift for spell-slinging, rune-craft, and spirit-speaking,\n\none mustn’t need these frivolous commodities to use a balm to mend a wound,\nshroud themselves in a nigh-invisible cloak with the swig from a bitter bottle, or set someone ablaze with bottled flame. Alchemy is not merely reproducing a wizard’s spell,\n\nbut it is shaping the spell in a way for the common man’s use. While magic still has its place in our world, Alchemy allows those without the gift to reap the same benefits as any mage might.\n\nChapter 1: The Fundamentals of Alchemy \n---------------\nThe Principle and Law of Equivalent Exchange:\n\nAs I was providing my services to a rather quaint hamlet, which also provided me information of the local flora and more of the same legends I always here of, I was approached by a man of common repute, and he produced a sarcastic, yet thought\n\nand he produced a sarcastic, yet thought provoking, question.\nThis question was, and I will attempt to reproduce the dialect as best as my phonetic ability will allow, “ ‘ow come, Mister, ‘hat ye’ can make all ‘dis ‘onderful stuff\n\nNow as shameful as his speech may be, the question remains the same. How is it, that alchemists are capable or reshaping the spells of sorcerers for the common folk out of, seemingly, nothing?\n\nThe answer to this question is simple to state, but fairly difficult to grasp, and this is the Principle of Equivalent Exchange. Much like the money one gives to the merchant for the apple or slab of meat, one cannot have something for nothing.\n\nAs the saying goes, “there is no such thing as a free brunch,” there is no such thing as a free potion. This fundamental rule applies to old alchemy, through the use of symbols and rituals, far more than what I call “Modern” alchemy.\n\nAlthough I will not get into ancient alchemy, I will state why this rule applies to Modern Alchemy. To craft a potion, for example a bottle of alchemist’s fire, one requires the materials. Much like a spell casted by a wizard, one cannot make something\n\nMuch like a spell casted by a wizard, one cannot make something out of nothing.\nKnow that to make a potion, and the possibilities are truly endless, one must take plants, objects, and other representations of what they wish to\n\nother representations of what they wish to make.\n\nFor example, alchemist’s fire could be best produced with an -inked out-, a mixture of -inked out-, -inked out-, and a dash of -inked out-. Why would one need these items?\n\nThe -inked out- provides the basic mixture of what we will make, and of course the better quality of the -inked out- the better quality of the Alchemist’s Fire, but of course we will get further into this in a later chapter.\n\n-inked out-, a -inked out- that grows most often in deserts, is often -inked out- and often associated with -inked out-. This provides an superb symbol for the element of -inked out-. -inked out-, another powerful symbol of -inked out-,\n\nmixes well with the crushed -inked out- to produce something truly strong. The-inked out-, an optional portion, is another symbol of -inked out-, albeit both weaker than -inked out- or\n\n-inked out- for both a -inked out- and -inked out-’s fire burns far greater than -inked out-.\n\nNow then, although you have these symbols of flame, rage, and warfare, one mustn’t simply toss objects into the metaphorical cauldron. Precision is necessary, as always.\n\nOne must measure their mixture carefully, or they will give too much. And giving too much will tip the scales of Equivalent Exchange, causing unpredictable results. Why is this you might ask?\n\nWhen balance is achieved through Equivalent Exchange, a mixture of the elements for the bottled spell of your desire, than all is well.\n\nBut when you disrupt this balance and push on the world, taking and forcing in too much of one or more element then the world will push back. Of course a word of caution is required,\n\nfor one may think taking less is the best option when balance is not a certainty. This is a common misconception for not providing enough of one element will result in the same conclusion, imbalance and chaos.\n\nThis can be easily associated with cooking, too much of one ingredient will spoil the recipe, not enough of an ingredient will produce similar results. Of course it could also produce blander results,\n\nand in that case a potion may not be spoiled but it will simply be weak. This is preferable to exploding, of course.\n\nPreparation and You:\n\nNovice Alchemists often question me, what advice would you provide the budding alchemist, what sip of wisdom could you provide one who desires to tap your fountain of knowledge? .\n\nThe answer to this is rather simple, preparation is key to any potion. What is meant by this is that to mix a potion that you have not mixed before, or do not mix often, you must have all the facts and supplies before you begin.\n\nThis is best provided in a short list of required procedures if one wishes to keep their eyebrows, fingers, and life.\n\n1. Have all the Facts\n2. Know the Recipe\n3. Clean and check all your instruments are in working order\n4. Ensure you have plenty of whatever ingredients you are using\n5. Keep a Calm Dispostion\n\nI believe the only topic that requires explanation is “Have all the Facts” and by this I mean that one should not mix a potion they know nothing about.\n\nEven having the recipe is not enough to craft a potion safely, but knowledge of its origins, ingredients, and uses are crucial. Although budding alchemists often overlook this step, it may save your life one day.\n\n((OOC Footnote: Due to the constraints of MC books, the Elememts of Alchemy must be made into a seperate book. It is titled \"The Tale of the Travelling Alchemist: Elements of Alchemy\"))", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Circle", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Druidic Circle\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nThe Druidic Order and a Druidic Circle are two different groups, but are tied closely together. The Order is not of a Circle, but a Circle is of the Order. All Druids who are taught under the Druidic Order are members of the Order, but those taught under\n\none particular Circle are not members of another Circle.\n\nDifferent Circles are rare to exist; this is because differing Circles have differing Druidic beliefs, studies, and structures. In the Order’s past, new Circles were fored because of\n\ndisagreements and differing beliefs, though in the end, those disagreements and differing beliefs were realized to have been senseless and the Circles reformed and conformed to prior belief and focus.\n\nDuring the First and Second Age of Schisms of the Druidic Order’s history, disagreements rose and differing beliefs accumulated which resulted in the Order splitting into multiple Circles. However, it became apparent to the Druids of all Circles during\n\nboth ages that in order to effectively and efficiently perform the Aspects’ will they’d have to stick together in one large Circle; it was noticed that they began to fail at bringing up and teaching new Druids. The Order is strongest as one unit.\n\nA Druidic Circle is defined as a set group of Druids who have a particular focus; that focus could be in the lines of responsibility or it could be an entire different belief. The focus, those teachings, studies, and et cetera,\n\nof the Druidic Order Circle of Malinor are true and are in true allegiance with the Aspects and Nature. A word to the wise: keep close to one another, Druii, and stay true to Nature and to both Aspects; don’t begin a third Age of Schisms. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("You and Waste", "§bLorar Minskin", "------------------- You and Waste\n-------------------  Written by Lorar Min.\n-------------------  A study on the effects of waste on the world around us.\n\n As you look at the world beneath your feet you do not see the waste and all things that are generated by us. Most of these things are hidden beneath our feet in a series of neverending tunnels and networks used to get rid of all the waste we put out.\n\n  So the first question I asked myself was what happened to all of that waste and sewage after it entered the sewers. So I went to check, and found out quite a few things. As I entered the sewers you could barely bear the stench of the waste getting to\n\nthe point of almost inducing vomit. As I reflected on this I thought how bad the oldworld used to be before we made an organized system of getting rid of our waste. After this reflection I continued on.\n After I continued for a few moments I was\n\ndisgusted by how the sewer system had fallen into disrepair so easily. I reconsidered trecking on before continuing in fear of the tunnels collapsing down on me. Though I had to have faith in the sewer's original builders before continuing on.\n  The next\n\nthing I happened to have seen is the variety of life down in the sewers. I was suprised by this fact and considered embracing it before realizing that most of this life wouldn't give another thought before taking a life. Luckily for me I hadn't\n\n encountered anything yet. After taking some samples from the sewers I've concluded that most of the life down there feed on flesh or the wildly-growing mushrooms down there.\n  After noticing these signs of life I realized that most were sensitive to\n\nlight, espicially the mushrooms certain life down there feeded on. As I brought the light closer to the wild-mushroom it shriveled back slightly, I noted this before continuing. The light slightly leads into my next topic, Lighting.\n  Although I know has\n\nbeen proven dangerous by alchemists to bring flame near some types of waste it doesn't excuse the fact that this sewer system I was in was so poorly-light that life grew wildly here. Perhaps more pockets need to be made to release the gas and\n\nsmoke into the air to allow for better lighting. Although the only disadvantage I see to this is the stench. The eye-watering stench could escape through these pockets and reach the street above.\n  Although I did notice one odd thing, as I\n\ngot farther and farther into the deeper,darker sections of the tunnels I noticed a haze. This haze would be no other than the gas emitted by human waste, and for creator's sake it reeked. As I searched around in this haze I noticed that the tunnels in\n\nthis area were starting to crack and crumble under the pressure of the gas, I realized quickly that this was a danger that could not go un-noticed. I realized that if the damage already done to the tunnel got any worse that the stench would slowly seap\n\nthrough the ground and finally into the streets. I noted this and tried to steer clear of the tunnel.\n The last thing that ended my journey was this horrid screeching sound. It was odd because it didn't sound far off from being a normal person. As I\n\nlooked around I found a short figure slowly approaching me. It muttered words in an grumble, his words never reaching my ears. As he got closer I noted why he was walking so slow, he was walking on all fours...He seemed to do it quite effectively. As he\n\ngot closer a sense in my body told me to run, run for the nearest place out. I weaved through the tunnels being followed by this figure. It lumbered after me yelling in a mumbo-jumbo sense. After feeling like there was no hope left I exited the sewers and\n\n breathed a sigh of relief. That \"Thing\" caused me not to want to continue my research. \n I personally concluded that wastes has alot of effects on the world and the living. From small things to large things it varies. We've also proven that some\n\n of the sewer systems need work. Work that may require quite a bit of mina's. But, maybe with the repairs we can eliminate the danger lurking below. The Sewer Gremlin.\n\n-Lorar \nAuthor's Note: Personally I'm not even sure what that\n\ncreature was, after talking to people around the city they were unable to identify it, perhaps, perhaps the fumes got to me and caused all sorts of problems. But you never know there could be a gremlin lurking down in the sewers of any town, perhaps even\n\nyour town. I advise you to check with the council of your town to see how your waste is disposed of and see if it meets the standards it needs to meet. That is all I have to say for now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat Manual", "§bTemp Thersist", "Combat     Basics\n\n         The 3 Stances\n\nHigh - Form is leaned in, Knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward. Referred to as the \"Counter,\" stance. Used to counter-act Mid-guard and stanceless men.\n\nMid-Guard - Form is relaxed, blade pommel parallel to the user's waistline. Knees bent and arms relax. Referred to as the \"Assaulting,\" stance. Attacks vary on situation, be it arc or thrust. Counters Low stance and untrained fodder.\n\nLow - Form is lowered, knees bent and body leaned in. The arms are left in a half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as the \"Wounding,\" stance. Counters High Guard, spearsmaan and isn't typically used to kill a target.\n\n             Movements\n\n\nWhen in combat, keep your foe in direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps forward or backward, instead, side-step in or out.\n\nWhen Assaulting - Nature may say rush at the target head-on. Instead, aim to the target's left or right with movement. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Once flanked, strike either the neck or lower back.\n\nWhen Countering - Side-step, parry, or retaliate. Know the range of the opponent's weapon. IF your range is superior, retaliate with a side-step and aim to cleave limb or behead the enemy. If your range is lesser, parry the blow of the enemy and close\n\nWhen Countering cont... \n\nthe gap, making an effort to disarm or hinder.\n\n         Crossbow Usage\n\nThe following is a petty guide for loading and firing a crossbow.\n\nSet weapon, if required. Simply setting it grip-first onto the ground.\n\nDraw back string, with device or hand.\n\nMove foot from grip.\n\nLift weapon and load with bolt/munition.\n\nShoulder weapon and aim.\n\nFire.\n\nRepeat as needed.\n\nNote loading device.\n\nCreated for usage by the Caerngard of Kaedrin. \n\n - Temp Thersist of Kaedrin.", ""),
        StaticBook("His Fungi", "§bMotsham Malog'Yar", "((This book was written by an orc, but since most of the Blah is mispronounced common, I only wrote the words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common. Sorry for the clunky OOC\n\npreface, but I just wanted to give the reader a heads-up.))    Many of those who gruk mi, gruk that mi have long been a devout worshiper of Orgon. Those who have visited the shrine of Orgon atop the plateau in San'Vitar, may have noticed the fungus which\n\npopulates the mound on which the shrine is erected. Very few people gruk the nature agh significance of the fungus, agh would ignorantly dismiss it as nub-thing more than a bunch of ugly mushrooms. These mushrooms, however, are actually a\n\nsupernatural phenomenon. The fungus which grows upon Orgon's mound is not of the natural world. It is a physical manifestation of Orgon's will agh influence spreading in the mortal plane. This is why lat will nub ever find any growing on their own in a\n\nnormal environment. Very few also gruk that the fungus is, in fact, carnivorous, but feeds almost exclusively during the feeding rituals of Orgon worship. Now, when mi blah the word \"carnivorous\", mi mean it very strongly. During the feeding ritual, the\n\nfungus almost instantly takes root in the flesh of the sacrifice, and begins literally consuming its prey. The process causes the victim to be rapidly digested alive within a matter of minutes. The fungus devours every last piece of its prey, leaving\n\nbehind neither flesh, blood, bones or organs. This is how Orgon has revealed to his followers that his sacrifices must be offered. Outside of the feeding ritual, the fungus feeds very rarely, occassionally digesting any insects that find themselves\n\ntrapped in the liquid secretions of the mushrooms. Now, onto the specifics. There are dub varieties of mushrooms which grow upon Orgon's sacrificial mounds: Orgon's bile and Orgon's gall. Both of these mushrooms have some similar qualities. Namely,\n\nneither should be taken without asking permission of Orgon and rulging him for his generosity; agh they should both be handled with care. \n Orgon's bile: These short, squat mushrooms are a bluish-purple color with white spots. On each spot grow many\n\ntiny black spores. The spores are easily broken, agh contain a foul-smelling black substance. It smells very much like decomposing flesh, and tastes like rotten eggs. Contact stains the skin. A slight taste of the mushroom or the oily, black substance\n\ncauses nausea (agh mi mean a VERY slight taste). Mi tested the effects of full consumption of the mushroom on a willing burz-albai named Mithras. Upon immediately eating the whole thing, he was beset by extreme nausea and vomiting, a cold sweat and\n\nsevere shaking. This was from only ash mushroom. Mi would strongly advise against eating more than ash or a particularly large specimen, as such could very possibly result in flattening. ((Note: these are the red mushrooms growing near Orgon's\n\nshrine))\n Orgon's gall: These somewhat taller mushrooms are related to Orgon's bile, agh are brown in color. The cap of the Orgon's gall mushroom is bowl shaped, agh constantly secretes a very bitter yellowish-brown fluid. This fluid pools in\n\nthe aforementioned bowl-shaped cap, and emits musty fumes which irritate the eyes upon exposure. Physical contact with the mushroom causes a slight burning sensation in the skin, as the fungus coats itself in its own digestive fluids. In small amounts,\n\nthe digestive fluids seem harmless, however mi have witnessed in mi own worship of Orgon how quickly these fungi digest their prey in large enough groups; agh mi gruk it safe to assume that a single mushroom could eventually cause significant damage\n\ngiven enough time. Mi tested the effects of Orgon's gall on a shara named Hagan, who exhibited an extremely dry mouth, blurred vision and hallucinations. As with Orgon's bile, mi would strongly recommend against eating dub or more of these mushrooms, as\n\noverconsumption could have dangerous effects, including flattening. Mi would also theorise that such could possibly lead to lasting impacts on mental health. \n Further discoveries concerning Orgon's bile or Orgon's gall will be recorded agh published in\n\nfuture books if needed.\n -Malog'Yar, witch doctor agh loyal servant of Orgon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task: Bonemeal", "§bLillith", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\n\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\n\nSpread of Bonemeal: \n\nThis is a simple task usually given early to a Dedicant. You give them a moderate amount of bonemeal and send them out into the wilderness to spread it out upon an empty plains or clearing to make the\n\nground lush and fertile. They can also perform this Task within the grove if there is an area suitable for it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Tales 3", "§bFarley III Stafyr", "Book of Tales\n        \n         Chapter III\n\n       Translated by\n       Isovar Kurben\n                 and\n  Novtorn Stonefire\n\n“Min Vatr war Prifyr, dr Soh vo Rigfyr.“ - Stafyr\n\nSilus's Note:\n\nFollowing translated sections of this quite extensive compendium of history and knowledge in regards to Humans,\n\nmore specifically to the old ancestry of the noble family of Stafyr, give a curious amount of insight onto the coming of the Stonefires, their “adventures” and encounters and how their heirlooms came to be. Though it has to be considered\n\nthat going for other sections which are not translated entirely as of this moment that other bloodlines, yes, even the Hansetian people themselves might have Almannir ancestry flowing in them. Fact is, this book is old and the tales reach far\n\nback. And I have only come to understand so much of old Rivachegian. Isovar’s work ends here, most likely because he did not pick up the book or was indisposed or probably dead already. So I shall pick up.\n\nIII Chapter- Promises\n\nStafyr, was his name. A son of Prifyr (S: This might be an indication that Prifyr had more children, hence this might indicate that Stafyr Stonefire actually had siblings. If those had children themselves, I\n\ncannot tell at this point.), who bested and has slain Fyrschlund, devourer of the Galdr and Almannir.\n\nStonefire, he chose, for it was the name of the eldest of Wealtfyr, the first Almannir Machr has awoken and\n\nbreathed his will and spirit into. To go with language and time, the name was renewed.\n\nRemembering the past in the name you give yourself, not to forget the peril his blood and people have gone through, and that he\n\ndescends from the last of the Almannir and that he shall hold up the principles of old, the Galdr have taught. Lawfulness, to never speak wrong justice and uphold righteousness, Honor, to do good and retain your name, Loyalty, to\n\nnever betray your friends and remain true to your kin and people, Family, for your blood is what flows in them as well as theirs flows in you, Truth, for you shall not speak lies as they have brought for the end of many a people, who were unwilling to see\n\nit. These five principles Stafyr held up high and induced them into his children as his father before him and his grandfather before him and all of his ancestry.For such the Almannir were given the ways of the Galdr, ancient but powerful ways.\n\n“Wenn mir nümma sen, denn sen ihr dia nöchschta um zum witrführa was dr Machr üs uferlet hot.”\n\nThose were the words of Obrma to Wealtfyr. A promise Wealtfyr has given to Obrma and which he promised his\n\nchildren would uphold from the first breath to the last of days and beyond. \n\nBut not alone the name it was, for the promise to be remembered, for the promise to be carried on. Prifyr left Stafyr the very crown of all the\n\nAlmannir, the simple crown of copper, embedded with one of the five gems of Himmlsbruck (S: still not sure, if this is a place), forged by the strong and gentle palms of Rugr, who saved Wealtfyr from his very demise at the same place.\n\nThe crown is to be worn by every true Altkönig, to lead their people and their blood through times of light and dark.\n\nSilus’ note:\n\nThe copper crown does actually exist from what I deem. I saw it upon Godwein’s head when I was a young boy and this aged, mushroom-covered gentleman was having a conversation with\n\nwith my uncle, the Emperor Godfrey. Curious, considering now that it is so old, perhaps it fields some kind of properties… magical perhaps. Curious, where the other four gems of the Galdr are. Ruby, Sapphire, Amethyst and Topaz.\n\nSaw that in some notes of Isovar.\n\nI best proceed with translating the upcoming chapters. It deems me that the other artifacts will get mentioned onwards. Tale of Thondor especially. I want to know how this falcon works..", ""),
        StaticBook("A book.", "§bJoe_Blackman", "Ah, Conjuration; the rarest Arcane Art known... Well, it won't be rare anytime soon. Of course, once you begin to learn the art, you will be reffered to as a \"Conjurer. A conjurer is an individual who access the Void and construct living organisms which\n\nare fueled wholly by the mana of their creator. Through the depths of thhe Void, a Conjuration user will be able to summon almight creatures and pretty flowers into reality. Alas, as a conjurer you will be constantly delivering your mana for virtually\n\nevery second your ersatz summon exists. You will soon come to a realisation that Conjuration uses the most of your mana unlike any other Arcane Science. In order to uphold the existance of your faux creature in reality, you must feed it precisely\n\na great portion of mana to flow within it. As the creature you summon will be downright complex, the process of building it within the Void will be rather tiresome and there is a good chance you may be drained completely of your mana until you reach\n\nunconsciousness, as tha thappens, your beast will be removed from the physical realm and be sent to Void. Yes, you can decide to desist the flow of mana beforehand, in which case the fauna will vanish to no consequence.\n\nNow, for you to construct an organism within the void, you must first have a sharp and great understanding of both the interior and exterior of the living entity you wish to formulate. This can be achieved by oftenly killing and dissecting the creature\n\nyou wish to summon. However, it is also best to keep very detailed anatomical diagrams of the beast you wish to conjure. Remember to have notes on the animal's exterior, interior and bone structure if you want to have an accurate understanding of it.\n\nIn the opaque void, the fabrics which generate the entity are summoned bone by bone, organ by organ and layer by layer the Conjurer crafts and sculpts their being into an exact copy of their previously existing self. As a result of poor research, the\n\nConjurer may fail at this point, producing a being unlike of its true and real form will result in an even and revolting entity which would certainly turn to a sludge once conjured. After a while of practice, the Conjurer would be able to summon the\n\ncreature exactly how it was before it was slain and have it formed with sheer stability. As it will behave akin to the life form it represents, it will follow its creator's commands.\n\nAs a Conjurer myself,  would highly reccomend you begin studying roses, then petite insects until you grow stronger and confident enough to move on to study and conjure anything larger.\n\nThink of Conjuration as art. You are the painter and the Void is the frame. What you paint in that frame will need to look beautiful and make sense in the judge's eyes. Bear in mind that the \"judge\" is the physical realm. If the judge thinks your work of\n\nart is good, it wll be acceped and be brought into reality. However, if it's horrible, it will be stamped on and crushed and it will appear as an abomination the mortal plane and you will be smakced in the face for your poor effort, that smack will tire\n\nyou. Keep practising and your artistic skills will improve and the judge will continue to accept your art. Overtime, your frame will expand (this, being your mana) and leave you open to produce larger paintings which the judge can view. Be warned though,\n\nthe larger the harder.\n\nAnd yes, you can produce hybrid fauna. I'll that for you to grasp the concept of that alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Borguk the Lazy", "§bZar'roc'Yar", "Azh upon a tik, there was an Uruk named Borguk. Borguk was a bub'hozh, yet lazy Uruk. He always wanted to have the easy way out.\n\nAzh day, Borguk was hungry, bub'hungry. He decided to go on a quick and easy hunt off into the Savannah\n\nSo there he sat, waiting, and waiting. Until he finally peeped a Jabbernak walking across the golden grasses of the Savannah. He peeped over the bushes and loaded a ligz into his O'lig.\n\nRight as he got a hosh shot, and was about\n\nto shoot, another Jabbernak came into view. Once the Jabbernaks met peeper to peeper, they began to stand off, then even klomp.\n\nBorguk decided to wait out the klomp, and wait for ash to flat, and then take that ash home to eat.\n\nIt didn't take long for ash of the bub'hosh Jabbernak to flat. Eager, Borguk hopped out of the bushes, going to tie up the flat Jabbernak, and haul it home. The living Jabbernak stomped on Borguk till he was flat, aswell.\n\nNub be lazy, learn from Borguk. \"Strength & Patience\" - Yar code", ""),
        StaticBook("An Ancient Tome", "§bThurak", "Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 17'th of The Deep Cold, 1486.\n\nThis book looks ancient, as if it predated the arrival of the Aegean Exodus to Asulon. It is filled with indecipherable texts and strange diagrams. While the text is unreadable, the pictures seem to show a method of golem creation.\n\nThe first stage of golem creation seems to be the creation of the core. The images show a block of gold held aloft by a being no dissimilar in appearance to a dwarf. It could possibly have been one of the race that built Karik. The picture also\n\ncontains what looks like a shaman of some sort, but definitely not one of dwarven descent. At the centre of the drawing is a bolt of unnatural looking lightning. It seems as if the Shaman is summoning the magical lightning to strike the core.\n\nIn the next diagram, the golden core and the dwarf holding it seem enveloped in some sort of field of lightning. A third diagram shows the dwarf holding the core, which is now transparent, with a mist swirling inside it. It is possible that this\n\nis making an impression of the dwarf’s essence and soul onto the core, rather than the crude rituals used in Aegis to transfer the soul entirely. Further on in the book, there is a diagram of a golden body being forged by the same dwarf\n\nthat held the core aloft. The anvil strongly resembles the anvil of Karik, albeit in better condition than the one in Karik today. The body  is far more intricate than the comparatively primitive golems of Aegis. The next diagram is a\n\ncross section of the golem. It seems to be made of several interlocking parts, all either forged or carved from what looks like no more than common ore or stone. In the centre of the body is a large central cavity. The final images show the craftsman\n\nplacing the core into the cavity, the body being enveloped in the magical lightning, and then the golem sitting up and looking at its creator. This book seems to confirm that the Ancients of Karik had the power to make golems, and used that power.\n\nGiven that golems have the ability to live almost indefinitely, this raises the question: Where are they all?", ""),
        StaticBook("Code of Chivalry", "§bJacob Chapel", "Knight's Code of Chivalry\nThe Knight's Code of Chivalry, as revised on the 7th of The Amber Cold, 1470, by Noble Ser Maric II Varodyr, the Winged Knight and scribed by Ser Akal Ipos.\n\nPrinted at 'Books of Oren', Petrus.\n\nA Knight shall live by honour, for glory, and guard the honour of fellow knights.\n\nHonour The Creator and maintain His Church.\n\nKeep the faith and act in righteousness.\n\nHe shall serve his liege lord valorously and with conviction.\n\nAnd persevere to the end in any enterprise begun and never turn his back upon an equal foe.\n\nA Knight shall refrain from the wanton giving of offence and despise pecuniary reward.\n\nGive succour to widows and orphans and regard the honor of women.\n\nHe shall offer that which is not needed, to those who are needy.\n\nAnd safeguard the helpless and uphold the weak.\n\nA Knight shall respect those placed in authority but fight for the welfare of all.\n\nAbstain from Injustice, cruelty and deceit.\n\nHe shall be vigilant and show courage, even in the face of evil.\n\nResolve not with swords what can be with words.\n\nAnd at all times speak the truth, even if faced with death.\n\nIn their blood the creator’s will shall be written.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro to Alchemy", "SapphireShard", "An Introduction to the Alchemist\nForward:\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities, and traditions.\n\nChapter 1: The Recipe for a good Alchemist.\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist; a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions.\nFor those who wish to follow\n\nthe noble path of an Alchemist, you must first consider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize\n\nthat it is simply an effort to save you. If you do not possess these qualities, dear reader, it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself or others.\nNow, allow me to go more in-depth about what\n\nthese traits mean, in order of their importance to an Alchemist:\nPatience. Alchemy, I'm afraid, is not a fast, nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time waiting for their alembic to boil so that the extract of\n\nyour ingredients may be collected for use, or simply waiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time it takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my\n\nopinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital to an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula- consisting of 25 'parts':\n7 parts waiting (brewing, waiting for the alembic's water to boil).\n5 parts setting\n\nup, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n5 parts testing (making sure your potion works).\n3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and\n\ncollecting the condensation using an alembic).\n1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely\n\ndull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated and rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish.\n\n\nSo, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\nCreativity. Please note, that I am writing here to explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something\n\ncompletely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in the art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There\n\ncomes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more explanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... There comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their\n\nown extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of their effects, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This is much more difficult than it may seem... But I shan't go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but\n\nrather, an introduction to the science.\nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone whom is impulsive and stupid... 'overly' enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of\n\nenthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience. Enthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... You are nothing, and you shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of\n\nthe list instead of the top, is simply because by reading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\n\nAn Introduction to the Alchemist Vol.II\nChapter 2: The Life of an Alchemist.\nThe Lifestyle.\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guilds need\n\nAlchemists, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the most fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted.\nAn Alchemist rarely stays in one\n\nlocation whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them. In my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one's options before taking a job. This\n\nis not to say that an Alchemist /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemist's choose a life of reclusion and introversion; preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency.\n\n\nAs an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and wounded. These paths will play a large roll in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one\n\nwho makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who creates healing syrums, as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means they are of no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company or guild.\n\nThis is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing much of their effectiveness, so all of the aforementioned employers could\n\nhave a use for an Alchemist of healing.\nDo not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however- and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of the science- think of it more as a specialization. I,\n\nfor example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions... Alchemist's Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries or small offensive guilds... even research companies.\n\n\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependant upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities, the life of an Alchemist is rarely dull, and, in my opinion, very fulfilling.\n\n\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\nMany jobs seem to have a set 'morality'. Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trustworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... The Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and\n\nis, much like one's business opportunities, dictated by the Alchemist's specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons, to fall into a darker more 'evil' morality, as they\n\nwould likely find their work with small groups of assassins or the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a 'good' morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people.\n\n\nThese are not set rules, of course, a healing Alchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is\n\nneutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist.\nThis section will be somewhat smaller, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist's abode will generally have only one constant; a\n\nlab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain an Alchemist's supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement... Well... The earth seems to be a\n\nbit more resistant to explosions that wooden or cobblestone walls.\nFarewell:\nI thank you, dear reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good eve, good day, and farewell.", ""),
        StaticBook("CH Handbook", "§bSaithor", "Introduction\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are a guild of Spellswords, Sellswords, Mages, and Scholars all alike, all seeking the same goal, knowledge, power, wealth, and fame.\nThe Hearts of this guild are brothers and sisters, bound by oath.\n\nPaths\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are divided into three categories. Knights, Mages, and Mechanists. No matter what path you pick, your brothers and sisters will protect you. And no matter what they pick, you will too.\n\nPeople of Honor\n-------------------Sonoren Klaren: He is the Ace of Hearts, our leader\nTalimeracahe: He is The Red Joker, second in command\nEdwyn Lynderly: He is the maker of the Crimson Hearth, the guild hall of the Crimson Hearts.\n\nTrainers o' the Paths\n-------------------Olympus: Trainer of the sword\nLelien: Trainer of the magic\nVirgo: Trainer of the Mechanists\nSaithor: Trainer of the bow and of the Realm\n\nRules\n-------------------1) Ye will protect your brothers and sisters\n2) You will obey all orders\n3) Knights will remain loyal\n4) Mages will heed to heal\n5) Mechanists will procede to prosper\n\nPath o' Knight\n-------------------The path of the Knight consists of the noble warriors of the Heart. They are the men and women who seek to be armed with a sword, those who know how to use one, and those who wish to know. They are loyal to the Hearts\n\nPath o' Mage\n-------------------The path of the Mage consists of the arcanic people of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the arts of magic. They heed to heal us, and will continue to do so.\n\nPath o' Mechanist\n-------------------The path of the Mechanist consists of the artisans and merchants of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the most money and fame they can get. They will procede to prosper.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeriels Teaching", "§bUncleUnicorn", "The Teachings\n        Of Aeriel\n   By: Varian Drake\n\nAeriel is all knowing, kind, wise, and pure. We mortals are sinful, inferior, negligent, and wicked.Some choose the path of destruction and misery. Others choose the path of wisdom and prosper-\n\nity. We periodically falter in the lines bound within our lives but we are persistent and willful. To understand Aeriel is to understand the world as a whole and the souls that inhabit it. The gift of happiness, of life, of beauty and serenity; All works\n\nof Aeriel from beyond, and her alone. With so much wonder and awe she conducts, it's no wonder that it shows through every day of the year. I however, have noticed the light diminish day by day. Little by little the torch starts to fade to the point where\n\nwe can't see it's full potential. Darkness starts to inhabit the torch, to breed and create an everlasting hatred within its flames. I see this torch daily with my own eyes you see. Whether it be war, thievery, or deception, darkness corrupts and does so\n\nwillingly among those who fall for it's idolized teachings. We can reverse these ideas however by acting more like our guide and teacher, Aeriel herself. Simply by helping those less fortunate land back of their feet or even saying no to taking part in a\n\n confrontation you don't believe in, we can potentially make this torch re-ignite for the better of humanity and take care of one another again. For we know deep in our hearts that the light will always prevail and display the true fact that darkness\n\ncould never be able to inhabit our existence. Each of us contain the torch but who will be the one who will keep it lit?", ""),
        StaticBook("Pale Crescent", "§bjdetterline", "The Order of the Pale Crescent\nLegitimized by King Heinrik\n \nPurposes\n \nThe Order has four major purposes that all of it's members abide to and strive towards. They are the following.\n\nI. Study the nature of supernatural and magical foes of the Kingdom and of all mortal races in order to increase combat effectiveness against them.\n\nII. Search for, acquire, and study artifacts or items with magical properties, being certain they never fall into hands that may abuse or misuse them.\n\nIII. Hunt down and eliminate or reform mages who violate the Tenets of the Pale Crescent. Mages receive a single warning before they are captured and reformed. A Mage who violates the Tenets after reformation will be hunted down and eliminated.\n\nIV. In the event of war or other international conflict, the Order will act in the interest of the Holy Kingdom of Oren first and foremost.\n\nThe Tenets of the Pale Crescent\n \nI. One may never use magic in combat unless life is at stake. Magic for utility is permissible, but ostentation is strictly forbidden.\n\nII. One may never teach practical magic to one the Order does not believe deserving or competent enough.\n\nIII. All who have the ability to use practical magic must make all of their personal information, including magical abilities, names, relationships and place of residence, available to the Order at will.\n\nVI. One may never practice magic with the intent of using it to do harm to innocents.\n \nV. None may share experimental or scholarly pursuits in magic to any outside of the Order. They can be shared freely within the Order.\n\nVI. One who uses practical magic and commits a capital offense in any nation, regardless of whether the offense was committed with magic, will be hunted and eliminated.\n\nVII. One who studies or practices dark magic, including necromancy must serve and live with the Order, or die.\n\nHierarchy and Prestige\nPrestige is a method used by the Order to record\neach member’s deeds and contributions to the Order.\n\nCommanders\n \nSovereign; Grandmaster of the order, handpicked by the previous Sovereign. Has complete autonomy over the Order, answering only to his legal superiors.\n\nConsuls; The Sovereign’s eyes, ears, and voice in his absence. All Consuls hold Sovereign authority when he is not present.\n\nOfficers\n \nCommandant; The sergeant and drill instructor of all able-bodied men of the Order, including Regulators and Artificiers.\n\nSteward; The economic administrator of the Order, handling matters of trade and resources.\n \nConciliator; May speak for the Order in matters of diplomacy when on official Order business.\n\nRegulators\n \nThose loyal and devoted (125+ Prestige) who follow the path of the blade. Regulators, as well as most men of the Crescent, are scholars as well as armsmen.\n\nArtificiers\n \nThose loyal and devoted (125+ Prestige) who follow the path of Magic. Artificiers are not only scholars of the supernatural, they are trained in the practical arts of magics of all kinds not considered heretical.\n\nArmsmen\nExecutors; The third rank for members of the Order, and last before they are either placed on either the Path of the Blade or the Path of Magic by command or by their choice.\n\nExecutors are expected to be considered veterans (75 Prestige Prerequisite).\n\nPracticioners; The second rank for members of the Order. At this rank the member swears an oath of their sword for the Order. They must be well trusted (25 Prestige Prerequisite).\n\nInitiates; A brand new members of the Order, yet to prove themselves at all. Swears no oaths.\n\nTo Apply to become a member of the Order of the Pale Crescent, come visit us in our town. Ask around, we are known by many. We walk tall wearing the large Pale Crescent on our tunics. Please bring a filled out application with:\n\nName: First and Last\nAge: Your age\nRace: Your racial origin\nNationality: Your country and culture of origin\nAmbition: Your reason for desiring to join the Order\nSkills: Any particular skills you may have.\n\nFeel free to come and talk with us and have us show you around.", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "§bJistuma", ">|<Monk>|<\n-=~Resurrection~=-\n\nIt is the salvation of many lives, but I wonder why I have seen nothing written on it. The monks, as is very well known, are able to save those that have passed away. While managing my stall at the sanctuary grounds I have been able to see for myself some\n\nof these happenings, or so I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike many others, is one I know very little about. Like all holy magics it seems to be manifested as a bright light, mostly used to heal those wounded. Besides the bright light, the monk performing it\n\nis praying to the Triumvirate. It appears to be like clerical healing, but it has other properties. Sometimes a monk arrives at the sanctuary a bit hurt after travels. It appears bandits and the like do not care that they are mugging what could be their\n\nsavior. What I have to say about those monks, is that unlike normal folk, their wounds heal faster. This is of course due to their magic, small flecks of light I have seen surrounding and healing the wounds. Then the monks are able to bring back the once\n\ndeceased fully mortal once more.\n\nThis is not to say they are necromancers. Those simply raise the dead, and they remain in a limbo state living and being deceased. The monks are able to bring the body and soul exactly like it was before the death, in\n\nnear perfect condition. From those I have talked to over the years in the Sanctuary, there is an always present effect of being saved. Present in all of those that I have seen, none have memories of their death or even of the events leading up to it.\n\nOther common effects are scars, sometimes showing how the poor soul met its end before, or of the tortures it passed. The ones that worry me the most is that sometimes the ones saved change… I have talked to some before and after saving, and changes can\n\nbe quite extreme. Some go crazy, others start to live in constant fear, some remain with pains in parts of their bodies. The changes they can go through are incredibly varied. I could conjure up reasons as to why that happens, all of them without means of\n\nproving so. I just believe death to be a terrible experience, that part of it continues on even after salvation.\n\nAnother interesting fact I have gathered, somehow by luck, is that the saved do not want to return to the location that they had\n\nperished. This particular thought came to me when one of the saved was hugged dearly by what I assumed was his lover. Before that, his body had been carried by another, a friend perhaps, and he and I had a chat about what happened. I knew of the exact\n\nlocation of his demise, and as him and the woman were moving away, he asked if they were passing through that exact area when returning home. With the confirmation of the woman, he started giving out other ways to reach their house. A big argument even\n\nhappened when the woman just wanted to go home as fast as she could with him, and he plainly refused to go through that area, which was the only road to their house. He didn’t know himself why he didn’t want to. Alas he returned to normal about half a day\n\nlater. Since then I started noticing other strange behaviors such as people staying in the sanctuary for longer times, not using their normal routes out of the sanctuary and returning shortly after leaving with a friend. I simply believe once more, that\n\nthe experience was so horrible, that those saved gain a subconscious fear of their death place. Besides, what would happen if they saw their own body? \n\nOn the mention of bodies, I do have to state as well, it is not necessary for the\n\nbody to be brought back to the monks for the resurrection. I have seen many monks bring bodies to the sanctuary, so I believe it might be quite easier with them. This is favorable, as in the lands of Anthos there are many evils. You can be decapitated,\n\neaten, thrown into lava, cut into little bits and drowned in the deepest of oceans. Your body may disappear and never been found once more, and you may this way still be saved. How they restore the body I do not know, and the monks seem not to answer when\n\nI ask them. They do answer a few questions. I learned, for instance, that the monks are neutral, and never take side in political views or wars. They also take this neutrality to those they save. I have seen those of evil whose purpose is to kill being\n\nsaved together with the children that never made any harm. This has brought problems to the monks before, many want others to remain dead.\n\nMost of the stories of the saved start simply with them explaining how they woke up in the monk’s care.\n\nSeems to always be the same as I stated. Some come back quite soon after their demise, already back before their friends and family run to the sanctuary to check, and others can take elven days. Yet this magic is not all powerful. As the monks mention,\n\nthey cannot save all. If the deceased does not walk out of the monks rooms an elven week after their death, they are forever lost. The same happens to those that take their own life. I believe that if they think that they don’t want to live anymore, then\n\nthey wouldn’t return to the land of the living.\n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals, they are those that save so many from their shortened lives.\n\n\n\nWritten by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452", ""),
        StaticBook("My wish!", "§bFaya", "My wish is to be a frost lady like Essa so we can be together and not make me wear gloves to touch her!", ""),
        StaticBook("Keep Walking", "Domainoft", "Keep Walking: A Tale of Truth by Silion Luthias\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\nVaehaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((8/28/13))\n\nHail friend, I am Silion Luthias, and I'm going to tell you a story. This particular story, happens to be one of great importance to me me, for it is the story\n\nof me, and my brothers. We've all been scarred, vruised, and crushed by the harshness of reality but, we've also all come together under odd circumstances, and have become traveling companions, and friends to the\n\nend. As I sit underground in my study, I look towards the future, for it's bright, and full of promise, and untold stories filled with adventure and hope. But, to look towards the future, you must keep the past in sight, so, to learn of our current\n\nadventures, you must know our pasts. :: There are 5 of us, Caden, Guraim, Gruol, Qwert, and I, Sillion. Each of us have tragedy in our past, but it has turned us into better people. First, we shall start with Qwert, one of two Dwarves in our party. ::\n\nQwert was born in the Farlands, a place I've yet to see His mother died during childbirth, and his father died in a fire, trying to save Qwert. From there, he was raised by a wolf mother, and her cubs, so, he was illeterate when he came to us. From\n\nthere, he moved onwards the Oren, and eventually was brought into our party via Caden, and here he resides still. :: Next, is Gruol, our Orc friend. Gruol was raised in the LOrcish fashion, but joined the Orcish Guard as a adult. But, during a routine\n\nsweep of the lands, the unit Gruol was placed in encountered a group of bandits looking for food amongst a group of homes. During the battle, most were slaughtered but, one of the humans in his teens started running. Gruol's captain ordered\n\nhim to hunt the boy down, and kill him. But, Gruol refused. :: Gruol was reported to The Rex, and was discharged immediatley . GRuol was shamed by his people, family, and country. So, he set off into the wilds, looking redemption, and riches.\n\nHowever, I found him, befriended him, and he travels with us as the group powerhouse, and is still looking to return his honor everyday. :: Now, we move on to my dear friend, Caden. Caden was the second member to join our party, and is our swordman.\n\nBut, his past is the most horrendous of all of ours, and it's time I document it for the world to know. Caden was raised in the Cathaldus Family, one of the most prestigous famlilies in Laurelin. He was taught sword fighting, archery, and perfect\n\nEnglish to name a few of the many privelges he had in his childhood. :: But, when he was quite young, he family adopted a young Orc child, I'Shaak. Caden was raised with him, learning from I'Shaak brutish capabilities, Caden became a force to\n\nreckoned with on the battlefield. However, I'Shaak caught a illness in his teen years, and died. THis gave Caden a respect for orcs, adn a hole in his heart, that has been left unfilled for too long. Then, in his first years of adulthood, a hit was\n\nordered upon his family. Caden was away, training with his blade, when his family was murdered in cold blood in their sleep. When Caden returned that night, exhausted from practice, he found his parents corpses strewn with blood and bile sliced open in\n\nplaces along their throats, chest, and stomach. But, to their dismay, a hred of clothing adorned the bedpost, plastered with blood. But, the true color still showed, purple tinged along the edges with green. It was the flag of a local mercenary company,\n\nand only their captain wore the colors. Sillion marched to the local fort his blade sharpened to a razor edge, and nothing but primal fury, and the lust for revenge swarming amongst his consicous. He trudged in, busting open the doors,\n\nand listened to the sounds of men rowdily drinking, laughing, and reveling in a well earned payment, most likley a very large one. Caden walked into the Main dininig hall, and stood, ready to charge. He ran his eye across the\n\nrows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. Caden drew in a breath, and screamed, \"YOU TOOK MY FAMILIES LIVES, I REQUIRE YOUR IN PAYMENT! YOU PATHETIC\n\nBLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!\" Caden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a hankerchief. He dipped the flailing hankerchief end into a torch, and hurled it onto the table, fire and glass flew around, men instantly went up in flames,\n\nsomefrom the initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb. amonsgt the chaos, most fled, or perished, but, the captain stood eyelocked with Caden. The captain brandished a beautiful gilded\n\naxe, imbuded with diamonds. The pair began stalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden's throat, but he deftly sropped, and instantaneously drove his blade into the captains right\n\nstomach, ripped the blade left, and stepped back to let his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. He looked up to Caden, blood seeping\n\nthrough his teeth, and whispered, \"Your father died in his sleep, but your mother was awoke by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. She squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like music\n\nto you, dagger-ear.\" Caden stared at him with pure fury, then raised his blade, and dropped it through the captains spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor. and landed amongst the pile of burnt bodies. Caden walked back to Laurelin, drenched in\n\nblood, dragging his blade, and staring into the distance, eyes blank. AS he entered, he prepared for a heros embrace, but was gripped by guards right away. They then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into\n\nprison for the murder of a entire company of mercenaries. As the men brought him through a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whos face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling lightly. Caden was jailed\n\nbut escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the wilds, crouching near a tree, holding a makeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. Once I got him eating, he told me this story, and I vowed I would help him find the\n\nmonster who hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 3", "§bArinislia", "Elven Lessons 3\n\nOriginally By: \nKalenz Unradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\n\nTo conjugate verbs in elven, one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated: \n\n-e - 1st sing\n\n-a - 2nd sing\n\n-e - 3rd sing\n\n-ae - 1st pl\n\n-an - 2nd pl\n\n-eyae - 3rd pl\n\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simply in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day.\n\nFor these two tenses, the following four words are used:\n\nKarin'ento- Next sunrise\n\nKarin'ante- Last sunrise\n\nKer'ento- Next sunset\n\nKer'ante- Last sunset\n\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are\n\nsimply added on the end of sentences to designate the tense. Ex. : Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night.\n\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech, these endings are often shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno, and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gruk'ku's Vyzh", "§bGruk'ku'Gorkil", "Frum Gruk'ku.\n\nDiz wil bi mi azh vyzh. Mi hef nevah mayd ah vyzh. Zo diz iz vi vyzh. Mi juzt vyzh fur teh urukz tu bi ztrung agein. Fur uz tu hef meny. Mi alzo vyzh fur mi tu git ah bone ztaff. Fur mi zhamanizm azh dat mi kannut luze.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wish", "§bAyche Raven'kor", "I wish for:\n\nMina\nFame\nPower\nMagic\nA bigger ship\n\n§II'd like to have an     adventure while fishing, I guess. Maybe a really big fish. Or a boot. Or a pair of boots. Or a shark. Food would be\n\nnice, too, I guess. I dunno.\n\nSigned,\n\nCaptain Ayche Raven'kor", ""),
        StaticBook("Embermoor", "§bThe Wanderer", "Embermoor is perhaps the most sinister regions of Athera. The swamp itself is only loosely connected to this realm, and the connection weakens as the moon rises. \n At night, vicious spirits attack travelers that are lost in Embermoor, possessing them, or\n\nworse. Necromancers stalk the swamp, preying on innocent travelers. Even the muck itself is hazardous, as it can drag a traveler under like quicksand.\n But perhaps most dangerous of all is the Necromatic Tower. In the dead center of Embermoor, many\n\nnecromancers reside there. The Tower is surrounded by dark ruins, all of evil origin. But, it is not the Necroamancers one must fear, nor the spirits of the dead. Nay, one should fear the Dread Knights in the Necromatic Tower, with their necromancer\n\nservants. \n Little is known of the Dread Knights, except they are all but immortal, and have a deep hatred for life and the living.\n Beware Embermoor, for those who enter shall never return!", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "§bRosso", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nElements of Alchemy\n\nVolume I-2 of V\n\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\n\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.” But what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is\n\nrequired before that question can be answered and in fact, if that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\n\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir and\n\nconcept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon. An ignorant outlook on this statement is that what is meant is the physical, literal meaning behind these elements but one must look into the symbolism, they must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into\n\neach of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual, may understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\n\nFire\n===\nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\n\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal. Fire can represent rage, anger,\n\nhatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will, and allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear\n\nat. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\nActions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action\n\nof burning, consuming, and destroying. Alchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon, but if\n\none were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos. It is true that Chaos is\n\noften something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized. Chaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and\n\npowerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick, two completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or\n\nsolely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used. The teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\n\nEarth\n===\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\n\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things, I will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\n\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength, the notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance, or\n\nstrength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion. Protecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also\n\nused in antidote potions, disease-curing potions, and, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders, often associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also\n\nrequired for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on. Many of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend, and using\n\nelements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation. Now, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon\n\ntransmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals, for metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\n\nWater\n===\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\n\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water. Often known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its\n\nname for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing, liquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on\n\ndrinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid, one must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\n\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life. But one\n\ncan also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic. Through oils, one may\n\nreap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made by distilling wine or other liquors.\n\nAir\n===\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\n\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception, and\n\neven flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes, the ways in which to represent Air are quite\n\nobvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion, are rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite\n\nrarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather, which is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions\n\ncentered around this element. Another, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and\n\nAir intermingle. With that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols, the next chapter will explain\n\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\n\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-2\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Death of Availer", "§bJosef Timothee", "THE DEATH OF THE\n WANDERING WIZARD\n\n\nOn Ahad, the 8th of the Deep Cold, 1336, the world of Aegis was struck by a terrible tragedy. I, Josef Timothee, record here my own experience during these events.\n\n\nI was in Al'Khazar when a voice rang out, filling all of Aegis. It identified itself as the Wandering Wizard. He said that he had three relics that needed to be taken to the Cloud Temple. If they were to fall into Undead hands, he claimed, terrible\n\ntrouble would result for the people of Aegis. He sent forth a cry over all the lands, asking for support on the journey from Al'Khazar to the Cloud Temple on the King's Road. A large crowd assembled with him in Al'Khazar, mostly humans but\n\nrepresentatives from other races there as well.\n\nThe procession headed down the King's Road and was immediately attacked. Lightning rained down from the skies, and monsters appeared out of thin air. But those in the crowd were ready, and struck back against Iblees minions. The monsters were defeated\n\nthrough sheer numbers of those opposing them, as well as the powerful magic of the Wandering Wizard. All along the journey, he kept up words of encouragement and urged the crowd onwards. The lightning and monsters were relentless, delaying\n\nthe journey terribly.\n\nBy the time the procession reached the Cloud Temple many had died trying to protect the Wizard en route. It was there that the Undead suddenly struck the most violently I have ever witnessed, not only casting lightning powerful enough\n\nto damage the Cloud Temple, but also changing the landscape around it to look like the Nether. Among this, explosions and lightning were striking everywhere, causing great suffering. The Wizard urged all present to take shelter in the Cloud Temple.\n\nI took this advice, having been clipped by lightning and set ablaze. Once inside, the extent of the damage was clear. Hundreds entered the Temple, many wounded by burns or monsters. The Temple shook as explosions rocked it from outside and pieces of it\n\nbroke off. Then...\n\nA new voice rang out, saying that the Wizard had been slain by the Undead. The outpouring of grief was immediate, and the attacks on the Temple ceased.\n\nSomeone shouted that the Undead had taken three objects from the Wizard that looked like eggs. The skies lightened, the landscape changed back, and the crowd left the Temple. But the world was altered permanently with the death of the\n\nWandering Wizard. It remains to be seen what the Undead will do with the stolen relics.", ""),
        StaticBook("Glee", "§bBarry Winterleaf", "Dedicant: Glee\nDate: 24/8/2015\nGuide: Barry\n\nTask: Druidic ranks\n\nSeek out those within the order with different ranks, interview them over tea and learn their duties within the order.\n\n*Barrys Signature*\n\nTask: Gather three which represent the aspects.\n\nAfter a lesson on the aspects, go out and find things you believe represent them and why.\n\n*Barrys signature*\n\ntask: Craft a staff\n\nTake a branch your tree gifted you and make a staff.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eye Transplant", "§bLaurinia", "12th of The Amber Cold 1479\n\nI was walking down the stone road when i was approached by a man in long dark robes. He said he had watched me care for my blind partner Sarai and asked if i was interested in learning how to heal people.\n\nOf course i agree'd with him and so now i am in his office learning how to recconect nerves. Specifically i am learning to recconect nerves in the eyes.\nMy teacher constantly has his hood up not once yet have i seen his face. However i presume he is an\n\nelf as we practice on nature, animals, and he has two small points in his hood.\n\n11th Malins Welcome\n We've been going over simple things for a few days now... I can now confidently heal nerve endings back into a working condition.. All we need now are a\n\npair of eyes for Sarai, its just finding a volunteer\n\n7th First Seed 1480\nLast night we attacked our target.. A middle aged women in which we stole the eyes of... Eyes which will now haunt me for the rest of my life.. .The vibrant blue colour of them\n\nstick with me and haunts me at night but they are soon to be my wifes. I guess over time ill adjust to them.\n\n13th First seed\nSarai can see it was a success", ""),
        StaticBook("my wish", "§bIyath the Toymaker", "I wish that I can be a master of the magic type Transfigureaton, or have a teacher that will stay and teach me.. thank you!\n\n-Iyath", ""),
        StaticBook("Honeysuckle Sun", "§bIndra Tresery", "Glistening, molten gold stares back as I\nlook up into your face, the feeling of warmth\nfills my soul with every breath.\nYour arms wrap me in layers of sweet\ncomfort and I close my eyes\nreveling in your warm golden touch,\nmy troubles forgotten.\n\nYour smile bathes my skin in light\nand I shiver from excitement, returning \nyour attention with delighted smiles and \ncarefree laughter.\nDuring times of trouble I could stay\nall day in your embrace, letting my\n\nfears and worries melt away \nwith one smile from you. \nThere are times I want to keep you to myself,\nto hide you away in our own little world forever, \nbut I cannot, your smiles and sweetness are\nnot just for me.\n\nThat worries me not, my love.\nFor I know that few moments a day we spend\nin each other’s embrace, that I am yours\nand you are mine:\n\nMy warm honeysuckle sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Back Into the...", "§bMonk Scribe", "Back Into the Light\n\nI remember\nOf what I said\nduring that weary, dreary, stormy night.\nThe Undead\nyou see.\nThey are here\nand there\nand well,\nalmost everywhere.\nOne for as far as I\n\ncan see.\n\nSkirmish here\nto Skirmish there.\nTheir magic never goes.\nFrom their Golden hoes,\nto their Undead robes,\nOf what\nthe World foretold.\nI see an opportunity\nto all.\n\nall who intend to join.\nFor it is\na chance.\nBack\ninto the light.\n\n- Written in Aegis by an unknown author.", ""),
        StaticBook("Le Clique Wish", "§bCery'lin", "100000 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("A wish..", "§bEnedor Pastly", "A teacher of fire Evocation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wish for a Well", "§bVondan Frostbeard", "Wealth in the form of coin", ""),
        StaticBook("A wish.", "§bElvira Mantisuku", "Wish\n~~~\n\nI wish for a white horse and a huge happy halloween to all around.\n\n- Elvira Mantisuku\n(Farryn)", ""),
        StaticBook("Fairy Ring", "§bKyral Rilann", "The following is from myself, Kyral, and my time spent meditating in a fairy circle.\n\nThese are the three days of this task.\n\nDay one\n\nSitting  in the tree when the all familiar humming noises filled my senses, it felt overwhelming, but I tried and tried to stay in as long as I could, focusing on the humming for as long as I could. Was I incomfortable? or\n\nwas it just the noise getting to me? At least this was my first time in, I had plenty of time to get used to such noises.\n\nI figure it will be easier the more I go in, but I need to pace myself, I feel a woman could go a little crazy if left inside that\n\nFairy ring for far too long. Did I mention it was hard resisting the urge to dance? I never dance and I felt myself wanting to do it more and more.\n\nI don't like dancing.\n\nDay two\n\nI easily entered the circle, finding it much easier then the last to meditate with my eyes closed. It was more amazing to focus in the humming I heard with my other senses, a whole new experience that left me more amazed at\n\nthis mystical ring, I can't comprehend the things I heard, but I think its the forest.. doing something.\n\nAs for leaving the circle, I left with only slight issues, having to get back in for this book, but I looked around the whole grove for signs of\n\npeople, and I skipped around the fairy circle.\n\nIt was amazing I felt, relieved. I hated to dance but it was just skipping, and I felt so much better.\n\nDay three\n\nThis day was one of the more amazing, I meditated after having had a long talk with one of my former Scions, talking about what I did and redemption. Having been calmed by that chat, I walked back into the fairy ring.\n\nI was not ready and i did not expect to hear what I did. It was like the Pulse of the realm was guiding itself to me, I felt everything moving and coming towards me, Meditating was hard, but i managed to keep it going, remembering my times as a Cleric and\n\nMage to keep me going, to focus on one of those feelings, one of those pulses of life.\n\nI almost did it, but I felt my thoughts filling my mind with crazy reasoning, and I needed to get out. This wasn't a safe day to be inside the circle. I feel that I am\n\ngetting closer to understanding the way the realm works, but I might be wrong, this Fairy circle continues to bring new and new things to me to realize, that the realm is forever changing.\n\nI skipped around the circle again, and stopped it at that.\n\nThis would be my final day, but I expect to be asked to meditate here from time to time.\n\n*The following pages\nseem to be sketches slid into the book*\n\n*A large Rainbow tree seems to be cut by a figure in this one, the top half of this page\ndepicts this.\n\nWhile the lower half depicts the tree igniting, leaving scrambled markings on the ground /#&!(@/ *\n\n*Another sketch seems to be the apple, blue in color being picked from the still standing rainbow tree, a hand extending to it as if this was a panel by panel sketch. but it stops there.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking V2", "§bLillian Hill", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Basic Cooking V.2\n   Soups And Stews.\n          \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   <><><><><><><><><><>\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n\nFor each of these recipes a bowl will be needed. These can be easily brought from most stores, or if you feel skilled enough, easy to carve yourself from wood. This is the second installment of the 'Basic Cooking' books.\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~Sailor's delight~~~\nIngredients: A cooked fish of your choice. \n\nAdd a small amount of water to your cooking pot, and allow it to warm. Meanwhile, finely dice your fish, making sure to skin and bone it, removing the head. Place\n\nthe chunks of fish in the hot water, and allow it to reach boiling point. At this point, you may feel free to add herbs or salts of your choice, such as tarragon, dill weed or basil. After the broth has boiled for half an elven hour, take a ladle and pour\n\nit into a bowl, taking care not to spill any of the liquid, as it may burn. Fish are an easy ingredient to attain, making this the perfect recipe for an easy and cost effective meal that would satisfy the hunger of your whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Mushroom Stew~~\nIngredients:\nOne red browncap shroom.\nOne brown browncap shroom.\n\nTo start with, add a large quantity of water to your cooking pot, lighting your fire underneath the\n\ncauldron of water. As the water warms, peel your mushrooms of the top layer, as this allows for flavour to soak into the water. Then continue to slice your mushrooms into a few reasonable size chunks. After the water has started to bubble, throw in the\n\nmushrooms, adding some salt and perhaps some butter or lard, if you have the resources to do so. Allow the mushrooms to cook, stirring the broth occasionally. Once the mushrooms have coloured slightly, and the aroma begins to fill the room, ladle the stew\n\ninto a bowl. An easy recipe, as this type of fungi are commonly found in the wild, or can be bought from a store. This recipe makes enough for one person, though can be easily changed to make enough for the whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Chicken Stew~~~\nIngredients:\nOne large piece of roat chicken.\nStart by lighting your fire and pour some water into the cooking pot to halfway, allowing it to heat and boil. Take the chicken and remove the skin. Then, make sure to\n\ncut it into bite size chunks, making sure to carefully place them in the cooking pot to avoid the splashing of water. After doing this, allow the chicken to cook before adding any extra vegtables. Once the chicken has browned further and the aroma fills\n\nthe room, remove the pot of broth from the heat and pour into a dining bowl. Allow to cook slightly before eating.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ <><><><><><><><><><><>\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pork Soup~~~~\n\nIngredients: \nCooked Pork\n\nStart off by lighting your fire and heating your cauldron, before placing the cooking pot over the boiling water. This creates a Bain Marie.\n\nAfter doing this, fill your cooking pot halfway with water. Next, slice up the pork, removing the fat. Place the slices into the cooking pot with salt and rosemary or sage. Stir the soup occasionally. After leaving it to cook for about half an elven hour,\n\nremove the bowl from the heat. Pour the soup into a serving bowl, though allow it to cool as the water would be boiling.\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Vegtable Soup~~\n\nIngredients:\nTwo baked potatoes. \nFour carrots.\n\nCreate the Bain Marie once more and add your cooking pot. Fill the cooking pot with warm water to about\n\na quarter of the way. While the water is warming, slice your potatoes into chunks, and add them to the water. Next, cut your carrots into thin round disks. Add these to the water. If you wish, salt and rosemary can be added to give the soup some seasoning\n\nand flavour. Soon after, remove the cooking pot from the heat. Pour the contents into a serving bowl. \n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("What is love?", "Mririshboys", "What is love?\n\n-------------------\n\nLove?\n\nWhat is love?\n\nMerely an entertaining hobby?\n\nOr merely just something to produce the next generation?\n\nOh how?\n\nHow do you love?\n\nHow do you get\n\nThat tender\n\nPassionate\n\nThumping\n\nSpeeding\n\nHeartbeat?\n\nFrom the long told fairy tales.\n\nWhat of the intense burning inside?\n\nThat were told by old couples.\n\nDoes love deserve your undivided attention?\n\nWhat is love?\n\nWhen one has not yet experienced?\n\nOr is it a simple personal journey\n\nThat everyone will pass one day?", ""),
        StaticBook("TOP-SECRET #001", "§bNydari Angroth", "CLASSIFED\n   INFORMATION\n\nKnown members of the Society of Snakes, as of the 10th of the Amber Cold, 1474:\n\nEliza\nMithius Dalma\nDahk'Kaan\nViolet Randuins\nViro\nSeiya Katashi\nAdam Grey\n\nVinnie the Chef\nArtemis Tenebris", ""),
        StaticBook("Seasons Vol. II", "SapphireShard", "I gripped my blade tighter the fools not knowing I was the Grand Knight of Oren, The second hand of the Emperor. I raised my blade in the air shouting “I am No Lordlin’ I am The one who sends ye to the nether!”\nWe clashed for almost an hour the two\n\nbeing better taught then I thought. I looked at my shield arm seeing it was gone turning my gaze to the Half-Elven man he was gripping his shoulder remaining silent as usual blood trickling down his fingers from the gash on his shoulder I left. As the\n\nHuman Bandit raised his blade once again to strike down at me I met his blade with mine and parried the blow. As I looked to my side the Half elven man was charging his blade held high. As he done so I took a position of the Upper hand Snake guard. As\n\nhe went to strike for my head my blade fell into his gullet I twisted and turned the blade as I let go of it the Half elven man now dying on the floor. His Ally shouting in rage as he raised his blade at me.\nI could do nothing but take the blow and\n\ntook a strike in the side of my chest grunting and looking at the man. My sight flashed and the next thing I knew, was an untameable amount of rage and fury. As I raised my hand and dashed to grab the man's face. He barely only six feet tall while I was\n\na full seven and no seeing my hand coming I grabbed his face shouting in rage words I do not even remember. But what I do remember is sticking my metal covered finger into his eye sockets and jaw. And applying all the force I have ever mustered in my\n\nlife to crush his skull. I remember hearing his cries of mercy, help, and agony. But I did not care I continued to do so until I heard a “Crack” and the bandit stopped moving and blood came out of his skull like a crimson creek. I stood for a\n\nmoment taking my Sword and shield into hand again. Only to collapse to my Knees looking down to the Merchant, and his wife the two happy yet horrified. I simply kneeled in blade my side bleeding as the couple got up and ran home.\nThat day will haunt\n\nme, and so will many others when unspeakable amounts of fury and rage took over cause of the scars you cause. You would simply burn with your cold, heartless, selfish burning winters. I continued my normal duties and tasks while\n\nslowly, all by myself I slowly slipped into a rage filled insanity. Only to be temporarily saved by the sudden doom of Asulon. The duty to save the Emperor, the Empire and its people and the little family I had left of my Brother. Before I knew it I\n\nwas on a boat the H.M.S Godfrey the II the Emperor of the Horen Seas. And we sailed for weeks only to reach a small Island where we are at now. Without you... As I continued to do my duties things calmed down, the settlement was built, the people,\n\nemperor and such were safe. And once again I began my decedent to the insanity of rage.\nBut as I could feel it taking over she appeared. An Old friend and ally she greeted to me looking different in much more different garbs she would wear.\n\nAnd told me of the tale of her banishment of her homeland and of the things she did to try to keep her people and families safe. I felt bad for her, an old friend of mine and told me of many pains, and sorrows we shared and all I could do is do what I\n\ncould do for any friend, offer them shelter and such. She took the offer but was not happy with it seemed. My days continued as normal as hers did and once again I had the annoyances of my Uncles wishes for me began courting again. I could feel\n\na breaking point coming...when it would happen though I did not know. Trying to stop my rage I sparred with the Recruits, friendly orcs, and fought the Hordes of Pigman until my body gave out. But still I felt the rage consuming my mind and heart.\n\n\nAs time went by I sat the edge of my bed several conversation went past on people telling me I am not the rage filled, half blood, oaf and monster many and myself claim for me to be. And how I told them they were wrong. These thoughts stung\n\nthe most but as I thought my Squire came in silently and gave me a notice. And left without a word I was curious to why he would do so and I took the letter and My eyes widened and began to be full of tears and I let out a shout of rage....and Sorrow.\n\nThe letter spoke of my Older brother, Duke Nicholas Silverblade the first. The only part of my family that is not extended and who truly cared for me was dead.\nI felt the breaking point coming I was about to go beyond a point of no return I looked for\n\nmy blade as I heard someone walk in their voice, gentle, calming and friendly. It was my friend I gave aid to. Her emerald green eyes, silver hair that flowed as if it was wind and her smooth and perfect colored skin. “U...Uthor? Are you alright, what\n\nhappened?” She walked over slowly sitting next to me looking me me worried. At first I pondered why one with her beauty would worry about a monster as Me but I told her the fate of my brother, and the last ten years of sorrow of the\n\ndeaths of my family members and loved ones. She shaked her head sighing “I am so sorry Uthor, but at least you can hope they are in a better place” I simply nodded to her “Aye, Elene I can.... But now my family is doomed” She tilted her head looking at\n\nme “How so?” I looked at her with a slight annoyance as I told her this a time before “I am a Half blood, a giant of one, an oaf and a monster of rage and now its is my duty to make sure I have heirs to carry on my brother , fathers and grandfathers\n\nlegacy. Who on earth would try to love one of me?”\nShe blushed slightly and reached for my hand grabbing is softly speaking as gentle as her grasp. “W...w....I...Would Uthor.” I looked down at her looking shocked and surprised. I\n\nremained speechless as I felt some of the rage, fury and sorrow slowly leave as I pondered is the emotion that drove me to this my savior as well? As I remained speechless her face reddened even more looking down and letting go of my hand “I...I am\n\nsorry Uthor...I Did-” I chuckled and took her hand back. “Elene, I have told you of what I am, if ye are willin’ to try to love such as me, I will not deny one as beautiful and carin’ as ye” as I said those words I already felt more....calm. She smiled\n\nand wrapped her arms around me resting her head upon my shoulders. And now once again I feel like the one I wished to be and I have hope for myself, my Family and my House. And this time I will not let anyone tear it away from me.\n\n\nI Roy Uthor Silverblade, First of my Name, Grand Knight of Oren, Lord of House Silverblade and now I guess...Duke of Furnestock. Can say I have returned from my trip from insanity and I am ready to do my duties and defend the Children of Horen\n\nand their allies. The Seasons have changed and so have I, I am ready for the new foes and allies to come now.\nFor Winter Silverblade, in her memory, for there is nothing left of her spirit in this world.\n~Roy Silverblade", ""),
        StaticBook("Kairn's Wish", "§bKairn Calithil", "I wish people liked me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Illusion of Time", "Minuscule_Evil", "The Illusion\n      of Time\n\n    Author Unknown\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nTime, what is it? To answer this question simply, it is an illusion. But how? What qualifies time as an illusion? Time does not exist, it is only man’s interpretation of how the universe flows and acts.\n\nTime is traditionally broken up into three parts: past, present and future. What is perceived as the past is anything that has previously occurred. What is present in whatever our conscious minds are currently experiencing.\n\nWhat is the future is what will occur. The past, present and future are perceptions. All that we see is our perceptions of the universe around. As said earlier: past, present and future are just ways of perceiving the universe.\n\nTherefore time is an illusion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Impure Love", "§bHileia'elr", "----Impure Love----\n\nWritten by Hileia'elr\n\nA romance novel of two Mali, coming from two very different backrounds.\n\nI was ready to leave Haelun'or for the first time in my life. Through my childhood, my parents kept me hidden from the outside world. In uncommon circumstances, I would be allowed to travel to the docks to view the ocean, but that was it.\n\nMost of my time was spent with my teachers, and I learned about science. I didn't dislike the subject, it just didn't quite suit me. Instead, I wanted to be one of the guards, as a sword in my hand was one of the best feelings I've ever experienced...\n\nHowever, once I was old enough, I wanted to explore the realm.\n\nI walked up the steps, towards the large gate. A Mali'ame stopped me. \"State your name, race, and business, Mali.\" he said. He was dressed in a green armour, with yellow trims.\n\n\"I am Elsil'ceru. I come from Haelun'or, and I come to Laureh'lin seeking supplies.\" My answer seemed to satisfy the guard, and he let me through. As I looked around, I saw Mali'Ame everywhere. I wasn't used to large crowds, so I rushed over to the side.\n\nI just simply wanted to escape the large, noisy streets filled with Elves and other beings. As I attempted to sit down, my foot caught on the corner of a nearby table, and I fell over. With me now on the ground, the large group of people stared at me.\n\nThey all looked at me as if they've never seen a boy on the ground. I stood up, and I felt fine... but my clothing was dirty. This was my largest concern. What if another High Elf was here? I would become a laughing stalk.\n\nI quickly ran into a nearby tavern. As I walked in, the girl behind the bar counter greeted me with, \"Karin'ay-\" but stopped short when she saw how dirty I was.\n\n\"Do you have a washroom available?\" I asked her. She pointed to a door in the back.\n\nNow cleaning up my clothes in a cauldron, I was looking around for something to dry off with. Turning around, I saw that the door was open. Another girl with purple eyes glanced at me, surprised, and she asked, \"Why are you in MY washroom?\"\n\nI didn't know what to say. I was in this girls private living space, using her supplies.\n\n\"Well, you see... the girl at the counter allowed me to clean up in here...\" She gave me a half smile, and allowed me to continue.\n\nUpon re-entering the tavern, I apologized to both girls, and explained the situation. \"That's fine,\" the girl at the counter said. \"We're happy to do whatever we can...\" She then proceeded to examine my hair and eyes closely. \"You aren't from Laureh'lin.\"\n\n\"No...\" I said. \"I'm from Haelun'or, this is my first time outside the walls.\" The second girl with purple eyes raised her eye brows. \"That makes two of us.\" she exclaimed. \"My name is Sioln'ker, and my friend is Talia'lir. She runs this tavern, I just\n\nfetch supplies for her.\"\n\n\"So you're a High Elf, then?\"\n\n\"Yes...\" she replied, \"but I left the Mother City when I was young to come here, and live with the Mali'Ame.\"\n\nI began to introduce myself as well.\n\n\"I am Elsil'ceru. I'm visiting this city in search for supplies not found in Haelun'or.\"\n\n\"What might you need?\" Asked Sioln'ker. \"We might have it in the storage room.\"\n\n\"I need some sticks, iron, and paper, if I can find them.\"\n\n\"Well, I know we have sticks somewhere. Follow me.\"\n\nAs the two of us entered the basement, there were boxes scattered around the floor. While she looked for my requested supplies, I began to ask, \"Why flee the Mother City for this tavern?\"\n\nI expected her to change to some dramatic, or nostalgic expression, but she remained neutral.\n\n\"Not enough living space there.\" She replied. \"While I did get a good education there, and I was very happy, it was far too chaotic there for me. The small\n\nrooms became an issue. I'd much rather live in an actual house. Plus, all the Mali there aren't accepting of anyone shy of perfection. So, I moved here, where I didn't have to follow proper manners all the time.\"\n\nI began my counter argument.\n\n\"But why live with another race? Surely, one of your status deserves to be with other Puritans, and not... Wood elves.\"\n\nShe raised her brow at me. \"Ah, I see... you're one of those ignorant and closed-minded Mali...\"\n\n\"Well, that's only because we ARE superior to every other race. I wouldn't say such things if it weren't true.\" I replied. \"We look beautiful, and we're well educated, unlike some of the other barbaric races.\"\n\nSioln'ker sighed at Elsil'ceru's response. \"Here, I found some sticks. Take them and go.\" she said. She then forced a bundle of sticks into my hands.\n\nWhile in the High Elven culture, it is normal to declare your own race\n\nsuperior to others- Yet, it also wasn't a young man's place to upset a lady such as herself.\n\nRunning up the stairs, sticks still in hand, I opened the door at the top of the small staircase and witnessed an\n\nalmost empty tavern. The only ones in the room were two guards sipping their drinks in the back, and Talia'lir, standing at the counter. She glanced at me and said, \"Sioln stormed out. What happened in the basement?\"\n\nTrying to think of a response, I quickly lied. \"She tripped, and stubbed her toe. I offered to take a look, but she said that she would go to a nearby doctor.\"\n\nTalia glared at me. \"Liar.\" she declared. \"There's no doctor on this side of the city.\"\n\nBlushing, I then told the truth. \"Ok, so I may have insulted her unintentionally, reguarding her... race...\"\n\n\"You brought up her leaving the Mother City, didn't you?\" she replied. \"You should at least have more manners than that, being a Puritan...\"\n\n\"I know...\" I responded. \"I want to find her and apologize.\"\n\nTalia forced a half smile. \"That wouldn't be a smart idea. She tends to be quite violent when upset. And she keeps a steel dagger in her boot all the time for protection, so you might want to\n\nstay clear of her until she's recovered.\"\n\nI just stood there, unsure of what to say. \"When can... Uh...\"\n\nTalia looked at me, confused.\n\n\"When, uhm... When can I apologize to her?\"\n\nTalia placed her elbow on the table, and her chin resting on her hand, smiling. \"We're closing in an hour, but come back by sunrise. She'll be here, ready for work. We won't be open, but I'll let you in before work hours.\"\n\nI let out a long sigh and\n\npacked my belongings.\n\n\"I suppose I'll be off, then.\"\n\nExiting the tavern, I noticed a sign on the side of it.\n\n\"Welcome to the Emerald Crescent!\"\n\nRight. The Emerald Crescent, I thought to myself. I'll return here after sunrise.\n\nAs it was now night, the streets were almost abandoned, with few night dwellers roaming the streets. I had on my expensive High Elven travel clothing, so I needed a roof to\n\nsleep under. But I wondered where that might be... I noticed several small shops outside the tavern, one was marked, \"Under renovation.\"\n\nThe tarp that was meant to go on the top of the shop lay there on the ground, so I used this as a blanket.\n\nDrifting off into sleep, I hoped that I wouldn't be mugged in the night.\n\nThankfully, the next morning, I woke up, unharmed and with all my belongings. I proceeded to walk the path to the tavern. As I was walking along the road, I figured that this city\n\nwasn't as horrible as I made it out to be.\n\nNow, almost to the tavern, I began climbing the stairs. In the window, I saw Talia cleaning the counter. That's when I heard a scream.\n\nThe scream came from behind the tavern. With no time to think, I\n\nsprinted around the side of the building to see two Valah and Sioln- One was holding her, and the other had a dagger out.\n\n\"Stay still, you greedy Mali!\"\n\nThey were obviously mugging her, simply because she was a High Elf.\n\nI was skilled with a sword, but had little to no training with hand to hand combat. However, it was my only option.\n\nSprinting into action, I went for the one with the dagger first. I hooked his ankle with my foot, bringing him to the ground.\n\nI stole the dagger, and gave him a boot to the face, rendering him unable to fight properly. With his ally on the ground, the other thug released Sioln and drew his own dagger.\n\n\"Kid, why don't you piss off before you get hurt?\" He said in a raspy voice.\n\nI smiled. \"I'd much rather take my chances.\" I said as I lunged towards his chest.\n\nHe failed miserably at blocking my blow, and fell to the ground, a dagger now in his torso.\n\nSioln rushed over to me with a smile.\n\n\"Thanks... they were trying to take my necklace.\" she said.\n\n\"Enough of that!\" I screamed back. \"I have to apologize to you... I can barely see as to how I could have been so ignorant. You were right, other races are intelligent... in fact, my own race is\n\nprobably the most stupid, for being so unaccepting and ignorant of foreign ideas...\"\n\nSioln stood there in awe. She didn't expect this type of reply at all.\n\n\"However... I don't take back what I said about High Elves being the\n\nmost beautiful.\"\n\nSioln began to make a pouting face.\n\n\"Because...\" I began again, \"you're the most beautiful person I've ever met, and no other race is superior when it comes to your attractivness...\"\n\nShe blushed, and took my hand into hers...\n\n\"If you could forgive me,\" I stated, \"I want to be just like you, and leave that dreaded city. This life seems far more like the one I would favor, over my life back in the Mother City.\"\n\n\"So, what you mean is...\" she began. \"What you're implying is that... you want to be wed?\"\n\nAll I did was smile. I said nothing, but she understood completely.\n\n\"Ok then, we'll get married soon...\" she said.\n\n\"Why not right in the tavern?\" I said with a sarcastic tone. She chuckled. \"That's not quite romantic enough, is it, Elsil?\" she replied.\n\nI swooped her off her feet. \"There's only one way to find out.\" I said.\n\nThe very next morning, it seemed as if the entire tavern was filled with not only Wood elves, but my own friends who had come all this way. Talia was in a long, flowing white dress. She leaned over and whispered to me, \"You look rather dashing. Nervous?\"\n\nI chuckled. I looked down at the blue robe I was wearing, along with the red undershirt. \"Of course I am.\" I began. \"But I'd bet anything she's just as nervous as I.\"\n\nJust then, a tall, marvelous figure walked through the door of the tavern.\n\nA tall, beautiful, slender, marvelous figure indeed. Sioln had on a long flowing green dress that didn't match my outfit at all.\n\nIt had just occurred to me that this was not a traditional wedding at all. But I didn't care. I was still getting married.\n\nStanding at the front of the tavern, we joined hands, and the ceremony had started.\n\n\n\nAnd so did our new lives.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wizard's Wish", "§bCecil", "Wishes are simply that. Wishes.\n\nHowever for the sake of holiday cheer.. That and I have been stuck in this blasted maze for over a day now..\n\nMy WISH is for the Pumpkin Crown. - Cecil, the Wizard\n\nP.S - I am lost.", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Lefor", "§bRosso", "Lefor was born into a normal dwarven family. His father worked in the mines, His mother at home. Lefor was raised in the mines as he helped his father there from a young age. When he came of age Lefor told his father he wanted to be more than just a miner\n\nHe wanted to serve his king by joining the army. Lefor’s father was stubborn but eventually let Lefor join a training camp, sending him off with the family armor and axe. Lefor had a hard time at the camp, he was smaller than many of the others but he\n\nstrived to be the best, and so he did after much hard work he finished training and was made sergeant of the battalion.\nBefore the beginning of the great War between the Orcs and Dwarves, tensions were high and there were many skirmishes between both race\n\nThe Orcs were bloodthirsty and hungry for land and the Dwarves had expanded very close to the orcish border. Neither the Warlords of the Orcs or the High Council of the Dwarves could maintain peace and so the war began. In the early stages of the war,\n\ndwarven losses were high and they slowly retreated. It was at the small village of Kas-Grit that Lefor and his men were stationed to protect the villages whilst they gathered their items in preparation to seek refuse in the Capital. On the final day\n\nbefore they were to head to the capital a great horde of orcs attacked, the villagers fled in panic and Lefor and his men fought their best to contain the great horde but the orcs were too many and Lefor gave orders to retreat and protect the villagers.\n\nLefor however did not leave, he told his men that he was going to hold back the orcs as long as he was able. The orcs attacked again and again but Lefor kept them at bay and so he slew many orcs fighting them in the narrow alley ways of the village.\n\nHowever Lefor finally tired and was cut down by the orcs and his head put upon a spike.\nThat day Lefor saved many dwarves and because of his bravery the king and council made him a Paragon. To be worshipped along with the stones of the earth. Lefor’s\n\nfamily were made nobles and his bloodline still survives in many dwarves. Lefor is seen as the incarnation of bravery, sacrifice and warrior-hood.\nEven today many warriors pray to Lefor before battle. So is the story of Paragon Lefor.\n\nParagon Lefor\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVearHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Anne's Diary", "§bAnne Winter", "Anne's Diary Entries\n-------------------http://tinyurl.com/Annewinter\n-------------------*The book looks to be a few years old, with some pages ripped out and others remaining almost in a perfect condition. The front cover of the diary is a snowflake-\n\n-but you can see that the symbol as been tampered with in an attempt to scratch the symbol off. The first few pages are completely missing and not until about page eleven there is text that you can read. The text is written with a curvy font. There are a-\n\n-few pages that stands out from the rest and would be easily noticed. Some entries are smaller than others and some can be several pages long, some even just a word. This diary contain some sensitive things and some less sensitive thoughts. It is filled-\n\n-with the emotions Anne has and her thoughts but also things that has happened to her recently or in the past.\n\n(( If you find this book please do not destroy it, putting a lot of work into this ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Squid", "§bMonk Scribe", "Tales of Squid\n\nOne of the most common creatures, squid are known to have existed in early Aegis and clear to modern day. They live among fish in water sources, including rivers, seas, oceans, ponds and even swimming pools. This\n\nmakes squid among the most adaptable aquatic animals.\n\nSquid are very peaceful and do not attack back it struck. The only real danger they pose is drowning, should one hunt them underwater for too long.\n\nThe ink sacs found in squid are very useful, as the thick black ink is used for writing, as a dye, in alchemy and other uses. This makes squid hunting a potentially lucrative business. \n\nThere are numerous types of squid. Apart from the everyday\n\ncommon squid, some are thought to perhaps only be myths.\n\nIt is said that the Halfling Petyr Brandybuck once raised an army of Battle Squid in combat against the Undead. Their large teeth and overwhelming numbers are thought to have\n\nplayed a part in victory. \n\nAlso sometimes seen are Flying Squid. Frequently mocked as a fairy tale, reports of them were quite common in Aegis. \n\nLastly, there have been reports for over a thousand years of\n\nGiant Squids that live in the deepest parts of the oceans. Although not often documented, some swear they have caused shipwrecks.\n\n- Scribed by the monks, original author unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana Pools", "Minuscule_Evil", "Mana Pools\n\n§§§p        by, Dunii\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nBased on my readings of magic and souls, I believe I have a theory that can go along with what I have learned.\n\nAs I have read, souls give off mana, which is a most basic form of life.\n\nThis mana, as I theorize, is specific to that of the being giving it off.\n\n§TThe void is, however, nothingness as well as the birthplace of everything.Under these pretences, one could assume that its these qualities that cause souls to be\n\nattracted to it.\n\nThe person’s soul, as said before, is unique and as it takes magic to use the mana given off by it. The person’s soul is, however, bound to the person’s body and it does not escape. This means one of two things.\n\nOne being that the person’s soul is bound to the person as long as they are alive.\n\nThe alternative is that the soul is simply there, constantly giving itself off, but never escape. This would mean that the soul is attracted to itself.\n\nA possibility of trapping a soul could then be tapping someone else’s mana and trapping it in a gem, therefore creating a theoretically infinite, or at the very least large, pool of mana for use.\n\nThere is one thing that eludes me, however: how would one tap someone else’s mana? Could it be done with the person’s consent? Is it possible for them to simply allow them to borrow some?\n\nEven then, the trapped mana could be just a finite part of the soul, that is constantly replaced by what will be referred to as the soul’s ‘origin’.\n\nIf this is the case, trapping someone’s ‘origin’ could allow one to have an infinite supply of mana.\n\nThis theory could be useful on lesser creatures such as cows, sheep, chickens and the like.\n\nHOWEVER, if this theory is usable on sentients the results would be devastating. It is for this that I ask that whoever this book is in possession of not to share this information heedlessly!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Book", "Anonymous", "*You happen upon a small, crumbling book. Its faded colours look as if they were once colourful and vibrant, implying that it may have been for a child. A simple picture of a snail can be made out on its rotting cover. Within is\n\nterrible poetry.\n\nOn the inside cover, however, there's some handwriting in ink scribbled in barely legible cursive*\n\n\"I remember you loving this book when you were the size of a pickle,\n\nDamni. I hope it gives you a little smile in the coming days, despite the dreadful rhyming.\n\nMuch love, your brother, Herbert.\n\nP.S. Don't stop making your pumpking pies!\"\n\n*On the next page, the book itself begins.\n\nFar back in the days of the silliest yore,\nWhen knights would woo ladies, and fight nothing but boar,\nThere was an old wizard; a white\n\nbeard to his ankles,\nHis name were Migweed Berleuth-\nPerrydankles.\n\nOld wizened Migweed were in a slump,\nWhilst in his chair resting his wrinkly rump.\nHe were tired of all these youngin's\n\na-many,\nRushing about and bothering him a-plenty.\n\nHe wanted to set a good example,\nFor all the chil’rens against their rushful debacle.\nSo he scratched his chin, and\n\nthunk’d a bunch,\nAnd decided instead he’d have some lunch.\n\nAnd ‘lo, he sat down with a pumpkin pie,\nAnd ate his fill with a serving of lye,\nThen slowly it came from across the old table,\nA small sloshing\n\nsnail, most slow and graceful.\n\n“Aha!” Exclaimed Migweed with a grin most cunning.\n“Ye will be he to send my message a-pummeling,\nInto the mind of many a young stoat!”\nThe snail, in reply,\n\nsaid nothing of note.\n\nThe snail were small, no greater than a mere finger,\nBut on such details Migweed weren’t one to linger.\nHe enchanted his magiks into his pumpkin pies,\nThat any who\n\ndined would grow ten times their size!\n\nMigweed fed the snail a piece most fat,\nAnd the snail were grown to the size of a cat!\nBut the snail loved the taste, and was the greedy sort,\nAnd ate and ate\n\n‘til he were the size of a fort!\n\nMigweed named his fort-snail Sluthery,\nAnd rode upon his shell through miles of shrubbery.\nBut at the first town, he met the sum of his fears.\nHe had died during\n\nthe trip--it had taken ten years!\n\nNot only were size that Sluthery did gain,\nBut also did grow his sluggish snail-brain.\nAnd what did he ask the scared townsfolk within?\n“Poompkim Poie!”\n\nhe glubbled with a grin.\n\nTown after town did he demand of pie,\nAnd fatter he grew as years went by.\nUntil one day he felt a wee-bit woozy.\nSo he found a nice field, and had himself a snoozy.\n\n\nBut this snooze were nary a quiet little matter,\nHe’s yet to wake up, and not getting any fatter!\nPlants and trees grew while he was so still.\nHis shell is bright green! He has become a hill!\n\n\nSo ends the tale of Sluthery the Slothful.\nBut, sweet reader, always be mindful;\nGrow no pumpkins, those who would tempt fate,\nOr you may find him sloshing towards -your- gate!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements", "§bSalamandra", "PROLOGUE\n This book was recovered from Aegis is dated around 1378 of the last age of Aegis. The writings were compiled from a series of entries by the mage Salamandra who has since dissappeared from existence.\n\n           FIRE \n Fire has been an important part of all cultures and religions in the past to modern day Aegis. Fire is bright, strong, takes charge, and wants control. Fire is never subtle, it proudly shows itself. Fire never stops unless acted upon\n\nby another element or force, and it consumes everything it touches.\n\n         WATER\n Water, the neccesity of life. All animals, plants, and even we, the races of Aegis, need it to survive. Water can often be associated with emotion, art, time, and especially healing. In great volume it is a wall of impenetrable force.\n\n         EARTH\n Earth is the first thing you need for almost everything, to ensure stability and endurance. Earth is a reliable element, peaceful and tranquil. Earth is the most passive and strong element, though in moving it can be quite destructive.\n\n            AIR\n Air is the representation of everything we cannot see; our spirits, our souls, our minds, and our hearts. Of that what lies beneath, or beyond some scholars say. The unpredictable and changing wind can be a hurricane or playful breeze\n\n       LIGHTNING\n Lightning is the greatly feared power of weather. Instantaneous and fleeting, its power appears in a moment and is gone in the next. Lightning can be a giver of life, but is most often a taker of it. In its temporal state it seeks a\n\nsubstance to enter into, thereby passing its tremendous power directly into the target. The charge is immediately settled as it meets with the ground, that great power spreading back into the earth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventure Book 1", "Tantaparo", "CREATE YOUR OWN............\n.............ADVENTURE...............\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nYou are stranded alone on an island. Do you check for other inhabitants or begins to find food?\n\n#1 - Pg. 2\n#2 - Pg. 3\n\nYou check for inhabitants, finding a cave with a lit torch. Do you look inside the cave, or do you run away quickly?\n\n#1 - Pg. 4\n#2 - Pg. 5\n\nYou begin to find food, locating two odd herbs: A red one and a blue one. Which do you eat?\n\n#1 - Pg. 6\n#2 - Pg. 7\n\nYou look inside the cave, finding ugly orcs and dwarves. Do you try to kill them or do you try to befriend them?\n\n#1 - Pg. 8\n#2 - Pg. 9\n\nYou run away from the cave, finding a huge monster. Do you try to fight it or run into the cave?\n\n#1 - Pg. 10\n#2 - Pg. 4\n\nYou eat the red herb, slowly beginning to cough up blood, until you die.\n\nRestart.\n\nYou eat the blue herb, filling your stomach's hunger. Regaining strength you decide to build a boat or a house.\n\n#1 - Pg. 11\n#2 - Pg. 12\n\nYou attempt to kill the orcs and dwarves, dying quickly to their blades.\n\nRestart.\n\nYou attempt to befriend the dwarves and orcs. They like you and decide to give you a blue herb.\n\nGo to Pg. 7\n\nYou attempt to kill the monster, hurting it, but netting yourself a short death.\n\nRestart.\n\nYou decide to build a boat, riding out into the ocean. Soon, a tidal wave comes, crushing and suffocating you.\n\nRestart.\n\nYou decide to build a house, the dwarves and orcs helping you. You stay alive and survive.\n\nGood work!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Joke Crystal", "§bOrithur", "Analysis of the 'Misfortune Crystal'\n-------------------\nOrigin unknown, the crystal occasionally, and periodically awakens with a reserved energy. An energy I suspect is built up during its times of inactivity.\n\nThe only visible use\n\nfor this strange relic's energy, is the unusually frustrating ability to produce 'jokes'. I use the word 'jokes' lightly as the dribble the crystal labels as a joke is anything but funny.\n\nI suspect the artifact is a product of a powerful enchanter\n\nor even a greater being, like an Aengul or Daemon. Its intention is very clearly to frustrate, so it is hard to believe that the crystal serves any key purpose. The true joke is its very existence.\n\nThe crystal holds a\n\npersonality of some sorts, but it is only practised through pathetic joke telling. I almost pity its mindless existence. Perhaps if it weren't possessed to deliver 'jokes' it would beg for death.\n\nRegardless, the crystal, although it lacks what most would\n\nconsider a 'body' or 'soul', it is in many ways an individual. This remain the only reason I have not destroyed the wretched thing.\n\n-Orithur of the Nine", ""),
        StaticBook("Wish", "§bEvangiline Wilkes", "Evangiline's wish is to be the greatest culinary mind in the realm.", ""),
